{"abstract":"It is common practice that allograft tissues for knee multiligament reconstruction, meniscus transplantation, cartilage replacement and other advanced procedures are made available through commercial banks. The aim was to present the 10-year experience with a local, non-commercial tissue bank, established in 2014. The allograft bank was connected to an existing organ donor program. Following organ procurement, the musculoskeletal tissue is removed and stored immediately, fresh frozen to − 80 degrees Celsius (except hyaline cartilage, which is stored at 5 degrees Celsius). The donor is tested for contagious disease and the grafts for bacteria. When all results are negative, the grafts are released. When thawed before use a swap is cultured. Consecutive, prospectively collected data were analyzed. There were 31 donations, resulting in 1160 grafts. Only 40 grafts (3.4%) had a positive bacteria culture and were discarded. 552 recipients have been treated by use of these allografts. All grafts had negative bacterial cultures in swaps obtained before thawing, and there were no recorded transplantation related complications. The expenses for local grafts were 10–15% of the costs for grafts obtained from foreign banks. Through the local donation program, it was possible to establish a tissue bank with controlled quality grafts at minimal costs, minimizing the need for transportation of frozen grafts retrieved in other countries. Centers for specialized orthopedic surgery using allograft tissue can be self-providing and reduce costs by retrieving and handling allograft tissues locally.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Azkia, Helia","Harritshøj, Lene Holm","Nielsen, Connie","Agerlin, Niels","Jensen, Mette G.","Hillingsø, Jens G.","Andersen, Pia C.","Krogsgaard, Michael Rindom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-790271"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Allograft","Bacterial contamination","Bank","Musculoskeletal"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a local non commercial tissue bank connected to an organ donor program can produce musculoskeletal allografts of uniform quality at very low costs ten years experience","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10561-024-10151-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-790271","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11584506","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85209892959","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39578258","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4f27187b-3dc3-4d82-92e5-524a81ce6afd"],"keyword":["Allograft","Bacterial contamination","Bank","Musculoskeletal","Organ donors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CEBDC90996B16C8731022EE2F081ECEC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10561-024-10151-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/416552570/s10561_024_10151_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical immunology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Helia","key":"azkiapau","last":"Azkia","name":"Azkia, Helia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Lene H.","key":"harritshøjpau","last":"Harritshøj","locid":"b6c88db4-c95b-4b79-a62b-50b6e5f32a8d","name":"Harritshøj, Lene Holm","name_org":"Harritshøj, Lene H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Connie","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Connie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"agerlinpau","last":"Agerlin","name":"Agerlin, Niels","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette G.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Mette G.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens G.","key":"hillingsøpau","last":"Hillingsø","name":"Hillingsø, Jens G.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia C.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Pia C.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Michael R.","key":"krogsgaardpau","last":"Krogsgaard","locid":"f704dca0-ca86-405a-a7f2-cce1f75f6b8f","name":"Krogsgaard, Michael Rindom","name_org":"Krogsgaard, Michael R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39578258"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10561-024-10151-2","issn":["13899333","15736814"],"issn_org":["13899333"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cell and Tissue Banking","paperid":"1","status":"p","title":"Cell and Tissue Banking","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209892959"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4f27187b-3dc3-4d82-92e5-524a81ce6afd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A local, non-commercial tissue bank connected to an organ donor program can produce musculoskeletal allografts of uniform quality at very low costs – ten years’ experience","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-790271","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Highly pathogenic avian influenza (HPAI) is a major concern in terms of animal and human health. Between October 2020 and September 2023, there were 36 HPAI outbreaks detected in poultry and other captive birds in Denmark. However, it is often not possible to determine the exact route of introduction. We conducted a case-control study to compare the odds of exposure to a range of potential risk factors for HPAI virus incursion into Danish poultry or other captive bird holdings with HPAI outbreaks (cases) and with no HPAI outbreaks (controls) during the HPAI epidemiological seasons 2020/2021, 2021/2022 and 2022/2023. The owners of 38 % of the eligible case holdings and 45 % of the eligible control holdings declined to participate, suggesting that HPAI virus infection is a sensitive subject for some owners. The study population included 18 cases and 34 controls. We collected data primarily through questionnaire-based interviews and estimated odds ratios (OR) within a Bayesian framework using a Beta conjugate prior to define the odds directly, with Monte Carlo integration from these posterior distributions of odds to estimate the relevant OR with 95 % credible intervals (CI) and Bayesian p-values. The results indicated that the odds of observing wild waterfowl or gulls on the roof or around farm buildings compared to observing none within 500 m of the holding was higher for case holdings (OR: 18.7, 95 % CI: 3.1–148, p: 0.022). This information can be used for future risk-based monitoring, biosecurity management and placement of captive bird holdings.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jensen, Helene Ane","Nielsen, Søren Saxmose","Kirkeby, Carsten","Denwood, Matt","Kjær, Lene Jung","Liang, Yuan","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Boklund, Anette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798777"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk factors for the incursion of highly pathogenic avian influenza virus into poultry and other captive bird holdings in denmark from 000000002020 to 000000002023 a case control study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.prevetmed.2025.106419","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798777","identifier":[{"id":"85214653591","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39808886","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-002e3f89-ff7e-4180-9fe1-497d7736d4bf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B3C7800A85B50A76408ECFF14B5D8A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/431510002/Risk_factors_for_the_incursion_of_highly_pathogenic_avian_influenza_virus_into_poultry_and_other_captive_bird_holdings_in_Denmark_from_2020_to_2023.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.prevetmed.2025.106419","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Animal Welfare and Disease Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Helene Ane","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"f34c993a-155f-4065-9269-440ee58100d6","name":"Jensen, Helene Ane","orcid":"0000-0002-4508-5023","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Saxmose","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8d00f12a-fe80-48ba-96c2-6769b91281e7","name":"Nielsen, Søren Saxmose","orcid":"0000-0003-2417-0787","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten Thure","key":"kirkebypau","last":"Kirkeby","locid":"ea24c9a4-7aa6-40f3-9afb-0af19f1e962d","name":"Kirkeby, Carsten","name_org":"Kirkeby, Carsten Thure","orcid":"0000-0001-9292-5526","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matt","key":"denwoodpau","last":"Denwood","locid":"e86ecd1c-385d-49a7-a2ca-45dfc187bc6e","name":"Denwood, Matt","orcid":"0000-0001-5212-4273","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Jung","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"b93ddd14-b340-4550-b3cf-eb9473b0d716","name":"Kjær, Lene Jung","orcid":"0000-0001-9659-4672","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yuan","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","locid":"15fec07b-8b15-410c-9db2-b2b7fda77736","name":"Liang, Yuan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anette Ella","key":"boklundpau","last":"Boklund","locid":"b56cee2e-0320-4c3d-a360-6dc1f5b2ee67","name":"Boklund, Anette","name_org":"Boklund, Anette Ella","orcid":"0000-0001-6359-3403","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39808886"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.prevetmed.2025.106419","issn":["01675877","18731716"],"issn_org":["01675877"],"journal":"Preventive Veterinary Medicine","paperid":"106419","status":"p","title":"Preventive Veterinary Medicine","volume":"236"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214653591"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-002e3f89-ff7e-4180-9fe1-497d7736d4bf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk factors for the incursion of highly pathogenic avian influenza virus into poultry and other captive bird holdings in Denmark from 2020 to 2023 : A case-control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798777","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"In urban drainage, hydrodynamically (HD) based models are often used for urban runoff estimation. Such models are computationally and data demanding, limiting their application, especially in real time. On the other hand, rainfall-runoff hydrologic models are rapid models that are more suitable for real-time applications. However, the use of hydrologic models requires knowledge of their performance relative to the performance of HD-based models. This paper demonstrates the potential of three simpler rainfall-runoff models in a small urban catchment. We show that a time-area surface model with a simple drainage routing model, a linear reservoir model, and an artificial neural network model performs with similar accuracy as a HD-based model. It is demonstrated that urban rainfall-runoff is modeled with high accuracy using both rain gauge and weather radar rainfall. With rain gauge rainfall, the artificial neural network performs the best of both simplified and HD-based models, with Nash–Sutcliffe Efficiency (NSE) = 0.97 on event-accumulated runoff and NSE = 0.83 on a 5-min time series. Using weather radar, rainfall reduces the runoff prediction accuracy. All investigated rainfall-runoff models are, however, shown to produce reliable runoff predictions in small urban areas using rain gauges and weather radar rainfall.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Janni Mosekær","Rasmussen, Michael R.","Thorndahl, Søren Liedtke","Kristensen, Lene Werner","Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-823536"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Janni Mosekær"],"keyword":["Radar QPE","Rainfall runoff","Runoff modeling","Urban drainage","Weather radar"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the potential of simple rainfall runoff models for estimating urban stormwater runoff with rain gauge and weather radar rainfall","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2166/wst.2025.101","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-823536","identifier":[{"id":"105012403638","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5ff597d6-dbb7-4127-96d4-ce3deebd2102"],"keyword":["Radar QPE","Rainfall-runoff","Runoff modeling","Urban drainage","Weather radar"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A2B5468BF1529D37136D33347E78FC3D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/790976959/Exploring_the_potential_of_simple_rainfall-runoff_models_for_estimating_urban_stormwater_runoff_with_rain_gauge_and_weather_radar_rainfall.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2166/wst.2025.101","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Civil and Environmental Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Urban Hydrology Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janni Mosekær","key":"nielsenjannimosekærpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"38f8643a-7f51-4daa-ba8e-18329f6b3ffa","name":"Nielsen, Janni Mosekær","orcid":"0000-0001-5227-2188","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Robdrup","key":"rasmussenmichaelrpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"97f39e8d-f121-4ce8-9157-10ce8955b1d8","name":"Rasmussen, Michael R.","name_org":"Rasmussen, Michael Robdrup","orcid":"0000-0001-5791-3976","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"thorndahlsørenliedtkepau","last":"Thorndahl","locid":"5faa528b-e2f0-41fd-8128-9d76ed5993f0","name":"Thorndahl, Søren Liedtke","name_org":"Thorndahl, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Werner","key":"kristensenlenewernerpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"c9fc85ad-c488-40a2-a583-e2d2e0550698","name":"Kristensen, Lene Werner","orcid":"0009-0000-8868-2867","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ellerbæk","key":"nielsenjesperellerbækpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f850e281-27d9-4783-84c8-3048e7819444","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Ellerbæk","orcid":"0000-0003-4596-0948","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2166/wst.2025.101","issn":["02731223","19969732"],"issn_org":["02731223"],"issue":"2","journal":"Water Science and Technology","pages":"269-284","publisher":"IWA Publishing","status":"p","title":"Water Science and Technology","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105012403638"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5ff597d6-dbb7-4127-96d4-ce3deebd2102"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Exploring the potential of simple rainfall-runoff models for estimating urban stormwater runoff with rain gauge and weather radar rainfall","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-823536","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Seriality in the Streaming Era explores the dynamic transformation of serialized storytelling in the digital era, where platforms like Netflix, Disney+, and Apple Podcasts have redefined how narratives are created, consumed, and experienced. This book examines the profound impact of streaming technologies on both fictional and nonfictional series, offering an in-depth analysis of how these formats have evolved. Drawing from case studies across a wide range of media—from television to podcasts, and social media platforms like Facebook and Snapchat—this book highlights how serialized storytelling has adapted to diverse formats and consumption habits. The authors explore key trends such as platform-specific narrative structures, audience engagement, and the blending of genres in both entertainment and journalism. With a focus on both the aesthetic and functional shifts in seriality, the book offers theoretical insights into the future of storytelling in a media landscape increasingly shaped by data-driven strategies and audience participation. Furthermore, the book tackles how seriality navigates the delicate balance between creativity and commercial demands. As a significant contribution, the book features interviews with key industry professionals in the field of serial media production. Seriality in the Streaming Era is an essential resource for scholars, students, and industry professionals, as well as anyone curious about the evolving role of serialized narratives in shaping modern media culture.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jakob Isak","Heiselberg, Lene","Walther, Bo Kampmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-824610"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"conclusion","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.routledge.com/Seriality-in-the-Streaming-Era/Heiselberg-KampmannWalther-Nielsen-Ronlev/p/book/9781032887869?srsltid=AfmBOopvfKRXERCfFlnBVTDRUJ22fdg6n6gaShpjaqx2X3HXbdNRwAN1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-824610","ids":["au-2216f89f-6d0c-40d8-bda0-e7538ba35889"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3E0E6FC5F19E9CF78199A56EEA8F1FFC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Media Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Isak","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f018a863-b025-4b4c-9503-1cfae0397235","name":"Nielsen, Jakob Isak","orcid":"0000-0002-1304-688X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"heiselbergpau","last":"Heiselberg","name":"Heiselberg, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo Kampmann","key":"waltherpau","last":"Walther","name":"Walther, Bo Kampmann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"Første","isbn":["9781032887869"],"pages":"151-159","place":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Seriality in the Streaming Era"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2216f89f-6d0c-40d8-bda0-e7538ba35889"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Conclusion","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-824610","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: No previous study has described in-hospital cardiac arrest (IHCA) aetiologies prospectively through a protocolised investigation. In this study, we investigated IHCA aetiologies in both IHCA patients achieving return of spontaneous circulation (ROSC) as well as IHCA patients not achieving ROSC. METHODS: Adult IHCA patients were included at Aarhus University Hospital in Denmark. In patients with ROSC, the investigation consisted of blood tests including toxicology, echocardiography, and whole-body computed tomography (CT). In patients without ROSC, the investigation consisted of blood tests including toxicology and whole-body CT- and magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). The primary outcome was the IHCA aetiology as determined by a four-person expert panel using pre-defined main- and subcategories. Secondary outcomes included the presumed cause as determined by cardiac arrest team leaders as well as the discrepancy between presumed and expert panel causes. RESULTS: 150 patients were included, and 71 (47%) achieved ROSC. Expert panel aetiologies (with between-expert ranges) were determined as cardiac in 29% (27-29%) and pulmonary in 30% (25-32%) of cases. Myocardial ischaemia and hypoxia were the most prevalent specific subcategories in 11% (10-15%) and 21% (14-23%) of cases, respectively. The cause was deemed unknown in 7% (0-14%) of cases, and presumed causes were deemed unknown in 26% of cases. Agreement between presumed and expert panel causes was low (Kappa: 0.16-0.42 across experts). CONCLUSION: The predominant aetiologies of IHCA are pulmonary and cardiac. A protocolised investigation, including post-mortem investigations, aided in disclosing IHCA aetiologies. Presumed causes are often unknown and often differ from expert panel causes.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Lind, Peter Carøe","Risager, Benjamin H","Gammelager, Henrik","Bro-Jeppesen, John","Svart, Mads","Boel, Lene Warner Thorup","Hasselstrøm, Jørgen Bo","Andersen, Charlotte Uggerhøj","Al-Mashhadi, Rozh","Nielsen, Tomas Frahm","Andersen, Lars W","Granfeldt, Asger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-824736"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"why do patients develop in hospital cardiac arrest a prospective clinical observational study why ihca","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-824736","identifier":[{"id":"40848870","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105015050941","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2ce43d77-669d-46c8-95e1-8eb28740c14c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8128F9A71E580ED0424D7BBDC51E4A75"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Anaesthesiology and Operation, Intensive care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter C","key":"lindpetercarøepau","last":"Lind","locid":"d62524ef-d9cd-473f-8331-920ba487f03e","name":"Lind, Peter Carøe","name_org":"Lind, Peter C","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Benjamin H","key":"risagerbenjaminhpau","last":"Risager","locid":"68f221ff-7898-4ec8-bc7c-629f9fe9af58","name":"Risager, Benjamin H","orcid":"0009-0001-3993-0358","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"gammelagerhenrikpau","last":"Gammelager","locid":"74961412-13a3-425c-84af-56bad91e1b5e","na