{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Lene","Nielsen, Tina Skau"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-795758"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["T0 2025"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effekt af processering på indholdet af pfas i vegetabilske fodermidler","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dme","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/420599495/Effekt_af_processering_p_indholdet_af_PFAS_i_vegetabilske_fodermidler_inkl_bilag.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-795758","ids":["au-20247811-9d1c-451b-8214-818fc1a1227b"],"keyword":["T0-2025"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-640E6B6EEA01DADC69DCF091C93049F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/420599495/Effekt_af_processering_p_indholdet_af_PFAS_i_vegetabilske_fodermidler_inkl_bilag.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIVET Monogastric Nutrition (MONU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"stødkildejørgensenpau","last":"Stødkilde-Jørgensen","locid":"7edb699b-a75e-48cd-a351-9ee9e1321d4d","name":"Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0001-9434-0118","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Skau","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"76cf0884-56f1-4cef-b905-4b79e8ce0120","name":"Nielsen, Tina Skau","orcid":"0000-0003-0541-4387","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-20247811-9d1c-451b-8214-818fc1a1227b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effekt af processering på indholdet af PFAS i vegetabilske fodermidler","type":"Memorandum/Exposition","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-795758","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aim: We aimed to investigate the causes of acute peripheral facial palsy (PFP) in Danish children and to explore whether neuroborreliosis-related PFP could be diagnosed without lumbar puncture using clinical symptoms and serum Borrelia burgdorferi (Bb) antibodies. Methods: This retrospective population-based cohort study included children undergoing lumbar puncture for PFP between 2019 and 2023 in Denmark's Capital Region. Diagnostic performance measures for neuroborreliosis-related PFP were compared between serum Bb IgG alone and clinical risk scores combining Bb IgG with clinical parameters. Results: Of the 326 patients with PFP, 137 (42%) were diagnosed with neuroborreliosis and 151 (46%) had Bell's palsy. Positive predictive value for serum Bb IgG alone was 88% (95% CI 79–93) and negative predictive value was 83% (95% CI 75–88). The positive predictive value of a risk score with seven additional parameters was 90% (95% CI 81–95) and negative predictive value 87% (95% CI 80–92). Conclusion: The positive predictive value of serum Bb IgG alone was high in our setting, where nearly half of children with PFP had neuroborreliosis. In high endemic settings, lumbar punctures may be reduced by (i) treating all children with PFP with doxycycline or (ii) treating Bb IgG positive children and performing lumbar puncture in seronegative children.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Bloch, Joakim","Schmidt, Lisbeth Samsø","Vissing, Nadja","Nielsen, Alex Christian Yde","Glenthøj, Jonathan Peter","Smith, Birgitte","Lisby, Jan Gorm","Nielsen, Lene","Tetens, Malte","Lebech, Anne Mette","Nygaard, Ulrikka"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-799139"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Borrelia antibodies","Borrelia burgdorferi","Lumbar puncture","Neuroborreliosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"peripheral facial palsy in children serum borrelia antibodies may reduce the need for lumbar puncture","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.17414","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-799139","identifier":[{"id":"85202921159","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39221969","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11627444","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-28cdd23a-7717-47bf-9318-97be5f0bc4a4"],"keyword":["Borrelia burgdorferi","borrelia antibodies","borrelia serology","lumbar puncture","neuroborreliosis","peripheral facial palsy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A2172709528BC8B9995D5BE56E8734A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/424463653/Acta_Paediatrica_2024_Bloch_Peripheral_facial_palsy_in_children_Serum_Borrelia_antibodies_may_reduce_the_need_for.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.17414","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Joakim","key":"blochjoakimpau","last":"Bloch","name":"Bloch, Joakim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Lisbeth","key":"schmidtlisbethsamsøpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"cac4bfbd-c7b5-48c1-946f-03a0d4596cea","name":"Schmidt, Lisbeth Samsø","name_org":"Schmidt, Lisbeth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nadja","key":"vissingnadjapau","last":"Vissing","name":"Vissing, Nadja","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alex Christian Yde","key":"nielsenalexchristianydepau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Alex Christian Yde","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonathan Peter","key":"glenthøjjonathanpeterpau","last":"Glenthøj","name":"Glenthøj, Jonathan Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Birgitte","key":"smithbirgittepau","last":"Smith","locid":"9c96e9e8-99b5-4d7f-a0c9-3d6f3a852d68","name":"Smith, Birgitte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan Gorm","key":"lisbyjangormpau","last":"Lisby","name":"Lisby, Jan Gorm","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"nielsenlenepau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malte","key":"tetensmaltepau","last":"Tetens","name":"Tetens, Malte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anne-Mette","key":"lebechannemettepau","last":"Lebech","locid":"f9b459b7-e203-4824-9d80-e7c0e5b56232","name":"Lebech, Anne Mette","name_org":"Lebech, Anne-Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-0943-3289","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ulrikka","key":"nygaardulrikkapau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"43b2e239-ddc1-4676-a8db-0a0f23906813","name":"Nygaard, Ulrikka","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39221969"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apa.17414","issn":["08035253","08035326"],"issn_org":["08035253"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Paediatrica","pages":"122-130","status":"p","title":"Acta Paediatrica","title_org":"Acta Pædiatrica","volume":"114"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85202921159"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-28cdd23a-7717-47bf-9318-97be5f0bc4a4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Peripheral facial palsy in children : Serum Borrelia antibodies may reduce the need for lumbar puncture","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-799139","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Today, Germanic languages, including German, English, Frisian, Dutch and the Nordic languages, are widely spoken in northwest Europe. However, key aspects of the assumed arrival and diversification of this linguistic group remain contentious1–3. By adding 712 new ancient human genomes we find an archaeologically elusive population entering Sweden from the Baltic region by around 4000 BP. This population became widespread throughout Scandinavia by 3500 BP, matching the contemporaneous distribution of Palaeo-Germanic, the Bronze Age predecessor of Proto-Germanic4–6. These Baltic immigrants thus offer a new potential vector for the first Germanic speakers to arrive in Scandinavia, some 800 years later than traditionally assumed7–12. Following the disintegration of Proto-Germanic13–16, we find by 1650 BP a southward push from Southern Scandinavia into presumed Celtic-speaking areas, including Germany, Poland and the Netherlands. During the Migration Period (1575–1375 BP), we see this ancestry representing West Germanic Anglo-Saxons in Britain, and Langobards in southern Europe. We find a related large-scale northward migration into Denmark and South Sweden corresponding with historically attested Danes and the expansion of Old Norse. These movements have direct implications for multiple linguistic hypotheses. Our findings show the power of combining genomics with historical linguistics and archaeology in creating a unified, integrated model for the emergence, spread and diversification of a linguistic group.","author_count":115,"contributors":["McColl, Hugh","Kroonen, Guus","Moreno Mayar, José Victor","Seersholm, Frederik Valeur","Scorrano, Gabriele","Pinotti, Thomaz","Vimala, Tharsika","Sindbæk, Søren M.","Ethelberg, Per","Fyfe, Ralph","Gaillard, Marie-José","Larsen, Hanne M. Ellegr ard","Mortensen, Morten Fischer","Demeter, Fabrice","Jørkov, M L S","Bergerbrant, Sophie","Damgaard, Peter de Barros","Allentoft, Morten E.","Vinner, Lasse","Gaunitz, Charleen"