{"abstract":"We present a case about a man in his 70s who was admitted to the emergency department, haemodynamically unstable and with complaints of chest pain and dyspnoea. A bedside transthoracic echocardiography showed enlargement of the aorta and pericardial effusion, and a subsequent CT of the aorta showed acute type A intramural haematoma (IMH). Emergency surgery was not possible due to comorbidities, and a wait-and-watch strategy (optimal medical therapy, with blood pressure and pain control and repetitive imaging) was selected. He was hospitalised for a total of 16 days, during which his condition stabilised. A 3-month follow-up CT showed complete regression of both the IMH and haemopericardium.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Illum, Emma","Hüche Nielsen, Lene","Mortensen, Stine Broch","Schneider, Ida Ransby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-801756"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Illum, Emma"],"keyword":["Arteries","Cardiothoracic surgery","Cardiovascular System","Pericardial disease"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term survival and rehabilitation of an inoperable patient with extensive type a aortic intramural haematoma haemopericardium and haemomediastinum","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85218941547","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-801756","identifier":[{"id":"39986670","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85218941547","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1f2fdfc6-d7e7-4c81-96b7-1db296539bb3"],"keyword":["Arteries","Cardiothoracic surgery","Cardiovascular system","Pain (palliative care)","Pericardial disease"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-10D08B113E7913CA28324BE2AE3A4041"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma","key":"illumpau","last":"Illum","locid":"0944ba99-85f7-46c0-b7b9-9d6babf62916","name":"Illum, Emma","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Hüche","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7916784d-f104-44e6-bae9-2aa9f6b95798","name":"Hüche Nielsen, Lene","name_org":"Nielsen, Lene Hüche","orcid":"0009-0003-4383-3889","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Broch","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"d9362fcc-2933-4bdf-a505-671b94aacd24","name":"Mortensen, Stine Broch","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Ransby","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","locid":"bf5d8ec8-2122-4832-ac29-2e6c777db63b","name":"Schneider, Ida Ransby","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39986670"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bcr-2024-262250","issn":["1757790X"],"issue":"2","journal":"BMJ Case Reports","paperid":"e262250","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Case Reports","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85218941547"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1f2fdfc6-d7e7-4c81-96b7-1db296539bb3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Long-term survival and rehabilitation of an inoperable patient with extensive type A aortic intramural haematoma, haemopericardium and haemomediastinum","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-801756","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Perforation of a major epicardial coronary artery during percutaneous coronary interventions (PCIs) is potentially lethal. Here the authors present a novel treatment strategy for managing a perforation in the bifurcation core with a complex 2-stent technique using polyurethane-covered stents. Specialized equipment for chronic total occlusion (CTO) interventions was used for recanalization of the main vessel and side branch. The procedure was tested in a bench setting and validated using 3-dimensional optical coherence tomography and micro-computed tomography. Discussion: The case emphasizes the need for complex CTO-PCI techniques in the treatment of acute non-CTO PCI. Novelty: To the best of our knowledge, this is the first report of a complex bifurcation technique for treatment of an epicardial perforation. Take-Home Message: It is feasible to treat an epicardial perforation in the bifurcation core with an advanced 2-stent technique. Ex vivo training for rare and severe complications may improve procedural outcome.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Holck, Emil Nielsen","Andreasen, Lene Nyhus","Hansen, Emilie Kjær","Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","Brüel, Annemarie","Johansen, Peter","Christiansen, Evald Høj","Jakobsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-806666"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Holck, Emil Nielsen"],"keyword":["Chronic total occlusion","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"complex treatment of a coronary bifurcation perforation with a dual covered stent strategy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaccas.2025.103382","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-806666","identifier":[{"id":"105000514237","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40185573","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12046829","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-6c62164d-7403-4bc0-bb33-39791ec7b644"],"keyword":["chronic total occlusion","coronary perforation","percutaneous coronary intervention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2FB5D132DF4A1B266A42967926347741"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaccas.2025.103382","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emil Nielsen","key":"holckpau","last":"Holck","locid":"8e9383af-7f88-4fa3-bbbc-35641f5cbf8e","name":"Holck, Emil Nielsen","orcid":"0009-0009-6697-1073","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Nyhus","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"4dcde74a-8de8-4b84-b795-c9d84cfc7af7","name":"Andreasen, Lene Nyhus","orcid":"0000-0002-9891-7890","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emilie Kjær","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"da5c3a7f-5eca-4a73-9f67-a72c3810633f","name":"Hansen, Emilie Kjær","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Skovhus","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"924ef2ac-827c-4260-9cd7-fbe300bbafeb","name":"Thomsen, Jesper Skovhus","orcid":"0000-0001-9386-6679","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annemarie","key"