de":"pau"}],"pub":{"place":"København","publisher":"Det Nationale Forskningscenter for Arbejdsmiljø","repno":"NFA-rapport","series":"NFA-rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-7a77c1bb-7d56-46b4-8b2e-9ebfcfb8aa98"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Undersøgelse af udvalgte elementer i indsatsmodellen for forebyggelse af sygefravær på offentlige arbejdspladser","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-811710","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Purpose Patients in temporary stays are typically older individuals with frailty and multimorbidity. However, limited knowledge exists about their medication use. This study aimed to describe prescription drug use among patients in temporary stays in Denmark. Methods We conducted a drug utilisation study on 11,424 patients in public healthcare-operated temporary stay units across 14 Danish municipalities between 2016 and 2023 (median age 81 years; 54% women). Prescription data were sourced from the Danish National Prescription Registry. Results Patients used a median of six drug classes (interquartile range [IQR] 4-10) in the four months before moving into a temporary stay facility; 68% used ≥ 5 drug classes, and 26% used ≥ 10. The most commonly used drug classes were paracetamol (49%), statins (30%), and proton pump inhibitors (29%). The monthly rate of new drug use increased from 23/100 patients six months before move-in to a peak of 262/100 patients in the first month after move-in, driven primarily by laxatives, analgesics, and antibiotics. High-risk drug use increased from 70 to 83% following move-in, with 49% of patients initiating at least one new high-risk drug, most commonly opioids (28%), potassium (17%), and anticoagulants and platelet inhibitors (15%). General practitioners initiated 60-70% of treatments and maintained 80-90%. Hospital physician prescriptions increased around move-in, peaking at 55% for initiation and 25% for maintenance in the first month after move-in. Conclusion Patients in temporary stays in Denmark demonstrate high medication use, including high-risk drugs, with a notable increase in treatment initiations around the time of move-in.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Harbi, Hanin","Lundby, Carina","Jensen, Peter Bjødstrup","Larsen, Søren Post","Rørbæk, Linda Grouleff","Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","Ryg, Jesper","Reilev, Mette","Edwards, Kasper","Pottegård, Anton"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827648"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pottegård, Anton"],"keyword":["Aged","Drug Utilization","Epidemology","Intermediate care facilities","Polypharmacy","Skilled nursing facilities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["REAGENS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"medication use patterns among older patients in temporary stays in denmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-025-01210-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827648","identifier":[{"id":"105004475411","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40332658","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-662de66a-77de-408c-a8e9-8efcd7bd46a9"],"keyword":["Aged","Drug utilization","Epidemology","Intermediate care facilities","Polypharmacy","Skilled nursing facilities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D6654C14DA6D6B3411E0126A442E8128"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-025-01210-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/411359356/s41999-025-01210-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["REAGENS"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics, Strategy and Leadership Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanin","key":"harbipau","last":"Harbi","name":"Harbi, Hanin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carina","key":"lundbypau","last":"Lundby","name":"Lundby, Carina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Bjødstrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Peter Bjødstrup","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Post","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Søren Post","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Linda Grouleff","key":"rørbækpau","last":"Rørbæk","name":"Rørbæk, Linda Grouleff","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Vestergaard","key":"ravnnielsenpau","last":"Ravn-Nielsen","name":"Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","name":"Ryg, Jesper","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"reilevpau","last":"Reilev","name":"Reilev, Mette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"edwardspau","last":"Edwards","locid":"e713de29-a31d-4da0-ba3d-a21f6525c79d","name":"Edwards, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-6328-1765","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","name":"Pottegård, Anton","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40332658"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s41999-025-01210-2","issn":["18787649"],"journal":"European Geriatric Medicine","pages":"1427-1435","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Geriatric Medicine","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004475411"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-662de66a-77de-408c-a8e9-8efcd7bd46a9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Medication use patterns among older patients in temporary stays in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827648","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD) presents a life-threatening condition, prevalent among young women, comprising up to 35% of acute coronary syndrome cases. It involves sudden, trauma-free splitting of coronary artery walls, reducing blood flow and mimicking symptoms of acute myocardial infarction. Despite recent attention, treatment remains debated. Hormonal changes, stress, migraines, physical and psychological aspects impact the prognosis. Ongoing research aims to refine diagnostic and therapeutic approaches, addressing long-term outcomes. In this review, we have summarised current aspects of SCAD to increase awareness of the condition.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Dam-Huus, Karoline Bjerg","Holmvang, Lene","Sørensen, Rikke","Charlot, Mette Gitz","Støttrup, Nicolaj Brejnholt","Nielsen, Lene Hüche","Bang, Lia Evi"],"cuid":["S02-084.97-793254"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Dam-Huus, Karoline Bjerg"],"keyword":["Coronary Vessel Anomalies diagnostic imaging","Diagnosis Differential","Female","Humans","Prognosis","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spontan koronararteriedissektion","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V07240453","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-084.97-793254","identifier":[{"id":"39651692","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85212245120","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-54608aee-1536-4a4e-87dd-a72880695d2b","sdu-d2105be9-2033-4896-9f2e-0965ba87716c"],"keywor