al Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline Bjerg","key":"damhuuspau","last":"Dam-Huus","name":"Dam-Huus, Karoline Bjerg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","name":"Holmvang, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Rikke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Gitz","key":"charlotpau","last":"Charlot","name":"Charlot, Mette Gitz","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicolaj Brejnholt","key":"støttruppau","last":"Støttrup","locid":"73ad5a61-0765-4d5c-8cbb-41362eeb666c","name":"Støttrup, Nicolaj Brejnholt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Hüche","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7916784d-f104-44e6-bae9-2aa9f6b95798","name":"Hüche Nielsen, Lene","name_org":"Nielsen, Lene Hüche","orcid":"0009-0003-4383-3889","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lia Evi","key":"bangpau","last":"Bang","name":"Bang, Lia Evi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lia","key":"evibangpau","last":"Evi Bang","name":"Evi Bang, Lia","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39651692"],"pub":{"doi":"10.61409/v07240453","issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"6","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","paperid":"V07240453","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"187"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-54608aee-1536-4a4e-87dd-a72880695d2b","sdu-d2105be9-2033-4896-9f2e-0965ba87716c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Spontan koronararteriedissektion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.97-793254","year":2025,"yearsub":2025}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In the CONPET study, multiple myeloma patients with abnormal 18FDG positron emission/computed tomography scan after upfront autologous stem cell transplantation were treated with four cycles of carfilzomib-lenalidomide-dexamethasone (KRd). Side effect registrations show that carfilzomib might cause dyspnea, cough, respiratory tract infections, and heart failure. The aims were to investigate patient-reported shortness of breath and dyspnea during KRd consolidation. METHODS: To assess shortness of breath, patients completed the Functional Assessment of Cancer Therapy-Pulmonary Symptom Index (FACT-PSI) and the EORTC QLQ-C30 to assess dyspnea. Shortness of breath was defined as decrease in FACT-PSI score or starting/increasing diuretic drugs. Mixed effect logistic regression was used for the effect analysis. Linear mixed model and clinical relevance were used to investigate dyspnea. RESULTS: A total of 50 patients were included, median age 62 years (interquartile range 54-67). 17% reported shortness of breath at Day 15 Cycles 1-4 versus 11% at Day 1 Cycles 2-4, Cycle 4 Day 29, and 1 month posttreatment (p-value 0.048). Compared with baseline, patients reported significant, and clinically relevant worsening in dyspnea during consolidation. CONCLUSION: Our study confirmed earlier findings of carfilzomib causing shortness of breath during KRd administration and revealed dyspnea during consolidation compared to baseline. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Clinicaltrials.gov: NCT03314636, EudraCT: 2017-000586-72.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Rosenberg, Tine","Möller, Sören","Abildgaard, Niels","Nørgaard, Jakob Nordberg","Lysén, Anna","Tsykonova, Galina","Joao, Cristina","Vangsted, Annette","Schjesvold, Fredrik","Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S02-087.27-793127"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene"],"country":["Norway","Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Haukeland University Hospital","NOVA University Lisbon","Oslo University Hospital","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Aged","Antineoplastic Combined Chemotherapy Protocols adverse effects","Carfilzomib","Clinical trial","Dexamethasone administration dosage","Dyspnea diagnosis","Female","Humans","Lenalidomide administration dosage","Male","Middle Aged","Multiple Myeloma drug therapy","Multiple myeloma","Oligopeptides administration dosage","Patient reported outcomes","Quality of Life","Side effects","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"health related quality of life during carfilzomib lenalidomide dexamethasone consolidation findings from the multiple myeloma conpet study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85210995772","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-087.27-793127","identifier":[{"id":"85210995772","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39638553","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-063b7cfa-94c8-4baa-9057-800342db8809","sdu-9173256f-6496-479b-b8dd-2857e0c55df7"],"keyword":["Aged","Antineoplastic Combined Chemotherapy Protocols/adverse effects","Dexamethasone/administration & dosage","Dyspnea/diagnosis","Female","Humans","Lenalidomide/administration & dosage","Male","Middle Aged","Multiple Myeloma/drug therapy","Oligopeptides/administration & dosage","Treatment Outcome","carfilzomib","clinical trial","multiple myeloma","patient-reported outcomes","quality of life","side effects"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":[