"key":"topelipau","last":"Topeli","name":"Topeli, Arzu","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"35 36","first":"Andreas","key":"barrattduepau","last":"Barratt-Due","name":"Barratt-Due, Andreas","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"37 38","first":"Caterina","key":"barbagliopau","last":"Barbaglio","name":"Barbaglio, Caterina","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"39 40 41","first":"Matthias","key":"kochanekpau","last":"Kochanek","name":"Kochanek, Matthias","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"42 43 44 45 46","first":"Ignacio","key":"martinloechespau","last":"Martin-Loeches","name":"Martin-Loeches, Ignacio","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4 5 6","first":"Nancy","key":"kentishbarnespau","last":"Kentish-Barnes","name":"Kentish-Barnes, Nancy","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40627074"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13613-025-01494-4","issn":["21105820"],"issue":"1","journal":"Annals of Intensive Care","paperid":"91","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Annals of Intensive Care","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105010205086"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7e16a405-ce2e-400c-b212-b493868542d7","ku-7abc1714-fb47-4e90-ad4c-91100da95cd9","sdu-2223b0d0-d8e3-450a-8c5f-e9a937dc4fa6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Platelet transfusion practice in the intensive care unit : the Nine-I international platelet transfusion survey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-822655","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates how the Danish legislation on parallel societies impact media coverage, identity and the planning of the areas affected by this policy. The paper is part of the Regeneration of Danish Disadvantaged Neighbourhoods: Long-term Evaluation (2019-2028) and draws on case studies of 15 areas in two rounds, including media analyses of a 12-month period. To untangle the aspects of the construction of the Danish concept ‘ghetto’, the paper focuses mainly on the case of Skovvejen-Skovparken, a joint venture of two housing associations categorised as a Danish ghetto in 2019, after collaborating on social initiatives for years. The paper applies concepts of place reputation and territorial stigmatisation as well as media studies on disadvantaged housing areas. It shows the following: First, the media analysis shows that the annual Danish list of parallel societies and the media coverage of it confirms and constructs a common place identity that all areas on the list become subject to. Second, the list initiates an informal battle between the areas on the list, and an informal hierarchy is constructed. Third, the paper gives examples of how the ‘naming’ of parallel societies is confirmed by planning strategies and physical analysis. The paper concludes that the parallel society legislation may simultaneously reinforce the spatial problems that it aims at counteracting.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mechlenborg, Mette","Sundstrup, Rikke Borg","Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","Nordberg, Lene Wiell","Bech-Danielsen, Claus","Stender, Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805687"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-30","place":"Delft","start":"2024-08-26","title":"European Network for Housing Research 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the construction of the danish ghetto in legislation media and planning the skovvejen skovparken case","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/795545500/The_construction_of_the_Danish_ghetto_Mechlenborg_et_al._may_2025.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Finansieret af Landsbyggefonden som led i følgeevalueringen"],"id":"S01-000.00-805687","ids":["aau-fc91b908-43d0-40d5-801e-2e31e969179c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4F1C37B222E8814300F0075A1BA13CF9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/795545500/The_construction_of_the_Danish_ghetto_Mechlenborg_et_al._may_2025.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Town, Housing and Property","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Sustainable Cities and Everyday Practice Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"mechlenborgpau","last":"Mechlenborg","locid":"429feb0f-1899-4126-bba7-9ae96ec42ce2","name":"Mechlenborg, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-9446-9795","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Borg","key":"sundstruppau","last":"Sundstrup","locid":"a2f7ee39-5fb3-4db0-8852-355feb84c69a","name":"Sundstrup, Rikke Borg","orcid":"0009-0003-0323-3125","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Skovgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"125da2cb-a5a5-47e8-84ab-be518f10a19f","name":"Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0308-1275","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Wiell","key":"nordbergpau","last":"Nordberg","locid":"4620ca55-6074-4b3d-98ed-0321710187b8","name":"Nordberg, Lene Wiell","orcid":"0000-0003-3344-0574","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"bechdanielsenpau","last":"Bech-Danielsen","locid":"f41ac22b-bb0d-4c3f-8d06-96efd65c0665","name":"Bech-Danielsen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-4822-6039","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie","key":"stenderpau","last":"Stender","locid":"a548a5d3-73b7-4461-9ed9-ba9c0432e2ac","name":"Stender, Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-1009-3138","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","subtitle":"Delft 2024","title":"BOOK OF ABSTRACTS"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fc91b908-43d0-40d5-801e-2e31e969179c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The construction of the Danish ’ghetto’ in legislation, media and planning : The Skovvejen-Skovparken-case","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805687","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Common ash (Fraxinus excelsior) is under intensive attack from the invasive alien pathogenic fungus Hymenoscyphus fraxineus, causing ash dieback at epidemic levels throughout Europe. Previous studies have found significant genetic variation among genotypes in ash dieback susceptibility and that host phenology, such as autumn yellowing, is correlated with susceptibility of ash trees to H. fraxineus; however, the genomic basis of ash dieback tolerance in F. excelsior requires further investigation. Here, we integrate quantitative genetics based on multiple replicates and genome-wide association analyses with machine learning to reveal the genetic architecture of ash dieback tolerance and of phenological traits in F. excelsior populations in six European countries (Austria, Denmark, Germany, Ireland, Lithuania, Sweden). Based on phenotypic data of 486 F. excelsior replicated genotypes we observed negative genotypic correlations between crown damage caused by ash dieback and intensity of autumn leaf yellowing within multiple sampling sites. Our results suggest that the examined traits are polygenic and using genomic prediction models, with ranked single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) based on GWAS associations as input, a large proportion of the variation was predicted by unlinked SNPs. Based on 100 unlinked SNPs, we can predict 55% of the variation in disease tolerance among genotypes (as phenotyped in genetic trials), increasing to a maximum of 63% when predicted from 9155 SNPs. In autumn leaf yellowing, 52% of variation is predicted by 100 unlinked SNPs, reaching a peak of 72% using 3740 SNPs. Based on feature permutations within genomic prediction models, a total of eight nonsynonymous SNPs linked to ash dieback crown damage and autumn leaf yellowing (three and five SNPs, respectively) were identified, these were located within genes related to plant defence (pattern triggered immunity, pathogen detection) and phenology (regulation of flowering and seed maturation, auxin transport). We did not find an overlap between genes associated with crown damage level and autumn leaf yellowing. Hence, our results shed light on the difference in the genomic basis of ADB tolerance and autumn leaf yellowing despite these two traits being correlated in quantitative genetic analysis. Overall, our methods show the applicability of genomic prediction models when combined with GWAS to reveal the genomic architecture of polygenic disease tolerance enabling the identification of ash dieback tolerant trees for breeding or conservation purposes.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Doonan, James","Budde, Katharina B.","Kosawang, Chatchai","Lobo, Albin","Verbylaite, Rita","Brealey, Jaelle C.","Martin, Michael D.","Pliura, Alfas","Thomas, Kristina","Konrad, Heino","Seegmüller, Stefan","Liziniewicz, Mateusz","Cleary, Michelle","Nemesio-Gorriz, Miguel","Fussi, Barbara","Kirisits, Thomas","Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","Heuertz, Myriam","Kjær, Erik Dahl","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811542"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","France","Germany","Ireland","Lithuania","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BOKU University","Bavarian Office for Forest Genetics (AWG)","Federal Research and Training Center for Forests","Forschungsanstalt für Waldökologie und Forstwirtschaft Rheinland-Pfalz","Kaunas Forestry and Environmental Engineering University of Applied Science","Lithuanian Research Centre for Agriculture and Forestry","Northwest German Forest Research Institute","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","SkogForsk","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","Teagasc - Irish Agriculture and Food Development Authority","Université de Bordeaux"],"keyword":["Ash dieback","Common ash","Disease","GWAS","Hymenoscyphus fraxineus","Machine learning","Phenology","SNPs","Tolerance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiple single trait gwas and supervised machine learning reveal the genetic architecture of i fraxinus excelsior i tolerance to ash dieback in europe","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/pce.15361","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-811542","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11963480","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39822124","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105001678322","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-faf99284-fb75-46eb-b955-6f87ebc51712"],"keyword":["GWAS","Hymenoscyphus fraxineus","SNPs","ash dieback","common ash","disease","invasive alien pathogen","machine learning","phenology","tolerance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-638353233EC1BE7755FF45F1E2D041B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/pce.15361","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/448635862/Multiple_Single_Trait_GWAS_and_Supervised_Machine_Learning_Reveal_the_Genetic_Architecture_of_Fraxinus_excelsior_Tolerance_to_Ash_Dieback_in_Europe.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Forest and Landscape Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"northwest german forest research institute","loc":["Ge