,"country":"fr","key":"université de bordeaux","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université de Bordeaux","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"James M.","key":"doonanpau","last":"Doonan","locid":"c05913af-39d1-4b2f-93f0-94af8789b4f2","name":"Doonan, James","name_org":"Doonan, James M.","orcid":"0000-0002-0523-5808","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Katharina B.","key":"buddepau","last":"Budde","name":"Budde, Katharina B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chatchai","key":"kosawangpau","last":"Kosawang","locid":"1b69b056-6473-427b-81f9-20fbd6797849","name":"Kosawang, Chatchai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Albin","key":"lobopau","last":"Lobo","locid":"50b0d4fe-6e8d-4245-aded-c406110ff0b0","name":"Lobo, Albin","orcid":"0000-0002-9580-2860","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rita","key":"verbylaitepau","last":"Verbylaite","name":"Verbylaite, Rita","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jaelle C.","key":"brealeypau","last":"Brealey","name":"Brealey, Jaelle C.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Michael D.","key":"martinpau","last":"Martin","name":"Martin, Michael D.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Alfas","key":"pliurapau","last":"Pliura","name":"Pliura, Alfas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Kristina","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","name":"Thomas, Kristina","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Heino","key":"konradpau","last":"Konrad","name":"Konrad, Heino","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Stefan","key":"seegmüllerpau","last":"Seegmüller","name":"Seegmüller, Stefan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Mateusz","key":"liziniewiczpau","last":"Liziniewicz","name":"Liziniewicz, Mateusz","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Michelle","key":"clearypau","last":"Cleary","name":"Cleary, Michelle","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Miguel","key":"nemesiogorrizpau","last":"Nemesio-Gorriz","name":"Nemesio-Gorriz, Miguel","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","first":"Barbara","key":"fussipau","last":"Fussi","name":"Fussi, Barbara","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","first":"Thomas","key":"kirisitspau","last":"Kirisits","name":"Kirisits, Thomas","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","first":"M. Thomas P.","key":"gilbertpau","last":"Gilbert","locid":"58c97189-c7e9-4486-afb1-e7669608599e","name":"Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","orcid":"0000-0002-5805-7195","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","first":"Myriam","key":"heuertzpau","last":"Heuertz","name":"Heuertz, Myriam","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39822124"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/pce.15361","issn":["01407791","13653040"],"issn_org":["01407791"],"issue":"5","journal":"Plant, Cell and Environment","pages":"3793-3809","status":"p","title":"Plant, Cell and Environment","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001678322","2-s2.0-85214972706"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-faf99284-fb75-46eb-b955-6f87ebc51712"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multiple, Single Trait GWAS and Supervised Machine Learning Reveal the Genetic Architecture of <i>Fraxinus excelsior</i> Tolerance to Ash Dieback in Europe","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-811542","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The plasticity of adaptive traits may be critical for population persistence in heterogeneous environments. However, its evolution is rarely investigated in forest pathogens, potentially limiting the accuracy of epidemic risk predictions. Ash dieback is an emblematic example of a forest epidemic caused by an invasive fungal pathogen-Hymenoscyphus fraxineus, which has likely been introduced to Eastern Europe from East Asia. We investigated the plasticity and thermal niche evolution of H. fraxineus during its spread across Europe. We characterized the reaction norms of in vitro mycelial growth and viability of H. fraxineus isolates from five European populations sampled along a latitudinal gradient spanning from Lithuania to Italy. While all populations responded uniformly to temperature decrease, their responses to temperature increase diverged markedly. The growth of H. fraxineus isolates from the northernmost population (Lithuania) was most negatively affected by high temperatures, whereas the southernmost isolates (Italy) showed optimal growth at a higher temperature compared to the other populations. Additionally, the viability of Lithuanian isolates was significantly reduced by higher temperatures compared to that of the other populations. These findings suggest that both growth plasticity and thermal niche have evolved during the pathogen's expansion in Europe, with potentially important implications for predicting and managing future epidemic risks. We further discuss how evolutionary processes may have shaped these phenotypic differences.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Becans, Clemence","Robin, Cecile","Budde, Katharina B.","Ghelardini, Luisa","Gross, Andrin","Lygis, Vaidotas","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Saint-Jean, Gilles","Soularue, Jean-Paul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818778"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Italy","Lithuania","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Northwest German Forest Research Institute","State Scientific Research Institute Nature Research Centre","Swiss Federal Institute for Forest, Snow and Landscape Research","University of Florence","Université de Bordeaux"],"keyword":["Ash dieback","Microbial evolution","Thermal plasticity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolution of thermal plasticity in i hymenoscyphus fraxineus i during ash dieback expansion in europe","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.71513","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818778","identifier":[{"id":"001510151100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"40534982","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105008567866","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12173838","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-2ad1458a-bacb-4528-a55b-3f2c213f3b4b"],"keyword":["<italic>Chalara fraxinea</italic>","<italic>Hymenoscyphus fraxineus</italic>","<italic>Hymenoscyphus pseudoalbidus</italic>","Ash dieback","Invasive fungal pathogen","Microbial evolution","Plasticity evolution","Thermal plasticity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F202EF4B8F4190BFD61A3172BE370D39"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/454749899/Ecology_and_Evolution_-_2025_-_B_cans_-_Evolution_of_Thermal_Plasticity_in_Hymenoscyphus_fraxineus_During_Ash_Dieback.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.71513","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"université de bordeaux","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université de Bordeaux","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"northwest german forest research institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Northwest German Forest Research Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of florence","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Florence","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute for forest snow and landscape research","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute for Forest, Snow and Landscape Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"lt","key":"state scientific research institute nature research centre","loc":["Lithuania","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"State Scientific Research Institute Nature Research Centre","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Forest and Landscape Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Clemence","key":"becanspau","last":"Becans","name":"Becans, Clemence","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cecile","key":"robinpau","last":"Robin","name":"Robin, Cecile","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Katharina B.","key":"buddepau","last":"Budde","name":"Budde, Katharina B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Luisa","key":"ghelardinipau","last":"Ghelardini","name":"Ghelardini, Luisa","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Andrin","key":"grosspau","last":"Gross","name":"Gross, Andrin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Vaidotas","key":"lygispau","last":"Lygis","name":"Lygis, Vaidotas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gilles","key":"saintjeanpau","last":"Saint-Jean","name":"Saint-Jean, Gilles","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jean-Paul","key":"soularuepau","last":"Soularue","name":"Soularue, Jean-Paul","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40534982"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ece3.71513","issn":["20457758"],"issue":"6","journal":"Ecology and Evolution","paperid":"e71513","status":"p","title":"Ecology and Evolution","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008567866"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2ad1458a-bacb-4528-a55b-3f2c213f3b4b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolution of Thermal Plasticity in <i>Hymenoscyphus fraxineus</i> During Ash Dieback Expansion in Europe","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818778","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Transposable elements (TEs) have been hypothesized to play a pivotal role in driving diversification by facilitating the emergence of novel phenotypes and the accumulation of divergence between species. Hybridization and adaptation to novel niches have been proposed to destabilize mechanisms constraining TE proliferation, potentially inducing a ‘TE burst’ that promotes TE accumulation on the genome. The rapid speciation and ecological diversification characteristic of adaptive radiations offer a unique opportunity to examine the link between TE accumulation and speciation, diversification, hybridization and adaptation. Here, focusing on all 15 species of the genus Scalesia (Asteraceae), a radiation endemic to the Galápagos Islands, we test whether diversification, hybridization, or shifts in ecological niche are associated with changes in TE accumulation in genomes. Our analyses reveal little to no variation in TE accumulation among Scalesia species nor its hybrid populations. Shifts in ecological niches, linked to climatic variation, did not result in discernible changes in TE accumulation, a surprising finding given the anticipated selective pressure imposed by aridity, a factor often linked to genome size reduction. We found no distinct patterns in the temporal accumulation of TEs, and no effects at the class or superfamily level. Our findings suggest that while TEs may play a key role in evolution at the locus level, their macroevolutionary association with diversification or speciation appears weak. Rather than actively driving evolutionary diversification, TEs may simply be'along for the ride.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Cerca, José","Díaz, Patricia Jaramillo","Goubert, Clément","Yang, Heidi","Bieker, Vanessa C.","Fernández-Mazuecos, Mario","Vargas, Pablo","Schley, Rowan","Li, Siyu","Guevara-Andino, Juan Ernesto","Petersen, Bent","Petersen, Gitte","Sinha, Neelima R.","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Leebens-Mack, James H.","Rivas-Torres, Gonzalo","Rieseberg, Loren H.","Martin, Michael D."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819521"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Ecuador","Malaysia","Norway","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Asian Institute of Medicine, Science and Technology","Charles Darwin Foundation Santa Cruz","International Union for Conservation of Nature","Karolinska Institutet","McGill University","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Stockholm University","Swedish Museum of Natural History","The Spanish National Research Council (CSIC)","Universidad San Francisco de Quito","Universidad de las Américas - Ecuador","University of Arizona","University of British Columbia","University of California at Davis","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Exeter","University of Georgia","University of Málaga","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no evidence of transposable element bursts in the galápagos i scalesia i adaptive radiation despite hybridization diversification and ecological niche shifts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13100-025-00362-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-819521","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12125827","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40450335","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105006890086","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-82fbf40a-c4c1-4135-851f-010c8c5598e5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C6CBAECBE1019138A778C6044182E0AD"],"oa_link":[{"