{"abstract":"While previous literature suggests that plant-based diets may be associated with a lower risk of breast cancer, evidence remains inconsistent. In this study, we investigated the association between adherence to plant-based diets and breast cancer risk in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (EPIC) study. Overall plant-based diet index (PDI), healthful (hPDI), and unhealthful PDI (uPDI) were calculated, and multivariable Cox models were used to estimate hazard ratios (HR) and 95% confidence intervals (CI) of breast cancer for the three indices. Mediation analysis was performed to assess the role of body mass index (BMI) and waist circumference (WC) in the association between hPDI and postmenopausal breast cancer risk. Over a median follow-up of 14.9 years, 10,805 incident invasive breast cancer cases were identified among 258,343 women. In the multivariable model, not adjusted for BMI, higher adherence to hPDI was inversely associated with breast cancer risk, with HR per 1-SD increase [95% (CI)] of 0.97 (0.94, 0.99). The corresponding HRs (95% CI) per 1-SD increase for overall PDI and uPDI were 0.98 (0.96, 1.00) and 1.01 (0.99, 1.03), respectively. The associations between hPDI and postmenopausal breast cancer were partly explained by BMI and WC, which mediated 30% and 52% of this association, respectively. Higher adherence to hPDI was associated with a slightly lower total breast cancer risk. For postmenopausal breast cancer, this association was partly explained by lower BMI or WC. These findings suggest that promoting healthful plant-based diets could support breast cancer risk reduction.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Shah, Sanam","Laouali, Nasser","Mahamat-Saleh, Yahya","Biessy, Carine","Nicolas, Geneviève","Rinaldi, Sabina","Zamora-Ros, Raul","Papadimitriou, Nikos","Morales-Berstein, Fernanda","Dahm, Christina C","Christensen, Anne Kristine Lundgård","Mellemkjaer, Lene","Nielsen, Anne Marie Overgaard","Mancini, Francesca Romana","Ren, Xuan","Marques, Chloé","Katzke, Verena","Le Cornet, Charlotte","El-Khoury, Christine","Schulze, Matthias B","Agnoli, Claudia","Simeon, Vittorio","Tumino, Rosario","Milani, Lorenzo","Castro-Espin, Carlota","Sánchez, Maria-Jose","Aizpurua, Amaia","Colorado-Yohar, Sandra M","Guevara, Marcela","Heath, Alicia","Aune, Dagfinn","Freisling, Heinz","Huybrechts, Inge","Dossus, Laure"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-826088"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Shah, Sanam"],"country":["Colombia","France","Germany","Italy","Morocco","Norway","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Andalusian School of public health","BioGipuzkoa Health Research Institute","Biomedical Research Institute of Murcia - Arrixaca","CIBERESP - Research Centre Network for Epidemiology and Public Health","Catalan Institute of Oncology-ICO","Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Nazionale dei Tumori","German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)","German Institute of Human Nutrition Potsdam-Rehbruecke","Hyblean Association for Epidemiological Research (AIRE-ONLUS)","IdiSNA, Navarra Institute for Health Research, Pamplona, Spain.","Imperial College London","Instituto de Investigación Biosanitaria ibs","International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC)","Ministry of Health of the Basque Government","Mohammed VI Polytechnic University","Norwegian Institute of Public Health","Oslo New University College, Oslo","Public Health Institute of Navarra","Universidad de Antioquia","Universite Paris-Saclay","University of Bristol","University of Campania Luigi Vanvitelli","University of Potsdam","University of Turin"],"keyword":["Body Mass Index","Breast cancer","Dietary pattern","Mediation","Plant based diet","Prospective study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plant based dietary patterns and breast cancer risk in the european prospective investigation into cancer and nutrition epic study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105010684302","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-826088","identifier":[{"id":"105010684302","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40658296","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-abe73d29-b95e-4c02-9a56-2fa29f1168bb"],"keyword":["body mass index","breast cancer","dietary pattern","mediation","plant-based diet","prospective study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7CCB78A85A00C2EB9D51380416CC0A80"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"international agency for research on cancer","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC)","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ma","key":"mohammed vi polytechnic university","loc":["Morocco","Africa"],"name":"Mohammed VI Polytechnic University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"catalan institute of oncology ico","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Catalan Institute of Oncology-ICO","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of bristol","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bristol","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Department of Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society rese