k":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"52 53","first":"Lene","key":"terslevpau","last":"Terslev","locid":"d10590c5-f19a-4682-ab40-30cb3dc6ffca","name":"Terslev, Lene","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"54 55 56","corresponding":null,"first":"Wolfgang","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Wolfgang","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"57 58","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"dejacopau","last":"Dejaco","name":"Dejaco, Christian","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39753294"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/rmdopen-2024-004667","issn":["20565933"],"issue":"1","journal":"RMD Open","paperid":"e004667","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"RMD Open","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214590138"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c08208c9-7a28-4489-b226-3697fbb8d976","ku-6a62b045-aa30-4cf3-b396-1a74e591e164","sdu-be9d8fc9-705e-4838-bf56-2062619f87c1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Reliability of the OMERACT Giant cell arteritis Ultrasonography Score (OGUS) : results of a patient-based exercise involving experts and non-experts in vascular ultrasonography","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.95-793422","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BackgroundAssessment of cancer patients<acute accent> quality of life (QoL) through patient-reported outcomes (PRO) during and after treatment is gaining ground. The HM-PRO is the first generic Haematological Malignancy specific PRO measure for use in clinical practice and clinical trials. Such generic tools are needed in Denmark. The study aim was to translate and cross-culturally adapt the HM-PRO into Danish and evaluate the psychometric properties.MethodsTranslation and cross-cultural adaptation of the original English HM-PRO into Danish followed established guidelines. After cognitive debriefing interviews, it underwent psychometric testing with a variety of hematologic malignancies. Construct validity, internal consistency, dimensionality, item response theory (IRT) and differential item functioning were investigated.Results295 patients were included for psychometric evaluation; confirmatory factor and bifactor analyses for both HM-PRO parts provided good evidence to support the suggested factor structure (Cronbach's-alpha Part-A = 0.81, Part-B = 0.84; Part-A CFA CFI = 0.922, TLI = 0.912; bi-factor CFI = 0.989, TLI = 0.978). IRT showed good item-fit and factor loadings and absence of local dependency.ConclusionThe HM-PRO has demonstrated favourable psychometric properties and can be used broadly within the Danish Healthcare system to monitor symptoms as well as QoL impact of patients with haematological cancer and optimize patient engagement during routine cancer care.What is the new aspect of your work?In response to the intention of the Danish Health Authority to systematically collect PRO data on health-related QoL in Danish cancer patients, this study investigates the translation and cross-cultural adaptation of the original English HM-PRO into Danish.What is the central finding of your work?Few issues were met with the translation and adaptation of HM-PRO into Danish.What is (or could be) the specific clinical relevance of your work?The HM-PRO has demonstrated favourable psychometric properties and can be used broadly within the Danish Healthcare system to monitor symptoms as well as QoL impact of patients with haematological cancer and optimize patient engagement during routine cancer care.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Salek, Sam","Möller, Sören","Abildgaard, Niels","Rosenberg, Tine","Larsen, Maria Torp","Asdahl, Peter H","Pedersen, Kasper Kofod","Lassen, Marie Therese","Andersen, Christen Lykkegaard","Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S04-099.00-822292"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Salek, Sam"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Hertfordshire"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Cross Cultural Comparison","Cross cultural adaptation","Danish HM PRO","Denmark","Female","Hematologic Neoplasms psychology","Humans","Male","Malignant lymphomas","Middle Aged","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Patient reported outcomes","Psychometrics","Quality of Life","Reproducibility of Results","Surveys and Questionnaires","Translating","Translations"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"translation cultural adaptation and validation of the danish version of the haematological malignancy patient reported outcome measure hm pro","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s41687-025-00869-2","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was a nationwide project with participation from six haematology departments across Denmark sponsored by the Department of Haematology, Odense University Hospital, Denmark. The study included three steps; (1) translation and cross-cultural adaptation, (2) cognitive debriefing and (3) psychometric testing. According to Danish law, this study was exempted for notification to the regulatory authorities. The study was approved by the Danish Data Protection Agency (Journal number 19/13870)."],"id":"S04-099.00-822292","identifier":[{"id":"105003864356","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12040771","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40299237","type":"pmid"},{"id":"001479110300003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-3f90f83d-b794-488b-b576-9c1b99e1d33f","au-ce4b17a7-07e1-434a-86d8-2222755047f2","ku-861ab694-3b8a-4b24-996d-39636ec0aef9","sdu-9e18ecb4-0731-4ea4-a5a0-0817052fd23a"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Cross-Cultural Comparison","Cross-cultural adaptation","Danish HM-PRO","Denmark","Female","Hematologic Neoplasms/psychology","Humans","Male","Malignant lymphomas","Middle Aged","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Patient-reported outcomes","Psychometrics","Quality of Life","Reproducibility of Results","Surveys and Questionnaires","Translating","Translations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-DA5A27551158D1B717881AD487BFEBEC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s41687-025-00869-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/449079812/s41687-025-00869-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/289726158/s41687-025-00869-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/794670850/Sal