ournal of Patient-Reported Outcomes","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003864356"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3f90f83d-b794-488b-b576-9c1b99e1d33f","au-ce4b17a7-07e1-434a-86d8-2222755047f2","ku-861ab694-3b8a-4b24-996d-39636ec0aef9","sdu-9e18ecb4-0731-4ea4-a5a0-0817052fd23a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Translation, cultural adaptation and validation of the Danish version of the haematological malignancy patient-reported outcome measure (HM-PRO)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.00-822292","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest is a leading cause of death worldwide. Establishing vascular access is critical for administering guideline-recommended drugs during cardiopulmonary resuscitation. Both the intraosseous route and the intravenous route are used routinely, but their comparative effectiveness remains unclear. METHODS: We conducted a randomized clinical trial to compare the effectiveness of initial attempts at intraosseous or intravenous vascular access in adults who had nontraumatic out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. The primary outcome was a sustained return of spontaneous circulation. Key secondary outcomes were survival at 30 days and survival at 30 days with a favorable neurologic outcome, defined by a score of 0 to 3 on the modified Rankin scale (scores range from 0 to 6, with higher scores indicating greater disability). RESULTS: Among 1506 patients who underwent randomization, 1479 were included in the primary analysis (731 in the intraosseous-access group and 748 in the intravenous-access group). The successful establishment of vascular access within two attempts occurred in 669 patients (92%) assigned to the intraosseous-access group and in 595 patients (80%) assigned to the intravenous-access group. Sustained return of spontaneous circulation occurred in 221 patients (30%) in the intraosseous-access group and in 214 patients (29%) in the intravenous-access group (risk ratio, 1.06; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.90 to 1.24; P = 0.49). At 30 days, 85 patients (12%) in the intraosseous-access group and 75 patients (10%) in the intravenous-access group were alive (risk ratio, 1.16; 95% CI, 0.87 to 1.56); a favorable neurologic outcome at 30 days occurred in 67 patients (9%) and 59 patients (8%), respectively (risk ratio, 1.16; 95% CI, 0.83 to 1.62). Prespecified adverse events were uncommon. CONCLUSIONS: There was no significant difference in sustained return of spontaneous circulation between initial intraosseous and intravenous vascular access in adults who had out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. (Funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation and others; IVIO EU Clinical Trials Register number, 2022-500744-38-00; ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT05205031.).","author_count":59,"contributors":["Vallentin, Mikael F.","Granfeldt, Asger","Lass Klitgaard, Thomas","Mikkelsen, Søren","Folke, Fredrik","Christensen, Helle Collatz","Povlsen, Amalie L.","Petersen, Alberthe H.","Winther, Sofie","Frilund, Lea W.","Meilandt, Carsten","Holmberg, Mathias J.","Winther, Kristian B.","Bach, Allan","Dissing, Thomas H.","Terkelsen, Christian J.","Christensen, Steffen","Rasmussen, Line Kirkegaard","Mortensen, Lone R.","Loldrup, Mads L.","Elkmann, Thomas","Nielsen, Anders G.","Runge, Charlotte","Klæstrup, Elise","Holm, Jimmy H.","Bak, Mikkel","Nielsen, Lars-Gustav R.","Pedersen, Mette","Kjærgaard-Andersen, Gunhild","Hansen, Peter M.","Brøchner, Anne C.","Christensen, Erika Frischknecht","Nielsen, Frederik Mølgaard","Nissen, Christian G.","Bjørn, Jeppe W.","Burholt, Peter","Obling, Laust E.R.","Holle, Sarah L.D.","Russell, Lene","Alstrøm, Henrik","Hestad, Søren","Fogtmann, Tanja H.","Buciek, Jens U.H.","Jakobsen, Karina","Krag, Mette","Sandgaard, Michael","Sindberg, Birthe","Andersen, Lars W."],"cuid":["S04-099.26-793025"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Lars W."],"keyword":["Cardiac arrest","Cardiology","Clinical Medicine","Clinical Medicine General","Critical care","Emergency Medicine General","Emergency medicine","Pulmonary Critical Care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Præhospitalet"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intraosseous or intravenous vascular access for out of hospital cardiac arrest","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/281833598/NEJMoa2407616.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation, the Tryg Foundation, Aarhus University, the Independent Research Fund Denmark, and Snedkermester Sophus Jacobsen og Hustru Astrid Jacobsens Fond through the Danish Heart Foundation."],"id":"S04-099.26-793025","identifier":[{"id":"39480221","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85214563180","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c706ef52-3848-4781-8855-6db2e52f15de","au-82668ae3-8a3c-4221-bc01-734feb8a9714","ku-4a8c869d-e3d6-4d10-a4f4-77a11d30fae3","sdu-957edf0b-ca42-4476-8c51-fa040903d478"],"keyword":["Cardiac Arrest","Cardiology","Clinical Medicine","Clinical Medicine General","Critical Care","Emergency Medicine","Emergency Medicine General","Pulmonary/Critical Care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-48D68C5443B7662FF64938C7D9350758"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/281833598/NEJMoa2407616.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Præhospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["