of Southern Denmark","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk","prehospital emergency medical services"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c706ef52-3848-4781-8855-6db2e52f15de","au-82668ae3-8a3c-4221-bc01-734feb8a9714","ku-4a8c869d-e3d6-4d10-a4f4-77a11d30fae3","sdu-957edf0b-ca42-4476-8c51-fa040903d478"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Intraosseous or Intravenous Vascular Access for Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.26-793025","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Objective: This study explored if the patient-experience and the affect heuristic influenced improvements in painful symptoms, in response to open label placebo injections in patients with knee OA. It furthermore explored if other cognitive biases or heuristics were involved in the response to open-label placebo. Method: A mixed method study in a pre-specified knee OA cohort. The influence of patient-experience, and the affect heuristic, on change in painful symptoms in response to an open-label placebo injection, were assessed using a questionnaire and multivariate linear regression. The group concept mapping method was used to characterise the expectations and hopes regarding the effect of an open-label placebo injection in non-responders and responders, defined as the lower- and upper quartile of the ΔVAS pain scores. Results: 103 participants received the questionnaire, and 60 finalised questionnaires were included in the analysis showing that the reduction in pain was associated with the patient-experience and that the affect heuristic acted as an effect modifier. Three workshops were held for non-responders (n ​= ​13) and responders (n ​= ​15) each generating respectively 113 and 119 statements. It was found that the two groups reported different expectations and hopes for the open label placebo injections. Conclusions: The patient-experience influenced the response to an open label placebo injection in patients with knee OA, and this influence was moderated by the strength of the affect heuristic. Furthermore, non-responders and responders reported different hopes and expectation towards the open label placebo injection indicating the presence of the optimism bias in the responder group.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Annfeldt, Tommy Kok","Ginnerup-Nielsen, Elisabeth","Wæhrens, Eva Elisabeth","Vase, Lene","Kristensen, Lars Erik","Jørgensen, Tanja Schjødt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-797166"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Annfeldt, Tommy Kok"],"keyword":["Cognitive bias","Heuristic","Knee OA","Open label placebo","Pain","Placebo response"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"do cognitive bias and heuristics influence improvement in knee pain in patients with knee osteoarthritis treated with open label placebo the chips study an exploratory study using questionnaire and group concept mapping","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ocarto.2025.100574","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-797166","identifier":[{"id":"39975810","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85216582984","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11836500","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-d638a74f-dd86-4535-b253-75c6b19c68d1"],"keyword":["Cognitive bias","Heuristic","Knee OA","Open-label placebo","Pain","Placebo response"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-DC48FBD13474DD6C42B7046182023950"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ocarto.2025.100574","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tommy Kok","key":"annfeldtpau","last":"Annfeldt","name":"Annfeldt, Tommy Kok","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth","key":"ginnerupnielsenpau","last":"Ginnerup-Nielsen","name":"Ginnerup-Nielsen, Elisabeth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Elisabeth","key":"wæhrenspau","last":"Wæhrens","name":"Wæhrens, Eva Elisabeth","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"vasepau","last":"Vase","locid":"efb21f77-3dc3-425c-b185-d30c3518d8ba","name":"Vase, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-0379-2256","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Erik","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Lars Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tanja Schjødt","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Tanja Schjødt","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39975810"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ocarto.2025.100574","issn":["26659131"],"issue":"1","journal":"Osteoarthritis and Cartilage Open","paperid":"100574","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Osteoarthritis and Cartilage Open","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85216582984"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d638a74f-dd86-4535-b253-75c6b19c68d1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Do cognitive bias and heuristics influence improvement in knee pain in patients with knee osteoarthritis treated with open label placebo? The CHIPS study - An exploratory study using questionnaire and group concept mapping","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-797166","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background . HIV viremia has been considered a cardiovascular disease (CVD) risk factor, but many studies have had insufficient data on potential confounders. We explored the association between viremia and CVD after adjusting for established risk factors and analyzed whether consideration of viremia would improve CVD prediction. Methods . Adults from RESPOND were followed from the first date with available data until the first of rigorously defined CVD, loss to follow-up, death, or administrative censoring. We first analyzed the associations between 6 measures of viremia (time-updated, before antiretroviral therapy [ART], viremia category, and measures of cumulative viremia) and CVD after adjusting for the variables in the D:A:D CVD score (age, sex/gender, smoking, family history, diabetes, recent abacavir, CD4 count, blood pressure, cholesterol, high-density lipoprotein, cumulative use of stavudine, didanosine, indinavir, lopinavir, and darunavir). We subsequently compared predictive performance with and without viremia in 5-fold internal cross-validation. Results. A total of 547 events were observed in 17 497 persons (median follow-up, 6.8 years). Although some viremia variables were associated with CVD in univariable analyses, there were no statistically significant associations after adjusting for potential confounders, neither for measures of current viral load, pre-ART viral load, highest viremia category during ART, nor cumulative viremia (modeled both as total cumulative viremia, cumulative viremia during ART, and recent cumulative viremia). Consistently, none of the viremia variables improved prediction capacity. Conclusions . In this large international cohort, HIV viremia was not associated with CVD when adjusting for established risk factors. Our results did not show viremia to be predictive of CVD among people with HIV.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Elvstam, Olof","Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Neesgaard, Bastian","Tau, Luba","Günthard, Huldrych F.","Zangerle, Robert","Vehreschild, Jörg Janne","Wit, Ferdinand","Sönnerborg, Anders","Kovari, Helen","Abutidze, Akaki","Petoumenos, Kathy","Jaschinski, Nadine","Hosein, Sean","Bogner, Johannes","Grabmeier-Pfistershammer, Katharina","Garges, Harmony","Rooney, Jim","Young, Lital","Law, Matthew","Kirk, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798965"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Central","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["for the RESPOND Study Group"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Belgium","Georgia","Germany","Israel","Netherlands","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["AIDS and Clinical Immunology Research Center","All Global Affiliations","European AIDS Treatment Group","Gilead Sciences","GlaxoSmithKline","Goethe University Frankfurt","HIV Monitoring Foundation","Innsbruck Medical University","Karolinska Institutet","Karolinska University Hospital","Klinik Hirslanden","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Lund University","Medical University of Vienna","Merck","Tel Aviv University","University Hospital Zürich","University of New South Wales","University of Zurich","Växjö Central Hospital"],"keyword":["Cardiovascular Diseases","Myocardial Infarction","Prediction","Stroke"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"viremia does not independently predict cardiovascular disease in people with hiv a respond cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ofid/ofaf016","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798965","identifie