iia","key":"valkonenpau","last":"Valkonen","name":"Valkonen, Miia","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"67 68","corresponding":null,"first":"Andry","key":"vandelouwpau","last":"van de Louw","name":"van de Louw, Andry","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"darmonpau","last":"Darmon","name":"Darmon, Michael","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcrc.2025.155149","issn":["08839441","15578615"],"issn_org":["08839441"],"journal":"Journal of Critical Care","paperid":"155149","publisher":"WB  Saunders","publisher_org":"W.B. Saunders","status":"p","title":"Journal of Critical Care","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009209646"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4308c8be-4de7-46b5-87ba-f73602162061","sdu-e9181f72-8c6f-4102-9eb5-cadc7d24cdf2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sex-based differences in ICU management and outcomes of immunocompromised patients : A post hoc analysis of the prospective multicenter multinational Efraim cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-822934","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Objective Ultrasonography is crucial for diagnosing giant cell arteritis (GCA); however, training opportunities are rare. This study tested the reliability of ultrasonography findings and measurements of the intima-media thickness (IMT) among ultrasonography experts by using phantoms of the axillary (AA) and temporal arteries (TA) created with high-resolution 3D printing. Methods Twenty-eight participants from 12 European countries received eight sets of phantoms of the AA and the superficial TA (including common, frontal and parietal branches), which were examined in a blinded fashion according to a predefined protocol and evaluated based on Outcome Measures in Rheumatology (OMERACT) GCA ultrasound definitions. Due to difficulties with the delineation of the intima-media complex, the parietal branch of the phantoms was modified, and a second round was conducted. The IMT was measured, and phantoms were classified as normal or vasculitic. Results In both rounds, the phantoms were correctly classified as normal/abnormal in >81% of cases yielding a Fleiss’ kappa of 0.80 (95% CI 0.78 to 0.81) in round 1 and 0.74 (95% CI 0.72 to 0.75) in round 2. IMT measurements revealed an intraclass correlation coefficient (ICC 1.1) of 0.98 (95% CI 0.98 to 0.99) in both rounds. Intrarater reliability was good with a median Cohens Kappa of 0.83 and median ICC of 0.78. Conclusion The study demonstrated high reliability among ultrasound experts in applying the OMERACT ultrasound definitions for GCA and in measuring the IMT using a 3D-printed phantom of the AA and TA. This phantom could assist clinicians in training to assess the large arteries of patients with suspected or established GCA.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Schremmer, Tobias","Dejaco, Christian","Recker, Florian","Aschwanden, Markus","Boumans, Dennis","Bruyn, George A.","Chrysidis, Stavros","Daikeler, Thomas","Nielsen, Berit Dalsgaard","De Miguel, Eugenio","Diamantopoulos, Andreas P.","Dohn, Uffe Moller","Duftner, Christina","Germano, Giuseppe","Haagsma, Cees","Hartung, Wolfgang","Hocevar, Alojzija","Iagnocco, Annamaria","Juche, Aaron","Karakostas, Pantelis","Karalilova, Rositsa","Keller, Kresten Krarup","Sarker, Borsha","Smith, Kate","Tischler, Verena","Macchioni, Pierluigi","Milchert, Marcin","Monti, Sara","Mukhtyar, Chetan","Naredo, Esperanza","Schmidt, Wolfgang A.","Seitz, Luca","Terslev, Lene","Wakefield, Richard J.","Schäfer, Valentin Sebastian"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-793332"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Schäfer, Valentin Sebastian"],"country":["Austria","Bulgaria","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Poland","Slovenia","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AUSL-IRCCS Reggio Emilia","All Global Affiliations","Asklepios Medical Center","Bonn University Hospital","Brunico Hospital","Hospital Universitario Fundación Jimenez Díaz-Quironsalud, Madrid, Spain.","Hospital of Bruneck","Hospital of Southern Norway","IIS-Fundacion Jimenez Diaz","IRCCS Azienda Unità Sanitaria Locale di Reggio Emilia","Immanuel Hospital Berlin-Wannsee Branch","Immanuel Krankenhaus Berlin","Innsbruck Medical University","Klinik für Gastroenterologie und Diabetologie, Vivantes Humboldt-Klinikum, Am Nordgraben 2, 13509, Berlin, Deutschland. norman.schoeffel@vivantes.de.","Medical University of Graz","Medical University of Innsbruck","Medical University of Plovdiv","NIHR Leeds Biomedical Research Centre","Norfolk and Norwich University Hospital NHS Trust","Norfolk and Norwich University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Pomeranian Medical University","Pomeranian Medical University in Szczecin","Tergooi Medical Centre","Universidad Autónoma de Madrid","University Hospital Basel","University Hospital Bonn","University Hospital La Paz","University Hospital of Basel","University Medical Centre Ljubljana","Un