{"abstract":"To compare γ-glutamyl di- and tripeptides generated by different Bacillus strains and investigate the impact of substrates on the production of γ-glutamyl peptides, six strains of four species, including B. subtilis, B. velezensis, B. amyloliquefaciens and B. paralicheniformis, were cultivated in a standard brain heart infusion (BHI) broth and a medium consisting of hemoglobin hydrolysates (HH) for six days. Quantitative analysis of free amino acids and γ-glutamyl peptides, as well as determination of bacterial growth and γ-glutamyltransferase activity were carried out. Results revealed that all Bacillus strains could generate a series of γ-glutamyl dipeptides in both media. Most strains produced higher concentrations of target peptides in the HH medium (up to 83.56 μM), which correlated with higher levels of free amino acids in the medium. Glutathione was detected only in the BHI medium with B. subtilis PRO84, B. velezensis PRO76, B. altitudinis PRO107, and B. paralicheniformis PRO109 (up to 0.61 μM), indicating the glutathione-forming ability of these Bacillus strains. Production of γ-glutamyl peptides was influenced by both the choice of strain and growth medium, with the medium exerting a more pronounced impact than the strain. This study highlights the importance of selecting the appropriate substrate and Bacillus strains to produce desired γ-glutamyl peptides as enhancers of koku, potentially inspiring the conversion of meat side streams into valuable kokumi seasonings.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Li, Qian","Zhang, Longteng","Jespersen, Lene","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","Lametsch, Rene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764832"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hainan University"],"keyword":["Bacillus","Hemoglobin hydrolysate","γ Glutamyl peptides"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of i bacillus i strains and growth medium in shaping γ glutamyl peptide production","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fbio.2024.105103","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764832","identifier":[{"id":"85203798070","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3c7118bd-b078-4cde-9e11-83ebced126e5"],"keyword":["Bacillus","Hemoglobin hydrolysate","γ-glutamyl peptides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1CD03B120F4BF731FBE81D9E4C00C105"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/407127549/1_s2.0_S2212429224015335_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fbio.2024.105103","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Analytics and Biotechnology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Ingredient and Dairy Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hainan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hainan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Qian","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"9f1a4f0b-a4f6-437c-8b8d-16580bd096df","name":"Li, Qian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Longteng","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"a491e5b8-b0ad-4190-b796-b7c49908664f","name":"Zhang, Longteng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"a156c6e3-9562-4d35-9305-53a39c62e076","name":"Jespersen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-2555-5948","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dennis Sandris","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René","key":"lametschpau","last":"Lametsch","locid":"70bd350a-6869-4a4a-b9bc-56a756376784","name":"Lametsch, Rene","name_org":"Lametsch, René","orcid":"0000-0002-4189-806X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fbio.2024.105103","issn":["22124292","22124306"],"issn_org":["22124292"],"journal":"Food Bioscience","paperid":"105103","status":"p","title":"Food Bioscience","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203798070"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3c7118bd-b078-4cde-9e11-83ebced126e5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The role of <i>Bacillus </i>strains and growth medium in shaping γ-glutamyl peptide production","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764832","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Health institutions advocate for psychosocial and recovery-oriented interventions alongside pharmacological treatment for severe mental illness. Participatory arts interventions appear promising in promoting personal recovery by fostering connectedness, hope, renegotiation of identity, meaning-making, and empowerment. Despite encouraging findings, however, the evidence base remains thin. Further, results from cognitive literature studies suggest possible impact on parameters of clinical recovery, but this has not been studied in clinical contexts. We developed REWRITALIZE, a structured, recovery-oriented, fifteen-session creative writing group intervention led by a professional author alongside a mental health professional. Participants engage with literary forms, write on them, share their texts, and partake in reflective discussions within a supportive, non-stigmatising environment, designed to promote self-expression, playful experimentation, agency, recognition, participatory meaning-making, renegotiation of identity and social engagement. The aim of this project is to evaluate REWRITALIZE for persons with severe mental illness through a randomised controlled trial (RCT) focusing on personal recovery outcomes. Additionally, an embedded pilot RCT will explore additional outcomes i.e., clinical recovery for a subgroup with schizophrenia spectrum disorders. Methods: The RCT is an investigator-initiated, randomised, two-arm, assessor-blinded, multi-center, waiting-list superiority trial involving 300 participants (age > 18) from six psychiatric centers in regions Capital and Zealand in Denmark, randomised to receive either the creative writing intervention combined with standard treatment or standard treatment alone. Assessments will be conducted before and after the intervention and at six months post intervention. The primary outcome is personal recovery at the end of intervention measured with the questionnaire of the process of recovery. Secondary outcomes include other measures of personal recovery, self-efficacy, mentalising, and quality of life. The pilot RCT, integrated within the RCT, will focus on 70 of the participants aged 18–35 with schizophrenia spectrum disorders, evaluating exploratory measures related to perspective-taking, social cognition, cognitive function, psychosocial functioning, and symptom pressure. Discussion: This is the first RCT for creative writing groups. It assesses whether REWRITALIZE, as adjunct to standard mental healthcare, is more effective for personal recovery than standard care. If successful, it would provide evidence for the efficacy of REWRITALIZE, potentially enabling its implementation across mental health centers in Denmark. Trial registration: Privacy (data protection agency): p-2023–14655. Danish National Center for Ethics: 2313949. Clinicaltrials.gov: NCT06251908. Registration date 02.02.2024.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Henningsson, Susanne","Brestisson, Jon Toke","Bjørkedal, Siv Therese Bogevik","Bundesen, Birgit","Nielsen, Keld Stehr","Ebersbach, Bea","Hjorthøj, Carsten","Eplov, Lene Falgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776972"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Creative writing","Psychosocial interventions","Recovery","Schizophrenia spectrum disorders","Severe mental illness"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Danish National Centre for Arts and Mental Health"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rewritalize your recovery a study protocol for a randomised controlled trial rct examining the effectiveness of the new recovery oriented creative writing group intervention rewritalize for people with severe mental illness","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12888-024-06254-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776972","identifier":[{"id":"85211322320","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39639282","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11619309","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-0f641016-1efc-4ee6-9736-f00ba25cb3a0"],"keyword":["Creative writing","Participatory arts","Psychosocial interventions","Recovery","Schizophrenia spectrum disorders","Severe mental illness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-039201B5BAD53EE19760FF72937B40E8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/414743916/s12888_024_06254_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12888-024-06254-5","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish National Centre for Arts and Mental Health"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Mental Health Services Glostrup"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Susanne","key":"henningssonpau","last":"Henningsson","name":"Henningsson, Susanne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jon Toke","key":"brestissonpau","last":"Brestisson","name":"Brestisson, Jon Toke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Siv Therese Bogevik","key":"bjørkedalpau","last":"Bjørkedal","name":"Bjørkedal, Siv Therese Bogevik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Birgit","key":"bundesenpau","last":"Bundesen","name":"Bundesen, Birgit","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Keld Stehr","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Keld Stehr","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bea","key":"ebersbachpau","last":"Ebersbach","name":"Ebersbach, Bea","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Carsten","key":"hjorthøjpau","last":"Hjorthøj","locid":"d4b636e3-7c21-48a0-b812-de219ca78a9e","name":"Hjorthøj, Carsten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Falgaard","key":"eplovpau","last":"Eplov","name":"Eplov, Lene Falgaard","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39639282"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12888-024-06254-5","issn":["1471244X"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Psychiatry","paperid":"891","status":"p","title":"BMC Psychiatry","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211322320"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0f641016-1efc-4ee6-9736-f00ba25cb3a0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"REWRITALIZE your recovery : a study protocol for a randomised controlled trial (RCT) examining the effectiveness of the new recovery-oriented creative writing group intervention REWRITALIZE for people with severe mental illness","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776972","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Mononuclear phagocytes (MNP), including macrophages and classical dendritic cells (cDC), are highly heterogeneous cells with distinct functions. Understanding MNP complexity in the intestinal lamina propria (LP), particularly in humans, has proved difficult due to the expression of overlapping phenotypic markers and the inability to isolate these cells without contamination from gut-associated lymphoid tissues (GALT). Here, we exploited our novel method for isolation of human GALT-free LP to carry out single-cell (sc)RNA-seq, CITE-seq and flow cytometry analysis of human ileal and colonic LP MNPs. As well as classical monocytes, non-classical monocytes, mature macrophage subsets, cDC1s, and cDC2s, we identified a CD1c+ cDC subset with features of both cDC2 and monocytes, which were transcriptionally similar to the recently described cDC3. While similar MNP subsets were present in both ileal and colonic LP, the proportions and transcriptional profiles of these populations differed between these sites and in diseased states, indicating local specialization and environmental imprinting. Using computational trajectory tools, we identified putative early committed pre-cDC subsets and developmental intermediates of mature cDC1, cDC2 and cDC3, as well as monocyte–to-macrophage trajectories. Collectively, our results provide novel insights into the heterogeneity and development of intestinal LP MNP and an important framework for studying the role of these populations in intestinal homeostasis and disease.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Fenton, Thomas M.","Wulff, Line","Jones, Gareth-Rhys","Vandamme, Julien","Jørgensen, Peter B","Bain, Calum C.","Lee, Julie","Izarzugaza, Jose Mg","Belling, Kirstine G","Ho, Gwo-Tzer","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Riis, Lene Buhl","Pers, Tune H.","Jakobsen, Henrik L.","Mowat, Alland M.","Brunak, Søren","Agace, William Winston"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777977"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh","University of Glasgow"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high dimensional profiling demonstrates complexity tissue imprinting and lineage specific precursors within the mononuclear phagocyte compartment of the human intestine","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2021.03.28.437379","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-777977","ids":["ku-6aab2f7b-419c-42d5-9348-cfcfa3765a3c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A4EFB12DBA2C18DEBEF6802E5950BAE3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2021.03.28.437379","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/410855745/2021.03.28.437379v2.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of glasgow","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Glasgow","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Thomas M.","key":"fentonpau","last":"Fenton","name":"Fenton, Thomas M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"wulffpau","last":"Wulff","name":"Wulff, Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gareth-Rhys","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","name":"Jones, Gareth-Rhys","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julien","key":"vandammepau","last":"Vandamme","name":"Vandamme, Julien","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter B","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Peter B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Calum C.","key":"bainpau","last":"Bain","name":"Bain, Calum C.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Julie","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Julie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jose Mg","key":"izarzugazapau","last":"Izarzugaza","name":"Izarzugaza, Jose Mg","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kirstine G","key":"bellingpau","last":"Belling","name":"Belling, Kirstine G","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gwo-Tzer","key":"hopau","last":"Ho","name":"Ho, Gwo-Tzer","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Ole Haagen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lene Buhl","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tune H","key":"perspau","last":"Pers","locid":"209c62ff-f452-48bc-8d42-63be1645edd5","name":"Pers, Tune H.","name_org":"Pers, Tune H","orcid":"0000-0003-0207-4831","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Henrik L.","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen, Henrik L.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Alland M.","key":"mowatpau","last":"Mowat","name":"Mowat, Alland M.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Søren","key":"brunakpau","last":"Brunak","locid":"9398f2a1-bef5-4491-9b57-083e6758eac2","name":"Brunak, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-0316-5866","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"William Winston","key":"agacepau","last":"Agace","name":"Agace, William Winston","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1101/2021.03.28.437379","pages":"123","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6aab2f7b-419c-42d5-9348-cfcfa3765a3c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"High-dimensional profiling demonstrates complexity, tissue imprinting, and lineage-specific precursors within the mononuclear phagocyte compartment of the human intestine","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777977","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The Bacillus Calmette-Guérin (BCG) vaccine may induce non-specific protection against unrelated infections. We tested the effect of BCG on the risk of infections among Danish senior citizens. Methods: Single-blinded randomised controlled trial including 1676 volunteers >65 years. Participants were randomised 1:1 to BCG or placebo and followed for 12 months. The primary outcome was acute infection leading to medical contact. Secondary outcomes were verified SARS-CoV-2 infection, self-reported respiratory symptoms, and all-cause hospitalisation. Data was analysed using Cox regression models, estimating hazard ratios (HR) with 95% confidence intervals (CI). Results: The incidence of acute infection was 52.1 and 58.2 per 100 person-years for BCG and placebo, respectively (HR=0.89, 95% CI=0.78–1.02). There was no effect of BCG on SARS-CoV-2 infections (0.97, 0.75–1.26) or all-cause hospitalisations (1.10, 0.80–1.50), but BCG was associated with more respiratory symptoms (1.21, 1.10–1.33). BCG reduced the incidence of acute infections among participants <75 years (0.82, 0.70–0.95) but not among those >75 years (1.14, 0.88–1.47). In participants, who were COVID-19 vaccinated before enrolment, BCG was associated with lower incidence of acute infections (0.65, 0.50–0.85). Conclusion: BCG did not reduce risk of acute infections among Danish seniors overall, but the effect was modified by age group and COVID-19 vaccination. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT04542330) and EU Clinical Trials Register (EudraCT number 2020-003904-15). Full trial protocol is available at ClinicalTrials.gov. In a randomised clinical trial among Danish senior citizens, BCG vaccination did not reduce the overall risk of acute infection, but BCG was associated with reduced risk in participants <75 years and participants who received COVID-19 vaccines prior to enrolment.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Madsen, Anne Marie Rosendahl","Gehrt, Lise","Schaltz-Buchholzer, Frederik","Möller, Sören","Christiansen, Rikke","Schellerup, Lars","Norberg, Lene Annette","Krause, Tyra Grove","Nielsen, Sebastian","Bliddal, Mette","Aaby, Peter","Benn, Christine Stabell"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783076"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"corresponding_author":["Madsen, Anne Marie Rosendahl"],"country":["Guinea-Bissau"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INDEPTH Network"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","BCG Vaccine","BCG Vaccine administration dosage","COVID 19 pandemic","COVID 19 prevention control","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Heterologous effects","Hospitalization statistics numerical data","Humans","Incidence","Infectious diseases","Male","Non specific effects of vaccines","Randomised controlled trial","SARS CoV 2 immunology","Senior citizens","Single Blind Method","Vaccination statistics numerical data"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"OT":["Odense Kommune"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluating the effect of bcg vaccination for non specific protection from infection in senior citizens during the covid 000000000019 pandemic a randomised clinical trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jinf.2024.106319","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-783076","identifier":[{"id":"39423874","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85206905767","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-4bd6062e-0595-4dea-8344-3cf9d51f1c69"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","BCG Vaccine/administration & dosage","BCG revaccination","BCG vaccine","COVID-19 pandemic","COVID-19/prevention & control","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Heterologous effects","Hospitalization/statistics & numerical data","Humans","Incidence","Infectious diseases","Male","Non-specific effects of vaccines","Randomised controlled trial","SARS-CoV-2/immunology","Senior citizens","Single-Blind Method","Vaccination/statistics & numerical data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C1C1A99D922C2CC0442A69AD98D8C2F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jinf.2024.106319","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/276334023/1-s2.0-S0163445324002536-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Central Administration, Vice-Chancellor's Office, DIAS","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Open - Bandim"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gw","key":"indepth network","loc":["Guinea-Bissau","Africa"],"name":"INDEPTH Network","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Odense Kommune"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordi