"orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cancan","key":"wangpedh","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Cancan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Laura","key":"junckerjensenpedh","last":"Juncker-Jensen","name":"Juncker-Jensen, Laura","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788794538039"],"pages":"1-4","place":"Copenhagen","status":"p","title":"Action Research Booklet"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-39fbc1c5-859b-4512-ace2-abfff8eb891d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A case of action research with a focus on collective learning about organisational challenges and solutions for democratically owned businesses","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789548","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The editions of Leonora Christina’s French autobiography (2021) and Otto Sperling’s biography of Leonora Christina (2022) have provided prerequisites for a thorough study of the two works and of their mutual relationship, including the question of the autobiography’s addressee. At least since 1730, Otto Sperling has been designated as the addressee, which Sebastian Olden-Jørgensen has argued against in two articles from 2022. Instead, he has put forward the hypothesis that the autobiography is addressed to Admiral Henrik Bielke. This hypothesis has motivated the present study. The procedure has been to collate the two texts and bring out all agreements and deviations (section 2). Next, the autobiography has been read closely to collect all information about the addressee (section 3), and the other sources for the addressee question have been scrutinized (section 4). Finally, the importance of the addressee question for the perception of the autobiography is assessed: Is it indeed a private letter or a defense addressed to an international audience? (section 5). The main results of the investigation are that the autobiography is not conform to the characteristics of a private letter, and that Otto Sperling was probably the “Monsieur” to whom the autobiography is directly addressed, but that the true addressee was the European network of the Ulfeldt family and other influential circles.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Akhøj Nielsen, Marita","Schøsler, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-799361"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Det danske Sprog- og Litteraturselskab"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adressaten for leonora christinas selvbiografi","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/457260393/02_HB2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-799361","ids":["ku-44475ef9-6d20-4f18-b5f4-a1212c147f23"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6B956AA93EA9E16811C75CC83460B185"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/457260393/02_HB2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/danskestudier/article/view/156740","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Det danske Sprog- og Litteraturselskab"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of English, Germanic and Romance Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marita","key":"akhøjnielsenpau","last":"Akhøj Nielsen","name":"Akhøj Nielsen, Marita","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"schøslerpau","last":"Schøsler","locid":"4638bb59-4175-4e41-9a72-07d80d794ed1","name":"Schøsler, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["0105449X","01064525"],"issn_org":["01064525"],"journal":"Danske Studier","pages":"27-61","status":"p","title":"Danske Studier","volume":"2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-44475ef9-6d20-4f18-b5f4-a1212c147f23"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Adressaten for Leonora Christinas selvbiografi","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-799361","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Due to changes in pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics, patients with impaired renal function suffer an increased risk of suboptimal and potentially harmful medication treatment. This necessitates careful consideration of medications affected by impaired renal function when performing medication reviews. The aim of this study was to develop a quick guide (a list of recommendations) for assessing renal risk medications in medication reviews led by hospital pharmacists. The list was based on the 100 most frequently used medications in Danish hospitals and primary care. After combining the 200 records, 29 duplicates were excluded resulting in a pool of 171 medications. Assessment by two clinical pharmacists led to the exclusion of 121 medications. Of the remaining 50 medications, seven were discussed among the two pharmacists, and two of these were also in the research group to reach a consensus. The renal risk quick guide comprised 50 medications. The most prevalent medications on the list were from Anatomical Therapeutic Chemical Classification System (ATC)-group N, C and L. Recommendations from two databases were included in the quick guide in order to provide clinical pharmacists with existing, updated evidence on medication use in impaired renal function. The next step is to test the feasibility of the quick guide in daily practice when performing medication reviews.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","Andersen, Trine Rune Høgh","Olesen, Charlotte","Hedegaard, Ulla","Coric, Faruk","Routhe, Lisa Greve","Revell, Joo Hanne Poulsen","Press, Anita Buch Grann","Houlind, Morten Baltzer","Kjeldsen, Lene Juel"],"cuid":["S02-084.91-768680"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard"],"keyword":["Aged","Clinical pharmacology","Denmark","Drug Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions prevention control","Female","Hospitals","Humans","Impaired renal function","Kidney drug effects","Male","Medication optimisation","Pharmacy Service Hospital organization administration","Practice Guidelines as Topic","Primary Health Care","Renal Insufficiency chemically induced","Risk Assessment","renal risk medication","risk assessment quick guide"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Universityhospital Sønderjylland"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of a quick guide for assessment of the most frequently used renal risk medication in danish hospitals and primary care","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.14068","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-084.91-768680","identifier":[{"id":"85201557724","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39161990","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1a8fb169-77a3-4d3e-867b-1924388af4f5","sdu-3f896c78-92f8-430a-92d0-130d345832eb"],"keyword":["Aged","Denmark","Drug-Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions/prevention & control","Female","Hospitals","Humans","Kidney/drug effects","Male","Pharmacists/organization & administration","Pharmacy Service, Hospital/organization & administration","Practice Guidelines as Topic","Primary Health Care","Renal Insufficiency/chemically induced","Risk Assessment","clinical pharmacology","impaired renal function","medication optimisation","renal risk medication","risk assessment quick guide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-23E20771AAD46121E45F2159291E39F9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi