9bb77-b340-412a-9523-d96ff4341b97"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The impact of an illness perception conversation on open-label placebo response in knee osteoarthritis : A randomised controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-768010","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Despite scarce evidence, guidelines recommend weight loss as a management strategy for patients with gout. We investigated the effect of an intensive dietary intervention on body weight and clinical measures of gout severity in individuals with obesity and gout. Methods: We conducted a 16-week randomized nonmasked parallel-group trial in Denmark, randomly assigning (one-to-one) individuals with obesity and gout to a low-energy diet or a control diet. The primary outcome was change in body weight. Key secondary outcomes were changes in serum urate (SU) level and visual analog scale-assessed pain and fatigue. Results: Between December 1, 2018, and June 1, 2019, 61 participants were included in the intention-to-treat population and randomly assigned to the intensive diet group (n = 29) or control diet group (n = 32). Participants had a mean age of 60.3 (SD 9.9) years and mean body mass index of 35.6 (SD 5.0), and 59 (97%) were men. After 16 weeks, there was a significant difference in change in body weight between the diet and control groups (-15.4 vs -7.7 kg; difference -7.7 kg [95% confidence interval -10.7 to -4.7], P < 0.001). Despite results being potentially in favor of a low-energy diet, we could not confirm differences in SU level changes and fatigue between groups. No differences in pain and gout flares were observed between groups. No serious adverse events or deaths occurred during the trial. Conclusion: An intensive dietary intervention was safe and effectively lowered body weight in people with obesity and gout, but the weight loss did not directly translate into effects on SU level, fatigue, and pain.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Christensen, Robin","Zobbe, Kristian","Nielsen, Sabrina M.","Stamp, Lisa K.","Henriksen, Marius","Overgaard, Anders F.","Dreyer, Lene","Knop, Filip K.","Singh, Jasvinder A.","Doherty, Michael","Richette, Pascal","Astrup, Arne","Ellegaard, Karen","Bartels, Else M.","Boesen, Mikael","Gudbergsen, Henrik","Bliddal, Henning","Kristensen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S03-082.07-734869"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Robin"],"country":["Czechia","France","New Zealand","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Assistance publique – Hôpitaux de Paris","Atlanta Veterans Affairs Medical Center","Birmingham VA Medical Center","Charles University","Hôpital Lariboisiere AP-HP","Institut national de la santé et de la recherche médicale","Paris Hospitals and Paris Descartes University","University of Alabama at Birmingham","University of Alabama at Birmingham (UAB)","University of Nottingham","University of Otago","Université Paris Cité","VA Medical Center"],"keyword":["Aged","Body Mass Index","Diet Reducing","Fatigue etiology","Female","Gout complications","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Obesity complications","Proof of Concept Study","Uric Acid blood","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-NOVO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-NP-NOVO","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"weight loss for patients with gout and concomitant obesity a proof of concept randomized trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/645143467/Christensen_et_al._2024_._Weight_Loss_for_Patients_with_Gout_and_Concomitant_Obesity_-_A_Proof-of-Concept_Randomized_T