nternational inception cohort study (PLOT-ICU)","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-722902","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Pre-exposure prophylaxis (PrEP) effectively prevents HIV, but its association with sexually transmitted infections (STIs) has raised concerns about risk compensation, potentially impacting the expansion of PrEP programmes. Aim: We examined the relationship between PrEP and the incidence of chlamydia, gonorrhoea and syphilis. Methods: In this prospective cohort study, we compared STI rates before and after PrEP initiation among users in the capital region of Denmark (2019–2022), calculating incidence rate ratios adjusted for age and testing frequency (aIRR). To pinpoint when increases began, we plotted weekly STI rates, adjusting the timeline to correspond with PrEP initiation. Results: The study included 1,326 PrEP users with a median age of 35 years. The STI incidence rate per 100,000 person-years rose from 35.3 before to 81.2 after PrEP start, with an aIRR of 1.35 (95% CI: 1.18–1.56). Notably, this increase preceded PrEP initiation by 10–20 weeks. Specific aIRR for chlamydia, gonorrhoea and syphilis were 1.23 (95% CI: 1.03–1.48), 1.24 (95% CI: 1.04–1.47) and 1.15 (95% CI: 0.76–1.72), respectively. In subanalyses for anatomical sites aIRR was 1.26 (95% CI: 1.01–1.56) for rectal chlamydia and 0.66 (95% CI: 0.45–0.96) for genital gonorrhoea. Conclusion: We found a 35% increase in STI incidence associated with PrEP use. It started before PrEP initiation, challenging the assumption that PrEP leads to risk compensation. Instead, the data suggest that individuals seek PrEP during periods of heightened sexual risk-taking. Consequently, PrEP programmes should include sexual health consultations, STI testing, treatment and prevention strategies to prevent HIV and improve sexual health.","author_count":13,"contributors":["von Schreeb, Sebastian","Pedersen, Susanne Kriegel","Christensen, Hanne","Jørgsensen, Kristina Melbardis","Harritshøj, Lene Holm","Hertz, Frederik Boetius","Ahlström, Magnus Glindvad","Lebech, Anne Mette","Lunding, Suzanne","Nielsen, Lars Nørregaard","Gerstoft, Jan","Kronborg, Gitte","Engsig, Frederik N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731376"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"questioning risk compensation pre exposure prophylaxis prep and sexually transmitted infections among men who have sex with men capital region of denmark 000000002019 to 000000002022","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2807/1560-7917.ES.2024.29.13.2300451","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-731376","identifier":[{"id":"85189135379","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10979528","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38551099","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-67f037a2-b952-4e9c-8c48-068e736a291b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B74DFF0DC0923EF377F84E4D909F6C09"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2807/1560-7917.ES.2024.29.13.2300451","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/387994882/eurosurv_29_13_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical immunology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Sebastian","key":"vonschreebpau","last":"von Schreeb","name":"von Schreeb, Sebastian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susanne Kriegel","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Susanne Kriegel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Hanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kristina Melbardis","key":"jørgsensenpau","last":"Jørgsensen","name":"Jørgsensen, Kristina Melbardis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Lene Holm","key":"harritshøjpau","last":"Harritshøj","locid":"b6c88db4-c95b-4b79-a62b-50b6e5f32a8d","name":"Harritshøj, Lene Holm","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Frederik Boetius","key":"hertzpau","last":"Hertz","name":"Hertz, Frederik Boetius","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Magnus Glindvad","key":"ahlströmpau","last":"Ahlström","name":"Ahlström, Magnus Glindvad","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Anne Mette","key":"lebechpau","last":"Lebech","locid":"f9b459b7-e203-4824-9d80-e7c0e5b56232","name":"Lebech, Anne Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-0943-3289","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Suzanne","key":"lundingpau","last":"Lunding","name":"Lunding, Suzanne","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars Nørregaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lars Nørregaard","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jan","key":"gerstoftpau","last":"Gerstoft","name":"Gerstoft, Jan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Gitte","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"6dfd64b6-b92a-46ff-9008-4c065e9cbddb","name":"Kronborg, Gitte","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Frederik N.","key":"engsigpau","last":"Engsig","name":"Engsig, Frederik N.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38551099"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2807/1560-7917.es.2024.29.13.2300451","issn":["1025496X"],"issue":"13","journal":"Eurosurveillance","paperid":"2300451","status":"p","title":"Eurosurveillance","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189135379"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-67f037a2-b952-4e9c-8c48-068e736a291b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Questioning risk compensation : pre-exposure prophylaxis (PrEP) and sexually transmitted infections among men who have sex with men, capital region of Denmark, 2019 to 2022","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731376","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Bone marrow lesions (BMLs) in knee osteoarthritis (OA) have been assessed histopathologically and by dynamic contrast-enhanced magnetic resonance imaging (DCE-MRI); however, a direct comparison of the results has not been reported. Purpose: To evaluate and compare the findings by DCE-MRI and histopathology of subchondral BMLs in knee OA. Material and Methods: In total, 19 patients with medial tibiofemoral knee OA undergoing total knee arthroplasty were analyzed. Preoperative MRI, including a DCE sequence, was performed, and bone biopsies were obtained from the resected specimens corresponding to BML areas. The contrast enhancement by DCE-MRI was analyzed using semi-quantitative (area under the curve [AUC]), peak enhancement [PE]), and quantitative (Ktrans, Kep) methods. Enhancement in the medial OA compartment was compared with similar areas in a normal lateral compartment, and the DCE characteristics of BMLs were correlated with semi-quantitatively graded histopathological features. Results: AUC and PE were significantly higher in medial tibial and femoral BMLs compared with the values in the lateral condyles; Ktrans and Kep were only significantly higher in the tibial plateau. In the tibia, AUC and PE were significantly correlated with the grade of vascular proliferation, and PE also with the degree of marrow fibrosis. There was no significant correlation between AUC/PE and histopathological findings in the femur and no correlation between quantitative DCE parameters and histopathological findings. Conclusion: BML characteristics by semi-quantitative DCE in the form of AUC and PE may be used as parameters for the degree of histopathological vascularization in the bone marrow whereas quantitative DCE data were less conclusive.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Flemming K","Sørensen, Flemming Brandt","Egund, Niels","Boel, Lene Warner Thorup","Holm, Carsten","Jurik, Anne Grethe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745225"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Flemming K"],"keyword":["Bone Marrow","Histopathology","Knee","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Osteoarthritis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bone marrow lesions in knee osteoarthritis assessed by dynamic contrast enhanced mri with histopathological correlations","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85193753577","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745225","identifier":[{"id":"38766869","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85193753577","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bd4b453a-fe3e-40af-85d4-67022faef1c6"],"keyword":["Bone marrow","histopathology","knee","magnetic resonance imaging","osteoarthritis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8AFC3D45EDF862FAF8664206A6D2D419"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Flemming Kromann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8a52bfeb-d0ec-4d2e-b8d1-8e003647cd69","name":"Nielsen, Flemming K","name_org":"Nielsen, Flemming Kromann","orcid":"0000-0002-4187-2791","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming Brandt","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"db856600-d106-4b0a-83f1-d7245f5249bd","name":"Sørensen, Flemming Brandt","orcid":"0000-0002-5446-1035","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"egundpau","last":"Egund","locid":"d6bab428-e7ec-43fb-828a-8c391aa09ebe","name":"Egund, Niels","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Warner","key":"boelpau","last":"Boel","locid":"cf69d33f-562c-489b-9564-9a9dc15c0a16","name":"Boel, Lene Warner Thorup","name_org":"Boel, Lene Warner","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"9e7ae879-3a15-470d-8ad8-3a3402c9162d","name":"Holm, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Grethe","key":"jurikpau","last":"Jurik","locid":"7c41cb37-5d88-416b-afd6-8c4f9d5501a0","name":"Jurik, Anne Grethe","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38766869"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/02841851241251639","issn":["02841851","16000455"],"issn_org":["02841851"],"issue":"7","journal":"Acta Radiologica","pages":"765-773","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"Acta Radiologica","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85193753577"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bd4b453a-fe3e-40af-85d4-67022faef1c6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Bone marrow lesions in knee osteoarthritis assessed by dynamic contrast-enhanced MRI with histopathological correlations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-745225","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper explores how the culture within a Danish university study programme affects students’ aspirations of becoming a high school chemistry teacher. We draw on ethnographic fieldwork and qualitative interviews to describe and analyse the culture of the programme. In the analysis we foreground the case of two students to understand their identity negotiations and changes in their teacher aspirations over time. By combining a ‘domains-of-power framework’ with the concept of ‘science identity’, we show how everyday practices formed a culture of power that positioned research in the centre and teaching as a less attractive career path. By unfolding the subtle mechanisms that together form a culture of power, which works both to include and exclude, we show the ways in which the two student’s aspirations for becoming high school chemistry teachers somewhat diminished over time. The study concludes that negotiating a science identity at a research-intensive university programme, makes it almost impossible to develop and keep an aspiration for becoming a high school teacher. To address the current and future shortage of science teachers across Europe, our findings underline the need for a more inclusive culture at the university to support science students’ diverse aspirations.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Katia Bill","Madsen, Lene Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747430"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"choosing not to be a chemistry teacher students negotiations of science identities at a research intensive university","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-747430","identifier":[{"id":"85150245254","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0d4c2628-68d4-4b72-b58e-aa9e61317025"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6401965A28A5C57D110966129C620A4B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Equity in Science Education","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, University Science Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Katia Bill","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"777255e6-39f6-474e-bda0-17da98814463","name":"Nielsen, Katia Bill","orcid":"0000-0002-7653-8646","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Lene Møller","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"dda148da-5b6d-4f4e-ab60-b7cf85637829","name":"Madsen, Lene Møller","orcid":"0000-0001-7149-9142","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/14749041231157919","issn":["14749041"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Educational Research Journal","pages":"544-460","status":"p","title":"European Educational Research Journal","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150245254"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0d4c2628-68d4-4b72-b58e-aa9e61317025"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Choosing (not) to be a chemistry teacher : Students’ negotiations of science identities at a research-intensive university","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747430","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Despite the importance of citrullination in physiology and disease, global identification of citrullinated proteins, and the precise targeted sites, has remained challenging. Here we employed quantitative-mass-spectrometry-based proteomics to generate a comprehensive atlas of citrullination sites within the HL60 leukemia cell line following differentiation into neutrophil-like cells. We identified 14,056 citrullination sites within 4,008 proteins and quantified their regulation upon inhibition of the citrullinating enzyme PADI4. With this resource, we provide quantitative and site-specific information on thousands of PADI4 substrates, including signature histone marks and transcriptional regulators. Additionally, using peptide microarrays, we demonstrate the potential clinical relevance of certain identified sites, through distinct reactivities of antibodies contained in synovial fluid from anti-CCP-positive and anti-CCP-negative people with rheumatoid arthritis. Collectively, we describe the human citrullinome at a systems-wide level, provide a resource for understanding citrullination at the mechanistic level and link the identified targeted sites to rheumatoid arthritis.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Rebak, Alexandra Stripp","Hendriks, Ivo A.","Elsborg, Jonas D.","Buch-Larsen, Sara C.","Nielsen, Claus H.","Terslev, Lene","Kirsch, Rebecca","Damgaard, Dres","Doncheva, Nadezhda T.","Lennartsson, Caroline L.E.","Rykær, Martin","Jensen, Lars Juhl","Christophorou, Maria A.","Nielsen, Michael L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-748388"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Babraham Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a quantitative and site specific atlas of the citrullinome reveals widespread existence of citrullination and insights into padi000000000004 substrates","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41594-024-01214-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-748388","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11189309","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"001158584200002","type":"wos"},{"id":"85184233102","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38321148","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7724d557-5d6a-4773-8076-914083fb283a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-10856DE0DC87EA8209EE77C6CF2376CB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41594-024-01214-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/397031879/s41594_024_01214_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Nielsen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"babraham institute","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Babraham Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alexandra S.","key":"rebakalexandrastripppau","last":"Rebak","locid":"92555e54-37e3-4fb4-b1c8-167079a27468","name":"Rebak, Alexandra Stripp","name_org":"Rebak, Alexandra S.","orcid":"0000-0001-7176-8605","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ivo A.","key":"hendriksivoapau","last":"Hendriks","locid":"ea030002-bd40-4a15-bdc8-b562d831b71c","name":"Hendriks, Ivo A.","orcid":"0000-0002-1439-3701","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas D.","key":"elsborgjonasdpau","last":"Elsborg","locid":"dbd544fa-a21d-4a87-b5ff-226aa2f424b6","name":"Elsborg, Jonas D.","orcid":"0000-0002-1506-4280","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sara C.","key":"buchlarsensaracpau","last":"Buch-Larsen","locid":"975fd164-f221-4968-a0d4-1e50e7887842","name":"Buch-Larsen, Sara C.","orcid":"0000-0001-6250-5467","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Claus H.","key":"nielsenclaushpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Claus H.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"terslevlenepau","last":"Terslev","name":"Terslev, Lene","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rebecca","key":"kirschrebeccapau","last":"Kirsch","locid":"04e546e5-2eb1-4c64-ab96-294089bd86de","name":"Kirsch, Rebecca","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dres","key":"damgaarddrespau","last":"Damgaard","name":"Damgaard, Dres","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nadezhda T.","key":"donchevanadezhdatpau","last":"Doncheva","locid":"6d6bc236-942a-4aa7-b1ec-c70eabf3c12e","name":"Doncheva, Nadezhda T.","orcid":"0000-0002-8806-6850","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline","key":"lennartssoncarolinelepau","last":"Lennartsson","locid":"10f5fb00-acc5-49cd-872e-16d5b6977207","name":"Lennartsson, Caroline L.E.","name_org":"Lennartsson, Caroline","orcid":"0000-0002-8392-6858","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"rykærmartinpau","last":"Rykær","locid":"151e26ea-3503-4bef-a274-ba7d5c262e78","name":"Rykær, Martin","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars J.","key":"jensenlarsjuhlpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"cae227d4-1222-4c3a-a7b0-34ad91d42e5a","name":"Jensen, Lars Juhl","name_org":"Jensen, Lars J.","orcid":"0000-0001-7885-715X","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Maria A.","key":"christophoroumariaapau","last":"Christophorou","name":"Christophorou, Maria A.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael L.","key":"nielsenmichaellpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b72d98f7-79fa-43a7-8066-783ed8034146","name":"Nielsen, Michael L.","orcid":"0000-0002-0067-9039","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38321148"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41594-024-01214-9","issn":["15459985","15459993"],"issn_org":["15459993"],"issue":"6","journal":"Nature Structural and Molecular Biology","pages":"977-995","status":"p","title":"Nature Structural and Molecular Biology","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184233102"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7724d557-5d6a-4773-8076-914083fb283a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A quantitative and site-specific atlas of the citrullinome reveals widespread existence of citrullination and insights into PADI4 substrates","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-748388","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"γ-Glutamyl peptides are an important class of kokumi compounds that enhance the palatability of food. To investigate the ability of Bacillus species to produce γ-glutamyl peptides, strains of B. subtilis, B. safensis, B. velezensis, B. altitudinis and B. paralicheniformis, were isolated from the fermented seed condiment “Kantong” and cultured in the dark in a conventional medium for 5 days. Quantitation of γ-glutamyl peptides was performed alongside analyses of bacterial growth and γ-glutamyltransferase (GGT) activity. Results showed that all strains could produce a variety of γ-glutamyl peptides. Compared to the other strains, strains of B. subtilis and B. safensis demonstrated greater capacities to generate target γ-glutamyl peptides, achieving maximum concentrations of 2.02 and 1.77 mg/L, respectively. Moreover, no direct correlation between GGT activity and γ-glutamyl peptide concentrations was observed during fermentation, and these two indicators were reported for the first time for B. safensis and B. paralicheniformis. This study provides valuable insights into the generation of γ-glutamyl peptides through Bacillus fermentation, facilitating the development of cost-effective and environmentally friendly approaches for producing kokumi seasonings.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Li, Qian","Zhang, Longteng","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","Jespersen, Lene","Lametsch, Rene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754707"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hainan University"],"keyword":["Bacillus","Glutamyl peptide","Kantong","Kokumi"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the capacity of i bacillus i species for production of kokumi γ glutamyl peptides a comparative study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lwt.2024.116542","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754707","identifier":[{"id":"85200165263","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9db43981-d80d-4800-b665-6745c7679f22"],"keyword":["Bacillus","Kantong","Kokumi","γ-glutamyl peptide","γ-glutamyltransferase (GGT)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C8FAABD27E57E0A7188E98F00E244600"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lwt.2024.116542","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/401978603/1_s2.0_S0023643824008211_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Analytics and Biotechnology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Ingredient and Dairy Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hainan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hainan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Qian","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"9f1a4f0b-a4f6-437c-8b8d-16580bd096df","name":"Li, Qian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Longteng","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"a491e5b8-b0ad-4190-b796-b7c49908664f","name":"Zhang, Longteng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dennis Sandris","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"a156c6e3-9562-4d35-9305-53a39c62e076","name":"Jespersen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-2555-5948","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"René","key":"lametschpau","last":"Lametsch","locid":"70bd350a-6869-4a4a-b9bc-56a756376784","name":"Lametsch, Rene","name_org":"Lametsch, René","orcid":"0000-0002-4189-806X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.lwt.2024.116542","issn":["00236438","10961127"],"issn_org":["00236438"],"journal":"LWT","paperid":"116542","status":"p","title":"LWT","title_org":"LWT - Food Science and Technology","volume":"206"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200165263"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9db43981-d80d-4800-b665-6745c7679f22"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring the capacity of <i>Bacillus </i>species for production of kokumi γ-glutamyl peptides : A comparative study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754707","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Corona-pandemiens afledte samfundsforandringer er emnet for denne rapport, som præsenterer resultater fra de første studier i Vidensporet, der indgår i regi af Realdanias indsats – ’RESPOND - Rammerne for den nye hverdag’. Rapporten bygger på en bred vifte af delstudier, som metodisk strækker sig fra det kvantitative overblik til det kvalitative nærstudie, og som tematisk går på tværs af samfundets væsentligste sfærer og dagsordener. Fokus er på livet i og omkring det byggede miljø.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Christensen, Toke Haunstrup","Bøje-Kovács, Bence János","Stender, Marie","Bech-Danielsen, Claus","Nørgaard, Helle","Jensen, Jesper Ole","Nordberg, Lene Wiell","Lindberg, Malene Rudolf","Mechlenborg, Mette","Javakhishvili-Larsen, Nino","Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","Grangaard, Sidse","Bonderup, Sirid"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-756901"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Byens rum","Corona","Covid 19","Det byggede miljø","Flyttemønstre","Fritidshuse","Hverdagsliv","Hybridarbejde","Institutioner","Naboskab"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pandemiens spor hvordan forandrer corona livet i det byggede miljø","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/740501572/Pandemiens_spor_01.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Forskningen denne rapport bygger på er tilvejebragt gennem videnssporet i den filantropiske forening Realdanias indsats 'RESPOND - rammerne for den nye hverdag'. Videnssporet er støttet af Realdania."],"id":"S01-000.00-756901","ids":["aau-785c6569-89f5-452b-ac17-362d8d080c0c"],"keyword":["Byens rum","Bytæthed","COVID-19","Corona","Det byggede miljø","Flyttemønstre","Fritidshuse","Hverdagsliv","Hybridarbejde","Institutioner","Naboskab"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E6F39A4CA5DD6797718B094C82F49D4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/740501572/Pandemiens_spor_01.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Town, Housing and Property","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Sustainable Cities and Everyday Practice Research Group","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toke Haunstrup","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3dc08a41-cd84-48b7-98ff-414af2fca7e4","name":"Christensen, Toke Haunstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-5473-6369","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bence János","key":"bøjekovácspau","last":"Bøje-Kovács","locid":"d5acba47-f7b4-4156-a5c8-082c75b50311","name":"Bøje-Kovács, Bence János","orcid":"0000-0002-2212-7286","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie","key":"stenderpau","last":"Stender","locid":"a548a5d3-73b7-4461-9ed9-ba9c0432e2ac","name":"Stender, Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-1009-3138","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"bechdanielsenpau","last":"Bech-Danielsen","locid":"f41ac22b-bb0d-4c3f-8d06-96efd65c0665","name":"Bech-Danielsen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-4822-6039","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helle","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"5e589f95-ffe6-4aa4-aaec-80ae719ac5ad","name":"Nørgaard, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-1657-6448","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Ole","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ba9f81ea-c5a0-4b37-a1ef-bcf1bc98535e","name":"Jensen, Jesper Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3730-0619","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Wiell","key":"nordbergpau","last":"Nordberg","locid":"4620ca55-6074-4b3d-98ed-0321710187b8","name":"Nordberg, Lene Wiell","orcid":"0000-0003-3344-0574","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene Rudolf","key":"lindbergpau","last":"Lindberg","locid":"5ae8eb7a-4f19-47c4-8601-df8924ebb4d8","name":"Lindberg, Malene Rudolf","orcid":"0000-0003-4148-5270","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"mechlenborgpau","last":"Mechlenborg","locid":"429feb0f-1899-4126-bba7-9ae96ec42ce2","name":"Mechlenborg, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-9446-9795","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nino","key":"javakhishvililarsenpau","last":"Javakhishvili-Larsen","locid":"b1e9bba1-55b1-454e-af85-da4592735cbe","name":"Javakhishvili-Larsen, Nino","orcid":"0000-0002-0357-5438","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Skovgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"125da2cb-a5a5-47e8-84ab-be518f10a19f","name":"Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0308-1275","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sidse","key":"grangaardpau","last":"Grangaard","locid":"c4f2ca7d-28eb-409c-8c7f-994af261017f","name":"Grangaard, Sidse","orcid":"0000-0003-3814-6614","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sirid","key":"bonderuppau","last":"Bonderup","locid":"cfb26409-31b1-4e61-aff5-0ffa45a04baa","name":"Bonderup, Sirid","orcid":"0000-0003-0095-1239","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["25973118"],"issue":"05","pages":"128","publisher":"Institut for Byggeri, By og Miljø (BUILD), Aalborg Universitet","repno":"BUILD Rapport, No. 05","series":"BUILD Rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-785c6569-89f5-452b-ac17-362d8d080c0c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Pandemiens spor : Hvordan forandrer corona livet i det byggede miljø","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-756901","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: Epidemiological studies have shown that subnormal levels of vitamin D (25(OH)D) are associated with a more aggravated clinical course of ulcerative colitis (UC). Despite an increased focus on the therapeutic importance of vitamin D and vitamin D receptor (VDR) signaling, the mechanisms underlying the effects of the vitamin D-VDR axis on UC remain elusive. Therefore, we aimed to investigate whether exposure to active vitamin D (1,25(OH)2D3)/VDR signaling in human organoids could influence the maintenance of the colonic epithelium. METHODS: Intestinal VDR expression was studied by immunohistochemistry, RNA expression arrays, and single-cell RNA sequencing of colonic biopsy specimens obtained from patients with UC and healthy individuals. To characterize the functional and transcriptional effects of 1,25(OH)2D3, we used patient-derived colonic organoids. The dependency of VDR was assessed by knocking out the receptor with CRISPR/Cas9. RESULTS: Our results suggest that 1,25(OH)2D3/VDR stimulation supports differentiation of the colonic epithelium and that impaired 1,25(OH)2D3/VDR signaling thereby may compromise the structure of the intestinal epithelial barrier, leading to flares of UC. Furthermore, a transcriptional response to VDR activity was observed primarily in fully differentiated cells at the top of the colonic crypt, and this response was reduced during flares of UC. CONCLUSIONS: We identified an important role of vitamin D signaling in supporting differentiated cell states in the human colonic epithelium, and thereby maintenance of the intestinal barrier integrity. This makes the vitamin D-VDR signaling axis an interesting target for therapeutic efforts to achieve and maintain remission in patients with UC.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Kellermann, Lauge","Hansen, Stine Lind","Maciag, Grzegorz","Granau, Agnete Marie","Johansen, Jens Vilstrup","Teves, Joji Marie","Bressan, Raul Bardini","Pedersen, Marianne Terndrup","Soendergaard, Christoffer","Baattrup, Astrid Moeller","Hammerhøj, Alexander","Riis, Lene Buhl","Gubatan, John","Jensen, Kim B","Nielsen, Ole Haagen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-778068"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of vitamin d receptor signalling and vitamin d on colonic epithelial cell fate decisions in ulcerative colitis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ecco-jcc/jjae074","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-778068","identifier":[{"id":"85206598134","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38747639","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11479711","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-73980cc5-81d7-4680-bc9b-2a260504914d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4113409CC6FF53CD6C4520CC58AFA774"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ecco-jcc/jjae074","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/410619300/jjae074.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lauge","key":"kellermannpau","last":"Kellermann","locid":"a33860c6-fe67-4e05-a3f3-bacb7bb5f022","name":"Kellermann, Lauge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stine Lind","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"98c79993-ac0e-4622-909d-234a2d431c6a","name":"Hansen, Stine Lind","orcid":"0000-0002-5967-286X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Grzegorz","key":"maciagpau","last":"Maciag","locid":"eb43581f-dafd-4099-becc-b9ff8a77c118","name":"Maciag, Grzegorz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Agnete Marie","key":"granaupau","last":"Granau","locid":"619282bf-857b-4a00-9578-92a245edb07e","name":"Granau, Agnete Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Vilstrup","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"39f6546d-6757-452a-8db1-2a76fee02e7d","name":"Johansen, Jens Vilstrup","orcid":"0000-0001-7094-6801","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joji Marie","key":"tevespau","last":"Teves","locid":"c468ca70-acd6-4863-9be2-9f36a0d34adb","name":"Teves, Joji Marie","orcid":"0000-0001-9289-2357","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Raul Bardini","key":"bressanpau","last":"Bressan","locid":"a7f187db-60db-4a5d-8e22-a516043d50bc","name":"Bressan, Raul Bardini","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne Terndrup","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"adadc836-6264-4601-a544-31d54ea2ad13","name":"Pedersen, Mar