 of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-75f3010e-e457-48c9-a24d-880db297ca46","ku-6e8965fc-7745-4107-afaa-611b07c7b920","sdu-0fe20f1c-2c9e-4bc0-b6f1-6998afb73a06"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Mosaic chromosomal alterations in hematopoietic cells and clinical outcomes in patients with multiple myeloma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-793309","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To compare tolerability and effectiveness of two different classes of biological Disease-Modifying Anti-Rheumatic Drugs (bDMARDs; interleukin (IL)-17- and IL-23(p19) inhibitors) relative to tumour necrosis factor inhibitors (TNFi) regarding the drug survival rates and treatment outcomes in patients with psoriatic arthritis (PsA). METHODS: We emulated a target trial on comparative effectiveness using observational data from a prospective cohort study based on the Parker Institute's PsA cohort - the PIPA cohort. All patients underwent interview and clinical examination programme at baseline and at follow-up visits at four and twelve months. The primary endpoint, drug survival, was assessed up to 12 months from baseline. We estimated hazard ratios from proportional hazards model and used propensity score adjustment in an attempt to deconfound and emulate a random treatment assignment. RESULTS: We included a total of 109 patients in the intention-to-monitor population at baseline initiating either TNFi (75 patients), IL17i (26 patients), or IL23(19)i (8 patients). Hazard ratios in the propensity adjusted model comparing IL-17i and IL-23(p19)i to TNFi were 1.36 (95% CI 0.59-3.14) and 0.56 (95% CI 0.10-3.24), respectively. TNFi and IL-17i had comparable effects regarding response rates and changes in clinical outcomes after 12 months, whereas IL-23(p19)i tended to perform better overall. CONCLUSION: No decisive differences between drugs were observed at group level regarding drug survival and clinical outcomes after 12 months. TNFi, IL-17i, and IL-23(p19)i may all be considered equally effective in the treatment of patients with PsA, advocating for investigating more in personalised treatment strategies.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Stisen, Zara R.","Nielsen, Sabrina M.","Skougaard, Marie","Mogensen, Mette","Jørgensen, Tanja Schjødt","Dreyer, Lene","de Wit, Maarten","Christensen, Robin","Kristensen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S04-092.50-741517"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stisen, Zara R."],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stichting Tools Patient Research Partner"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Antirheumatic Agents therapeutic use","Arthritis Psoriatic drug therapy","Biological Therapy","Drug survival","Female","Humans","Interleukin 17 antagonists inhibitors","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Psoriatic arthritis","Treatment Outcome","Tumor Necrosis Factor Inhibitors therapeutic use","Tumor Necrosis Factor alpha antagonists inhibitors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Ukendt"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tolerability and comparative effectiveness of tnf il 000000000017 and il 000000000023 p000000000019 inhibitors in psoriatic arthritis a target trial emulation study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/550215337/Stisen_et_al._2023_._Tolerability_and_comparative_effectiveness_of_TNF-_IL-17-_and_IL-23_p19_inhibitors_in_psoriatic_arthritis_-_A_target_trial_emulation_study.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by The Danish Rheumatism Association (R197-A7060), Danish Psoriasis Association and Minister Erna Hamiltons Legat for videnskab og kunst. The Parker Institute, Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospital is supported by a core grant from the Oak Foundation (OCAY-18-774-OFIL). None of the funders was involved in the process of collecting, analysing, interpreting or presenting the data."],"id":"S04-092.50-741517","identifier":[{"id":"85195060817","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37713434","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-b7a0fce0-939e-4684-b77e-3a11e003c9c7","au-acdfa6c5-be8b-46b4-82f4-9644cbd34dd0","ku-360933aa-45ea-4bc2-8f78-ae534588a6fa","sdu-e28699f9-c094-436f-bacb-3bd6052950e3"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Antirheumatic Agents/therapeutic use","Arthritis, Psoriatic/drug therapy","Female","Humans","Interleukin-17/antagonists & inhibitors","Interleukin-23 Subunit p19/antagonists & inhibitors","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Treatment Outcome","Tumor Necrosis Factor Inhibitors/therapeutic use","Tumor Necrosis Factor-alpha/antagonists & inhibitors","biological therapy","drug survival","psoriatic arthritis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-61CEA741825D54753B5DC5CBF66C296A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/550215337/Stisen_et_al._2023_._Tolerability_and_comparative_effectiveness_of_TNF-_IL-17-_and_IL-23_p19_inhibitors_in_psoriatic_arthritis_-_A_target_trial_emulation_study.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Bispebjerg og Frederiksberg Universitets Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university o