":"0000-0001-8901-7850","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38801970"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijid.2024.107111","issn":["12019712","18783511"],"issn_org":["12019712"],"journal":"International Journal of Infectious Diseases","paperid":"107111","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Infectious Diseases","volume":"146"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196316682"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ebb35e57-082c-48bf-a97d-04202c86af1f","au-3c5c57c1-7a5f-45db-be00-cb9344b49615","ku-17a3fa9e-b2a8-416f-a762-fa10ee30e24c","sdu-8dd92032-b7a8-4e7b-b8ab-5ffe6e27950d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Development of antibody levels and subsequent decline in individuals with vaccine induced and hybrid immunity to SARS-CoV-2","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.89-741595","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The DANIsh VASculitis cohort study, DANIVAS, is an observational national multicenter study with the overall aim to prospectively collect protocolized clinical data and biobank material from patients with polymyalgia rheumatica (PMR) and giant cell arteritis (GCA) diagnosed and/or followed at Danish rheumatology departments. A long-term key objective is to investigate whether the use of new clinically implemented diagnostic imaging modalities facilitates disease stratification in the GCA-PMR disease spectrum. In particular, we aim to evaluate treatment requirements in GCA patients with and without large-vessel involvement, treatment needs in PMR patients with and without subclinical giant cell arteritis, and the prognostic role of imaging with respect to aneurysm development. Hence, in GCA and PMR, imaging stratification is hypothesized to be able to guide management strategies. With an established infrastructure within rheumatology for clinical studies in Denmark, the infrastructure of the Danish Rheumatologic Biobank, and the possibility to cross-link data with valid nationwide registries, the DANIVAS project holds an exceptional possibility to collect comprehensive real-world data on diagnosis, disease severity, disease duration, treatment effect, complications, and adverse events. In this paper, we present the research protocol for the DANIVAS study. Clinical trial registration: https://clinicaltrials.gov/, identifier NCT05935709.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Nielsen, Berit D.","Kristensen, Salome","Donskov, Agnete","Terslev, Lene","Dreyer, Lene Wohlfahrt","Colic, Ada","Hetland, Merete Lund","Højgaard, Pil","Ellingsen, Torkell","Hauge, Ellen Margrethe","Chrysidis, Stavros","Keller, Kresten K."],"cuid":["S04-100.00-766938"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Berit D."],"keyword":["Giant cell arteritis","Imaging","Polymyalgia rheumatica","Prognosis","Prospective observational study","cohort study or longitudinal study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish vasculitis cohort study protocol for a national multicenter prospective study including incident and prevalent patients with giant cell arteritis and polymyalgia rheumatica","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmed.2024.1415076","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The author(s) declare that financial support was received for the research, authorship, and/or publication of this article. The study has received grants for the establishment and implementation of the database from AbbVie (Agr-2021-731-16898) and The Danish Rheumatism Association (R214-A8127). The funders were not involved in the study design, data collection or analysis plan, the writing of this article, or the decision to submit it for publication."],"id":"S04-100.00-766938","identifier":[{"id":"39026552","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11256208","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85198637447","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a83a3962-bacd-4a91-be0d-01243fe00847","au-7a886af5-5bd0-4531-ab77-bb73c1ea62a4","ku-ef8aa0ed-f357-48a1-a549-e3c5f0a21772","sdu-f40e25f4-71d7-409d-8d48-62a1731cbeee"],"keyword":["cohort study (or longitudinal study)","giant cell arteritis","imaging","polymyalgia rheumatica","prognosis","prospective observational study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-33BC3CC488D4684D8292DD9