{"abstract":"Almene boliger var tiltænkt samfundets mest udsatte. Men en række politiske indgreb har gjort det langt sværere for udsatte at få adgang til dem.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","Andersen, Hans Thor","Nordberg, Lene Wiell"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-736324"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Almene boliger","Social ulighed","Udsatte borgere"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forskere politik i den almene boligsektor har øget den sociale ulighed","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.altinget.dk/by/artikel/forskere-boligen-er-derfra-vores-verden-gaar-derfor-er-det-problematisk-at-politik-i-den-almene-boligsektor-har-oeget-den-sociale-ulighed?toke=325caca1f98147648c8f8f417c00007a","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-736324","ids":["aau-c276ec72-461e-47d0-be3d-b67514ada37a"],"keyword":["Almene boliger","Social ulighed","Udsatte borgere"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FF23F987BE813D8A69AD4B4A7BEF91C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.altinget.dk/by/artikel/forskere-boligen-er-derfra-vores-verden-gaar-derfor-er-det-problematisk-at-politik-i-den-almene-boligsektor-har-oeget-den-sociale-ulighed?toke=325caca1f98147648c8f8f417c00007a","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Town, Housing and Property","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Transformation of Housing and Places Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Skovgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"125da2cb-a5a5-47e8-84ab-be518f10a19f","name":"Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0308-1275","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Thor","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3e5ea6c9-85ba-4f6f-a9ce-59d5383c7db3","name":"Andersen, Hans Thor","orcid":"0000-0002-0684-4701","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Wiell","key":"nordbergpau","last":"Nordberg","locid":"4620ca55-6074-4b3d-98ed-0321710187b8","name":"Nordberg, Lene Wiell","orcid":"0000-0003-3344-0574","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"newspaper":"Altinget - By og Bolig","status":"p","title":"Altinget - By og Bolig"},"review":"Undetermined","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","11. Sustainable Cities and Production","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c276ec72-461e-47d0-be3d-b67514ada37a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Forskere : Politik i den almene boligsektor har øget den sociale ulighed","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-736324","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Holistic rehabilitation approaches addressing the numerous complex challenges in young persons with acquired brain injury are required. The purpose of this study was to describe and evaluate the holistic person-centered youth mentoring intervention program, which is based on occupational therapy. Methods: Prospectively collected data were extracted from a national clinical quality database (n = 59). Proportions of young persons receiving different aspects of support and proportions rating the intervention as meaningful were calculated. One-year changes in occupation, work ability, and social interactions were calculated. Results: The young persons most frequently received support for energy management (75%) and structuring of everyday life (61%). Seventy-three percent rated the intervention as meaningful. One year post-inclusion, occupation and work ability had increased by 35% and 58%, respectively, and it had declined by 10% and 26%, respectively. The 1-year increase and decrease in social interactions were less clear (15% and 25%, respectively). One-year changes did not differ between those who entered the program early or late after injury indicating the potential beneficial effect of the program. Conclusion: The findings could indicate that the program has a unique value in supporting young persons with acquired brain injury to create a meaningful everyday life through occupation, work ability, and social interaction.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Odgaard, Lene","Bystrup, Mette Ryssel","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Stabel, Henriette Holm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-737237"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Odgaard, Lene"],"keyword":["Acquired brain injury","Mentoring","Occupational Therapy","Return to work","Social relations","holistic rehabilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"youth mentoring a new holistic intervention targeting the needs of young persons with acquired brain injury","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85189040018","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-737237","identifier":[{"id":"40336718","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85189040018","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12033871","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-70182b5d-8243-421b-b046-c9bfeb2c4fe2"],"keyword":["Acquired brain injury","holistic rehabilitation","mentoring","occupational therapy","return to work","social relations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7E1DACD7A730586ADB326644460D9C91"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hammel Neurocenter, Universitetsklinik for Neurorehabilitering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"1b80fe7b-ba0a-45b3-aca1-48bc19a97a44","name":"Odgaard, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-9830-3282","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Ryssel","key":"bystruppau","last":"Bystrup","locid":"16ff1725-138f-4fa9-a244-4e602a67eb94","name":"Bystrup, Mette Ryssel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Feldbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henriette Holm","key":"stabelpau","last":"Stabel","locid":"95dbd7bb-fcde-4b0c-9bdf-c6dc2bbf7bb4","name":"Stabel, Henriette Holm","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40336718"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/03080226241241991","issn":["03080226","14776006"],"issn_org":["03080226"],"issue":"7","journal":"British Journal of Occupational Therapy","pages":"398-406","publisher":"SAGE Publications Inc.","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Occupational Therapy","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189040018"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-70182b5d-8243-421b-b046-c9bfeb2c4fe2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Youth mentoring : A new holistic intervention targeting the needs of young persons with acquired brain injury","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-737237","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To examine whether patient involvement using a Patient Decision Aid has a positive effect on pain levels, by giving them an active role in choosing a pain schedule for postoperative pain assessment and pain management. Design: A nonmatched case-control study. Methods: 101 adults 18 years or older were included to choose between 1 of 3 possible schedules for postoperative pain management. Perioperative variables, for example, patients’ assessments of pain were registered at the hospital and further variables after discharge at postoperative day 1 (POD1), POD3, and POD7, for example, patients’ ability to sleep and assessment of nausea. Findings: Less pain after discharge was seen among patients choosing pain schedule II at POD1 (P = .0439). A significantly higher consumption of opioids (P = 0010) on POD1 in patients who have chosen pain schedule II. Conclusions: Improved patient involvement by choosing a user-controlled pain schedule (pain schedule II) in postoperative pain management increased patient empowerment.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Olsen, Susanne Winther","Lehmkuhl, Lene","Hamborg, Lone W.","Torkov, Anne Karina A.","Fog-Nielsen, Rie","Lauridsen, Jørgen Trankjær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-740670"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Olsen, Susanne Winther"],"keyword":["Adult","Analgesics Opioid therapeutic use","Case Control Studies","Cholecystectomy Laparoscopic","Humans","Laparoscopic cholecystectomy","Laparoscopy","Pain","Pain Management","Pain Postoperative drug therapy","Pain assessment","Patient decision aid","Perioperative","Postoperative","Shared decision making"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"postoperative pain relief after ambulatory laparoscopic surgery a nonmatched case control study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jopan.2023.08.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-740670","identifier":[{"id":"37999689","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85179102900","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-7a17a706-2812-4090-92ed-6ec465b693ed"],"keyword":["Adult","Analgesics, Opioid/therapeutic use","Case-Control Studies","Cholecystectomy, Laparoscopic","Humans","Laparoscopy","Pain Management","Pain, Postoperative/drug therapy","laparoscopic cholecystectomy","pain","pain assessment","patient decision aid","perioperative","postoperative","shared decision-making"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A95FEB5AD2DA9CD72C149084E7606115"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jopan.2023.08.002","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/259372783/1-s2.0-S108994722300919X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne W.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"71a92f4b-306a-4347-9ea6-e02f9f5003f6","name":"Olsen, Susanne Winther","name_org":"Olsen, Susanne W.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"lehmkuhlpau","last":"Lehmkuhl","locid":"2452a119-9a90-487a-8665-a5a