urnal of Rare Diseases","paperid":"284","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Orphanet Journal of Rare Diseases","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200050588"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bc12a0af-2898-42f1-bd92-a619f2c19806","au-91e45ff7-ac1c-4797-b074-407769615372","ku-e5b8486f-dd04-4293-b400-ee840bc5cc2f","sdu-a3985b47-bbe2-4685-89ae-4a2a573ec0a3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"DAHEAN : A Danish nationwide study ensuring quality assurance through real-world data for suspected hereditary anemia patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-755897","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Chronic pain is the hallmark symptom of joint diseases. This study examined the differences in quantitative sensory testing between patients with psoriatic arthritis (PsA), hand osteoarthritis (hand-OA) and a pain-free control group and differences between patients with and without concomitant fibromyalgia (cFM). Methods: All patients and pain-free controls were assessed using pressure pain thresholds (PPT), temporal summation of pain (TSP), conditioned pain modulation (CPM) and clinical pain intensities. Psychological distress was assessed with the Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale, Pain Catastrophizing Scale, and Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index. Disability was assessed with the Health Assessment Questionnaire and pain quality with the painDETECT questionnaire. cFM was identified using the revised 2016 American College of Rheumatology diagnostic criteria. Results: Patients with hand-OA (n = 75) or PsA (n = 58) had statistically significant lower PPTs and CPM, greater TSP, and higher scores of psychological distress (p < 0.05) than controls (n = 20). Patients with cFM (58%) had higher scores of depression (p = 0.001), anxiety (p = 0.004), catastrophizing (p = 0.012), disability (p < 0.001), higher painDETECT score (p = 0.001), TSP (p = 0.027), and reduced sleep quality (p = 0.021) when compared to patients without cFM. Conclusion: Patients with hand-OA and PsA exhibited signs of pain sensitization and a higher degree of psychological distress and disability than pain-free individuals. Patients with cFM had greater TSP, painDETECT score, disability, catastrophizing, and reduced sleep quality, than patients without, indicating greater degree of pain sensitization, psychological burden, and disability. Statement of significance: This paper shows that a significant proportion of patients with hand osteoarthritis and psoriatic arthritis with moderate pain intensity have significantly increased signs of pain sensitization and markers of psychological distress. A large proportion of these patients fulfil the criteria for concomitant fibromyalgia and these patients show even greater propensity towards pain sensitization and psychological distress.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Vela, Jonathan","Dreyer, Lene","Petersen, Kristian Kjær","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Duch, Kirsten","Amris, K.","Kristensen, Salome"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-687280"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Vela, Jonathan"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantitative sensory testing psychological profiles and clinical pain in patients with psoriatic arthritis and hand osteoarthritis experiencing pain of at least moderate intensity","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejp.2183","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-687280","identifier":[{"id":"85171144962","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f9f8cd7e-d2a0-4945-a5cb-cd7db629e52c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CC304F088A6F9B341DED3112AA688808"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejp.2183","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/649358037/Vela_et_al._2024_._Quantitative_sensory_testing_psychological_profiles_and_clinical_pain_in_patients_with_psoriatic_arthritis_and_hand_osteoarthritis_experiencing_pain_of_at_least_moderate_intensity.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Rheumatology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"velapau","last":"Vela","locid":"d37a71fc-d46e-4ea6-b522-4b4f649c44d7","name":"Vela, Jonathan","name_org":"Vela, J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.","key":"dreyerpau","last":"Dreyer","locid":"b12f9d3c-1fa5-4513-8002-c9fd87d60d53","name":"Dreyer, Lene","name_org":"Dreyer, L.","orcid":"0000-0002-5156-2922","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K. K.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"03b38a92-c53c-4b31-a786-05e4893a3e14","name":"Petersen, Kristian Kjær","name_org":"Petersen, K. K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-000X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","name_org":"Arendt-Nielsen, L.","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K. Skjærbæk","key":"duchpau","last":"Duch","locid":"952b4bf9-4968-4e9f-8f30-204e8c36d539","name":"Duch, Kirsten","name_org":"Duch, K. Skjærbæk","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"amrispau","last":"Amris","name":"Amris, K.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"9b80939c-06cf-4c5f-8a04-3107ac4426db","name":"Kristensen, Salome","name_org":"Kristensen, S.","orcid":"0000-0001-5812-5234","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ejp.2183","issn":["10903801","15322149"],"issn_org":["10903801"],"issue":"2","journal":"European Journal of Pain","pages":"310-321","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pain","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171144962"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f9f8cd7e-d2a0-4945-a5cb-cd7db629e52c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Quantitative sensory testing, psychological profiles and clinical pain in patients with psoriatic arthritis and hand osteoarthritis experiencing pain of at least moderate intensity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-687280","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To estimate the prevalence of convergence insufficiency (CI) in adult patients with post-concussion syndrome and determine the impact of CI on symptom load. METHODS: Cross-sectional study of 103 patients with neurological symptoms 2-6 months after a concussion. Symptoms were assessed with the Rivermead Post Concussion Symptoms Questionnaire (RPQ), and CI was diagnosed using near point of convergence, vergence facility, and the Convergence Insufficiency Symptom Survey. The RPQ score for patients with and without CI was compared, and sensitivity, specificity, and area under the receiver operating characteristic curve for the two visually related RPQ questions as indicators of CI were calculated. RESULTS: The proportion of patients diagnosed with symptomatic CI was 20.4% (95% confidence interval: 13.1-29.5%). The RPQ score was significantly higher for patients with symptomatic CI both before (p = .01) and after removal of the two visually related questions in the RPQ-questionnaire (p = .03). The two visually related RPQ questions were unable to detect CI. CONCLUSION: In patients with post-concussion syndrome, the load of nonvisual symptoms is higher in the presence of CI. A prospective interventional study on CI is required to study the relationship between CI and other post-concussion symptoms.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nisted, Ivan","Hellemose, Line Amalie Aarestrup","Eggertsen, Peter Preben","Odgaard, Lene","Bek, Toke","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-727633"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nisted, Ivan"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Brain concussion","Convergence insufficiency","Cross Sectional Studies","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Post Concussion Syndrome diagnosis","Post concussion symptoms","Prevalence","Surveys and Questionnaires","Young Adult","mTBI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"convergence insufficiency in patients with post concussion syndrome is accompanied by a higher symptom load a cross sectional study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02699052.2024.2334355","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-727633","identifier":[{"id":"38530005","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85189504662","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-714574e8-907e-4d5b-99b9-6298f7dfba72"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Cross-Sectional Studies","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Ocular Motility Disorders/etiology","Post-Concussion Syndrome/diagnosis","Post-concussion symptoms","Prevalence","Surveys and Questionnaires","Young Adult","brain concussion","convergence insufficiency","mTBI","oculomotor disturbance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3087D80CA4624AB9327AAF6194BEDCB2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02699052.2024.2334355","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivan","key":"nistedpau","last":"Nisted","locid":"4807a102-3f84-4a9c-865c-a8a4f432ba4b","name":"Nisted, Ivan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Amalie","key":"hellemosepau","last":"Hellemose","locid":"afe072ab-8f00-447c-81ee-80312fe86f2a","name":"Hellemose, Line Amalie Aarestrup","name_org":"Hellemose, Line Amalie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Preben","key":"eggertsenpau","last":"Eggertsen","locid":"f57dbf45-6d72-4081-86e0-d07ba83d89a2","name":"Eggertsen, Peter Preben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"1b80fe7b-ba0a-45b3-aca1-48bc19a97a44","name":"Odgaard, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-9830-3282","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toke","key":"bekpau","last":"Bek","locid":"ffc6d181-f10a-40f1-9446-0a5680b91ab8","name":"Bek, Toke","orcid":"0000-0002-0409-2534","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Feldbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38530005"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/02699052.2024.2334355","issn":["02699052","1362301X"],"issn_org":["02699052"],"issue":"8","journal":"Brain Injury","pages":"645-651","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Brain Injury","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189504662"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-714574e8-907e-4d5b-99b9-6298f7dfba72"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Convergence insufficiency in patients with post-concussion syndrome is accompanied by a higher symptom load : a cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-727633","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Numerous pathogenic processes are mediated by short noncoding RNAs (sncRNA). Twenty percent of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) patients are labelled as IBD unclassified (IBDU) at disease onset. Most IBDU patients are reclassified as Crohn’s disease (CD) or ulcerative colitis (UC) within few years. Since the therapeutic methods for CD and UC differ, biomarkers that can forecast the categorization of IBDU into CD or UC are highly desired. Here, we investigated whether sncRNAs can predict CD or UC among IBDU patients. 35 IBDU patients who were initially diagnosed with IBDU were included in this retrospective investigation; of them, 12, 15, and 8 were reclassified into CD (IBDU-CD), UC (IBDU-UC), or remained as IBDU (IBDU-IBDU), respectively. Eight IBD patients, were included as references. SncRNA profiling on RNA from mucosal biopsies were performed using Affymetrix miRNA 4.0 array. Selected probe sets were validated using RT-qPCR. Among all patients and only adults, 306 and 499 probe sets respectively were differentially expressed between IBDU-CD and IBDU-UC. Six of the probe sets were evaluated by RT-qPCR, of which miR-182-5p, miR-451a and ENSG00000239080 (snoU13) together with age and sex resulted in an AUC of 78.6% (95% CI: 60–97) in discriminating IBDU-CD from IBDU-UC. Based on the three sncRNAs profile it is possible to predict if IBDU patients within 3 years will be reclassified as CD or UC. We showed that the expression profile of IBDU patients differ from that of definite CD or UC, suggesting that a subgroup of IBDU patients may compose a third unique IBD subtype.","author_count":7,"contributors":["James, Jaslin P.","Riis, Lene Buhl","Søkilde, Rolf","Malham, Mikkel","Høgdall, Estrid","Langholz, Ebbe","Nielsen, Boye Schnack"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731675"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-BION"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-BION","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short noncoding rnas as predictive biomarkers for the development from inflammatory bowel disease unclassified to crohn s disease or ulcerative colitis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0297353","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-731675","identifier":[{"id":"38408066","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85186076716","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10896517","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"001196528400021","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-834e743d-6a7b-4358-90f8-009308582e06"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-67A0C9F857D21D7C3BB8F5A24DE1A5DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0297353","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385009695/journal.pone.0297353.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"bioneer","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-BION","l3nn":"Bioneer","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Bioneer","namevar":["Bioneer"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-BION","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jaslin P.","key":"jamespau","last":"James","name":"James, Jaslin P.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lene Buhl","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rolf","key":"søkildepau","last":"Søkilde","name":"Søkilde, Rolf","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"malhampau","last":"Malham","name":"Malham, Mikkel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Estrid","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","locid":"a48f77b8-ee6d-4a52-a3f3-deb515bdd48f","name":"Høgdall, Estrid","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ebbe","key":"langholzpau","last":"Langholz","locid":"c3ab9fb7-1eed-4843-bc2b-9a97abe090c4","name":"Langholz, Ebbe","orcid":"0000-0002-8558-8442","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Boye Schnack","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Boye Schnack","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38408066"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0297353","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"2 February","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0297353","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"PLoS ONE","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186076716"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-834e743d-6a7b-4358-90f8-009308582e06"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Short noncoding RNAs as predictive biomarkers for the development from inflammatory bowel disease unclassified to Crohn’s disease or ulcerative colitis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731675","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Aims: The World Health Organization states that physical inactivity is one of the leading behavioural risk factors for disability and mortality in Europe. Social prescribing holds promise as a possible solution by connecting patients from general practice to community-based physical activity. Although research within social prescribing exists, the process of connecting general practice patients to community-based physical activity is not well investigated. This scoping review aimed to summarise and synthesise knowledge on social prescribing provided by health professionals in general practice towards community-based physical activity. Methods: A systematic search for literature in PubMed, Embase, Scopus, SportsDiscus and other sources was conducted to identify initiatives connecting general practice to community-based physical activity. Semi-structured interviews were then conducted with subject-specific national experts. Finally, preliminary findings from the literature and the interviews were used in a co-creation process with experts to synthesise and finalise the results of a thematic analysis across data sources. Results: Based on 19 records, five expert interviews and subsequent co-creation, we identified three themes: (a) barriers and facilitators, (b) organisational perspectives and (c) value-based considerations. Conclusions: This review illuminates the complex nature of social prescribing programmes that connect general practice patients to community-based physical activity in Denmark. It also presents practical and fundamental considerations when applying social prescribing across different settings.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Lene Gissel","Nielsen, Rasmus Oestergaard","Hawkins, Jemma","Kallestrup, Per","Midtgaard, Julie","Ryom, Knud"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-774128"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ryom, Knud"],"keyword":["Co creation","Exercise","Health promotion","Health services research","Interview","Primary Health Care","Referral and Consultation","Review","Social prescribing","community referral"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"social prescribing initiatives connecting general practice patients with community based physical activity a scoping review with expert interviews","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85211218011","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-774128","identifier":[{"id":"39643946","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85211218011","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-fc9d88c4-825b-4a72-a2cd-3611e2788dcf"],"keyword":["Health promotion","co-creation","community referral","exercise","health services research","interview","primary health care","referral and consultation","review","social prescribing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7CCA1600290A8BAAC205833C42443B9B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Gissel","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"09dbbcf4-a99a-4d25-a01c-800a7b767113","name":"Rasmussen, Lene Gissel","orcid":"0000-0002-7828-5697","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"R.O.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2d1ea8cb-28f5-48df-baa8-9724c2e17005","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus Oestergaard","name_org":"Nielsen, R.O.","orcid":"0000-0001-5757-1806","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jemma","key":"hawkinspau","last":"Hawkins","name":"Hawkins, Jemma","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"kallestruppau","last":"Kallestrup","locid":"edc492e6-b4ed-4c50-8948-986e774b6f70","name":"Kallestrup, Per","orcid":"0000-0001-6041-4510","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie","key":"midtgaardpau","last":"Midtgaard","name":"Midtgaard, Julie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud","key":"ryompau","last":"Ryom","locid":"6294b7a6-a4e0-418b-9d18-5d000ab81d14","name":"Ryom, Knud","orcid":"0000-0001-5947-3038","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39643946"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/14034948241299878","issn":["14034948","16511905"],"issn_org":["14034948"],"journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Public Health","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"e","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Public Health"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211218011"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["au-fc9d88c4-825b-4a72-a2cd-3611e2788dcf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Social prescribing initiatives connecting general practice patients with community-based physical activity : A scoping review with expert interviews","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-774128","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This paper is the result of discussions and reflections following the INTERACT 2023 Workshop on HCI for Digital Democracy and Citizen Participation organised by Working Group 13.8 on Interaction Design for International Development. The workshop covered diverse case studies, experiences in this area including examples of decision-making in cooperatives, municipal budgeting, policy making, and citizen driven innovation. In this article we highlight the need for interdisciplinary collaboration uniting researchers, citizens, platform developers and policy makers with the goal of crafting a sociotechnical design and evaluation framework for platforms for Digital Democracy and Citizen Participation. So far there have been very few efforts at truly interdisciplinary evaluations and comparisons of such platforms. These efforts require a focus on the process and product of the design of such platforms to identify and assess the sociotechnical gaps between democratic requirements and digital affordances. To do this effectively we need to address questions such as how to identify and assess the nature and type of citizen participation in the process of design of these platforms? What are the best digital tools and methods to support communication, community formation and deliberation in democratic processes? How can different approaches towards systems design promote democratic participation, especially including underrepresented groups, helping bridge the digital divide in DPP? How should the design process be led by democratic requirements and not by technology affordances? The paper presents how these questions can be addressed in the context of a sociotechnical design process inspired by design thinking.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Abdelnour-Nocera, José L.","Gutiérrez, Juan José Gómez","Alvarez, Maria Estela Peralta","Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776406"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Seville","University of West London"],"keyword":["Citizen participation","Democracy","Digital platforms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a sociotechnical design and evaluation framework for digital democracy and citizen participation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776406","identifier":[{"id":"85200677008","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-65db9ec9-5687-40e2-80c4-a72f001e4b39"],"keyword":["Citizen participation","Democracy","Digital Platforms","Sociatechnical"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7F42C9E5C234A3593A3560D9FF0FA570"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of west london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of West London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"university of seville","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Seville","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"José L.","key":"abdelnournocerapau","last":"Abdelnour-Nocera","name":"Abdelnour-Nocera, José L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan José Gómez","key":"gutiérrezpau","last":"Gutiérrez","name":"Gutiérrez, Juan José Gómez","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Estela Peralta","key":"alvarezpau","last":"Alvarez","name":"Alvarez, Maria Estela Peralta","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_1","issn":["03029743"],"pages":"3-12","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Design for Equality and Justice","volume":"14536"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200677008"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-65db9ec9-5687-40e2-80c4-a72f001e4b39"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Sociotechnical Design and Evaluation Framework for Digital Democracy and Citizen Participation.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776406","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Understanding the patient perspective is a significant part of the deprescribing process. This study aimed to explore the attitudes of older patients with psychiatric disorders towards deprescribing. A total of 72 of psychiatric outpatients (68% women; median age 76 years) completed the validated Danish version of the revised Patients' Attitudes Towards Deprescribing (rPATD) questionnaire. Patients used a median of eight medications (interquartile range 6–12), with 88%, 49% and 24% using antidepressants, antipsychotics and anxiolytics, respectively. Fifty-one percent of patients reported an intrinsic desire to stop one of their medications, while 92% would be willing to stop one on their physician's advice. Seventy-five percent of patients would be worried about missing out on future benefits following deprescribing and 37% had previous bad deprescribing experiences. Use of ≥8 regular medications was associated with more concerns about stopping medication and greater perceived burden of using medication, while use of antipsychotics was not associated with any differences in rPATD factor scores. It is crucial for health care professionals to be aware of patients' specific concerns and past experiences to promote a patient-centred deprescribing approach that takes into account the needs and preferences of older patients with psychiatric disorders.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lundby, Carina","Nielsen, Marianne","Simonsen, Trine","Galsgaard, Stine","Haastrup, Maija Bruun","Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","Pottegård, Anton"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783624"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Lundby, Carina"],"keyword":["Aged","Attitudes","Deprescribing","Deprescriptions","Female","Geriatric psychiatry","Humans","Male","Older people","Outpatients","Polypharmacy","Psychotropics","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attitudes towards deprescribing in geriatric psychiatry a survey among older psychiatric outpatients","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13952","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank all patients for participating in the study and staff in the three geriatric psychiatry outpatient clinics for identifying patients for study participation. The authors would like to acknowledge Open Patient data Explorative Network (OPEN), Odense University Hospital. The study is funded by the Development and Research Fund (Danish Regions and ). Sundhedskartellet"],"id":"S01-000.00-783624","identifier":[{"id":"85175456386","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37823673","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b9290fa9-c842-476f-9c26-f0633175040c"],"keyword":["Aged","Deprescriptions","Female","Humans","Male","Outpatients","Polypharmacy","Surveys and Questionnaires","attitudes","deprescribing","geriatric psychiatry","older people","psychotropics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9161F3BAA7D0F6A39AA1D92E2762B469"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13952","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/276841984/Basic_Clin_Pharma_Tox_-_2023_-_Lundby_-_Attitudes_towards_deprescribing_in_geriatric_psychiatry_A_survey_among_older.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology, Pharmacy and Environmental Medicine","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carina","key":"lundbypau","last":"Lundby","locid":"ef58a4be-0ffe-42f3-80ec-7f6cecf96102","name":"Lundby, Carina","orcid":"0000-0002-2121-6252","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Marianne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","name":"Simonsen, Trine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"galsgaardpau","last":"Galsgaard","name":"Galsgaard, Stine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maija Bruun","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","locid":"8449006f-7fb6-43b1-b126-0c07acab539e","name":"Haastrup, Maija Bruun","orcid":"0000-0002-1776-4846","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Vestergaard","key":"ravnnielsenpau","last":"Ravn-Nielsen","name":"Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name"