{"abstract":"Background/Objectives: Genicular artery embolization (GAE) has demonstrated potential as a treatment for knee osteoarthritis by targeting inflammation and pain, although current evidence remains limited. This study used imaging biomarkers to objectively assess synovitis and possible ischemic complications following GAE. Methods: This was a prospective, single-center trial including participants with mild-to-moderate knee osteoarthritis. Ultrasound, contrast-enhanced (CE), and non-CE-MRI were performed two days before and one and six months after GAE. Ultrasound biomarkers included synovial hypertrophy, effusion, and Doppler activity. A combined effusion-synovitis score was assessed on non-CE-MRI, while CE-MRI allowed differentiation between synovium and effusion and was used to calculate whole-joint and local synovitis scores. The post-GAE MRIs were reviewed for ischemic complications. Results: Seventeen participants (aged 43–71) were treated. Significant reductions were observed in ultrasound-assessed synovial hypertrophy and Doppler activity, as well as in CE-MRI local and whole-joint synovitis scores. While reductions in effusion were noted in both ultrasound and MRI, these changes did not reach statistical significance. At one month, MRI revealed three cases of nonspecific osteonecrosis-like areas, which resolved completely by six months. Conclusions: This study demonstrated a reduction in synovitis and no permanent ischemic complication following GAE in knee osteoarthritis. Larger studies with longer follow-up are needed to confirm the long-term efficacy and safety of the procedure.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hindsø, Louise","Hölmich, Per","Petersen, Michael Mørk","Xu, Jack J.","Heerwagen, Søren","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Riis, Robert G.C.","Hansen, Adam Espe","Terslev, Lene","Taudorf, Mikkel","Lönn, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-790212"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Inflammation","Knee osteoarthritis","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Trans arterial embolization","Ultrasound"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reduction in synovitis following genicular artery embolization in knee osteoarthritis a prospective ultrasound and mri study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics14222564","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-790212","identifier":[{"id":"39594229","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85210572463","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11592601","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-476d70fb-436c-4526-94e8-2e362416bc39"],"keyword":["inflammation","knee osteoarthritis","magnetic resonance imaging","trans-arterial embolization","ultrasound"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6481824D7ACA99A5A75162EABEA7D597"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics14222564","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/420385071/diagnostics_14_02564_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Louise","key":"hindsøpau","last":"Hindsø","name":"Hindsø, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Per","key":"hölmichpau","last":"Hölmich","locid":"dbb82dee-c9f9-47c8-b3d8-f810ae75ee69","name":"Hölmich, Per","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Michael M.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9eb5f936-2e76-4f2f-917e-a3b50f56f0e6","name":"Petersen, Michael Mørk","name_org":"Petersen, Michael M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jack J.","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Jack J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"heerwagenpau","last":"Heerwagen","name":"Heerwagen, Søren","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Michael B.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","name_org":"Nielsen, Michael B.","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Robert G.C.","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","name":"Riis, Robert G.C.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Adam E.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Hansen, Adam E.","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lene","key":"terslevpau","last":"Terslev","locid":"d10590c5-f19a-4682-ab40-30cb3dc6ffca","name":"Terslev, Lene","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mikkel","key":"taudorfpau","last":"Taudorf","locid":"9d4498dc-be26-4ddf-9416-6382e21a7f48","name":"Taudorf, Mikkel","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lars","key":"lönnpau","last":"Lönn","locid":"c30d6f51-c103-4f4b-a7db-30af02137484","name":"Lönn, Lars","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39594229"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/diagnostics14222564","issn":["20754418"],"issue":"22","journal":"Diagnostics","paperid":"2564","status":"p","title":"Diagnostics","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85210572463"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-476d70fb-436c-4526-94e8-2e362416bc39"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reduction in Synovitis Following Genicular Artery Embolization in Knee Osteoarthritis : A Prospective Ultrasound and MRI Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-790212","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Inequality in health persists in childbearing families in socially or mentally vulnerable positions. The FACAM project was developed as an intervention aiming to enhance health outcomes for childbearing families. Purpose: The aim of this study was to gain a deeper understanding of the experiences and perspectives of care professionals in multidisciplinary and cross-sectorial collaboration, and their experiences of interactions with childbearing families within the context of the FACAM project. Methods: Eight focus groups were conducted with 32 multidisciplinary care professionals working with childbearing families in vulnerable positions. A thematic analysis was conducted, with positioning theory as the theoretical framework focusing on storylines, positioning and speech-acts. Results: Two overall themes were constructed. Theme one: Cross-sectorial collaboration and the influence on the care provided. Theme two: Interaction with and assessment of women and families’ care needs and their influence on the care provided, with three subthemes; a) Establishment of a trustful relationship, b) Assessments of vulnerable positions in relation to function in everyday life, c) Interactions with the woman or family depending on their needs. Conclusion: Care professionals found needs-adapted and tailored care meaningful. Well-functioning multidisciplinary and cross-sectorial collaboration was important to support the families.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nygaard, Lene","Davis, Deborah Lee","Ibsen, Inge Olga","Pontoppidan, Maiken","Nohr, Ellen A","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-812606"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Nygaard, Lene"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Canberra"],"keyword":["Adult","Attitude of Health Personnel","Collaboration","Cooperative Behavior","Family","Female","Focus Groups","Focus group","Health Personnel psychology","Humans","Integrated care","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Care Team","Perinatal Care","Qualitative","Qualitative Research","Trust","Vulnerable groups","Vulnerable populations"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"care professionals experiences within a multidisciplinary and cross sectorial intervention for childbearing women and families in vulnerable positions a focus group study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17482631.2024.2410503","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-812606","identifier":[{"id":"39401328","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85206275169","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11486020","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-a21aad40-0c35-4662-9aa6-7d17217ddf77"],"keyword":["Adult","Attitude of Health Personnel","Cooperative Behavior","Family","Female","Focus Groups","Health Personnel/psychology","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Care Team","Qualitative","Qualitative Research","Trust","Vulnerable Populations","collaboration","focus group","integrated care","perinatal care","vulnerable groups"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-FD94294651E0B69169B8F46EEAC72000"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17482631.2024.2410503","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/275289546/Care_professionals_experiences_within_a_multidisciplinary_and_cross-sectorial_intervention_for_childbearing_women_and_families_in_vulnerable_position.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"or