nd Well-Being","paperid":"2410503","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"e","title":"International Journal of Qualitative Studies on Health and Well-Being","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206275169"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["vive-77d0b12f-d3cc-4977-9067-ec13fb1b4a7c"],"src":["VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Care professionals' experiences within a multidisciplinary and cross-sectorial intervention for childbearing women and families in vulnerable positions: a focus group study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-813253","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: The prevalence of patients with chronic kidney disease (CKD) and polypharmacy is increasing and has amplified the importance of examining inappropriate prescribing (IP) in CKD. This review focuses on the latest research regarding the prevalence of IP in CKD and the related adverse clinical effects and explores new interventions against IP. Method: A literature search was performed using PubMed, EMBASE and the Cochrane Library searching articles published between June 2016 and March 2022. Results: Twenty-seven studies were included. An IP prevalence of 12.6% to 96% and 0.3% to 66% was reported in hospital and outpatient settings, respectively. In nonhospital settings, the prevalence of IP varied between 3.9% and 60%. IP was associated with higher risk of hospitalisation (HR 1.46, 95% CI 1.17–1.81), higher bleeding rate (HR 2.34, 95% CI 1.32 to 3.37) and higher risk of all-cause mortality (OR 1.07, 95% CI 1.02 to 1.13). Three studies reported the impact of interventions on IP. Conclusion: This review highlights widespread IP in CKD patients across healthcare settings, with varying prevalence rates. IP is substantially linked to adverse outcomes in patients. While limited interventions show promise, urgent research is needed to develop effective strategies addressing IP and improving CKD patient care.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hamzaei, Zohra","Houlind, Morten Baltzer","Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","Christensen, Louise Westberg Strejby","Walls, Anne Byriel","Aharaz, Anissa","Olesen, Charlotte","Coric, Faruk","Revell, Joo Hanne Poulsen","Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","Andersen, Trine Rune Høgh","Hedegaard, Ulla"],"cuid":["S02-083.33-768692"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hedegaard, Ulla"],"keyword":["Chronic kidney disease","Drug Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions","Drug related problems","Hospitals","Humans","Inappropriate Prescribing","Prevalence","Renal Insufficiency","Renal Insufficiency Chronic complications","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Copenhagen University Hospital – The Hospital Pharmacy"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inappropriate prescribing in patients with kidney disease a rapid review of prevalence associated clinical outcomes and impact of interventions","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13986","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.33-768692","identifier":[{"id":"85185453008","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38348501","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1ca8d390-eb4e-4dc3-b2b5-a0fa50eb8b5d","sdu-43abe1f2-dcab-450b-998b-47655571fc66"],"keyword":["Drug-Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions","Hospitals","Humans","Prevalence","Renal Insufficiency, Chronic/complications","chronic kidney disease","drug-related problems","inappropriate prescribing","renal insufficiency","treatment outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-99D5348D097D6D81771F305BAD7E1282"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13986","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/277565766/Basic_Clin_Pharma_Tox_-_2024_-_Hamzaei_-_Inappropriate_prescribing_in_patients_with_kidney_disease_A_rapid_review_of.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/387738243/Basic_Clin