{"abstract":"Objective: The objective of this study is to characterize bladder mucosal trauma associated with intermittent catheterization with conventional eyelet catheters (CECs) and to assess if a microhole zone catheter (MHZC) design concept reduces this adverse effect. Materials and Methods: A porcine model was developed to reflect human catheterization and bladder drainage. Nine pigs were randomized for catheterization with CEC (n = 6) or MHZC (n = 3). The bladder was drained repeatedly 20 times through the catheter. Cystoscopy was performed before and after the procedure, and bladders were analysed by histopathology. Two additional pigs were used for cystoscopy visualization of suction events in vivo. Cystoscopy, gross pathology, histopathological score, leucocyte infiltration, and intracatheter pressure at flow stops during voiding were compared for each group. Results: A significant higher pressure gradient was measured inside the CECs compared with MHZCs during flow stop. Consequently, CECs resulted in suction events inflicting bladder trauma characterized by loss of epithelium, oedema, haemorrhage, and neutrophil tissue infiltration. No significant trauma was identified when using MHZC. Conclusions: Considerable mucosal bladder trauma is inflicted by CECs which may be an overlooked risk factor for urinary tract infection. Catheters can be designed to minimize mucosal suction and reduce associated trauma. This may be a solution to reduce infection frequency and increase user comfort. Furthermore, the study demonstrates the potential of pigs as an attractive animal model for investigating urinary catheter performances.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Stærk, Kristian","Schrøder, Brit","Jensen, Louise Kruse","Petersen, Troels","Andersen, Thomas Emil","Nielsen, Lene Feldskov"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-725224"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Thomas Emil","Stærk, Kristian"],"keyword":["Large animal model","Pig","Urinary catheter","bladder trauma","intermittent catheter","microhole zone catheter","mucosal suction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COLO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COLO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"catheter associated bladder mucosal trauma during intermittent voiding an experimental study in pigs","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/bco2.295","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was supported by an unconditional research grant to T. A. from Coloplast. Funding information"],"id":"S02-100.00-725224","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10869658","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38371199","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85178198375","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-95435516-8657-4721-89f7-e938ffba346b","sdu-2724008f-3041-4195-a621-3d33a5952f1e"],"keyword":["bladder trauma","intermittent catheter","large animal model","microhole zone catheter","mucosal suction","pig","urinary catheter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7CDBDE4F96668435639CD98522431B45"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/bco2.295","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/255744093/BJUI_Compass_-_2023_-_St_rk_-_Catheter_associated_bladder_mucosal_trauma_during_intermittent_voiding_An_experimental_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385650764/BJUI_Compass_2023_St_rk_Catheter_associated_bladder_mucosal_trauma_during_intermittent_voiding_An_experimental_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Microbiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"coloplast","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COLO","l3nl":"Coloplast Group","l3nn":"Coloplast","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Coloplast","namevar":["Coloplast"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COLO","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Pathobiological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"stærkpau","last":"Stærk","locid":"0e1429ba-881e-4a1a-b489-bdfbbaae2599","name":"Stærk, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-2410-0375","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Brit","key":"schrøderpau","last":"Schrøder","name":"Schrøder, Brit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Louise Kruse","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"1edba00c-b457-4660-85a3-24c07c4919f6","name":"Jensen, Louise Kruse","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Troels","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Troels","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Emil","key":"an