 Terese L.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5d60011a-316a-4fad-b53b-dec099bf65bf","name":"Pedersen, Gitte","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Nina","key":"weispau","last":"Weis","locid":"3a88aaad-c729-432b-b725-999664af7a45","name":"Weis, Nina","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39119767"],"pub":{"doi":"10.61409/v03240175","issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","paperid":"V03240175","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"186"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201033682"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-43602f74-ecee-4379-b977-a5d0c0cb721b","ku-88f8afd8-ffd6-4b9e-a789-db81e361697c","sdu-7bc88e74-db0c-48b0-87db-f8bf28744441"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Graviditet og infektion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-091.90-803671","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Decisions regarding maintenance therapy in patients with multiple myeloma should be based on both treatment efficacy and health-related quality of life (HRQL) consequences. In the CARFI trial, patients with first relapse of multiple myeloma underwent salvage autologous stem cell transplantation (salvage ASCT) before randomization to carfilzomib-dexamethasone maintenance therapy (Kd) or observation. The primary clinical endpoint was time to progression, which was extended by 8 months by Kd. The aim of this paper is to present the all HRQL endpoints of the CARFI trial including the HRQL effect of Kd maintenance therapy relative to observation. The primary HRQL endpoint was assessed by EORTC QLQ-C30 Summary score (QLQ-C30-sum) at 8 months follow-up. A key secondary HRQL endpoint was quality-adjusted progression-free-survival (QAPFS). Methods: HRQL was assessed with EORTC QLQ-C30, EORTC QLQ-MY20 and FACT/GOG-Ntx at randomization and every second month during follow-up. HRQL data were analyzed with linear mixed effect models until 8 months follow-up. QAPFS per individual was calculated by multiplying progression-free survival (PFS) by two quality-adjustment metrics, the QLQ-C30-sum and EORTC Quality of Life Utility Measure-Core 10 dimensions (QLU-C10D). The QAPFS per treatment group was estimated with the Kaplan-Meier method. P < 0.05 was used for statistical significance, and a between-group minimal important difference of 10 points was interpreted as clinically relevant for the QLQ-C30-sum. Results: 168 patients were randomized. HRQL questionnaire compliance was 93%. For the QLQ-C30-sum, the difference of 4.62 points (95% confidence interval (CI) -8.9: -0.4, p = 0.032) was not clinically relevant. PFS was 19.3 months for the Kd maintenance group and 16.8 months for the observation group; difference = 2.5 months (95% CI 0.5; 4.5). QAPFS based on the QLQ-C30-sum for the Kd maintenance group was 18.0 months (95% CI 16.4; 19.6) and for the observation group 15.0 months (95% CI 13.5; 16.5); difference = 3.0 months (95% CI 0.8–5.3). QAPFS based on the QLU-C10D for the Kd maintenance group was 17.5 months (95% CI 15.9; 19.2) and 14.0 months (95% CI 12.4; 15.5) for the observation group; difference = 3.5 months (95% CI 1.1–5.9). Conclusions: Kd maintenance therapy after salvage ASCT did not adversely affect overall HRQL, but adjustment for HRQL reduced the PFS compared to unadjusted PFS. PFS of maintenance therapy should be quality-adjusted to balance the benefits and HRQL impact.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard","Schjesvold, Fredrik","Möller, Sören","Guldbrandsen, Nina","Hansson, Markus","Remes, Kari","Peceliunas, Valdas","Abildgaard, Niels","Gregersen, Henrik","King, Madeleine T."],"cuid":["S03-100.00-724379"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene","Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard"],"country":["Australia","Finland","Lithuania","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Oslo University Hospital","Skaane University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","The University of Sydney","Turku University Central Hospital","Turku University Hospital","University of Oslo","University of Sydney","University of Turku","Vilnius University","Vilnius University Hospital"],"keyword":["Carfilzomib","Dexamethasone therapeutic use","Health related quality of life","Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplantation","Humans","Multiple Myeloma drug therapy","Multiple myeloma","Oligopeptides","Progression Free Survival","Quality of Life","Randomized clinical trial","Transplantation Autologous"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"health related quality of life and quality adjusted progression free survival for carfilzomib and dexamethasone maintenance following salvage autologous stem cell transplantation in patients with multiple myeloma a randomized phase 000000000002 trial by the nordic myeloma study group","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s41687-024-00691-2","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Our heartfelt thanks go to Henrik Rode Eshøj. Sadly, Henrik passed away during the time of analyzing the data and writing the manuscript. Henrik made a great contribution in rearranging the PRO data collection into electronic data capturing in the CARFI trial and other clinical trial conducted by the Nordic Myeloma Study Group. In addition, Henrik was the key manager in establishing the statistical analysis plan, which is the foundation of this work. Thank you to Sanne Kjær at the Clinical Trial Unit, Aalborg University Hospital for administrative assistance and Nana Hyldig for data preparation. Also, we would like to express our thanks to the participating patients for taking time to complete the questionnaires and to the study coordinators at the including sites for administrating the paper questionnaires."],"id":"S03-100.00-724379","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10844184","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85184449271","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38315268","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-e59fb6a3-c456-4507-8f62-f146ced1f8c1","au-fa10abbd-6201-49dd-8242-e75162794745","sdu-b784a32b-b32a-4fcc-9261-9fa73cc20781"],"keyword":["Carfilzomib","Dexamethasone/therapeutic use","Health-related quality of life","Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplantation","Humans","Multiple Myeloma/drug therapy","Multiple m