{"abstract":"Urinary tract infections (UTIs) are the main complication associated with clean intermittent catheterization (CIC) and are facilitated by post-void residual urine and trauma to the mucosa during voiding. The risk of UTI may be diminished by reducing the residual volumes and preventing microtrauma caused by mucosal suction through the eyelets of conventional eyelet catheters (CEC). A new micro-hole zone catheter (MHZC) was developed and tested in an ex vivo porcine lower urinary tract model and in vivo, in pigs, against a CEC. It was shown that, irrespective of the micro-hole diameter, the new catheter ensured increased flowrates and significantly lower residual volumes at the first flow-stop. Furthermore, with a micro-hole diameter of 0.4 mm, mucosal suction was virtually eliminated, regardless of the insertion depth or simulated intra-abdominal pressure mimicking sitting or standing humans. Pressure profile experiments and endoscopy studies indicated that the bladder gradually folds against the drainage tip of the new catheter, without blocking the flow, and, unlike with the CEC, sharp pressure variations and flow-stops did not occur during voiding. The MHZC outperformed the CEC in all tested scenarios and decreased residual volumes, thus potentially decreasing the risk of UTIs.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Schrøder, Brit","Tentor, Fabio","Miclăuş, Teodora","Stærk, Kristian","Andersen, Thomas Emil","Spinelli, Michele","Rendeli, Claudia","Del Popolo, Giulio","Bagi, Per","Nielsen, Lene Feldskov"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-723611"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Lene Feldskov"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Careggi University Hospital","Catholic University of the Sacred Heart","Ospedale Niguarda Ca’ Granda"],"keyword":["Animals","Humans","Swine","Urinary Bladder","Urinary Tract Infections prevention control","Urinary retention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["AML Christensen"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COLO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-COLO","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"new micro hole zone catheter reduces residual urine and mucosal microtrauma in a lower urinary tract model","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-52505-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-723611","identifier":[{"id":"38280939","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10821950","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85183408474","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-c8ee5cbe-1898-4c87-9be1-6f9c8b3a6d57"],"keyword":["Animals","Catheters/adverse effects","Humans","Intermittent Urethral Catheterization/adverse effects","Swine","Urinary Bladder","Urinary Retention","Urinary Tract Infections/prevention & control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C1E11F2DD635C690172DE971A0E0890E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-52505-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/254598803/s41598-024-52505-6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"coloplast","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COLO","l3nl":"Coloplast Group","l3nn":"Coloplast","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Coloplast","namevar":["Coloplast A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COLO","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["AML Christensen"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Microbiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"ospedale niguarda ca granda","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ospedale Niguarda Ca’ Granda","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"catholic university of the sacred heart","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Catholic University of the Sacred Heart","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"it","key":"careggi university hospital","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Careggi University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit","key":"schrøderpau","last":"Schrøder","name":"Schrøder, Brit","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"tentorpau","last":"Tentor","name":"Tentor, Fabio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Teodora","key":"miclăuşpau","last":"Miclăuş","name":"Miclăuş, Teodora","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"stærkpau","last":"Stærk","locid":"0e1429ba-881e-4a1a-b489-bdfbbaae2599","name":"Stærk, Kristian","orcid