{"abstract":"Thrombocytopenia is a commonly observed phenomenon in sepsis and a frequent cause of anxiety for the clinician at the bedside, raising a host of questions, including the concerns about a low platelet count, the interaction between sepsis and platelets, the other causes of thrombocytopenia, or the indications of platelet transfusion. Though much of the effect of sepsis on platelet physiology and function is yet unknown, in this article we have undertaken to address many of these common questions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Leone, Marc","Nielsen, Nathan D.","Russell, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754477"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","United States"],"glorg":["Aix-Marseille University","All Global Affiliations","University of New Mexico"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ten tips on sepsis induced thrombocytopenia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-754477","identifier":[{"id":"85192948857","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38739278","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-622d683b-79ae-4379-941a-be0749514056"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DB828D8490517607C966A81947F5D0BF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"aix marseille university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Aix-Marseille University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of new mexico","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of New Mexico","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marc","key":"leonepau","last":"Leone","name":"Leone, Marc","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nathan D.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Nathan D.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Lene","key":"russellpau","last":"Russell","locid":"8de8452e-0962-4fb8-be22-f0464cb450c7","name":"Russell, Lene","orcid":"0000-0001-7352-8728","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38739278"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00134-024-07478-5","issn":["03424642","09351701"],"issn_org":["03424642"],"issue":"7","journal":"Intensive Care Medicine","pages":"1157-1160","status":"p","title":"Intensive Care Medicine","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192948857"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-622d683b-79ae-4379-941a-be0749514056"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ten tips on sepsis-induced thrombocytopenia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754477","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The endophytic mycobiome is present in all studied plant compartments, including fruits and seeds. Here, we studied the mycobiome of seed wings as they are transferred with seeds in common ash and tested whether the mycobiome differs among trees. To achieve this, we used ITS1-based amplicon sequencing and two genotypes of F. excelsior as a model to compare the mycobiome of mother trees and their wings. RESULTS: We compared the mycobiome of 57 seed wings to the seed stalks (57) collected from two genotypes of F. excelsior using three ramets of each genotype. Alpha diversity indices (ACE, Fisher and Observed OTUs) suggested a higher richness of the mycobiome associated with the seed wing than the seed stalk within each genotype. However, there were neither significant differences in Shannon diversity between the mycobiomes from the two tissue types nor the two genotypes. PERMANOVA revealed significant differences in the mycobiome composition between tissue types (P < 0.001). It also showed a significant difference between seed wings (P = 0.04), but not between seed stalks of the two genotypes. Our results suggest that Fraxinus excelsior mother trees disperse different sets of mycobiomes with their seed wings, which may be important for germination and seedling establishment-especially in the light of ash dieback.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Long, Feng","Doonan, James","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Kjær, Erik Dahl","Kosawang, Chatchai"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754664"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Genotype","Mycobiome"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mother trees of common ash i fraxinus excelsior i disperse different sets of mycobiome through their seed wings","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13104-024-06863-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754664","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11289985","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85200177402","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39080773","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-901f76a7-7a6c-477a-b44f-fd5dbde6799d"],"keyword":["Endophytes/physiology","Fraxinus/microbiology","Genotype","Mycobiome","Seeds/microbiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0A840F5B08C161679FB92263F51006EC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13104-024-06863-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/402105971/Mother_trees_of_common_ash_Fraxinus_excelsior_disperse_different_sets_of_mycobiome_through_their_seed_wings.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Forest and Landscape Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Feng","key":"longpau","last":"Long","locid":"88bae5d7-47cc-4beb-b49b-44d82659b5f1","name":"Long, Feng","orcid":"0000-0001-8895-2193","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"James M.","key":"doonanpau","last":"Doonan","locid":"c05913af-39d1-4b2f-93f0-94af8789b4f2","name":"Doonan, James","name_org":"Doonan, James M.","orcid":"0000-0002-0523-5808","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene R.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","name_org":"Nielsen, Lene R.","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik D.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","name_org":"Kjær, Erik D.","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chatchai","key":"kosawangpau","last":"Kosawang","locid":"1b69b056-6473-427b-81f9-20fbd6797849","name":"Kosawang, Chatchai","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39080773"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13104-024-06863-z","issn":["17560500"],"journal":"BMC Research Notes","paperid":"213","status":"p","title":"BMC Research Notes","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200177402"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-901f76a7-7a6c-477a-b44f-fd5dbde6799d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mother trees of common ash (<i>Fraxinus excelsior</i>) disperse different sets of mycobiome through their seed wings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754664","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Studies assessing the presence of painful temporomandibular disorders (TMD) in post-traumatic headache (PTH) attributed to mild traumatic brain injury are lacking. We aimed to (1) measure the prevalence of painful TMD and assess its association with demographic and trauma-related factors in patients with PTH and (2) compare the headache characteristics and post-concussion burden between the PTH patients with and without painful TMD. METHODS: This study embedded in a population-based epidemiologic cohort study (N = 2,832) assessed mild traumatic brain injury patients (18-60 years) 2-4 months after their trauma. PTH patients (n = 382) were identified and invited to fill out questionnaires assessing post-concussion symptoms and burden, headache characteristics, presence of painful TMD and demographics. RESULTS: The prevalence of painful TMD was 22.5%. Living with a partner/spouse (OR = 0.31, 95% CI: 0.13-0.75, P = 0.010) and having a secondary education (OR = 0.28, 95% CI: 0.08-0.99, P = 0.048) was significantly associated with decreased risk of having painful TMD. PTH patients with painful TMD reported significantly higher headache intensity (P < 0.042), increased symptom burden (P = 0.007), reduced workability after trauma (P = 0.019) and were frequently on full-time sick leave compared to those without painful TMD. CONCLUSIONS: PTH patients had a high prevalence of painful TMD. Living with a partner/spouse and having a secondary education decreased the risk of having painful TMD. Patients with painful TMD were significantly heavily burdened compared to those without painful TMD. CLINICAL RELEVANCE: Presence of painful TMD in PTH patients may compromise the rehabilitation plan and complicate the management of these patients.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kothari, Mohit","Odgaard, Lene","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Kothari, Simple F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-773056"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kothari, Simple F."],"keyword":["Concussion","Mild traumatic brain injury","Orofacial pain","Post traumatic headache","Temporomandibular disorders"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence of painful temporomandibular disorders in individuals with post traumatic headache attributed to mild traumatic brain injury","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85211399436","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-773056","identifier":[{"id":"85211399436","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39621147","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-92549a74-7a38-4e74-8f5e-c7b0b46f2ce4"],"keyword":["Concussion","Mild traumatic brain injury","Orofacial pain","Post-traumatic headache","Temporomandibular disorders"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AFEFF34AC6DB91FA36792C3BC3106654"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hammel Neurocenter, Universitetsklinik for Neurorehabilitering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mohit","key":"kotharimohitpau","last":"Kothari","locid":"04b2613a-b642-417f-9f1d-08167c4832ec","name":"Kothari, Mohit","orcid":"0000-0002-8191-9769","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"odgaardlenepau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"1b80fe7b-ba0a-45b3-aca1-48bc19a97a44","name":"Odgaard, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-9830-3282","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Feldbæk","key":"nielsenjørgenfeldbækpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simple F.","key":"kotharisimplefpau","last":"Kothari","locid":"1df588d0-1708-42c9-96e6-5dda22803afc","name":"Kothari, Simple F.","orcid":"0000-0001-8043-2927","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39621147"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00784-024-06086-3","issn":["14326981","14363771"],"issn_org":["14326981"],"issue":"12","journal":"Clinical Oral Investigations","paperid":"678","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Clinical Oral Investigations","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211399436"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-92549a74-7a38-4e74-8f5e-c7b0b46f2ce4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prevalence of painful temporomandibular disorders in individuals with post‑traumatic headache attributed to mild traumatic brain injury","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-773056","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We investigate three small employee-owned businesses: a consultancy, a business within art restoration, and a software business, and how they apply and reshape digital resources to commonly govern their businesses as there is no single tool that caters to their specific needs. Using the concept of digital bricolage as a lens, we find that the businesses apply a combination of digital resources at hand to meet their needs, they use these tools in well-known ways, and create new solutions, but do not look for ideal solutions. We furthermore find that believing in a common set of values shapes “the bricolage”, an aspect not found in the literature. These shared values further inform how technologies are used in practice. The values are shared internally but differ between the businesses. This has implications for the design of future tools that can help businesses govern collective decision-making.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776381"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design","Employee ownership"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing it for governance the case of employee owned businesses the case of employee owned businesses","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776381","identifier":[{"id":"85200656394","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2680c5af-21f5-4d28-a533-141becbc0080"],"keyword":["Design","Digital bricolage","Employee ownership"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-17D899CE01AB1036901E7FBC7AD7EEDD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_2","issn":["03029743"],"pages":"13-26","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Interact 2023","title":"Design for Equality and Justice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200656394"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2680c5af-21f5-4d28-a533-141becbc0080"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing IT for Governance - The Case of Employee-Owned Businesses. : The Case of Employee-Owned Businesses","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776381","year":"2024","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"How can organisations introduce and evaluate service design (SD) tools? This tutorial answers these questions through the introduction of ‘organisational usability’ and ‘design maturity’ as frameworks to help organisations assess their readiness to adopt and use SD tools. Customer journeys, service blueprints, and ecosystem mapping, among other SD tools, are perceived as straightforward by some organisations, however, organisations with low SD maturity can face challenges in how to utilise and leverage their potential. The tutorial introduces means of understanding how an organisation is likely to experience or is currently experiencing SD and the accompanying tools. Tutorial participants will be provided with insights and an assessment framework for successful organisational SD interventions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Abdelnour-Nocera, José L.","Nielsen, Lene","Li, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776426"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Infinite Interactive LTD, UK","University of West London"],"keyword":["Service Design","Service blueprint"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introducing and evaluating service design tools in organisations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85206560674","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776426","identifier":[{"id":"85206560674","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-977e2189-d92d-4ed2-9bc8-a5979639647f"],"keyword":["design maturity","ecosystem mapping","organisational usability","service blueprint","service design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-315E21420CE58B99AFD0E482AF8236A2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of west london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of West London","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"infinite interactive ltd uk","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Infinite Interactive LTD, UK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"José L.","key":"abdelnournocerapau","last":"Abdelnour-Nocera","name":"Abdelnour-Nocera, José L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Christina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3677045.3685468","isbn":["9798400709654"],"pages":"1-3","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '24 Adjunct: Adjunct Proceedings of the 2024 Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206560674"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-977e2189-d92d-4ed2-9bc8-a5979639647f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introducing and Evaluating Service Design Tools in Organisations.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776426","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Vaccination before solid organ transplantation is recommended since post-transplantation immunosuppression is known to impair vaccine responses. However, little is known about post-transplantation seroprotection rates in organ transplant recipients vaccinated pre-transplantation. We aimed to investigate the proportion of transplant recipients vaccinated against hepatitis B virus (HBV) and invasive pneumococcal disease (IPD) pre-transplantation at the time of listing for transplantation with post-transplantation seroprotection. We included 136 solid organ transplant (SOT) recipients vaccinated at the time of listing for transplantation. We investigated post-transplantation antibody concentrations against HBV and IPD. Established antibody thresholds were used to define seroprotection. The proportions of SOT recipients with post-transplantation seroprotection were 27.9% (n = 38) and 42.6% (n = 58) against HBV and IPD, respectively. Compared to completing HBV vaccination pre-transplantation, completing post-transplantation vaccination (adjusted odds ratio (aOR): 7.8, 95% CI: 2.5–24.5, p < 0.001) and incomplete vaccination (aOR: 6.3, 95% CI: 1.2–32.6, p = 0.028) were associated with non-response against HBV, after adjustment for confounders. Importantly, patients with seroprotection at the time of listing had lower odds of non-response against HBV (aOR: 0.04, 95% CI: 0.0–0.1, p < 0.001) and IPD (aOR: 0.3, 95% CI: 0.1–0.7, p = 0.007) compared to those without seroprotection. SOT recipients vaccinated pre-transplantation had low post-transplantation seroprotection rates against HBV and IPD. However, SOT recipients with seroprotection at the time of listing had lower odds of non-response, suggesting early vaccination should be a priority.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Hornung, Lise Bank","Hamm, Sebastian Rask","Hald, Annemette","Harboe, Zitta Barrella","Lundbo, Lene Fogt","Wareham, Neval Ete","Heftdal, Line Dam","Ekenberg, Christina","Bjerrum, Stephanie","Holler, Jon Gitz","Mathiesen, Inger Hee Mabuza","Krohn, Paul Suno","Bjerring, Peter Nissen","Gustafsson, Finn","Perch, Michael","Rasmussen, Allan","Nielsen, Susanne Dam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-778186"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Hepatitis B","Invasive pneumococcal disease","Solid organ transplantation","Vaccination"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"post transplantation seroprotection rates in liver lung and heart transplant recipients vaccinated pre transplantation against hepatitis b virus and invasive pneumococcal disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/vaccines12101092","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-778186","identifier":[{"id":"001342851000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85207387048","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11511315","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39460259","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7ec0d540-ad06-4d31-ad7c-f3043f835b5f"],"keyword":["hepatitis B","invasive pneumococcal disease","solid organ transplantation","vaccination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-76C4A1E651D3BE68A547C68125637E0D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/411120978/vaccines_12_01092.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/vaccines12101092","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: infection medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lise Bank","key":"hornungpau","last":"Hornung","name":"Hornung, Lise Bank","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian Rask","key":"hammpau","last":"Hamm","name":"Hamm, Sebastian Rask","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annemette","key":"haldpau","last":"Hald","name":"Hald, Annemette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Zitta Barrella","key":"harboepau","last":"Harboe","locid":"2b596a33-5659-4236-b5ea-c0991866af44","name":"Harboe, Zitta Barrella","orcid":"0000-0001-5552-0095","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Fogt","key":"lundbopau","last":"Lundbo","name":"Lundbo, Lene Fogt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Neval Ete","key":"warehampau","last":"Wareham","name":"Wareham, Neval Ete","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Dam","key":"heftdalpau","last":"Heftdal","name":"Heftdal, Line Dam","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"ekenbergpau","last":"Ekenberg","name":"Ekenberg, Christina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stephanie","key":"bjerrumpau","last":"Bjerrum","name":"Bjerrum, Stephanie","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon Gitz","key":"hollerpau","last":"Holler","name":"Holler, Jon Gitz","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inger Hee Mabuza","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","name":"Mathiesen, Inger Hee Mabuza","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Paul Suno","key":"krohnpau","last":"Krohn","name":"Krohn, Paul Suno","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Peter Nissen","key":"bjerringpau","last":"Bjerring","locid":"50ed707a-3ca4-4f60-a9dc-64a9925b77e2","name":"Bjerring, Peter Nissen","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Finn","key":"gustafssonpau","last":"Gustafsson","locid":"6716eef1-891b-4209-a823-e96e765b9433","name":"Gustafsson, Finn","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Michael","key":"perchpau","last":"Perch","locid":"e0a136a6-8b36-4735-9db2-8847ce581fc6","name":"Perch, Michael","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Allan","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Susanne Dam","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2baa36fa-2709-482a-9595-52c5b9537801","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39460259"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/vaccines12101092","issn":["2076393X"],"issue":"10","journal":"Vaccines","paperid":"1092","status":"p","title":"Vaccines","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207387048"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7ec0d540-ad06-4d31-ad7c-f3043f835b5f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Post-Transplantation Seroprotection Rates in Liver, Lung, and Heart Transplant Recipients Vaccinated Pre-Transplantation against Hepatitis B Virus and Invasive Pneumococcal Disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-778186","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Her præsenteres den anden af i alt fire undersøgelser, der gennemføres i Sundparken i perioden frem til 2030. Formålet er løbende at kortlægge Sundparkens fysiske og sociale udvikling. Resultaterne vil efterfølgende blive sammenholdt med resultater fra tilsvarende undersøgelser i 14 andre boligområder, der ligesom Sundparken er omfattet af Parallelsamfundsaftalens krav om omfattende fysiske forandringer. Vi vil gerne takke nøglepersoner, beboere og brugere i området Sundparken, Horsens Kommune og Boligselskabet ALBO, som har ladet sig interviewe til evalueringen. Tak også til den tilknyttede studentermedhjælper Maja Wolters.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nordberg, Lene Wiell","Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","Bech-Danielsen, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-794155"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ghetto","Parallelsamfundsaftalen","Transformation","Udsatte boligområder"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sundparken 000000002024 følgeevaluering 000000000002 runde","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/770150568/Powerpoint_2._bes_g_SUNDPARKEN_PUBL.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Følgeevalueringen er finansieret af Landsbyggefonden."],"id":"S01-000.00-794155","ids":["aau-1673cb2a-0ac8-45c8-bb7a-73f174ff4cbb"],"keyword":["Ghetto","Parallelsamfundsaftalen","Transformation","Udsatte boligområder"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-32DEC5300C36C3965E7B3B477038A25F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/770150568/Powerpoint_2._bes_g_SUNDPARKEN_PUBL.pdf","version":"Published Vers