gsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-761974","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"To evaluate tumour necrosis factor inhibitor (TNFi) drug-levels and presence of anti-drug antibodies (ADAb) in patients with inflammatory arthritis who taper TNFi compared to TNFi continuation. Patients with rheumatoid arthritis, psoriatic arthritis, or axial spondyloarthritis on stable TNFi dose and in low disease activity ≥ 12 months were randomised (2:1) to disease activity-guided tapering or control. Blood samples at baseline, 12- and 18-months were evaluated for TNFi drug-levels and ADAb. In total, 129 patients were randomised to tapering (n = 88) or control (n = 41). Between baseline and month 18, a significant shift in TNFi drug-levels were observed in the tapering group resulting in fewer patients with high drug-levels (change: - 14% [95% CI - 27 to - 1%]) and more with low drug-levels (change: 18% [95% CI 5-31%]). Disease activity was equivalent between groups at 18 months, mean difference: RA - 0.06 (95% CI - 0.44 to 0.33), PsA 0.03 (95% CI - 0.36 to 0.42), and axSpA 0.16 (- 0.17 to 0.49), equivalence margins ± 0.5 disease activity points. ADAb were detected in eight patients, all from the tapering group. TNFi drug-level category or ADAb were not predictive for achieving successful tapering at 18 months. TNFi drug-levels decreased during tapering which indicate adherence to the tapering algorithm. Despite the difference in TNFi drug-levels at 18 months, disease activity remained equivalent, and only few tapering patients had detectable ADAb. These data do not support using TNFi drug-level and/or ADAb to guide the tapering decision but future research with larger trials is needed.Trial registration: EudraCT: 2017-001970-41, December 21, 2017.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Uhrenholt, Line","Sørensen, Mads E. R.","Lauridsen, K. B.","Duch, Kirsten","Dreyer, Lene","Christensen, Robin","Hauge, Ellen-Margrethe","Loft, Anne Gitte","Rasch, Mads N. B.","Horn, Hans Christian","Taylor, Peter C.","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Kristensen, Salome"],"cuid":["S03-099.92-761612"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Uhrenholt, Line"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Antibodies blood","Antirheumatic Agents administration dosage","Arthritis Psoriatic drug therapy","Arthritis Rheumatoid drug therapy","Axial spondyloarthritis","Clinical trial","Drug tapering","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Psoriatic arthritis","Rheumatoid arthritis","Spondylarthritis drug therapy","Treatment Outcome","Tumor Necrosis Factor alpha antagonists inhibitors","Tumour necrosis factor inhibitors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring tnfi drug levels and anti drug antibodies during tapering among patients with inflammatory arthritis secondary analyses from the randomised biodopt trial","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00296-024-05665-7","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by Aalborg University Hospital. This work was supported by: The Danish Regions Medicine Grants (16/2885), The Danish Rheumatism Association (R188-A6592), Manufacturer Vilhelm Pedersen and Wife\\u2019s Grant after recommendation from The Novo Nordisk Foundation (0060515), Aase and Ejnar Danielsen Grant (19-10-0285), The Health Science Research Fund of the North Denmark Region (2016-017615), an