{"abstract":"This chapter thoroughly introduces personas, the many domains it is used within, the different data collection methods, and the criticism. This chapter suggests a new process for persona creation and includes advice to practitioners and researchers who want to work with the approach. Moreover, this chapter introduces scenarios, journey maps, and storyboarding, which are viewed as methods that need to include personas to have a proper focus. Narrative theory and the use of storytelling in personas and scenarios/journeys/storyboards are described, and the relation between personas and characters and scenarios and plots are established. Finally, this chapter includes three talks on characters with scriptwriter Kevin Doyle, on persona practice with principal and UX practitioner Ilana Westerman, and on scenarios and narrative theory with Professor Austen Rainer.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776415"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"personas scenarios journey maps and storyboards","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85204855530","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776415","identifier":[{"id":"85204855530","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-74e6d7dd-ec57-49cf-bc74-4cec1b288d87"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-846A04AB8F53CA49B7846574D2B47C97"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Constantine","key":"stephanidispedh","last":"Stephanidis","name":"Stephanidis, Constantine","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gavriel","key":"salvendypedh","last":"Salvendy","name":"Salvendy, Gavriel","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003495161","eisbn":["9781003495161"],"pages":"71","place":"Boca Raton","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"User Experience Methods and Tools in Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-74e6d7dd-ec57-49cf-bc74-4cec1b288d87"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Personas, Scenarios, Journey Maps, and Storyboards","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776415","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Respiratory syncytial virus (RSV) and influenza cause significant health challenges, particularly for individuals with comorbid conditions and older adults. However, information on the clinical manifestations and outcomes of adults hospitalized with RSV in Europe remains limited. Methods: This multicenter observational cohort study of adults hospitalized with RSV or influenza A or B from March 2016 to April 2020 investigated the clinical manifestations, mortality risk factors, and association with 90-day mortality rates by logistic regression analysis after adjustment for covariates. Results: Of 988 patients hospitalized with either virus, 353 had RSV, 347 had influenza A, and 288 had influenza B infection. Patients with RSV, compared with those with influenza A or B, were more likely to have comorbid conditions (83% for RSV vs 72% for influenza A [P = .03] and 74% for influenza B [P = .001]) or pneumonia (41% vs 29% [P = .03] and 24% [P <. 001], respectively). After adjustment for covariates, RSV infection was associated with an increased all-cause mortality rate within 90 days compared with influenza B (odds ratio, 2.16 [95% confidence interval, 1.20-3.87]; P = .01) but not influenza A (1.38 [.84-2.29]; P = .21). Increasing age and present pneumonia were identified as independent mortality risk factors in patients with RSV. Conclusions: Older adults hospitalized with RSV infections are at a higher risk of dying within 90 days of hospitalization than patients admitted with influenza B but at a similar risk as those admitted with influenza A, emphasizing the detrimental effects and severity of older patients being infected with RSV. Our findings underscore the need for strategic testing and vaccination approaches to mitigate the impact of RSV among older adults.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Clausen, Clara Lundetoft","Egeskov-Cavling, Amanda Marie","Hayder, Noor","Sejdic, Adin","Roed, Casper","Gitz Holler, Jon","Nielsen, Lene","Eiberg, Mads Frederik","Rezahosseini, Omid","Østergaard, Christian","Harboe, Zitta Barrella","Fischer, Thea K.","Benfield, Thomas","Lindegaard, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777528"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ADULTS","Clinical epidemiology","Mortality","Respiratory infections","Respiratory syncytial virus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical manifestations and outcomes in adults hospitalized with respiratory syncytial virus and influenza a b a multicenter observational cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ofid/ofae513","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-777528","identifier":[{"id":"85207631399","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39411215","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11474596","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-42a3bdb1-ee45-4415-9136-d4be74f2d1f1"],"keyword":["adults","clinical epidemiology","mortality","respiratory infections","respiratory syncytial virus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F0189C00471CDB0623C40D7400758BB6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ofid/ofae513","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/411695165/ofae513.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Clara Lundetoft","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Clara Lundetoft","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Amanda Marie","key":"egeskovcavlingpau","last":"Egeskov-Cavling","name":"Egeskov-Cavling, Amanda Marie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Noor","key":"hayderpau","last":"Hayder","name":"Hayder, Noor","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adin","key":"sejdicpau","last":"Sejdic","name":"Sejdic, Adin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Casper","key":"roedpau","last":"Roed","locid":"3432c3fc-2d9a-4f77-b3cd-fa54a8352fb0","name":"Roed, Casper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon","key":"gitzhollerpau","last":"Gitz Holler","name":"Gitz Holler, Jon","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Frederik","key":"eibergpau","last":"Eiberg","name":"Eiberg, Mads Frederik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Omid","key":"rezahosseinipau","last":"Rezahosseini","name":"Rezahosseini, Omid","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christian","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","name":"Østergaard, Christian","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Zitta Barrella","key":"harboepau","last":"Harboe","locid":"2b596a33-5659-4236-b5ea-c0991866af44","name":"Harboe, Zitta Barrella","orcid":"0000-0001-5552-0095","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Thea K.","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"97c4bf8d-8bd1-470b-8e0b-91eb4faf7703","name":"Fischer, Thea K.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"benfieldpau","last":"Benfield","name":"Benfield, Thomas","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Birgitte","key":"lindegaardpau","last":"Lindegaard","locid":"f8c3a235-1f94-4c1d-afe3-c6c7f9b31002","name":"Lindegaard, Birgitte","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39411215"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ofid/ofae513","issn":["23288957"],"issue":"10","journal":"Open Forum Infectious Diseases","paperid":"ofae513","status":"p","title":"Open Forum Infectious Diseases","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207631399"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-42a3bdb1-ee45-4415-9136-d4be74f2d1f1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Clinical Manifestations and Outcomes in Adults Hospitalized With Respiratory Syncytial Virus and Influenza a/B : A Multicenter Observational Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777528","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Insulin resistance impairs the cellular insulin response, and often precedes metabolic disorders, like type 2 diabetes, impacting an increasing number of people globally. Understanding the molecular mechanisms in hepatic insulin resistance is essential for early preventive treatments. To elucidate changes in insulin signal transduction associated with hepatocellular resistance, we employed a multi-layered mass spectrometry-based proteomics approach focused on insulin receptor (IR) signaling at the interactome, phosphoproteome, and proteome levels in a long-term hyperinsulinemia-induced insulin-resistant HepG2 cell line with a knockout of the insulin-like growth factor 1 receptor (IGF1R KO). The analysis revealed insulin-stimulated recruitment of the PI3K complex in both insulin-sensitive and -resistant cells. Phosphoproteomics showed attenuated signaling via the metabolic PI3K-AKT pathway but sustained extracellular signal-regulated kinase (ERK) activity in insulin-resistant cells. At the proteome level, the ephrin type-A receptor 2 (EphA2) showed an insulin-induced increase in expression, which occurred through the ERK signaling pathway and was concordantly independent of insulin resistance. Induction of EphA2 by insulin was confirmed in additional cell lines and observed uniquely in cells with high IR-to-IGF1R ratio. The multi-layered proteomics dataset provided insights into insulin signaling, serving as a resource to generate and test hypotheses, leading to an improved understanding of insulin resistance.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Sarah Hyllekvist","Emdal, Kristina B","Pedersen, Anna-Kathrine","Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","Kildegaard, Helene Faustrup","Demozay, Damien","Pedersen, Thomas Åskov","Grønborg, Mads","Slaaby, Rita","Nielsen, Peter Kresten","Olsen, Jesper V."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-778989"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multi layered proteomics identifies insulin induced upregulation of the epha000000000002 receptor via the erk pathway which is dependent on low igf000000000001r level","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-77817-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-778989","identifier":[{"id":"39572596","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11582730","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85209743902","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c49d08de-2bc8-4e16-990c-f5673e9fbaf9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9357CFFE2AE4C709BA2718C0581726A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-77817-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/414440128/s41598_024_77817_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Olsen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Sarah Hyllekvist","key":"jørgensensarahhyllekvistpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"71f04b19-9dbf-46e4-98e8-946aa0a4173f","name":"Jørgensen, Sarah Hyllekvist","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina Bennet","key":"emdalkristinabpau","last":"Emdal","locid":"3572a14b-cc9b-4db0-9c0f-245e1fe18118","name":"Emdal, Kristina B","name_org":"Emdal, Kristina Bennet","orcid":"0000-0002-9789-0665","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Kathrine","key":"pedersenannakathrinepau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e50fa07a-adf6-4b6c-8c00-8a59742d2bc7","name":"Pedersen, Anna-Kathrine","name_org":"Pedersen, Anna Kathrine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene Nygaard","key":"axelsenlenenygaardpau","last":"Axelsen","name":"Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helene Faustrup","key":"kildegaardhelenefaustruppau","last":"Kildegaard","name":"Kildegaard, Helene Faustrup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Damien","key":"demozaydamienpau","last":"Demozay","name":"Demozay, Damien","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas Åskov","key":"pedersenthomasåskovpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Thomas Åskov","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mads","key":"grønborgmadspau","last":"Grønborg","name":"Grønborg, Mads","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rita","key":"slaabyritapau","last":"Slaaby","name":"Slaaby, Rita","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter Kresten","key":"nielsenpeterkrestenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Peter Kresten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Velgaard","key":"olsenjespervpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"16f5cd56-244f-4fe8-bebd-13ee7bd17822","name":"Olsen, Jesper V.","name_org":"Olsen, Jesper Velgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-4747-4938","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39572596"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-024-77817-5","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"28856","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209743902"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c49d08de-2bc8-4e16-990c-f5673e9fbaf9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multi-layered proteomics identifies insulin-induced upregulation of the EphA2 receptor via the ERK pathway which is dependent on low IGF1R level","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-778989","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: With decreasing number of hospital beds, more citizens are discharged to temporary care at skilled nursing facilities, requiring increasingly complex care in a non-hospital setting. We mapped challenges related to the transition of citizens from hospital to temporary care at a skilled nursing facility in relation to medication management, responsibility of medical treatment, and communication. Methods: Descriptive study of citizens discharged from Odense University Hospital to temporary care from May 2022 to March 2023. Results: We included 209 citizens (53% women, median age 81 years). Most citizens (97%; n = 109/112) had their medication changed during hospital admission. Citizens used a median of eight medications, including risk medications (96%, n = 108). Medication-related challenges occurred for 37% (n = 77) of citizens and most often concerned missing alignment of medication records. Half of citizens (47%, n = 99) moved into temporary care with all medication needed for further dispensing. Nurses conducted in median three telephone calls (interquartile range [IQR 1–4]) and sent in median two correspondences (IQR 1–3) per citizen within the first 5 days. Nurses most often called the hospital physician (41% of telephone calls, n = 265/643) and sent correspondences to the general practitioner (55% of correspondences, n = 257/469). For 31% (n = 29/95) of citizens requiring action from nursing staff, this could have been avoided if the nurses had had access to the discharge letter. Conclusion: We identified several challenges related to the transition of patients from hospital to temporary care, most often related to medication. A third of actions related to medication management were considered avoidable with improved practices around communication.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","Bjørk, Emma","Nielsen, Marianne","Galsgaard, Stine","Pottegård, Anton","Lundby, Carina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-782952"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Communication","Continuity of care","Female","Humans","Male","Medication management","Multimorbidity","Patient Discharge statistics numerical data","Patient Transfer statistics numerical data","Skilled nursing facilities","Transitional care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenges related to transitioning from hospital to temporary care at a skilled nursing facility a descriptive study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-024-01003-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-782952","identifier":[{"id":"38878222","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85196022561","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11377456","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-3532ae07-b2d5-4b77-a472-f748b19b50a3"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Communication","Continuity of care","Female","Humans","Male","Medication management","Multimorbidity","Patient Discharge/statistics & numerical data","Patient Transfer/statistics & numerical data","Skilled Nursing Facilities","Skilled nursing facility","Transitional Care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A507A1F581313C508BCECC974E8260A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41999-024-01003-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/276852479/s41999-024-01003-z.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","