{"abstract":"The original version of this Article contained a repeated error, where the pressure unit was incorrectly given as ‘mbar’ instead of ‘mmHg’. In the Results and discussion section, under the subheading ‘Intra-catheter pressure’, “The average pressure variation for Brand A was − 364 ± 42 mbar, − 248 ± 81 mbar for Brand B and − 272 ± 59 mbar for Brand C at 20 cmH2O. When the abdominal pressure was adjusted to 50 cmH2O, the average pressure for Brand A was − 383 ± 50 mbar, − 323 ± 47 mbar for Brand B and − 330 ± 93 mbar for Brand C.” now reads: “The average pressure variation for Brand A was − 364 ± 42 mmHg, − 248 ± 81 mmHg for Brand B and − 272 ± 59 mmHg for Brand C at 20 cmH2O. When the abdominal pressure was adjusted to 50 cmH2O, the average pressure for Brand A was − 383 ± 50 mmHg, − 323 ± 47 mmHg for Brand B and − 330 ± 93 mmHg for Brand C.” Additionally, “The measured intra-catheter pressure variation for Brand B at 20 cmH 2O was equal to − 296 ± 56 mbar (N = 9, SD) for the tests where mucosal suction was perceived by the operator. Conversely, the intra-catheter pressure variation that could be measured at the first flow-stop for Brand B at 20 cmH2O when mucosal suction was not detected by the operator was equal to − 180 ± 64 mbar (N = 6, SD). A similar scenario was seen for Brand C at 50 cmH 2O, where the measured intra-catheter pressure variation was equal to − 373 ± 62 mbar (N = 11, SD) when mucosal suction was perceived by the operator, and to − 212 ± 45 mbar (N = 4, SD) when mucosal suction was not perceived by the operator.” now reads: “The measured intra-catheter pressure variation for Brand B at 20 cmH 2O was equal to − 296 ± 56 mmHg (N = 9, SD) for the tests where mucosal suction was perceived by the operator. Conversely, the intra-catheter pressure variation that could be measured at the first flow-stop for Brand B at 20 cmH2O when mucosal suction was not detected by the operator was equal to − 180 ± 64 mmHg (N = 6, SD). A similar scenario was seen for Brand C at 50 cmH 2O, where the measured intra-catheter pressure variation was equal to − 373 ± 62 mmHg (N = 11, SD) when mucosal suction was perceived by the operator, and to − 212 ± 45 mmHg (N = 4, SD) when mucosal suction was not perceived by the operator.” Furthermore, “What remains to be understood is whether a pressure variation of, for example − 250 mbar, is sufficient to cause discomfort to the IC users, or even cause microtraumas to the bladder mucosa, and if the speed at which the peak is generated has any relevance.” now reads: “What remains to be understood is whether a pressure variation of, for example − 250 mmHg, is sufficient to cause discomfort to the IC users, or even cause microtraumas to the bladder mucosa, and if the speed at which the peak is generated has any relevance.” Under the subheading ‘In-vivo animal studies’ of the same section, “During bladder emptying, the pressure difference at first flowstop was equal to − 96 mbar (Fig. 15).” now reads: “During bladder emptying, the pressure difference at first flowstop was equal to − 96 mmHg (Fig. 15).” Finally, the error was also present in Table 1 and in Figures 10, 11, 12, 13 and 15. The correct and incorrect values of Table 1 appear below. Table 1 Incorrect: (Table presented.) Correct: (Table presented.) The original Figures 10, 11, 12, 13 and 15, and accompanying legends appear below. The original Article has been corrected.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Tentor, Fabio","Grønholt Schrøder, Brit","Nielsen, Simon","Schertiger, Lars","Stærk, Kristian","Andersen, Thomas Emil","Bagi, Per","Feldskov Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671922"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COLO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-COLO","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"erratum author correction development of an ex vivo porcine lower urinary tract model to evaluate the performance of urinary catheters scientific reports 000000002022 000000000012 000000000001 000000017818","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-32920-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-671922","identifier":[{"id":"37081107","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85153687248","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10119277","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-e3a42baa-ec6d-42a4-b3a9-40454b932c18"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD09B342BDD8738AF0015F6429FBD5CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/228919626/s41598_023_32920_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-32920-x","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"coloplast","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COLO","l3nl":"Coloplast Group","l3nn":"Coloplast","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Coloplast","namevar":["Coloplast A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COLO","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Microbiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"tentorpau","last":"Tentor","name":"Tentor, Fabio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit","key":"grønholtschrøderpau","last":"Grønholt Schrøder","name":"Grønholt Schrøder, Brit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Simon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"schertigerpau","last":"Schertiger","name":"Schertiger, Lars","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"stærkpau","last":"Stærk","locid":"0e1429ba-881e-4a1a-b489-bdfbbaae2599","name":"Stærk, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-2410-0375","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"emilandersenpau","last":"Emil Andersen","locid":"87fae7cd-ed6a-4d21-80cc-e13da9f91099","name":"Andersen, Thomas Emil","name_org":"Emil Andersen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-9453-1141","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"bagipau","last":"Bagi","name":"Bagi, Per","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"feldskovnielsenpau","last":"Feldskov Nielsen","name":"Feldskov Nielsen, Lene","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37081107"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-023-32920-x","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"6443","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153687248"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Coloplast Group","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e3a42baa-ec6d-42a4-b3a9-40454b932c18"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Erratum : Author Correction: Development of an ex-vivo porcine lower urinary tract model to evaluate the performance of urinary catheters (Scientific reports (2022) 12 1 (17818))","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671922","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Paludiculture can be a tool to incentivise rewetting of agricultural peatlands with the option for biomass utilisation in green protein biorefineries. However, the economic feasibility for green protein paludiculture depends on product maximisation. This study explored the potential of a ratio vegetation index (RVI) model, with inclusion of climatic factors relevant for biomass growth, to predict crude protein (CP) contents in green protein precipitates from biorefining Phalaris arundinacea and Festuca arundinacea cultivated under different management intensities on a wet fen. Assessing yields for two years of cultivation, we found that timing of harvest was a key variable for CP extractability using the biorefinery technique. Biomass and protein yields were similar between management treatments and years, but extractability was enhanced in the dryer of the two years. This study highlighted the potential of an RVI model to predict, under varying climatic conditions, CP contents in the protein precipitate with good model performance (R 2 = 0.64, NRMSE = 0.23) and accuracy. In 92 % of occurrences, the model was able to predict statistically similar CP contents compared to measured CP in the protein product, with an average deviation between measured and predicted annual values of 1.7 % across species and management intensities. The findings highlight an option for maximising the overall efficiency of green protein paludiculture by determining the optimal timing of harvest, thereby demonstrating an economic potential to incentivise paludiculture farming.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Claudia","Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Lene","Jørgensen, Uffe","Lærke, Poul Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-675086"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Claudia"],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Fen","Festuca arundinacea","Peatland","Phalaris arundinacea"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ratio vegetation indices have the potential to predict extractable protein yields in green protein paludiculture","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.19189/MaP.2022.OMB.Sc.1883464","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-675086","identifier":[{"id":"85159103980","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-69a2d79c-990b-454f-9661-7252e80adc71"],"keyword":["Festuca arundinacea","Phalaris arundinacea","biorefinery","fen","peatland"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9C6F6BA99D0705C896E76C8BF6DCA61C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.19189/MaP.2022.OMB.Sc.1883464","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Climate and Water","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Soil Physics and Hydropedology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claudia","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"66d68122-06cf-4e2c-9f01-b6df8fdecb1c","name":"Nielsen, Claudia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"stødkildejørgensenpau","last":"Stødkilde-Jørgensen","locid":"7edb699b-a75e-48cd-a351-9ee9e1321d4d","name":"Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0001-9434-0118","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uffe","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"efa7e924-c197-4060-8904-110cf0a30837","name":"Jørgensen, Uffe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Poul Erik","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"03fcd9e2-3402-466b-86fc-f3c8163d9306","name":"Lærke, Poul Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-2224-3893","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.19189/map.2022.omb.sc.1883464","issn":["1819754X"],"journal":"Mires and Peat","paperid":"10","publisher":"The International Mire Conservation Group (IMCG)","status":"p","title":"Mires and Peat","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159103980"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-69a2d79c-990b-454f-9661-7252e80adc71"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Ratio vegetation indices have the potential to predict extractable protein yields in green protein paludiculture","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-675086","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The realisation of recovery as an overarching goal of mental health care services has proven difficult to achieve in practice. At present, concepts of recovery are contested and unclear, which affects their implementation in psychiatric practices. We examined social psychiatric policies about recovery with the aim to explore their underlying assumptions about recovery. Relevant texts from the policies' knowledge bases were subjected to reflexive thematic analysis. We developed a central theme: \"A clinical standardisation of the concept of recovery\". The theme involved meaning clusters that encompassed conflicting and commonly shared assumptions about recovery across the text corpus. We discussed the findings from discourse analytical and governmentality perspectives. In conclusion, the policies' aim of providing clarity about recovery was circumvented by the very knowledge bases used to support their endeavours.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Jacob M","Buus, Niels","Berring, Lene Lauge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-685502"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Jacob M"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Monash University"],"keyword":["Humans","Mental Disorders therapy","Mental Health Recovery","Mental Health Services","Public policy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mental health recovery in social psychiatric policies a reflexive thematic analysis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph20126094","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S