{"abstract":"European ash, Fraxinus excelsior is facing the double threat of ongoing devastation by the invasive fungal pathogen, Hymenoscyphus fraxineus and the imminent arrival of the non-native emerald ash borer (EAB), Agrilus planipennis. The spread of EAB which is currently moving westwards from European Russia and Ukraine into central Europe, poses an additional substantial threat to European ash, F. excelsior. While the molecular basis for resistance or variation in resistance among European ash genotypes is heavily investigated, comparatively little is known about the molecular ash traits involved in resistance against EAB. In this study we have gathered transcriptomic data from EAB inoculated genotypes of F. excelsior that have previously shown different levels of susceptibility to EAB. Resultant datasets show differential gene expression in susceptible and resistant genotypes in response to EAB infestation. This data will provide important information on the molecular basis of resistance to the EAB and allow the development of management plans to combat a pending threat of a culturally and ecologically important European tree species.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Doonan, James","Kosawang, Chatchai","Eisenring, Michael","Ladd, Tim","Roe, Amanda D.","Budde, Katharina B.","Jørgensen, Hans Jørgen Lyngs","Queloz, Valentin","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Gossner, Martin M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695543"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Germany","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ETH Zürich","Natural Resources Canada","Swiss Federal Institute for Forest, Snow and Landscape Research","University of Göttingen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transcriptome profiling of i fraxinus excelsior i genotypes infested by emerald ash borer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02588-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695543","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10556020","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85173328780","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37798274","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-234b46fb-6fbe-40f4-8b2d-a30a09ee821a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C950FC1E61406420B0FC7F331A9B2713"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/369257154/s41597_023_02588_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02588-z","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Forest and Landscape Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute for forest snow and landscape research","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute for Forest, Snow and Landscape Research","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"natural resources canada","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Natural Resources Canada","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of göttingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Göttingen","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"James","key":"doonanpau","last":"Doonan","locid":"c05913af-39d1-4b2f-93f0-94af8789b4f2","name":"Doonan, James","orcid":"0000-0002-0523-5808","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chatchai","key":"kosawangpau","last":"Kosawang","locid":"1b69b056-6473-427b-81f9-20fbd6797849","name":"Kosawang, Chatchai","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"eisenringpau","last":"Eisenring","name":"Eisenring, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tim","key":"laddpau","last":"Ladd","name":"Ladd, Tim","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Amanda D.","key":"roepau","last":"Roe","name":"Roe, Amanda D.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Katharina B.","key":"buddepau","last":"Budde","name":"Budde, Katharina B.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans Jørgen Lyngs","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"1b3f39b0-a166-4a0c-96ea-e6c3dd0de338","name":"Jørgensen, Hans Jørgen Lyngs","orcid":"0000-0002-5902-6550","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Valentin","key":"quelozpau","last":"Queloz","name":"Queloz, Valentin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","first":"Martin M.","key":"gossnerpau","last":"Gossner","name":"Gossner, Martin M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37798274"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41597-023-02588-z","issn":["20524463"],"issue":"680","journal":"Scientific Data","paperid":"680","status":"p","title":"Scientific Data","title_org":"Scientific data","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173328780"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-234b46fb-6fbe-40f4-8b2d-a30a09ee821a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transcriptome profiling of <i>Fraxinus excelsior</i> genotypes infested by emerald ash borer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695543","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Urinary tract infections (UTIs) are one of the most common bacterial infections worldwide. The diagnosis is mainly dependent on the quantitative identification of uropathogens in urine from suspected patients and therefore, it is essential that bacterial count in urine specimens accurately reflects the bacterial population inside the bladder. In this study, we collected the first- and last urine specimens during a single full voiding from pigs with experimentally induced UTI and compared the urine density and bacterial counts of the collected specimens. We found that specimens from the same voiding varied in density and in bacterial counts by up to a thousand-fold with significant impact on diagnostic sensitivity. In conclusion, the porcine bladder can simultaneously contain intravesical compartments of varying density and bacterial counts that greatly influences microbiological analysis. The distribution of bacteria in intravesical compartments is critical to consider when using pigs as biomedical models of UTI. Furthermore, the similarities of porcine and human anatomy and physiology, suggest that the results are likely to be translatable to human, in which case potential UTIs could be overlooked by today’s diagnostic procedures.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Stærk, Kristian","Langhorn, Louise","Feldskov Nielsen, Lene","Andersen, Thomas Emil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713523"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Stærk, Kristian"],"keyword":["Large animal model","Pig","Swine","Urinary Bladder","Urinary tract infection UTI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COLO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COLO","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intravesical compartments in the bladder can affect microbiological culturing outcome an experimental study in pigs","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fruro.2022.1028778","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-713523","identifier":[{"id":"85183835496","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-01641373-ee6c-476e-a590-8261ba9b3d74"],"keyword":["large animal model","pig","swine","urinary bladder","urinary tract infection (UTI)","urine dipstick test","uropathogenic escherichia coli (UPEC)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-228CE0C3589B6D3540255BAECA4F3D49"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fruro.2022.1028778","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/245977714/fruro_02_1028778.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Microbiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"coloplast","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COLO","l3nl":"Coloplast Group","l3nn":"Coloplast","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Coloplast","namevar":["Coloplast A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COLO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"stærkpau","last":"Stærk","locid":"0e1429ba-881e-4a1a-b489-bdfbbaae2599","name":"Stærk, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-2410-0375","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"langhornpau","last":"Langhorn","locid":"6edd2d76-1416-4d4a-a33f-28c5108f4b87","name":"Langhorn, Louise","orcid":"0000-0001-5787-1120","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"feldskovnielsenpau","last":"Feldskov Nielsen","name":"Feldskov Nielsen, Lene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Emil","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"87fae7cd-ed6a-4d21-80cc-e13da9f91099","name":"Andersen, Thomas Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-9453-1141","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fruro.2022.1028778","issn":["26739828"],"journal":"Frontiers in Urology","paperid":"1028778","publisher":"Frontiers","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Urology","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85183835496"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Coloplast Group","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-01641373-ee6c-476e-a590-8261ba9b3d74"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Intravesical compartments in the bladder can affect microbiological culturing outcome: An experimental study in pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713523","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
