637b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Resilience of European ash forests influenced by ash dieback","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-720239","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"There is a call for more students to continue into computer science (CS), but as many leave their studies before completing, there is a potential in retaining students rather than focusing on recruitment alone. The retention literature proposes ‘sense of belonging’ as a key concept. This paper contributes with nuancing how sense of belonging is shaped differently within different spaces at the same CS study-programme, by drawing on narrative interviews and ethnographic fieldwork with BA-students, analysed through a spatial analytic lens. By applying the metaphors of a solar system and force fields, we investigate how sense of belonging was constructed within relational spaces and students’ identity-negotiations within them. Three spaces are found: The study-lounge (the epicenter of the solar system), the pulsating planet, and the distant isolated planet. Conclusions show how the epicenter are enforced by teaching and learning activities, and how broadening what counts hold potential to retain students.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holmegaard, Henriette Tolstrup","Madsen, Lene Møller","Nielsen, Katia Bill"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720934"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer science identities","Narrative interviews","Relational space","Sense of belonging"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"you have to ask the right questions a spatial analysis of the sense of belonging within higher education computer science","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-720934","identifier":[{"id":"85169898054","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-841f2d41-146a-4307-9f38-734c4575882c"],"keyword":["Computer science identities","celebrated identities","narrative interviews","relational space","sense of belonging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7C2A6F6DD4151FEC19340176FE008F7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Equity in Science Education","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, University Science Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henriette Tolstrup","key":"holmegaardpau","last":"Holmegaard","locid":"bc622573-dbe6-4d64-ace0-6fe07399c353","name":"Holmegaard, Henriette Tolstrup","orcid":"0000-0003-4245-3983","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Lene Møller","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"dda148da-5b6d-4f4e-ab60-b7cf85637829","name":"Madsen, Lene Møller","orcid":"0000-0001-7149-9142","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katia Bill","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"777255e6-39f6-474e-bda0-17da98814463","name":"Nielsen, Katia Bill","orcid":"0000-0002-7653-8646","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/03043797.2023.2254289","issn":["03043797","14695898"],"issn_org":["03043797"],"issue":"6","journal":"European Journal of Engineering Education","pages":"1037-1050","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Engineering Education","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85169898054"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-841f2d41-146a-4307-9f38-734c4575882c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"‘You have to ask the right questions' : a spatial analysis of the sense of belonging within higher education computer science","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-720934","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Vaccination is an evidence-based strategy to prevent or reduce the severity of infectious diseases (ID). Here, we aimed to describe the experience of implementing a vaccination clinic specifically targeting liver, heart, lung, and combined dual organ transplantation at a single transplantation center in Denmark. In this cohort of 242 solid organ transplant (SOT) candidates, we investigated seroprotection and the proportion of recommended vaccinations documented before transplantation. Furthermore, we registered completed vaccinations after ID consultations. The median age in our cohort was 53 years (IQR, 42–60), 60% were males (n = 135), and liver transplants (n = 138; 57%) were the most frequently planned organ transplants. Before the consultation to the vaccination clinic, influenza and pneumococcal vaccines had the highest proportion of documented vaccination (58% and 37%, respectively). Serological protection was more frequently observed for measles, mumps, or rubella (MMR, approximately 90% for each), while only 30% (n = 72) of SOT candidates showed seroprotection against pneumococcal disease. All SOT candidates required at least one of the recommended vaccines, and over 90% required three or more. At least 10% of patients in our cohort needed a live attenuated vaccine for either MMR or yellow fever. The most frequently administered vaccine was the tetanus–diphtheria-acelullar pertussis (Tdap) booster (n = 217; 90%), influenza vaccination was either administered (n = 16; 7%) or recommended (n = 226; 93%), PCV13 was administered (n = 155; 64%) or recommended (n = 27; 11%), and PPSV23 was either administered (n = 18; 7.4%) or recommended (n = 140; 58%). All SOT candidates adhered completely to their vaccination schedules. Based on our findings, we recommend prioritizing vaccination before transplantation by providing ID consultations for SOT candidates.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Harboe, Zitta Barrella","Hald, Annemette","Ekenberg, Christina","Ete Wareham, Neval","Fogt Lundbo, Lene","Holler, Jon Gitz","Qvist, Tavs","Rask Hamm, Sebastian","Bjerrum, Stephanie","Rezahosseini, Omid","Suno Krohn, Paul","Gustafsson, Finn","Perch, Michael","Rasmussen, Allan","Nielsen, Susanne Dam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721621"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"implementation of a vaccination clinic for adult solid organ transplant candidates a single center experience","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vaccine.2023.09.036","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721621","identifier":[{"id":"37775467","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85173835742","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b67af574-6831-4a9f-a85d-7d463b7c5695"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-33A5F3AAAEBCB1A3A648FFD442810E03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379045330/1_s2.0_S0264410X23011064_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vaccine.2023.09.036","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: infection medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet","Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Zitta Barrella","key":"harboepau","last":"Harboe","locid":"2b596a33-5659-4236-b5ea-c0991866af44","name":"Harboe, Zitta Barrella","orcid":"0000-0001-5552-0095","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Annemette","key":"haldpau","last":"Hald","name":"Hald, Annemette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"ekenbergpau","last":"Ekenberg","name":"Ekenberg, Christina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Neval","key":"etewarehampau","last":"Ete Wareham","name":"Ete Wareham, Neval","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"fogtlundbopau","last":"Fogt Lundbo","name":"Fogt Lundbo, Lene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jon Gitz","key":"hollerpau","last":"Holler","name":"Holler, Jon Gitz","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tavs","key":"qvistpau","last":"Qvist","name":"Qvist, Tavs","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sebastian","key":"raskhammpau","last":"Rask Hamm","name":"Rask Hamm, Sebastian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Stephanie","key":"bjerrumpau","last":"Bjerrum","name":"Bjerrum, Stephanie","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Omid","key":"rezahosseinipau","last":"Rezahosseini","name":"Rezahosseini, Omid","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Paul","key":"sunokrohnpau","last":"Suno Krohn","name":"Suno Krohn, Paul","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Finn","key":"gustafssonpau","last":"Gustafsson","locid":"6716eef1-891b-4209-a823-e96e765b9433","name":"Gustafsson, Finn","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Michael","key":"perchpau","last":"Perch","locid":"e0a136a6-8b36-4735-9db2-8847ce581fc6","name":"Perch, Michael","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Allan","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Allan","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Susanne","key":"damnielsenpau","last":"Dam Nielsen","locid":"2baa36fa-2709-482a-9595-52c5b9537801","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","name_org":"Dam Nielsen, Susanne","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37775467"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vaccine.2023.09.036","issn":["0264410X","13552732"],"issn_org":["0264410X"],"issue":"45","journal":"Vaccine","pages":"6637-6644","status":"p","title":"Vaccine","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173835742"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b67af574-6831-4a9f-a85d-7d463b7c5695"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Implementation of a vaccination clinic for adult solid organ transplant candidates : A single-center experience","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-721621","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: While outcomes of posterior cruciate ligament (PCL) injuries treated surgically are well described, prospective studies reporting outcomes of exercise interventions are lacking. Purpose: The purpose of this study was to investigate changes in patient-reported outcomes of a physiotherapy-led exercise and support brace intervention in patients with acute injury of the PCL over a two-year follow-up period. Furthermore, this study sought to investigate changes in isometric knee muscle strength over an eight-month follow-up period, and finally to report conversion to surgical reconstruction over a two-year follow-up period. Study design: Case series study, prospective. Methods: Fifty patients with an acute injury of the PCL were treated with a brace and a physiotherapy-led exercise intervention and followed prospectively. Changes in patient-reported outcomes were measured with the International Knee Documentation Committee Subjective Knee Form (IKDC-SKF) and the Knee injury and Osteoarthritis Outcome Score (KOOS) from baseline (diagnosis) to two-year follow-up. Furthermore, changes in isometric knee flexion and extension strength were measured with a static strength dynamometer from 16 weeks after diagnosis to one-year follow-up. Conversion to surgery was prospectively extracted from medical records. Mean changes were analyzed with a mixed effects model with time as a fixed factor. Results: The IKDC-SKF score improved 28 (95%CI 24-33) IKDC points from baseline to two-year follow-up. Isometric knee flexion strength of the injured knee increased 0.18 (95%CI 0.11-0.25) Nm/kg from 16 weeks after diagnosis to one-year follow-up, corresponding to an increase of 16%. In contrast, isometric knee extension strength of the injured knee did not change (0.12 (95%CI 0.00-0.24) Nm/kg, p=0.042). Over two years, seven patients converted to PCL surgical reconstruction. One and two-year follow-up were completed by 46 and 31 patients, respectively. Conclusions: The physiotherapy-led exercise and support brace intervention demonstrated clinically relevant improvements in patient-reported outcomes and knee flexion strength, and the risk of PCL surgical reconstruction was considered low within the first two years.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Randi","Jacobsen, Julie Sandell","Blaabjerg, Birgitte","Nielsen, Torsten Grønbech","Miller, Lene Lindberg","Lind, Martin"],"cuid":["S02-098.87-681376"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Randi"],"keyword":["Exercise","Knee strength","PCL","Physiotherapy","Posterior cruciate ligament","disease health science and nursing"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient reported outcomes and muscle strength after a physiotherapy led exercise and support brace intervention in patients with acute injury of the posterior cruciate ligament a two year follow up study","src":["au","via"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.26603/001c.83214","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.87-681376","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10399121","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85166761418","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37547839","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-5e2e0099-231e-45bc-b914-e5706f68a656","via-e6c41c90-a85b-4486-8550-33fbd9840303"],"keyword":["Exercise","Knee strength","PCL","Physiotherapy","disease, health science and nursing","posterior cruciate ligament"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0CCCEE5742C59CCDD3EDC0CDED2718EC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.26603/001c.83214","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Physiotherapy and Occupational Therapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus Univeristy Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Sundhed og velfærdsteknologi","VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Sundhed og velfærdsteknologi, Programme in Rehabilitation","VIA, Uddannelser, Sundhedsuddannelserne, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen Aarhus N"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Randi Gram","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"8e88c4c2-b2ae-4b2f-b47d-f56a528634a0","name":"Rasmussen, Randi","name_org":"Rasmussen, Randi Gram","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie Sandell","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"b0f635e7-61e3-4f91-8692-81571d884a22","name":"Jacobsen, Julie Sandell","orcid":"0000-0002-3323-3631","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"879dd69d-e359-458b-a6a1-1c42f6149882","name":"Blaabjerg, Birgitte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten Gronbech","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"33da3303-c376-4195-b3d6-7767956a26fe","name":"Nielsen, Torsten Grønbech","name_org":"Nielsen, Torsten Gronbech","orcid":"0000-0001-5354-1781","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Lindberg","key":"millerpau","last":"Miller","locid":"7e1b0171-af03-47af-bf29-00daeab6a85c","name":"Miller, Lene Lindberg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"lindpau","last":"Lind","locid":"5a1298e3-a4d7-4818-88f4-da6cdbf1784d","name":"Lind, Martin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37547839"],"pub":{"doi":"10.26603/001c.83214","issn":["15586162","21592896"],"issn_org":["21592896"],"issue":"4","journal":"International Journal of Sports Physical Therapy","pages":"807-819","publisher":"American Physical Therapy Association, Sports Physical Therapy Section","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Sports Physical Therapy","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85166761418"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5e2e0099-231e-45bc-b914-e5706f68a656","via-e6c41c90-a85b-4486-8550-33fbd9840303"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","VIA University College"],"title":"Patient-reported Outcomes and Muscle Strength after a Physiotherapy-led Exercise and Support Brace Intervention in Patients with Acute Injury of the Posterior Cruciate Ligament: A Two-year Follow-up Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.87-681376","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background Hop performance evaluation in children after anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) reconstruction may benefit from comparison to healthy controls. Thus, the purpose was to investigate the hop performance in children one year after ACL reconstruction with a comparison to healthy controls. Methods Hop performance data from children with ACL reconstruction one year post-surgery and healthy children were compared. Four one-legged hop test data were analyzed: 1) single hop (SH), 2) 6 m timed hop (6 m-timed), 3) triple hop (TH), and 4) cross-over hop (COH). Outcomes were the best result (longest/fastest hop) from each leg and limb asymmetry. Differences in hop performance between-limbs (operated versus non-operated) and between-groups were estimated. Results 98 children with ACL reconstruction and 290 healthy children were included. Few statistically significant group differences were observed. Girls with ACL reconstruction outperformed healthy controls in two tests on the operated leg SH, COH) and in three tests on the non-operated leg (SH, TH, COH). However, the girls performed 4–5% worse on the operated leg when compared to the non-operated leg in all hop tests. No statistically significant between-group differences in the limb asymmetry were found. Conclusion The hop performance in children with ACL reconstruction one year post-surgery was largely comparable to the level of healthy controls. Despite this, we cannot exclude that neuromuscular deficits exist among the children with ACL reconstruction. The inclusion of a healthy control group for evaluating hop performance evoked complex findings regarding the ACL reconstructed girls. Thus, they may represent a selected group.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Alkjær, Tine","Zebis, Mette Kreutzfeldt","Herzog, R.B.","Lundgaard-Nielsen, M.","Skovgaard, Lene Theil","Krogsgaard, Michael Rindom","Warming, S."],"cuid":["S02-099.92-039465"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Alkjaer, T."],"keyword":["ACL","Children","Knee","Performance","Reconstruction","Rehabilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of hop performance in children with anterior cruciate ligament reconstruction using healthy reference data a cross sectional study","src":["kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.knee.2023.02.007","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.92-039465","identifier":[{"id":"36863117","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85149187096","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kp-d39d8024-68f8-4cf9-a6fb-af74c12e5e40","ku-47b252ec-e67b-4e8d-b66c-91d826482a65"],"keyword":["ACL","Children","Knee","Performance","Reconstruction","Rehabilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2585B9F705BB4347C1E3DBB88526DF37"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.knee.2023.02.007","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/337780420/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Exercise and Muscle"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for sundhedsuddannelser - Dekan, ITJ Forskning og udvikling","Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for sundhedsuddannelser - Dekan, Inst. for Terapeut- og Jordemoderudd. - Inst.chef","Sundhed for børn og voksne – Institut for Terapeut og Jordemoderuddannelser, Arbejdsliv - Bedre forebyggelse og behandling af skader og sygdomme der påvirker arbejdsevnen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"T.","key":"alkjaerpau","last":"Alkjaer","locid":"d0ff1f22-b755-48d5-b5c9-94a9ef4367ac","name":"Alkjær, Tine","name_org":"Alkjaer, T.","orcid":"0000-0002-9105-3882","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 3","first":"M.K.","key":"zebispau","last":"Zebis","locid":"9a8ea147-c7b8-4ebb-a1ed-3a0ec12f9b9b","name":"Zebis, Mette Kreutzfeldt","name_org":"Zebis, M.K.","orcid":"0000-0001-5301-3241","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"R.B.","key":"herzogpau","last":"Herzog","name":"Herzog, R.B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"M.","key":"lundgaardnielsenpau","last":"Lundgaard-Nielsen","name":"Lundgaard-Nielsen, M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"L.T.","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"10dc01f7-6427-497e-bad6-fb5f5b3c6a70","name":"Skovgaard, Lene Theil","name_org":"Skovgaard, L.T.","orcid":"0000-0002-4708-4948","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"M.R.","key":"krogsgaardpau","last":"Krogsgaard","locid":"f704dca0-ca86-405a-a7f2-cce1f75f6b8f","name":"Krogsgaard, Michael Rindom","name_org":"Krogsgaard, M.R.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"S.","key":"warmingpau","last":"Warming","name":"Warming, S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36863117"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.knee.2023.02.007","issn":["09680160","18735800"],"issn_org":["09680160"],"journal":"The Knee","pages":"19-27","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"The Knee","title_org":"Knee","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149187096"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-d39d8024-68f8-4cf9-a6fb-af74c12e5e40","ku-47b252ec-e67b-4e8d-b66c-91d826482a65"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evaluation of hop performance in children with anterior cruciate ligament reconstruction using healthy reference data: A cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.92-039465","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background and High percentages of atrial pacing have been associated with an increased risk of atrial fibrillation. This study is aimed at evaluAims ating whether atrial pacing minimization in patients with sinus node dysfunction reduces the incidence of atrial fibrillation. Methods In a nationwide, randomized controlled trial, 540 patients with sinus node dysfunction and an indication for first pacemaker implantation were assigned to pacing programmed to a base rate of 60 bpm and rate-adaptive pacing (DDDR-60) or pacing programmed to a base rate of 40 bpm without rate-adaptive pacing (DDD-40). Patients were followed on remote monitoring for 2 years. The primary endpoint was time to first episode of atrial fibrillation longer than 6 min. Secondary endpoints included longer episodes of atrial fibrillation, and the safety endpoint comprised a composite of syncope or presyncope. Results The median percentage of atrial pacing was 1% in patients assigned to DDD-40 and 49% in patients assigned to DDDR-60. The primary endpoint occurred in 124 patients (46%) in each treatment group (hazard ratio [HR] 0.97, 95% confidence interval [CI] 0.76–1.25, P = .83). There were no between-group differences in atrial fibrillation exceeding 6 or 24 h, persistent atrial fibrillation, or cardioversions for atrial fibrillation. The incidence of syncope or presyncope was higher in patients assigned to DDD-40 (HR 1.71, 95% CI 1.13–2.59, P = .01). Conclusions Atrial pacing minimization in patients with sinus node dysfunction does not reduce the incidence of atrial fibrillation. Programming a base rate of 40 bpm without rate-adaptive pacing is associated with an increased risk of syncope or presyncope.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Kronborg, Mads Brix","Frausing, Maria Hee Jung Park","Malczynski, Jerzy","Riahi, Sam","Haarbo, Jens","Holm, Katja Fiedler","Larroudé, Charlotte Ellen","Albertsen, Andi Eie","Svendstrup, Lene","Hintze, Ulrik","Pedersen, Ole Dyg","Davidsen, Ulla","Fischer, Thomas","Johansen, Jens Brock","Kristensen, Jens","Gerdes, Christian","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis"],"cuid":["S03-099.32-697716"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["DANPACE II Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Kronborg, Mads Brix"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Atrial pacing","Pacemaker","Quality of Life","Sinus node disease","Syncope"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"atrial pacing minimization in sinus node dysfunction and risk of incident atrial fibrillation a randomized trial","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/eurheartj/ehad564","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["M.B.K. received speakers fee from Abbot, M.H.J.P.F. received consulting fees from Medtronic outside this work, J.B.J. received consulting fees from Medtronic outside this work, and J.C.N. received grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation and the Danish Heart Foundation outside this work. The DANPACE II trial was supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark (4183-00251B) Danish Heart Foundation (13-04-R94_A4523-22757), Karen Elise Jensen’s Foundation, Arvid Nilssons Foundation, and the Danish Pacemaker and ICD Registry. Biotronik, Boston Scientific, Medtronic, and St. Jude Medical sponsored remote monitoring in the study period."],"id":"S03-099.32-697716","identifier":[{"id":"37638973","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85176296434","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10590128","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-5e3e2f41-351a-4b2e-b580-b6a42bd4d01a","au-78405aa5-409a-4d4f-bd34-701599efe23e","sdu-e67917ef-ca0a-46fa-a782-40ea0f43f13a"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Atrial pacing","Pacemaker","Quality of life","Sinus node disease","Syncope"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-8886544E860DCCA38A76AE582AC4DEED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/406491807/ehad564.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/245046263/ehad564_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/eurheartj/ehad564","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/559686932/Kronborg_et_al._2023_._Atrial_pacing_minimization_in_sinus_node_dysfunction_and_risk_of_incident_atrial_fibrillation_-_a_randomized_trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital Central and West Jutland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg Unive