ponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"bodilsenjacoboth","last":"Bodilsen","locid":"260dd517-12cb-4490-b8c0-c69efb455878","name":"Bodilsen, Jacob","name_org":"Bodilsen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-7398-814X","rank":27,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"K. T.","key":"petersenkristinetoftoth","last":"Petersen","locid":"a73caa4d-7a8d-426e-b032-243e3959bb81","name":"Petersen, Kristine Toft","name_org":"Petersen, K. T.","rank":28,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"R. K.","key":"thistedrikkekrogoth","last":"Thisted","locid":"9499cebb-fd5b-4b0d-8236-d91752d05f5d","name":"Thisted, Rikke Krog","name_org":"Thisted, R. K.","rank":29,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["37351453"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ofid/ofad248","issn":["23288957"],"issue":"6","journal":"Open Forum Infectious Diseases","paperid":"ofad248","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Open Forum Infectious Diseases","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164243150"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9ccfc9d4-eca1-47f6-80f2-282f834f7b14","au-4a13f79a-9b90-4fc2-91d2-ec0f61b7c92a","ku-d0e65ef3-6750-4e3f-ab5a-37d6fbedcc63","sdu-fbff81e9-fd1b-4b88-92e1-c85c141f66de"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association of Self-Reported Systemic Reactions Following SARS-CoV-2 Vaccination With Immunological Response in The Danish National Cohort Study of Effectiveness and Safety of SARS-CoV-2 Vaccines (ENFORCE)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-097.91-724278","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Tree diseases constitute a significant threat to biodiversity worldwide. Pathogen discovery in natural habitats is of vital importance to understanding current and future threats and prioritising efforts towards developing disease management strategies. Ash dieback is a fungal disease of major conservational concern that is infecting common ash trees, Fraxinus excelsior, in Europe. The disease is caused by a non-native fungal pathogen, Hymenoscyphus fraxineus. Other dieback causing-species have not previously been identified in the genus Hymenoscyphus. Here, we discover the pathogenicity potential of two newly identified related species of Asian origin, H. koreanus and H. occultus, and one Europe-native related species, H. albidus. We sequence the genomes of all three Hymenoscyphus species and compare them to that of H. fraxineus. Phylogenetic analysis of core eukaryotic genes identified H. albidus and H. koreanus as sister species, whilst H. occultus diverged prior these and H. fraxineus. All four Hymenoscyphus genomes are of comparable sizes (55-62 Mbp) and GC contents (42–44%) and encode for polymorphic secretomes. Surprisingly, 1,133 predicted secreted proteins are shared between the ash dieback pathogen H. fraxineus and the three related Hymenoscyphus endophytes. Amongst shared secreted proteins are cell death-inducing effector candidates, such as necrosis, and ethylene-inducing peptide 1-like proteins, NLPs, that are upregulated during in planta growth of all Hymenoscyphus species. Indeed, pathogenicity tests showed that all four related Hymenoscyphus species develop pathogenic growth on European ash stems, with native H. albidus being the least virulent. Our results identify the threat Hymenoscypohus species pose to the survival of European ash trees, and highlight the importance of promoting pathogen surveillance in environmental landscapes. Identifying new pathogens and including them in the screening for durable immunity of common ash trees is key to the long-term survival of ash.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rafiqi, Maryam","Kosawang, Chatchai","Peers, Jessica A.","Jelonek, Lukas","Yvanne, Hélène","McMullan, Mark","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-670032"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Morocco","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Justus Liebig University Giessen","Mohammed VI Polytechnic University","Norwich Research Park","Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"endophytic fungi related to the ash dieback causal agent encode signatures of pathogenicity on european ash","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2023.01.04.522732","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-670032","ids":["ku-3770b4c1-2343-452c-a072-8b355e836a90"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-400E779F0E50CBE874CB84CE29DF05EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/347483881/Endophytic_fungi_related_to_the_ash_dieback_causal_agent_encode_signatures_of_pathogenicity_on_European_ash_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2023.01.04.522732","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"royal botanic gardens kew","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ma","key":"mohammed vi polytechnic university","loc":["Morocco","Africa"],"na