{"abstract":"Background: Bone mineral density (BMD) loss may be accelerated in people with HIV (PLWH). It is unknown whether a polygenic risk score (PRS) is associated with low BMD in PLWH. Methods: Swiss HIV Cohort Study participants of self-reported European descent underwent ≥2 per-protocol dual x-ray absorptiometry (DXA) measurements ≥2 years apart (2011-2020). Univariable and multivariable odds ratios (ORs) for DXA-defined osteoporosis were based on traditional and HIV-related risk factors and a genome-wide PRS built from 9413 single-nucleotide polymorphisms associated with low BMD in the general population. Controls were free from osteoporosis/osteopenia on all DXA measurements. Results: We included 438 participants: 149 with osteoporosis and 289 controls (median age, 53 years; 82% male, 95% with suppressed HIV RNA). Participants with unfavorable osteoporosis PRS (top vs bottom quintile) had univariable and multivariable-adjusted osteoporosis ORs of 4.76 (95% CI, 2.34-9.67) and 4.13 (1.86-9.18), respectively. For comparison, hepatitis C seropositivity, 5-year tenofovir disoproxil fumarate exposure, and parent history of hip fracture yielded univariable osteoporosis ORs of 2.26 (1.37-3.74), 1.84 (1.40-2.43), and 1.54 (0.82-2.9). Conclusions: In PLWH in Switzerland, osteoporosis was independently associated with a BMD-associated PRS after adjustment for established risk factors, including exposure to tenofovir disoproxil fumarate.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Schwenke, Johannes M.","Thorball, Christian W.","Schoepf, Isabella C.","Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Hasse, B.","Lamy, Olivier","Calmy, Alexandra","Wandeler, G.","Marzolini, C.","Kahlert, Christian R.","Bernasconi, Enos","Kouyos, R. D.","Günthard, H. F.","Ledergerber, Bruno","Fellay, Jacques","Burkhalter, Felix","Tarr, P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-748401"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["Swiss HIV Cohort Study (SHCS)"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cantonal Hospital St. Gallen","ETH Zürich","Geneva University Hospitals","Kantonsspital Baselland","Lausanne University Hospital","University Hospital Basel","University Hospital Bern","University Hospital Zürich","University of Basel","University of Bern","University of Geneva","University of Lausanne","University of Zurich","Università della Svizzera italiana"],"keyword":["Aging","HIV infection","Low bone mineral density","Osteoporosis","Polygenic risk score"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of a polygenic risk score with osteoporosis in people living with hiv the swiss hiv cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jiad179","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-748401","identifier":[{"id":"37225667","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85173444253","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7891da11-c19b-43b8-a936-765e347274c9"],"keyword":["HIV infection","aging","low bone mineral density","osteoporosis","polygenic risk score"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F62B620B5ECA6850864CFA3C0EC63B97"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/397033389/jiad179.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jiad179","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"university of basel","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Basel","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"university of lausanne