{"abstract":"Background: Patient involvement in care in the intensive care unit (ICU) is complex. Knowledge about the nature and extent of patient involvement in the Intensive care unit is scarce. Aim: The aim of the study was to explore the critical care nursing staff's perception of patient involvement in their care in the ICU. Study Design: A phenomenological, hermeneutic research study was carried out using qualitative data. Data were collected in two focus group interviews analysed using Ricoeur's theory of interpretation. The study was conducted in a level 2 medical-surgical 8-bed ICU in a regional hospital in Southern Denmark. Results: Critical care nurses found it important to maintain involvement in intensive care. Depending on the patient's ability to partake in care, approaches for patient involvement ranged from (1) continually adjusting care activities according to the patient's bodily responses, (2) formation of a relationship with the patient to enable personalized care and (3) making room for self-determined care progressing with the patient's recovery. Conclusion: Critical care nurses' perception of patient involvement depended on the patient's level of consciousness. When unconscious, patient involvement was possible but took a physical approach. However, the power inequality in the nurse–patient relationship must be expressed if patient involvement in the ICU is to take place. Relevance to Clinical Practice: Results suggest that nurses' perception of patient involvement in the ICU depends on the patient's level of consciousness. Patient involvement may be possible even when the patient is unconscious but it takes a more physical approach. It is essential that the power inequality in the nurse–patient relationship must be expressed if patient involvement in the ICU is to take place.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Egelund Hansen, Anja","Lehmkuhl, Lene","Nielsen, Anne Højager"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-698070"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Egelund Hansen, Anja"],"keyword":["Critical care","Focus Groups","Focus group interview","Humans","Intensive Care Units","Nurses","Patient Participation","Patient involvement","Perception","Qualitative","Qualitative Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"critical care nurses perception of patient involvement in care a qualitative focus group","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/nicc.12815","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-698070","identifier":[{"id":"85133713941","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35811495","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f30d7121-62ff-4f99-899f-02abc26c917e","sdu-8b8fb438-0598-4e26-ad6e-a2963a7da09f"],"keyword":["Focus Groups","Humans","Intensive Care Units","Nurses","Perception","Qualitative Research","critical care","focus group interview","patient involvement","patient participation","qualitative"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-240606F90DFB0804732EAF4703405B14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/nicc.12815","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/205700258/Nursing_in_Critical_Care_2022_Egelund_Hansen_Critical_care_nurses_perception_of_patient_involvement_in_care_A.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/398433933/Nursing_in_Critical_Care_-_2022_-_Egelund_Hansen_-_Critical_care_nurses_perception_of_patient_involvement_in_care_A.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Urology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Operation og Intensiv, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja","key":"egelundhansenpau","last":"Egelund Hansen","locid":"58285a0c-0c0a-43bf-9674-5ef291273d62","name":"Egelund Hansen, Anja","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"lehmkuhlpau","last":"Lehmkuhl","locid":"2452a119-9a90-487a-8665-a5afb541e0bd","name":"Lehmkuhl, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-2196-5621","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne","key":"højagernielsenpau","last":"Højager Nielsen","locid":"b275cdfd-dad4-4004-bf1d-725ff3f3ee40","name":"Nielsen, Anne Højager","name_org":"Højager Nielsen, Anne","orcid":"0000-0002-8955-9374","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35811495"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/nicc.12815","issn":["13621017","14785153"],"issn_org":["13621017"],"issue":"6","journal":"Nursing in Critical Care","pages":"878-884","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Nursing in Critical Care","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133713941"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f30d7121-62ff-4f99-899f-02abc26c917e","sdu-8b8fb438-0598-4e26-ad6e-a2963a7da09f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Critical care nurses' perception of patient involvement in care : A qualitative focus group","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-698070","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"I Danmark dør mennesker med svære psykiske lidelser i gennemsnit 7-10 år tidligere end den øvrige befolkning. Selvom en del af denne overdødelighed skyldes selvmord, kan størstedelen, op imod 60 procent, tilskrives somatiske sygdomme. Den store overdødelighed tydeliggør behovet for øget forebyggelse, tidlig diagnosticering og kvalitet i den somatiske behandling af patienter med psykisk lidelse. Dette er den første af to rapporter, som Behandlingsrådet publicerer vedrørende ulighed i sundhed i 2023 og 2024 under temaet ”Ulighed i den somatiske behandling af patienter med psykiske lidelser”. Rapporterne fokuserer på det danske sundhedsvæsen. Formålet med Behandlingsrådets analyse (2022) er at belyse eventuelle uligheder i somatisk behandling og sygdomsudfald hos patienter med psykisk lidelse sammenlignet med patienter uden psykisk lidelse. Endvidere undersøges betydningen af uddannelse og geografisk bopæl i forhold til eventuelle uligheder mellem patienter med og uden psykisk lidelse","author_count":29,"contributors":["Grønbæk, Morten Klöcker","Andersen, Pernille Tanggaard","Vestergaard, Mogens","Fleming, Emma","Hageman, Ida","Larsen, Finn Breinholt","Caspersen, Lene","Larsen, Beth Bülow","Ulrichsen, Susanne Stockmal","Borup, Kit","Andersen, Lisbeth Lauge","Nielsen, René Ernst","Nordentoft, Merete","Tipsmark, Line Stjernholm","Andersen, Lærke Mai Bonde","Christensen, Pernille Skovgaard","Jeppesen, Josefine Klakk","Johnsen, Søren Paaske","Knudsen, Søren Valgreen","Valentin, Jan Brink"],"cuid":["S03-081.32-792812"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["Dansk Center for Klinisk Sundhedstjenesteforskning (DACS), Aalborg Universitet","Fagudvalget for ulighed i somatisk behandling af patienter med psykiske lidelser","Projektgruppen i Behandlingsrådets sekretariat"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Bedre Psykiatri"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"behandlingsrådets rapport vedrørende ulighed i somatisk behandling af patienter med psykiske lidelser","src":["aau","sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://behandlingsraadet-dk.b-cdn.net/media/c0wagvp4/behandlingsr%C3%A5dets-rapport-vedr-ulighed-i-somatisk-behandling-af-patienter-med-psykiske-lidelser-2022-v-1-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-081.32-792812","ids":["aau-2c1c2630-91c1-4065-8f2f-667b323e3db8","sdu-e4cfb78e-2fd6-4313-b65b-3f07b2785d5f","ucl-9f55b2c6-ec48-4f2d-9821-7f8c7d673877"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-3-C6D1215EF37E7072510C922984DAE64D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://behandlingsraadet-dk.b-cdn.net/media/c0wagvp4/behandlingsr%C3%A5dets-rapport-vedr-ulighed-i-somatisk-behandling-af-patienter-med-psykiske-lidelser-2022-v-1-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Health Promotion"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU",