{"abstract":"Fem forskere på Build ved Aalborg Universitet har fulgt Parallelsamfundsaftalen og de 15 berørte områder tæt, siden den blev indført i 2018. De fremlægger deres foreløbige resultater i dette debatindlæg.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bech-Danielsen, Claus","Mechlenborg, Mette","Nordberg, Lene Wiell","Stender, Marie","Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-705038"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fysisk omdannelse","Omdannelsesområder","Parallelsamfundsaftalen","Transformation","Udsatte boligområder"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"build forskere om nye resultater fra parallelsamfundsaftalen beboere mister både deres bolig og sociale netværk","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://byrummonitor.dk/Debat/art9644798/Beboere-mister-b%C3%A5de-deres-bolig-og-sociale-netv%C3%A6rk","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-705038","ids":["aau-399d298f-67f1-4928-aa89-21a83860d467"],"keyword":["Fysisk omdannelse","Omdannelsesområder","Parallelsamfundsaftalen","Transformation","Udsatte boligområder"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1D2EE98758984B8DCAF2C07261BDC656"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://byrummonitor.dk/Debat/art9644798/Beboere-mister-b%C3%A5de-deres-bolig-og-sociale-netv%C3%A6rk","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Town, Housing and Property","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Transformation of Housing and Places Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"bechdanielsenpau","last":"Bech-Danielsen","locid":"f41ac22b-bb0d-4c3f-8d06-96efd65c0665","name":"Bech-Danielsen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-4822-6039","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"mechlenborgpau","last":"Mechlenborg","locid":"429feb0f-1899-4126-bba7-9ae96ec42ce2","name":"Mechlenborg, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-9446-9795","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Wiell","key":"nordbergpau","last":"Nordberg","locid":"4620ca55-6074-4b3d-98ed-0321710187b8","name":"Nordberg, Lene Wiell","orcid":"0000-0003-3344-0574","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie","key":"stenderpau","last":"Stender","locid":"a548a5d3-73b7-4461-9ed9-ba9c0432e2ac","name":"Stender, Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-1009-3138","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Skovgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"125da2cb-a5a5-47e8-84ab-be518f10a19f","name":"Nielsen, Rikke Skovgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0308-1275","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"newspaper":"Byrumsmonitor","status":"p","title":"Byrumsmonitor"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-399d298f-67f1-4928-aa89-21a83860d467"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Build-forskere om nye resultater fra Parallelsamfundsaftalen : Beboere mister både deres bolig og sociale netværk.","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705038","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: On average, older patients use five or more medications daily. A consequence is an increased risk of adverse drug reactions, interactions, or medication errors. Therefore, it is important to understand the challenges experienced by the patients, relatives, and healthcare professionals pertinent to the concomitant use of many drugs. Methods: We conducted a qualitative study using focus group interviews to collect information from patients, relatives, and healthcare professionals regarding older patients' management of prescribed medicine. We interviewed seven patients using five or more medications daily, three relatives, three general practitioners, nine nurses from different healthcare sectors, one home care assistant, two hospital physicians, and four pharmacists. Results: The following themes were identified: (1) Unintentional non-adherence, (2) Intentional non-adherence, (3) Generic substitution, (4) Medication lists, (5) Timing and medication schedule, (6) Medication reviews and (7) Dose dispensing/pill organizers. Conclusion: Medication is the subject of concern among patients and relatives. They become confused and insecure about information from different actors and the package leaflets. Therefore, patients often request a thorough medication review to provide an overview, knowledge of possible side effects and interactions, and a clarification of the medication's timing. In addition, patients, relatives and nurses all request an indication of when medicine should be taken, including allowable deviations from this timing. Therefore, prescribing physicians should prioritize communicating information regarding these matters when prescribing.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Mikkelsen, Thorbjørn Hougaard","Søndergaard, Jens","Kjær, Niels Kristian","Nielsen, Jesper Bo","Ryg, Jesper","Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","Mogensen, Christian Backer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713873"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mikkelsen, Thorbjørn Hougaard"],"keyword":["Continuity of care","Experiences","Focus group interviews","Medication Errors","Non adherence","Older people","Polypharmacy","Qualitative Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"handling polypharmacy a qualitative study using focus group interviews with older patients their relatives and healthcare professionals","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-023-04131-6","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was supported by a grant from VELUX FONDEN grant no. 34175. VELUX FONDEN did not participate in or influence the design of the study as well as the collection, analysis, and interpretation of data nor in writing the manuscript."],"id":"S01-000.00-713873","identifier":[{"id":"85167371702","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10410867","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37553585","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-3e6d2251-4191-4e6e-b226-b096b46b8f02"],"keyword":["Adverse drug interactions","Continuity of care","Experiences","Focus group interviews","Medication errors","Non-adherence","Older people","Polypharmacy","Qualitative research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-70413FBBAC1427146547DA023FAC187F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12877-023-04131-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/253008747/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Emergency Medicine (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Hospital Sønderjylland, Research Unit of Emergency Medicine (Aabenraa)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorbjørn Hougaard","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"5317cc05-4505-4a6c-bc7b-ba4d4a4ab90e","name":"Mikkelsen, Thorbjørn Hougaard","orcid":"0000-0001-8432-0260","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Kristian","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"8fa36491-a268-47f4-88ce-05581af1f852","name":"Kjær, Niels Kristian","name_org":"Kjaer, Niels Kristian","orcid":"0000-0002-1301-2663","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"75938cc2-43d6-4c8d-a506-6b1c0472a382","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5764-5462","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","locid":"c63490d8-ba13-4875-bf40-82c4aebbab6f","name":"Ryg, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8641-3062","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Juel","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"b3d44e3d-440c-41f1-b52d-838b0338bf55","name":"Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","orcid":"0009-0008-2559-9319","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Backer","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","locid":"86d86954-82ad-43c3-9ce6-b898d1f64da5","name":"Mogensen, Christian Backer","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37553585"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12877-023-04131-6","issn":["14712318"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Geriatrics","paperid":"477","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Geriatrics","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85167371702"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3e6d2251-4191-4e6e-b226-b096b46b8f02"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Handling polypharmacy : a qualitative study using focus group interviews with older patients, their relatives, and healthcare professionals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713873","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Red blood cell (RBC) transfusion is common among patients admitted to the intensive care unit (ICU). Despite multiple randomized clinical trials of hemoglobin (Hb) thresholds for transfusion, little is known about how these thresholds are incorporated into current practice. Objective: To evaluate and describe ICU RBC transfusion practices worldwide. Design, Setting, and Participants: International, prospective, cohort study that involved 3643 adult patients from 233 ICUs in 30 countries on 6 continents from March 2019 to October 2022 with data collection in prespecified weeks. Exposure: ICU stay. Main Outcomes and Measures: The primary outcome was the occurrence of RBC transfusion during ICU stay. Additional outcomes included the indication(s) for RBC transfusion (consisting of clinical reasons and physiological triggers), the stated Hb threshold and actual measured Hb values before and after an RBC transfusion, and the number of units transfused. Results: Among 3908 potentially eligible patients, 3643 were included across 233 ICUs (median of 11 patients per ICU [IQR, 5-20]) in 30 countries on 6 continents. Among the participants, the mean (SD) age was 61 (16) years, 62% were male (2267/3643), and the median Sequential Organ Failure Assessment score was 3.2 (IQR, 1.5-6.0). A total of 894 patients (25%) received 1 or more RBC transfusions during their ICU stay, with a median total of 2 units per patient (IQR, 1-4). The proportion of patients who received a transfusion ranged from 0% to 100% across centers, from 0% to 80% across countries, and from 19% to 45% across continents. Among the patients who received a transfusion, a total of 1727 RBC transfusions were administered, wherein the most common clinical indications were low Hb value (n = 1412 [81.8%]; mean [SD] lowest Hb before transfusion, 7.4 [1.2] g/dL), active bleeding (n = 479; 27.7%), and hemodynamic instability (n = 406 [23.5%]). Among the events with a stated physiological trigger, the most frequently stated triggers were hypotension (n = 728 [42.2%]), tachycardia (n = 474 [27.4%]), and increased lactate levels (n = 308 [17.8%]). The median lowest Hb level on days with an RBC transfusion ranged from 5.2 g/dL to 13.1 g/dL across centers, from 5.3 g/dL to 9.1 g/dL across countries, and from 7.2 g/dL to 8.7 g/dL across continents. Approximately 84% of ICUs administered transfusions to patients at a median Hb level greater than 7 g/dL. Conclusions and Relevance: RBC transfusion was common in patients admitted to ICUs worldwide between 2019 and 2022, with high variability across centers in transfusion practices..","author_count":40,"contributors":["Raasveld, Senta Jorinde","De Bruin, Sanne","Reuland, Merijn C.","Van Den Oord, Claudia","Schenk, Jimmy","Aubron, Cécile","Bakker, Jan","Cecconi, Maurizio","Feldheiser, Aarne","Meier, Jens","Müller, Marcella C.A.","Scheeren, Thomas W.L.","McQuilten, Zoe","Flint, Andrew","Hamid, Tarikul","Piagnerelli, Michaël","Tomić Mahečić, Tina","Benes, Jan","Russell, Lene","Aguirre-Bermeo, Hernan","Triantafyllopoulou, Konstantina","Chantziara, Vasiliki","Gurjar, Mohan","Myatra, Sheila Nainan","Pota, Vincenzo","Elhadi, Muhammed","Gawda, Ryszard","Mourisco, Mafalda","Lance, Marcus","Neskovic, Vojislava","Podbregar, Matej","Llau, Juan V.","Quintana-Diaz, Manual","Cronhjort, Maria","Pfortmueller, Carmen A.","Yapici, Nihan","Nielsen, Nathan D.","Shah, Akshay","De Grooth, Harm Jan","Vlaar, Alexander P.J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721606"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, North","America, South","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["InPUT Study Group"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Bangladesh","Belgium","Chile","Croatia","Czechia","Ecuador","France","Germany","Greece","India","Italy","Kenya","Libya","Netherlands","Poland","Portugal","Serbia","Slovenia","Spai