48-2","issn":["09405429","14325233"],"issn_org":["09405429"],"issue":"12","journal":"Acta Diabetologica","pages":"1663-1673","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Acta Diabetologica","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85165105409"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8ff69269-8dc5-4873-8405-eba92d3c8787","sdu-13a725f1-aa40-44c7-be44-35c75d554439"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Applying WHO2013 diagnostic criteria for gestational diabetes mellitus reveals currently untreated women at increased risk","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.41-716453","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Commercially available artificial intelligence (AI) tools can assist radiologists in interpreting chest radiographs, but their real-life diagnostic accuracy remains unclear. Purpose: To evaluate the diagnostic accuracy of four commercially available AI tools for detection of airspace disease, pneumothorax, and pleural effusion on chest radiographs. Materials and Methods: This retrospective study included consecutive adult patients who underwent chest radiography at one of four Danish hospitals in January 2020. Two thoracic radiologists (or three, in cases of disagreement) who had access to all previous and future imaging labeled chest radiographs independently for the reference standard. Area under the receiver operating characteristic curve, sensitivity, and specificity were calculated. Sensitivity and specificity were additionally stratified according to the severity of findings, number of findings on chest radiographs, and radiographic projection. The χ2 and McNemar tests were used for comparisons. Results: The data set comprised 2040 patients (median age, 72 years [IQR, 58–81 years]; 1033 female), of whom 669 (32.8%) had target findings. The AI tools demonstrated areas under the receiver operating characteristic curve ranging 0.83–0.88 for airspace disease, 0.89–0.97 for pneumothorax, and 0.94–0.97 for pleural effusion. Sensitivities ranged 72%–91% for airspace disease, 63%–90% for pneumothorax, and 62%–95% for pleural effusion. Negative predictive values ranged 92%–100% for all target findings. In airspace disease, pneumothorax, and pleural effusion, specificity was high for chest radiographs with normal or single findings (range, 85%–96%, 99%–100%, and 95%–100%, respectively) and markedly lower for chest radiographs with four or more findings (range, 27%–69%, 96%–99%, 65%–92%, respectively) (P < .001). AI sensitivity was lower for vague airspace disease (range, 33%–61%) and small pneumothorax or pleural effusion (range, 9%–94%) compared with larger findings (range, 81%–100%; P value range, > .99 to < .001). Conclusion: Current-generation AI tools showed moderate to high sensitivity for detecting airspace disease, pneumothorax, and pleural effusion on chest radiographs. However, they produced more false-positive findings than radiology reports, and their performance decreased for smaller-sized target findings and when multiple findings were present.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Plesner, Louis Lind","Müller, Felix C.","Brejnebøl, Mathias W.","Laustrup, Lene C.","Rasmussen, Finn","Nielsen, Olav W.","Boesen, Mikael","Brun Andersen, Michael"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-741688"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Plesner, Louis Lind"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["RAIT.dk"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"commercially available chest radiograph ai tools for detecting airspace disease pneumothorax and pleural effusion","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/414916389/Commercially_Available_Chest_Radiograph_AI_Tools_for_Detecting_Airspace_Disease_Pneumothorax_and_Pleural_Effusion.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-741688","identifier":[{"id":"37750768","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85174232403","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1390db80-93f5-412c-8749-d5978f9ecc6c","ku-409aea94-167e-41ec-8541-d7e9931623a7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8F94F9421DC84B095D5F0F05CA5E5CED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/414916389/Commercially_Available_Chest_Radiograph_AI_Tools_for_Detecting_Airspace_Disease_Pneumothorax_and_Pleural_Effusion.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["RAIT.dk"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Louis Lind","key":"plesnerpau","last":"Plesner","name":"Plesner, Louis Lind","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Felix C.","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, Felix C.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mathias W.","key":"brejnebølpau","last":"Brejnebøl","name":"Brejnebøl, Mathias W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene C.","key":"laustruppau","last":"Laustrup","name":"Laustrup, Lene C.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Finn","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"1c4dadf5-d001-4c6c-9f23-347af298c53d","name":"Rasmussen, Finn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Olav W.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d9fc9e11-583d-43d9-994c-df128b7bf5cc","name":"Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","name_org":"Nielsen, Olav W.","orcid":"0000-0003-3532-9431","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Mikael","key":"boesenpau","last":"Boesen","locid":"b449f652-d441-4b23-836f-2d5111ef64dd","name":"Boesen, Mikael","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Michael","key":"brunandersenpau","last":"Brun Andersen","locid":"2011438d-efaa-4cd0-a092-8e9970e0b885","name":"Andersen, Michael Brun","name_org":"Brun Andersen, Michael","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37750768"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1148/radiol.231236","issn":["00338419","15271315"],"issn_org":["00338419"],"issue":"3","journal":"Radiology","paperid":"e231236","publisher":"Radiological Society of North America Inc.","status":"p","title":"Radiology","volume":"308"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174232403"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1390db80-93f5-412c-8749-d5978f9ecc6c","ku-409aea94-167e-41ec-8541-d7e9931623a7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Commercially Available Chest Radiograph AI Tools for Detecting Airspace Disease, Pneumothorax, and Pleural Effusion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-741688","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Thrombocytopenia (platelet count < 150 × 109/L) is common in intensive care unit (ICU) patients and is likely associated with worse outcomes. In this study we present international contemporary data on thrombocytopenia in ICU patients. Methods: We conducted a prospective cohort study in adult ICU patients in 52 ICUs across 10 countries. We assessed frequencies of thrombocytopenia, use of platelet transfusions and clinical outcomes including mortality. We evaluated pre-selected potential risk factors for the development of thrombocytopenia during ICU stay and associations between thrombocytopenia at ICU admission and 90-day mortality using pre-specified logistic regression analyses. Results: We analysed 1166 ICU patients; the median age was 63 years and 39.5% were female. Overall, 43.2% (95% confidence interval (CI) 40.4-46.1) had thrombocytopenia; 23.4% (20-26) had thrombocytopenia at ICU admission, and 19.8% (17.6-22.2) developed thrombocytopenia during their ICU stay. Absence of acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS), non-cancer-related immune deficiency, liver failure, male sex, septic shock, and bleeding at ICU admission were associated with the development of thrombocytopenia during ICU stay. Among patients with thrombocytopenia, 22.6% received platelet transfusion(s), and 64.3% of in-ICU transfusions were prophylactic. Patients with thrombocytopenia had higher occurrences of bleeding and death, fewer days alive without the use of life-support, and fewer days alive and out of hospital. Thrombocytopenia at ICU admission was associated with 90-day mortality (adjusted odds ratio 1.7; 95% CI 1.19-2.42). Conclusion: Thrombocytopenia occurred in 43% of critically ill patients and was associated with worse outcomes including increased mortality. Platelet transfusions were given to 23% of patients with thrombocytopenia and most were prophylactic.","author_count":120,"contributors":["Anthon, Carl Thomas","Pène, Frédéric","Perner, Anders","Azoulay, Elie","Puxty, Kathryn","Van De Louw, Andry","Barratt-Due, Andreas","Chawla, Sanjay","Castro, Pedro","Póvoa, Pedro","Coelho, Luis","Metaxa, Victoria","Kochanek, Matthias","Liebregts, Tobias","Kander, Thomas","Hästbacka, Johanna","Andreasen, Jo Bønding","Péju, Edwige","Nielsen, Lene Bjerregaard","Hvas, Christine Lodberg","Dufranc, Etienne","Canet, Emmanuel","Lundqvist, Linda","Wright, Christopher John","Schmidt, Julien","Uhel, Fabrice","Ait-Oufella, Hafid","Krag, Mette","Cos Badia, Elisabet","Díaz-Lagares, Cándido","Menat, Sophie","Voiriot, Guillaume","Clausen, Niels Erikstrup","Lorentzen, Kristian","Kvåle, Reidar","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Holten, Aleksander Rygh","Strand, Kristian","Tzalavras, Asterios","Bestle, Morten H.","Klepstad, Pål","Fernandez, Sara","Vimpere, Damien","Costa, Carolina","Graça, Carina","Lueck, Catherina","Juhl, Christian Svendsen","Costa, Carolina","Bådstøløkken, Per Martin","Miranda, Teresa","Lêdo, Lia Susana Aires","Sousa Torres, Joao Carlos","Granholm, Anders","Møller, Morten Hylander","Russell, Lene","Khalil, Ahmed","Yehia, Ahmed","Salem, Haney","Farahat, Hesham","Sudevan, Manu","Biggart, Melissa","Fatima, Nirmeen","Elkhonezy, Mohammed","Bunzel, Anne Marie","Siegumfeldt, Rine M.","Vestergaard, Stine R.","Pelle, Juliette","Lê, Minh Pierre","Vigneron, Clara","Bertrix, Morgane","Cirera, Paul","Laghlam, Driss","Bredin, Swann","Marin, Nathalie","Toppenberg, Maria","Benelli, Brice","Seguin, Amélie","Garret, Charlotte","Guillotin, Florian","Blonz, Gauthier","Lascarrou, Jean Baptiste","Lemarie, Jérémie","Desmedt, Luc","Agbakou, Maïté","Carpentier, Mathieu","Martin, Maëlle","Benkalfate, Naïla","Zambon, Olivier","Decamps, Paul","Wilquin, Pauline L.","Benguerfi, Soraya","Gardner, John","Remor, Natalie","Carr, Sheila","Yang, Gloria","Gernez, Coralie","Thiry, Ingrid","Missri, Louai","Denneborg, Moritz K.G.","Brown, Katherine","Casares, Vanessa","Sivula, Mirka","Lappi, Elina","Pettilä, Leena","Heinonen, Jonna","Saario, Minttu","Mecheri, Manal K.","Elabbadi, Alezandre","Desnos, Cyrielle","Lafarge, Antoine","Mghirbi, Olfa","Sjøbø, Brit","Christoffersen, Cecilie","Bestle, Frederik H.","Lemos, Claudia","Gonçalves, Cristiana V.","Jacinto, Nuno M.B.","Anselmo, Monica P.","Hoeper, Marius M.","Hoff, Marja","Simões Freire, Pedro M."],"cuid":["S03-091.33-715671"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["The PLOT-ICU Collaborators and the Nine-I Study Group","on behalf of the PLOT-ICU Collaborators and the Nine-I Study Group"],"corresponding_author":["Russell, Lene"],"country":["Finland","France","Germany","Norway","Portugal","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Akershus University Hospital","All Global Affiliations","Assistance publique – Hôpitaux de Paris","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Bicêtre Paris-Saclay hospital","Cornell University","EPE","Glasgow Royal Infirmary","Hannover Medical School","Haukeland University Hospital","Helsinki University Hospital","Hospital Central do Funchal","Hospital General Granollers","Hospital General de Granollers","Hospital São José","Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron, Barcelona, Spain.","Hospital da Luz","Hospital de Sao Jose","Hôpital Avicenne","Hôpital Tenon","King's College Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","King's College London","Lund University","Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center","NHS Greater Glasgow and Clyde","NOVA University Lisbon","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Oslo University Hospital","Paris-Cité University","Pennsylvania State University","Queen Elizabeth University Hospital","Santa Cruz Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","Sorbonne University","St. Olav's University Hospital","St. Olavs Hospital - University Hospital Trondheim","Stavanger University Hospital","Tampere University","Tampere University Hospital","Universite Paris 5","Universite de Nant