emos, Claudia","rank":115,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"56","first":"Cristiana V.","key":"gonçalvescristianavpau","last":"Gonçalves","name":"Gonçalves, Cristiana V.","rank":116,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"56","first":"Nuno M.B.","key":"jacintonunombpau","last":"Jacinto","name":"Jacinto, Nuno M.B.","rank":117,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"56","first":"Monica P.","key":"anselmomonicappau","last":"Anselmo","name":"Anselmo, Monica P.","rank":118,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"58","first":"Marius M.","key":"hoepermariusmpau","last":"Hoeper","name":"Hoeper, Marius M.","rank":119,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Marja","key":"hoffmarjapau","last":"Hoff","name":"Hoff, Marja","rank":120,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"60","first":"Pedro M.","key":"simõesfreirepedrompau","last":"Simões Freire","name":"Simões Freire, Pedro M.","rank":121,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37812225"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00134-023-07225-2","issn":["03424642","09351701"],"issn_org":["03424642"],"issue":"11","journal":"Intensive Care Medicine","pages":"1327-1338","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Intensive Care Medicine","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173919249"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5a438517-901c-449e-b0ad-fc4335e2f92b","au-eb915366-241a-45e4-a91d-bc808fe7038b","ku-5a3597de-1dfd-490f-a51f-6c6231ea758c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Thrombocytopenia and platelet transfusions in ICU patients: an international inception cohort study (PLOT-ICU)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-091.33-715671","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Primary percutaneous coronary intervention with implantation of a metallic drug-eluting stent (DES) is the standard treatment for patients presenting with ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI). Implantation of a bioresorbable scaffold (BRS) during STEMI represents a novel strategy without intravascular metal. OBJECTIVE: The aim of the study was to investigate 12-month healing response in an STEMI population after implantation of either the Absorb BRS or Xience DES (Abbott Vascular, USA). METHODS: The present trial was a prospective, randomized, controlled, nonblinded, noninferiority study with planned inclusion of 120 patients with STEMI. Patients were randomly assigned 1:1 to treatment with Absorb BRS or Xience DES. Implantation result and healing response were evaluated by angiography and optical coherence tomography (OCT) at baseline and 12-month follow-up. The primary endpoint was minimum flow area (MFA) assessed at 12 months. Coronary stent healing index (CSHI) was calculated from OCT images. RESULTS: Out of 66 included patients, 58 had follow-up OCT after 12 months, and 49 entered matched analysis. One death occurred in each group; none were stent-related. MFA was 5.13 ± 1.70 mm2 (95% CI, 4.44-5.82) in the BRS group compared with 6.30 ± 2.49 mm2 (95% CI, 5.22-7.37) (P = 0.06) in the DES group. Noninferiority could not be evaluated. CSHI for both groups had a median score of 3. CONCLUSION: The DES group performed numerically better in primary and secondary endpoints, but the CSHI showed good stent healing in both groups.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Eriksen, Erlend","Neghabat, Omeed","Saeed, Sahrai","Herstad, Jon","Nordrehaug, Jan Erik","Tuseth, Vegard","Holm, Niels Ramsing","Holck, Emil Nielsen","Sejr-Hansen, Martin","Maule, Camilla Fox","Barkholt, Trine Ørhøj","Andreasen, Lene Nyhus","Christiansen, Evald Høj","Bleie, Øyvind"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-151012"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Eriksen, Erlend"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bergen"],"keyword":["Bioresorbable scaffold","Drug eluting stent","Optical coherence tomography","Primary percutaneous coronary intervention","ST elevation myocardial infarction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"everolimus eluting bioresorbable scaffold versus everolimus eluting metallic stent in primary percutaneous coronary intervention of st segment elevation myocardial infarction a randomized controlled trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85143557636","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-151012","identifier":[{"id":"36484214","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85143557636","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-25b93d64-9cbb-499a-bc36-d3d149bc8cac"],"keyword":["ST-elevation myocardial infarction","bioresorbable scaffold","drug-eluting stent","optical coherence tomography","primary percutaneous coronary intervention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A1E93ABDA1FE39C58E636081A252178"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"university of bergen","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Bergen","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-A