{"abstract":"This reflective paper proposes a research agenda that investigates and questions how and if we need to assess the service design tools and their usability in the context of organisations’ design maturity. Maps and tool in the service design toolbox are perceived as straightforward by some organisations, however for organisations with low service design maturity such tools can pose challenges in how to utilise and leverage their potential. As a direction for future studies, this research agenda sheds light on how common service design tools are affected by organisational usability and maturity.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Harre, Olivia Thomassen","Abdelnour-Nocera, Jose","Li, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-692467"],"event":{"end":"2023-07-14","place":"Rio De Janeiro, br","start":"2023-07-11","title":"ServDes 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Infinite Interactive LTD","University of West London"],"keyword":["Organisational design maturity","Service Design","Tools","Usability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proposing organisational usability as an enabler of organisational service design maturity","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ecp203039","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-692467","ids":["aau-1f1e4387-32d5-40ea-afcc-47f2b4cbaa25"],"keyword":["Service Design","organisational design maturity","tools","usability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-BE9F22F954D25A6B1B5DD17862FB4D9E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ecp203039","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/614531061/ServDes_2023_paper_4107_Proposing_organisational_usability_as_an_enabler_of_organisational_service_design_maturity_AJUSTADO.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Architecture and Urban Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of west london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of West London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"infinite interactive ltd","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Infinite Interactive LTD","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olivia Thomassen","key":"harrepau","last":"Harre","locid":"4b238a51-1331-435b-8d5a-778a43447357","name":"Harre, Olivia Thomassen","orcid":"0009-0001-3681-3770","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jose","key":"abdelnournocerapau","last":"Abdelnour-Nocera","name":"Abdelnour-Nocera, Jose","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carla","key":"cipollapedh","last":"Cipolla","name":"Cipolla, Carla","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Claudia","key":"montalvãopedh","last":"Mont’Alvão","name":"Mont’Alvão, Claudia","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Larissa","key":"fariaspedh","last":"Farias","name":"Farias, Larissa","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manuela","key":"quaresmapedh","last":"Quaresma","name":"Quaresma, Manuela","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3384/ecp203039","eisbn":["9789180754767"],"issn":["16503686"],"pages":"759-768","place":"Rio de Janeiro","publisher":"Linköping University Electronic Press","series":"Linköping Electronic Conference Proceedings","status":"p","subtitle":"Entanglements and Flows. Service Encounters and Meanings. Conference Proceedings","title":"ServDes 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1f1e4387-32d5-40ea-afcc-47f2b4cbaa25"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Proposing organisational usability as an enabler of organisational service design maturity","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-692467","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Concussion, the mildest form of traumatic brain injury, is an important public health concern due to high healthcare costs because of post-concussion symptoms (PCS). The majority of affected individuals apparently recover from the concussion within 1-3 months, but up to a third develop persistent PCS lasting more than 3 months. PCS is associated with substantial ongoing disability and distress. Recognition is growing that PCS is best understood in terms of an interaction between biological, psychological and social factors. However, evidence for effective non-pharmacological treatment strategies is scarce. Brief tele-health interventions to prevent prolonged PCS have demonstrated promising results and are likely to be cost-effective. Recently, the effect of a novel intervention “Get going After concussIoN” (GAIN) for people with persistent severe PCS was examined, showing a significantly larger reduction in PCS in the intervention group 3 months post-intervention than in the control group. Adapting the treatment principles and developing a down-scaled version of GAIN for adults with persistent mild to moderate PCS is hence warranted. OBJECTIVE: To present the adaption and development processes of the intervention GAIN Lite; a digital intervention aimed at preventing cornification among adults with mild to moderate post-concessional symptoms. DESIGN: An iterative method based on the UK Medical Research Council’s framework for developing and evaluating complex interventions combined with guidance for adapting interventions to new contexts guided the overall process. The approach was target-population based. SETTING: GAIN Lite was developed in the Central Denmark Region and led by Hammel Neurorehabilitation Centre and University Research Clinic in collaboration with a broad range of stakeholders; people having had a concussion; therapists delivering the intervention; researchers and various experts, namely the people behind the original GAIN study. RESULTS: The intervention has two major components: 1) six e-learning videos with a total duration of 50 minutes, and 2) up to four individual online sessions with a maximum duration of 60 minutes each. CONCLUSIONS: A systematic approach has been applied in the development process. Transparency in the development processes of GAIN Lite may improve prerequisites for research and clinical implementation. The GAIN Lite intervention will be developed over a two-year period, from January 2021 to January 2023, before implementation into a randomized clinical trial.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pedersen, Sedsel Kristine Stage","Thastum, Mille","Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","Odgaard, Lene","Pallesen, Hanne","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Silverberg, Noah D.","Brunner, Iris"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-694274"],"event":{"end":"2023-04-01","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2023-03-29","title":"14th World Congress on Brain Injury","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of British Columbia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of the intervention get going after concussion lite gain lite to reduce impairing post concessional mild to moderate symptoms in adults a feasibility study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-694274","ids":["au-cae716ec-03b9-47f0-a8f2-413d4ea7cb07"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DAFDB3912C6DA38D1A1887924C39C296"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hammel Neurocenter, Universitetsklinik for Neurorehabilitering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of british columbia","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of British Columbia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sedsel Kristine Stage","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ff1299e4-49ee-4f85-9b71-23594688783f","name":"Pedersen, Sedsel Kristine Stage","orcid":"0000-0003-4616-2382","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mille","key":"thastumpau","last":"Thastum","locid":"c3813500-c313-4961-a854-ad2dba72d7d9","name":"Thastum, Mille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erhard Trillingsgaard","key":"næssschmidtpau","last":"Næss-Schmidt","locid":"c1a1a6b6-deb0-4e07-8cc0-f7d3beeaca85","name":"Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2539-0362","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"1b80fe7b-ba0a-45b3-aca1-48bc19a97a44","name":"Odgaard, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-9830-3282","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne","key":"pallesenpau","last":"Pallesen","locid":"4a0d3edf-5b53-46f4-8396-5301309b5131","name":"Pallesen, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0001-6010-2306","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Feldbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Noah D.","key":"silverbergpau","last":"Silverberg","name":"Silverberg, Noah D.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Iris","key":"brunnerpau","last":"Brunner","locid":"d1e88a58-cd2f-4fd0-a2f3-2cee204ba1ab","name":"Brunner, Iris","orcid":"0000-0002-7194-3087","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cae716ec-03b9-47f0-a8f2-413d4ea7cb07"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Development of the intervention Get going After concussIoN Lite (GAIN Lite) to reduce impairing post-concessional mild-to-moderate symptoms in adults - A Feasibility Study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-694274","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: The aim of the study was to investigate whether patients with bipolar disorder (BD) in remission differ in personality traits compared with a healthy control group. Methods: A sample of patients with BD (n = 44) was compared with an individually matched control group (n = 44) using the Danish version of the Revised NEO Personality Inventory (NEO PI-R). Paired t-tests were used to analyze differences between the two groups and multiple regression models to evaluate predictors of NEO scores in the patient group. Results: Patients with BD reported significantly higher scores on both Neuroticism and Openness to Experience and lower scores on Conscientiousness. No differences were found on Extraversion and Agreeableness. The effect size for Neuroticism and its facets had a range from 0.77 to 1.45 SD. Statistically significant group differences were seen on 15 of 30 lower-level traits within all five high-order dimensions. There were large effect sizes for Trust (0.77) and Self-discipline (0.85), while the other statistically significant group differences were smaller with effect sizes in the range from 0.43 to 0.74 SD. However, patients with BD showed a profile with high-order dimensions and lower-level traits within one standard deviation from the mean score except for the lower-level trait Depression. Conclusions: Our findings suggest that patients with BD differ from healthy control persons with respect to higher levels of Neuroticism, Openness to Experience and lower scores on Agreeableness and on Conscientiousness, but prospective studies are needed to evaluate the implications of this finding.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Seeberg Nielsen, Lene","Krarup Larsen, Sarah","Csillag, Claudio","Mortensen, Erik Lykke","Vinberg, Maj"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695507"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bipolar disorder","FFM","NEO PI R","Neuroticism","Personality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"personality and bipolar disorder personality profiles of patients with remitted bipolar disorder and matched controls in a danish sample","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/373968589/NordJPersonality.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695507","identifier":[{"id":"85159494792","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37191348","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1bd239d5-66e0-4efa-9c53-cd16f980d23b"],"keyword":["Bipolar disorder","FFM","NEO PI-R","neuroticism","personality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2002C31D1C397EC099404438565A16AE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/373968589/NordJPersonality.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"seebergnielsenpau","last":"Seeberg Nielsen","name":"Seeberg Nielsen, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah","key":"kraruplarsenpau","last":"Krarup Larsen","name":"Krarup Larsen, Sarah","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Claudio","key":"csillagpau","last":"Csillag","locid":"754d3472-c1df-48fa-b922-83694c80acec","name":"Csillag, Claudio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Erik Lykke","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"18527abd-c96b-4863-82e0-5bcbc4687934","name":"Mortensen, Erik Lykke","orcid":"0000-0002-6985-451X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Maj","key":"vinbergpau","last":"Vinberg","locid":"c42cfaf1-2554-44d1-bb45-c0fccac79e8c","name":"Vinberg, Maj","orcid":"0000-0002-5982-1335","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37191348"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/08039488.2023.2210137","issn":["08039488","08039496"],"issn_org":["08039488"],"issue":"7","journal":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","pages":"661-668","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159494792"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1bd239d5-66e0-4efa-9c53-cd16f980d23b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Personality and bipolar disorder : personality profiles of patients with remitted bipolar disorder and matched controls in a Danish sample","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695507","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This reflective paper proposesa research agenda that investigatesand questions how andif we need to assess the service design tools and their usability in the context of organisations’design maturity. Maps and tool intheservice design toolbox are perceived as straightforward by some organisations, however for organisations with low service design maturitysuch tools can pose challenges in how to utilise and leverage their potential. As a direction for future studies, this research agendasheds light on howcommon servicedesign toolsareaffected by organisational usability and maturity.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Harre, Olivia Thomassen","Abdelnour-Nocera, Jose","Li, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712565"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Infinite Interactive LTD, UK","University of West London"],"keyword":["Design toolbox challenges","Organisational design maturity","Research agenda","Service design tools","Usability assessment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proposing organisational usability as an enabler of organisational service design maturity","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ecp203","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712565","ids":["itu-f2918f36-941b-4c88-bf32-4396ca50f114"],"keyword":["Design toolbox challenges","Organisational design maturity","Research agenda","Service design tools","Usability assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-4-64D2D6278D114201C79B9C1925557C3C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ecp203","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of west london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of West London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"infinite interactive ltd uk","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Infinite Interactive LTD, UK","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Olivia Thomassen","key":"harrepau","last":"Harre","name":"Harre, Olivia Thomassen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jose","key":"abdelnournocerapau","last":"Abdelnour-Nocera","name":"Abdelnour-Nocera, Jose","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3384/ecp203","eisbn":["16503740"],"isbn":["9789180754767"],"pages":"759-768","publisher":"Linköping University Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Entanglements and Flows Service Encounters and Meanings","title":"ServDes2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f2918f36-941b-4c88-bf32-4396ca50f114"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Proposing organisational usability as an enabler of organisational service design maturity","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712565","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Thrombocytopenia (platelet count < 150 × 109/L) is common in intensive care unit (ICU) patients and is likely associated with worse outcomes. In this study we present international contemporary data on thrombocytopenia in ICU patients. Methods: We conducted a prospective cohort study in adult ICU patients in 52 ICUs across 10 countries. We assessed frequencies of thrombocytopenia, use of platelet transfusions and clinical outcomes including mortality. We evaluated pre-selected potential risk factors for the development of thrombocytopenia during ICU stay and associations between thrombocytopenia at ICU admission and 90-day mortality using pre-specified logistic regression analyses. Results: We analysed 1166 ICU patients; the median age was 63 years and 39.5% were female. Overall, 43.2% (95% confidence interval (CI) 40.4–46.1) had thrombocytopenia; 23.4% (20–26) had thrombocytopenia at ICU admission, and 19.8% (17.6–22.2) developed thrombocytopenia during their ICU stay. Absence of acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS), non-cancer-related immune deficiency, liver failure, male sex, septic shock, and bleeding at ICU admission were associated with the development of thrombocytopenia during ICU stay. Among patients with thrombocytopenia, 22.6% received platelet transfusion(s), and 64.3% of in-ICU transfusions were prophylactic. Patients with thrombocytopenia had higher occurrences of bleeding and death, fewer days alive without the use of life-support, and fewer days alive and out of hospital. Thrombocytopenia at ICU admission was associated with 90-day mortality (adjusted odds ratio 1.7; 95% CI 1.19–2.42). Conclusion: Thrombocytopenia occurred in 43% of critically ill patients and was associated with worse outcomes including increased mortality. Platelet transfusions were given to 23% of patients with thrombocytopenia and most were prophylactic.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Anthon, Carl Thomas","Pène, Frédéric","Perner, Anders","Azoulay, Elie","Puxty, Kathryn","Van De Louw, Andry","Barratt-Due, Andreas","Chawla, Sanjay","Castro, Pedro","Póvoa, Pedro","Coelho, Luis","Metaxa, Victoria","Kochanek, Matthias","Liebregts, Tobias","Kander, Thomas","Hästbacka, Johanna","Andreasen, Jo Bønding","Péju, Edwige","Nielsen, Lene Bjerregaard","Hvas, Christine Lodberg","Dufranc, Etienne","Canet, Emmanuel","Lundqvist, Linda","Wright, Christopher John","Russell, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713884"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["The PLOT-ICU Collaborators and the Nine-I Study Group"],"corresponding_author":["Russell, Lene"],"country":["Finland","France","Germany","Norway","Portugal","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Essen University Hospital","Glasgow Royal Infirmary","Hospital Cochin","Hospital Henri Mondor","King's College London","Lund University","Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center","NOVA University Lisbon","Oslo University Hospital","Paris Hospitals and Paris Descartes University","San Francisco Xavier Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","Tampere University Hospital","The Pennsylvania State University","University Hospital Cologne","University Hospital of Nantes","University of Barcelona","University of Helsinki","Weill Cornell Medicine","the Queen Elisabeth University Hospital"],"keyword":["Adult","Bleeding","Cohort Studies","Critical Illness","Female","Hemorrhage etiology","Humans","Intensive Care Units","Intensive care unit","Male","Middle Aged","Platelet Transfusion","Platelet Transfusion adverse effects","Prospective Studies","Retrospective Studies","Thrombocytopenia","Thrombocytopenia epidemiology","Thrombosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-