 Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2a6144b9-4cb9-4a0b-8d46-43cc1cf42f8d","sdu-84b22f1b-4444-42ff-8120-3563ee63b9c7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Colchicine twice a day for hand osteoarthritis (COLOR) : a double-blind, randomised, placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.87-673072","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Malnutrition is associated with high rates of complication, longer hospital stays, and increased morbidity and mortality. Malnutrition defined as undernutrition is common in patients with acquired brain injury (ABI); however, estimates vary remarkably. This study aimed to describe malnutrition at admission and after 4 weeks of subacute inpatient neurorehabilitation in patients with ABI using the new global consensus definition of malnutrition. METHODS: One hundred thirty-three patients with moderate to severe ABI consecutively admitted to a specialized neurorehabilitation hospital within a period of 4 months were screened for inclusion, of which 92 were included. Malnutrition was defined as at least 1 phenotypic criterion (weight loss, low body mass index, low muscle mass) and at least 1 etiologic criterion (reduced food intake, inflammation). Malnutrition on admission and after 4 weeks was compared using the McNemar test. RESULTS: The proportion of patients with malnutrition at admission was 42%, with more men (46%) than women (36%) fulfilling the criteria for malnutrition. The most frequent phenotypic and etiologic criteria were weight loss (56%) and inflammation (74%), respectively. During the 4 weeks of rehabilitation, the proportion of male patients fulfilling the individual criteria \"weight loss\"(difference, -21.4%) and \"inflammation\"(difference, -18.9%) decreased significantly; \"low muscle mass\"decreased borderline significant (difference, -8.9%), whereas \"low body mass index\"did not change. The proportion of female patients fulfilling individual criteria for malnutrition was stable or increased nonsignificantly. CONCLUSION: Malnutrition was common at admission to neurorehabilitation in patients with moderate to severe ABI, with more men than women fulfilling the criteria for malnutrition. The nutritional status improved after 4 weeks of rehabilitation in male patients, whereas it was largely unchanged in female patients. The results provide the basis for monitoring high-quality nutritional nursing care.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Aadal, Lena","Holst, Mette","Rasmussen, Henrik Højgaard","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Odgaard, Lene"],"cuid":["S02-099.95-665987"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Odgaard, Lene"],"keyword":["Bioimpedance analysis","Brain Injuries","Brain Injuries complications","Female","GLIM criteria","Humans","Male","Malnutrition","Malnutrition epidemiology","Nursing","Nursing research","Nutrition Assessment","Nutritional Status","Prevalence","Rehabilitation","Stroke","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"malnutrition in patients with moderate to severe acquired brain injury prevalence during 000000000004 weeks of subacute rehabilitation","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85149880576&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.95-665987","identifier":[{"id":"36749958","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85149880576","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e0e7437a-e8a6-4bc0-9bb3-63ec1ee04a46","au-fe7c0caa-2846-4aa9-aaea-95a108c90c00"],"keyword":["Brain Injuries/complications","Female","GLIM criteria","Humans","Male","Malnutrition/epidemiology","Nutrition Assessment","Prevalence","bioimpedance analysis","brain injuries","malnutrition","nursing","nursing research","nutritional status","rehabilitation","stroke","weight loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8CD03FF46AD8B82FB702F6DD9C926B8A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hammel Neurocenter, Universitetsklinik for Neurorehabilitering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Centre for Nutrition and Bowel Disease","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lena","key":"aadalpau","last":"Aadal","locid":"a3a1966b-710e-489c-a729-810645c717b5","name":"Aadal, Lena","orcid":"0000-0001-7365-3916","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"28beee90-db56-4b02-8832-fef8820eb5f4","name":"Holst, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-7458-9458","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Højgaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c242f457-53f4-4b88-82f3-d7fb297cf98c","name":"Rasmussen, Henrik Højgaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Feldbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"1b80fe7b-ba0a-45b3-aca1-48bc19a97a44","name":"Odgaard, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-9830-3282","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36749958"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/jnn.0000000000000688","issn":["08880395","19452810"],"issn_org":["08880395"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Neuroscience Nursing","pages":"38-44","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Neuroscience Nursing","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149880576"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e0e7437a-e8a6-4bc0-9bb3-63ec1ee04a46","au-fe7c0caa-2846-4aa9-aaea-95a108c90c00"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Malnutrition in Patients With Moderate to Severe Acquired Brain Injury : Prevalence During 4 Weeks of Subacute Rehabilitation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.95-665987","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Intensive care unit (ICU) patients with Coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) have an increased risk of thromboembolic complications. We describe the occurrence of thromboembolic and bleeding events in all ICU patients with COVID-19 in Denmark during the first and second waves of the pandemic. METHODS: This was a sub-study of the Danish Intensive Care Covid database, in which all patients with SARS-CoV-2 admitted to Danish ICUs from 10th March 2020 to 30th June 2021 were included. We registered coagulation variables at admission, and all thromboembolic and bleeding events, and the use of heparins during ICU stay. Variables associated with thrombosis and bleeding and any association with 90-day mortality were estimated using Cox regression analyses. RESULTS: We included 1369 patients in this sub-study; 158 (12%, 95% confidence interval 10-13) had a thromboembolic event in ICU and 309 (23%, 20-25) had a bleeding event, among whom 81 patients (6%, 4.8-7.3) had major bleeding. We found that mechanical ventilation and increased D-dimer were associated with thrombosis and mechanical ventilation, low platelet count and presence of haematological malignancy were associated with bleeding. Most patients (76%) received increased doses of thromboprophylaxis during their ICU stay. Thromboembolic events were not associated with mortality in adjusted analysis (hazard ratio 1.35 [0.91-2.01, p = .14], whereas bleeding events were 1.55 [1.18-2.05, p = .002]). CONCLUSIONS: Both thromboembolic and bleeding events frequently occurred in ICU patients with COVID-19. Based on these data, it is not apparent that increased doses of thromboprophylaxis were beneficial.","author_count":30,"contributors":["Russell, Lene","Weihe, Sarah","Madsen, Emilie Kabel","Hvas, Christine Lodberg","Leistner, Jens Wolfgang","Michelsen, Jens","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Bastiansen, Anders","Nielsen, Frederik Mølgaard","Meier, Nick","Andreasen, Anne Sofie","Ribergaard, Niels-Erik","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Sølling, Christoffer Grant","Buck, David Levarett","Bundgaard, Helle","Pedersen, Helle Scharling","Darfelt, Iben Strøm","Poulsen, Lone Musaeus","Ibsen, Michael","Plovsing, Ronni R.","Sigurdsson, Sigurdur T.","Iversen, Susanne","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Mohr, Thomas","Espelund, Ulrick Skipper","Jørgensen, Vibeke","Haase, Nicolai","Perner, Anders"],"cuid":["S03-091.33-004156"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Russell, Lene"],"keyword":["Anticoagulants adverse effects","Bleeding","COVID 19 complications","Covid 19","Critical care","Hemorrhage","Humans","Intensive Care Units","SARS CoV 2","Thromboprophylaxis","Thrombosis","Venous Thromboembolism epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Hjørring Regional Hospital"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thromboembolic and bleeding events in icu patients with covid 000000000019 a nationwide observational study","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14157","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Anders Perner holds grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation to do trials in ICU patients, including those with COVID‐19. Bodil Steen Rasmussen holds a grant from the Novo Nordisk Foundation for a trial in COVID‐19 patients. The Department of Intensive Care, Rigshospitalet, has received research funds from Fresenius Kabi, Pfizer, AM‐Pharma and Sygeforsikringen ‘Danmark’."],"id":"S03-091.33-004156","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9874434","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36263897","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85141525308","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-54fc80e4-96a1-4df7-bea8-ab067d6bd25a","au-24eeb516-8696-420f-9b42-766e9f782a2e","sdu-d7d06e58-1d0d-4640-b65a-c2432952f697"],"keyword":["Anticoagulants/adverse effects","COVID-19","COVID-19/complications","Critical Care","Hemorrhage","Humans","Intensive Care Units","SARS-CoV-2","Venous Thromboembolism/epidemiology","bleeding","thromboprophylaxis","thrombosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-7-4CD97EEF47B136BF914DE26DF9F698BE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/513850862/Russell_et_al._2022_._Thromboembolic_and_bleeding_events_in_ICU_patients_with_COVID_19_A_nationwide_observational_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14157","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/414662955/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_-_2022_-_Russell_-_Thromboembolic_and_bleeding_events_in_ICU_patients_with_COVID_19_A_nationwide_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/217820815/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_2022_Russell_Thromboembolic_and_bleeding_events_in_ICU_patients_with_COVID_19_A_nationwide_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":