e":"Suppl. 2","journal":"Quality of Life Research","pages":"97","paperid":"309.2","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Quality of Life Research","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-96e8fb77-f377-4c58-a939-a3031e037255"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Quality adjusted progression-free-period of Carfilzomib-dexamethasone maintenance therapy for patients with multiple myeloma treated for first relapse – findings from a Nordic Myeloma Study Group randomized phase II trial","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-723423","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Early healing after drug-eluting stent (DES) implantation may reduce the risk of stent thrombosis. The aim of this study was to compare patterns of early healing after implantation of the thin strut everolimus-eluting Synergy DES (Boston Scientific) or the biolimus-eluting Biomatix Neoflex DES (Biosensors). METHODS AND RESULTS: A total of 160 patients with the chronic or acute coronary syndrome were randomized 1:1 to Synergy or Biomatrix DES. Optical coherence tomography (OCT) was performed at baseline and at either 1- or 3-month follow-up. The primary endpoint was a coronary stent healing index (CSHI), a weighted index of strut coverage, neointimal hyperplasia, malapposition, and extrastent lumen. A total of 133 cases had OCT follow-up and 119 qualified for matched OCT analysis. The median CSHI score did neither differ significantly between the groups at 1 month: Synergy 8.0 (interquartile range [IQR]: 3.0; 14.0) versus Biomatrix 8.5 (IQR: 4.0; 15.0) (p = 0.47) nor at 3 months: Synergy 6.5 (IQR: 2.0; 13.0) versus Biomatrix 6.0 (IQR: 4.0; 11.0) (p = 0.83). Strut coverage was 84.6% (IQR: 72.0; 97.9) for Synergy versus 77.6% (IQR: 70.1; 90.3) for Biomatrix (p = 0.15) at 1 month and 90.3% (IQR 79.0; 98.8) (Synergy) versus 83.9% (IQR: 77.5; 92.6) (Biomatrix) (p = 0.068) at 3 months. Pooled 1- and 3-month coverage was 88.6% (IQR: 74.4; 98.4) for Synergy compared with 80.7% (IQR: 73.2; 90.8) for Biomatrix (p = 0.02). CONCLUSIONS: The early healing response after treatment with the Synergy or Biomatrix DES did not differ significantly as determined by a healing index. The Synergy DES showed overall better early stent strut coverage.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Andreasen, Lene Nyhus","Balleby, Ida R","Barkholt, Trine Ørhøj","Hebsgaard, Lasse","Terkelsen, Christian Juhl","Holck, Emil Nielsen","Jensen, Lisette O","Maeng, Michael","Dijkstra, Jouke","Antonsen, Lisbeth","Kristensen, Steen Dalby","Tu, Shengxian","Lassen, Jens F","Christiansen, Evald Høj","Holm, Niels Ramsing"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-021990"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andreasen, Lene N.","Andreasen, Lene Nyhus"],"country":["China","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leiden University","Shanghai Jiao Tong University"],"keyword":["Absorbable Implants","Coronary Artery Disease therapy","Drug Eluting Stents","Drug eluting stent","Everolimus","Humans","Optical coherence tomography","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention","Polymers","Prosthesis Design","Tomography Optical Coherence","Treatment Outcome","stent enhancement"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early healing after treatment of coronary lesions by thin strut everolimus or thicker strut biolimus eluting bioabsorbable polymer stents the sort out viii oct study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ccd.30579","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank project coordinators Pia S. Ottosen and Lars Jørgensen, and the study secretary Helle Bargsteen at Aarhus University Hospital, and statistician Lone H. J. Mogensen and data manager Jakob Hjort at the Institute of Clinical Medicine, Aarhus University. The study was supported by institutional research grants provided by Boston Scientific and Biosensors International."],"id":"S02-100.00-021990","identifier":[{"id":"36740229","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85147496435","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7fc98102-1f73-4199-8013-648f2f8fe3a4","sdu-ba131185-85a9-4548-9008-cb8f985cb797"],"keyword":["Absorbable Implants","Coronary Artery Disease/therapy","Drug-Eluting Stents","Everolimus","Humans","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention","Polymers","Prosthesis Design","Tomography, Optical Coherence","Treatment Outcome","drug-eluting stent","optical coherence tomography","stent enhancement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-54FC412E20508C20996F0E0D5C3F5ACE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/405983224/Cathet_Cardio_Intervent_-_2023_-_Andreasen_-_Early_healing_after_treatment_of_coronary_lesions_by_thin_strut_everolimus_or.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ccd.30579","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/221116285/Cathet_Cardio_Intervent_2023_Andreasen_Early_healing_after_treatment_of_coronary_lesions_by_thin_strut_everolimus_or.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU Unive