{"abstract":"How and why has the formal policy development on PPPs in Denmark evolved? How and why do PPP projects develop in Danish healthcare sector? Despite limited policy guidelines and no PPP Act, a regional approach to PPPs has occurred in the healthcare sector. There are active projects in five hospital cases that use the PPP model. PPP projects in the Danish healthcare sector develop from a mixture of reasons, which include strategic interventions from finance institutions, change in specific formal rules on financing, and necessity for regional governments to find alternatives to public financing.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Greve, Carsten","Christensen, Lene Tolstrup","Tvarnø, Christina D.","Nøhr Nielsen, Sandie","Denta, Sarah Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-299477"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Lene Tolstrup"],"keyword":["Denmark","Healthcare sector","Infrastructure","PPP policy development"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"public private partnerships in the healthcare sector limited policy guidelines but active project development in denmark","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-299477","identifier":[{"id":"000612734400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85100232927","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-fc074d7b-1bdf-4228-9802-c861c582c9a3"],"keyword":["Denmark","Healthcare sector","Infrastructure","PPP policy development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D2B8F3E5362940EDFCAE335F46B151FB"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten","key":"grevepau","last":"Greve","locid":"9967d01c-3509-4b97-8982-e9cae18b75ad","name":"Greve, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-6334-5741","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Tolstrup","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"43e4a30d-d511-4fbc-914a-2c52557d6ee8","name":"Christensen, Lene Tolstrup","orcid":"0000-0003-4991-4164","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christina D.","key":"tvarnøpau","last":"Tvarnø","locid":"551ecf4f-edf8-4741-9dcd-95e6cfe17172","name":"Tvarnø, Christina D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandie","key":"nøhrnielsenpau","last":"Nøhr Nielsen","locid":"e6a5dcdf-f8a7-4521-b1fb-60ca7bf25b75","name":"Nøhr Nielsen, Sandie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah Maria","key":"dentapau","last":"Denta","locid":"1d998ffd-8151-44cf-96f0-314db0cdbedf","name":"Denta, Sarah Maria","orcid":"0009-0008-4500-0692","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17487870.2020.1855174","issn":["17487870","17487889"],"issn_org":["17487870"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Economic Policy Reform","pages":"121-135","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Journal of Economic Policy Reform","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100232927"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-fc074d7b-1bdf-4228-9802-c861c582c9a3"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Public-private Partnerships in the Healthcare Sector : Limited Policy Guidelines, but Active Project Development in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-299477","year":"2022","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Fødevarevirksomheder samarbejder med flere danske universiteter i det højteknologiske laboratoriecenter FOODHAY, hvor avanceret biomarkør- og screeningsudstyr blandt andet bliver brugt til at udvikle fremtidens sunde, sikre og bæredygtige fødevarer","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kornholt, Heidi","Koss, Lene Hundborg","Nielsen, Anne Louise Dannesboe","Bundgaard, Lise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-355828"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"foodhay samarbejde om biomarkører og screening","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-355828","ids":["dtu-ab95cedb-565a-44be-a6de-197af9282bc4"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9F9739E1C0280499BFBF6E0303B6144C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Heidi","key":"kornholtpau","last":"Kornholt","locid":"a86f0b8a-a05f-4def-ad94-d7e1ae726470","name":"Kornholt, Heidi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Hundborg","key":"kosspau","last":"Koss","name":"Koss, Lene Hundborg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Louise Dannesboe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anne Louise Dannesboe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise","key":"bundgaardpau","last":"Bundgaard","name":"Bundgaard, Lise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09025057"],"issue":"4","journal":"Plus Proces","publisher":"TechMedia AS","publisher_org":"TechMedia A/S","status":"p","title":"Plus Proces","volume":"36"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ab95cedb-565a-44be-a6de-197af9282bc4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"FOODHAY-samarbejde om biomarkører og screening","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-355828","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: To quantify the potential decline in dynamic lung volumes following coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) in the general population. Methods: A prospective matched cohort study of adult Copenhagen General Population Study (CGPS) participants with a prepandemic spirometry available. CGPS individuals with positive severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) polymerase chain reaction (PCR) test performed repeat spirometry, a questionnaire regarding respiratory symptoms, and diffusing capacity test for carbon monoxide. A matched uninfected CGPS control sample was used, and simple regression and linear mixed effect models were computed to study lung function decline. Results: A total of 606 individuals were included; 92/107 (85.9%) with positive SARS-CoV-2 PCR test experienced coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) symptoms and 12 (11.2%) were hospitalized. Spirometry was performed at median 5.6 months (interquartile range, 3.9-12.8) after positive SARS-CoV-2 PCR test. COVID-19 was associated with adjusted 7.3 mL (95% confidence interval [CI],. 3-14.3) and 22.6 mL (95% CI, 13.1-32.0) steeper decline in annual forced expiratory volume in first second (FEV1) and FVC or total 113.8 and 301.3 mL lower FEV1 and FVC from baseline to follow-up. Results were robust in analyses restricted to individuals not requiring hospitalization. Conclusions: COVID-19-related declines of dynamic lung volume in the general population not requiring hospitalization were small but measurable.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Iversen, Katrine K.","Afzal, Shoaib","Ahlström, Magnus G.","Nordestgaard, Børge G","Schneider, Uffe V.","Nielsen, Lene","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Benfield, Thomas","Ronit, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-412115"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coronavirus disease 2019","Forced vital capacity","Respiratory symptoms","Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2","Spirometry","forced expiratory volume in 1 second"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lung function decline in relation to covid 000000000019 in the general population a matched cohort study with prepandemic assessment of lung function","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jiab636","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-412115","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8755346","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85125371990","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34979029","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1f61541f-f6bc-4148-af3c-863de863a235"],"keyword":["coronavirus disease 2019","forced expiratory volume in 1 second","forced vital capacity","respiratory symptoms","severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2","spirometry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-545B67B1CE0902B70C91D9C4035FF481"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jiab636","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/321553528/Lung_Function_Decline_in_Relation_to_COVID_19_i.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Katrine K.","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Katrine K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Shoaib","key":"afzalpau","last":"Afzal","locid":"5292675c-4f94-4371-94bc-04b2e716ee01","name":"Afzal, Shoaib","orcid":"0000-0002-1442-4694","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Magnus G.","key":"ahlströmpau","last":"Ahlström","name":"Ahlström, Magnus G.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Børge G.","key":"nordestgaardpau","last":"Nordestgaard","locid":"733103b5-ddc2-416f-a686-48e694154a82","name":"Nordestgaard, Børge G","name_org":"Nordestgaard, Børge G.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Uffe V.","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","name":"Schneider, Uffe V.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Klaus","key":"kofoedpau","last":"Kofoed","locid":"ec141562-c77f-498d-af6e-db9e08a4e895","name":"Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","name_org":"Kofoed, Klaus","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Thomas","key":"benfieldpau","last":"Benfield","locid":"03fdbbba-4bc0-41aa-845b-81ba0bded9ba","name":"Benfield, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-0698-9385","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andreas","key":"ronitpau","last":"Ronit","name":"Ronit, Andreas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34979029"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/infdis/jiab636","issn":["00221899","15376613"],"issn_org":["00221899"],"issue":"8","journal":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","pages":"1308-1316","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","title_org":"Journal of Infectious Diseases","volume":"225"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125371990"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1f61541f-f6bc-4148-af3c-863de863a235"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lung Function Decline in Relation to COVID-19 in the General Population : A Matched Cohort Study With Prepandemic Assessment of Lung Function","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-412115","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Testicular germ cell tumours (TGCTs) have a high sensitivity to chemotherapy and a high cure rate, although with serious adverse effects. In the search for tumour suppressive drugs, the RANKL inhibitor Denosumab, used to treat osteoporosis, came up as a candidate since RANKL signalling was recently identified in the testis. Methods: Expression of RANKL, RANK and OPG, and the effects of RANKL inhibition were investigated in human TGCTs, TGCT-derived cell-lines, and TGCT-xenograft models. Serum RANKL was measured in TGCT-patients. Results: RANKL, RANK, and OPG were expressed in germ cell neoplasia in situ (GCNIS), TGCTs, and TGCT-derived cell lines. RANKL-inhibition reduced proliferation of seminoma-derived TCam-2 cells, but had no effect on embryonal carcinoma-derived NTera2 cells. Pretreatment with Denosumab did not augment the effect of cisplatin in vitro. However, inhibition of RANKL in vivo reduced tumour growth exclusively in the TCam-2-xenograft model and Denosumab-treatment decreased proliferation in human GCNIS cultures. In TGCT-patients serum RANKL had no prognostic value. Conclusions: This study shows that the RANKL signalling system is expressed in GCNIS and seminoma where RANKL inhibition suppresses tumour growth in vitro and in vivo. Future studies are needed to determine whether RANKL is important for the malignant transformation or transition from GCNIS to invasive tumours.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Andreassen, Christine Hjorth","Lorenzen, Mette","Nielsen, John E.","Kafai Yahyavi, Sam","Toft, Birgitte Grønkær","Ingerslev, Lars Roed","Clemmensen, Christoffer","Rasmussen, Lene Juel","Bokemeyer, Carsten","Juul, Anders","Jørgensen, Anne Juul","Jensen, Martin Blomberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-419563"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Hamburg"],"leve