{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Sand, Anne-Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-129005"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deltagelse","Medbestemmelse","Selvorganisering","Unge"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-DSKD"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-DSKD"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"retfærdiggørelse af selvorganisering mellem ulighed og kritik","src":["arkk"],"src-code":["DI-ART-DSKD"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/69485955/Sand_2022_Retf_rdigg_relse_af_selvorganisering_mellem_ulighed_og_kritik.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-129005","ids":["arkk-55547b18-3687-4c21-87f4-ee28ac55e7e7"],"keyword":["Deltagelse","Medbestemmelse","Nej","Selvorganisering","Sociologisk kritik","Unge","Urbane kulturer"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ABBA3D4A07910428F4F067082D405EAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/69485955/Sand_2022_Retf_rdigg_relse_af_selvorganisering_mellem_ulighed_og_kritik.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"design school kolding","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-DSKD","l3nn":"Design School Kolding","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Design School Kolding","namevar":["Design School Kolding","Design School Kolding, Design for Play - Lab for Play and Design"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-DSKD","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne-Lene","key":"sandpau","last":"Sand","locid":"42f07f0b-895a-40fc-a8fe-f15cc9d5b4d7","name":"Sand, Anne-Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-0617-8913","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria","key":"bruseliusjensenpedh","last":"Bruselius-Jensen","name":"Bruselius-Jensen, Maria","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne-Mette W.","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anne-Mette W.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788772164656"],"isbn":["9788772164649"],"pages":"142-161","place":"Frydenlund Academic","status":"p","subtitle":"- tendenser, udfordringer og opmærksomhedspunkter","title":"Unges medbestemmelse og samfundsdeltagelse"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkk-55547b18-3687-4c21-87f4-ee28ac55e7e7"],"src":["Design School Kolding"],"title":"Retfærdiggørelse af selvorganisering - mellem ulighed og kritik","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-129005","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Renal perfusion may redistribute from cortex to medulla during systemic hypovolaemia and after renal ischaemia for other reasons, but there is no consensus on this matter. We studied renal perfusion after renal ischaemia and reperfusion. Methods: Renal perfusion distribution was examined by use of 153Gadolinium-labeled microspheres (MS) after 2 h (hrs) and 4 h ischaemia of the pig kidney followed by 4 h of reperfusion. Intra-arterial injected MS are trapped in the glomeruli in renal cortex, which means that MS are not present in the medulla under normal physiological conditions. Results: Visual evaluation after reperfusion demonstrated that MS redistributed from the renal cortex to the medulla in 6 out of 16 pigs (38%) subjected to 4 h ischaemia and in one out of 18 pigs subjected to 2 h ischaemia. Central renal uptake of MS covering the medullary/total renal uptake was significantly higher in kidneys subjected to 4 h ischaemia compared with pigs subjected to 2 h ischaemia (69 ± 5% vs. 63 ± 1%, p < 0.001), and also significantly higher than in the contralateral kidney (69 ± 5% vs. 63 ± 2%, p < 0.001). Analysis of blood and urine demonstrated no presence of radioactivity. Conclusion: The study demonstrated the presence of MS in the renal medulla in response to renal ischaemia and reperfusion suggesting that severe ischaemia and reperfusion of the pig kidney leads to opening of functional shunts bypassing glomeruli.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rehling, Michael","Pedersen, Stine S","Frøkiær, Jørgen","Nielsen, Lene Elsebeth","Flø, Christian","Jespersen, Bente","Keller, Anna Krarup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-159782"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Keller, Anna Krarup"],"keyword":["Microspheres","Renal blood flow","Renal perfusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"corticomedullary shunting after ischaemia and reperfusion in the porcine kidney","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12882-022-02780-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-159782","identifier":[{"id":"35428270","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85128415211","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9013123","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-3541933f-0846-4079-a90b-d8e7d47fe1ee"],"keyword":["Microspheres","Renal blood flow","Renal ischaemia","Renal perfusion","Renal redistribution","Renal shunts"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B50BFC5EB0F78DAA491D742441FB66E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12882-022-02780-0","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Nuclear Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"rehlingpau","last":"Rehling","locid":"ff6eb9ad-54ef-4594-bdfa-46efb47edfb5","name":"Rehling, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Gram","key":"skjøthpau","last":"Skjøth","locid":"8b05f7e2-3436-4c80-8c04-e9d331d26b7d","name":"Pedersen, Stine S","name_org":"Skjøth, Stine Gram","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"frøkiærpau","last":"Frøkiær","locid":"49d24192-9cad-4d32-88ee-cf46bb315b72","name":"Frøkiær, Jørgen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Elsebeth","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c9ca3b12-deee-4fb0-a4b3-42b378a642f1","name":"Nielsen, Lene Elsebeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"fløpau","last":"Flø","locid":"0af7efc2-fa90-4539-8a15-4db7f844521b","name":"Flø, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-1326-7495","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"9e482e87-a01d-4d24-9a00-45470c9fd19d","name":"Jespersen, Bente","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna Krarup","key":"kellerpau","last":"Keller","locid":"dfc7b528-236e-4072-90fe-df0750735ada","name":"Keller, Anna Krarup","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35428270"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12882-022-02780-0","issn":["14712369"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Nephrology","paperid":"146","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Nephrology","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85128415211"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3541933f-0846-4079-a90b-d8e7d47fe1ee"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Corticomedullary shunting after ischaemia and reperfusion in the porcine kidney?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-159782","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Avanceret proteomisk og metabolomisk udstyr indgår i det højteknologiske laboratoriecenter FOODHAY, hvor fødevarevirksomheder samarbejder med forskere om at udvikle fremtidens fødevarer. Proteomik- og metabolomikplatformen omfatter udstyr, som kan identificere fødevarernes mindre bestanddele","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kornholt, Heidi","Koss, Lene Hundborg","Nielsen, Anne Louise Dannesboe","Strandsby, Kristine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335100"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"foodhay samarbejde om proteomik og metabolomik","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-335100","ids":["dtu-664b67d1-1948-43ae-975b-975b8f5c10b3"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-77538499EC2D098A16BA71F078E01EEA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Heidi","key":"kornholtpau","last":"Kornholt","locid":"a86f0b8a-a05f-4def-ad94-d7e1ae726470","name":"Kornholt, Heidi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Hundborg","key":"kosspau","last":"Koss","name":"Koss, Lene Hundborg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Louise Dannesboe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anne Louise Dannesboe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine","key":"strandsbypau","last":"Strandsby","name":"Strandsby, Kristine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09025057"],"issue":"6","journal":"Plus Proces","publisher":"TechMedia AS","publisher_org":"TechMedia A/S","status":"p","title":"Plus Proces","volume":"36"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-664b67d1-1948-43ae-975b-975b8f5c10b3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"FOODHAY-samarbejde om proteomik og metabolomik","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335100","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Studies in human-computer interaction recommend creating fewer than ten personas, based on stakeholders’ limitations to cognitively process and use personas. However, no existing studies offer empirical support for having fewer rather than more personas. Investigating this matter, thirty-seven participants interacted with five and fifteen personas using an interactive persona system, choosing one persona to design for. Our study results from eye-tracking and survey data suggest that when using interactive persona systems, the number of personas can be increased from the conventionally suggested ‘less than ten’, without significant negative effects on user perceptions or task performance, and with the positive effects of increasing engagement with the personas, having a more diverse representation of the end-user population, as well as users accessing personas from more varied demographic groups for a design task. Using the interactive persona system, users adjusted their information processing style by spending less time on each persona when presented with fifteen personas, while still absorbing a similar amount of information than with five personas, implying that more efficient information processing strategies are applied with more personas. The results highlight the importance of designing interactive persona systems to support users’ browsing of more personas.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Salminen, joni","Jung, Soon-Gyo","Nielsen, Lene","Şengün, Sercan","Jansen, Bernard J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383001"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Qatar","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qatar Computing Research institute","University of Vaasa","lllinois State University"],"keyword":["Personas","User segmentation","User study","number of personas"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how does varying the number of personas affect user perceptions and behavior challenging the small personas hypothesis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhcs.2022.102915","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383001","identifier":[{"id":"85136714610","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-758cff4d-e904-4190-a654-1548ae53b96d"],"keyword":["Personas","User segmentation","number of personas","user study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2BE68C9A6E87E26EE755743D76590F54"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhcs.2022.102915","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1071581922001367/pdfft?md5=769975908dc0bd636510fd50bf1a5f9b&pid=1-s2.0-S1071581922001367-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101333592/1-s2.0-S1071581922001367-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"university of vaasa","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Vaasa","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"qa","key":"qatar computing research institute","loc":["Qatar","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Qatar Computing Research institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"lllinois state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"lllinois State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"joni","key":"salminenpau","last":"Salminen","name":"Salminen, joni","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Soon-Gyo","key":"jungpau","last":"Jung","name":"Jung, Soon-Gyo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sercan","key":"şengünpau","last":"Şengün","name":"Şengün, Sercan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernard J.","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","name":"Jansen, Bernard J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhcs.2022.102915","issn":["10715819","10959300"],"issn_org":["10715819"],"journal":"International Journal of Human-Computer Studies","pages":"102915","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Human-Computer Studies","volume":"168"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136714610"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-758cff4d-e904-4190-a654-1548ae53b96d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How does varying the number of personas affect user perceptions and behavior? : Challenging the ‘small personas’ hypothesis!","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383001","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Personas are a technique for enhanced understanding of users and customers to improve the user-centered design of systems and products. Their creation can be categorized using three persona creation methodologies: Qualitative, Quantitative, and Mixed Methods. Despite the apparent differences in these methodologies, no previous review has systemically compared and contrasted the strengths and weaknesses of each of these methodologies for persona development.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jansen, Bernard J.","Nielsen, Lene","Guan, Kathleen","Salminen, joni"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383782"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Qatar","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgetown University","Qatar Computing Research institute"],"keyword":["Algorithmically Generated Personas","Persona Analytics","Persona Science"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to create personas three persona creation methodologies with implications for practical employment","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17705/1pais.14301","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383782","identifier":[{"id":"85131374088","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ad3af1ee-b60e-4a80-bb14-5c52e604eb17"],"keyword":["Algorithmically-Generated Personas","Persona Analytics","Persona Science"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9FE21D2FE4ED172886EC80A62BDD492C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102674664/Osuva_Jansen_Jung_Nielsen_Guan_Salminen_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102597727/How_to_Create_Personas_Three_Persona_Creation_Methodologies_with.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17705/1pais.14301","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/pajais/vol14/iss3/1/","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1267&context=pajais","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://osuva.uwasa.fi/bitstream/handle/10024/14158/Osuva_Jansen_Jung_Nielsen_Guan_Salminen_2022.pdf?sequence=2","type":"rem","url":"https://osuva.uwasa.fi/bitstream/handle/10024/14158/Osuva_Jansen_Jung_Nielsen_Guan_Salminen_2022.pdf?sequence=2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"qa","key":"qatar computing research institute","loc":["Qatar","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Qatar Computing Research institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"georgetown university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgetown University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernard J.","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","name":"Jansen, Bernard J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathleen","key":"guanpau","last":"Guan","name":"Guan, Kathleen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"joni","key":"salminenpau","last":"Salminen","name":"Salminen, joni","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17705/1pais.14301","issn":["19437544"],"issue":"3","journal":"Pacific Asia Journal of the Association for Information Systems","paperid":"1","publisher":"Association for Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Pacific Asia Journal of the Association for Information Systems","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131374088"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ad3af1ee-b60e-4a80-bb14-5c52e604eb17"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How to Create Personas : Three Persona Creation Methodologies with Implications for Practical Employment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383782","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Context: Falling insulin requirements often lead to considerations of whether a pregnancy can continue safely or if delivery is indicated. Objective: To evaluate prevalence and predictors of falling insulin requirements in pregnant women with preexisting diabetes delivering preterm and to explore the relationship to fetal asphyxia and neonatal morbidity. Methods: A prospective cohort study of 101 consecutive singleton pregnant women with preexisting diabetes delivering preterm < 37 weeks (68 type 1 and 33 type 2 diabetes) where the prevalence of falling insulin requirements (≥20%) before delivery was recorded. Results: In total, 27% (27/101) experienced falling insulin requirements of median 30% (interquartile range 24-40) before delivery. In all women with type 1 diabetes, the prevalence was 37% (25/68), whereas it was 43% (24/56) in those with indicated preterm delivery and 6% (2/33) among women with type 2 diabetes. In women with type 1 diabetes and indicated preterm delivery, falling insulin requirements were first identified at 34+ 5 (33+ 6-35+ 4) weeks + days and delivery occurred 3 (1-9) days later. Gestational age at delivery, prevalence of suspected fetal asphyxia, and neonatal morbidity were similar in women with and without falling insulin requirements. Neither glycemic control, nausea, or preeclampsia was associated with falling insulin requirement. Conclusion: Falling insulin requirements often preceded preterm delivery in women with type 1 diabetes, foremost when preterm delivery was indicated, but was not related to fetal asphyxia or neonatal morbidity. Whether falling insulin requirements in late pregnancy are a warning sign of placental insufficiency or mainly reflects variations in normal physiology needs further investigation.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Søholm, Julie C.","Do, Nicoline C.","Vestgaard, Marianne","Ásbjörnsdóttir, Björg","Nørgaard, Sidse K.","Pedersen, Berit W.","Storgaard, Lone","Nielsen, Birgitte B.","Holmager, Pernille","Ringholm, Lene","Damm, Peter","Mathiesen, Elisabeth R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-510569"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Diabetes","Obstetric outcome","Pregnancy","Preterm delivery"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"falling insulin requirement in pregnant women with diabetes delivering preterm prevalence predictors and consequences","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-510569","identifier":[{"id":"85130766741","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35303076","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c4374c4a-4076-4d9b-b326-083cf139b7a0"],"keyword":["diabetes","falling insulin requirement","obstetric outcome","pregnancy","preterm delivery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F13416CB82AE9DF4FE749086D13F8BFF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Julie C.","key":"søholmpau","last":"Søholm","name":"Søholm, Julie C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicoline C.","key":"dopau","last":"Do","name":"Do, Nicoline C.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marianne","key":"vestgaardpau","last":"Vestgaard","name":"Vestgaard, Marianne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Björg","key":"ásbjörnsdóttirpau","last":"Ásbjörnsdóttir","name":"Ásbjörnsdóttir, Björg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sidse K.","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","name":"Nørgaard, Sidse K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Berit W.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Berit W.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lone","key":"storgaardpau","last":"Storgaard","name":"Storgaard, Lone","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte B.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Birgitte B.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Pernille","key":"holmagerpau","last":"Holmager","name":"Holmager, Pernille","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"ringholmpau","last":"Ringholm","name":"Ringholm, Lene","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Peter","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","locid":"884d03d5-5981-4d33-80c6-adb21f836deb","name":"Damm, Peter","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Elisabeth R.","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"3acd58f4-6d64-4a89-a406-d2f43b310500","name":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35303076"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/clinem/dgac159","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","volume":"107"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130766741"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c4374c4a-4076-4d9b-b326-083cf139b7a0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Falling Insulin Requirement in Pregnant Women With Diabetes Delivering Preterm : Prevalence, Predictors, and Consequences","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-510569","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Intermittent catheterization is the gold standard method for bladder management in individuals with urinary retention and/or incontinence. It is therefore important to understand the performance of urinary catheters, especially on parameters associated to risks of developing urinary tract infections, and that may impact the quality of life for urinary catheter users. Examples of such parameters include, urine flowrate, occurrence of flow-stops, and residual urine left in the bladder after flow-stop. Reliable in-vitro and/or ex-vivo laboratory models represent a strong asset to assess the performance of urinary catheters, preceding and guiding in-vivo animal studies and/or human clinical studies. Existing laboratory models are generally simplified, covering only portions of the catheterization process, or poorly reflect clinical procedures. In this work, we developed an ex-vivo porcine lower urinary tract model that better reflects the catheterization procedure in humans and allows to investigate the performance of standard of care catheters. The performance of three standard of care catheters was investigated in the developed model showing significant differences in terms of flowrate. No differences were detected in terms of residual volume in the bladder at first flow-stop also when tuning the abdominal pressure to mimic a sitting down and standing up position. A newly discovered phenomenon named hammering was detected and measured. Lastly, mucosal suction was observed and measured in all standard of care catheters, raising the concern for microtrauma during catheterization and a need for new and improved urinary catheter designs. Results obtained with the ex-vivo model were compared to in-vivo studies, highlighting similar concerns.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Tentor, Fabio","Grønholt Schrøder, Brit","Nielsen, Simon","Schertiger, Lars","Stærk, Kristian","Andersen, Thomas Emil","Bagi, Per","Feldskov Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-584574"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Tentor, Fabio"],"keyword":["Animals","Humans","Quality of Life","Swine","Urinary Bladder","Urinary Catheterization methods","Urinary Catheters","Urinary Retention therapy","Urinary Tract Infections epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COLO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-COLO","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of an ex vivo porcine lower urinary tract model to evaluate the performance of urinary catheters","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-21122-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-584574","identifier":[{"id":"85140456138","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36280778","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9592621","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-27a97d7d-5dbb-4d89-ac10-178bb1f431ca"],"keyword":["Animals","Humans","Quality of Life","Swine","Urinary Bladder","Urinary Catheterization/methods","Urinary Catheters","Urinary Retention/therapy","Urinary Tract Infections/epidemiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9A79B8F9AA98A6C3B79F66B2717A2476"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-21122-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/211489705/Development_of_an_ex_vivo_porcine_lower_urinary_tract_model_to_evaluate_the_performance_of_urinary_catheters.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"coloplast","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COLO","l3nl":"Coloplast Group","l3nn":"Coloplast","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Coloplast","namevar":["Coloplast Research"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COLO","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Microbiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"tentorpau","last":"Tentor","name":"Tentor, Fabio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit","key":"grønholtschrøderpau","last":"Grønholt Schrøder","name":"Grønholt Schrøder, Brit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Simon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"schertigerpau","last":"Schertiger","name":"Schertiger, Lars","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"stærkpau","last":"Stærk","locid":"0e1429ba-881e-4a1a-b489-bdfbbaae2599","name":"Stærk, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-2410-0375","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"emilandersenpau","last":"Emil Andersen","locid":"87fae7cd-ed6a-4d21-80cc-e13da9f91099","name":"Andersen, Thomas Emil","name_org":"Emil Andersen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-9453-1141","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"bagipau","last":"Bagi","name":"Bagi, Per","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"feldskovnielsenpau","last":"Feldskov Nielsen","name":"Feldskov Nielsen, Lene","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36280778"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-022-21122-6","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"17818","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140456138"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Coloplast Group","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-27a97d7d-5dbb-4d89-ac10-178bb1f431ca"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Development of an ex-vivo porcine lower urinary tract model to evaluate the performance of urinary catheters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-584574","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The number of patients with dementia admitted to hospitals is increasing. However, the care and treatment of these patients tends to be suboptimal. A response to this is a widespread implementation of educational initiatives. Nevertheless, the effect of such initiatives is questioned. The aim of this study was to investigate the impact of a dementia education intervention by examining the self-reported outcomes of general hospital staff and exploring the staff’s experiences of these outcomes. An explanatory sequential mixed-methods design framed the study method. The quantitative data collection included repeated questionnaires: pre-intervention (n = 849), one month post-intervention (n = 618), and five months post-intervention (n = 468) followed by a qualitative data collection using interviews (n = 16). The GRAMMS guideline was followed. The integration of the quantitative and qualitative results suggests that the impact of the education intervention can be ascribed to the interdisciplinary focus, which facilitated a comprehensive commitment to creating careful solutions for patients with dementia. A prioritization of person over task seems to be assisted by an improved interdisciplinary cooperation initiated by the inclusion of all employed staff at the hospital in a dementia education intervention.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Toubøl, Annemarie","Moestrup, Lene","Thomsen, Katja","Ryg, Jesper","Hansen, Dennis Lund","Foldager, Mette","Jakobsen, Søren","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne"],"cuid":["S02-093.23-049094"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Toubøl, Annemarie"],"keyword":["Dementia Friendly Hospital","Hospitals","Mixed methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of an education intervention on the approach of hospital staff to patients with dementia in a danish general hospital setting an explanatory sequential mixed methods study","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/20571585211022971","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.23-049094","identifier":[{"id":"85132285292","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-7008cd0a-0f13-48bd-b820-3e4422078426","ucl-150d2e66-e83a-4f53-9385-00e8fb0e2fe8"],"keyword":["dementia education","dementia-friendly hospital","explanatory sequential design","hospitals","mixed methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9C044674ADCB1353E8044BB3C755334F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/20571585211022971","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Anvendt Sundhedsforskning","UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen i Vejle"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Geriatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annemarie Ginnerup","key":"toubølpau","last":"Toubøl","locid":"28296f4e-241d-4748-bb8e-5364a07e3d11","name":"Toubøl, Annemarie Ginnerup","orcid":"0000-0003-4794-8862","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Katja","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"26fcee0e-9fd1-47db-847b-ba123b840681","name":"Thomsen, Katja","orcid":"0000-0002-0454-836X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"moestruppau","last":"Moestrup","locid":"b5ec9bc0-552c-4f92-9dd2-df00a997660c","name":"Moestrup, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-0978-664X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"rygpau","last":"Ryg","locid":"c63490d8-ba13-4875-bf40-82c4aebbab6f","name":"Ryg, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8641-3062","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis","key":"lundhansenpau","last":"Lund Hansen","locid":"f43fdc60-e5bf-441a-884b-d1ef5a373194","name":"Hansen, Dennis Lund","name_org":"Lund Hansen, Dennis","orcid":"0000-0002-4478-1297","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"foldagerpau","last":"Foldager","locid":"49f35a8b-a980-4605-8675-6e98f1a77052","name":"Foldager, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"71b9b920-5bcf-4afe-99fd-c350132a7468","name":"Jakobsen, Søren","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe Susanne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52791e3c-f692-493c-9085-fd6de2c829ac","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-3954-7551","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Lund","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"beb26e20-c770-48ba-a985-9dfbf9392541","name":"Hansen, Dennis Lund","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/20571585211022971","issn":["20571585","20571593"],"issn_org":["20571585"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nordic Journal of Nursing Research","pages":"28-41","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Nursing Research","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132285292"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-7008cd0a-0f13-48bd-b820-3e4422078426","ucl-150d2e66-e83a-4f53-9385-00e8fb0e2fe8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"The impact of an education intervention on the approach of hospital staff to patients with dementia in a Danish general hospital setting : An explanatory sequential mixed-methods study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.23-049094","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Drug survival is an important proxy measure for effectiveness of treatments for inflammatory diseases such as rheumatoid arthritis (RA), axial spondyloarthritis (AxSpA), psoriatic arthritis (PsA), and psoriasis. The objective of this study was to examine the real-life drug survival of biologics and novel small-molecule therapies across various disease entities such as RA, AxSpA, PsA, and psoriasis. Methods: We performed a nationwide cohort study using the prospective nationwide registries DANBIO and DERMBIO, comprising all patients treated with biologics or novel small-molecule therapies for RA, AxSpA, PsA, and psoriasis between January 2015 through May 2021 (DANBIO) and November 2009 to November 2019 (DERMBIO). Drug survival was visualized using Kaplan-Meier curves, and Cox proportional hazards models were used to calculate adjusted Hazard Ratios (HRs) with 95% confidence intervals (CIs) for risk of discontinuing therapy. Findings: The study comprised a total of 12,089 patients (17,903 treatment series), including 5,104 RA patients (7,867 series), 2,157 AxSpA patients (3,016 series3), 2,551 PsA patients (3,313 series), and 2,577 psoriasis patients (3,707 series). In confounder-adjusted models drug survival in RA was highest for rituximab followed by baricitinib, etanercept and tocilizumab respectively. For AxSpA, drug survival was high for golimumab compared to all other drugs, followed by secukinumab and etanercept and lowest for infliximab. For PsA, tofacitinib and infliximab had the lowest drug survival compared to all other drugs. All other drugs performed almost equally well with a tendency of a somewhat higher drug survival for golimumab, followed by secukinumab and ixekizumab. For psoriasis, drug survival was generally highest for guselkumab. Interpretation: Differing treatment responses to drugs with various modes of action across RA, AxSpA, PsA and psoriasis emphasize that although these diseases have many overlaps in their pathogenesis, there is a need for an individualized treatment approach that considers the underlying disease, patient profile, and treatment history. Funding: None","author_count":18,"contributors":["Egeberg, Alexander","Rosenø, Nana Aviaaja Lippert","Aagaard, David","Lørup, Erik Hillo","Nielsen, Mia-Louise","Nymand, Lea","Kristensen, Lars Erik","Thyssen, Jacob P.","Thomsen, Simon Francis","Cordtz, René","Loft, Nikolai","Skov, Lone","Bryld, Lars Erik","Rasmussen, Mads Kirchheiner","Højgaard, Pil","Kristensen, Salome","Dreyer, Lene"],"cuid":["S03-099.88-010613"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Egeberg, Alexander"],"keyword":["Axial spondyloarthritis","Drug survival","Psoriasis","Psoriatic arthritis","Rheumatoid arthritis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["DERMBIO - National Psoriasis Database"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drug survival of biologics and novel immunomodulators for rheumatoid arthritis axial spondyloarthritis psoriatic arthritis and psoriasis a nationwide cohort study from the danbio and dermbio registries","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85124755183&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-099.88-010613","identifier":[{"id":"000820186100014","type":"wos"},{"id":"35183936","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85124755183","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-deada1d2-f1dc-49e5-ae49-28367ffee361","au-01c61e02-8d81-4026-8d1a-2efd5f368ee7","ku-c2