n, Lene Hyldahl","name_org":"Ebbesen, Lene H.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7 6 8","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John","key":"bæchpau","last":"Bæch","locid":"fb89f6a9-0739-4b83-b3ee-c8485e627df1","name":"Bæch, John","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva K.","key":"haastruppau","last":"Haastrup","name":"Haastrup, Eva K.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pär","key":"josefssonpau","last":"Josefsson","name":"Josefsson, Pär","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"thorsgaardpau","last":"Thorsgaard","name":"Thorsgaard, Michael","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Peter","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","locid":"99209ae2-af19-43b5-8bf5-1363deca3794","name":"Brown, Peter","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7 8","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tarec C.","key":"elgalalypau","last":"El-Galaly","locid":"1d601b96-c71c-4a76-ac06-4d95e0a50a74","name":"El-Galaly, Tarec Christoffer","name_org":"El-Galaly, Tarec C.","orcid":"0000-0002-4406-380X","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Stauffer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dd2de49b-c3d9-49cb-bb8d-e92119e0b2d1","name":"Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","orcid":"0000-0002-8418-6708","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Joachim","key":"weischenfeldtpau","last":"Weischenfeldt","locid":"06986045-e643-4b44-ae62-6ecea626f524","name":"Weischenfeldt, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0002-3917-5524","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Kirsten","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"82ff4ce1-979f-44c9-b095-72c4a3dca507","name":"Grønbæk, Kirsten","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35124694"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41409-022-01580-2","issn":["02683369","09513078"],"issn_org":["02683369"],"issue":"4","journal":"Bone Marrow Transplantation","pages":"674-677","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Bone Marrow Transplantation","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124283381"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-180888cb-e12c-4272-b760-31584bef8733","au-1206caaa-eac2-4dab-943f-be9cc7d4a653","ku-13899c42-55cb-4340-ba2a-fc233c31ca3e","sdu-2ced833c-ddf3-4c17-a0ab-56e56ce17df0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Level of unique T cell clonotypes is associated with clonal hematopoiesis and survival in patients with lymphoma undergoing ASCT","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-093.19-001236","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Overweight patients with cancer are frequently reduced in chemotherapy dose due to toxicity concerns, although previous studies have indicated that dose reduction (DR) of overweight patients results in comparable toxicity but may compromise overall survival (OS). Current evidence regarding DR in patients with acute myeloid leukaemia (AML) is limited. To investigate the association between DR and outcome among overweight patients with AML we analysed a Danish nationwide cohort of overweight adult AML patients treated with remission induction chemotherapy. Among 536 patients identified, 10.1% were categorized as DR defined as 95% or less of full body surface area (BSA)-based dose. Risk factors for DR were high body mass index (BMI) and BSA, therapy-related AML and favourable cytogenetics. No significant differences were observed for rates of complete remission (CR), 30- and 90-day mortality between DR and non-DR patients. Furthermore, DR did not affect median relapse-free survival (RFS) [DR, 14.5 (95% confidence interval, 9.0-41.7) months; non-DR, 15.0 (12.3-19.3)] with an adjusted difference in five-year restricted mean survival time (Δ5y-RMST) of 0.2 (-8.4 to 8.8) months nor median OS (DR, 17.0 [11.9 to 45.5] months; non-DR, 17.5 [14.8 to 20.5]) with an adjusted Δ5y-RMST of 0.8 (-5.7 to 7.3) months. In conclusion, we found no statistically significant association between DR and outcomes among overweight patients with AML. However, we acknowledge the limited sample size and encourage further studies in this important subject.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Kristensen, Daniel Tuyet","Nielsen, Lars Børty","Jakobsen, Lasse Hjort","Kristensen, Tove-Christina Choe","Jepsen, Lene Østergaard","Schöllkopf, Claudia","Theilgaard-Mönch, Kim","El-Galaly, Tarec Christoffer","Roug, Anne Stidsholt","Severinsen, Marianne Tang"],"cuid":["S04-095.76-006726"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Kristensen, Daniel Tuyet"],"keyword":["Chemotherapy","Dose reduction","Overweight and obesity","Survival","acute leukaemia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of chemotherapy dose reductions in overweight patients with acute myeloid leukaemia a danish nationwide cohort study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bjh.18448","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Our profound gratitude to everyone who has participated in forming and collecting data for The Danish Acute Leukaemia Registry (DNLR) and The Danish Clinical Quality Program—National Clinical Registries (RKKP) for providing and governing the data. Financial support for this study was provided by the Danish Cancer Society (Grant R94‐A5768‐B2403) (for Marianne T. Severinsen)."],"id":"S04-095.76-006726","identifier":[{"id":"85137495477","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36083781","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9825846","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-8ab86ca7-f4a6-4b05-aa5e-4439a3925960","au-6fdd8d8f-c31f-433a-8670-41344b355d8a","ku-08e58f93-9ff0-4543-afc1-a7b000efba51","sdu-508cd54d-9afa-451a-9cae-34ee0dc9c7c0"],"keyword":["acute leukaemia","chemotherapy","dose reduction","overweight and obesity","survival"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-E5EB45E33C3E8FD6EB53F138624FB538"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://www