{"abstract":"Improving the long-term prognosis of ulcerative colitis (UC) requires sustained deep mucosal colonic healing with histologic remission, making the study of colonic tissue regeneration essential. In experimental colitis models, lipid metabolites are recognized as pivotal components of this process. This study aimed to describe the kinetics of wound healing and lipid metabolites engaged in regeneration in the normal colonic mucosa and how they are affected in UC to reveal new therapeutic targets. Experimental colonic wounds were created endoscopically in quiescent UC (n=21) and controls (n=9), and the healing process was surveilled by serial endoscopies and cross-sectional wound biopsies post-wounding. Biopsies were analyzed by liquid chromatography coupled with mass spectrometry. Endoscopic wound scores were significantly higher in UC at day two (p=0.001) and seven (p<0.0001) post-wounding, demonstrating a prolonged wound healing process. The wound scores were correlated with lipid mediators crucial for normal regeneration and sustained UC-specific changes in key phospholipids and eicosanoids, i.e., lysophosphatidylcholine, phosphatidylcholine, lysophosphatidic acid, phosphatidylglycerol, phosphatidylinositol, prostaglandin D2, and prostaglandin E1, were observed. A prolonged wound healing process is identified in quiescent UC with altered disease specific lipidomic trajectories providing potential novel therapeutic avenues for stimulating mucosal regeneration as an add-on to the traditional immune suppression treatment.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bjerrum, Jacob Tveiten","Wang, Yulan","Zhang, Jingtao","Riis, Lene Buhl","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Seidelin, Jakob Benedict"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-526733"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanyang Technological University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lipidomic trajectories characterize delayed mucosal wound healing in quiescent ulcerative colitis and identify potential novel therapeutic targets","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7150/ijbs.67112","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-526733","identifier":[{"id":"35342362","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8935238","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85127220635","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-df2c6cd8-fc68-4d2f-a003-05a0d3730424"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4A28376C14E17802147C290F822E3E21"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7150/ijbs.67112","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/308896664/v18p1813.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Gastroenterology and Hepatology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Haematology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sg","key":"nanyang technological university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Nanyang Technological University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob Tveiten","key":"bjerrumpau","last":"Bjerrum","locid":"fe4b37d0-7b36-4636-925f-e1d395b9e573","name":"Bjerrum, Jacob Tveiten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yulan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yulan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jingtao","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jingtao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Buhl","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Ole Haagen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59658c4-dde8-4749-9b5c-f4ec5910dd02","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","orcid":"0000-0003-4612-8635","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Benedict","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","locid":"e31587ea-e362-4ce5-942d-bc27c0f0d340","name":"Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","orcid":"0000-0003-3230-7966","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35342362"],"pub":{"doi":"10.7150/ijbs.67112","issn":["14492288"],"issue":"5","journal":"International Journal of Biological Sciences","pages":"1813-1828","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Biological Sciences","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127220635"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-df2c6cd8-fc68-4d2f-a003-05a0d3730424"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lipidomic Trajectories Characterize Delayed Mucosal Wound Healing in Quiescent Ulcerative Colitis and Identify Potential Novel Therapeutic Targets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-526733","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Many patients with alcohol use disorders are challenged by cravings leading to repeated relapses. Both cue exposure therapy (CET) and acamprosate target alcohol cravings and are often combined (CET + acamprosate). The main aim of this study was to investigate whether aftercare treatment consisting of CET combined with acamprosate is equivalent to (A) CET as monotherapy, (B) aftercare as usual (AAU) as monotherapy or (C) AAU combined with acamprosate. Methods: Patients were randomized to receive either CET with urge-specific coping skills (USCS) as aftercare or AAU. Acamprosate prescription data were extracted from patient case records. Alcohol consumption, cravings, and USCS were assessed at pre-aftercare, post-aftercare, and 6-month follow-up. Results: Overall, patients increased their alcohol consumption during and following aftercare treatment, thereby relapsing despite any treatment. However, CET + acamprosate achieved greater abstinence compared to AAU + acamprosate at follow-up (p=.047). CET + acamprosate also reduced number of drinking days (p=.020) and number of days with excessive drinking (p=.020) at post-aftercare, when compared to AAU monotherapy. CET monotherapy increased sensible drinking at post-aftercare compared to AAU monotherapy (p=.045) and AAU + acamprosate (p=.047). Only CET monotherapy showed improvement in cravings, when compared to AAU at follow-up (mean urge level: p=.032; peak urge level: p=.014). Conclusion: The study showed that CET both as monotherapy and combined with acamprosate was superior to AAU monotherapy and AAU + acamprosate in reducing alcohol consumption. Only CET + acamprosate was capable of reducing alcohol consumption in the longer term, indicating that anti-craving medication may not impede CET from exerting an effect on alcohol consumption. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov ID: NCT02298751 (24/11-2014).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Stryhn, Lene","Larsen, Mathias Bach","Mejldal, Anna","Sibbersen, Christian","Nielsen, Dorthe Grüner","Nielsen, Bent","Nielsen, Anette Søgaard","Stenager, Elsebeth","Mellentin, Angelina Isabella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-583215"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Stryhn, Lene"],"keyword":["Acamprosate","Acamprosate therapeutic use","Aftercare","Alcohol use disorders","Alcoholism drug therapy","Craving","Cues","Humans","Implosive Therapy","Relapse prevention","Secondary prevention","cue exposure therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"relapse prevention for alcohol use disorders combined acamprosate and cue exposure therapy as aftercare","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85116655376","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-583215","identifier":[{"id":"85116655376","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34622734","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-22f3f0e5-1ffd-4c95-8f70-24d639ce9274"],"keyword":["Acamprosate/therapeutic use","Aftercare","Alcohol use disorders","Alcoholism/drug therapy","Cues","Humans","Implosive Therapy","Secondary Prevention","acamprosate","craving","cue exposure therapy","relapse prevention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1DDE8BA002F4D44A0E42DB1B855B0DD9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, UCAR - Unit for Clinical Alcohol Research (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Mental Health Services in the Region of Southern Denmark, Research Unit of Mental Health Services Aabenraa"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"stryhnlenepau","last":"Stryhn","locid":"6f276c8c-9cd8-4fe8-b66b-90c2494ad761","name":"Stryhn, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-4385-9013","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Bach","key":"larsenmathiasbachpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d67c164a-23c5-4647-9efe-29bd89c18bee","name":"Larsen, Mathias Bach","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"mejldalannapau","last":"Mejldal","locid":"1ba21bed-e6bf-45ab-97bf-8a8ed6f8c439","name":"Mejldal, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4612-4338","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sibbersenchristianpau","last":"Sibbersen","name":"Sibbersen, Christian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe Grüner","key":"nielsendorthegrünerpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"45c544fc-760e-4676-9179-794ecaec78a4","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Grüner","orcid":"0000-0003-1235-8336","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bent","key":"nielsenbentpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"adc563a7-67eb-4f54-82b6-40cacc21d300","name":"Nielsen, Bent","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anette Søgaard","key":"nielsenanettesøgaardpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"63429b82-37e7-4fc5-84dd-f73ef3f5658a","name":"Nielsen, Anette Søgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8569-4165","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elsebeth","key":"stenagerelsebethpa