,"SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Incidence rates and employment trends in schizophrenia spectrum disorders, bipolar affective disorders and recurrent depression in the years 2000-2013 : a Danish nationwide register-based study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-086.25-672176","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Increasing knowledge of the microbiome has led to significant advancements in the agrifood system. Case studies based on microbiome applications have been reported worldwide and, in this review, we have selected 14 success stories that showcase the importance of microbiome research in advancing the agrifood system. The selected case studies describe products, methodologies, applications, tools, and processes that created an economic and societal impact. Additionally, they cover a broad range of fields within the agrifood chain: the management of diseases and putative pathogens; the use of microorganism as soil fertilizers and plant strengtheners; the investigation of the microbial dynamics occurring during food fermentation; the presence of microorganisms and/or genes associated with hazards for animal and human health (e.g., mycotoxins, spoilage agents, or pathogens) in feeds, foods, and their processing environments; applications to improve HACCP systems; and the identification of novel probiotics and prebiotics to improve the animal gut microbiome or to prevent chronic non-communicable diseases in humans (e.g., obesity complications). The microbiomes of soil, plants, and animals are pivotal for ensuring human and environmental health and this review highlights the impact that microbiome applications have with this regard.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Olmo, Rocío","Wetzels, Stefanie Urimare","Armanhi, Jaderson Silveira Leite","Arruda, Paulo","Berg, Gabriele","Cernava, Tomislav","Cotter, Paul D.","Araujo, Solon Cordeiro","de Souza, Rafael Soares Correa","Ferrocino, Ilario","Frisvad, Jens Christian","Georgalaki, Marina","Hansen, Hanne Helene","Kazou, Maria","Kiran, George Seghal","Kostic, Tanja","Krauss-Etschmann, Susanne","Kriaa, Aicha","Lange, Lene","Maguin, Emmanuelle","Mitter, Birgit","Nielsen, Mette Olaf","Olivares, Marta","Quijada, Narciso Martín","Romaní-Pérez, Marina","Sanz, Yolanda","Schloter, Michael","Schmitt-Kopplin, Philippe","Seaton, Sarah Craven","Selvin, Joseph","Sessitsch, Angela","Wang, Mengcen","Zwirzitz, Benjamin","Selberherr, Evelyne","Wagner, Martin"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-030993"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Olmo, Rocío"],"country":["Austria","Brazil","China","France","Germany","Greece","India","Ireland","Italy","Spain","United States"],"glorg":["Agricultural University of Athens","All Global Affiliations","Austrian Institute of Technology","BOKU University","Brazil National Association of Inoculant Producers and Importers (ANPII)","CSIC","CSIC - Institute of Agrochemistry and Food Technology","FFoQSI GmbH","FFoQSI GmbH-Austrian Competence Centre for Feed and Food Quality","Graz University of Technology","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Indigo Ag, Inc.","Indigo Agriculture","Kiel University","Leibniz Institute for Agricultural Engineering and Bioeconomy","Leibniz Institute for Agricultural Engineering and Bioeconomy (ATB)","Paris-Saclay University","Pondicherry University","Research Center Borstel - Leibniz Lung Center","SCA Consultoria em Microbiologia Agrícola","Symbiomics Microbiome Solutions","Teagasc - Irish Agriculture and Food Development Authority","The Spanish National Research Council (CSIC)","Universidade Estadual de Campinas","Universite Paris-Saclay","University College Cork","University of Natural Resources and Life Sciences, Vienna","University of Potsdam","University of Turin","University of Veterinary Medicine Vienna","Université Paris-Saclay","Zhejiang University"],"keyword":["Agrifood system","Food microbiome","Microbiome based applications","Multi omics analyses","Success case studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org