name":"Wang, Mengcen","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"35 36","corresponding":null,"first":"Benjamin","key":"zwirzitzpau","last":"Zwirzitz","name":"Zwirzitz, Benjamin","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Evelyne","key":"selberherrpau","last":"Selberherr","name":"Selberherr, Evelyne","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"wagnerpau","last":"Wagner","name":"Wagner, Martin","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35903477"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2022.834622","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"834622","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","publisher_org":"Frontiers Media S.A.","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134905598"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","bioeconomy, research and advisory (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ff56f6c4-c22b-415b-83cb-2c56129b52d9","dtu-33cc2cca-2348-4fda-a3c1-dd821f4862f9","ku-fbf73f53-6f96-46da-a1be-e394af76d2dc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Microbiome Research as an Effective Driver of Success Stories in Agrifood Systems – A Selection of Case Studies","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-030993","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: A tightening of the lingual frenulum may cause breastfeeding difficulties. Surgical release of the restricted frenulum is accomplished by a frenotomy. Between 2015 and 2019, frenotomy procedures in Danish primary healthcare doubled. Causality has not previously been established. The primary aim of this study was to investigate infant/maternal symptom relief and parent satisfaction following frenotomy and discuss potential causes for the increasing frenotomy frequency in Danish infants. METHODS: Between April 2019 and April 2020, 230 breastfed infants less-than 12 months had a frenotomy performed in three private ENT clinics. Parents of 163 infants participated in a phone interview. RESULTS: A moderate to high degree of symptom relief was reported in 138 (85%) infants and 127 (78%) mothers. If more than one preoperative symptom was reported, post-operative infant/maternal symptom relief increased significantly, and maternal symptom alleviation occurred more quickly. Also, infant and maternal symptom relief increased significantly when \"infant breastfeeding difficulty\" or \"maternal nibble/breast pain during breastfeeding\" was reported preoperatively. Most parents (95%) would have a frenotomy performed on their child again under similar circumstances. CONCLUSIONS: Most parents reported a moderate to high degree of infant and maternal symptom relief following frenotomy. Parent satisfaction was compelling. A uniform assessment tool may sharpen diagnostic criteria and eventually stabilise the frenotomy frequency in Danish infants. FUNDING: none. TRIAL REGISTRATION: not relevant.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Siggaard, Lene Dahl","Tingsgaard, Peter","Lüscher, Michael","Holm, Jonas Peter","Nielsen, Jakob Korsholm","Berrett, Thomas Qvist"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-055808"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Siggaard, Lene Dahl"],"keyword":["Ankyloglossia surgery","Breast Feeding","Denmark","Female","Humans","Infant","Lingual Frenum surgery","Mothers","Parents","Personal Satisfaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Øre- Næse- & Halsklinikken Tingsgaard"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","Øre- Næse- & Halsklinikken Tingsgaard"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parent reported infant and maternal symptom relief following frenotomy in infants with tongue tie","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/471338128/Siggaard_et_al._2022_._Parent_reported_infant_and_maternal_symptom_relief_following_frenotomy_in_infants_with_tongue_tie.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-055808","identifier":[{"id":"85129576858","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35485787","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-13c56cf0-5b30-4048-aa20-2e9c9e4da262"],"keyword":["Ankyloglossia/surgery","Breast Feeding","Denmark","Female","Humans","Infant","Lingual Frenum/surgery","Mothers","Parents","Personal Satisfaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5BB5A50D9767FAE195917BE3944C8D18"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/471338128/Siggaard_et_al._2022_._Parent_reported_infant_and_maternal_symptom_relief_following_frenotomy_in_infants_with_tongue_tie.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Otorhinolaryngology, Head and Neck Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Øre- Næse- & Halsklinikken Tingsgaard"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Dahl","key":"siggaardpau","last":"Siggaard","locid":"af298046-98eb-441b-b95d-995119d0f82e","name":"Siggaard, Lene Dahl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"tingsgaardpau","last":"Tingsgaard","name":"Tingsgaard, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"lüscherpau","last":"Lüscher","name":"Lüscher, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Peter","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jonas Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Korsholm","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jakob Korsholm","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Qvist","key":"berrettpau","last":"Berrett","name":"Berrett, Thomas Qvist","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35485787"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["22451919"],"issue":"5","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","paperid":"A12210934","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"69"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129576858"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-13c56cf0-5b30-4048-aa20-2e9c9e4da262"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Parent-reported infant and maternal symptom relief following frenotomy in infants with tongue-tie","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-055808","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This paper aims to foster a paradox lens on competing demands to ensure their productive engagement in design. Competing demands are inevitable and ubiquitous features of today’s systems. Thus, being subject to competing demands is a pervasive and inherent feature of designerly work. Drawing from organizational studies, we first outline four main streams of competing demands underlying today’s systems; related to time, cognition, social interactions, and focus. We demonstrate the importance of a purposeful conceptualization of competing demands by exemplifying how different conceptualizations can lead to different responses. We suggest employing a paradox lens on competing demands, which stresses that seemingly contradictory or even mutually exclusive factors can and ought to coexist and therefore should be leveraged simultaneously. Through a series of research-through-design experiments we explore how framing competing demands according to paradoxes impacts the way they are approached in design practice, and how paradoxes can be engaged with through design.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Neuhoff, Rike","Harre, Olivia","Simeone, Luca","Holst Laursen, Lea","Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-077723"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-02","place":"Bilbao, es","start":"2022-06-25","title":"Design Research Society Conference 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Neuhoff, Rike"],"keyword":["Competing demands","Design research","Paradoxes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engaging with competing demands in systems through design fostering a paradox lens","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access"