{"abstract":"Objective To investigate the association between long term residential exposure to road traffic and railway noise and risk of incident dementia. Design Nationwide prospective register based cohort study. Setting Denmark. Participants 1 938 994 adults aged ≥60 years living in Denmark between 1 January 2004 and 31 December 2017. Main outcome measures Incident cases of all cause dementia and dementia subtypes (Alzheimer's disease, vascular dementia, and Parkinson's disease related dementia), identified from national hospital and prescription registries. Results The study population included 103 500 participants with incident dementia, and of those, 31 219 received a diagnosis of Alzheimer's disease, 8664 of vascular dementia, and 2192 of Parkinson's disease related dementia. Using Cox regression models, 10 year mean exposure to road traffic and railway noise at the most (L den max) and least (L den min) exposed façades of buildings were associated with a higher risk of all cause dementia. These associations showed a general pattern of higher hazard ratios with higher noise exposure, but with a levelling off or even small declines in risk at higher noise levels. In subtype analyses, both road traffic noise and railway noise were associated with a higher risk of Alzheimer's disease, with hazard ratios of 1.16 (95% confidence interval 1.11 to 1.22) for road L den max ≥65 dB compared with <45 dB, 1.27 (1.22 to 1.34) for road L den min ≥55 dB compared with <40 dB, 1.16 (1.10 to 1.23) for railway L den max ≥60 dB compared with <40 dB, and 1.24 (1.17 to 1.30) for railway L den min ≥50 dB compared with <40 dB. Road traffic, but not railway, noise was associated with an increased risk of vascular dementia. Results indicated associations between road traffic L den min and Parkinson's disease related dementia. Conclusions This nationwide cohort study found transportation noise to be associated with a higher risk of all cause dementia and dementia subtypes, especially Alzheimer's disease.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Cantuaria, Manuella Lech","Waldorff, Frans Boch","Wermuth, Lene","Pedersen, Ellen Raben","Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","Thacher, Jesse Daniel","Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","Ketzel, Matthias","Khan, Jibran","Valencia, Victor H.","Schmidt, Jesper Hvass","Sørensen, Mette"],"cuid":["S03-094.74-014782"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cantuaria, Manuella Lech"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Aged","Causality","Dementia epidemiology","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Incidence","Male","Middle Aged","Noise Transportation adverse effects","Proportional Hazards Models","Prospective Studies","Registries"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"residential exposure to transportation noise in denmark and incidence of dementia national cohort study","src":["au","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.n1954","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["11Department of Clinical Research, University of Southern Denmark, Odense, Denmark 12OPEN, Odense Patient data Explorative Network, Odense University Hospital, Odense, Denmark 13BRIDGE, Brain Research - Inter-Disciplinary Guided Excellence, Department of Clinical Research, Faculty of Health Sciences, University of Southern Denmark, Odense, Denmark 14Department of Natural Science and Environment, Roskilde University, Roskilde, Denmark Contributors: MS, MLC, JHS, FBW, LW, ERP, OR-N, JDT, and AHP conceived and designed the study and contributed to the methodology definition. JDT, AHP, MS, and OR-N contributed to exposure assessment. MK and JK geocoded addresses and estimated air pollution. VHV geocoded addresses and estimated proportion of green space. MS, OR-N, and AHP acquired health and confounder data. MLC classified register data and conducted the statistical analysis. MLC and MS wrote the first draft of the manuscript. All authors commented and contributed to the interpretation of results and the final manuscript. The corresponding author attests that all listed authors meet the authorship criteria. Funding: This work was funded by the William Demant Foundation (grant No: 18-0964) and the Independent Research Fund Denmark (grant No: 7016-00036B). The funders had no role in the design and conduct of the study; collection, analysis, and interpretation of data, writing of the manuscript, and decision to submit the manuscript for publication. disclosure form and declare: MLC and JHV report grants from the William Demant Foundation during the conduct of the study. JHV also received grants from Innovation Fund Denmark and William Demant Foundation, and a joined grant from Hearing aid Industry (Oticon, WSA, GN Hearing), outside the submitted work; no other support for the submitted work; no financial relationships with any organizations that might have an interest in the submitted work in the previous three years; no other relationships or activities that could appear to have influenced the submitted work. Data sharing: As this study is based on data from the Danish national registers, which belong to the Danish Ministry of Health and Statistics Denmark, the authors are not allowed to share data in raw form."],"id":"S03-094.74-014782","identifier":[{"id":"34497091","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8424489","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85114799096","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1e02c978-b150-4872-b400-739d76c583c9","ruc-f6f6255a-4d59-47c9-9676-b864bfd17650","sdu-55af94c6-eec9-4b6d-b61a-4e80a0590525"],"keyword":["Aged","Causality","Dementia/epidemiology","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Incidence","Male","Middle Aged","Noise, Transportation/adverse effects","Proportional Hazards Models","Prospective Studies","Registries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-7-2CCB23469EF30FD83A56632760CD620B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/78572389/bmj.n1954.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/273770972/bmj.n1954.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/191815874/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.n1954","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Applied AI and Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Kræftens Bekæmpelse"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Manuella Lech","key":"cantuariapau","last":"Cantuaria","locid":"8f037fd9-8e4b-4926-ad07-466bc021a3da","name":"Cantuaria, Manuella Lech","orcid":"0000-0003-3201-9606","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Frans Boch","key":"waldorffpau","last":"Waldorff","locid":"fe7333f7-ac6d-4ad4-84b7-fdf7b5bf6d22","name":"Waldorff, Frans Boch","orcid":"0000-0002-7859-633X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"wermuthpau","last":"Wermuth","locid":"0a2f7ea5-6a32-4590-a4f7-268caaa4ad2c","name":"Wermuth, Lene","orcid":"0000-0001-6930-8562","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ellen Raben","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"b7a104b3-f660-4af6-a5eb-aa39f455e89f","name":"Pedersen, Ellen Raben","orcid":"0000-0001-9917-9837","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aslak Harbo","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Aslak Harbo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesse Daniel","key":"thacherpau","last":"Thacher","name":"Thacher, Jesse Daniel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"raaschounielsenpau","last":"Raaschou-Nielsen","locid":"9ae8831f-2034-4c09-84bc-01cd649e3b55","name":"Raaschou-Nielsen, Ole","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"ketzelpau","last":"Ketzel","locid":"798900d2-1d54-4c53-a4ca-671c12aa3015","name":"Ketzel, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-9519-1935","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jibran","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"c8fe96cd-050e-4aa9-8303-e03e7e92bf3e","name":"Khan, Jibran","orcid":"0000-0003-2080-2871","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Victor H.","key":"valenciapau","last":"Valencia","locid":"e073b447-a515-4272-887d-fe99110207e2","name":"Valencia, Victor H.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Hvass","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"db84fc4e-28da-45af-a608-13ce8f4ec719","name":"Schmidt, Jesper Hvass","orcid":"0000-0001-7683-1407","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 6","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34497091"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmj.n1954","issn":["09598146","17561833"],"issn_org":["09598146"],"journal":"BMJ","paperid":"n1954","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ","title_org":"The BMJ","volume":"374"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114799096"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1e02c978-b150-4872-b400-739d76c583c9","ruc-f6f6255a-4d59-47c9-9676-b864bfd17650","sdu-55af94c6-eec9-4b6d-b61a-4e80a0590525"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","RUC Roskilde University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Residential exposure to transportation noise in Denmark and incidence of dementia : National cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-094.74-014782","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Social media platforms provide new possibilities within health research. With Facebook being the largest social network in the world, it constitutes a potential platform for recruitment and data collection from women of reproductive age. Women in Denmark and in other Western countries postpone motherhood and risk infertility due to their advanced age when they try to conceive. To date, no study has explored Danish women’s reflections on the timing of motherhood within a social media setting. Objective: The aim of this study was to explore the challenges and opportunities of using Facebook as a platform for qualitative health research in Danish women of reproductive age. Methods: This study was a qualitative study based on 3 online focus groups on Facebook with 26 Danish women of reproductive age discussing the timing of motherhood in January 2020. Results: Conducting online focus groups on Facebook was successful in this study as the web-based approach was found suitable for developing qualitative data with women of reproductive age and made recruitment easy and free of charge. All participants found participating in an online focus group to be a positive experience. More than half of the women participating in the online focus groups found it advantageous to meet on Facebook instead of meeting face-to-face. Conclusions: Conducting online focus groups on Facebook is a suitable method to access qualitative data from women of reproductive age. Participants were positive toward being a part of an online focus group. Online focus groups on social media have the potential to give women of reproductive age a voice in the debate of motherhood.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Temmesen, Camilla Gry","Nielsen, Henriette Svarre","Andersen, Heidi Lene Myglegård","Petersen, Kathrine Birch","Clemensen, Jane"],"cuid":["S04-095.74-041551"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Temmesen, Camilla Gry"],"keyword":["Facebook","Internet","Motherhood","Online focus groups","Participatory Design","Reproduction","Reproductive age","Social media","Women"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["The Fertility Partnership DK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using social media for qualitative health research in danish women of reproductive age online focus group study on facebook","src":["ku","pha","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/24108","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank the women who participated in this study. This study was funded by The Fertility Department, University Hospital Zealand, Region Zealand, Denmark."],"id":"S04-095.74-041551","identifier":[{"id":"34057418","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8204231","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85107431100","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-39125fce-ce12-4517-b893-a7c50233929f","pha-52be00a8-4d5f-4f35-95b5-05c1197e6a11","pha-e1c2cb41-b0d6-4566-9a95-d3dbd42c8430","sdu-1d799cc0-f7be-4a74-8990-53b82dca7378"],"keyword":["Facebook","Internet","Motherhood","Online focus groups","Participatory design","Reproduction","Reproductive age","Social media","Women"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-8E81A07F06BAB6D5A938EE2F5F2463C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/272184092/PDF_5_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/183501509/PDF.pdf","version":"Publis