,"last":"Jørgensen","locid":"efa7e924-c197-4060-8904-110cf0a30837","name":"Jørgensen, Uffe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Poul Erik","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"03fcd9e2-3402-466b-86fc-f3c8163d9306","name":"Lærke, Poul Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-2224-3893","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f2d8644c-d2e8-42a2-854b-88f63ffe25b8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"PEATWISE – Effect of cropping management on protein yield and extractability from selected flooding-tolerant perennial grasses cultivated on a riparian fen","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-267872","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"n a user experiment, we tried out a novel data collection approach consisting of combining surveys with the think aloud method. We coin the phrase “think-aloud survey method”, where participants think-aloud while completing a questionnaire. We analyzed the transcripts and found that the think aloud survey provides deeper insights into the reasoning behind the participants’ Likert scale choices and responses to open-ended questions, along with an enhanced understanding of the tasks and prompting the participants to explicate their choices. All resulting in more insights for design. The think- aloud survey method further offers other insights into usability issues and encourages the participants to provide system improvement proposals. The think-aloud survey method is useful for researchers and practitioners applying a large number of usability evaluations and wanting to dig deeper into the motivations for choice.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Salminen, Joni","Jung, Soon-Gyo","Jansen, Bernard J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383027"],"event":{"acronym":"INTERACT","title":"IFIP TC.13 International Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Qatar"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qatar Computing Research institute"],"keyword":["Interface design","Surveys","Tests"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"think aloud surveys a method for eliciting enhanced insights during user studies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-85607-6_67","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383027","identifier":[{"id":"85115239424","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-776f504e-7ffc-41c5-b3ef-8dd9d5669c3b"],"keyword":["Interface design","Surveys","Tests"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8F2C9F54265A56B91587B14D01D38ED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86422129/Think_Aloud_Surveys_interact2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-85607-6_67","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"qa","key":"qatar computing research institute","loc":["Qatar","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Qatar Computing Research institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joni","key":"salminenpau","last":"Salminen","name":"Salminen, Joni","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Soon-Gyo","key":"jungpau","last":"Jung","name":"Jung, Soon-Gyo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernard J.","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","name":"Jansen, Bernard J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"C.","key":"arditopedh","last":"Ardito","name":"Ardito, C.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-85607-6_67","eisbn":["9783030856076"],"isbn":["9783030856069"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"504-508","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Human-Computer Interaction – INTERACT 2021","volume":"12936"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115239424"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-776f504e-7ffc-41c5-b3ef-8dd9d5669c3b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Think-Aloud Surveys : A Method for Eliciting Enhanced Insights During User Studies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383027","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"User studies have found persona application challenging. We ar- gue that a potential reason for the challenges is the organization’s readiness to apply personas. This research reports the on-going efort of developing the Persona Readiness Scale, a survey instru- ment for organizations’ readiness for personas. The scale involves twenty-two items from seven dimensions: Need Readiness, Culture Readiness, Knowledge Readiness, Resource Readiness, Data and Systems Readiness, Capability Readiness, and Goal Readiness. Or- ganizations can apply the current scale to evaluate their persona readiness but using the dimensions for statistical analyses requires further empirical validation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Salminen, joni","Nielsen, Lene","Jung, Soon-Gyo","Jansen, Bernard J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383611"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Qatar"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qatar Computing Research institute"],"keyword":["Persona adoption","Personas","Psychometrics","Survey instrument"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a measurement scale of organizational readiness for personas","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421931/Towards_a_Measurement_Scale_of_Organizational_Readiness_for_Personas.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383611","identifier":[{"id":"85105799400","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a0c80fd0-fd9e-46ab-bcfb-c0b22efab56a"],"keyword":["Persona adoption","Psychometrics","Survey instrument","personas"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-11480548E5CD8CFCD5708B0E307B2B9C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3411763.3451763","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421931/Towards_a_Measurement_Scale_of_Organizational_Readiness_for_Personas.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"qa","key":"qatar computing research institute","loc":["Qatar","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Qatar Computing Research institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"joni","key":"salminenpau","last":"Salminen","name":"Salminen, joni","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Soon-Gyo","key":"jungpau","last":"Jung","name":"Jung, Soon-Gyo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernard J.","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","name":"Jansen, Bernard J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3411763.3451763","pages":"1-7","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"the 2021 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems.","title":"Extended Abstracts of","volume":"Article 384"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-