","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"hellebergcarstenpau","last":"Helleberg","name":"Helleberg, Carsten","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Kærgaard","key":"mylinannekærgaardpau","last":"Mylin","name":"Mylin, Anne Kærgaard","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Kaergaard","key":"mylinannekaergaardpau","last":"Mylin","name":"Mylin, Anne Kaergaard","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"abildgaardnielspau","last":"Abildgaard","locid":"595418b9-29f8-4fd3-8663-1b32eab3451a","name":"Abildgaard, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-6852-2014","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 9 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Kongsgaard","key":"kongsgaardnielsenlenepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"897c29d3-45a2-4178-81b1-b0ba61db5a25","name":"Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene","name_org":"Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-2083-3870","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-63e48441-10b6-4110-93f5-55f26f819b0e","sdu-f86b5827-8646-499b-9882-6150f702744a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Danish Patients with multiple myeloma report no change in quality of life during the COVID-19 pandemic","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.33-019927","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In general, governments and health authorities have taken precautions during the COVID-19 pandemic to reduce the viral spread and protect vulnerable citizens. Patients with multiple myeloma (MM) have an increased risk of being infected with COVID-19 and developing a fatal course due to the related immunodeficiency. We investigated how Danish patients with MM reported their quality of life (QoL) pre-COVID and during COVID, in an ongoing longitudinal QoL survey. The responses given during the first and second wave of the COVID-19 pandemic were pooled, analyzed and compared to the same period the year before. We hypothesized that locking down the society would have caused deteriorated QoL and that patients living alone and those under the age of 65 would be particularly affected by the situation. Surprisingly, our study showed the opposite. Statistically significant and clinically relevant differences were primarily found during the first lock down and represented reduced fatigue, improved role functioning, decreased insomnia and improved physical health summaries in patients below 65 years of age. These results indicate that Danish patients with MM might have felt protected and safe by COVID restrictions. Otherwise, the questionaries used in QoL-MM survey may not have been able to capture the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic. Importantly, this indicates that QoL survey data obtained in clinical studies, in countries with highly developed health-care systems using standard questionnaires during the pandemic, allow room for interpretation without being adjusted for the impacts of the pandemic.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Redder, Louise","Møller, Søren","Johnsen, Anna Thit","Jarden, Mary","Andersen, Christen Lykkegaard","Jensen, Bo Amdi","Frederiksen, Henrik","Gregersen, Henrik","Klostergaard, Anja","Steffensen, Morten Saaby","Pedersen, Per Trøllund","Hinge, Maja","Frederiksen, Mikael","Helleberg, Carsten","Mylin, Anne Kærsgaard","Abildgaard, Niels","Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard"],"cuid":["S02-093.17-041144"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Redder, Louise"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quality of life in danish patients with multiple myeloma during the covid 000000000019 pandemic","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/covid1010024","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.17-041144","identifier":[{"id":"85191090697","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2cac1ae2-5ad2-4da4-a60f-842f33bc843b","sdu-d54de071-04a1-4df2-b04b-82ec76c46ef0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B897C13A57B1469588D50B078A1D792B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/196380107/covid_01_00024_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/covid1010024","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/300379797/Quality.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southe