pital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-aaa96218-d77f-4736-be6c-eea0046ff465","ku-4d63144d-898d-4297-87b8-53bb1ec7aba5","sdu-ad03ab6b-d9f9-42d4-b3bc-478f693023f8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"OMERACT definition and reliability assessment of chronic ultrasound lesions of the axillary artery in giant cell arteritis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.60-025112","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: COVID-19, caused by the Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2), has great health implications in older patients, including high mortality. In general, older patients often have atypical symptom presentations during acute illness due to a high level of comorbidity. The purpose of this study was to investigate the presentation of symptoms at hospital admissions in older patients with COVID-19 and evaluate its impact on disease outcome. METHODS: This retrospective study included patients ≥80 years of age with a positive test for SARS-CoV-2, who were admitted to one of three medical departments in Denmark from March 1st to June 1st, 2020. RESULTS: A total of 102 patients (47% male) with a mean age of 85 years were included. The most common symptoms at admission were fever (74%), cough (62%), and shortness of breath (54%). Furthermore, atypical symptoms like confusion (29%), difficulty walking (13%), and falls (8%) were also present. In-hospital and 30-day mortality were 31% (n = 32) and 41% (n = 42), respectively. Mortality was highest in patients with confusion (50% vs 38%) or falls (63% vs 39%), and nursing home residency prior to hospital admission was associated with higher mortality (OR 2.7, 95% CI 1.1-6.7). CONCLUSIONS: Older patients with SARS-Cov-2 displayed classical symptoms of COVID-19 but also geriatric frailty symptoms such as confusion and walking impairments. Additionally, both in-hospital and 30-day mortality was very high. Our study highlights the need for preventive efforts to keep older people from getting COVID-19 and increased awareness of frailty among those with COVID-19.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Karlsson, Linda Katharina","Jakobsen, Lasse Hjort","Hollensberg, Louise","Ryg, Jesper","Midttun, Mette","Frederiksen, Henrik","Glenthøj, Andreas","Kodahl, Anette Raskov","Secher-Johnsen, Joanna","Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard","Bofill, Nuria Gonzalez","Knudtzen, Fredrikke Christie","Lund, Cecilia Margareta"],"cuid":["S04-095.12-006576"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Lund, Cecilia Margareta"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Comorbidity","Covid 19","Delirium","Falls","Female","Frailty","Frailty epidemiology","Hospitalization","Humans","Illness","Male","Multimorbidities","Older adults","Outcomes","Retrospective Studies","SARS CoV 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical presentation and mortality in hospitalized patients aged 000000000080 years with covid 000000000019 a retrospective cohort study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7836891/pdf/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-095.12-006576","identifier":[{"id":"85100207797","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33476754","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000698677200029","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7836891","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-87e55a40-3548-45b5-bc49-5c6332485ea4","au-e5d8e557-85f0-4fd7-a977-75c2fe3dff44","ku-958f62df-8a7c-4882-93ed-1bda6ac16d66","sdu-367f6d77-fbc4-4078-bb74-1b9e2fa79912"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","COVID-19","Comorbidity","Delirium","Falls","Female","Frailty","Frailty/epidemiology","Hospitalization","Humans","ILLNESS","Male","Multimorbidities","OLDER-ADULTS","OUTCOMES","Retrospective Studies","SARS-CoV-2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-