ll,"first":"Carsten","key":"hellebergcarstenpau","last":"Helleberg","name":"Helleberg, Carsten","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Kaergaard","key":"mylinannekaergaardpau","last":"Mylin","name":"Mylin, Anne Kaergaard","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Kærgaard","key":"mylinannekærgaardpau","last":"Mylin","name":"Mylin, Anne Kærgaard","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"abildgaardnielspau","last":"Abildgaard","locid":"595418b9-29f8-4fd3-8663-1b32eab3451a","name":"Abildgaard, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-6852-2014","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 7 1 8","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Kongsgaard","key":"kongsgaardnielsenlenepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"897c29d3-45a2-4178-81b1-b0ba61db5a25","name":"Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene","name_org":"Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-2083-3870","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11136-021-02976-1","issn":["09629343"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Quality of Life Research","paperid":"(104.3)","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Quality of Life Research","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6cfe1352-bb8a-4ae1-a76a-b9b5c96b673a","au-4bac1c0c-43d5-40b9-ab7f-998399c5d346","sdu-a4f2540f-c5a4-4869-943f-29c8ba9a0ed3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The COVID-19 pandemic does not affect the quality of life reportings of Danish patients with multiple myeloma","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-089.04-005292","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Venous thromboembolism (VTE) is a potentially fatal complication of severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) infection, and thromboprophylaxis should be balanced against risk of bleeding. This study examined risks of VTE and major bleeding in hospitalized and community-managed SARS-CoV-2 patients compared with control populations. METHODS: Using nationwide population-based registries, 30-day risks of VTE and major bleeding in SARS-CoV-2 positive patients were compared with those of SARS-CoV-2 test-negative patients and with an external cohort of influenza patients. Medical records of all COVID-19 patients at 6 departments of infectious diseases in Denmark were reviewed in detail. RESULTS: The overall 30-day risk of VTE was 0.4% (40/9460) among SARS-CoV-2 patients (16% hospitalized), 0.3% (649/226 510) among SARS-CoV-2 negative subjects (12% hospitalized), and 1.0% (158/16 281) among influenza patients (59% hospitalized). VTE risks were higher and comparable in hospitalized SARS-CoV-2 positive (1.5%), SARS-CoV-2 negative (1.8%), and influenza patients (1.5%). Diagnosis of major bleeding was registered in 0.5% (47/9460) of all SARS-CoV-2 positive individuals and in 2.3% of those hospitalized. Medical record review of 582 hospitalized SARS-CoV-2 patients observed VTE in 4% (19/450) and major bleeding in 0.4% (2/450) of ward patients, of whom 31% received thromboprophylaxis. Among intensive care patients (100% received thromboprophylaxis), risks were 7% (9/132) for VTE and 11% (15/132) for major bleeding. CONCLUSIONS: Among people with SARS-CoV-2 infection in a population-based setting, VTE risks were low to moderate and were not substantially increased compared with SARS-CoV-2 test-negative and influenza patients. Risk of severe bleeding was low for ward patients, but mirrored VTE risk in the intensive care setting.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Dalager-Pedersen, Michael","Lund, Lars Christian","Mariager, Theis","Winther, Rannva","Hellfritzsch, Maja","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Thomsen, Reimar Wernich","Johansen, Nanna Borup","Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz","Nielsen, Stig Lønberg","Omland, Lars","Lundbo, Lene Fogt","Israelsen, Simone Bastrup","Harboe, Zitta Barrella","Pottegård, Anton","Nielsen, Henrik","Bodilsen, Jacob"],"cuid":["S03-096.87-005621"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Bodilsen, Jacob"],"keyword":["Anticoagulants","Bleeding","Cohort Studies","Covid 19","Deep venous thrombosis","Hemorrhage","Hemorrhage epidemiology","Humans","Infection","Pulmonary embolism","Risk Factors","SARS CoV 2","Sepsis","VTE","Venous Thromboembolism epidemiology","Venous thromboembolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Danish Medicines Agency"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"venous thromboembolism and major bleeding in patients with coronavirus disease 000000002019 covid 000000000019 a nationwide population based cohort study","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/467047096/Dalager_Pedersen_et_al._2021_Accepted_Manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S03-096.87-005621","identifier":[{"id":"33400771","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7929126","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85122841385","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000743384700016","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-73fe1b8e-f0a2-41f3-97a0-ef9eef231942","au-f626e788-239e-47cc-8a3c-26a36d943448","sdu-40cb204a-2144-4736-ab43-9d2c34ae79e5"],"keyword":["Anticoagulants","COVID-19","Cohort Stud