2","journal":"Clinical Infectious Diseases","pages":"2283-2293","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Clinical Infectious Diseases","volume":"73"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122841385"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-73fe1b8e-f0a2-41f3-97a0-ef9eef231942","au-f626e788-239e-47cc-8a3c-26a36d943448","sdu-40cb204a-2144-4736-ab43-9d2c34ae79e5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Venous Thromboembolism and Major Bleeding in Patients With Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) : A Nationwide, Population-Based Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-096.87-005621","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: To evaluate health-care utilisation and costs, myeloma complications and survival in Danish patients with multiple myeloma (MM) before and after implementation of new early-line treatments in 2009. Methods: Based on data from the Danish National Health Registers, 3518 patients diagnosed with MM during 2002-2005 or 2010-2013 and randomly matched control individuals were identified, and health-care utilisation and costs were estimated. Results: Health-care utilisation showed a marked shift from inpatient admissions towards outpatient visits. From early to late period, the mean annual number of outpatient visits increased by 22% and 28% in patients <65 years and ≥65 years, respectively. Additionally, the mean annual outpatient service costs increased correspondingly from 17 001€ to 23 643€ in younger patients and from 11 317€ to 16 144€ in the elderly. Increasing outpatient costs were outbalanced by lower inpatient admission costs and the adjusted total mean annual costs decreased in younger patients, probably partly due to fewer myeloma complications. The five-year survival rates increased markedly in both younger (HR = 0.51) and elderly (HR = 0.69) patients. Conclusion: Despite the introduction of new expensive early-line MM treatments in 2009, health-care costs remained stable due to a shift in health-care utilisation towards outpatient clinic care and fewer complications.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hannig, Louise Hur","Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard","Ibsen, Rikke","Arnheim‐Dahlström, Lisen","Kjellberg, Jakob","Abildgaard, Niels"],"cuid":["S03-097.68-666087"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hannig, Louise Hur"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet"],"keyword":["Health Care Costs","Multiple myeloma","Retrospective","Survival","care costs"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of changed treatment patterns in multiple myeloma on health care utilisation and costs myeloma complications and survival a population based comparison between two time periods in denmark","src":["au","sdu","vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/182044642/ejh.13615.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["LH declares research grants from Celgene. LKN declares no conflict of interest. LAD was during study conduct an employee of Celgene and now an employee of War On Cancer. RI is an employee of i2minds. JK is an employee of VIVE—The Danish National Center for Social Research. NA declares research grants from Janssen, Takeda, Amgen, Celgene and BMS."],"id":"S03-097.68-666087","identifier":[{"id":"85104138614","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33675553","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000639081200001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-0edc3088-802b-432b-bd99-cdb75a63b387","sdu-2bfe1bd3-ca27-4523-b761-0f8e0f0c3972","vive-5afd11c7-3a16-4339-b035-717a0c967310"],"keyword":["Multiple myeloma","care costs","health&#8208","health-care costs","retrospective","survival"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-471CACCC5E494D7C3628A627B379EC9D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/182044642/ejh.13615.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"]