02-0943-3289","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Niels","key":"obelnielspau","last":"Obel","locid":"47b44abc-6c99-4a76-b8b0-ca53b033951b","name":"Obel, Niels","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33417703"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/infdis/jiab013","issn":["00221899","15376613"],"issn_org":["00221899"],"issue":"5","journal":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","pages":"850-859","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","volume":"224"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116957716"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c6e279b9-a443-4ea9-81a5-32878f6845c1","au-2c1df405-f925-4b89-8c01-cba0b2b0a5b2","ku-c1e320e5-cf01-44cc-bac9-0944d96fcea6","sdu-60aa6e2e-2150-4406-bf55-5740eb1d6344"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Characteristics and Long-term Prognosis of Danish Patients With Varicella Zoster Virus Detected in Cerebrospinal Fluid Compared With the Background Population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.97-009551","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In general, governments and health authorities have taken precautions during the COVID-19 pandemic to reduce the viral spread and protect vulnerable citizens. Patients with multiple myeloma (MM) have an increased risk of being infected with COVID-19 and developing a fatal course due to the related immunodeficiency. We investigated how Danish patients with MM reported their quality of life (QoL) pre-COVID and during COVID, in an ongoing longitudinal QoL survey. The responses given during the first and second wave of the COVID-19 pandemic were pooled, analyzed and compared to the same period the year before. We hypothesized that locking down the society would have caused deteriorated QoL and that patients living alone and those under the age of 65 would be particularly affected by the situation. Surprisingly, our study showed the opposite. Statistically significant and clinically relevant differences were primarily found during the first lock down and represented reduced fatigue, improved role functioning, decreased insomnia and improved physical health summaries in patients below 65 years of age. These results indicate that Danish patients with MM might have felt protected and safe by COVID restrictions. Otherwise, the questionaries used in QoL-MM survey may not have been able to capture the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic. Importantly, this indicates that QoL survey data obtained in clinical studies, in countries with highly developed health-care systems using standard questionnaires during the pandemic, allow room for interpretation without being adjusted for the impacts of the pandemic.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Redder, Louise","Möller, Sören","Johnsen, Anna Thit","Jarden, Mary","Amdi, Bo","Andersen, Christen Lykkegaard","Frederiksen, Henrik","Gregersen, Henrik","Klostergaard, Anja","Steffensen, Morten Saaby","Pedersen, Per Trøllund","Hinge, Maja","Frederiksen, Mikael","Helleberg, Carsten","Mylind, Anne Kærgaard","Abildgaard, Niels","Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-170461"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Redder, Louise"],"keyword":["Multiple myeloma","Quality of Life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quality of life in danish patients with multiple myeloma during the covid 000000000019 pandemic","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85191090697","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-170461","identifier":[{"id":"85191090697","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-48257f32-c498-4f57-8cd7-24e93ebd0b3c"],"keyword":["COVID-19 pandemic 4","EORTC QLQ-C30 5","EORTC QLQ-CIPN20 7","EORTC QLQ-MY20 6","SF12v2","multiple myeloma","quality of life"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1DC29F390267777C52A11F57556675AC"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev and Gentofte Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University (AAU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"redderlouisepau","last":"Redder","name":"Redder, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sören","key":"möllersörenpau","last":"Möller","name":"Möller, Sören","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Thit","key":"johnsenannathitpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Anna Thit","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mary","key":"jardenmarypau","last":"Jarden","name":"Jarde