inal microbiota","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-728360","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The basement membrane (BM) is a special type of extracellular matrix and presents the major barrier cancer cells have to overcome multiple times to form metastases. Here we show that BM stiffness is a major determinant of metastases formation in several tissues and identify netrin-4 (Net4) as a key regulator of BM stiffness. Mechanistically, our biophysical and functional analyses in combination with mathematical simulations show that Net4 softens the mechanical properties of native BMs by opening laminin node complexes, decreasing cancer cell potential to transmigrate this barrier despite creating bigger pores. Our results therefore reveal that BM stiffness is dominant over pore size, and that the mechanical properties of ‘normal’ BMs determine metastases formation and patient survival independent of cancer-mediated alterations. Thus, identifying individual Net4 protein levels within native BMs in major metastatic organs may have the potential to define patient survival even before tumour formation. The ratio of Net4 to laminin molecules determines BM stiffness, such that the more Net4, the softer the BM, thereby decreasing cancer cell invasion activity.","author_count":31,"contributors":["Reuten, Raphael","Zendehroud, Sina","Nicolau, Monica","Fleischhauer, Lutz","Laitala, Anu","Kiderlen, Stefanie","Nikodemus, Denise","Wullkopf, Lena","Nielsen, Sebastian Rune","McNeilly, Sarah","Prein, Carina","Rafaeva, Maria","Schoof, Erwin M.","Furtwängler, Benjamin","Porse, Bo T.","Kim, Hyobin","Won, Kyoung Jae","Sudhop, Stefanie","Zornhagen, Kamilla Westarp","Suhr, Frank","Maniati, Eleni","Pearce, Oliver M.T.","Koch, Manuel","Oddershede, Lene Broeng","Van Agtmael, Tom","Madsen, Chris D.","Mayorca-Guiliani, Alejandro E.","Bloch, Wilhelm","Netz, Roland R.","Clausen-Schaumann, Hauke","Erler, Janine T."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-033391"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Erler, Janine T.","Reuten, Raphael"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Free University of Berlin","German Sport University Cologne","KU Leuven","Lund University","Munich University of Applied Sciences","Queen Mary University of London","University of Cologne","University of Glasgow"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"basement membrane stiffness determines metastases formation","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277308049/229131.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-033391","identifier":[{"id":"33495631","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85099754752","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-241b20bf-9983-473b-aaf3-6007d5075ed0","ku-301b723a-cd17-48a7-a5ea-bdbc1316921f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8406E8CBC9F7B6FF2381F88D2010B974"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/334263947/229131_2_47.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277308049/229131.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC