{"abstract":"Inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) is a chronic inflammatory condition driven by diverse genetic and nongenetic programs that converge to disrupt immune homeostasis in the intestine. We have reported that, in murine intestinal epithelium with telomere dysfunction, DNA damage-induced activation of ataxia-telangiectasia mutated (ATM) results in ATM-mediated phosphorylation and activation of the YAP1 transcriptional coactivator, which in turn up-regulates pro-IL-18, a pivotal immune regulator in IBD pathogenesis. Moreover, individuals with germline defects in telomere maintenance genes experience increased occurrence of intestinal inflammation and show activation of the ATM/YAP1/pro-IL-18 pathway in the intestinal epithelium. Here, we sought to determine the relevance of the ATM/YAP1/pro-IL-18 pathway as a potential driver of IBD, particularly older-onset IBD. Analysis of intestinal biopsy specimens and organoids from older-onset IBD patients documented the presence of telomere dysfunction and activation of the ATM/YAP1/ precursor of interleukin 18 (pro-IL-18) pathway in the intestinal epithelium. Employing intestinal organoids from healthy individuals, we demonstrated that experimental induction of telomere dysfunction activates this inflammatory pathway. In organoid models from ulcerative colitis and Crohn’s disease patients, pharmacological interventions of telomerase reactivation, suppression of DNA damage signaling, or YAP1 inhibition reduced pro-IL-18 production. Together, these findings support a model wherein telomere dysfunction in the intestinal epithelium can initiate the inflammatory process in IBD, pointing to therapeutic interventions for this disease.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Chakravarti, Deepavali","Lee, Rumi","Multani, Asha S.","Santoni, Andrea","Keith, Zachery","Hsu, Wen Hao","Chang, Kyle","Reyes, Laura","Rashid, Asif","Wu, Chang Jiun","Li, Jun","Zhang, Jiexin","Shim, Hong Seok","Chandra, Krishna","Deng, Pingna","Spring, Denise J.","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Riis, Lene Buhl","Mayigegowda, Kavya Kelagere","Blutt, Sarah E.","Zhang, Jianhua","Younes, Mamoun","DuPont, Andrew","Thirumurthi, Selvi","Vilar, Eduardo","Estes, Mary K.","Colla, Simona","Shroyer, Noah F.","DePinho, Ronald A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-402134"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baylor College of Medicine","Rice University","University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center"],"keyword":["DNA damage","Inflammatory bowel disease","Telomere dysfunction","YAP1"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"telomere dysfunction instigates inflammation in inflammatory bowel disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8307535/pdf/pnas.202024853.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-402134","identifier":[{"id":"85109879044","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34253611","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8307535","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-0ea17d11-5df2-49bc-9484-8a689994b7c9"],"keyword":["DNA damage","Inflammatory bowel disease","Pro-IL-18","Telomere dysfunction","Yap1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1749DD2D210087FD2D9585769036CCA3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8307535/pdf/pnas.202024853.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of texas md anderson cancer center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"baylor college of medicine","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Baylor College of Medicine","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"rice university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Rice University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Gastroenterology and Hepatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of texas health science center at houston","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Deepavali","key":"chakravartideepavalipau","last":"Chakravarti","name":"Chakravarti, Deepavali","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rumi","key":"leerumipau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Rumi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Asha S.","key":"multaniashaspau","last":"Multani","name":"Multani, Asha S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andrea","key":"santoniandreapau","last":"Santoni","name":"Santoni, Andrea","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Zachery","key":"keithzacherypau","last":"Keith","name":"Keith, Zachery","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wen Hao","key":"hsuwenhaopau","last":"Hsu","na