{"abstract":"Purpose: People with severe mental illness experience disproportionately high rates of unemployment. Nonetheless, a substantial amount of research has demonstrated vocational benefits of the Individual Placement and Support (IPS) model and IPS supplemented with cognitive remediation (IPSE). The present study sought to examine demographic and clinical predictors of employment or education among people with severe mental illness and to investigate if IPS or IPSE can compensate for risk factors for unemployment. Methods: Seven hundred twenty participants were randomly assigned to IPS, IPSE or Service as Usual. During the 18-month follow-up period participants in the two experimental groups obtained significantly more work or education. A series of univariate and multiple logistic regression analyses were conducted to assess the predictive power of demographic and clinical factors for the total population and for the three groups individually. Results: The strongest predictor for vocational recovery, besides treatment allocation, was previous work history (OR = 1.78; 95% CI = 1.28–2.47). Men had a lower probability for vocational recovery compared to women (OR = 0.71; 95% CI = 0.50–0.99) and higher age was also negatively associated with work or education (OR = 0.79; 95% CI = 0.67–0.93). Moreover, vocational recovery was predicted by higher readiness for change, measured on the readiness for change scale (OR = 1.42; 95% CI = 1.19–1.70). Participation in IPS or IPSE could not compensate for negative risk factors such as low cognitive function or negative symptoms. Conclusions: In a multiple logistic regression analysis age, previous work history and motivation for change were statistically significant predictors of obtaining work or education among people with severe mental illness who participated in the Danish IPS trial.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Christensen, Thomas","Wallstrøm, Iben Gammelgård","Bojesen, Anders Bo","Nordentoft, Merete","Eplov, Lene Falgaard"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-045343"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Thomas Nordahl"],"keyword":["Cognitive remediation","Individual Placement and Support IPS","Severe mental illness","Supported employment","Vocational rehabilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predictors of work and education among people with severe mental illness who participated in the danish individual placement and support study findings from a randomized clinical trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85106443504&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was funded by the Danish Agency for Labour Market and Recruitment; the Danish foundation TrygFonden; and the Obel Family Foundation. The funders of the study had no role in the study design, data collection, data analysis, data interpretation or writing of the report."],"id":"S02-100.00-045343","identifier":[{"id":"85106443504","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34032866","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-af2568ec-5187-4f5b-aab3-0019644db8e3","sdu-ccffbfb4-77ba-4534-b23f-25a9d160557f"],"keyword":["Cognitive remediation","Individual Placement and Support (IPS)","Severe mental illness","Supported employment","Vocational rehabilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8EB5D659EDAF6642097C82EBB7181C1D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Psykiatrisk Center København"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Psychiatry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Thomas Nordahl","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"0ec1a3b8-44bb-4c8c-b242-f71e7acab6e4","name":"Christensen, Thomas","name_org":"Christensen, Thomas Nordahl","orcid":"0000-0003-4953-0814","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben Gammelgård","key":"wallstrømpau","last":"Wallstrøm","locid":"9ae2751d-62bd-4ac8-b6a0-88bcea6bd9ce","name":"Nielsen, Iben Gammelgaard","name_org":"Wallstrøm, Iben Gammelgård","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders Bo","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","name":"Bojesen, Anders Bo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Merete","key":"nordentoftpau","last":"Nordentoft","locid":"6d0fe19c-7c81-463b-8bc8-822d71584b69","name":"Nordentoft, Merete","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene Falgaard","key":"eplovpau","last":"Eplov","name":"Eplov, Lene Falgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34032866"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00127-021-02107-8","issn":["09337954","14339285"],"issn_org":["09337954"],"issue":"9","journal":"Social Psychiatry and Psychiatric Epidemiology","pages":"1669-1677","publisher":"D. Steinkopff-Verlag","status":"p","title":"Social Psychiatry and Psychiatric Epidemiology","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106443504"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-af2568ec-5187-4f5b-aab3-0019644db8e3","sdu-ccffbfb4-77ba-4534-b23f-25a9d160557f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Predictors of work and education among people with severe mental illness who participated in the Danish individual placement and support study : findings from a randomized clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-045343","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The COVID-19 pandemic has led to an unprecedented demand for real-time surveillance data in order to inform critical decision makers regarding the management of the pandemic. The aim of this review was to describe how the Danish national microbiology database, MiBa, served as a cornerstone for providing data to the real-time surveillance system by linkage to other nationwide health registries. The surveillance system was established on an existing IT health infrastructure and a close network between clinical microbiologists, information technology experts, and public health officials. In 2020, testing capacity for SARS-CoV-2 was ramped up from none to over 10,000 weekly PCR tests per 100,000 population. The crude incidence data mirrored this increase in testing. Real-time access to denominator data and patient registries enabled adjustments for fluctuations testing activity, providing robust data on crude SARS-CoV-2 incidence during the changing diagnostic and management strategies. The use of the same data for different purposes, for example, final laboratory reports, information to the public, contact tracing, public health, and science, has been a critical asset for the pandemic response. It has also raised issues concerning data protection and critical capacity of the underlying technical systems and key resources. However, even with these limitations, the setup has enabled decision makers to adopt timely interventions. The experiences from COVID-19 may motivate a transformation from traditional indicator-based public health surveillance to an all-encompassing information system based on access to a comprehensive set of data sources, including diagnostic and reference microbiology.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Schønning, Kristian","Dessau, Ram Benny","Jensen, Thøger Gorm","Thorsen, Nicklas Myrthue","Wiuff, Camilla","Nielsen, Lene","Gubbels, Sophie","Denwood, Matt","Thygesen, Uffe Høgsbro","Christensen, Lasse Engbo","Møller, Camilla Holten","Møller, Jens Kjølseth","Ellermann-Eriksen, Svend","Østergaard, Christian","Lam, Janni Uyen Hoa","Abushalleeh, Nour","Meaidi, Marianna","Olsen, Stefan","Mølbak, Kåre","Voldstedlund, Marianne"],"cuid":["S03-086.61-019318"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Voldstedlund, Marianne"],"keyword":["Basic reproduction number","COVID 19 Testing","COVID 19 diagnosis","Covid 19","Databases Factual","Denmark epidemiology","Electronic reporting","Electronics","Health Care Sector","Humans","Microbiological test results","National surveillance","Registries","SARS CoV 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electronic reporting of diagnostic laboratory test results from all healthcare sectors is a cornerstone of national preparedness and control of covid 000000000019 in denmark","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apm.13140","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-086.61-019318","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8239934","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33949007","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85107264556","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000658288600001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-5b68b6aa-45b1-469e-804e-bfe0eb6ba55c","ku-ea4369ab-7a47-428c-a210-5a442534eb40","sdu-69b6cad9-f3ba-4a06-89a4-098de41991fe"],"keyword":["Basic Reproduction Number","COVID-19","COVID-19 Testing","COVID-19/diagnosis","Databases, Factual","Denmark/epidemiology","Electronics","Health Care Sector","Humans","Registries