{"abstract":"Phenomycin is a bacterial mini-protein of 89 amino acids discovered more than 50 years ago with toxicity in the nanomolar regime toward mammalian cells. The protein inhibits the function of the eukaryotic ribosome in cell-free systems and appears to target translation initiation. Several fundamental questions concerning the cellular activity of phenomycin, however, have remained unanswered. In this paper, we have used morphological profiling to show that direct inhibition of translation underlies the toxicity of phenomycin in cells. We have performed studies of the cellular uptake mechanism of phenomycin, showing that endosomal escape is the toxicity-limiting step, and we have solved a solution phase high-resolution structure of the protein using NMR spectroscopy. Through bioinformatic as well as functional comparisons between phenomycin and two homologs, we have identified a peptide segment, which constitutes one of two loops in the structure that is critical for the toxicity of phenomycin.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Hansen, Bente Kring","Larsen, Camilla Kjeldgaard","Nielsen, Jakob Toudahl","Svenningsen, Esben B","Van, Lan Bich","Jacobsen, Kristian Mark","Bjerring, Morten","Flygaard, Rasmus Kock","Jenner, Lasse B","Nejsum, Lene Niemann","Brodersen, Ditlev E","Mulder, Frans A.A.","Tørring, Thomas","Poulsen, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-232771"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Université de Strasbourg"],"keyword":["Cell penetrating peptide","NMR structure","Natural product","Ribosome"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structure and function of the bacterial protein toxin phenomycin","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/early/2019/11/29/847772.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-232771","identifier":[{"id":"32220302","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85083019610","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b55a6a68-30c8-41f5-a297-10d15998bede"],"keyword":["NMR structure","cell-penetrating peptide","mini-protein","natural product","protein synthesis inhibitor","protein toxin","ribosome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C6CFD7A3738238707164D4577DF24B5E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/early/2019/11/29/847772.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"université de strasbourg","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université de Strasbourg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Kring","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3f32b0a5-11b4-4137-8a23-11362648542f","name":"Hansen, Bente Kring","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla K","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1869df06-59cf-4b58-a8e9-bfc3df30c9a9","name":"Larsen, Camilla Kjeldgaard","name_org":"Larsen, Camilla K","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob T","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"65a61a5c-0f7e-4ccf-8b23-6e06d931fc