":"Larsen, Thomas S.","orcid":"0000-0002-8418-6708","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas S","key":"larsenthomasspau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Thomas S","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"grønbækkirstenpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"82ff4ce1-979f-44c9-b095-72c4a3dca507","name":"Grønbæk, Kirsten","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32203146"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41375-020-0795-z","issn":["08876924","14765551"],"issn_org":["08876924"],"issue":"12","journal":"Leukemia","pages":"3256-3268","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Leukemia","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082878611"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4014b49d-93fc-4dc8-a1a9-579363896a62","au-1f8d9610-a4df-426b-81ce-51d87cb39a2b","ku-be29c6de-7a2a-4fc9-806a-259b778fde79","sdu-2cbeab5b-bf1d-45f2-b73c-48e193b1de5d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Clinical impact of clonal hematopoiesis in patients with lymphoma undergoing ASCT : a national population-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-003150","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objectives The overall study aim was to synthesise understandings and experiences regarding the concept of spiritual care (SC). More specifically, to identify, organise and prioritise experiences with the way SC is conceived and practised by professionals in research and the clinic. Design Group concept mapping (GCM). Setting The study was conducted within a university setting in Denmark. Participants Researchers, students and clinicians working with SC on a daily basis in the clinic and/or through research participated in brainstorming (n=15), sorting (n=15), rating and validation (n=13). Results Applying GCM, ideas were identified, organised and prioritised online. A total of 192 unique ideas of SC were identified and organised into six clusters. The results were discussed and interpreted at a validation meeting. Based on input from the validation meeting a conceptual model was developed. The model highlights three overall themes: (1) 'SC as an integral but overlooked aspect of healthcare' containing the two clusters SC as a part of healthcare and perceived significance; (2) 'delivering SC' containing the three clusters quality in attitude and action, relationship and help and support, and finally (3) 'the role of spirituality' containing a single cluster. Conclusion Because spirituality is predominantly seen as a fundamental aspect of each individual human being, particularly important during suffering, SC should be an integral aspect of healthcare, although it is challenging to handle. SC involves paying attention to patients' values and beliefs, requires adequate skills and is realised in a relationship between healthcare professional and patient founded on trust and confidence.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Hvidt, Niels Christian","Nielsen, Kristina Tomra","Kørup, Alex K.","Prinds, Christina","Hansen, Dorte Gilså","Viftrup, Dorte Toudal","Assing Hvidt, Elisabeth","Hammer, Elisabeth Rokkjær","Falkø, Erik","Locher, Flemming","Boelsbjerg, Hanne Bess","Wallin, Johan Albert","Thomsen, Karsten Flemming","Schrøder, Katja","Moestrup, Lene","Nissen, Ricko Damberg","Stewart-Ferrer, Sif","Stripp, Tobias Kvist","Steenfeldt, Vibeke Østergaard","Søndergaard, Jens","Wæhrens, Eva Ejlersen"],"cuid":["S06-096.42-026543"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","corresponding_author":["Hvidt, Niels Christian"],"keyword":["Group Concept Mapping","Medical ethics","Occupational Therapy","Palliative care","Public health","Rehabilitation medicine","Spiritual care","Sygdom sundhedsvidenskab og sygepleje","health nutrition and quality of life"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-UCS"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-UCS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what is spiritual care professional perspectives on the concept of spiritual care identified through group concept mapping","src":["au","pha","sdu","ucl","ucn","ucsyd"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-UCS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2020-042142","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S06-096.42-026543","identifier":[{"id":"33372078","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7772306","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85098580136","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bf2aab36-92c7-4382-b7dd-60055b775597","pha-18cc88e6-0215-4c37-a933-11052064f55b","sdu-42dcfce8-a653-4a59-aac6-048942bfd1ac","ucl-b9d519ca-837d-414c-85a6-300a37efdd73","ucn-d092f161-6016-48a6-947a-0a32b49a3535","ucsyd-757ef584-301f-4d04-964c-0c5234a0f089"],"keyword":["Sygdom, sundhedsvidenskab og sygepleje","group concept mapping","health, nutrition and quality of life","medical ethics","occupational therapy","palliative care","public health","rehabilitation medicine","spiritual care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-9-5449B572BCB4B22A812E28E5D833E9CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/doi:%2010.1136/bmjopen-2020-042142","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://bmjopen.bmj.com/content/10/12/e042142.info","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.pha.dk/ws/files/79343946/what_is_spiritual_care.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://bmjopen.bmj.com/content/bmjopen/10/12/e042142.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/175591848/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2020-042142","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.ucl.dk/ws/files/77096172/BMJ_Open._What_is_Spiritual_Care_2020.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, AgeCare - Academy of Geriatric Cancer Research (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"