{"abstract":"This research paper presents a user persona of Indian mothers of preterm neonates. Many of these preterm neonates require hospitalization in Neona-tal Intensive Care Units (NICUs), leading to mental stress for mothers and their families. The mother’s persona is proposed based on hypothesis, user interviews and data analysis. The participant mothers of preterm neonates are graduates and homemakers from semiurban areas around Pune, India. These mothers prefer non-vegetarian diet, they visit a pediatrician more fre-quently and presently, they do not use any mobile healthcare app or YouTube videos for information about neonatal care. A mobile app will be developed for these mothers in future with due consideration to their user persona.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bhutkar, Ganesh","Dongre, Aditya","Deshmukh, Shahaji","Nielsen, Lene","Joshi, Jaydeep"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384638"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["India"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bharati Vidyapeeth","Vishwakarma Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Homemakers","Indian mothers","Mental stress","Mobile healthcare app","Neonatal Intensive Care Units","Neonatal care information","Pediatrician visits","Preterm neonates","Semiurban areas","User persona"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user persona of mother of preterm neonate","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18573/book3.s","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384638","identifier":[{"id":"85085209800","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e50c6707-58f2-4c44-b0d1-8b05cb0993dd"],"keyword":["Homemakers","Indian mothers","Mental stress","Mobile healthcare app","Neonatal Intensive Care Units","Neonatal care information","Pediatrician visits","Preterm neonates","Semiurban areas","User persona"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-43C89089B478BFA23F1E0ACB7547B1CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18573/book3.s","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85520411/User_Persona_of_Mother_of_Preterm_Neonate.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"in","key":"vishwakarma institute of technology","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Vishwakarma Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"bharati vidyapeeth","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Bharati Vidyapeeth","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ganesh","key":"bhutkarpau","last":"Bhutkar","name":"Bhutkar, Ganesh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aditya","key":"dongrepau","last":"Dongre","name":"Dongre, Aditya","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shahaji","key":"deshmukhpau","last":"Deshmukh","name":"Deshmukh, Shahaji","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaydeep","key":"joshipau","last":"Joshi","name":"Joshi, Jaydeep","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"F.","key":"loizidespedh","last":"Loizides","name":"Loizides, F.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"M.","key":"wincklerpedh","last":"Winckler","name":"Winckler, M.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"U.","key":"chatterjeepedh","last":"Chatterjee","name":"Chatterjee, U.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"J.","key":"abdelnournocerapedh","last":"Abdelnour-Nocera","name":"Abdelnour-Nocera, J.","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"A.","key":"parmaxipedh","last":"Parmaxi","name":"Parmaxi, A.","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18573/book3.s","pages":"151-156","publisher":"Cardiff University Press","status":"p","title":"Human Computer Interaction and Emerging Technologies: Adjunct Proceedings from the INTERACT 2019 Workshops"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e50c6707-58f2-4c44-b0d1-8b05cb0993dd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"User Persona of Mother of Preterm Neonate","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384638","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The highly valuable timber species Dalbergia cochinchinensis is severely threatened due to habitat loss and illegal logging throughout its distribution in mainland Southeast Asia and is listed on CITES Appendix II. This study proposes a strategy for conservation and sustainable management of the species based on assessment of genetic structure within and among natural populations. We developed SNP markers from RAD sequencing and used these in combination with SSR genotypes from a previous study to assess the genetic diversity in 26 populations of D. cochinchinensis across its entire range in Laos, Thailand, Cambodia and Vietnam. The species is able of clonal reproduction and we found that trees closer than 45 meters from each other can be clones. Genetic diversity and clustering analysis showed a clear division of populations into five geographical groups with differing levels of diversity. Assignment tests correctly identified the region of origin for approximately 90% of the samples, which demonstrates that despite a low number of successfully identified SNPs, the SSR + SNP marker panel has the potential for tracking the geographic origin of D. cochinchinensis timber for use in CITES regulation and enforcement. We propose the five identified groups to be considered as Management Units and that conservation and breeding programs should be based on a network of in situ and ex situ conservation stands representing the genetic variation among and within these units. We recommend that conservation efforts are directed towards community owned and managed lands, as this has proven an effective strategy locally.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Hartvig, Ida","So, Thea","Changtragoon, Suchitra","Tran, Hoa Thi","Bouamanivong, Somsanith","Ogden, Rob","Senn, Helen","Vieira, Filipe Garrett","Turner, Frances","Talbot, Richard","Theilade, Ida","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Kjær, Erik Dahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-452980"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Cambodia","Laos","Thailand","United Kingdom","Vietnam"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of National Parks, Wildlife and Plant Conservation","Ministry of Agriculture","Ministry of Science and Technology","Royal Zoological Society of Scotland","University of Edinburgh","Vietnam Academy of Agricultural Sciences"],"keyword":["CITES","Conservation genetics","Dalbergia","Threatened species","Tropical trees"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"conservation genetics of the critically endangered siamese rosewood i dalbergia cochinchinensis i recommendations for management and sustainable use","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/287066630/Revised_Manuscript_Conservation_genetics_of_Dalbergia.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-452980","identifier":[{"id":"85084707057","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-638b481e-64de-4223-8c21-15688ee0ae1f"],"keyword":["CITES","Conservation genetics","Dalbergia","Rosewood","Threatened species","Timber species","Tropical trees"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-71527A4F1247F3F3B7921A364A0B2BE8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/287066630/Revised_Manuscript_Conservation_genetics_of_Dalbergia.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"kh","key":"ministry of agriculture","loc":["Cambodia","Asia, South"],"name":"Ministry of Agriculture","used":1},{"affno"