020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Lektor Ingrid Jepsen, underviser Lene Toxvig og lektor Annegrethe Nielsen har udviklet en workshop, der viser betydningen af at engagere sig i viden om naturvidenskabelige, humanvidenskabelige og samfundsvidenskabelige tilgange. Workshoppen afholdes for jordemoderstuderende men er relevant for alle professionsbachelorstuderende. I workshoppen faciliteres læringsrum, hvor de studerende får mulighed for at forstå, udvikle og forbinde forskellige epistemologiske tilgange med deres konkrete faglige praksis. Dermed tydeliggøres, hvorfor videnskabsteori er både vigtig og relevant, og hvordan denne form for viden er en grundlæggende del af professionen.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jepsen, Ingrid","Toxvig, Lene","Nielsen, Annegrethe","Petersen, Inge-Kathrine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-652155"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Refleksiv praksislæring","Videnskabsteori","Workshop","teori praksis uddannelse"],"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"at gøre videnskabsteori epistemologi praksisrelevant for de studerende","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-652155","ids":["ucn-c65c90a1-d506-4745-a7f5-ceccabbc359e"],"keyword":["Læring, pædagogik og undervisning","Refleksiv Praksislæring","Videnskabsteori","Workshop","teori-praksis uddannelse"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C60E8109230296EA6A6034266FCEF200"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Jordemoderuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Metropol EVU"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid","key":"jepsenpau","last":"Jepsen","locid":"e33e2f76-5b3e-4c7a-b9a1-0947cdac786a","name":"Jepsen, Ingrid","orcid":"0000-0002-7897-7036","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"toxvigpau","last":"Toxvig","locid":"59772880-3647-455e-8903-2ef41d6f7d10","name":"Toxvig, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-8579-3681","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Annegrethe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Annegrethe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Inge-Kathrine","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1e79fbfb-5c13-4c84-9912-2f7e1dd859ea","name":"Petersen, Inge-Kathrine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-c65c90a1-d506-4745-a7f5-ceccabbc359e"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"At gøre videnskabsteori/epistemologi praksisrelevant for de studerende","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-652155","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The intestine contains some of the most diverse and complex immune compartments in the body. Here we describe a method for isolating human gut-associated lymphoid tissues (GALTs) that allows unprecedented profiling of the adaptive immune system in submucosal and mucosal isolated lymphoid follicles (SM-ILFs and M-ILFs, respectively) as well as in GALT-free intestinal lamina propria (LP). SM-ILF and M-ILF showed distinct patterns of distribution along the length of the intestine, were linked to the systemic circulation through MAdCAM-1+ high endothelial venules and efferent lymphatics, and had immune profiles consistent with immune-inductive sites. IgA sequencing analysis indicated that human ILFs are sites where intestinal adaptive immune responses are initiated in an anatomically restricted manner. Our findings position ILFs as key inductive hubs for regional immunity in the human intestine, and the methods presented will allow future assessment of these compartments in health and disease.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Fenton, Thomas M.","Jørgensen, Peter B.","Niss, Kristoffer","Rubin, Samuel J.S.","Mörbe, Urs M.","Riis, Lene B.","Da Silva, Clément","Plumb, Adam","Vandamme, Julien","Jakobsen, Henrik L.","Brunak, Søren","Habtezion, Aida","Nielsen, Ole H.","Lindbom, Bengt Johansson","Agace, William Winston"],"cuid":["S02-099.22-033338"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Agace, William Winston"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Stanford University","Stanford University School of Medicine"],"keyword":["Colon","IgA","PP"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immune profiling of human gut associated lymphoid tissue identifies a role for isolated lymphoid follicles in priming of region specific immunity","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.immuni.2020.02.001","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.22-033338","identifier":[{"id":"000520600200016","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7155934","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85081279962","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32160523","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-223b9d4f-db76-4e97-b766-bfd972dbe6e6","ku-304df76a-9411-4949-bbbd-7585634fd308"],"keyword":["ILF","IgA","PP","colon","human intestinal regional mucosal follicles","iIeum"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A0AC262DBB468206B6CC6454813F31DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/211005201/filestore.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7155934/pdf/nihms-1568648.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.immuni.2020.02.001","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Immunobiology and Biomimetics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Techno