{"abstract":"Background: Previous studies indicate that genetic susceptibility and phenotype of rheumatoid arthritis (RA) differ between the populations.Objectives: To compare the clinical, serologic expression and the presence of shared epitopes (SE) of incident RA in two different populations, one from Northern and the other from Southern Europe.Methods: Data on incident RA patients fulfilling EULAR/ACR 2010 classifications criteria for RA were collected at Rheumatology Departments in Denmark and Turkey in 2015-2016. Patients were assessed using the same standardized protocol in both populations. SE carrier status were assigned, according to the du Montcel classification based, into six allele groups: S1, S2, S3D, S3P and X, where S2 and S3P are RA risk-enhancing alleles and S1 and S3D are RA protective alleles of the shared epitope(1).Results: 109 incident RA patients from Denmark and 114 incident RA patients from Turkey were enrolled. Genetic data were available from 87Table 1. Characteristics of incident rheumatoid arthritis patients in Denmark and TurkeyView this table:Table 2. Shared epitope allele carrier frequencies.We found no associations between the risk-enhancing alleles and the presence of IgM rheumatoid factor or ACPA.Conclusion: The Turkish patients were younger and had lower disease activity than Danish at the time of diagnosis. Our study found an enhanced genetic susceptibility to RA in Danish compared to Turkish patients with a higher prevalence of risk-enhancing RA alleles and a lower prevalence of protective alleles.References: [1]Tezenas du Montcel S, Michou L, Petit-Teixeira E, Osorio J, Lemaire I, Lasbleiz S, et al. New classification of HLAtextendashDRB1 alleles supports the shared epitope hypothesis of rheumatoid arthritis susceptibility. Arthritis Rheum 2005; 52: 1063textendash8.Disclosure of Interests: None declared","author_count":11,"contributors":["Lauridsen, K. B.","Linauskas, Asta","Rasmussen, Claus","Can, G.","Onen, F.","Dreyer, Lene","Steffensen, Rudi","Nielsen, Kaspar René","Steen Krogh, N.","Akar, S.","Akkoc, N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-115719"],"event":{"end":"2020-06-03","place":"E-congress, online","start":"2020-06-03","title":"Annual European Congress of Rheumatology: EULAR 2020 (e-congress, online)","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Turkey"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dokuz Eylul University","Manisa Celal Bayar University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["DANBIO, Hjorring, Denmark"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic susceptibility and phenotype of rheumatoid arthritis in danish and turkish patients","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ard.bmj.com/content/79/Suppl_1/1401.1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-115719","ids":["aau-e1cef670-9293-466e-aca2-e3751282a7c3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A59DDF2208921E0082A02E4A37125C71"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Immunology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["DANBIO, Hjorring, Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"tr","key":"dokuz eylul university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Dokuz Eylul University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Zitelab"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"tr","key":"manisa celal bayar university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Manisa Celal Bayar University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K. B.","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"34b19ba6-f0ce-4a8e-bc6f-75462f8b8832","name":"Lauridsen, K. B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"linauskaspau","last":"Linauskas","locid":"92b80fcd-204b-4559-b21c-f5a64513edaa","name":"Linauskas, Asta","name_org":"Linauskas, A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"C.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"16534364-e0f1-4da9-adc4-97ddf1b44140","name":"Rasmussen, Claus","name_org":"Rasmussen, C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"canpau","last":"Can","name":"Can, G.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"onenpau","last":"Onen","name":"Onen, F.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.","key":"dreyerpau","last":"Dreyer","locid":"b12f9d3c-1fa5-4513-8002-c9fd87d60d53","name":"Dreyer, Lene","name_org":"Dreyer, L.","orcid":"0000-0002-5156-2922","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"steffensenpau","last":"Steffensen","locid":"a44dd162-a3b7-45f1-b8aa-a3a22b679931","name":"Steffensen, Rudi","name_org":"Steffensen, R.","orcid":"0000-0002-2080-1177","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K. R.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"bc41abea-4b3e-473b-b7a6-8d2c7515f572","name":"Nielsen, Kaspar René","name_org":"Nielsen, K. R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","corresponding":null,"first":"N.","key":"steenkroghpau","last":"Steen Krogh","name":"Steen Krogh, N.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"akarpau","last":"Akar","name":"Akar, S.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"N.","key":"akkocpau","last":"Akkoc","name":"Akkoc, N.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/annrheumdis-2020-eular.3963","issn":["00034967","14682060"],"issn_org":["00034967"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","pages":"1401-1401","paperid":"AB0202","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","volume":"79"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","zitelab"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e1cef670-9293-466e-aca2-e3751282a7c3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Genetic susceptibility and phenotype of rheumatoid arthritis in Danish and Turkish patients","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-115719","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This work presents the identification and proposed biosynthetic pathway for a compound of mixed polyketide-nonribosomal peptide origin that we named acurin A. The compound was isolated from an extract of the filamentous fungus Aspergillus aculeatus, and its core structure resemble that of the mycotoxin fusarin C produced by several Fusarium species. Based on bioinformatics in combination with RT-qPCR experiments and gene-deletion analysis, we identified a biosynthetic gene cluster (BGC) in A. aculeatus responsible for the biosynthesis of acurin A. Moreover, we were able to show that a polyketide synthase (PKS) and a nonribosomal peptide synthetase (NRPS) enzyme separately encoded by this BGC are responsible for the synthesis of the PK-NRP compound, acurin A, core structure. In comparison, the production of fusarin C is reported to be facilitated by a linked PKS-NRPS hybrid enzyme. Phylogenetic analyses suggest the PKS and NRPS in A. aculeatus resulted from a recent fission of an ancestral hybrid enzyme followed by gene duplication. In addition to the PKS- and NRPS-encoding genes of acurin A, we show that six other genes are influencing the biosynthesis including a regulatory transcription factor. Altogether, we have demonstrated the involvement of eight genes in the biosynthesis of acurin A, including an in-cluster transcription factor. This study highlights the biosynthetic capacity of A. aculeatus and serves as an example of how the CRISPR/Cas9 system can be exploited for the construction of fungal strains that can be readily engineered.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Wolff, Peter B.","Nielsen, Maria Lund","Slot, Jason C.","Andersen, Lasse Norup","Petersen, Lene Maj","Isbrandt, Thomas","Holm, Dorte Koefoed","Mortensen, Uffe Hasbro","Nødvig, Christina Spuur","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","Hoof, Jakob Blæsbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-358354"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ohio State University"],"keyword":["Aspergillus aculeatus","CRISPR Cas9","NRPS","PKS","Secondary metabolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"acurin a a novel hybrid compound biosynthesized by individually translated pks and nrps encoding genes in aspergillus aculeatus","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fgb.2020.103378","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-358354","identifier":[{"id":"32234543","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85083113251","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b3fc8b17-77ce-4600-bfdf-c29e5cf7d29d"],"keyword":["Acurin A","Aspergillus aculeatus","CRISPR/Cas9","Hybrid compound","NRPS","PKS","Secondary metabolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D19CE840D446357AB4EE5B4D0FFADAE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fgb.2020.103378","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/209786632/1_s2.0_S1087184520300694_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/209697337/1_s2.0_S1087184520300694_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Synthetic Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Synthetic Biology, Eukaryotic Molecular Cell Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"ohio state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ohio State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter B.","key":"wolffpau","last":"Wolff","locid":"df7eba21-df08-438a-a488-8456b01a0ee7","name":"Wolff, Peter B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria L.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3161157c-75e3-4aa2-8376-8fbc8cb8b1ee","name":"Nielsen, Maria Lund","name_org":"Nielsen, Maria L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jason C.","key":"slotpau","last":"Slot","name":"Slot, Jason C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse N.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8ced82e2-4db1-4522-8690-046e4b2093b1","name":"Andersen, Lasse Norup","name_org":"Andersen, Lasse N.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene M.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"7a1c5a02-7eb8-40e3-a1ec-621fb3c37652","name":"Petersen, Lene Maj","name_org":"Petersen, Lene M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"isbrandtpau","last":"Isbrandt","locid":"0a0ca6df-f39c-4d4f-b7ce-d476ea20cc7d","name":"Isbrandt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-3938-0816","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte K.","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"aedc7b19-7dd8-4af4-a8cc-5a73f5783c91","name":"Holm, Dorte Koefoed","name_org":"Holm, Dorte K.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uffe H.","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"dec3038b-f004-4c96-84a1-52825e1c0ce8","name":"Mortensen, Uffe Hasbro","name_org":"Mortensen, Uffe H.","orcid":"0000-0002-7794-7273","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christina S.","key":"nødvigpau","last":"Nødvig","locid":"c366600e-4f20-4ef6-91f9-6af646b03f81","name":"Nødvig, Christina Spuur","name_org":"Nødvig, Christina S.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas O.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"bd958d52-71b6-4720-b30a-cc9305633b43","name":"Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","name_org":"Larsen, Thomas O.","orcid":"0000-0002-3362-5707","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob B.","key":"hoofpau","last":"Hoof","locid":"339ce5a8-3232-410d-9484-abbc0f5b81b3","name":"Hoof, Jakob Blæsbjerg","name_org":"Hoof, Jakob B.","orcid":"0000-0002-7650-9300","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32234543"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fgb.2020.103378","issn":["10871845","10960937"],"issn_org":["10871845"],"journal":"Fungal Genetics and Biology","paperid":"103378","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Fungal Genetics and Biology","volume":"139"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083113251"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b3fc8b17-77ce-4600-bfdf-c29e5cf7d29d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Acurin A, a novel hybrid compound, biosynthesized by individually translated PKS- and NRPS-encoding genes in Aspergillus aculeatus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-358354","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This manual is the product of a collaboration between Gladsaxe municipality and the Institute for Social Work, at University College Copenhagen. The aim of the project, which was entitled ‘Focus on Inclusion and Outcomes using FIT in Children’s Services’, was to improve the quality of interventions when children and their families come into contact with statutory children’s services in Gladsaxe municipality, which lies North of Copenhagen in Denmark. More specifically, the aim was to develop Feedback Informed Treatment (FIT) for use in statutory children’s services with at-risk children for all Danish municipalities. Gladsaxe Municipality, which had had a positive experience with FIT in its family counselling services, paved the way, testing the approach, while staff from University College Copenhagen developed the manual and gathered the underlying empirical data. This development process took two years and in-volved interviews, extensive field work, and the production of short films featuring staff from Gladsaxe municipality and their children, showing the approach. The films which supplement the manual illustrate how to enhance the quality of work within children’s services using the approach.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Mackrill, Thomas","Nielsen, Sussie","Kronbæk, Mette","Nedergård, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-389850"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["social work and social conditions"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feedback informed treatment manual for statutory children s services","src":["kp"],"src-code":["DI-UC-KP"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.kp.dk/ws/files/73383959/FIT_Manual_UK.PDF","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-389850","ids":["kp-92dcdcad-e45a-4b9c-a88a-228d5301e1a6"],"keyword":["social work and social conditions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-429F14859C9B2FF344F0C57FD87A0837"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.kp.dk/ws/files/73383959/FIT_Manual_UK.PDF","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for pædagogiske og samfundsfaglige uddannelser-Dekan, Inst. for Socialrådgiveruddannelse - Inst.chef","Københavns Professionshøjskole, Socialrådgiveruddannelserne1"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"mackrillpau","last":"Mackrill","locid":"8160e5e2-eec9-4305-82e2-eebdf8e0b1e7","name":"Mackrill, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sussie","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"26086851-9f89-4b31-aba4-28204f7ab2ec","name":"Nielsen, Sussie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"kronbækpau","last":"Kronbæk","locid":"bfe4b47e-2fa4-47b6-a343-0a4de73ee4c3","name":"Kronbæk, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-6428-3033","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nedergårdpau","last":"Nedergård","locid":"41d141af-9f71-441c-ade2-5135e0b78432","name":"Nedergård, Lene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793894143"],"pages":"100","place":"København","publisher":"Københavns Professionshøjskole","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-92dcdcad-e45a-4b9c-a88a-228d5301e1a6"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Feedback informed treatment - : manual for statutory children's services","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-389850","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) includes Crohn’s disease (CD) and ulcerative colitis (UC). These are chronic autoimmune diseases of unknown etiology affecting the gastrointestinal tract. The IBD population includes a heterogeneous group of patients with varying disease courses requiring personalized treatment protocols. The complexity of the disease often delays the diagnosis and the initiation of appropriate treatments. In a subset of patients, IBD leads to colitis-associated cancer (CAC). MicroRNAs are single-stranded regulatory noncoding RNAs of 18 to 22 nucleotides with putative roles in the pathogenesis of IBD and colorectal cancer. They have been explored as biomarkers and therapeutic targets. Both tissue-derived and circulating microRNAs have emerged as promising biomarkers in the differential diagnosis and in the prognosis of disease severity of IBD as well as predictive biomarkers in drug resistance. In addition, knowledge of the cellular localization of differentially expressed microRNAs is a prerequisite for deciphering the biological role of these important epigenetic regulators and the cellular localization may even contribute to an alternative repertoire of biomarkers. In this review, we discuss findings based on RT-qPCR, microarray profiling, next generation sequencing and in situ hybridization of microRNA biomarkers identified in the circulation and in tissue biopsies.","author_count":6,"contributors":["James, Jaslin P.","Riis, Lene Buhl","Malham, Mikkel","Høgdall, Estrid","Langholz, Ebbe","Nielsen, Boye S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-437065"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biomarkers","Circulating miRNA","Crohn s disease CD","MicroRNA miRNA","inflammatory bowel disease IBD","ulcerative colitis UC"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-BION"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-BION","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microrna biomarkers in ibd differential diagnosis and prediction of colitis associated cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms21217893","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-437065","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7660644","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33114313","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85094573990","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4914386e-99ed-4e27-a3a2-c415001235d8"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Circulating miRNA","Colitis-associated cancer (CAC)","Crohn’s disease (CD)","Inflammatory bowel disease (IBD)","MicroRNA (miRNA)","Ulcerative colitis (UC)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1854E9179F450FCD951179F79AE32B91"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/251183978/ijms_21_07893.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms21217893","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"bioneer","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-BION","l3nn":"Bioneer","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Bioneer","namevar":["Bioneer"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-BION","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jaslin P.","key":"jamespau","last":"James","locid":"db7a60ca-ab78-4f9f-980c-5ca8309b9ce6","name":"James, Jaslin P.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Buhl","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"malhampau","last":"Malham","locid":"abd36094-4e38-424b-98cb-7cce541fec0f","name":"Malham, Mikkel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Estrid","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","locid":"a48f77b8-ee6d-4a52-a3f3-deb515bdd48f","name":"Høgdall, Estrid","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ebbe","key":"langholzpau","last":"Langholz","locid":"c3ab9fb7-1eed-4843-bc2b-9a97abe090c4","name":"Langholz, Ebbe","orcid":"0000-0002-8558-8442","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Boye S.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Boye S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33114313"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijms21217893","issn":["14220067","16616596"],"issn_org":["16616596"],"issue":"21","journal":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","pages":"1-19","paperid":"7893","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85094573990"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4914386e-99ed-4e27-a3a2-c415001235d8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MicroRNA biomarkers in IBD-differential diagnosis and prediction of colitis-associated cancer","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-437065","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Intestinal organoids have widespread research and biomedical applications, such as disease modeling, drug testing and regenerative medicine. However, the transition towards clinical use has in part been hampered by the dependency on animal tumor-derived basement membrane extracts (BMEs), which are poorly defined and ill-suited for regulatory approval due to their origin and batch-to-batch variability. In order to overcome these limitations, and to enable clinical translation, we tested the use of a fully defined hydrogel matrix, QGel CN99, to establish and expand intestinal organoids directly from human colonic biopsies. We achieved efficient de novo establishment, expansion and organoid maintenance, while also demonstrating sustained genetic stability. Additionally, we were able to preserve stemness and differentiation capacity, with transcriptomic profiles resembling normal colonic epithelium. All data proved comparable to organoids cultured in the BME-benchmark Matrigel. The application of a fully defined hydrogel, completely bypassing the use of BMEs, will drastically improve the reproducibility and scalability of organoid studies, but also advance translational applications in personalized medicine and stem cell-based regenerative therapies.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bergenheim, Fredrik","Fregni, Giulia","Buchanan, Cara Field","Riis, Lene Buhl","Heulot, Mathieu","Touati, Jeremy","Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","Rizzi, Simone Carlo","Nielsen, Ole Haagen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-497455"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cell Differentiation","Extracellular matrix","Hydrogel","Intestinal stem cells"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a fully defined 000000000003d matrix for i ex vivo i expansion of human colonic organoids from biopsy tissue","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biomaterials.2020.120248","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-497455","identifier":[{"id":"32891909","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85090159010","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ae20452f-e531-4aad-8aa4-c3aa9a173907"],"keyword":["Cell differentiation","Extracellular matrix","Human colonic organoids","Hydrogel","Intestinal stem cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F0E854BEC76E03BD344F65E7DFCF69D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biomaterials.2020.120248","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250253785/1_s2.0_S0142961220304944_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Fredrik","key":"bergenheimpau","last":"Bergenheim","name":"Bergenheim, Fredrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Giulia","key":"fregnipau","last":"Fregni","name":"Fregni, Giulia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cara Field","key":"buchananpau","last":"Buchanan","name":"Buchanan, Cara Field","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1