{"abstract":"Paludiculture, defined as agriculture on wet or rewetted peatlands has been proposed as a mitigation strategy to reverse unsustainable environmental impacts such as land subsidence, nutrient release to surface water and greenhouse gas emissions from traditional agriculture on drained peatland. In particular, the production of biomass feedstock from flood-tolerant perennial grasses for green biorefining to protein and other value-added products may be a viable economic and environmental sustainable option for temperate peatlands. However, optimal quality characteristics of the biomass for protein extraction have yet to be defined. In 2018, field plots cultivated with different flood-tolerant perennial grasses were established in an agricultural fen peatland in Denmark. Of these, a total of eight plots cultivated with reed canary grass (RCG) and tall fescue were each subdivided into six sub-plots with different management regarding harvest and fertilisation. Harvest frequencies ranged from one to five times in the period between mid-May to mid-October at intervals of 4-6 weeks. The sub-plots received fertilisation of 100 kg ha-1 of both N and K prior to each harvest. Protein extractability of the grasses was assessed by lab-scale biorefinery techniques using a screw press followed by precipitation of true protein in the resulting juice. This was compared with protein fractions classified by the Cornell Net Carbohydrate and Protein System (CNCPS). The biorefinery extractable protein yields (fresh weight) ranged from 10 % to 25 % of the fresh mass input, dependent on treatment, with summer harvests having the lowest yield. Evaluation of the easily extractable crude protein (CP) CNCPS fractions B1 and B2 showed yields of between 61.8 – 110.7 g CP kg-1 DM. Preliminary processing of data showed that the cumulative yields of extractable crude protein for the growing season seems highly affected by management.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Claudia","Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Lene","Jørgensen, Uffe","Lærke, Poul Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-167448"],"event":{"end":"2020-05-08","start":"2020-05-04","title":"EGU General Assembly 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Claudia"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protein yield and extractability of flood tolerant perennial grasses cultivated on a riparian fen affected by harvest and fertilisation frequency","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-167448","ids":["au-42f08955-1832-4010-ab7e-27495e8ac168"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2281F9D76A6D474DD7B857DBBB85BACD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Climate and Water"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claudia","key":"kallanielsenpau","last":"Kalla Nielsen","locid":"66d68122-06cf-4e2c-9f01-b6df8fdecb1c","name":"Nielsen, Claudia","name_org":"Kalla Nielsen, Claudia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"stødkildejørgensenpau","last":"Stødkilde-Jørgensen","locid":"7edb699b-a75e-48cd-a351-9ee9e1321d4d","name":"Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0001-9434-0118","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uffe","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"efa7e924-c197-4060-8904-110cf0a30837","name":"Jørgensen, Uffe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Poul Erik","key":"lærkepau","last":"Lærke","locid":"03fcd9e2-3402-466b-86fc-f3c8163d9306","name":"Lærke, Poul Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-2224-3893","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-42f08955-1832-4010-ab7e-27495e8ac168"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Protein yield and extractability of flood-tolerant perennial grasses cultivated on a riparian fen, affected by harvest and fertilisation frequency","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-167448","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To evaluate if High-volume Image-guided Injection (HVIGI)-treatment for chronic mid-portion Achilles tendinopathy (AT) improve function and reduce pain at 12-months follow-up. Methods: Patients with resistant mid-portion AT who failed to improve after a three-month eccentric loading program were included in the study. Maximal tendon thickness was assessed with ultrasound. All patients were injected with 10 mL of 0.5% Marcaine, 0.5 mL Triamcinolonacetonid (40 mg/mL) and 40 mL of 0.9% NaCl saline solution under real-time ultrasound-guidance and high pressure. All outcome measures were recorded at baseline and 12 months. A standardized eccentric rehabilitation protocol was prescribed after HVIGI-treatment. Clinical outcome was assessed with the Victorian Institute of Sports Assessment-Achilles tendon questionnaire (VISA-A) and statistically analyses were performed. Results: The study included 30 single treatment HVIGI procedures in AT in 28 patients (23 men, 5 women) with a mean age of 45.1 (range 16–63). The mean duration of symptoms before HVIGI was 37 months. The baseline VISA-A score of 50 ± 15 (range 14–74) improved to 61 ± 21 (range 31–94) after 1 year (p = 0.04). Of the 30 AT procedures 10 patients (11 AT) were not satisfied after the initial HVIGI procedure. Of these, 8 patients (9 AT) needed additional HVIGI and two patients needed surgery. Of the remaining 18 patients (19 AT), 10 patients had more than a 10-point improvement in the VISA-A score after 1 year. Conclusions: In this retrospective case-study, only 10 patients (33%) did benefit of a single HVIGI treatment at 12-months and an 11-point significant improvement was seen at on the VISA-A score.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Torsten Grønbech","Miller, Lene Lindberg","Mygind-Klavsen, Bjarne","Lind, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-215075"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Torsten Grønbech"],"keyword":["Achilles","Achilles tendon","Eccentric training","HVIGI","High volume image guided injection","Tendinopathy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of high volume image guided injection in the chronic non insertional achilles tendinopathy a retrospective case series","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40634-020-00264-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-215075","identifier":[{"id":"85086940192","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32594331","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000704723900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7320968","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-968e4774-e6b5-48e4-8ab2-9083b8e79039"],"keyword":["Achilles","Achilles tendon","Eccentric training","HVIGI","High-volume image-guided injection","Tendinopathy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8C4FD33B0D24B26251C22EFF065F8D0D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40634-020-00264-4","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Orthopaedic surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten Grønbech","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"33da3303-c376-4195-b3d6-7767956a26fe","name":"Nielsen, Torsten Grønbech","orcid":"0000-0001-5354-1781","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Lindberg","key":"millerpau","last":"Miller","locid":"89e35381-5a14-4e36-8f64-abe7df8e4cac","name":"Miller, Lene Lindberg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne","key":"mygindklavsenpau","last":"Mygind-Klavsen","locid":"ba3c3b44-35ee-4ec0-a8a3-93178867532f","name":"Mygind-Klavsen, Bjarne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"lindpau","last":"Lind","locid":"5a1298e3-a4d7-4818-88f4-da6cdbf1784d","name":"Lind, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32594331"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40634-020-00264-4","issn":["21971153"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Experimental Orthopaedics","paperid":"45","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Experimental Orthopaedics","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086940192"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-968e4774-e6b5-48e4-8ab2-9083b8e79039"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The effect of high-volume image-guided injection in the chronic non-insertional Achilles tendinopathy : a retrospective case series","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-215075","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this workshop is to engage in co-design of personas to explore the interplay of autonomous technologies with user experience and engagement. Automating a process that is embedded into people's everyday lives and activities will surely impact their experience. In a time where there is strong push towards more and more automation in our daily life, the workshop will explore the value of co-design in bringing to the fore the opportunities and issues of such trend on users’ experiences and engagements in multiple contexts such as work, health, entertainment and learning. Through the co-design of personas in future scenarios of automation the workshop will concretely identify valuable automation design goals for user experience and engagement drawing on participants’ knowledge from industry projects and academic research.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Abdelnour-Nocera, José","Cabrero, Daniel","Campos, Pedro","Gonçalves, Frederica","Clemmensen, Torkil","Gissing, Robin","Nielsen, Lene","Saadati, Parisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-297619"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","end":"2020-10-29","place":"Online","start":"2020-10-25","title":"11th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction. NordiCHI 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Madeira Interactive Technologies Institute","Personas Technology Ltd","University of West London"],"keyword":["Automation","Co design","Interaction design","Personas","User experience"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co designing personas for user experience and engagement in automation","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-297619","identifier":[{"id":"85095826196","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-e97e68b8-db04-4b38-a7e8-57fb1951b045"],"keyword":["Automation","Co-design","Interaction design","Personas","User experience"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-C5840DA2E35237EEA3B9EF76222803C5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of west london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of West London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"madeira interactive technologies institute","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Madeira Interactive Technologies Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"personas technology ltd","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Personas Technology Ltd","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"José","key":"abdelnournocerapau","last":"Abdelnour-Nocera","name":"Abdelnour-Nocera, José","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"cabreropau","last":"Cabrero","name":"Cabrero, Daniel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"campospau","last":"Campos","name":"Campos, Pedro","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederica","key":"gonçalvespau","last":"Gonçalves","name":"Gonçalves, Frederica","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torkil","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"8f33094c-9f68-4674-ba9c-33a67db0d011","name":"Clemmensen, Torkil","orcid":"0000-0002-0934-2336","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"gissingpau","last":"Gissing","name":"Gissing, Robin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Parisa","key":"saadatipau","last":"Saadati","name":"Saadati, Parisa","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3419249.3420093","eisbn":["9781450375795"],"place":"New York, NY","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM International Conference Proceeding Series","status":"p","subtitle":"Shaping Experiences, Shaping Society","title":"NordiCHI '20: Proceedings of the 11th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123041028"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-e97e68b8-db04-4b38-a7e8-57fb1951b045"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Co-designing Personas for User Experience and Engagement in Automation","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-297619","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper explores how an IT company wants to change from product-centricity to servitization. A cross-functional customer journey workshop mapped the current state from the customer’s point of view, and by identifying opportunities, it identifies gaps in becoming a service organization. Activities in the workshop focused on mapping a current customer journey and a proposition of a customer journey. The case explores how a service design workshop and tools can be used in strategic work, to support and facilitate a discussion on changes needed to be customer-centric, going beyond technology and features. The workshop and maps proved useful in facilitating and visualizing the current organizational state and identifying opportunities for what it takes to shift to servitization. This case contributes to practical aspects of how service design tools can support organizational transformation towards servitization.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Harre, Olivia Thomassen","Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384025"],"event":{"acronym":"ServDes","title":"ServDes - Service Design and Innovation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Customer Centricity","Customer Journey Mapping","Organizational Transformation","Service Design","Servitization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from product centricity to services design workshops and maps as tools in strategy articulation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85683057/103_Harre_Nielsen_SP.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384025","ids":["itu-bcbaeac2-f896-48a2-a4d8-3231d6be21df"],"keyword":["Customer Journey Mapping","Customer-Centricity","Organizational Transformation","Service Design","Servitization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-10A93DA7AA8F1C02B6B92C79DB6E3AF3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85683057/103_Harre_Nielsen_SP.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olivia Thomassen","key":"harrepau","last":"Harre","locid":"8949ca8c-746d-4a53-b816-ec9ebf06764c","name":"Harre, Olivia Thomassen","orcid":"0009-0001-3681-3770","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Y.","key":"akamapedh","last":"Akama","name":"Akama, Y.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"L.","key":"fennessypedh","last":"Fennessy","name":"Fennessy, L.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"S.","key":"harringtonpedh","last":"Harrington","name":"Harrington, S.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"A.","key":"farragopedh","last":"Farrago","name":"Farrago, A.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789179297794"],"pages":"311","place":"Melbourne, Australia","publisher":"Linköping University Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Linköping Electronic Conference Proceedings 173","title":"ServDes.2020: Tensions, Paradoxes, Plurality"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bcbaeac2-f896-48a2-a4d8-3231d6be21df"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From product centricity to services: Design workshops and maps as tools in strategy articulation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384025","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Testicular germ cell tumours (TGCTs) are characterised by an overall high cisplatin-sensitivity which has been linked to their continued expression of pluripotency factors. Recently, the Nodal signalling pathway has been implicated in the regulation of pluripotency factor expression in fetal germ cells, and the pathway could therefore also be involved in regulating expression of pluripotency factors in malignant germ cells, and hence cisplatin-sensitivity in TGCTs. Methods: We used in vitro culture of the TGCT-derived cell line NTera2, ex vivo tissue culture of primary TGCT specimens and xenografting of NTera2 cells into nude mice in order to investigate the consequences of manipulating Nodal and Activin signalling on pluripotency factor expression, apoptosis, proliferation and cisplatin-sensitivity. Results: The Nodal signalling factors were markedly expressed concomitantly with the pluripotency factor OCT4 in GCNIS cells, seminomas and embryonal carcinomas. Despite this, inhibition of Nodal and Activin signalling either alone or simultaneously did not affect proliferation or apoptosis in malignant germ cells in vitro or ex vivo. Interestingly, inhibition of Nodal signalling in vitro reduced the expression of pluripotency factors and Nodal pathway genes, while stimulation of the pathway increased their expression. However, cisplatin-sensitivity was not affected following pharmacological inhibition of Nodal/Activin signalling or siRNA-mediated knockdown of the obligate co-receptor CRIPTO in NTera2 cells in vitro or in a xenograft model. Conclusion: Our findings suggest that the Nodal signalling pathway may be involved in regulating pluripotency factor expression in malignant germ cells, but manipulation of the pathway does not appear to affect cisplatin-sensitivity or tumour cell proliferation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Harpelunde Poulsen, K.","Nielsen, J. E.","Grønkær Toft, B.","Joensen, Ulla Nordström","Rasmussen, Lene Juel","Blomberg Jensen, M.","Mitchell, R. T.","Juul, Anders","Rajpert-De Meyts, E.","Jorgensen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-430680"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh"],"keyword":["Testicular cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of nodal signalling on pluripotency factor expression tumour cell proliferation and cisplatin sensitivity in testicular germ cell tumours","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-020-06820-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-430680","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7181506","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32326899","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85084031253","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3e54273b-50aa-4ee4-bfc4-c82b7d88230f"],"keyword":["Cisplatin-sensitivity","Expression of pluripotency factors","GCNIS","Nodal and Activin signalling","Testicular cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1478F4A2AF65C665204596D90B7ECDF7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-020-06820-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/243007378/s12885_020_06820_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Urology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"K.","key":"harpelundepoulsenpau","last":"Harpelunde Poulsen","name":"Harpelunde Poulsen, K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J. E.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, J. E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"B.","key":"grønkærtoftpau","last":"Grønkær Toft","name":"Grønkær Toft, B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"U. N.","key":"joensenpau","last":"Joensen","locid":"8df5abc2-4b6f-462e-b702-5079bdf76876","name":"Joensen, Ulla Nordström","name_org":"Joensen, U. N.","orcid":"0000-0001-5400-4531","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"L. J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"54d5267c-3c91-45bc-ace5-1d0edb1b250d","name":"Rasmussen, Lene Juel","name_org":"Rasmussen, L. J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"M.","key":"blombergjensenpau","last":"Blomberg Jensen","name":"Blomberg Jensen, M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"R. T.","key":"mitchellpau","last":"Mitchell","name":"Mitchell, R. T.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"A.","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","name_org":"Juul, A.","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"E.","key":"rajpertdemeytspau","last":"Rajpert-De Meyts","name":"Rajpert-De Meyts, E.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"A.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"46015f76-041c-4177-aa3a-8bcfd13eda19","name":"Jorgensen, Anders","name_org":"Jørgensen, A.","orcid":"0000-0001-6012-6965","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32326899"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12885-020-06820-6","issn":["14712407"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Cancer","paperid":"349","status":"p","title":"BMC Cancer","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084031253"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3e54273b-50aa-4ee4-bfc4-c82b7d88230f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Influence of Nodal signalling on pluripotency factor expression, tumour cell proliferation and cisplatin-sensitivity in testicular germ cell tumours","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-430680","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Author summary Birt-Hogg-Dube (BHD) syndrome is a dominantly inherited genetic disease characterized by predisposition to fibrofolliculomas, lung cysts, and renal cancer. The disease is linked to germline variants in the folliculin (FLCN) tumor suppressor gene. Here, we present a combined computational and experimental study, focusing on rare BHD-linked missense and single amino acid deletion variants. Our data show that many disease-causing FLCN variants lead to structural destabilization and rapid proteasomal degradation of the FLCN protein. The reduced level of FLCN, in turn, leads to degradation of the FLCN binding partners FNIP1 and FNIP2. Additional results show that the turnover of FLCN is regulated by the deubiquitylating enzyme Ubp15/USP7 and molecular chaperones. We propose that for some missense variants, stabilization and resulting restoration of function may hold therapeutic potential, and that our computational saturation scan encompassing both missense variants and single site deletions in FLCN may allow classification of rare FLCN variants of uncertain clinical significance. Germline mutations in the folliculin (FLCN) tumor suppressor gene are linked to Birt-Hogg-Dube (BHD) syndrome, a dominantly inherited genetic disease characterized by predisposition to fibrofolliculomas, lung cysts, and renal cancer. Most BHD-linked FLCN variants include large deletions and splice site aberrations predicted to cause loss of function. The mechanisms by which missense variants and short in-frame deletions in FLCN trigger disease are unknown. Here, we present an integrated computational and experimental study that reveals that the majority of such disease-causing FLCN variants cause loss of function due to proteasomal degradation of the encoded FLCN protein, rather than directly ablating FLCN function. Accordingly, several different single-site FLCN variants are present at strongly reduced levels in cells. In line with our finding that FLCN variants are protein quality control targets, several are also highly insoluble and fail to associate with the FLCN-binding partners FNIP1 and FNIP2. The lack of FLCN binding leads to rapid proteasomal degradation of FNIP1 and FNIP2. Half of the tested FLCN variants are mislocalized in cells, and one variant (Delta E510) forms perinuclear protein aggregates. A yeast-based stability screen revealed that the deubiquitylating enzyme Ubp15/USP7 and molecular chaperones regulate the turnover of the FLCN variants. Lowering the temperature led to a stabilization of two FLCN missense proteins, and for one (R362C), function was re-established at low temperature. In conclusion, we propose that most BHD-linked FLCN missense variants and small in-frame deletions operate by causing misfolding and degradation of the FLCN protein, and that stabilization and resulting restoration of function may hold therapeutic potential of certain disease-linked variants. Our computational saturation scan encompassing both missense variants and single site deletions in FLCN may allow classification of rare FLCN variants of uncertain clinical significance.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Clausen, Lene","Stein, Amelie","Grønbæk-Thygesen, Martin","Nygaard, Lasse","Søltoft, Cecilie Lützen","Nielsen, Sofie V.","Lisby, Michael","Ravid, Tommer","Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","Hartmann-Petersen, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-470575"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hebrew University of Jerusalem"],"keyword":["In silico","MISFOLDED PROTEINS","Molecular Chaperones","Protein quality control","Spontaneous pneumothorax","Tumor suppressor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"folliculin variants linked to birt hogg dubé syndrome are targeted for proteasomal degradation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1009187","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-470575","identifier":[{"id":"33137092","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7660926","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85095873951","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000588362700006","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-80dbc47d-37b5-42ba-b134-8613d054672c"],"keyword":["AMINO-ACID DELETION","BHD GENE","CO-CHAPERONES","IN-SILICO","MISFOLDED PROTEINS","MOLECULAR CHAPERONES","NIHON RAT MODEL","PROTEIN-QUALITY CONTROL","SPONTANEOUS PNEUMOTHORAX","TUMOR-SUPPRESSOR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7180C1627818105090C511FA0D08907E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/252469972/Folliculin_variants_linked_to_Birt_Hogg_Dub_syndrome_are_targeted_for_proteasomal_degradation.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1009187","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Biomolecular Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"hebrew university of jerusalem","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Hebrew University of Jerusalem","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"60754bbd-4d35-4fc1-a020-21185a472880","name":"Clausen, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Amelie","key":"steinpau","last":"Stein","locid":"883406ce-8afb-4747-a574-9c46516128db","name":"Stein, Amelie","orcid":"0000-0002-5862-1681","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"grønbækthygesenpau","last":"Grønbæk-Thygesen","locid":"862836e9-af0a-4ed1-aed5-e035725e0f97","name":"Grønbæk-Thygesen, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lasse","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","name":"Nygaard, Lasse","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cecilie L.","key":"søltoftpau","last":"Søltoft","locid":"d1109dde-8f68-46f6-9904-590f89e6c205","name":"Søltoft, Cecilie Lützen","name_org":"Søltoft, Cecilie L.","orcid":"0000-0002-3194-0287","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sofie V.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2fb2e8f9-1e4a-4302-9b63-4b64ba5b6f45","name":"Nielsen, Sofie V.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"lisbypau","last":"Lisby","locid":"cab97fc6-55a6-4615-af05-d077341b5ae0","name":"Lisby, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-4830-5247","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tommer","key":"ravidpau","last":"Ravid","name":"Ravid, Tommer","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kresten","key":"lindorfflarsenpau","last":"Lindorff-Larsen","locid":"be20a4d8-92c4-44b9-9dfb-b6ad6471a58c","name":"Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","orcid":"0000-0002-4750-6039","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"hartmannpetersenpau","last":"Hartmann-Petersen","locid":"fea900ee-b167-45e9-af2c-00038ff06862","name":"Hartmann-Petersen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-7791","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33137092"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pgen.1009187","issn":["15537390","15537404"],"issn_org":["15537404"],"issue":"11","journal":"PLoS Genetics","paperid":"e1009187","status":"p","title":"PLoS Genetics","title_org":"PLOS Genetics","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85095873951"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-80dbc47d-37b5-42ba-b134-8613d054672c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Folliculin variants linked to Birt-Hogg-Dubé syndrome are targeted for proteasomal degradation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-470575","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: The impact of neutropenia in critically ill immunocompromised patients admitted in a context of acute respiratory failure (ARF) remains uncertain. The primary objective was to assess the prognostic impact of neutropenia on outcomes of these patients. Secondary objective was to assess etiology of ARF according to neutropenia. Methods: We performed a post hoc analysis of a prospective multicenter multinational study from 23 ICUs belonging to the Nine-I network. Between November 2015 and July 2016, all adult immunocompromised patients with ARF admitted to the ICU were included in the study. Adjusted analyses included: (1) a hierarchical model with center as random effect; (2) propensity score (PS) matched cohort; and (3) adjusted analysis in the matched cohort. Results: Overall, 1481 patients were included in this study of which 165 had neutropenia at ICU admission (11%). ARF etiologies distribution was significantly different between neutropenic and non-neutropenic patients, main etiologies being bacterial pneumonia (48% vs 27% in neutropenic and non-neutropenic patients, respectively). Initial oxygenation strategy was standard supplemental oxygen in 755 patients (51%), high-flow nasal oxygen in 165 (11%), non-invasive ventilation in 202 (14%) and invasive mechanical ventilation in 359 (24%). Before adjustment, hospital mortality was significantly higher in neutropenic patients (54% vs 42%; p = 0.006). After adjustment for confounder and center effect, neutropenia was no longer associated with outcome (OR 1.40, 95% CI 0.93–2.11). Similar results were observed after matching (52% vs 46%, respectively; p = 0.35) and after adjustment in the matched cohort (OR 1.04; 95% CI 0.63–1.72). Conclusion: Neutropenia at ICU admission is not associated with hospital mortality in this cohort of critically ill immunocompromised patients admitted for ARF. In neutropenic patients, main ARF etiologies are bacterial and fungal infections.","author_count":28,"contributors":["Mokart, Djamel","Darmon, Michael","Schellongowski, Peter","Pickkers, Peter","Soares, Marcio","Rello, Jordi","Bauer, Philippe R.","van de Louw, Andry","Lemiale, Virginie","Taccone, Fabio Silvio","Martin-Loeches, Ignacio","Salluh, Jorge","Rusinova, Katerina","Mehta, Sangeeta","Antonelli, Massimo","Kouatchet, Achille","Barratt-Due, Andreas","Valkonen, Miia","Landburg, Precious Pearl","Bukan, Ramin Brandt","Pène, Frédéric","Metaxa, Victoria","Burghi, Gaston","Saillard, Colombe","Nielsen, Lene Bjerregaard","Canet, Emmanuel","Bisbal, Magali","Azoulay, Elie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-578740"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["for the Efraim investigators and the Nine-I study group"],"corresponding_author":["Mokart, Djamel"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Brazil","Canada","Czechia","Finland","France","Ireland","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","United Kingdom","United States","Uruguay"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Angers University Hospital","Charles University","D’Or Institute for Research and Education","Erasme University Hospital ULB","Fundacion Jimenez Dıaz and CIBER de Enfermedades Respiratorias (CIBERES)","Graduate School of Health Economics and Management","Helsinki University Hospital","Hospital Maciel Montevideo","King's College Hospital","Mayo Clinic","Medical University of Vienna","Oslo University Hospital","Paoli-Calmettes Institute","Paris Descartes University","Paris Diderot University","Radboud University Medical Center","The Pennsylvania State University","Trinity College Dublin","University Hospital of Nantes","University Medical Center Groningen","University of Toronto","Université de Montpellier – Université Paul Valéry – EPHE","Vall d'Hebron Institut de Recerca"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":[