kero, Sorella","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"eshojhenrikpau","last":"Eshoj","locid":"fae95446-d3b2-4cf5-a9cc-23a7ab55ed16","name":"Eshoj, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-9148-7197","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9 10","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"kongsgaardnielsenlenepau","last":"Kongsgaard Nielsen","locid":"621d166f-6298-48ed-9f2d-d8d52bb40446","name":"Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-2083-3870","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Esa","key":"jantunenesapau","last":"Jantunen","name":"Jantunen, Esa","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline","key":"heckmancarolinepau","last":"Heckman","name":"Heckman, Caroline","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1182/blood-2020-138447","issn":["00064971","15280020"],"issn_org":["00064971"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Blood","paperid":"20","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Blood","volume":"136"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-83a430b2-9b36-4a4e-aecf-0e0300b23c12"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Carfilzomib, Elotuzumab and Dexamethasone for Relapsed or Refractory Myeloma Patients","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-610887","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The quality of patient-reported outcome (PRO) data can be compromised by non-response (NR) to scheduled questionnaires, particularly if reasons for NR are related to health problems, which may lead to unintended bias. The aim was to investigate whether electronic reminders and real-time monitoring improve PRO completion rate. METHODS: The population-based study \"Quality of life in Danish multiple myeloma patients\" is a longitudinal, multicentre study with consecutive inclusion of treatment-demanding newly diagnosed or relapsed patients with multiple myeloma. Education of study nurses in the avoidance of NR, electronic reminders, 7-day response windows and real-time monitoring of NR were integrated in the study. Patients complete PRO assessments at study entry and at 12 follow-up time points using electronic or paper questionnaires. The effect of the electronic reminders and real-time monitoring were investigated by comparison of proportions of completed questionnaires before and after each intervention. RESULTS: The first 271 included patients were analysed; of those, 249 (85%) chose electronic questionnaires. Eighty-four percent of the 1441 scheduled PRO assessments were completed within the 7-day response window and 11% after real-time monitoring, achieving a final PRO completion rate of 95%. A significant higher proportion of uncompleted questionnaires were completed after the patients had received the electronic reminder and after real-time monitoring. CONCLUSIONS: Electronic reminders and real-time monitoring contributed to a very high completion rate in the study. To increase the quality of PRO data, we propose integrating these strategies in PRO studies, however highlighting that an increase in staff resources is required for implementation.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard","King, Madeleine","Möller, Sören","Jarden, Mary","Andersen, Christen Lykkegaard","Frederiksen, Henrik","Gregersen, Henrik","Klostergaard, Anja","Steffensen, Morten Saaby","Pedersen, Per Trøllund","Hinge, Maja","Frederiksen, Mikael","Jensen, Bo Amdi","Helleberg, Carsten","Mylin, Anne Kærsgaard","Abildgaard, Niels"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-007375"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The University of Sydney","University of Sydney"],"keyword":["Adult","Bias","Female","Health related quality of life","Humans","Longitudinal Studies","Male","Middle Aged","Missing data","Multiple myeloma","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Patient reported outcomes","Patient reported outcomes completion rate","Quality of Life","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"strategies to improve patient reported outcome completion rates in longitudinal studies","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11136-019-02304-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-100.00-007375","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6994453","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85074042991","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31549365","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-98141fa9-9525-4f96-9ef7-d27488fc5d70","au-ce32a80e-ee68-489d-b906-9707773e16cf","ku-04afcec9-3876-4f6e-9443-c26388a0bc14","sdu-d4bf8a5c-f854-4a8c-869c-4be1d39aee67"],"keyword":["Adult","Bias","Female","Health-related quality of life"