versity","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Strategies to improve patient-reported outcome completion rates in longitudinal studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-007375","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To estimate national frequency of posttraumatic epilepsy (PTE) after severe traumatic brain injury (TBI) and assess injury severity (Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) and posttraumatic amnesia (PTA)) as prognostic factors for PTE. Methods: Data on patients ≥18 years surviving severe TBI 2004–2016 were retrieved from the Danish Head Trauma Database (n = 1010). The cumulative incidence proportion (CIP) was estimated using death as competing event. The association between injury severity and PTE was assessed using multivariable competing risk regressions. Results: CIP of PTE 28 days and one year post-TBI was 6.8% (95% confidence interval (CI) 5.4–8.5) and 18.5% (95% CI 16.1–21.1%), respectively. Injury severity was not associated with PTE within 28 days post-TBI but indicated higher PTE-rates in less severely injured patients. PTA-duration >70 days was associated with PTE 29–365 days post-TBI (Adjusted sub-hazard ratio 4.23 (95% CI 1.79–9.99)). GCS was not associated with PTE 29–365 days post-TBI. Conclusion: The PTE frequency was higher compared to previous estimates. Increasing injury severity was associated with PTE 29–365 days post-TBI when measured with PTA, but not with GCS. Though nonsignificant, the increased PTE-risk within 28 days in lower severity suggests an underdiagnosing of PTE.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Siig Hausted, Hanna","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Odgaard, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-161325"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Siig Hausted, Hanna"],"keyword":["Anticonvulsants","Epilepsy","Seizures","Traumatic brain injury","posttraumatic epilepsy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epilepsy after severe traumatic brain injury frequency and injury severity","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85086847665","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-161325","identifier":[{"id":"32506958","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85086847665","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-380c02f4-7733-4bed-aec9-b4aeb50e2749"],"keyword":["Epilepsy","anticonvulsants","posttraumatic epilepsy","seizures","traumatic brain injury"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6D7E4B50DCF8B24E60B130ED3A124A56"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Regionshospital Hammel Neurocenter"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanna","key":"siighaustedpau","last":"Siig Hausted","locid":"0e2f245e-506c-4e70-bc66-de5fd133b780","name":"Siig Hausted, Hanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen F.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","name_org":"Nielsen, Jørgen F.","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"1b80fe7b-ba0a-45b3-aca1-48bc19a97a44","name":"Odgaard, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-9830-3282","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32506958"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/02699052.2020.1763467","issn":["02699052","1362301X"],"issn_org":["02699052"],"issue":"7","journal":"Brain Injury","pages":"889-894","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Brain Injury","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086847665"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-380c02f4-7733-4bed-aec9-b4aeb50e2749"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Epilepsy after severe traumatic brain injury : frequency and injury severity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-161325","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The purpose of the present study was to investigate the effects of a 3-month multimodal intervention including patient education, a simple hip exercise program, footwear adjustment, and foot orthoses to reduce symptoms in patients with patellafemoral pain (PFP). Methods: Patients were diagnosed based on a physical examination, patient symptoms and ruled out intra-articular knee pathologies by MRI. Patients were educated on PFP and participated in a 3-month exercise program; shoes with solid heel-caps were recommended, and custom made orthoses with arch support were recommended to patients with foot pronation. The Anterior Knee Pain Scale (AKPS) and the pain numeric rating scale (NRS) were used to evaluate the outcomes of the intervention and collected at baseline, 3 and 12-months follow-ups. Results: Sixty-five patients (age 18 years (9–32)) were included in a consecutive prospective cohort. The AKPS score improved from 71 ± 24 to 89 ± 9 (p < 0.01) at 12 months follow up. The NRS-rest and NRS-activity improved from 3 to 0 (p < 0.01) and 7 to 3 (p < 0.01) respectively. 78% of the patients clinically improved (i.e., demonstrated a > 10-point improvement (minimal clinically important difference (MCID))) considering the AKPS; and 76% and 73% clinically improved (i.e., demonstrated (MCID) a ≥ 2-point improvement) in their NRS-rest and NRS-activity, respectively. No patients experienced a decrease in their AKPS score or an increase in their NRS-rest and NRS-activity scores at 12-months. Conclusion: A 3-month PFP multimodal treatment strategy focusing on patient education, footwear adjustment, orthoses, and simple hip muscle exercises significantly improved functional outcomes and reduced pain at a 12 month follow-up.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Torsten Grønbech","Miller, Lene Lindberg","Mygind-Klavsen, Bjarne","Lind, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-179523"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Knee pain","Patellofemoral pain","Patient education"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a simple rehabilitation regime improves functional outcome in patients with patellafemoral pain after 000000000012 month","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85079062540","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-179523","identifier":[{"id":"85079062540","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000704729200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7007455","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32034562","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-580b19dd-aca5-4864-9f04-b48354d68dc1"],"keyword":["Hip exercises","Knee pain","Patellofemoral pain","Patient education"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-84B1AF482673D0C1376A4A51CE0243E3"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Orthopaedic surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten Grønbech","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"33da3303-c376-4195-b3d6-7767956a26fe","name":"Nielsen, Torsten Grønbech","orcid":"0000-0001-5354-1781","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Lindberg","key":"millerpau","last":"Miller","locid":"7e1b0171-af03-47af-bf29-00daeab6a85c","name":"Miller, Lene Lindberg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarne","key":"mygindklavsenpau","last":"Mygind-Klavsen","locid":"ba3c3b44-35ee-4ec0-a8a3-93178867532f","name":"Mygind-Klavsen, Bjarne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"lindpau","last":"Lind","locid":"5a1298e3-a4d7-4818-88f4-da6cdbf1784d","name":"Lind, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32034562"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40634-020-00223-z","issn":["21971153"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Experimental Orthopaedics","paperid":"5","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Experimental Orthopaedics","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079062540"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-580b19dd-aca5-4864-9f04-b48354d68dc1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A simple rehabilitation regime improves functional outcome in patients with patellafemoral pain after 12 month","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-179523","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Forward Osmosis (FO) is a promising technology that can offer sustainable solutions in the biorefinery wastewater and desalination fields, via low energy water recovery. However, microbial biomass and organic matter accumulation on membrane surfaces can hinder the water recovery and potentially lead to total membrane blockage. Biofouling development is a rather complex process and can be affected by several factors such as nutrient availability, chemical composition of the solutions, and hydrodynamic conditions. Therefore, operational parameters like cross-flow velocity and pH of the filtration solution have been proposed as effective biofouling mitigation strategies. Nevertheless, most of the studies have been conducted with the use of rather simple solutions. As a result, biofouling mitigation practices based on such studies might not be as effective when applying complex industrial mixtures. In the present study, the effect of cross-flow velocity, pH, and cell concentration of the feed solution was investigated, with the use of complex solutions during FO separation. Specifically, fermentation effluent and crude glycerol were used as a feed and draw solution, respectively, with the purpose of recirculating water by using FO alone. The effect of the abovementioned parameters on (i) ATP accumulation, (ii) organic foulant deposition, (iii) total water recovery, (iv) reverse glycerol flux, and (v) process butanol rejection has been studied. The main findings of the present study suggest that significant reduction of biofouling can be achieved as a combined effect of high-cross flow velocity and low feed solution pH. Furthermore, cell removal from the feed solution prior filtration may further assist the reduction of membrane blockage. These results may shed light on the challenging, but promising field of FO process dealing with complex industrial solutions.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kalafatakis, Stavros","Zarebska, Agata","Lange, Lene","Hélix-Nielsen, Claus","Skiadas, Ioannis V.","Gavala, Hariklia N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-313785"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Gavala, Hariklia N."],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Crude glycerol","Forward osmosis","Fouling mitigation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biofouling mitigation approaches during water recovery from fermented broth via forward osmosis","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/membranes10110307","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-313785","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7693741","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85094648289","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33121090","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-1edfe7b1-6ce7-4bdc-8e55-ef3f99892093"],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Crude glycerol","Forward osmosis","Fouling mitigation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-136A9F5B5C76D7A8BCC718DA2A987D08"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/membranes10110307","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/223178742/membranes_10_00307_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stavros","key":"kalafatakispau","last":"Kalafatakis","locid":"d0bee752-71f6-462b-b243-3a41d2607cf3","name":"Kalafatakis, Stavros","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Agata","key":"zarebskapau","last":"Zarebska","locid":"e5f99d6e-5a9a-4be6-b701-fb593c86305c","name":"Zarebska, Agata","orcid":"0000-0003-4323-3050","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"langepau","last":"Lange","locid":"17702b2f-b3d2-424f-a934-af4d2c8d7ed7","name":"Lange, Lene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"hélixnielsenpau","last":"Hélix-Nielsen","locid":"bea497c9-caba-420a-81f8-8f2730634b31","name":"Hélix-Nielsen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-9392-7133","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ioannis V.","key":"skiadaspau","last":"Skiadas","locid":"d4f1e1e5-c6e4-41b1-8e13-0be7add5248b","name":"Skiadas, Ioannis V.","orcid":"0000-0001-6183-4592","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hariklia N.","key":"gavalapau","last":"Gavala","locid":"8c0c1393-f8b4-4dd9-acbc-52787d20a7fc","name":"Gavala, Hariklia N.","orcid":"0000-0002-3924-5334","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33121090"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/membranes10110307","issn":["20770375"],"issue":"11","journal":"Membranes","paperid":"307","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Membranes","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85094648289"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1edfe7b1-6ce7-4bdc-8e55-ef3f99892093"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Biofouling Mitigation Approaches during Water Recovery from Fermented Broth via Forward Osmosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-313785","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this workshop is to engage in co-design of personas to explore the interplay of autonomous technologies with user experience and engagement. Automating a process that is embedded into people’s everyday lives and activities will surely impact their experience. In a time where there is strong push towards more and more automation in our daily life, the workshop will explore the value of co-design in bringing to the fore the opportunities and issues of such trend on users’ experiences and engagements in multiple contexts such as work, health, entertainment and learning. Through the co-design of personas in future scenarios of automation the workshop will concretely identify valuable automation design goals for user experience and engagement drawing on participants’ knowledge from industry projects and academic research.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Abdelnour-Nocera, Jose","Cabrero, Daniel G","Campos, Pedro","Gonçalves, Frederica","Clemmensen, Torkil","Gissing, Robin","Nielsen, Lene","Saadati, Parisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384472"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ITI/LARSyS, ARDITI","Independent Innovation Consultant Robin Gissing","Personas Technology Ltd","University of West London"],"keyword":["Co design","Personas","User experience","automation trends","autonomous technologies"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co designing personas for user experience and engagement in automation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all",