"1d601b96-c71c-4a76-ac06-4d95e0a50a74","name":"El-Galaly, Tarec Christoffer","name_org":"El-Galaly, Tarec C","orcid":"0000-0002-4406-380X","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32301251"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/cam4.2981","issn":["20457634"],"issue":"12","journal":"Cancer Medicine","pages":"4395-4404","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Cancer Medicine","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083509558"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1e19321a-16ab-48e6-815f-306c0faa3080","au-47b19775-0b64-4089-aba1-147543b46293","sdu-c25b805c-11c3-4b27-9c11-46ed8a087087"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Depression and anxiety in Hodgkin lymphoma patients : A Danish nationwide cohort study of 945 patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-001512","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The long-term clinical course of patients with an enterovirus central nervous system infection (ECI) is poorly understood. METHODS: We performed a nationwide population-based cohort study of all Danish patients with ECI diagnosed 1997-2016 (n = 1745) and a comparison cohort from the general population individually matched on date of birth and sex (n = 17 450). Outcomes were categorized into mortality and risk of cancer and likely measures of neurological sequelae: neuropsychiatric morbidities, educational landmarks, use of hospital services, employment, receipt of disability pension, income, number of sick leave days, and nursing home residency. RESULTS: Mortality in the first year was higher among patients with ECI (mortality rate ratio [MRR] = 10.0; 95% confidence interval [CI], 4.17-24.1), but thereafter mortality was not higher (MMR = 0.94; 95% CI, 0.47-1.86). Long-term outcomes for patients with ECI were not inferior to those of the comparison cohort for risk of cancer, epilepsy, mental and behavioral disorders, dementia, depression, school start, school marks, high school education, use of hospital services, employment, receipt of disability pension, income, days of sick leave, or nursing home residency. CONCLUSIONS: Diagnosis of an ECI had no substantial impact on long-term survival, health, or social/educational functioning.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Omland, Lars H","Holm-Hansen, Charlotte","Lebech, Anne-Mette","Dessau, Ram B","Bodilsen, Jacob","Andersen, Nanna S","Roed, Casper","Christiansen, Claus B","Ellermann-Eriksen, Svend","Midgley, Sofie","Nielsen, Lene","Benfield, Thomas","Hansen, Ann-Brit E","Andersen, Christian Ø","Rothman, Kenneth J","Sørensen, Henrik T","Fischer, Thea K","Obel, Niels"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-012156"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston University"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Child","Child Preschool","Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Disabled Persons psychology","Educational Status","Employment statistics numerical data","Enterovirus Infections epidemiology","Enterovirus isolation purification","Female","Humans","Infant","Infant Newborn","Male","Meningitis","Middle Aged","Sentinel Surveillance","Survivors psychology","Viral meningitis","Young Adult","enterovirus meningitis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Department of Medicine, Boston Medical Center, Boston University School of Medicine, Boston University, Boston, Massachusetts, United States."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term survival health social functioning and education in patients with an enterovirus central nervous system infection denmark 000000001997 000000002016","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85088531687","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S04-100.00-012156","identifier":[{"id":"85088531687","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32236420","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-ffa60cdc-69d6-4d56-bfec-9c4e242a5e40","au-74ae747e-4e53-4184-a8c6-112e1ca3c47e","ku-cd901a7d-501f-4b50-a646-2cfa6bdef17f","sdu-9dfdb6d4-f3ac-469f-87c6-ab1f1dc4dd82"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Central Nervous System Infections/epidemiology","Child","Child, Preschool","Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Disabled Persons/psychology",