{"abstract":"We present a blue mussel exposure system where the fate of microplastics (polystyrene beads) is tracked during exposure and depuration phases. This enabled the establishment of a complete mass balance. Quantification of beads in mussels was done with a novel enzymatic digestion protocol. We found a similar relative distribution of beads for two environmentally realistic concentrations (5 and 100 beads L-1 ) and no substantial egestion of particles within 2h depuration.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rist, Sinja","Steensgaard, Ida M.","Guven, Olgac","Nielsen, Torkel Gissel","Jensen, Lene Hartmann","Møller, Lene Friis","Hartmann, Nanna B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-309892"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rist, Sinja"],"keyword":["Aquatic invertebrates","Emerging pollutants","Enzymatic digestion","Fate and transport","Microplastics","Quantification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the fate of microplastics during uptake and depuration phases in a blue mussel exposure system","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/154952360/Rist_et_al_2018_Environmental_Toxicology_and_Chemistry_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Acknowledgment—We thank S. Kruse for support in the laboratory work at DTU Environment. Furthermore, we acknowledge the Technical University of Denmark for funding through the DTU-EPFL collaborative PhD grant of S. Rist. O. Guven was supported by the Scientific and Technical Research Council of Turkey (TUBITAK) under the BIDEB 2219-International Postdoctoral Research Scholarship Program."],"id":"S01-000.00-309892","identifier":[{"id":"85057603169","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30273991","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-1194a23a-3fea-4737-ab52-a179b57cbb93"],"keyword":["aquatic invertebrates","emerging pollutants","enzymatic digestion","fate and transport","microplastics","quantification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0E1007F697C7DBFB4550F4DE8433F729"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/154952360/Rist_et_al_2018_Environmental_Toxicology_and_Chemistry_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Environmental Fate & Effect of Chemicals"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sinja","key":"ristpau","last":"Rist","locid":"d93a16a8-6e2b-40ca-b3cc-0f99ee1f0d6b","name":"Rist, Sinja","orcid":"0000-0003-3002-0793","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida M.","key":"steensgaardpau","last":"Steensgaard","name":"Steensgaard, Ida M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olgac","key":"guvenpau","last":"Guven","locid":"8c95cef7-4a27-4b38-b5bd-f7fe32a6bb2b","name":"Guven, Olgac","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torkel Gissel","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"01c1c5b7-65c0-4be3-8389-524d51184bc5","name":"Nielsen, Torkel Gissel","orcid":"0000-0003-1057-158X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Hartmann","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"fd3b95a0-1d8b-4e67-8594-41b83751adb4","name":"Jensen, Lene Hartmann","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Friis","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"ab01928b-01dc-425d-82ca-8094ce170708","name":"Møller, Lene Friis","orcid":"0000-0003-4207-4991","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna B.","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"8dccdf12-c16c-4cd8-a41f-a58c6a0b6dfc","name":"Hartmann, Nanna B.","orcid":"0000-0002-0442-245X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30273991"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/etc.4285","issn":["07307268","15528618"],"issn_org":["07307268"],"issue":"1","journal":"Environmental Toxicology and Chemistry","pages":"99-105","publisher":"24150509","status":"p","title":"Environmental Toxicology and Chemistry","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057603169"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1194a23a-3fea-4737-ab52-a179b57cbb93"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The fate of microplastics during uptake and depuration phases in a blue mussel exposure system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309892","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Ultrasound (US) examination of the entheses is increasingly used. However, little is known about US findings in the entheses in asymptomatic persons. The aim of this study was to investigate the appearance of US signs in the enthuses of the lower limb in asymptomatic subjects. METHODS: We recruited 64 subjects, eight women and eight men whose ages covered four decades, from 20 to 60 years. None had tendon or joint disease in the lower limbs. Participants were examined by a rheumatologist and blood samples were collected to rule out enthesis pathology. The enthesis of the dominant leg were examined with grey-scale and Doppler US to evaluate increased thickness, changed structure, enthesophytes/calcifications, erosions, and colour Doppler signal. RESULTS: Ultrasound examination of 320 entheses was made. At enthesis level, elementary lesions were seen at 73 (22.8%) sites, at subject-level 47 (73.4%) persons showed elementary lesions, in 27 (57%) only one enthesis was affected. Doppler activity was seen in four sites, three at the quadriceps insertion. Most common US elementary lesion was enthesophytes at the Achilles and quadriceps tendon insertion. A tendency towards more elementary lesions was seen in men, and a slight increase was seen with increasing age, however, not statistically significance. CONCLUSIONS: Our findings suggest that US can be used to diagnose/examine subjects in adulthood for pathological changes in the entheses; however, caution should be taken regarding enthesophytes of the quadriceps and Achilles tendon.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Guldberg-Møller, Jørgen","Terslev, Lene","Nielsen, Sabrina M","Kønig, Merete Juhl","Torp-Pedersen, Søren T","Torp-Pedersen, Arendse","Christensen, Robin","Bliddal, Henning","Ellegaard, Karen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-427955"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Achilles tendon","Adult","Cartilage Articular diagnostic imaging","Cross Sectional Studies","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Tendons diagnostic imaging","Ultrasonography Doppler","Ultrasonography methods","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ultrasound pathology of the entheses in an age and gender stratified sample of healthy adult subjects a prospective cross sectional frequency study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.clinexprheumatol.org/abstract.asp?a=12621","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-427955","identifier":[{"id":"85066444037","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30620269","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-39f959a0-5e1c-4e45-b355-c898c28493eb"],"keyword":["Achilles Tendon","Adult","Cartilage, Articular/diagnostic imaging","Cross-Sectional Studies","Female","Fibrocartilage/diagnostic imaging","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Tendons/diagnostic imaging","Ultrasonography, Doppler","Ultrasonography/methods","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B680C285C94DD047FC86C6B9CC366CE"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jørgen","key":"guldbergmøllerjørgenpau","last":"Guldberg-Møller","name":"Guldberg-Møller, Jørgen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"terslevlenepau","last":"Terslev","locid":"d10590c5-f19a-4682-ab40-30cb3dc6ffca","name":"Terslev, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sabrina M","key":"nielsensabrinampau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Sabrina M","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Merete Juhl","key":"kønigmeretejuhlpau","last":"Kønig","name":"Kønig, Merete Juhl","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren T","key":"torppedersensørentpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Søren T","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Arendse","key":"torppedersenarendsepau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Arendse","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Robin","key":"christensenrobinpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Robin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henning","key":"bliddalhenningpau","last":"Bliddal","locid":"b9301e7d-d932-44d7-8fdc-b467e8ff1aa8","name":"Bliddal, Henning","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karen","key":"ellegaardkarenpau","last":"Ellegaard","name":"Ellegaard, Karen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30620269"],"pub":{"issn":["0392856X","1593098X"],"issn_org":["0392856X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Clinical and Experimental Rheumatology","pages":"408-413","status":"p","title":"Clinical and Experimental Rheumatology","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066444037"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-39f959a0-5e1c-4e45-b355-c898c28493eb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ultrasound pathology of the entheses in an age and gender stratified sample of healthy adult subjects : a prospective cross-sectional frequency study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-427955","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: Atherosclerosis in obesity and type 2 diabetes (T2DM) is associated with low-grade inflammation (LGI) and dyslipidemia, where especially small, dense lipoprotein particles are atherogenic. The glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist, liraglutide, reduces cardiovascular events by poorly understood mechanisms. We investigated the effect of liraglutide combined with metformin on LGI and lipoprotein density profiles in patients with stable coronary artery disease (CAD) and newly diagnosed T2DM. METHODS: We conducted a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, cross-over trial over a 12 + 12-week period, with ≥2-week wash-out. INTERVENTION: liraglutide/metformin vs. placebo/metformin. Lipoproteins were separated by continuous density gradient ultracentrifugation, and LDL divided into five subfractions between 226 and 270 Å, considering particle size ≤255 Å as the atherogenic pattern. Plasma C-reactive protein and tumor necrosis factor-α were assessed by the enzyme-linked immunosorbent-assay. RESULTS: 28 out of 41 randomized patients completed all visits. Intention-to-treat analysis was performed but one patient had statin dosage and was excluded from the analysis. 95% of the patients were on statin therapy. Overall, liraglutide did not affect lipid subfractions or markers of LGI compared to placebo. The combination of liraglutide and metformin reduced the total LDL subfractions, primarily by reducing the most atherogenic subfraction LDL5, and reduced CRP but not TNF-α. Explorative analyses suggested that the subfraction LDL5 during the wash-out period rebounded significantly at least in a per-protocol analysis of the sub-group of patients starting the liraglutide therapy. CONCLUSIONS: In patients with CAD and newly diagnosed T2DM on stable statin therapy, liraglutide combined with metformin may improve the atherogenic LDL lipid profile and CRP.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Anholm, Christian","Kumarathurai, Preman","Pedersen, Lene Rørholm","Samkani, Amirsalar","Walzem, Rosemary L","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Kristiansen, Ole Peter","Fenger, Mogens","Madsbad, Sten","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Haugaard, Steen Bendix"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-504285"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Texas A&M University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liraglutide in combination with metformin may improve the atherogenic lipid profile and decrease c reactive protein level in statin treated obese patients with coronary artery disease and newly diagnosed type 000000000002 diabetes a randomized trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-504285","identifier":[{"id":"31326727","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85069506954","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b9b2fd48-9450-406a-98e7-add0d65df108"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24C4EE7E9C4051160BD16F3D856227AB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"texas a m university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Texas A&M University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"anholmpau","last":"Anholm","name":"Anholm, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Preman","key":"kumarathuraipau","last":"Kumarathurai","name":"Kumarathurai, Preman","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rørholm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Lene Rørholm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Amirsalar","key":"samkanipau","last":"Samkani","locid":"92d770d5-3de6-46ce-bd0d-2be7b47ef9b0","name":"Samkani, Amirsalar","orcid":"0000-0002-2742-3893","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rosemary L","key":"walzempau","last":"Walzem","name":"Walzem, Rosemary L","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Olav Wendelboe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d9fc9e11-583d-43d9-994c-df128b7bf5cc","name":"Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","orcid":"0000-0003-3532-9431","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ole Peter","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Ole Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mogens","key":"fengerpau","last":"Fenger","name":"Fenger, Mogens","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ahmad","key":"sajadiehpau","last":"Sajadieh","locid":"2f54d4de-84ea-41ba-9d41-d30368bc7b59","name":"Sajadieh, Ahmad","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Steen Bendix","key":"haugaardpau","last":"Haugaard","locid":"6fef997b-dc58-4cc9-ab00-4a3e92968454","name":"Haugaard, Steen Bendix","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31326727"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.atherosclerosis.2019.07.007","issn":["00219150","15675688"],"issn_org":["00219150"],"journal":"Atherosclerosis","pages":"60-66","status":"p","title":"Atherosclerosis","volume":"288"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069506954"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b9b2fd48-9450-406a-98e7-add0d65df108"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Liraglutide in combination with metformin may improve the atherogenic lipid profile and decrease C-reactive protein level in statin treated obese patients with coronary artery disease and newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes : A randomized trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-504285","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Congenital cytomegalovirus (CMV) infection is a major cause of birth defects ranging from developmental disorders to stillbirth. Most newborns affected by CMV do not present with symptoms at birth but are at risk of sequelae at later stages of their childhood. Stored dried blood spots (DBS) taken at birth can be used for retrospective diagnosis of hereditary diseases, but detection of pathogens is challenged by potentially low pathogen concentrations in the small blood volume available in a DBS. Here we test four different extraction methods for optimal recovery of CMV DNA from DBS at low to high CMV titers. The recovery efficiencies varied widely between the different extractions (from 3% to 100%) with the most efficient method extracting up to 113-fold more CMV DNA than the least efficient and 8-fold more than the reference protocol. Furthermore, we amplified four immunomodulatory CMV genes from the extracted DNA: the UL40 and UL111A genes which occur as functional knockouts in some circulating CMV strains, and the highly variable UL146 and US28 genes. The PCRs specifically amplified the CMV genes at all tested titers with sufficient quality for sequencing and genotyping. In summary, we here report an extraction method for optimal recovery of CMV DNA from DBSs that can be used for both detection of CMV and for genotyping of polymorphic CMV genes in congenital CMV infection.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Berg, Christian","Friis, Martin B","Rosenkilde, Mette M.","Benfield, Thomas","Nielsen, Lene","von Lüttichau, Hans Rudolf","Sundelin, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-506847"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of highly efficient protocols for extraction and amplification of cytomegalovirus dna from dried blood spots for detection and genotyping of polymorphic immunomodulatory genes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0222053","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-506847","identifier":[{"id":"31513621","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85072145468","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6742235","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-bdff651e-ed9b-4eb4-9e55-37adae30cb7c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-62D5163F2774643168491A009D42022C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0222053","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/238482557/OA_Development_of_highly_efficient_protocols_for.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","locid":"86f72e63-bf6f-4dd2-ae8b-7b29f88ffa96","name":"Berg, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-0539-7081","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin B","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, Martin B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette M","key":"rosenkildepau","last":"Rosenkilde","locid":"d902feb8-1594-4fa8-bcb1-9f646dc30dd3","name":"Rosenkilde, Mette M.","name_org":"Rosenkilde, Mette M","orcid":"0000-0001-9600-3254","ran