blication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Line","key":"bechnielsenpedh","last":"Bech Nielsen","name":"Bech Nielsen, Line","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788799911912"],"pages":"8-14","place":"København","publisher":"Kunstskolen for voksne udviklingshæmmede","status":"p","title":"Kunstskolens 25 års jubilæum 1994-2019"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-744bc4eb-51a8-4312-a142-bef51ff3d0ad"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Billedkunst og handicap","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-195711","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Approximately one-third of patients undergoing spine surgery have symptoms of anxiety and depression that correlate with pain, disability, and lower health-related quality of life. The use of web-based informative strategies before surgery and principles from cognitive behavioral therapy, have been applied in other patient groups, facilitating mobility and encouraging beneficial coping behavior. PURPOSE: To examine the effect of a web-based Spine Platform featuring Interaction and Information by Animation (w-SPIINA) on symptoms of anxiety and depression, pain, disability, and health-related quality of life. STUDY DESIGN: A single-center, two-arm, randomized controlled trial PATIENT SAMPLE: One hundred fourteen consecutive patients scheduled for instrumented lumbar spine fusion due to degenerative disc disease or spondylolisthesis. OUTCOME MEASURES: Primary outcome was the change in self-reported Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS) scores from baseline to 3-month follow-up. Secondary outcomes were change in HADS 1-day before surgery 2 days and 6 months after and changes in self-reported disability measured on the Oswestry disability index (ODI), quality of life (EQ-5D-5L questionnaire), and the low back pain rating scale (LBPRS) 2 days and 3 and 6 months after surgery. METHOD: Patients were randomized to either a control group receiving a standard information regimen or an intervention group gaining access to w-SPIINA in addition to the standard regimen. The independent charity Helsefonden contributed $45,000, the Health Research Fund of the Regional Hospital Central Jutland contributed $10,000, and the Toyota foundation contributed $10,000 to remunerate a dedicated investigator. The authors have no conflict of interest to declare. RESULTS: There was no statistically significant difference within the w-SPIINA group and the control group regarding changes in HADS at 3-month follow-up (p≥.37). Approximately 40% reached minimum clinically important difference (MCID) in the w-SPIINA group on the HADS at 3 months. In the control group 50% reached MCID on anxiety subscale and 35% on the depression subscale at 3 months. No statistically significant differences were found between groups with regard to the overall outcomes at any of the predefined time points. CONCLUSION: Providing patients with access to w-SPIINA in addition to a standard information regimen had no additional effect on HADS and patient-reported outcomes1 day before, 2 days, 3 or 6 months after surgery. However, a high compliance and degree of interaction with w-SPIINA indicates that this mode of web-based support could be applicable in this group of patients.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Strøm, Janni","Nielsen, Claus Vinther","Bastrup, Lene","Andersen, Niels Trolle","Laursen, Malene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228258"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animation","Anxiety","Cognitive behavioral therapy","Depression","HOSPITAL ANXIETY","Improvement","Information","Low back pain","Lumbar spine fusion","Online","Oswestry disability index","Randomized trial","Rehabilitation","SCALE","Support groups","Surgery","Web based platform"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a web based platform to accommodate symptoms of anxiety and depression by featuring social interaction and animated information in patients undergoing lumbar spine fusion a randomized clinical trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spinee.2018.11.011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228258","identifier":[{"id":"85058002069","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000466162500007","type":"wos"},{"id":"30500464","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ad8504dd-c690-4c44-9397-ee3fa02185c7"],"keyword":["COGNITIVE-BEHAVIORAL THERAPY","HOSPITAL ANXIETY","IMPROVEMENT","LOW-BACK-PAIN","ONLINE","OSWESTRY DISABILITY INDEX","REHABILITATION","SCALE","SUPPORT GROUPS","SURGERY","animation","anxiety","depression","information","lumbar spine fusion","randomized trial","web-based platform"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6E596A9207290CD4B661D4DCD8804FE9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spinee.2018.11.011","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/197687437/1_s2.0_S1529943018312506_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - University Clinic for Interdisciplinary Orthopaedic Pathways (UCOP)","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Klinisk Socialmedicin og Rehabilitering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Janni","key":"strømpau","last":"Strøm","locid":"1547e0db-85ca-42d3-9bc5-758ecf0d7c56","name":"Strøm, Janni","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus Vinther","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"033d1aa9-948f-4ed4-be3e-200d0100b399","name":"Nielsen, Claus Vinther","orcid":"0000-0002-2467-1103","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Bastrup","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"532c69b5-512e-421d-8981-88829f8a74ab","name":"Bastrup, Lene","name_org":"Jørgensen, Lene Bastrup","orcid":"0000-0001-7873-6139","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Trolle","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"233c3f15-ef6b-4fec-b594-5504c1dfa2c0","name":"Andersen, Niels Trolle","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"abfa584f-e66b-4fba-9c23-4e8a0a1058cf","name":"Laursen, Malene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30500464"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.spinee.2018.11.011","issn":["15299430","18781632"],"issn_org":["15299430"],"issue":"5","journal":"Spine Journal","pages":"827-839","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Spine Journal","title_org":"The spine journal : official journal of the North American Spine Society","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058002069"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ad8504dd-c690-4c44-9397-ee3fa02185c7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A web-based platform to accommodate symptoms of anxiety and depression by featuring social interaction and animated information in patients undergoing lumbar spine fusion : a randomized clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-228258","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"People relate to other people, not to simplified types or segments. This is the concept that underpins this book. Personas, a user centered design methodology, covers topics from interaction design within IT, through to issues surrounding product design, communication, and marketing. Project developers need to understand how users approach their products from the product’s infancy, and regardless of what the product might be. Developers should be able to describe the user of the product via vivid depictions, as if they – with their different attitudes, desires and habits – were already using the product. In doing so they can more clearly formulate how to turn the product's potential into reality. Based on 20 years’ experience in solving problems for businesses and 15 years of research, currently at the IT University of Copenhagen, Lene Nielsen is Denmark’s leading expert in the persona method. She has a PhD in personas and scenarios, and through her research and practical experiences has developed her own approach to the method – 10 Steps to Personas. This second edition of Personas – User Focused Design presents a step-by-step methodology of personas which will be of interest to developers of IT, communications solutions and innovative products. This book also includes three new chapters and considerable expansion on the material in the first edition.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383756"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"personas user focused design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383756","ids":["itu-ab5435c0-badd-4355-a17f-6b769d83daa8"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-FD7A556E85A9E3838F0B84D1645D454B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-1-4471-7427-1","edition":"2.","eisbn":["9781447174271"],"isbn":["9781447174264"],"pages":"179","place":"London","publisher":"Springer","series":"Human-Computer Interaction Series","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ab5435c0-badd-4355-a17f-6b769d83daa8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Personas : User Focused Design","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383756","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BackgroundHyperinsulinemia aggravates insulin resistance and cardio-vascular disease. How the insulinotropic glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist liraglutide in a physiologic post-prandial setting may act on pancreatic alpha and beta-cell function in patients with coronary artery disease (CAD) and type 2 diabetes (T2DM) is less clear.MethodsInsulin resistant patients with established CAD and newly diagnosed well-controlled T2DM were recruited to a placebo-controlled, cross-over trial with two treatment periods of 12weeks and a 2weeks wash-out period before and in-between. Treatment was liraglutide or placebo titrated from 0.6mg q.d. to 1.8mg q.d. within 4weeks and metformin titrated from 500mg b.i.d to 1000mg b.i.d. within 4weeks. Before and after intervention in both 12weeks periods insulin, C-peptide, glucose, and glucagon were measured during a meal test. Beta-cell function derived from the oral glucose tolerance setting was calculated as changes in insulin secretion per unit changes in glucose concentration (B-total) and whole-body insulin resistance using ISIcomposite.ResultsLiraglutide increased the disposition index [B(total)xISI(composite), by 40% (n=24, p<0.001)] compared to placebo. Post-prandial insulin and glucose was reduced by metformin in combination with liraglutide and differed, but not significantly different from placebo, moreover, glucagon concentration was unaffected. Additionally, insulin clearance tended to increase during liraglutide therapy (n=26, p=0.06).ConclusionsThe insulinotropic drug liraglutide may without increasing the insulin concentration reduce postprandial glucose but not glucagon excursions and improve beta-cell function in newly diagnosed and well-controlled T2DM.Trial registration Clinicaltrials.gov ID: NCT01595789","author_count":11,"contributors":["Anholm, Christian","Kumarathurai, Preman","Jurs, Anders","Pedersen, Lene Rorholm","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Kristiansen, Ole Peter","Fenger, Mogens","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Haugaard, Steen Bendix"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-395785"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Beta cell function","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Glucagon","Insulin clearance","Insulin sensitivity","Meal test"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liraglutide improves the beta cell function without increasing insulin secretion during a mixed meal in patients who exhibit well controlled type 000000000002 diabetes and coronary artery disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13098-019-0438-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-395785","identifier":[{"id":"000469875100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85066462864","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6543623","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31164926","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-03db0f39-30d5-47dd-b742-e3619d44bd2c"],"keyword":["Beta-cell function","Diabetes mellitus type 2","GLP1-receptor agonist","Glucagon","Insulin clearance","Insulin sensitivity","Meal test"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4975C805719B1C277D84ED5E8DD12C02"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13098-019-0438-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/227693129/OA_Liraglutide_improves_the_beta_cell_function_without_increasing_insulin_secretion.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"anholmpau","last":"Anholm","name":"Anholm, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Preman","key":"kumarathuraipau","last":"Kumarathurai","name":"Kumarathurai, Preman","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"jurspau","last":"Jurs","name":"Jurs, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rorholm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Lene Rorholm","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olav Wendelboe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d9fc9e11-583d-43d9-994c-df128b7bf5cc","name":"Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","orcid":"0000-0003-3532-9431","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ole Peter","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Ole Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mogens","key":"fengerpau","last":"Fenger","name":"Fenger, Mogens","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ahmad","key":"sajadiehpau","last":"Sajadieh","locid":"2f54d4de-84ea-41ba-9d41-d30368bc7b59","name":"Sajadieh, Ahmad","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen Bendix","key":"haugaardpau","last":"Haugaard","locid":"6fef997b-dc58-4cc9-ab00-4a3e92968454","name":"Haugaard, Steen Bendix","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31164926"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13098-019-0438-6","issn":["17585996"],"journal":"Diabetology & Metabolic Syndrome","paperid":"42","status":"p","title":"Diabetology & Metabolic Syndrome","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066462864"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-03db0f39-30d5-47dd-b742-e3619d44bd2c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Liraglutide improves the beta-cell function without increasing insulin secretion during a mixed meal in patients, who exhibit well-controlled type 2 diabetes and coronary artery disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-395785","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Elevated levels of non-esterified fatty acids (NEFA) play a role in insulin resistance, impaired beta-cell function and they are a denominator of the abnormal atherogenic lipid profile that characterizes obese patients with type 2 diabetes (T2DM). We hypothesized that the GLP-1 receptor agonist liraglutide, in combination with metformin, would reduce lipolysis. In a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, cross-over trial, 41 T2DM patients with coronary artery disease were randomized and treated with liraglutide-metformin vs placebo-metformin during 12- + 12-week periods with a wash-out period of at least 2 weeks before and between the intervention periods. NEFA kinetics were estimated using the Boston Minimal Model of NEFA metabolism, with plasma NEFA and glucose levels measured during a standard 180-minute frequently sampled intravenous glucose tolerance test. Liraglutide-metformin reduced estimates of lipolysis. Furthermore, placebo-metformin increased estimates of lipid oxidation, while treatment with liraglutide eliminated this effect. We conclude that liraglutide exerts a clinically relevant reduction in estimates of lipolysis and lipid oxidation which is explained, in part, by improved insulin secretion, as revealed by an intravenous glucose tolerance test.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Anholm, Christian","Kumarathurai, Preman","Samkani, Amirsalar","Pedersen, Lene R.","Boston, Raymond C.","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Kristiansen, Ole P.","Fenger, Mogens","Madsbad, Sten","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Haugaard, Steen Bendix"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-458557"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clinical trial","GLP 1 analogue","Liraglutide","Metformin","Randomised trial","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of liraglutide on estimates of lipolysis and lipid oxidation in obese patients with stable coronary artery disease and newly diagnosed type 000000000002 diabetes a randomized trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-458557","identifier":[{"id":"31050161","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85066603420","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6d0c2d79-903b-46ed-836b-672cd79829a9"],"keyword":["GLP-1 analogue","clinical trial","liraglutide","metformin","randomised trial","type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4C73ADEE8282102233F49738DAD49DC5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"anholmpau","last":"Anholm","name":"Anholm, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Preman","key":"kumarathuraipau","last":"Kumarathurai","name":"Kumarathurai, Preman","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Amirsalar","key":"samkanipau","last":"Samkani","locid":"92d770d5-3de6-46ce-bd0d-2be7b47ef9b0","name":"Samkani, Amirsalar","orcid":"0000-0002-2742-3893","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene R.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Lene R.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Raymond C.","key":"bostonpau","last":"Boston","name":"Boston, Raymond C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olav W.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d9fc9e11-583d-43d9