{"abstract":"Multiple myeloma (MM) is an incurable but treatment-sensitive cancer. For most patients, this means treatment with multiple lines of anti-myeloma therapy and a life with disease- and treatment-related symptoms and complications. Health-related quality of life (HRQoL) issues play an important role in treatment decision-making. Methodological challenges in longitudinal HRQoL measurements and analyses have been identified, including non-responses (NR) to scheduled questionnaires. Publications were identified for inclusion in a systematic review of longitudinal HRQoL studies in MM, focussing on methodological aspects of HRQoL measurement and analysis. Diversity in timing of HRQoL data collection and applied statistical methods were noted. We observed a high rate of NR, but the impact of NR was investigated in only 8/23 studies. Thus, evidence-based knowledge of HRQoL in patients with MM is compromised. To improve quality of HRQoL results and their implementation in daily practice, future studies should follow established guidelines.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Kongsgaard","Abildgaard, Niels","Jarden, Mary","Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeld"],"cuid":["S02-093.19-047134"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene"],"keyword":["Attitude to Health","Clinical Trials as Topic statistics numerical data","Datasets as Topic","Health related quality of life","Humans","Missing data","Multiple Myeloma drug therapy","Multiple myeloma","Patient Acceptance of Health Care","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Quality of Life","Review","Statistical analysis","Surveys and Questionnaires","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"methodological aspects of health related quality of life measurement and analysis in patients with multiple myeloma","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/249629613/Methodological_aspects_of_health_related_quality_of_life_measurement_and_analysis_in_patients_with_multiple_myeloma_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-093.19-047134","identifier":[{"id":"30656677","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85060210120","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ebf1929e-6f00-4099-b4db-33d70b59ce52","sdu-0a9bc421-ba97-4e53-91aa-7042db748453"],"keyword":["Attitude to Health","Clinical Trials as Topic/statistics & numerical data","Datasets as Topic","Humans","Multicenter Studies as Topic/statistics & numerical data","Multiple Myeloma/drug therapy","Patient Acceptance of Health Care","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Quality of Life","Surveys and Questionnaires","Treatment Outcome","health-related quality of life","missing data","multiple myeloma","review","statistical analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F74827DA02DDFF54C7DA8EDBA6678300"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/249629613/Methodological_aspects_of_health_related_quality_of_life_measurement_and_analysis_in_patients_with_multiple_myeloma_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170612811/bjh.15759.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Haematology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Haematology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"kongsgaardnielsenpau","last":"Kongsgaard Nielsen","locid":"621d166f-6298-48ed-9f2d-d8d52bb40446","name":"Kongsgaard Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-2083-3870","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"abildgaardpau","last":"Abildgaard","locid":"595418b9-29f8-4fd3-8663-1b32eab3451a","name":"Abildgaard, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-6852-2014","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Mary","key":"jardenpau","last":"Jarden","locid":"f716d3db-6f75-41b0-94a0-884f7dcd1259","name":"Jarden, Mary","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tobias Wirenfeld","key":"klausenpau","last":"Klausen","name":"Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeld","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30656677"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bjh.15759","issn":["00071048"],"issue":"1","journal":"British Journal of Haematology","pages":"11-24","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Haematology","volume":"185"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060210120"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ebf1929e-6f00-4099-b4db-33d70b59ce52","sdu-0a9bc421-ba97-4e53-91aa-7042db748453"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Methodological aspects of health-related quality of life measurement and analysis in patients with multiple myeloma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.19-047134","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Individual placement and support (IPS) seems to be an effective vocational intervention for people with severe mental illness, but its effects have not yet been shown in the Danish welfare model. Also, effects may be enhanced by adding cognitive remediation and work-focused social skills training (IPS with enhancements [IPSE]). Objectives: To investigate the effects of IPS vs IPSE vs service as usual (SAU) on a population of individuals with severe mental illness in Denmark. Design, Setting, and Participants: This was an investigator-initiated, 3-group, parallel, assessor-blinded randomized clinical trial that used early-intervention teams or community mental health services in 3 Danish cities to recruit participants with severe mental illness. Participants were randomly assigned to receive IPS, IPSE, or SAU from November 2012 to February 2016, and follow-up continued until August 2017. Interventions: Participants allocated to the IPS intervention received vocational support per the principles of the IPS model. Participants in the IPSE arm received cognitive remediation and social skills training in addition to IPS. The group receiving SAU received vocational rehabilitation at the Danish job centers. Main Outcomes and Measures: The primary outcome was the number of hours in competitive employment or education during the 18-month follow-up. Secondary outcomes included intergroup differences in employment or education at any point during follow-up; time to employment or education; and cognitive and social functioning, self-esteem, and self-efficacy. Results: Of the 720 included participants (mean [SD] age, 32.8 [9.9] years; 276 [38.3%] women), 243 received IPS, 238 received IPSE, and 239 received SAU. Most participants (551 [76.5%]) were diagnosed with a schizophrenia spectrum disorder. During the 18-month follow-up, the IPSE group worked or studied a mean (SD) of 488.1 (735.6) hours, compared with 340.8 (573.8) hours in the group receiving SAU (success-rate difference [SRD], 0.151 [95% CI, 0.01-0.295]; P = .016). The mean (SD) in the IPS group was 411 (656.9) (SRD, 0.127 [95% CI, -0.017 to 0.276]; P = .004). There was no difference between IPS and IPSE in any vocational outcomes, and the 3 groups showed no differences in any nonvocational outcomes, except that the IPS and IPSE groups were more satisfied with the services received than the group receiving SAU (IPS vs SAU: SRD, 0.310 [95% CI, 0.167-0.445]); IPSE vs SAU: SRD, 0.341 [95% CI, 0.187-0.478]). Conclusions and Relevance: Compared with SAU, IPS and IPSE seem to be viable routes to increase employment and education rates in people with severe mental illness in Denmark, but no additional effects were observed by enhancing IPS. Trial Registration: ClinicalTrials.gov identifier: NCT01722344.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Christensen, Thomas Nordahl","Wallstrøm, Iben Gammelgård","Stenager, Elsebeth","Bojesen, Anders Bo","Gluud, Christian","Nordentoft, Merete","Eplov, Lene Falgaard"],"cuid":["S02-099.96-047659"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Christensen, Thomas Nordahl"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of individual placement and support supplemented with cognitive remediation and work focused social skills training for people with severe mental illness a randomized clinical trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85072030852","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.96-047659","identifier":[{"id":"85072030852","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31483451","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6727676","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-fd15cf11-4f87-4966-9d0a-b42a4b215436","sdu-c319e67f-36fb-44d8-9366-e1628f020bed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-56CE98B9B96129945CB37F710DBDD680"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Psychiatry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Mental Health Services Glostrup"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Mental Health Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Thomas Nordahl","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Thomas Nordahl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben Gammelgård","key":"wallstrømpau","last":"Wallstrøm","locid":"9ae2751d-62bd-4ac8-b6a0-88bcea6bd9ce","name":"Nielsen, Iben Gammelgaard","name_org":"Wallstrøm, Iben Gammelgård","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elsebeth","key":"stenagerpau","last":"Stenager","locid":"eb4df80b-bc61-471f-9e05-0da8981b8f9c","name":"Stenager, Elsebeth","orcid":"0000-0002-4752-3648","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Anders Bo","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","name":"Bojesen, Anders Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"gluudpau","last":"Gluud","name":"Gluud, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Merete","key":"nordentoftpau","last":"Nordentoft","locid":"6d0fe19c-7c81-463b-8bc8-822d71584b69","name":"Nordentoft, Merete","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Falgaard","key":"eplovpau","last":"Eplov","name":"Eplov, Lene Falgaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31483451"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamapsychiatry.2019.2291","issn":["15383636","2168622X"],"issn_org":["2168622X"],"issue":"12","journal":"JAMA Psychiatry","pages":"1232-1240","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA Psychiatry","volume":"76"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072030852"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","mental health centre"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fd15cf11-4f87-4966-9d0a-b42a4b215436","sdu-c319e67f-36fb-44d8-9366-e1628f020bed"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effects of Individual Placement and Support Supplemented With Cognitive Remediation and Work-Focused Social Skills Training for People With Severe Mental Illness : A Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.96-047659","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The Illness Management and Recovery program (IMR) is developed to support people with severe mental illnesses in their recovery-process. The theory behind the program highlight the importance of helping people develop tailored illness management skills which will help achieve personal and clinical recovery. However, little is known about participants' experience with IMR in relation to their recoveryprocess. The aim of the present study is to describe the participants' lived experience with IMR, explore whether they experienced changes, and examine how these changes related to their recovery during or after their participation in IMR. A Qualitative study. The participants' experience with the IMR program in relation to their recovery unveiled three main themes; \"Social connection with other IMR-group members', 'In IMR, we talked about our everyday lives with mental illness' and 'In IMR we learned about recovery as a personal experience'.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jensen, Sofie B","Eplov, Lene F","Gammelgaard, Iben","Mueser, Kim T","Petersen, Kirsten Schultz"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-009285"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Sofie B."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston University"],"keyword":["Clinical and personal recovery","Hope","IMR","Illness Management and Recovery","Lived experience","Severe mental illness"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Mental Health Center Copenhagen, Copenhagen Research Center for Mental Health - CORE"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"participants lived experience with the illness management and recovery imr program in relation to their recovery process","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85062514445&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-009285","identifier":[{"id":"30810903","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85062514445","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c0c307e0-2cdb-432d-a896-581df480de78","sdu-6291741b-91a2-4599-86cd-a280cbe3bec5"],"keyword":["Clinical and personal recovery","Hope","IMR","Illness management and recovery","Lived experience","Severe mental illness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-10432BD2B7CB7DF4C4AD8F27E8BCA886"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Mental Health Center Copenhagen, Copenhagen Research Center for Mental Health - CORE"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Psykiatrisk Center København"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Psychiatry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","cou