ms of the Cl atom, OH radical and O3 reactions, and role of (E)-(Z) isomerization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-395371","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"PGC-1α has been suggested to regulate exercise training-induced metabolic adaptations and autophagy in skeletal muscle. The factors regulating PGC-1α are however not fully resolved. The aim was to investigate the impact of β-adrenergic signaling in PGC-1α mediated metabolic adaptations in skeletal muscle with exercise training. Muscle was obtained from muscle specific PGC-1α knockout (MKO) mice and LOX/LOX 1) 3h after a single exercise bout with or without prior injection of propranolol or 3h after a single injection of clenbuterol and 2) after 5 weeks of wheel running exercise training with or without propranolol treatment or after 5 weeks of clenbuterol treatment. A single clenbuterol injection and an acute exercise bout increased similarly the mRNA content of both N-Terminal and full-length PGC-1α isoforms and prior propranolol treatment reduced the exercise-induced increase of all isoforms. Furthermore, a single clenbuterol injection elicited a PGC-1α-dependent increase in Cyt c and VEGF mRNA, whereas prolonged clenbuterol treatment increased fiber size but reduced capillary density. Exercise training increased the protein content of OXPHOS, LC3I, and Parkin in a PGC-1α-dependent manner without effect of propranolol, while an exercise training-induced increase in Akt2 and p62 protein required PGC-1α and was blunted by prolonged propranolol treatment. This suggests that β-adrenergic signaling is not required for PGC-1α mediated exercise training-induced adaptations in mitochondrial proteins, but contributes to exercise training mediated adaptations in insulin signaling and autophagy regulation through PGC-1α. Furthermore, changes observed with acute stimulation of compounds like clenbuterol and propranolol may not lead to corresponding adaptations with prolonged treatment.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Brandt, Nina","Nielsen, Lene","Buch, Bjørg Thiellesen","Gudiksen, Anders","Jørgensen, Stine Ringholm","Hellsten, Ylva","Bangsbo, Jens","Pilegaard, Henriette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-402525"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Autophagy","Clenbuterol","Exercise","PGC 1α","Propranolol","Skeletal muscle","Training","β adrenergic signaling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of β adrenergic signaling in pgc 000000000001α mediated adaptations in mouse skeletal muscle","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-402525","identifier":[{"id":"85043480873","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28874356","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-0f436a70-00ca-41a3-be9b-2f936966dcf0"],"keyword":["Autophagy","Clenbuterol","Exercise","PGC-1α","PGC-1α isoforms","Propranolol","Skeletal muscle","Training","β-adrenergic signaling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3745E0BB8C1A6D6EBB3F2FDBCE663984"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Cell Biology and Physiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Human Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nina","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"77d392a2-c514-4c7f-bd91-722b456fa7ab","name":"Brandt, Nina","orcid":"0000-0001-6833-0047","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bjørg Thiellesen","key":"buchpau","last":"Buch","name":"Buch, Bjørg Thiellesen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"gudiksenpau","last":"Gudiksen","locid":"c606f51e-8e40-4c33-a459-45f96c93b102","name":"Gudiksen, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stine","key":"ringholmjørgensenpau","last":"Ringholm Jørgensen","locid":"e3e24567-4419-4742-9b22-1f3f20a6b1c1","name":"Jørgensen, Stine Ringholm","name_org":"Ringholm Jørgensen, Stine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ylva","key":"hellstenpau","last":"Hellsten","locid":"902a8d03-73c1-41fa-a0a3-7f250470e2f0","name":"Hellsten, Ylva","orcid":"0000-0002-2435-9558","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"bangsbopau","last":"Bangsbo","locid":"24839560-f889-42a6-9b73-97b69f101548","name":"Bangsbo, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1305-9274","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henriette","key":"pilegaardpau","last":"Pilegaard","locid":"bca00b25-e11a-407d-936f-6982a39ef1d8","name":"Pilegaard, Henriette","orcid":"0000-0002-1071-0327","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28874356"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/ajpendo.00082.2017","issn":["01931849","15221555"],"issn_org":["01931849"],"issue":"1","journal":"American Journal of Physiology: Endocrinology and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Physiology: Endocrinology and Metabolism","volume":"314"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85043480873"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0f436a70-00ca-41a3-be9b-2f936966dcf0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impact of β-adrenergic signaling in PGC-1α-mediated adaptations in mouse skeletal muscle","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-402525","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background Disagreement among healthcare professionals on the clinical relevance of drug-related problems can lead to suboptimal treatment and increased healthcare costs. Elderly patients with chronic non-cancer pain and comorbidity are at increased risk of drug related problems compared to other patient groups due to complex medication regimes and transition of care. Objective To investigate the agreement among healthcare professionals on their classification of clinical relevance of drug-related problems in elderly patients with chronic non-cancer pain and comorbidity. Setting Multidisciplinary Pain Centre, Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen, Denmark. Method A pharmacist performed medication review on elderly patients with chronic non-cancer pain and comorbidity, identified their drug-related problems and classified these problems in accordance with an existing categorization system. A five-member clinical panel rated the drug-related problems’ clinical relevance in accordance with a five-level rating scale, and their agreement was compared using Fleiss’ κ. Main outcome measure Healthcare professionals’ agreement on clinical relevance of drug related problems, using Fleiss’ κ. Results Thirty patients were included in the study. A total of 162 drug related problems were identified, out of which 54% were of lower clinical relevance (level 0–2) and 46% of higher clinical relevance (level 3–4). Only slight agreement (κ = 0.12) was found between the panellists’ classifications of clinical relevance using a five-level rating scale. Conclusion The clinical pharmacist identified drug related problems of lower and higher clinical relevance. Poor overall agreement on the severity of the drug related problems was found among the panelists.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bech, Christina Flagstad","Frederiksen, Tina","Villesen, Christine Tilsted","Højsted, Jette","Nielsen, Per Rotbøll","Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","Nørgaard, Lotte Stig","Christrup, Lona Louring"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-441181"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"healthcare professionals agreement on clinical relevance of drug related problems among elderly patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-441181","identifier":[{"id":"85038107073","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29248987","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4ff1eb22-9e7e-4c27-ba14-ca8c153f0c19"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86F567C82D8041F8747FEB83A288D128"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Social and Clinical Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christina Flagstad","key":"bechpau","last":"Bech","name":"Bech, Christina Flagstad","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tina","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Tina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christine Tilsted","key":"villesenpau","last":"Villesen","name":"Villesen, Christine Tilsted","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jette","key":"højstedpau","last":"Højsted","name":"Højsted, Jette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Per Rotbøll","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Per Rotbøll","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Juel","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lotte Stig","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"7dbf5d7d-7d8c-4260-b41c-0446c7cc7740","name":"Nørgaard, Lotte Stig","orcid":"0000-0002-3490-0475","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lona Louring","key":"christruppau","last":"Christrup","locid":"acf7258c-1e63-48a1-9bef-d6b6c5b8eeca","name":"Christrup, Lona Louring","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29248987"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11096-017-0572-x","issn":["22107703","22107711"],"issn_org":["22107703"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Clinical Pharmacy","pages":"119-125","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Clinical Pharmacy","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85038107073"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4ff1eb22-9e7e-4c27-ba14-ca8c153f0c19"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Healthcare professionals’ agreement on clinical relevance of drug-related problems among elderly patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-441181","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Indochina is a biodiversity hot spot and harbors a high number of endemic species, most of which are poorly studied. This study explores the genetic structure and reproductive system of the threatened endemic timber species Dalbergia cochinchinensis and Dalbergia oliveri using microsatellite data from populations across Indochina and relates it to landscape characteristics and life-history traits. We found that the major water bodies in the region, Mekong and Tonle Sap, represented barriers to gene flow and that higher levels of genetic diversity were found in populations in the center of the distribution area, particularly in Cambodia. We suggest that this pattern is ancient, reflecting the demographic history of the species and possible location of refugia during earlier time periods with limited forest cover, which was supported by signs of old genetic bottlenecks. The D. oliveri populations had generally high levels of genetic diversity (mean He = 0.73), but also strong genetic differentiation among populations (global GST = 0.13), while D. cochinchinensis had a moderate level of genetic diversity (mean He = 0.55), and an even stronger level of differentiation (global GST = 0.25). These differences in genetic structure can be accounted for by a higher level of gene flow in D. oliveri due to a higher dispersal capacity, but also by the broader distribution area for D. oliveri, and the pioneer characteristics of D. cochinchinensis. This study represents the first detailed analysis of landscape genetics for tree species in Indochina, and the found patterns might be common for other species with similar ecology.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hartvig, Ida","So, Thea","Changtragoon, Suchitra","Tran, Hoa Thi","Bouamanivong, Somsanith","Theilade, Ida","Kjær, Erik Dahl","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446001"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["Cambodia","Thailand","Vietnam"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Cambodia","Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment, Thailand","Vietnam Academy of Agricultural Sciences"],"keyword":["Forest cover change","Indochina","Landscape genetics","Mekong River","Tropical trees"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["National Herbarium of Laos Biotechnology and Ecology Institute Ministry of Science and Technology Vientiane"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"population genetic structure of the endemic rosewoods i dalbergia cochinchinensis i and i d oliveri i at a regional scale reflects the indochinese landscape and life history traits","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.3626","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-446001","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5756888","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85036577897","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29321891","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-57e8bbd8-896e-439c-be10-53823804118c"],"keyword":["Forest cover change","Indochina","Landscape genetics","Mekong River","Plant mating systems","Tropical trees"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FABE47B495A3A5AD06BD409A4ACA8354"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.3626","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/187585260/Population_genetic_structure_of_the_endemic_rosewoods_Dalbergia_cochinchinensis_and_D._oliveri_at_a_regional_scale_reflects_the_Indochinese_landscape_and_life_history_traits.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"kh","key":"ministry of agriculture forestry and fisheries cambodia","loc":["Cambodia","Asia, South"],"name":"Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Cambodia","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"th","key":"ministry of natural resources and environment thailand","loc":["Thailand","Asia, South"],"name":"Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment, Thailand","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"vn","key":"vietnam academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["Vietnam","Asia, South"],"name":"Vietnam Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["National Herbarium of Laos Biotechnology and Ecology Institute Ministry of Science and Technology Vientiane"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Global Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ida","key":"hartvigpau","last":"Hartvig","locid":"445ddaaa-d012-4915-9a41-a4428d87a592","name":"Hartvig, Ida","orcid":"0000-0002-1509-6864","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thea","key":"sopau","last":"So","name":"So, Thea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Suchitra","key":"changtragoonpau","last":"Changtragoon","name":"Changtragoon, Suchitra","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Hoa Thi","key":"tranpau","last":"Tran","name":"Tran, Hoa Thi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Somsanith","key":"bouamanivongpau","last":"Bouamanivong","name":"Bouamanivong, Somsanith","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Ida","key":"theiladepau","last":"Theilade","locid":"6fe4cbce-90c9-497d-8bdc-7073f13ee37e","name":"Theilade, Ida","orcid":"0000-0003-3502-1277","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29321891"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ece3.3626","issn":["20457758"],"issue":"1","journal":"Ecology and Evolution","pages":"530-545","status":"p","title":"Ecology and Evolution","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85036577897"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-57e8bbd8-896e-439c-be10-53823804118c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Population genetic structure of the endemic rosewoods <i>Dalbergia cochinchinensis</i> and <i>D. oliveri</i> at a regional scale reflects the Indochinese landscape and life-history traits","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446001","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this study simultaneously monitored drinking patterns from multiple pens in one weaner section and one finisher section herd are modeled in a multivariate dynamic linear model (DLM). Correlations between the monitored data are incorporated in the model allowing it to include interactions between pens in each section. A two-sided tabular CUSUM is applied as control chart, whereby alarms for outbreaks of unwanted events amongst the pigs can be generated for specific pens in the herd. Area-specific alarms enable the manager to include specific knowledge of the animals in the targeted area and choose the best suited intervention.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dominiak, Katarina Nielsen","Hindsborg, Jeff","Pedersen, Lene Juul","Kristensen, Anders Ringgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-525520"],"event":{"end":"2018-07-14","place":"Lleida, es","start":"2018-07-12","title":"2nd International Conference on Agro Big Data and Decision Support Systems in Agriculture","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"area specific predictions of unwanted events using multivariate modeling of water data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/228452338/Proceedings_Lleida_bigDSSagro2018.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-525520","ids":["ku-dd1b04a5-3ea8-46de-82ec-568d237a3d6f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-80AF9E0820FF04E0F8AD9BD1CD8016B9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/228452338/Proceed