{"abstract":"The importance of patient involvement is increasing in healthcare, and initiatives are constantly implemented to reach the ideal of involved and educated patients. This secondary analysis was initially embedded in a randomized controlled study where the aim was to gain insight into perceptions and experiences within a group of women undergoing fertility treatment through two focus group interviews. In this secondary analysis, we investigated how patient involvement was strived for in both clinical practice and research. During the analysis, it became apparent that the women exercised and maintained a clear perspective on their hope for a child, Project Child, while the interviewer pursued a treatment perspective, Project Treatment. Despite different perspectives, the conversation during the interviews seemed effortless, and it became apparent how the interviewer and the participants were actually focusing partly on the same, but primarily on different issues but without addressing or acknowledging this. Knowledge and awareness of the difference in perspectives is important when healthcare professionals seek to involve patients both in clinical practice and in research. Patient involvement in both research and clinical practice has shown to be a challenge and entails that pathways are organized and decisions shared by healthcare professionals.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Handberg, Charlotte","Beedholm, Kirsten","Bregnballe, Vibeke","Nielsen, Annette Nellemann","Seibæk, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-233443"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fertility treatment","Focus Groups","Hermeneutic phenomenology","Patient Centered Care","Patient involvement","Research Design","Secondary analysis","patient involvement in research"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reflections on patient involvement in research and clinical practice a secondary analysis of women s perceptions and experiences of egg aspiration in fertility treatment","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85020400554","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-233443","identifier":[{"id":"28597981","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85020400554","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b6752b31-8a1e-42a8-a02b-1edab648a39d"],"keyword":["fertility treatment","focus groups","hermeneutic-phenomenology","patient involvement","patient involvement in research","patient-centered care","research design","secondary analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2CD9B0DFC5F7BECE91D8247F9A00A3CE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Klinisk Socialmedicin og Rehabilitering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"handbergpau","last":"Handberg","locid":"282bd838-2f69-4679-9331-15174eec2360","name":"Handberg, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-1378-2449","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten","key":"beedholmpau","last":"Beedholm","locid":"17104b38-0b79-4815-8338-6a1e2de650cf","name":"Beedholm, Kirsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibeke","key":"bregnballepau","last":"Bregnballe","locid":"ed1feb62-9575-41b3-be0f-8538ee44be76","name":"Bregnballe, Vibeke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette Nellemann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Annette Nellemann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"seibækpau","last":"Seibæk","locid":"2bf95667-24b9-444b-b3e1-a62965aac67a","name":"Seibæk, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-2396-8669","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28597981"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/nin.12210","issn":["13207881","14401800"],"issn_org":["13207881"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nursing Inquiry","paperid":"e12210","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Nursing Inquiry","volume":"24 (1)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020400554"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b6752b31-8a1e-42a8-a02b-1edab648a39d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reflections on Patient Involvement in Research and Clinical Practice: A Secondary Analysis of Women’s Perceptions and Experiences of Egg Aspiration in Fertility Treatment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-233443","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Forward osmosis (FO) is a low energy-intensive process since the driving force for water transport is the osmotic pressure difference, Δπ, between the feed and draw solutions, separated by the FO membrane, where πdraw > πfeed. The potential of FO in wastewater treatment and desalination have been extensively studied; however, regeneration of the draw solution (thereby generating clean water) requires application of an energy-intensive process step like reverse osmosis (RO). In this study, the potential of applying FO for direct water recirculation from diluted fermentation effluent to concentrated feedstock, without the need for an energy-intensive regeneration step (e.g. RO), has been investigated. Butanol production during crude glycerol fermentation by Clostridium pasteurianum, has been selected as a model process and the effect of cross-flow velocity and the dilution of draw solution on the water flux during short-term experiments (200 min), were investigated. Statistical analysis revealed that the dilution of the draw solution is the most influential factor for the water flux. Subsequent modelling of an integrated FO-fermentation process, showed that water recoveries could lead to substantial financial benefits, although the integrated FO-fermentation process demonstrated lower water flux than expected. FTIR analyses of the membrane surface implied that the decrease in water flux was due to the presence of proteins, polysaccharides and other extracellular polymeric substances on the membrane active layer, indicating the presence of a fouling layer. Based on these findings, possible fouling alleviation strategies and future research directions are discussed and proposed.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kalafatakis, Stavros","Braekevelt, S.","Lymperatou, Anna","Zarebska, Agata","Hélix-Nielsen, Claus","Lange, Lene","Skiadas, Ioannis V.","Gavala, Hariklia N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-323683"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Gavala, Hariklia N."],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Crude glycerol"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"application of forward osmosis technology in crude glycerol fermentation biorefinery potential and challenges","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://rdcu.be/b0XMu","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-323683","identifier":[{"id":"29691653","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85045932638","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4039bd47-6946-402f-a25a-9be7cbd16178"],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Crude glycerol","Forwards osmosis","Novel draw solution application"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-33DE024B8CFC6E25483106AA3FEBAAC8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://rdcu.be/b0XMu","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Aquaporin A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":