{"abstract":"Background Biting midges of the genus Culicoides (Diptera: Ceratopogonidae) are vectors of bluetongue virus (BTV), African horse sickness virus and Schmallenberg virus (SBV). Outbreaks of both BTV and SBV have affected large parts of Europe. The spread of these diseases depends largely on vector distribution and abundance. The aim of this analysis was to identify and quantify major spatial patterns and temporal trends in the distribution and seasonal variation of observed Culicoides abundance in nine countries in Europe. Methods We gathered existing Culicoides data from Spain, France, Germany, Switzerland, Austria, Denmark, Sweden, Norway and Poland. In total, 31,429 Culicoides trap collections were available from 904 ruminant farms across these countries between 2007 and 2013. Results The Obsoletus ensemble was distributed widely in Europe and accounted for 83% of all 8,842,998 Culicoides specimens in the dataset, with the highest mean monthly abundance recorded in France, Germany and southern Norway. The Pulicaris ensemble accounted for only 12% of the specimens and had a relatively southerly and easterly spatial distribution compared to the Obsoletus ensemble. Culicoides imicola Kieffer was only found in Spain and the southernmost part of France. There was a clear spatial trend in the accumulated annual abundance from southern to northern Europe, with the Obsoletus ensemble steadily increasing from 4000 per year in southern Europe to 500,000 in Scandinavia. The Pulicaris ensemble showed a very different pattern, with an increase in the accumulated annual abundance from 1600 in Spain, peaking at 41,000 in northern Germany and then decreasing again toward northern latitudes. For the two species ensembles and C. imicola, the season began between January and April, with later start dates and increasingly shorter vector seasons at more northerly latitudes. Conclusion We present the first maps of seasonal Culicoides abundance in large parts of Europe covering a gradient from southern Spain to northern Scandinavia. The identified temporal trends and spatial patterns are useful for planning the allocation of resources for international prevention and surveillance programmes in the European Union.","author_count":39,"contributors":["Cuéllar, Ana Carolina","Kjær, Lene Jung","Kirkeby, Carsten","Skovgård, Henrik","Nielsen, Søren Achim","Stockmarr, Anders","Andersson, Gunnar","Lindstrom, Anders","Chirico, Jan","Lühken, Renke","Steinke, Sonja","Kiel, Ellen","Gethmann, Jörn","Conraths, Franz J.","Larska, Magdalena","Hamnes, Inger","Sviland, Ståle","Hopp, Petter","Brugger, Katharina","Rubel, Franz","Balenghien, Thomas","Garros, Claire","Rakotoarivony, Ignace","Allène, Xavier","Lhoir, Jonathan","Chavernac, David","Delécolle, Jean Claude","Mathieu, Bruno","Delécolle, Delphine","Setier-Rio, Marie Laure","Venail, Roger","Scheid, Bethsabée","Chueca, Miguel Ángel Miranda","Barceló, Carlos","Lucientes, Javier","Estrada, Rosa","Mathis, Alexander","Tack, Wesley","Bødker, Rene"],"cuid":["S03-094.73-025576"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cuellar, Ana Carolina","Cuéllar, Ana Carolina"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","France","Germany","Norway","Poland","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Avia-GIS NV","Bernhard Nocht Institute for Tropical Medicine","CIRAD","CIRAD - The French Agricultural Research Centre for International Development","Centre de coopération internationale en recherche agronomique pour le développement","EID Méditerranée","Friedrich-Loeffler-Institute","Institute for Veterinary Public Health","National Veterinary Institute","National Veterinary Institute (SVA)","National Veterinary Institute Norway","National Veterinary Research Institute","Norwegian Veterinary Institute","Oldenburg Universitet","University of Oldenburg","University of Veterinary Medicine Vienna","University of Zaragoza","University of Zurich","University of the Balearic Islands","Université de Strasbourg","Université du Strasbourg"],"keyword":["Culicoides abundance","Culicoides distribution","Europe","Seasonal abundance","Spatial pattern","Temporal trend","Vector borne disease","Vector season"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spatial and temporal variation in the abundance of culicoides biting midges diptera ceratopogonidae in nine european countries","src":["au","dtu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13071-018-2706-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-094.73-025576","identifier":[{"id":"85042583531","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5828119","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29482593","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b10e02a9-4b49-4eb1-b31e-5cf540c0e1af","dtu-51127db3-ef20-4fb8-8ff3-21ed14638beb","ruc-ea81d53c-14ef-4f6f-99fd-734d888823f4"],"keyword":["Culicoides abundance","Culicoides distribution","Europe","Seasonal abundance","Spatial pattern","Temporal trend","Vector season","Vector-borne disease"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-51ACB96195BEA203C38401C0B80CF4B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://parasitesandvectors.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s13071-018-2706-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13071-018-2706-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/144429843/Cuellar_et_al_20