inn","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"sellebjergfpau","last":"Sellebjerg","name":"Sellebjerg, F.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Egon","key":"stenageregonpau","last":"Stenager","locid":"59ce8891-bead-46fd-8d17-3853a7636602","name":"Stenager, Egon","orcid":"0000-0002-4877-5193","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thor","key":"petersenthorpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"bc6cd2a2-c97f-4438-8709-d90a32f75eef","name":"Petersen, Thor","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30413632"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1212/wnl.0000000000006645","issn":["00283878","1526632X"],"issn_org":["00283878"],"issue":"24","journal":"Neurology","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Neurology","volume":"91"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058607500"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5ca4d801-82a2-4642-8284-a8dd96d7c302","au-fca3d621-b695-4811-883f-1975c1c1f397","ku-7e24c104-2f23-4f92-a9aa-aedf13800bdc","sdu-efa8f294-4ea8-411c-9594-59e59e0e307a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Nationwide prevalence and incidence study of neuromyelitis optica spectrum disorder in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.39-004500","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Identification of fetal kidney anomalies invites questions about underlying causes and recurrence risk in future pregnancies. We therefore investigated the diagnostic yield of next-generation sequencing in fetuses with bilateral kidney anomalies and the correlation between disrupted genes and fetal phenotypes. Fetuses with bilateral kidney anomalies were screened using an in-house-designed kidney-gene panel. In families where candidate variants were not identified, whole-exome sequencing was performed. Genes uncovered by this analysis were added to our kidney-panel. We identified likely deleterious variants in 11 of 56 (20%) families. The kidney-gene analysis revealed likely deleterious variants in known kidney developmental genes in six fetuses and TMEM67 variants in two unrelated fetuses. Kidney histology was similar in the latter two fetuses - presenting a distinct prenatal form of nephronophthisis. Exome sequencing identified ROBO1 variants in one family and a GREB1L variant in another family. GREB1L and ROBO1 were added to our kidney-gene panel and additional variants were identified. Next-generation sequencing substantially contributes to identifying causes of fetal kidney anomalies. Genetic causes may be supported by histological examination of the kidneys. This is the first time that SLIT-ROBO signaling is implicated in human bilateral kidney agenesis.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Rasmussen, M","Sunde, L","Nielsen, M L","Ramsing, M","Petersen, Astrid Christine","Hjortshøj, T D","Olsen, T E","Tabor, A","Hertz, J M","Johnsen, I","Sperling, L","Petersen, O B","Jensen, U B","Møller, F G","Petersen, Michael Bjørn","Lildballe, D L"],"cuid":["S04-099.78-002443"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"keyword":["CAKUT","Journal Article","Kidney dysplasia","NGS","Prenatal screening","kidney agenesis","kidney anomalies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Department of Clinical Genetics, Rigshospitalet, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"targeted gene sequencing and whole exome sequencing in autopsied fetuses with prenatally diagnosed kidney anomalies","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129581824/Targeted_Gene_Sequencing_and_Whole_Exome_Sequencing_in_Autopsied_Fetuses_with_Prenatally_Diagnosed_Kidney_Anomalies.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S04-099.78-002443","identifier":[{"id":"85042352116","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29194579","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-30ff7af9-d8f8-4a59-88ca-c0e7e493ea6f","au-8bae1db7-64df-42ee-8f63-978e53792132","ku-bc273620-8218-42f3-bd13-efdd4a37e17e","sdu-5e54db47-a821-4ffd-8c1b-f2a821698f79"],"keyword":["CAKUT","Journal Article","NGS","kidney agenesis","kidney anomalies","kidney dysplasia","prenatal screening"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-E35CFCB8FEF48824731773ECF36D3B4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129581824/Targeted_Gene_Sequencing_and_Whole_Exome_Sequencing_in_Autopsied_Fetuses_with_Prenatally_Diagnosed_Kidney_Anomalies.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/321278609/Targeted_Gene_Sequencing_and_Whole_Exome_Sequencing_in_Autopsied_Fetuses_with_Prenatally_Diagnosed_Kidney_Anomalies.pdf","version":"Authors Fin