{"abstract":"Purpose To assess effects of an inpatient multicomponent occupational rehabilitation program compared to less comprehensive outpatient rehabilitation on sickness absence in persons with musculoskeletal- or mental health disorders. Methods Randomized clinical trial with parallel groups. Participants were individuals 18-60 years old on sick-leave for 2-12 months with a sick-leave diagnosis within the musculoskeletal, psychological or general and unspecified chapters of ICPC-2, identified in a national register. The inpatient program (4 + 4 days) consisted of Acceptance and Commitment Therapy (ACT), physical training and work-related problem-solving including creating a return to work plan and a workplace visit if considered relevant. The outpatient program consisted primarily of ACT (6 sessions during 6 weeks). Both programs were group based. Primary outcome was cumulated number of sickness absence days at 6 and 12 months follow-up. Secondary outcome was time until sustainable return to work. Results 168 individuals were randomized to the inpatient program (n = 92) or the outpatient program (n = 76). We found no statistically significant difference between the programs in median number of sickness absence days at 6 and 12 months follow-up. In the outpatient program 57% of the participants achieved sustainable return to work (median time 7 months), in the inpatient program 49% (log rank, p = 0.167). The hazard ratio for sustainable return to work was 0.74 (95% CI 0.48-1.32, p = 0.165), in favor of the outpatient program. Conclusions This study provided no support that the more comprehensive 4 + 4 days inpatient multicomponent occupational rehabilitation program reduced sickness absence compared to the outpatient rehabilitation program.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Aasdahl, Lene","Pape, Kristine","Vasseljen, Ottar","Johnsen, Roar","Gismervik, Sigmund","Halsteinli, Vidar","Fleten, Nils","Nielsen, Claus Vinther","Fimland, Marius Steiro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-193061"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","St. Olavs University Hospital (Trondheim)","UiT The Arctic University of Norway"],"keyword":["Cognitive Therapy","Mental health","Musculoskeletal Diseases","Return to work","Sick Leave"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of inpatient multicomponent occupational rehabilitation versus less comprehensive outpatient rehabilitation on sickness absence in persons with musculoskeletal or mental health disorders a randomized clinical trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10926-017-9708-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-193061","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5820389","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85017454378","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28401441","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6f9dcca2-f604-449e-8e97-e52ecb417f96"],"keyword":["cognitive therapy","mental health","musculoskeletal diseases","return to work","sick leave"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D9A52DE31F5D2B5980CED6D4ABBEEB73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10926-017-9708-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/169240043/Aasdahl2018_Article_EffectOfInpatientMulticomponen.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"st olavs university hospital","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"St. Olavs University Hospital (Trondheim)","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"uit the arctic university of norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UiT The Arctic University of Norway","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Klinisk Socialmedicin og Rehabilitering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"aasdahlpau","last":"Aasdahl","name":"Aasdahl, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine","key":"papepau","last":"Pape","name":"Pape, Kristine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ottar","key":"vasseljenpau","last":"Vasseljen","name":"Vasseljen, Ottar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Roar","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Roar","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sigmund","key":"gismervikpau","last":"Gismervik","name":"Gismervik, Sigmund","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vidar","key":"halsteinlipau","last":"Halsteinli","name":"Halsteinli, Vidar","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils","key":"fletenpau","last":"Fleten","name":"Fleten, Nils","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus Vinther","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"033d1aa9-948f-4ed4-be3e-200d0100b399","name":"Nielsen, Claus Vinther","orcid":"0000-0002-2467-1103","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marius Steiro","key":"fimlandpau","last":"Fimland","name":"Fimland, Marius Steiro","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28401441"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10926-017-9708-z","issn":["10530487","15733688"],"issn_org":["10530487"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Occupational Rehabilitation","pages":"170-179","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Occupational Rehabilitation","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017454378"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6f9dcca2-f604-449e-8e97-e52ecb417f96"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effect of Inpatient Multicomponent Occupational Rehabilitation Versus Less Comprehensive Outpatient Rehabilitation on Sickness Absence in Persons with Musculoskeletal- or Mental Health Disorders : A Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-193061","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this research, we investigate if and how more photos than a single headshot can heighten the level of information provided by persona profiles. We conduct eye-tracking experiments and qualitative interviews with variations in the photos: a single headshot, a headshot and images of the persona in different contexts, and a headshot with pictures of different people representing key persona attributes. The results show that more contextual photos significantly improve the information end users derive from a persona profile; however, showing images of different people creates confusion and lowers the informativeness. Moreover, we discover that choice of pictures results in various interpretations of the persona that are biased by the end users' experiences and preconceptions. The results imply that persona creators should consider the design power of photos when creating persona profiles.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Salminen, joni","Nielsen, Lene","Jung, Soon-Gyo","An, Jisun","Kwak, Haewoon","Jansen, Bernard J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382617"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Qatar"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qatar Computing Research institute"],"keyword":["Online data representations","Personas","User perceptions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"is more better impact of multiple photos on perception of persona profiles","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83457574/Is_more_better_PURE.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382617","identifier":[{"id":"85046943377","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5ae14de2-8659-44e8-9e80-b4e5dbf051c0"],"keyword":["online data representations","personas","user perceptions"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8899BC5163CF62919E4EF4C6FF27E5C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83457574/Is_more_better_PURE.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"qa","key":"qatar computing research institute","loc":["Qatar","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Qatar Computing Research institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"joni","key":"salminenpau","last":"Salminen","name":"Salminen, joni","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Soon-Gyo","key":"jungpau","last":"Jung","name":"Jung, Soon-Gyo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jisun","key":"anpau","last":"An","name":"An, Jisun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Haewoon","key":"kwakpau","last":"Kwak","name":"Kwak, Haewoon","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernard J.","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","name":"Jansen, Bernard J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3173574.3173891","eisbn":["9781450356206"],"pages":"1-13","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"CHI '18","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046943377"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5ae14de2-8659-44e8-9e80-b4e5dbf051c0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"“Is More Better?” : Impact of Multiple Photos on Perception of Persona Profiles","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382617","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Disruption of human fetal testis development is widely accepted to underlie testicular germ cell cancer (TGCC) origin and additional disorders within testicular dysgenesis syndrome (TDS). However, the mechanisms for the development of testicular dysgenesis in humans are unclear. We used ex vivo culture and xenograft approaches to investigate the importance of Nodal and Activin signaling in human fetal testis development. Inhibition of Nodal, and to some extent Activin, signaling disrupted seminiferous cord formation, abolished AMH expression, reduced androgen secretion, and decreased gonocyte numbers. Subsequent xenografting of testicular tissue rescued the disruptive effects on seminiferous cords and somatic cells but not germ cell effects. Stimulation of Nodal signaling increased the number of germ cells expressing pluripotency factors, and these persisted after xenografting. Our findings suggest a key role for Nodal signaling in the regulation of gonocyte differentiation and early human testis development with implications for the understanding of TGCC and TDS origin.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Anne","Macdonald, Joni","Nielsen, John E","Kilcoyne, Karen R","Perlman, Signe","Lundvall, Lene","Langhoff Thuesen, Lea","Juul Hare, Kristine","Frederiksen, Hanne","Andersson, Anna-Maria","Skakkebæk, Niels Erik","Juul, Anders","Sharpe, Richard M","Rajpert-De Meyts, Ewa","Mitchell, Rod T"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394520"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nodal signaling regulates germ cell development and establishment of seminiferous cords in the human fetal testis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2018.10.064","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-394520","identifier":[{"id":"85056248201","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30428358","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-01baedbc-d213-4b87-9884-4060041a3533"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3743AA2C6E9B59B1B54C9EA049A2E3FA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2018.10.064","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Anne","rank":1,"