,"name":"Maeng, Michael","name_org":"Mæng, Michael","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen D","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"6d64271d-8a2c-41ea-891d-e85555bbd47a","name":"Kristensen, Steen Dalby","name_org":"Kristensen, Steen D","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars R","key":"krusellpau","last":"Krusell","locid":"660b49df-f279-4bc2-8ff9-50fe259b2d33","name":"Krusell, Lars Romer","name_org":"Krusell, Lars R","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens F","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"569ae3f1-67b8-4b02-9b3f-6469767f33e3","name":"Lassen, Jens Flensted","name_org":"Lassen, Jens F","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper M","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a5cb9465-6652-4dda-806d-a8f33c29ff82","name":"Jensen, Jesper Møller","name_org":"Jensen, Jesper M","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28862968"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/jaha.117.005587","issn":["20479980"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of the American Heart Association","paperid":"e005587","publisher":"American Heart Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Heart Association","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030699040"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-24d7d104-41e4-48c9-86cf-d0ed73adf683","sdu-c266f0c7-34cb-4a33-b696-043ee021e2d7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Myocardial Perfusion Imaging Versus Computed Tomography Angiography-Derived Fractional Flow Reserve Testing in Stable Patients With Intermediate-Range Coronary Lesions : Influence on Downstream Diagnostic Workflows and Invasive Angiography Findings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.95-015277","year":"2017","yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"Personas have become a popular method in new product development. Personas have traditionally, and are still, primarily created to represent users from a single national culture at a time during the design process. This, however, is unsatisfactory for companies operating on a global market as they show an increasing interest in international personas. However, research on personas in a global context is limited. To address this gap, this paper provides an overview of extant research on international personas. Secondly, it presents an empirical study on challenges Danish IT companies experience when using the persona method to collect and present insights about their international users. A key finding in both the literature review and the empirical study was the ambiguity concerning the concept of culture. Therefore, the paper draws on theories about culture, and especially practice theory, to discuss how challenges related to perceptions of culture and intercultural communication might be overcome when working with international personas. In particular, it is suggested that the persona method could benefit from creating narratives that focus more on the similar practices enacted by international users and less on perceived differences in national culture.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Iben","Hautopp, Heidi","Nielsen, Lene","Madsen, Sabine"],"cuid":["S03-099.95-000232"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Globalization","Personas","Practice theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"developing international personas a new intercultural communication practice in globalized societies","src":["aau","itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.immi.se/intercultural/nr43/jensen.html","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.95-000232","identifier":[{"id":"85016975035","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-04887337-8c31-4751-943d-c0c71a98d26b","itu-de0c3330-6650-48cc-8b49-7f37e331e916","ruc-e2575a0f-4f4d-4214-9b72-5cd1478b9caf"],"keyword":["Keywords: personas, practice theory, globalization","globalization","personas","practice theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FD7937375930B7AA55C450122C1B4C17"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83026039/Developing_International_Personas_Journal_of_intercultural_communication.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/316217719_Developing_international_personas_A_new_intercultural_communication_practice_in_globalized_societies","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://immi.se/oldwebsite/nr43/jensen.html","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.immi.se/intercultural/nr43/jensen.html","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, Centre for Education Policy Research (Learning)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosoph