{"abstract":"Aspergillus aculeatus is known for the commercial utilization in production of several enzymes. We have identified two stereoisomeric compounds of mixed polyketide-nonribosomal peptide origin in the extracts of A. aculeatus that we named acurin A and acurin B. The structures of the compounds strongly resemble the structure of the mycotoxin fusarin C produced by several Fusarium species. CRISPR-Cas9 was used to construct a non-homologous end-joining deficient strain of A. aculeatus, which enabled efficient gene deletions in the acurin gene cluster. Using RT-qPCR in combination with metabolite profiling of gene deletion strains, the acurin producing gene cluster was delineated, which allowed us to propose a biosynthetic pathway for formation of acurin. Our results show that acurin, in contrast to fusarin C, is biosynthesized by an individual polyketide synthase and non-ribosomal synthetase. At least six other enzymatic activities are required for the biosynthesis of acurin. This study shows how we exploit the CRISPR-Cas9 system for the rapid construction of fungal host strains that can be readily engineered to generate valuable knowledge.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Nielsen, Maria Lund","Wolff, Peter B.","Petersen, Lene Maj","Andersen, Lasse Norup","Isbrandt, Thomas","Holm, Dorte Koefoed","Mortensen, Uffe Hasbro","Nødvig, Christina Spuur","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","Hoof, Jakob Blæsbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-355360"],"event":{"end":"2017-03-19","place":"Pacific Grove, us","start":"2017-03-14","title":"29th Fungal Genetics Conference","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biosynthesis of acurin a and b in aspergillus aculeatus","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/162625431/29FGC_Abstract_Book.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-355360","ids":["dtu-aa0fc8bd-bb4e-4f7f-891c-6e2b255404a8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-637F62DE8153F314332BB8E62066C179"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/162625431/29FGC_Abstract_Book.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Microbial and Chemical Ecology, Natural Product Discovery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.L.","key":"nielsenmarialundpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3161157c-75e3-4aa2-8376-8fbc8cb8b1ee","name":"Nielsen, Maria Lund","name_org":"Nielsen, M.L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P.P.","key":"wolffpeterbpau","last":"Wolff","locid":"df7eba21-df08-438a-a488-8456b01a0ee7","name":"Wolff, Peter B.","name_org":"Wolff, P.P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.M.","key":"petersenlenemajpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"7a1c5a02-7eb8-40e3-a1ec-621fb3c37652","name":"Petersen, Lene Maj","name_org":"Petersen, L.M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L.N.","key":"andersenlassenoruppau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8ced82e2-4db1-4522-8690-046e4b2093b1","name":"Andersen, Lasse Norup","name_org":"Anderse