{"abstract":"Aims: The aims of the study were to investigate the effects of the GLP-1 receptor agonist liraglutide as add-on to metformin on insulin sensitivity (Si) and glucose effectiveness (Sg) in addition to its positive effects on beta-cell function in overweight/obese patients with coronary artery disease (CAD) and type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM). Methods: The design of the study was a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, cross-over trial in patients with stable CAD and newly diagnosed well-controlled T2DM. Patients were treated with liraglutide/metformin vs placebo/metformin for a 12 + 12-week period with ≥2-week wash-out. First phase insulin secretion (AIRg), Si and Sg were estimated by the Bergman Minimal Model, enabling calculation of beta-cell function; Disposition Index (DI) = AIRg × Si. A total of 30 patients from among 41 randomized were available for paired analysis. Results: Baseline characteristics were: HbA1c 47 mmol/mol (SD 6), BMI 31.6 kg/m2 (SD 4.8), fasting plasma-glucose 6.9 mmol/L (IQR 6.1; 7.4) and HOMA-IR 4.9 (IQR 3.0; 7.5). Liraglutide treatment improved AIRg by 3-fold, 497 mU × L−1 × min (IQR 342; 626, P <.0001) and DI by 1-fold, 766 (SD 824, P <.0001). Despite a significant weight loss of −2.7 kg (−6.7; −0.6) during liraglutide treatment, we found no improvement in HOMA-IR, Si or Sg. Weight loss during liraglutide therapy did not result in a carry-over effect. Conclusion: Liraglutide as add-on to metformin induces a clinically significant improvement in beta-cell function in overweight/obese, high cardiovascular risk patients with newly diagnosed well-controlled T2DM and CAD. The effect of liraglutide on DI is mediated entirely by improved AIRg whereas the effects on Si and Sg are neutral.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Anholm, Christian","Kumarathurai, Preman","Pedersen, Lene R.","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Kristiansen, Ole P.","Fenger, Mogens","Madsbad, Sten","Sajadieh, Ahmad","Haugaard, Steen Bendix"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-543446"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Beta cell function","Glucose effectiveness","Insulin sensitivity","Liraglutide","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liraglutide effects on beta cell insulin sensitivity and glucose effectiveness in patients with stable coronary artery disease and newly diagnosed type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-543446","identifier":[{"id":"85013684704","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28124822","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-fb4b820c-8106-4842-a9e9-a9d101f8df8b"],"keyword":["beta-cell function","glucose effectiveness","insulin sensitivity","liraglutide","type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D2BC670C89AE53285CCB66A840DEBD50"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"anholmpau","last":"Anholm","name":"Anholm, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Preman","key":"kumarathuraipau","last":"Kumarathurai","name":"Kumarathurai, Preman","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene R.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Lene R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olav W.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d9fc9e11-583d-43d9-994c-df128b7bf5cc","name":"Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","name_org":"Nielsen, Olav W.","orcid":"0000-0003-3532-9431","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ole P.","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Ole P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mogens","key":"fengerpau","last":"Fenger","name":"Fenger, Mogens","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ahmad","key":"sajadiehpau","last":"Sajadieh","locid":"2f54d4de-84ea-41ba-9d41-d30368bc7b59","name":"Sajadieh, Ahmad","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen B.","key":"haugaardpau","last":"Haugaard","locid":"6fef997b-dc58-4cc9-ab00-4a3e92968454","name":"Haugaard, Steen Bendix","name_org":"Haugaard, Steen B.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28124822"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/dom.12891","issn":["14628902","14631326"],"issn_org":["14628902"],"issue":"6","journal":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","pages":"850-857","status":"p","title":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85013684704"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fb4b820c-8106-4842-a9e9-a9d101f8df8b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Liraglutide effects on beta-cell, insulin sensitivity and glucose effectiveness in patients with stable coronary artery disease and newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-543446","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
