outhern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c48c7097-e87c-4373-9696-dbcf38ec4694"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Health-related quality of life in non-transplant eligible newly diagnosed multiple myeloma patients treated with melphalan/prednisolone plus either thalidomide or lenalidomide; results of the HOVON87/NMSG18 study. Quality of Life Research","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-629527","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In Denmark, influenza A virus of the subtype H3N2 has been dominating the 2016/17 season, as in most countries of the Northern Hemisphere. OBJECTIVES: This study was conducted as part of the Danish seasonal influenza surveillance programme to genetically characterize circulating H3N2 viruses and determine the seasonal vaccine effectiveness (VE) overall in the Danish population and further on the virus cluster level. STUDY DESIGN: Influenza virus positive samples submitted for the national surveillance programme were genetically characterized by sequencing. VE estimates against influenza A and the circulating virus clusters were determined in patients above 65 years using the test-negative case-control design. RESULTS: The genetic characterization revealed several genetically drifted viruses, which could be divided into four main clusters by the defining amino acid substitutions: 3C.2a/N121K/S144K, 3C.2a/T131K/R142K, 3C.2a1, and 3C.2a1/N121K. Some of the drifted viruses appeared to be more prominent in vaccinated or non-vaccinated individuals, respectively. Overall the adjusted VE was 7.4% (95% confidence interval (CI): -6.0-19.2) among inpatients and 19.3% (95% CI: -5.7-38.4) among outpatients, respectively. VE for the four main virus clusters was; cluster 3C.2a1: 38.8% (95% CI: -29.8-71.1), cluster 3C.2a/N121K/S144K: 9.2% (95% CI: -63.0-49.4), cluster 3C.2a/T131K/R142K: 19.0% (95% CI: -85.3-64.6), and cluster 3C.2a1/N121K: -12.2% (95%CI: -129.7-45.2). CONCLUSIONS: Several genetically drifted H3N2 viruses have been circulating in Denmark in the 2016-17 influenza season. An overall low VE was estimated and VE for the four main virus cluster indicate different VEs between the circulating drifted H3N2 viruses.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Trebbien, Ramona","Kølsen Fischer, Thea","Krause, Tyra Grove","Nielsen, Lene","Nielsen, Xiaohui Chen","Sandborg Weinreich, Lenette","Lis-Tønder, Joanna","Skov, Marianne Nielsine","Christiansen, Claus Bohn","Emborg, Hanne-Dorthe"],"cuid":["S02-096.59-005027"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"changes in genetically drifted h000000000003n000000000002 influenza a viruses and vaccine effectiveness in adults 000000000065 years and older during the 000000002016 000000000017 season in denmark","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85022064208","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.59-005027","identifier":[{"id":"000410608400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85022064208","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28697450","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-67c21dd5-171b-4ffb-9ee4-2f02a843da39","sdu-459b1ddd-bc12-4e2a-bd1f-f5494a9bb2b7"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FBF3BB7BE31BD61325B6CEE636358F5E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Microbiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienramonapau","last":"Trebbien","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thea K","key":"fischertheakølsenpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"b998a645-13b1-4b43-a8fe-2516562d5365","name":"Fischer, Thea Kølsen","name_org":"Fischer, Thea K","orcid":"0000-0003-4812-980X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thea","key":"kølsenfischertheapau","last":"Kølsen Fischer","name":"Kølsen Fischer, Thea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tyra Grove","key":"krausetyragrovepau","last":"Krause","name":"Krause, Tyra Grove","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenlenepau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaohui Chen","key":"chennielsenxiaohuipau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"eba27666-a4e1-4ea4-a439-aa50a1c57f36","name":"Chen Nielsen, Xiaohui","name_org":"Nielsen, Xiaohui Chen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaohui Chen","key":"nielsenxiaohuichenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Xiaohui Chen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lenette Sandborg","key":"sandborgweinreichlenettepau","last":"Weinreich","locid":"feede90f-728f-45d6-b394-aa3534430b4d","name":"Sandborg Weinreich, Lenette","name_org":"Weinreich, Lenette Sandborg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lenette Sandborg","key":"weinreichlenettesandborgpau","last":"Weinreich","name":"Weinreich, Lenette Sandborg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"listønderjoannapau","last":"Lis-Tønder","locid":"ef829d21-3c81-4f47-b612-e7f963ac7f02","name":"Lis-Tønder, Joanna","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne Nielsine","key":"skovmariannenielsinepau","last":"Skov","locid":"5b2553ab-dfde-4995-8c58-7840a16be668","name":"Skov, Marianne Nielsine","orcid":"0000-0002-2619-0864","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Bohn","key":"christiansenclausbohnpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Claus Bohn","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne-Dorthe","key":"emborghannedorthepau","last":"Emborg","name":"Emborg, Hanne-Dorthe","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28697450"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcv.2017.06.007","issn":["13866532","18735967"],"issn_org":["13866532"],"journal":"Journal of Clinical Virology","pages":"1-7","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Virology","volume":"94"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85022064208"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-67c21dd5-171b-4ffb-9ee4-2f02a843da39","sdu-459b1ddd-bc12-4e2a-bd1f-f5494a9bb2b7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Changes in genetically drifted H3N2 influenza A viruses and vaccine effectiveness in adults 65 years and older during the 2016/17 season in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.59-005027","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The expression of Caudal-related homeobox transcription factor 2 (CDX2) is impaired by tumor necrosis factor-α (TNF-α)-mediated activation of nuclear factor-κB (NF-κB) in ulcerative colitis (UC). Laminin subunit γ2 (LAMC2) is an epithelial basement membrane protein implicated in cell migration, proliferation, differentiation, as well as tumor invasion and intestinal inflammation, and its expression is enhanced by TNF-α in a NF-κB-dependent regulation of the recently identified LAMC2 enhancer. The aim was to determine whether CDX2 is involved in the basal regulation of LAMC2 in epithelial cells and to assess the influence of inflammation. Transcriptional regulation of LAMC2 was examined by reporter gene assays, overexpression, and shRNA-mediated knock-down of CDX2. CDX2-DNA interactions were assessed by chromatin immunoprecipitation on Caco-2 cells without or with TNF-α, as well as in purified colonic human epithelial cells. Immunohistochemical staining and quantitative reverse-transcription polymerase chain reaction analyses were used to measure the expression of CDX2 and LAMC2 in colonic biopsies from healthy controls and patients with UC. These data indicate that CDX2 directly regulates LAMC2 gene expression through interaction with elements in the LAMC2 promoter region. We further revealed an inverse effect of inflammation on CDX2 and LAMC2. The data presented provide a novel insight into how CDX2 is implicated in the transcriptional regulation of LAMC2 in intestinal epithelial cells, a function that is impaired during mucosal inflammation where a high level of TNF-α is present. J. Cell. Biochem. 9999: 1-10, 2016. © 2016 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Coskun, Mehmet","Soendergaard, Christoffer","Joergensen, Steffen","Dahlgaard, Katja","Riis, Lene Buhl","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Sandelin, Albin Gustav","Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald"],"cuid":["S02-096.66-040075"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["CDX2","Gene regulation","Inflammation","Ulcerative colitis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"regulation of laminin γ000000000002 expression by cdx000000000002 in colonic epithelial cells is impaired during active inflammation","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/57178048/Coskun_et_al_2016_Journal_of_Cellular_Biochemistry.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-096.66-040075","identifier":[{"id":"27333824","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85006814763","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0c149eb2-3986-40d8-aa5d-75e2c1888270","ruc-9ce59303-6bf2-4115-92aa-b241d47bb5f0"],"keyword":["CDX2","GENE REGULATION","INFLAMMATION","LAMC2","ULCERATIVE COLITIS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-750C900F594294B6BC446857E071EDC9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/57178048/Coskun_et_al_2016_Journal_of_Cellular_Biochemistry.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mehmet","key":"coskunpau","last":"Coskun","locid":"6a19eccb-de97-41ce-9daa-a75afe94aa20","name":"Coskun, Mehmet","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christoffer","key":"soendergaardpau","last":"Soendergaard","name":"Soendergaard, Christoffer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Steffen","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7eb83c10-af24-4020-8aa8-b279d959f475","name":"Jørgensen, Steffen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Katja","key":"dahlgaardpau","last":"Dahlgaard","locid":"bd84257d-f62e-4de3-b1f4-aa6253e79f76","name":"Dahlgaard, Katja","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Buhl","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Ole Haagen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59658c4-dde8-4749-9b5c-f4ec5910dd02","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","orcid":"0000-0003-4612-8635","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Albin Gustav","key":"sandelinpau","last":"Sandelin","locid":"372289e2-612f-4629-9dbf-9e3de03fdd46","name":"Sandelin, Albin Gustav","orcid":"0000-0002-7109-7378","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"3b39117d-6f4e-47c7-a61d-5192c15b00a9","name":"Troelsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-4177-3267","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27333824"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jcb.25636","issn":["07302312","07331959"],"issn_org":["07302312"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Cellular Biochemistry","pages":"298-307","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cellular Biochemistry","volume":"118"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85006814763"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0c149eb2-3986-40d8-aa5d-75e2c1888270","ruc-9ce59303-6bf2-4115-92aa-b241d47bb5f0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Regulation of Laminin γ2 Expression by CDX2 in Colonic Epithelial Cells Is Impaired During Active Inflammation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.66-040075","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background: Social deficits and emotional dysregulation have been suggested as explanations for the relational difficulties experienced by patients with borderline personality disorder (BPD). The neuropeptide oxytocin (OXT) is a possible neurobiological underpinning of these adversities, and this study examines possible correlations between BPD symptomatology and serum OXT. Methods: Thirty-eight female participants (BPD group n = 18, matched control group n = 20) with a mean age of 29.5 years (standard deviation 9.2) were assessed for personality disorders, general psychopathology, childhood trauma and perceived stress. OXT was measured in serum samples. Results: We found no significant difference between patient and control group in terms of OXT levels. However, post hoc analysis showed a relationship in the patient group between civil status and OXT (p < 0.05), indicating higher levels of OXT for patients in a romantic relationship. Discussion: The idea of OXT as a pro-social love hormone is perhaps too simplistic, and factors like attachment style, exposure to trauma and psychiatric disorders must be considered in order to understand its diverse functions. Conclusions: Contrary to our expectations, we did not find lower serum OXT levels in the BPD group. However, BPD patients in a romantic relationship had higher levels of serum OXT than single BPD patients.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bomann, Anne Cathrine","Jørgensen, Martin Balslev","Bo, Sune","Nielsen, Marianne","Gede, Lene Bjerring","Elfving, Betina","Simonsen, Erik"],"cuid":["S03-096.47-672146"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Journal Article","health nutrition and quality of life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Psychiatric Research Unit, Region Zealand Psychiatry, Region Zealand, Slagelse, Denmark"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the neurobiology of social deficits in female patients with borderline personality disorder the importance of oxytocin","src":["au","ku","pha"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85017469657","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-096.47-672146","identifier":[{"id":"85017469657","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28397403","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-62022440-ce2a-4a86-ab08-e4afc92df4dd","ku-f0d7b9e7-53ea-43e3-87a0-ecc2bd8104ac","pha-da11eb9a-68f2-4720-be9f-b19e8b718eaf"],"keyword":["Journal Article","health, nutrition and quality of life"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-D41D095B7A1DB759E5C7B83BDEB05902"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Region Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Psychiatric Research Unit, Region Zealand Psychiatry, Region Zealand, Slagelse, Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Sundhed, Social og Engineeringområdet, Bioanalytikeruddannelsen - Næstved"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Cathrine","key":"bomannpau","last":"Bomann","name":"Bomann, Anne Cathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Martin Balslev","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"dfc70acd-d15d-44f9-891e-6a7646d1727d","name":"Jørgensen, Martin Balslev","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sune","key":"bopau","last":"Bo","name":"Bo, Sune","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3905bc20-e34d-45d5-a361-b103d7053f11","name":"Nielsen, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0001-8022-2364","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Bjerring","key":"gedepau","last":"Gede","name":"Gede, Lene Bjerring","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"bjerringgedepau","last":"Bjerring Gede","name":"Bjerring Gede, Lene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Betina","key":"elfvingpau","last":"Elfving","locid":"b7b26927-4ed5-45ec-a82b-c8a860d592ca","name":"Elfving, Betina","orcid":"0000-0001-6939-5088","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Erik","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"a00e5cad-92bc-40ab-8ebc-92298c919f9d","name":"Simonsen, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-6134-2392","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28397403"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/pmh.1369","issn":["19328621"],"issue":"2","journal":"Personality and Mental Health","pages":"91-100","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Personality and Mental Health","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017469657"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University College Absalon","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-62022440-ce2a-4a86-ab08-e4afc92df4dd","ku-f0d7b9e7-53ea-43e3-87a0-ecc2bd8104ac","pha-da11eb9a-68f2-4720-be9f-b19e8b718eaf"],"src":["AB University College Absalon","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The neurobiology of social deficits in female patients with borderline personality disorder : The importance of oxytocin","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-096.47-672146","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In Lotus japonicus, a LysM receptor kinase, EPR3, distinguishes compatible and incompatible rhizobial exopolysaccharides at the epidermis. However, the role of this recognition system in bacterial colonization of the root interior is unknown. Here we show that EPR3 advances the intracellular infection mechanism that mediates infection thread invasion of the root cortex and nodule primordia. At the cellular level, Epr3 expression delineates progression of infection threads into nodule primordia and cortical infection thread formation is impaired in epr3 mutants. Genetic dissection of this developmental coordination showed that Epr3 is integrated into the symbiosis signal transduction pathways. Further analysis showed differential expression of Epr3 in the epidermis and cortical primordia and identified key transcription factors controlling this tissue specificity. These results suggest that exopolysaccharide recognition is reiterated during the progressing infection and that EPR3 perception of compatible exopolysaccharide promotes an intracellular cortical infection mechanism maintaining bacteria enclosed in plant membranes.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Kawaharada, Yasuyuki","Nielsen, Mette Wibroe","Kelly, Simon","James, Euan K","Andersen, Kasper Røjkjær","Rasmussen, Sheena Ricafranca","Füchtbauer, Winnie Sophie","Madsen, Lene Heegaard","Heckmann, Anne Birgitte","Radutoiu, Simona","Stougaard, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-182646"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The James Hutton Institute"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differential regulation of the epr000000000003 receptor coordinates membrane restricted rhizobial colonization of root nodule primordia","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms14534","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-182646","identifier":[{"id":"85013764057","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5331223","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28230048","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-5d7133c9-1b99-4cfe-9d0c-f10cbe724730"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A4A966EB96B1A1067A670849895A39FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/ncomms14534.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms14534","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Plant Molecular Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"the james hutton institute","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The James Hutton Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yasuyuki","key":"kawaharadapau","last":"Kawaharada","locid":"e0a9708b-7fe6-4940-acb0-f90a573e423d","name":"Kawaharada, Yasuyuki","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette W","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c3db9e3-0fde-4bb4-b56f-f212474b398a","name":"Nielsen, Mette Wibroe","name_org":"Nielsen, Mette W","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"kellypau","last":"Kelly","locid":"9cfb1d00-d015-4f01-9b9c-3df2ec6a968d","name":"Kelly, Simon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Euan K","key":"jamespau","last":"James","name":"James, Euan K","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper Røjkjær","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"b2286f54-e599-4401-93da-c1e6a7681c2f","name":"Andersen, Kasper Røjkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-4415-8067","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sheena R","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"9eafa274-b431-4cef-91fb-1c5233d184cd","name":"Rasmussen, Sheena Ricafranca","name_org":"Rasmussen, Sheena R","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Winnie","key":"füchtbauerpau","last":"Füchtbauer","locid":"8cfc7344-cb59-42f3-8482-74346ec21fa1","name":"Füchtbauer, Winnie Sophie","name_org":"Füchtbauer, Winnie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene H","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"0c3d64a2-4dc9-45c7-9579-cbb86a7d9e1a","name":"Madsen, Lene Heegaard","name_org":"Madsen, Lene H","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne B","key":"heckmannpau","last":"Heckmann","locid":"ed197727-bb80-496d-b2fe-90fb276815f5","name":"Heckmann, Anne Birgitte","name_org":"Heckmann, Anne B","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simona","key":"radutoiupau","last":"Radutoiu","locid":"ab9305e9-16d3-4c5e-bb7b-9bcefa37d5a5","name":"Radutoiu, Simona","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"stougaardpau","last":"Stougaard","locid":"f18b1608-17eb-4ff2-92d9-251f14f48a28","name":"Stougaard, Jens","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28230048"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms14534","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"14534","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85013764057"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5d7133c9-1b99-4cfe-9d0c-f10cbe724730"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Differential regulation of the Epr3 receptor coordinates membrane-restricted rhizobial colonization of root nodule primordia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-182646","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Digital devices play an important role in medical treatment and will in the future play a larger role in connection to cures of health-related issues. Traditionally medicine has been tested by clinical double blind, randomized trials to document the efficacy and safety profile. When it comes to the use of digital devices in treatments the protocols from the field of medicine is adopted. The question is whether or not this evidence based approach is useful when dealing with digital devices and whether the understanding of the efficiency of a treatment can be obtained without also looking at usability and lifestyle issues. Based on a case study of epilepsy, a literature study of protocols for investigating treatments using digital medical devices, the set-up of studies, the design of a current protocol for clinical trials, and finally preliminary results, we discuss if clinical trials have to include usability studies to determine if a treatment is effective.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Christensen, Lars Rune","Sabers, Anne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383454"],"event":{"acronym":"OzCHI","title":"Conference of the Australian Computer-Human Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clinical trial","Evidence Based Medicine","Lifestyle issues","Medical devise","Usability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"do we have to include hci issues in clinical trials of medical devices a discussion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82435103/p352_nielsen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383454","identifier":[{"id":"85044224245","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-94c9f649-64da-4c13-824b-83662c3aec88"],"keyword":["Clinical Trial","Evidence-based medicine","Lifestyle issues","Medical devise","usability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4D81C3DFF6A30D0D8F14FF904475BD44"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82435103/p352_nielsen.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"saberspau","last":"Sabers","name":"Sabers, Anne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3152771.3156135","eisbn":["9781450353793"],"pages":"352-355","place":"Brisbane","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"November 28-December 1, 2017, Brisbane, QLD, Australia","title":"OzCHI '17, Proceedings of the 29th Australian Conference on Computer-Human Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044224245"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-94c9f649-64da-4c13-824b-83662c3aec88"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Do we have to Include HCI Issues in Clinical Trials of Medical Devices? : – A Discussion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383454","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Inhibitors of molecular chaperones and the ubiquitin-proteasome system have already been clinically implemented to counter certain cancers, including multiple myeloma and mantle cell lymphoma. The efficacy of this treatment relies on genomic alterations in cancer cells causing a proteostatic imbalance, which makes them more dependent on protein quality control (PQC) mechanisms than normal cells. Accordingly, blocking PQC, e.g. by proteasome inhibitors, may cause a lethal proteotoxic crisis in cancer cells, while leaving normal cells unaffected. Evidence, however, suggests that the PQC system operates by following a better-safe-than-sorry principle and is thus prone to target proteins that are only slightly structurally perturbed, but still functional. Accordingly, implementing PQC inhibitors may also, through an entirely different mechanism, hold potential for other cancers. Several inherited cancer susceptibility syndromes, such as Lynch syndrome and von Hippel-Lindau disease, are caused by missense mutations in tumor suppressor genes, and in some cases, the resulting amino acid substitutions in the encoded proteins cause the cellular PQC system to target them for degradation, although they may still retain function. As a consequence of this over-meticulous PQC mechanism, the cell may end up with an insufficient amount of the abnormal, but functional, protein, which in turn leads to a loss-of-function phenotype and manifestation of the disease. Increasing the amounts of such proteins by stabilizing with chemical chaperones, or by targeting molecular chaperones or the ubiquitin-proteasome system, may thus avert or delay the disease onset. Here, we review the potential of targeting the PQC system in hereditary cancer susceptibility syndromes.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kampmeyer, Caroline","Nielsen, Sofie V.","Clausen, Lene","Stein, Amelie","Gerdes, Anne-Marie","Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","Hartmann-Petersen, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-412419"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blocking protein quality control to counter hereditary cancers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85028772568&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-412419","identifier":[{"id":"85028772568","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28779490","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1fdb47aa-a6c6-4642-a406-4f42b6f4a05e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D4722F10E436551BDE47515AC16221FB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Biomolecular Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline","key":"kampmeyerpau","last":"Kampmeyer","locid":"27b771d4-c06b-433d-8c56-2aa43dc74cf5","name":"Kampmeyer, Caroline","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sofie V.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Sofie V.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"60754bbd-4d35-4fc1-a020-21185a472880","name":"Clausen, Lene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Amelie","key":"steinpau","last":"Stein","locid":"883406ce-8afb-4747-a574-9c46516128db","name":"Stein, Amelie","orcid":"0000-0002-5862-1681","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne-Marie Axø","key":"gerdespau","last":"Gerdes","locid":"3a494e19-760a-4865-a142-60a74f697013","name":"Gerdes, Anne-Marie","name_org":"Gerdes, Anne-Marie Axø","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kresten","key":"lindorfflarsenpau","last":"Lindorff-Larsen","locid":"be20a4d8-92c4-44b9-9dfb-b6ad6471a58c","name":"Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","orcid":"0000-0002-4750-6039","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"hartmannpetersenpau","last":"Hartmann-Petersen","locid":"fea900ee-b167-45e9-af2c-00038ff06862","name":"Hartmann-Petersen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-7791","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28779490"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/gcc.22487","issn":["10452257","10982264"],"issn_org":["10452257"],"issue":"12","journal":"Genes, Chromosomes & Cancer","pages":"823-831","status":"p","title":"Genes, Chromosomes & Cancer","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85028772568"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1fdb47aa-a6c6-4642-a406-4f42b6f4a05e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Blocking protein quality control to counter hereditary cancers","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-412419","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":17,"contributors":["Villari, C.","Dowkiw, A.","Enderle, R.","Ghasemkhani, M.","Kirisits, T.","Kjær, Erik Dahl","Marciulyniene, D.","McKinney, Lea Vig","Metzler, B.","Munoz, F.","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Pliura, A.","Stener, L. G.","Suchockas, V.","Rodriguez-Saona, L.","Bonello, P.","Cleary, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-417986"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of ft ir for rapid phenotyping of european ash resistance levels to ash dieback","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-417986","identifier":[{"id":"000423236200341","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-2917cfe3-86e2-4074-8c1d-4fbb851aeae3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DA5CBC0A4D3C433FC3B2720B9297D685"],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"C.","key":"villaripau","last":"Villari","name":"Villari, C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"A.","key":"dowkiwpau","last":"Dowkiw","name":"Dowkiw, A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"R.","key":"enderlepau","last":"Enderle","name":"Enderle, R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M.","key":"ghasemkhanipau","last":"Ghasemkhani","name":"Ghasemkhani, M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"T.","key":"kirisitspau","last":"Kirisits","name":"Kirisits, T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"E.","ke