A Dermatology","volume":"153"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029534056"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-40a9f7d1-1726-422b-95e9-0760366106cd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The follicular skin microbiome in patients with hidradenitis suppurativa and healthy controls","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-432123","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The gut microbiota is believed to affect a wide variety of mental disorders, including depression. The hypothesis involves bacterial signalling to the host through metabolic, endocrinal, immunologic and neuronal pathways. Few studies of patients with depression have shown altered microbiota profiles and increased levels of systemic endotoxin, which can be detected by leucocytes and result in expression of cytokines. Studies performed so far have lacked statistical power and provide no causal explanation for the gut-brain hypothesis. Further research into the matter is certainly warranted.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Knudsen, Julie Kristine","Jensen, Zenia Funch","Christensen, Alice Højer","Günther, Stig","Nielsen, Lene Nørby","Deutscher, Peter","Arnfred, Sidse"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-442408"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gut microbiota and depressive symptoms","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-442408","identifier":[{"id":"85060128220","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29208194","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-51fdd990-627d-4aff-b83e-d467fdf8efe6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-DAF72FCD594C000FF5EF1BB1DF0A66F6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Julie Kristine","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Julie Kristine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zenia Funch","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Zenia Funch","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alice Højer","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Alice Højer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stig","key":"güntherpau","last":"Günther","name":"Günther, Stig","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Nørby","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene Nørby","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"deutscherpau","last":"Deutscher","name":"Deutscher, Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sidse","key":"arnfredpau","last":"Arnfred","locid":"e855bb74-5684-469e-a4f1-8243dc8ae1d6","name":"Arnfred, Sidse","orcid":"0000-0001-5375-4226","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29208194"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"47","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"179"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-51fdd990-627d-4aff-b83e-d467fdf8efe6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gut microbiota and depressive symptoms","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-442408","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The aim of the TAILOR trial is to investigate the effect of closely monitored tapering/discontinuation versus maintenance therapy with antipsychotic medication in patients with newly diagnosed schizophrenia or persistent delusional disorder and with minimum 3 months' remission of psychotic symptoms. METHODS AND DESIGN: Two hundred and fifty patients will be included from the psychiatric early intervention program, OPUS, in two regions in Denmark. Inclusion criteria are: ICD-10 diagnoses schizophrenia (F20, except F20.6) or persistent delusional disorder (F22), minimum 3 months' remission of psychotic symptoms and in treatment with antipsychotic medication (except clozapine). The patients will be randomized to maintenance therapy or tapering/discontinuation with antipsychotic medication in a 1-year intervention. The tapering/discontinuation group will be using a smartphone application to monitor early warning signs of psychotic relapse. Patients will be assessed at baseline, 1-, 2- and 5-year follow-up regarding psychotic and negative symptoms, side-effects of antipsychotic medication, social functioning, cognitive functioning, perceived health status, patient satisfaction, substance and alcohol use, sexual functioning and quality of life. The primary outcome will be remission of psychotic symptoms and no antipsychotic medication after 1 year. Secondary outcome measures will include: co-occurrence of remission of psychotic symptoms and 0-1-mg haloperidol equivalents of antipsychotic medication after 1-year intervention; antipsychotic dose; antipsychotic side effects; negative symptoms; social functioning; cognitive functioning; and patient satisfaction. Exploratory outcomes will include remission, clinical recovery, substance and alcohol use, sexual functioning, quality of life, self-beliefs of coping and user experience of support from health workers. Safety measures will include death, admissions to psychiatric hospital, severe self-harm and psychotic relapses. DISCUSSION: The TAILOR trial will contribute knowledge about the effect of tapering/discontinuation of antipsychotic medication in the early phases of schizophrenia and related disorders and the results may guide future clinical treatment regimens of antipsychotic treatment. TRIAL REGISTRATION: EU Clinical Trials Register - EudraCT number: 2016-000565-23 . Registered on 5 February 2016.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Stürup, Anne Emilie","Jensen, Heidi Dorthe","Dolmer, Signe","Birk, Merete","Albert, Nikolai","Nielsen, Mai","Hjorthøj, Carsten","Eplov, Lene","Ebdrup, Bjørn H","Mors, Ole","Nordentoft, Merete"],"cuid":["S02-090.82-666319"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tailor tapered discontinuation versus maintenance therapy of antipsychotic medication in patients with newly diagnosed schizophrenia or persistent delusional disorder in remission of psychotic symptoms study protocol for a randomized clinical trial","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-017-2172-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.82-666319","identifier":[{"id":"85030152255","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5622425","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28962668","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-79304bc5-b4bc-4022-a7bf-eb9467bc58eb","ku-5a39a31a-e0a2-45c6-82fa-b95987a5fe07"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CD54E17A0804B0A812C223C6660FCAAC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis