{"abstract":"Ensuring ethical value exchange is moving to the forefront of the global challenges that HCI will have to address in the coming years In this position paper, we argue that applying a context-sensitive, sociotechnical approach to HCI can help meet the challenge. The background is that the life of marginalized people in contemporary society is challenging and uncertain. The marginalized can face health and cognitive issues as well as a lack of stability of social structures such as family, work and social inclusion. Three questions are of concern when innovating together with people ‘at the margins’: how can we describe users without attempting to stereotype badly, what sociotechnical HCI methods fit the local societal context, and how to make the design sustainable in face of current planetary challenges (e.g., climate change)? We adapt the sociotechnical HCI approach called human work interaction design (HWID) to meet the challenges of designing for ethical value exchange. We present three cases of service design, and suggest how to add a fourth similar case using the HWID approach during the INTERACT ‘field trip plus workshop’. We conclude that applying a context sensitive sociotechnical HCI framework implies that both the backend and frontend of service design and product innovations should be executed and valorized from with the local context.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Abdelnour-Nocera, José","Nielsen, Lene","Christensen, Lars Rune","Clemmensen, Torkil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-280450"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-29","place":"Mumbai, in","start":"2017-09-25","title":"The 16th IFIP TC13 International Conference on Human–Computer Interaction","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of West London"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socio technical hci for ethical value exchange a case of service design and innovation at the margins in resource constrained environments","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/82305437/INTERACT_2017_Adjunct_FINAL_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-280450","ids":["cbs-3539ea27-45a9-45ec-a1ec-bb5799cf9a36"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2B05578A9DE5C4D584F721ADCCED6A4C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/82305437/INTERACT_2017_Adjunct_FINAL_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of west london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of West London","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"José","key":"abdelnournocerapau","last":"Abdelnour-Nocera","name":"Abdelnour-Noc