{"abstract":"We develop a methodology for persona generation using real time social media data for the distribution of products via online platforms. From a large social media account containing more than 30 million interactions from users from 181 countries engaging with more than 4,200 digital products produced by a global media corporation, we demonstrate that our methodology can first identify both distinct and impactful user segments and then create persona descriptions by automatically adding pertinent features, such as names, photos, and personal attributes. We validate our approach by implementing the methodology into an actual working system that leverages large scale online user data for generation of persona descriptions. We present the overall methodological approach, data analysis process, and system development. Findings show this method can develop believable personas representing real groups of people using real-time online user data. Results have implications for those distributing products via online platforms.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jung, Soon-Gyo","An, Jisun","Kwak, Haewoon","Ahmad, Moeed","Nielsen, Lene","Jansen, Bernard J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383599"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","end":"2017-05-11","place":"Denver, Colorado, us","start":"2017-05-06","title":"ACM CHI2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Qatar"],"glorg":["Al Jazeera Media Network","All Global Affiliations","Qatar Computing Research institute"],"keyword":["Personas","User Analytics","User Experience Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"persona generation from aggregated social media data","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82391190/jansen_personas_chi2017LBR.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383599","identifier":[{"id":"85019559311","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a026a867-0b71-405e-9366-a6ad713e157d"],"keyword":["Personas","User Analytics","User Experience Research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DE4AC414917100DFC0249EDCE88F7777"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82391190/jansen_personas_chi2017LBR.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"qa","key":"qatar computing research institute","loc":["Qatar","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Qatar Computing Research institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"qa","key":"al jazeera media network","loc":["Qatar","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Al Jazeera Media Network","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Soon-Gyo","key":"jungpau","last":"Jung","name":"Jung, Soon-Gyo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jisun","key":"anpau","last":"An","name":"An, Jisun","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Haewoon","key":"kwakpau","last":"Kwak","name":"Kwak, Haewoon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Moeed","key":"ahmadpau","last":"Ahmad","name":"Ahmad, Moeed","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernard J.","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","name":"Jansen, Bernard J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3027063.3053120","eisbn":["9781450346566"],"pages":"1748-1755","place":"Denver, Colorado","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 CHI Conference Extended Abstracts on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019559311"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a026a867-0b71-405e-9366-a6ad713e157d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Persona Generation from Aggregated Social Media Data","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383599","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND & AIMS: Inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) may increase risk of small bowel cancer (SBC). However, little is known of the characteristics and features of IBD-SBC, due to a low number of cases worldwide. We performed a population-based study of IBD and SBC to calculate risk and increase our understanding of clinical characteristics and histopathological and molecular features. METHODS: The study population consisted of all individuals aged 16 years or older living in Denmark during 1978-2010. Through linkage between national registers and subsequent scrutiny of medical records and pathology descriptions, we identified 40 cases of IBD-SBC. Risk was calculated by standardized incidence ratio (SIR) (observed/expected); patient characteristics were derived from medical files, and surgery specimens were obtained from hospitals nationwide for histopathological and molecular analyses. RESULTS: During 241,620 person-years of follow-up, 23 patients with Crohn's disease developed small bowel adenocarcinoma (SIR, 14.38; 95% confidence interval, 8.78-22.20) and 9 developed neuroendocrine tumors (SIR, 6.83; 95% confidence interval, 3.13-12.97). No significantly increased risk of SBC was found among patients with ulcerative colitis. Most patients with SBC had moderate-to-severe Crohn's disease with small bowel and upper gastrointestinal involvement. Assessment of surgical specimens of small bowel adenocarcinomas revealed a clear transition from inflammation to dysplasia and cancer, whereas no tumors had evidence of microsatellite instability. CONCLUSIONS: In a population-based study of patients in Denmark with IBD and SBC, we found risk of adenocarcinomas and neuroendocrine tumors to be increased among persons with Crohn's disease. Most patients with IBD-SBC had extensive IBD of moderate-to-severe activity. Adenocarcinomas appeared to develop via an inflammation-dysplasia-carcinoma pathway, but differed from IBD-related colorectal adenocarcinomas in their molecular features.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bojesen, Rasmus Dahlin","Riis, Lene Buhl","Høgdall, Estrid","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Jess, Tine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-411119"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inflammatory bowel disease and small bowel cancer risk clinical characteristics and histopathology a population based study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-411119","identifier":[{"id":"85033483382","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28694132","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1db465f4-7580-4cf6-8ebe-1960f55540ec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-231AE48C18976438812AE44FAA6FD187"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus Dahlin","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","name":"Bojesen, Rasmus Dahlin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Buhl","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Estrid","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","locid":"a48f77b8-ee6