"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Gunnleivsdóttir","key":"hansenmariagunnleivsdóttirpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Maria Gunnleivsdóttir","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Maria Gunnleivsdottir","key":"hansenmariagunnleivsdottirpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Maria Gunnleivsdottir","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771562699"],"pages":"890","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Aarhus University","repno":"Scientific Report from DCE – Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","series":"Scientific Report from DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-55a45681-9dbe-491c-9da8-d7e88886767e","ku-8895783a-4437-44fa-8048-50c27de32ee5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Denmark's National Inventory Report 2017 : Emission Inventories 1990-2015 - Submitted under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change and the Kyoto Protocol","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.67-018900","year":"2017","yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In immunocompromised patients with acute hypoxemic respiratory failure (ARF), initial management aims primarily to avoid invasive mechanical ventilation (IMV). METHODS: To assess the impact of initial management on IMV and mortality rates, we performed a multinational observational prospective cohort study in 16 countries (68 centers). RESULTS: A total of 1611 patients were enrolled (hematological malignancies 51.9%, solid tumors 35.2%, systemic diseases 17.3%, and solid organ transplantation 8.8%). The main ARF etiologies were bacterial (29.5%), viral (15.4%), and fungal infections (14.7%), or undetermined (13.2%). On admission, 915 (56.8%) patients were not intubated. They received standard oxygen (N = 496, 53.9%), high-flow oxygen (HFNC, N = 187, 20.3%), noninvasive ventilation (NIV, N = 153, 17.2%), and NIV + HFNC (N = 79, 8.6%). Factors associated with IMV included age (hazard ratio = 0.92/year, 95% CI 0.86-0.99), day-1 SOFA (1.09/point, 1.06-1.13), day-1 PaO2/FiO2 (1.47, 1.05-2.07), ARF etiology (Pneumocystis jirovecii pneumonia (2.11, 1.42-3.14), invasive pulmonary aspergillosis (1.85, 1.21-2.85), and undetermined cause (1.46, 1.09-1.98). After propensity score matching, HFNC, but not NIV, had an effect on IMV rate (HR = 0.77, 95% CI 0.59-1.00, p = 0.05). ICU, hospital, and day-90 mortality rates were 32.4, 44.1, and 56.4%, respectively. Factors independently associated with hospital mortality included age (odds ratio = 1.18/year, 1.09-1.27), direct admission to the ICU (0.69, 0.54-0.87), day-1 SOFA excluding respiratory score (1.12/point, 1.08-1.16), PaO2/FiO2 < 100 (1.60, 1.03-2.48), and undetermined ARF etiology (1.43, 1.04-1.97). Initial oxygenation strategy did not affect mortality; however, IMV was associated with mortality, the odds ratio depending on IMV conditions: NIV + HFNC failure (2.31, 1.09-4.91), first-line IMV (2.55, 1.94-3.29), NIV failure (3.65, 2.05-6.53), standard oxygen failure (4.16, 2.91-5.93), and HFNC failure (5.54, 3.27-9.38). CONCLUSION: HFNC has an effect on intubation but not on mortality rates. Failure to identify ARF etiology is associated with higher rates of both intubation and mortality. This suggests that in addition to selecting the appropriate oxygenation device, clinicians should strive to identify the etiology of ARF.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Azoulay, Elie","Pickkers, Peter","Soares, Marcio","Perner, Anders","Rello, Jordi","Bauer, Philippe R","van de Louw, Andry","Hemelaar, Pleun","Lemiale, Virginie","Taccone, Fabio Silvio","Martin Loeches, Ignacio","Meyhoff, Tine Sylvest","Salluh, Jorge","Schellongowski, Peter","Rusinova, Katerina","Terzi, Nicolas","Mehta, Sangeeta","Antonelli, Massimo","Kouatchet, Achille","Barratt-Due, Andreas","Valkonen, Miia","Landburg, Precious Pearl","Bruneel, Fabrice","Bukan, Ramin Brandt","Pène, Frédéric","Metaxa, Victoria","Moreau, Anne Sophie","Souppart, Virginie","Burghi, Gaston","Girault, Christophe","Silva, Ulysses V A","Montini, Luca","Barbier, François","Nielsen, Lene B","Gaborit, Benjamin","Mokart, Djamel","Chevret, Sylvie"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-043044"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["Efraim investigators and the Nine-I study group"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Brazil","Canada","Czechia","Finland","France","Ireland","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Angers University Hospital","Assistance Publique Hôpitaux de Paris","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Barretos Cancer Hospital","Catholic University of the Sacred Heart","Charles University","D’Or Institute for Research and Education","General university hospital in Prague","Helsinki University Hospital","Institut National de la Sante et de la Recherche Medicale (INSERM)","King's College Hospi