{"abstract":"Valid assessments of physical activity (PA) and cardiorespiratory fitness (CRF) is essential in epidemiological studies to define dose-response relationship for e.g. formulating thorough recommendations of an appropriate pattern of PA to maintain good health. The aim of this study was to validate the Danish step test, the physical activity questionnaire Active-Q and self-rated fitness against directly measured maximal oxygen uptake (VO2 max). A population based subsample (n=125) was included from the 'Diet, Cancer and Health - Next Generations' (DCH-NG) cohort which is under establishment. Validity coefficients, which express the correlation between measured and 'true' exposure, were calculated and misclassification across categories was evaluated. The validity of the Danish step test was moderate (women: r=0.66, and men: r=0.56), however, men were systematically underestimated (43% misclassification). When validating the questionnaire-derived measures of PA, leisure time physical activity was not correlated with VO2 max. Positive correlations were found for sports overall, but these were only significant for men: total hours per week of sports (r=0.26), MET-hours per week of sports (r=0.28) and vigorous sports (0.28) alone were positively correlated with VO2 max. Finally, the percentage of misclassification was low for self-rated fitness (women: 9% and men: 13%). Thus, self-rated fitness was found to be a superior method to the Danish step test, as well as being less cost prohibitive and more practical than the VO2 max method. Finally, even if correlations were low, they support the potential for questionnaire outcomes, particularly sports, vigorous sports and self-rated fitness to be used to estimate CRF. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lerche, Lene","Olsen, Anja","Petersen, Kristina Elin Nielsen","Rostgaard-Hansen, Agnetha Linn","Dragsted, Lars Ove","Nordsborg, Nikolai Baastrup","Tjønneland, Anne","Halkjær, Jytte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-398709"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cardiorespiratory fitness","Epidemiology","Fitness test","Maximal oxygen uptake","Self reported physical activity","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validity of physical activity and cardiorespiratory fitness in the danish cohort diet cancer and health next generations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-398709","identifier":[{"id":"28267247","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85017535048","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-08be6d8e-2993-405b-8115-f965a06a8aa3"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Fitness test","Maximal oxygen uptake","Self-reported physical activity","Validation","cardiorespiratory fitness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-46D000738DFAEC8CD466CD4D4ACAB892"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"lerchepau","last":"Lerche","name":"Lerche, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anja","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Anja","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina Elin Nielsen","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Kristina Elin Nielsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Agnetha Linn","key":"rostgaardhansenpau","last":"Rostgaard-Hansen","name":"Rostgaard-Hansen, Agnetha Linn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars Ove","key":"dragstedpau","last":"Dragsted","locid":"d24a722b-d957-4276-a1ee-8f0144cb1ab9","name":"Dragsted, Lars Ove","orcid":"0000-0003-0609-6317","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nikolai Baastrup","key":"nordsborgpau","last":"Nordsborg","locid":"375f99fd-c332-42de-a495-27cf33762d27","name":"Nordsborg, Nikolai Baastrup","orcid":"0000-0001-7077-9265","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"tjønnelandpau","last":"Tjønneland","name":"Tjønneland, Anne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jytte","key":"halkjærpau","last":"Halkjær","name":"Halkjær, Jytte","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28267247"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/sms.12873","issn":["09057188","16000838"],"issn_org":["09057188"],"issue":"12","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","pages":"1864-1872","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017535048"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-08be6d8e-2993-405b-8115-f965a06a8aa3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Validity of physical activity and cardiorespiratory fitness in the Danish cohort 'Diet, Cancer and Health - Next Generations'","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-398709","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In Europe, common ash (Fraxinus excelsior) is being decimated because of the invasive fungus Hymenoscyphus fraxineus. In its native range in Asia this ascomycete is considered a harmless leaf associate of F. mandshurica and F. chinensis subsp. rhynchophylla. Field observations from Europe suggest that there is species-specific variation in disease susceptibility among European and North American Fraxinus species, but a wider comparison at the genus level has been missing so far. We assessed disease symptoms and pathogen apothecium development in 17 Fraxinus species from Asia, Europe and North America exposed to high infection pressure in a Danish arboretum. We also tested their susceptibility to pathogen infection through controlled stem and leaf inoculations and subsequently assessed the level of pathogen DNA by a qPCR assay. The results suggested the presence of a phylogenetic signal in disease susceptibility where closely related Asian, European and North American species in section Fraxinus had relatively high levels of H. fraxineus DNA in the leaves and supported high production of apothecia. Leaves from some North American species also contained relatively high levels of H. fraxineus DNA, supported moderate production of apothecia and developed lesions—stating the need to avoid introduction of H. fraxineus to North America.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","McKinney, Lea Vig","Hietala, Ari M.","Kjær, Erik Dahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-461220"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian Institute of Bioeconomy Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the susceptibility of asian european and north american em fraxinus em species to the ash dieback pathogen em hymenoscyphus fraxineus em reflects their phylogenetic history","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10342-016-1009-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-461220","identifier":[{"id":"84994796724","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7177db14-1705-4500-b5f6-9f845e4944b2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9EA0240A8D5D9E6A93B19CE115293C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/203414646/Nielsen2017_Article_TheSusceptibilityOfAsianEurope.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10342-016-1009-0","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"norwegian institute of bioeconomy research","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian Institute of Bioeconomy Research","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lea Vig","key":"mckinneypau","last":"McKinney","locid":"060df27a-59d3-4457-81a2-185cca16ae68","name":"McKinney, Lea Vig","orcid":"0000-0001-6601-4614","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ari M.","key":"hietalapau","last":"Hietala","name":"Hietala, Ari M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10342-016-1009-0","issn":["16124669","16124677"],"issn_org":["16124669"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Journal of Forest Research","pages":"59-73","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Forest Research","volume":"136"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994796724"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7177db14-1705-4500-b5f6-9f845e4944b2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The susceptibility of Asian, European and North American <em>Fraxinus</em> species to the ash dieback pathogen <em>Hymenoscyphus fraxineus</em> reflects their phylogenetic history","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-461220","year":"2017","yearsub":"2016"}
