,{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L. B.","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","locid":"532c69b5-512e-421d-8981-88829f8a74ab","name":"Bastrup, Lene","name_org":"Jorgensen, L. B.","orcid":"0000-0001-7873-6139","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M. T.","key":"hoybyepau","last":"Hoybye","locid":"8a655916-655e-4727-87a7-df4800aaeff5","name":"Høybye, Mette Terp","name_org":"Hoybye, M. T.","orcid":"0000-0001-6914-2697","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["10705503","15327558"],"issn_org":["10705503"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"International Journal of Behavioral Medicine","paperid":"O217","publisher":"Routledge Worlds","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Behavioral Medicine","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8d3b59c0-a4f1-4d63-82c1-06751402806c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"DOES INFORMATION BECOME ACTUAL KNOWLEDGE IN SURGICAL SPINE PATIENTS? A QUALITATIVE STUDY","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-209875","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Baggrund: Det er i løbet af det sidste årti blevet klart, at den naturlige bakterieflora i tarmen (kaldet tarmens mikrobiota) har meget stor betydning for menneskers generelle sundhedstilstand. Således er tarmmikrobiotaens sammensætning og aktivitet blevet koblet til en række vestlige livstilssygdomme som fx metabolisk syndrom. Restkoncentrationer af pesticider i fødevarer kan påvirke mikrobiota da flere pesticider, heriblandt glyphosat, er kendetegnet ved også at besidde antimikrobielle egenskaber. I forbindelse med risikovurdering af pesticider og fastlæggelse af grænseværdier for indtag er mikrobielle påvirkninger med eventuelt negative langsigtede konsekvenser stort set ikke belyst. Formål: At undersøge påvirkningen og minimums effekt koncentrationen (MEC) af pesticidet glyphosat, samt de hjælpestoffer (adjuvanter), der er til stede i det kommercielle produkt Roundup® på tarmmikrobiotaens sammensætning og funktion. Hypoteser: 1. Glyphosat påvirker forskellige bakteriegrupper i menneskets tarm forskelligt, og har dermed effekt på bakteriesamfundets (tarmmikrobiotaens) overordnede sammensætning og funktion. 2. Det kommercielle produkt Roundup® påvirker mikroorganismer ved lavere koncentrationer end det rene aktive stof på grund af tilsatte hjælpestoffer (adjuvanter). 3. Det er muligt ved brug af in vitro og in vivo modeller at bestemme minimums effekt koncentrationen (MEC) af glyphosat, og dermed at forudsige hvilke koncentrationer, der er biologisk relevante i tarmen. 4. Tarmmikrobiotaen bidrager til omsætningen og nedbrydningen af glyphosat. Resultater: Tidligere studier har vist at forskellige bakteriearter har forskellig MIC værdier overfor glyphosat og har indikeret at gavnlige bakterier i tarmen har lavere MIC-værdier end potentielt patogene bakterier af slægten Clostridium og Salmonella (Shehata et al. 2012). I vores studier har vi brugt samme vækstmedium og -betingelser for alle de undersøgte bakterier og vi finder generelt lav variation i MIC-værdier mellem de forskellige bakteriegrupper (Tabel 1). Da glyphosat hæmmer dannelsen af aromatiske aminosyrer er det muligt at tilstrækkelige niveauer af disse i vækstmediet nedsætter effekten af glyphosat væsentligt. Dette vil blive undersøgt nærmere ved de fremtidige in vitro dyrkningsforsøg.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Nørby","Bohse Hendriksen, Niels","Bay Gosewinkel, Ulrich","Licht, Tine Rask","Bahl, Martin Iain"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-319232"],"event":{"end":"2016-01-29","place":"Vejle, dk","start":"2016-01-28","title":"Miljøstyrelsens Bekæmpelsesmiddelforskningskonference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tarmmikrobiota som følsom indikator for biologisk relevante restkoncentrationer af kemiske pesticider i fødevarer eksemplificeret ved glyphosat roundup","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/120984737/Poster_MST_Bek_mpelsesmiddelforskningskonference_2016.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-319232","ids":["dtu-31598543-14de-46a9-97db-8bf5331bc202"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-285A65486EAEDF86D54CA75BBE67A38B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/120984737/Poster_MST_Bek_mpelsesmiddelforskningskonference_2016.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Gut Microbiology and Immunology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Nørby","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d4e59d1c-9588-4f40-b090-7419ff27d463","name":"Nielsen, Lene Nørby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"bohsehendriksenpau","last":"Bohse Hendriksen","name":"Bohse Hendriksen, Niels","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrich","key":"baygosewinkelpau","last":"Bay Gosewinkel","name":"Bay Gosewinkel, Ulrich","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tine Rask","key":"lichtpau","last":"Licht","locid":"b5270ea1-1dc7-4db8-8644-c7ef75331664","name":"Licht, Tine Rask","orcid":"0000-0002-6399-9574","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Iain","key":"bahlpau","last":"Bahl","locid":"6e2651b2-1c65-49a5-81c3-9065190c95e2","name":"Bahl, Martin Iain","orcid":"0000-0003-1579-8038","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-31598543-14de-46a9-97db-8bf5331bc202"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Tarmmikrobiota som følsom indikator for biologisk relevante restkoncentrationer af kemiske pesticider i fødevarer eksemplificeret ved glyphosat (Roundup®)","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-319232","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Emerging diseases often originate from host shifts of introduced pests or pathogens. Genetic resistance of the host to such diseases might be limited or absent due to the lack of coevolutionary history. We review six examples of major disease outbreaks on native tree species caused by different introduced pests and pathogens that led to large ecological and economical losses. In all six cases, high tree mortality was observed in natural populations with some surviving individuals exhibiting varying levels of genetic resistance. The abundance and distribution of resistant individuals and the heritability of resistance traits varies substantially among the cases. While chestnut blight wilt combined with ink disease has virtually eliminated mature Castanea dentata trees from North America, other severe emerging diseases, such as the ash dieback, have left many surviving trees and genetic variation in resistance to such diseases has been documented. We argue that the evolutionary potential of tree species to respond to new emerging diseases should not be underestimated. However, the risk of increased levels of inbreeding and loss of genetic diversity caused by low population sizes is a major concern. Maintenance of broad genetic diversity is an important issue in conservation and forestry management. We expect that future research targeting the genetic background of biotic resistance towards emerging diseases and the role of endophytic communities in protecting trees will facilitate the informed and science-based guidance required to manage and maintain forests with high resilience. International cooperation on limiting disease spread and the provision of early invasive pest or pathogen detection systems are essential.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Budde, Katharina Birgit","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Ravn, Hans Peter","Kjær, Erik Dahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-428623"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the natural evolutionary potential of tree populations to cope with newly introduced pests and pathogens lessons learned from forest health catastrophes in recent decades","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/168294591/Budde_et_al_2016_acceptedMS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-428623","identifier":[{"id":"84980451954","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3afe7156-5137-4ff8-942f-c6e76877265a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8E478A3EC0BC4033A64BF0F8B0DB4B3E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/168294591/Budde_et_al_2016_acceptedMS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Katharina Birgit","key":"buddepau","last":"Budde","locid":"c7613d2d-1b13-440f-a6cf-4763c626ba9e","name":"Budde, Katharina Birgit","orcid":"0000-0002-5361-2815","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans Peter","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"525f4a95-93fc-4689-9fd4-42a507bf76d6","name":"Ravn, Hans Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s40725-016-0029-9","issn":["21986436"],"issue":"1","journal":"Current Forestry Reports","pages":"18-29","status":"p","title":"Current Forestry Reports","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84980451954"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3afe7156-5137-4ff8-942f-c6e76877265a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Natural Evolutionary Potential of Tree Populations to Cope with Newly Introduced Pests and Pathogens : Lessons Learned From Forest Health Catastrophes in Recent Decades","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-428623","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Childhood asthma is a global problem affecting the respiratory health of children. Physical activity (PA) plays a role in the relationship between asthma and respiratory health. We hypothesized that a low level of PA would be associated with asthma in children and adolescents. The objectives of our study were to (1) summarize the evidence available on associations between PA and asthma prevalence in children and adolescents and (2) assess the role of PA in new-onset or incident asthma among children and adolescents. METHODS: We searched Medline, the Cochrane Library, and Embase and extracted data from original articles that met the inclusion criteria. Summary odds ratios (ORs) and confidence intervals (CIs) were used to express the results of the meta-analysis (forest plot). We explored heterogeneity using funnel plots and the Graphic Appraisal Tool for Epidemiology (GATE). RESULTS: We retrieved 1,571 titles and selected 11 articles describing three cohort and eight cross-sectional studies for inclusion. A meta-analysis of the cohort studies revealed a risk of new-onset asthma in children with low PA (OR [95 % CI] 1.32 [0.95; 1.84] [random effects] and 1.35 [1.13; 1.62] [fixed effects]). Three cross-sectional studies identified significant positive associations between childhood asthma or asthma symptoms and low PA. CONCLUSIONS: Children and adolescents with low PA levels had an increased risk of new-onset asthma, and some had a higher risk of current asthma/or wheezing; however, there was some heterogeneity among the studies. This review reveals a critical need for future longitudinal assessments of low PA, its mechanisms, and its implications for incident asthma in children. The systematic review was prospectively registered at PROSPERO (registration number: CRD42014013761; available at: http://www.crd.york.ac.uk/PROSPERO [accessed: 24 March 2016]).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lochte, Lene","Nielsen, Kim G.","Petersen, Poul Erik","Platts-Mills, Thomas A E"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-431991"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"childhood asthma and physical activity a systematic review with meta analysis and graphic appraisal tool for epidemiology assessment","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12887-016-0571-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-431991","identifier":[{"id":"85008402803","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27091126","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4836150","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-407673bb-abbb-43fc-88fe-e0881c0ba81a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9DA8AE6F4BAA48650FB29BF6F505C4E2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/170192693/art_3A10.1186_2Fs12887_016_0571_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12887-016-0571-4","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Section 01 - Prosthetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"lochtepau","last":"Lochte","locid":"93ba9aa9-2612-4a57-9233-69ff6b2ee4c4","name":"Lochte, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-4955-1869","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim G","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"eabd2b94-b01a-4243-bb5a-b6dd696edd6a","name":"Nielsen, Kim G.","name_org":"Nielsen, Kim G","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Poul Erik","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"7d95b3ce-48e1-47fb-a08b-ec7e4b884b08","name":"Petersen, Poul Erik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas A E","key":"plattsmillspau","last":"Platts-Mills","name":"Platts-Mills, Thomas A E","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27091126"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12887-016-0571-4","issn":["14712431"],"journal":"BMC Pediatrics","paperid":"50","status":"p","title":"BMC Pediatrics","title_org":"B M C Pediatrics","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85008402803"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-407673bb-abbb-43fc-88fe-e0881c0ba81a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Childhood asthma and physical activity : a systematic review with meta-analysis and Graphic Appraisal Tool for Epidemiology assessment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-431991","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Tree disease epidemics are a global problem, impacting food security, biodiversity and national economies. The potential for conservation and breeding in trees is hampered by complex genomes and long lifecycles, with most species lacking genomic resources. The European Ash tree Fraxinus excelsior is being devastated by the fungal pathogen Hymenoscyphus fraxineus, which causes ash dieback disease. Taking this system as an example and utilizing Associative Transcriptomics for the first time in a plant pathology study, we discovered gene sequence and gene expression variants across a genetic diversity panel scored for disease symptoms and identified markers strongly associated with canopy damage in infected trees. Using these markers we predicted phenotypes in a test panel of unrelated trees, successfully identifying individuals with a low level of susceptibility to the disease. Co-expression analysis suggested that pre-priming of defence responses may underlie reduced susceptibility to ash dieback.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Harper, Andrea L.","McKinney, Lea Vig","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Havlickova, Lenka","Li, Yi","Trick, Martin","Fraser, Fiona","Wang, Lihong","Fellgett, Alison","Sollars, Elizabeth S A","Janacek, Sophie H.","Downie, J. Allan","Buggs, Richard J A","Kjær, Erik Dahl","Bancroft, Ian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471179"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Bioinformatics Institute","John Innes Centre","Queen Mary University of London","The Earlham Institute","University of York"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"molecular markers for tolerance of european ash i fraxinus excelsior i to dieback disease identified using associative transcriptomics","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84954128405&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-471179","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4725942","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84954128405","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26757823","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-81eafcdf-d0dd-4b19-94d8-b25f680a3be9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B19171659B4AEFE6EB9843A6C1F66E75"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of york","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of York","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"john innes centre","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"John Innes Centre","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"the earlham institute","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Earlham Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"european bioinformatics institute","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"European Bioinformatics Institute","used":1},{"affno":6,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Andrea L.","key":"harperpau","last":"Harper","name":"Harper, Andrea L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lea Vig","key":"mckinneypau","last":"McKinney","locid":"060df27a-59d3-4457-81a2-185cca16ae68","name":"McKinney, Lea Vig","orcid":"0000-0001-6601-4614","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lenka","key":"havlickovapau","last":"Havlickova","name":"Havlickova, Lenka","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yi","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Martin","key":"trickpau","last":"Trick","name":"Trick, Martin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Fiona","key":"fraserpau","last":"Fraser","name":"Fraser, Fiona","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lihong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Lihong","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alison","key":"fellgettpau","last":"Fellgett","name":"Fellgett, Alison","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Elizabeth S A","key":"sollarspau","last":"Sollars","name":"Sollars, Elizabeth S A","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Sophie H.","key":"janacekpau","last":"Janacek","name":"Janacek, Sophie H.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"J. Allan","key":"downiepau","last":"Downie","name":"Downie, J. Allan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Richard J A","key":"buggspau","last":"Buggs","name":"Buggs, Richard J A","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ian","key":"bancroftpau","last":"Bancroft","name":"Bancroft, Ian","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26757823"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/srep19335","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"19335","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84954128405"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-81eafcdf-d0dd-4b19-94d8-b25f680a3be9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Molecular markers for tolerance of European ash (<i>Fraxinus excelsior</i>) to dieback disease identified using Associative Transcriptomics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471179","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"AIM: Type 1 diabetes requires extensive self-management to avoid complications and may have negative effects on the everyday life of people with the disease. The aim of this study was to compare adults with type 1 diabetes to the general population in terms of health-related quality of life, occupational status (level of employment, working hours and sick leave) and education level. METHODS: 2415 adults (aged 18-98years) with type 1 diabetes were compared to 48,511 adults (aged 18-103years) from the general population. Data were obtained from two cross-sectional surveys conducted in 2010 and 2011 of adults living or treated in the Capital Region in Denmark. Differences between adults with type 1 diabetes and the general population were standardised for age and sex and analyzed using linear probability models and negative binomial regression. Differences were further analyzed in subgroups. RESULTS: Compared to the general population, adults with type 1 diabetes experienced lower health-related quality of life, were more frequently unemployed, had more sick leave per year and were slightly better educated. Differences in health-related quality of life and employment increased with age and were larger among women, as compared to men. No significant differences were found with regard to working hours. CONCLUSION: Our findings suggest that type 1 diabetes is associated with lower health-related quality of life, higher unemployment and additional sick leave. The negative association with type 1 diabetes is more pronounced in women and older adults.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Helena B.","Ovesen, Louise L.","Mortensen, Laust Hvas","Lau, Cathrine J.","Joensen, Lene E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-477702"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"type 000000000001 diabetes quality of life occupational status and education level a comparative population based study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-477702","identifier":[{"id":"27662040","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84988418801","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8ceaa5d6-9a9e-45bc-ac50-c20e92a2c0e3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-274D9FBA9DCA4206CD236E9CAC1E1653"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Helena B.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Helena B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise L.","key":"ovesenpau","last":"Ovesen","name":"Ovesen, Louise L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Laust H.","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"d0e91c79-42a7-44be-a8a8-5a1d560fdeb0","name":"Mortensen, Laust Hvas","name_org":"Mortensen, Laust H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6399-495X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Cathrine J.","key":"laupau","last":"Lau","name":"Lau, Cathrine J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene E.","key":"joensenpau","last":"Joensen","name":"Joensen, Lene E.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27662040"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.diabres.2016.08.021","issn":["01688227","15721671"],"issn_org":["01688227"],"journal":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","pages":"62-68","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","volume":"121"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84988418801"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8ceaa5d6-9a9e-45bc-ac50-c20e92a2c0e3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Type 1 diabetes, quality of life, occupational status and education level : A comparative population-based study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-477702","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: While the association between renal impairment and cardiovascular disease (CVD) is well established in the general population, the association remains poorly understood in human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-positive individuals. METHODS: Individuals with ≥2 estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) measurements after 1 February 2004 were followed until CVD, death, last visit plus 6 months, or 1 February 2015. CVD was defined as the occurrence of centrally validated myocardial infarction, stroke, invasive cardiovascular procedures, or sudden cardiac death. RESULTS: During a median follow-up duration of 8.0 years (interquartile range, 5.4-8.9 years) 1357 of 35 357 individuals developed CVD (incidence rate, 5.2 cases/1000 person-years [95% confidence interval {CI}, 5.0-5.5]). Confirmed baseline eGFR and CVD were closely related with 1.8% of individuals (95% CI, 1.6%-2.0%) with an eGFR > 90 mL/minute/1.73 m(2) estimated to develop CVD at 5 years, increasing to 21.1% (95% CI, 6.6%-35.6%) among those with an eGFR ≤ 30 mL/minute/1.73 m(2) The strong univariate relationship between low current eGFR and CVD was primarily explained by increasing age in adjusted analyses, although all eGFRs ≤ 80 mL/minute/1.73 m(2) remained associated with 30%-40% increased CVD rates, and particularly high CVD rates among individuals with an eGFR ≤ 30 mL/minute/1.73 m(2) (incidence rate ratio, 3.08 [95% CI, 2.04-4.65]). CONCLUSIONS: Among HIV-positive individuals in a large contemporary cohort, a strong relation between confirmed impaired eGFR and CVD was observed. This finding highlights the need for renal preventive measures and intensified monitoring for emerging CVD, particularly in older individuals with continuously low eGFRs.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Lundgren, Jens","Ross, Mike","Kirk, Ole","Law, Matthew","Morlat, Philippe","Fontas, Eric","Smit, Colette","Fux, Christoph A","Hatleberg, Camilla Ingrid","De Wit, Stephane","Sabin, Caroline A","Mocroft, Amanda"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-487447"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"renal impairment and cardiovascular disease in hiv positive individuals the d a d study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-487447","identifier":[{"id":"27485357","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84990923829","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5034954","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-9d481516-c830-4199-b856-07b85795be4f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-98751A657BAF819C901A703B05AD6EDE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Ryom","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ryom","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens D","key":"lundgrenpau","last":"Lundgren","loci