"first":"Lene","key":"eklundjürgensenlenepedh","last":"Eklund-Jürgensen","name":"Eklund-Jürgensen, Lene","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Erland","key":"koldingnielsenerlandpedh","last":"Kolding Nielsen","name":"Kolding Nielsen, Erland","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"lundtoftehenrikpedh","last":"Lundtofte","name":"Lundtofte, Henrik","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus","key":"mariagerrasmuspedh","last":"Mariager","name":"Mariager, Rasmus","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob K.","key":"meilejakobkpedh","last":"Meile","name":"Meile, Jakob K.","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788763545464"],"issn":["01058746"],"pages":"461-503","place":"København","publisher":"Det kongelige bibliotek København","series":"Danish Humanist Texts and Studies","status":"p","subtitle":"Festskrift til John T. Lauridsen","title":"Kildekunst”:  Historiske &amp; kulturhistoriske studier"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4f5d4ccb-932f-4fba-821f-3a137a78e164"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Staten, studenterne og det røde universitet 1970-1982","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-174546","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Aim and Introduction Identification of abnormal kidneys in the fetus may lead to termination of the pregnancy and raises questions about the underlying cause and recurrence risk in future pregnancies. In this study, we investigate the effectiveness of targeted next generation sequencing in fetuses with prenatally detected kidney anomalies in order to uncover genetic explanations and assess recurrence risk. Also, we aim to study the relation between genetic findings and post mortem kidney histology. Methods The study comprises fetuses diagnosed prenatally with bilateral kidney anomalies that have undergone postmortem examination. The approximately 110 genes included in the targeted panel were chosen on the basis of their potential involvement in embryonic kidney development, cystic kidney disease, or the renin-angiotensin system. DNA was extracted from fetal tissue samples or cultured chorion villus cells, aminocytes, or fibroblasts. Data analysis was performed using CLC Genomics workbench, publicly available databases, and prediction tools. The Regional Ethical Committee approved the study. Results Samples from 61 fetuses from 57 families were included in the study. Two fetuses had mutations in the nephronophthisis associated gene, TMEM67 and six fetuses had mutations in kidney developmental genes. For these fetuses kidney histology is presented. Conclusion and Perspectives In eight (14%) fetuses we identified a likely genetic cause of the kidney anomalies. Ten fetuses from eight families, in which no mutations were identified, have been selected for exome sequencing in order to uncover novel genes associated to fetal kidney anomalies.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Maria","Sunde, Lone","Nielsen, Marlene Louise","Ramsing, Mette","Petersen, Astrid","Hjortshøj, Tina Duelund","Olsen, Tina Elisabeth","Tabor, Ann","Hertz, Jens Michael","Johnsen, Iben","Sperling, Lene Søndergaard","Petersen, Olav Bjørn","Jensen, Uffe Birk","Petersen, Michael Bjørn","Lildballe, Dorte Launholt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-261016"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-24","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2016-05-21","title":"European Society of Human Genetics Conference 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fetal","Kidney"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fetal kidney anomalies next generation sequencing","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-261016","ids":["au-e6a809d4-2e20-46c8-a5b4-b57a25ba2707"],"keyword":["Fetal","Kidney"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69C06F899D16C87DD77B21C173E144BD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department for Clinical Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital (AUH)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"rasmussenmariapau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"bf012d73-b919-4994-abf4-c68e58c5aa51","name":"Rasmussen, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lone","key":"sundelonepau","last":"Sunde","locid":"c9861e75-ca9f-4b1c-8db0-b7fd1148b2e7","name":"Sunde, Lone","orcid":"0000-0002-8479-165X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marlene Louise","key":"nielsenmarlenelouisepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5c72ecc2-f5bb-4afb-bedd-9b96add5e7db","name":"Nielsen, Marlene Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"ramsingmettepau","last":"Ramsing","name":"Ramsing, Mette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid","key":"petersenastridpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"792c89ce-a07d-429d-87a4-ddfc8ce46b02","name":"Petersen, Astrid","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina Duelund","key":"hjortshøjtinaduelundpau","last":"Hjortshøj","name":"Hjortshøj, Tina Duelund","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina Elisabeth","key":"olsentinaelisabethpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Tina Elisabeth","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann","key":"taborannpau","last":"Tabor","name":"Tabor, Ann","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Michael","key":"hertzjensmichaelpau","last":"Hertz","name":"Hertz, Jens Michael","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben","key":"johnsenibenpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Iben","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Søndergaard","key":"sperlinglenesøndergaardpau","last":"Sperling","name":"Sperling, Lene Søndergaard","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olav Bjørn","key":"petersenolavbjørnpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"b9f12bfe-d3f4-446a-b40b-37ac968b84c4","name":"Petersen, Olav Bjørn","orcid":"0000-0001-8517-4082","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uffe Birk","key":"jensenuffebirkpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"54eb5276-38e5-433b-b654-7f770ddba0ed","name":"Jensen, Uffe Birk","orcid":"0000-0002-6205-6355","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Bjørn","key":"petersenmichaelbjørnpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"5c66c198-0aec-4bae-9086-0be08739daa6","name":"Petersen, Michael Bjørn","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Launholt","key":"lildballedortelaunholtpau","last":"Lildballe","locid":"de19a867-a649-4c19-9154-facd7daef4a9","name":"Lildballe, Dorte Launholt","orcid":"0000-0003-0223-1673","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e6a809d4-2e20-46c8-a5b4-b57a25ba2707"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Fetal Kidney Anomalies: Next Generation Sequencing","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-261016","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Nelfinavir exhibits potent anticancer properties against a range of tumours. However, in 2006/2007, nelfinavir supplies were accidently contaminated with a carcinogen. This analysis investigated the association between nelfinavir use and cancer risk in HIV-positive persons. DESIGN: Observational cohort study. METHODS: D:A:D study data was analysed using Poisson regression models to examine associations between cancer incidence and cumulative nelfinavir exposure, current nelfinavir exposure, and exposure to nelfinavir between 1 July 2006-30 June 2007. RESULTS: A total of 42 006 individuals (50% white, 73% male) contributed 303 005 person-years of follow-up between 1 January 2004 and 1 February 2014. At study enrolment, median age was 40 [interquartile range (IQR) 33-46] years and 8305 individuals had a history of nelfinavir use [median duration 1.7 (IQR 0.7-3.4) years]. During follow-up, nelfinavir was used by 2476 individuals for a median of 1.7 (IQR 0.7-3.8) years; 1063 were exposed to nelfinavir between 1 July 2006 and 30 June 2007. Overall, 2279 cancers were diagnosed at a rate of 0.75 [95% confidence interval (95% CI) 0.72-0.78] per 100 person-years. Neither greater cumulative exposure to nelfinavir [adjusted risk ratio (aRR) 0.93 for every additional 5 years, 95% CI 0.82-1.06, P = 0.26] nor current use of nelfinavir (aRR 0.98 vs other protease inhibitor use, 95% CI 0.68-1.41, P = 0.92) were associated with cancer risk. The adjusted risk of cancer for participants exposed to nelfinavir between 1 July 2006 and 30 June 2007 compared to those receiving other treatment over this period was 1.07 (95% CI 0.78-1.46, P = 0.68). CONCLUSION: Nelfinavir use was not associated with a lower cancer incidence than other protease inhibitor regimens. As of February 2014, exposure to the 2006/2007 contamination of nelfinavir does not appear to be associated with increased cancer incidence.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Boettiger, David C","Sabin, Caroline A","Grulich, Andrew","Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Bonnet, Fabrice","Reiss, Peter","Monforte, Antonella d'arminio","Kirk, Ole","Phillips, Andrew","Bower, Mark","Fätkenheuer, Gerd","Lundgren, Jens","Law, Matthew"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394042"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["Data collection on Adverse events of Anti-HIV Drugs (D:A:D) study group"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"is nelfinavir exposure associated with cancer incidence in hiv positive individuals","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-394042","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4889546","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26854812","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84957636509","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-00f79d0e-c836-489c-a5bc-14e7345b0d25"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39E65A2517953A85D596CE949EE4AD96"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, CHIP"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"data collection on adverse events of anti hiv drugs study group","name":"Data collection on Adverse events of Anti-HIV Drugs (D:A:D) study group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"David C","key":"boettigerpau","last":"Boettiger","name":"Boettiger, David C","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Caroline A","key":"sabinpau","last":"Sabin","name":"Sabin, Caroline A","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew","key":"grulichpau","last":"Grulich","name":"Grulich, Andrew","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Ryom","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0087fd9d-3a4d-4da5-9f4d-2ba51ec7d7a8","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ryom","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fabrice","key":"bonnetpau","last":"Bonnet","name":"Bonnet, Fabrice","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"reisspau","last":"Reiss","name":"Reiss, Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonella d'arminio","key":"monfortepau","last":"Monforte","name":"Monforte, Antonella d'arminio","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole","key":"kirkpau","last":"Kirk","locid":"67bce469-8913-44ac-8d6d-7dff1171c771","name":"Kirk, Ole","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew","key":"phillipspau","last":"Phillips","name":"Phillips, Andrew","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mark","key":"bowerpau","last":"Bower","name":"Bower, Mark","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gerd","key":"fätkenheuerpau","last":"Fätkenheuer","name":"Fätkenheuer, Gerd","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens D","key":"lundgrenpau","last":"Lundgren","locid":"af310f7a-c49b-4381-bcb4-cf56e3fd80d8","name":"Lundgren, Jens","name_org":"Lundgren, Jens D","orcid":"0000-0001-8901-7850","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew","key":"lawpau","last":"Law","name":"Law, Matthew","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26854812"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/qad.0000000000001053","issn":["02699370"],"issue":"10","journal":"AIDS","pages":"1629-37","status":"p","title":"AIDS","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84957636509"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-00f79d0e-c836-489c-a5bc-14e7345b0d25"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Is nelfinavir exposure associated with cancer incidence in HIV-positive individuals?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-394042","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Small bowel cancer (SBC) is a rare and highly heterogeneous disease in respect to both anatomical distribution and histological morphology. We aimed to conduct a Danish nationwide population-based cohort study of the incidence of, phenotypes of, stage of, synchronous/metachronous cancer occurrence of and survival from SBC during 1994-2010. METHODS: The study population included all individuals aged 16 years or older living in Denmark during 1994-2010 (n = 7,070,142). Patients with SBC were identified through the Danish Cancer Registry. Incidence rates were calculated overall and according to the anatomical origin and morphological subtype. Patients were followed up from the date of cancer diagnosis to the date of emigration, death or the end of the study (31 December 2010). RESULTS: SBC was diagnosed in 1088 patients during 1994-2010. The total annual incidence of SBC was 1.10 per 100,000 [95 % confidence interval (CI) 1.04 to 1.17 per 100,000], with an annual percentage change of 1.9 % (95 % CI 0.6-3.1 %, p = 0.003) during the observation period. This increase was mainly explained by an increase in the occurrence of duodenal adenocarcinomas, with an annual percentage change of 7.5 % (95 % CI 4.9-10.2 %, p < 0.001). Further, 29 % of all SBC patients had metastatic cancer at the time of diagnosis and 32 % had one or more synchronous/metachronous cancers. All morphological subtypes were associated with poor 5-year prognoses, in particular duodenal adenocarcinomas, with a 5-year survival rate of only 16 % (95 % CI 12-22 %). CONCLUSIONS: The incidence of SBC has increased in recent decades, mainly because of a large increase in the incidence of duodenal adenocarcinomas, which are also associated with the poorest prognosis.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bojesen, Rasmus Dahlin","Andersson, Mikael","Riis, Lene Buhl","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Jess, Tine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-493484"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Department of Epidemiology Research, State Serum Institute, National Institute for Health Data and Disease Control, Artillerivej 5, 2300, Copenhagen, Denmark. rasmus.bojesen@gmail.com."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incidence of phenotypes of and survival from small bowel cancer in denmark 000000001994 000000002010 a population based study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-493484","identifier":[{"id":"84957608401","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26847562","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a7866dd4-6256-43ef-93bd-57fa3a3c380c"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-33A32033E4619B853C7DBFD720BB00EB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Epidemiology Research, State Serum Institute, National Institute for Health Data and Disease Control, Artillerivej 5, 2300, Copenhagen, Denmark. rasmus.bojesen@gmail.com."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus Dahlin","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","name":"Bojesen, Rasmus Dahlin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikael","key":"anderssonpau","last":"Andersson","name":"Andersson, Mikael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene Buhl","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Ole Haagen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59658c4-dde8-4749-9b5c-f4ec5910dd02","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","orcid":"0000-0003-4612-8635","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tine","key":"jesspau","last":"Jess","name":"Jess, Tine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26847562"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00535-016-1171-7","issn":["09441174","14355922"],"issn_org":["09441174"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of Gastroenterology","pages":"891-9","status":"p","title":"Journal of Gastroenterology","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84957608401"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a7866dd4-6256-43ef-93bd-57fa3a3c380c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Incidence of, phenotypes of and survival from small bowel cancer in Denmark, 1994-2010 : a population-based study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-493484","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Ovarian cancer has a high mortality rate, especially in Denmark where mortality rates have been reported higher than in adjacent countries with similar demographics. This study therefore examined recent survival and mortality among Danish ovarian cancer patients over an 18-year study period. METHODS: This nationwide registry-based observational study used data from the Danish Gynecology Cancer Database, Danish Pathology Registry, and Danish National Patient Registry. All patients with ovarian cancer diagnosed between 1995 and 2012 were included in the study. The data sources were linked via the patients' personal identification number and the analyses included data on cancer stage, age, survival, surgery status and comorbidity. The computed outcome measures were age-adjusted mortality rates and age-adjusted overall and relative survival rates for one and five years. RESULTS: We identified 9972 patients diagnosed with ovarian cancer in the period 1995-2012. The absolute one-year mortality rate decreased from 42.8 (CI 40.3-45.6) in 1995-1999 to 28.3 (CI 25.9-30.9) in 2010-2012, and the five-year mortality rate decreased from 28.2 (CI 27.0-29.5) in 1995-1999 to 23.9 (CI 22.9-25.0) in 2005-2009. After stratification by age, comorbidity and cancer stage, the decrease in one-year mortality was most substantial in the 65-74 year old age group 41.1 (CI 38.8-43.5) to 26.5 (CI 24.4-28.7) and for stage III 39.1 (CI 35.1-43.6) to 22.9 (CI 19.9-26.5) and stage IV 91.3 (CI 80.8-103.2) to 41.9 (CI 35.5-49.5). For overall survival, we showed an increase in one-year survival from 68% (CI 66-69%) in 1995-1999 to 76% (CI 74-78%) in 2010-2012 and an increase in five-year survival from 33% (CI 32-35%) in 1995-1999 to 36% (CI 34-38%) in 2005-2009. Relative survival showed similar increases through the period. CONCLUSIONS: Ovarian cancer survival in Denmark has improved substantially from 1995 to 2012, bringing Denmark closer to the standards set by adjacent countries.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Edwards, Hellen McKinnon","Noer, Mette Calundann","Sperling, Cecilie Dyg","Nguyen-Nielsen, Mary","Lundvall, Lene","Christensen, Ib Jarle","Høgdall, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-522651"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Denmark","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Middle Aged","Mortality","Ovarian Neoplasms","Registries"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"survival of ovarian cancer patients in denmark results from the danish gynaecological cancer group dgcg database 000000001995 000000002012","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-522651","identifier":[{"id":"84976385212","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27355258","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d8567aca-2e0f-43b4-9a61-8826532591fb"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Denmark","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Middle Aged","Mortality","Ovarian Neoplasms","Registries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-484DD3C4FE357E7EB71B6E4A001958DC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Hellen McKinnon","key":"edwardspau","last":"Edwards","name":"Edwards, Hellen McKinnon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette Calundann","key":"noerpau","last":"Noer","name":"Noer, Mette Calundann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cecilie Dyg","key":"sperlingpau","last":"Sperling","name":"Sperling, Cecilie Dyg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mary","key":"nguyennielsenpau","last":"Nguyen-Nielsen","name":"Nguyen-Nielsen, Mary","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"lundvallpau","last":"Lundvall","name":"Lundvall, Lene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ib Jarle","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b8f0594e-4a73-4cf7-9117-a9eb69323873","name":"Christensen, Ib Jarle","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Claus","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","locid":"c5c660ee-f61a-4d1f-a38d-7851491ce186","name":"Høgdall, Claus","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27355258"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2016.1182641","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"S2","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"36-43","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84976385212"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d8567aca-2e0f-43b4-9a61-8826532591fb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Survival of ovarian cancer patients in Denmark : Results from the Danish gynaecological cancer group (DGCG) database, 1995-2012","type":"Journal Article","url":"ht