{"abstract":"AIM: Increasing evidence points to lipoprotein composition rather than reverse cholesterol transport in the cardioprotective properties of high-density lipoproteins (HDL). HDL binding to receptors at the surface of cardiomyocytes activates signalling pathways promoting survival, but downstream targets are largely unknown. Here, we investigate the pathways by which the Sphingosine-1-Phosphate (S1P) constituent of HDL limits cell death induced by cardiac ischemia/reperfusion (I/R). METHODS AND RESULTS: Apolipoprotein M (ApoM) transgenic (Apom-Tg) mice, in which plasma S1P is increased by 296%, and wild-type (WT) mice were subjected to in vivo I/R. Infarct size, neutrophil infiltration into the infarcted area and serum Troponin I were less pronounced in Apom-Tg mice. In vitro experiments suggest that this cardioprotection depends on direct effects of S1P on cardiomyocytes, whereas leukocyte recruitment seems only indirectly affected. Importantly, short-term S1P treatment at the onset of reperfusion was sufficient to reduce ischemia/reperfusion injury in isolated perfused hearts. Mechanistic in vitro and ex vivo studies revealed that 5 min of S1P treatment induced phosphorylation of the gap junction protein Connexin43 (Cx43) on Serine368, which was mediated by S1P2 and S1P3, but not by S1P1, receptors in cardiomyocytes. Finally, S1P-induced reduction of infarct size after ex vivo I/R was lost in hearts of mice with a truncated C-terminus of Cx43 (Cx43(K258/KO)) or in which the Serine368 is mutated to a non-phosphorylatable Alanine (Cx43(S368A/S368A)). CONCLUSION: Our study reveals an important molecular pathway by which modulating the apoM/S1P axis has a therapeutic potential in the fight against ischemia/reperfusion injury in the heart.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Morel, Sandrine","Christoffersen, Christina","Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","Montecucco, Fabrizio","Rochemont, Viviane","Frias, Miguel A","Mach, Francois","James, Richard W","Naus, Christian C","Chanson, Marc","Lampe, Paul D","Nielsen, Morten Schak","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Kwak, Brenda R"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-405644"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sphingosine 000000000001 phosphate reduces ischemia reperfusion injury by phosphorylating the gap junction protein connexin000000000043","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-405644","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4752044","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84959922603","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26762268","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-147a6e11-0e8c-456b-94cf-d22eea497242"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F5B75C2E11C69E9610B4E8B9DE3715F8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Sandrine","key":"morelsandrinepau","last":"Morel","name":"Morel, Sandrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenchristinapau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene N","key":"axelsenlenenygaardpau","last":"Axelsen","locid":"2632f623-a6d6-49e1-884c-0560715787be","name":"Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","name_org":"Axelsen, Lene N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montecuccofabriziopau","last":"Montecucco","name":"Montecucco, Fabrizio","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Viviane","key":"rochemontvivianepau","last":"Rochemont","name":"Rochemont, Viviane","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Miguel A","key":"friasmiguelapau","last":"Frias","name":"Frias, Miguel A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Francois","key":"machfrancoispau","last":"Mach","name":"Mach, Francois","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Richard W","key":"jamesrichardwpau","last":"James","name":"James, Richard W","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian C","key":"nauschristiancpau","last":"Naus","name":"Naus, Christian C","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marc","key":"chansonmarcpau","last":"Chanson","name":"Chanson, Marc","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul D","key":"lampepauldpau","last":"Lampe","name":"Lampe, Paul D","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten S","key":"nielsenmortenschakpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b203113e-fe9b-4863-8eb0-3022ca8cc9e2","name":"Nielsen, Morten Schak","name_org":"Nielsen, Morten S","orcid":"0000-0002-9718-5421","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars B","key":"nielsenlarsbopau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, Lars B","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Brenda R","key":"kwakbrendarpau","last":"Kwak","name":"Kwak, Brenda R","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26762268"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/cvr/cvw004","issn":["00086363","17553245"],"issn_org":["00086363"],"journal":"Cardiovascular Research","pages":"385-396","status":"p","title":"Cardiovascular Research","volume":"109"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84959922603"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Univer