{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Odgaard, Lene","Johnsen, Søren Paaske","Pedersen, Asger Roer","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-259834"],"event":{"end":"2016-03-05","start":"2016-03-02","title":"International Brain injury associations World Congress on Brain injury","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"return to work after severe traumatic brain injury is low in denmark a nationwide follow up study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-259834","identifier":[{"id":"000376388200149","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-e491d027-3c0a-4389-a6f7-3b1c7dac2087"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4C4D63CE655772CE37BD695D12936A98"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Regionshospital Hammel Neurocenter"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"1b80fe7b-ba0a-45b3-aca1-48bc19a97a44","name":"Odgaard, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-9830-3282","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Soren Paaske","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"4664f7a0-39e7-4f46-9121-1c3999eb3d09","name":"Johnsen, Søren Paaske","name_org":"Johnsen, Soren Paaske","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger Roer","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a9b1b4b8-df5b-437d-a84f-fcc1778ce6eb","name":"Pedersen, Asger Roer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jorgen Feldbaek","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","name_org":"Nielsen, Jorgen Feldbaek","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["02699052","1362301X"],"issn_org":["02699052"],"issue":"5-6","journal":"Brain Injury","pages":"544-544","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Brain Injury","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e491d027-3c0a-4389-a6f7-3b1c7dac2087"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Return to work after severe traumatic brain injury is low in Denmark : A nationwide follow-up study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-259834","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Renal ischemia/reperfusion (I/R) can lead to impaired urine concentration ability and increased fractional excretion of sodium (FeNa). Local ischemic preconditioning improves renal water and sodium handling after I/R injury. Here, we investigate whether remote ischemic perconditioning (rIPeC) prevents dysregulation of renal water and salt handling in response to I/R injury and mechanisms that may be involved. Rats were subjected to right nephrectomy and randomized into a sham group or an I/R group. In the I/R group, rats were subjected to 37 min of renal ischemia and 3 days of reperfusion. rIPeC was applied to the abdominal aorta. Blood and urine were collected on day 3 postoperatively for clearance studies. The expression of aquaporins (AQPs) and the sodium transporter Na-K-ATPase were analyzed using immunoblotting and immunohistochemistry. I/R injury resulted in polyuria, increased FeNa, and decreased urine osmolality compared to sham rats. rIPeC attenuated the increase in FeNa and the decrease in urine osmolality. Expression of AQP1, AQP2, phosphorylated AQP2 (pAQP2), and Na-K-ATPase was downregulated in I/R rats. rIPeC attenuated the reductions in AQP2 and pAQP2 expression. Immunohistochemistry revealed decreased labeling of Na-K-ATPase in the outer medulla in I/R kidneys compared to kidneys from sham and I/R + rIPeC rats. After renal ischemia, the expression of Na-K-ATPase was substantially reduced in the outer medullary thick ascending limb. In conclusion, our data suggest that rIPeC might prevent dysregulation of renal water and salt handling via regulation of AQP2 expression and phosphorylation as well as via regulation of Na-K-ATPase expression in I/R rat kidneys.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kristensen, Marie Louise Vindvad","Lassen, Casper Kierulf","Nielsen, Per Mose","Krag, Søren Rasmus Palmelund","Birn, Henrik","Nejsum, Lene Niemann","Nørregaard, Rikke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-266823"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Aorta Abdominal","Aquaporin 2","Constriction","Disease Models Animal","Down Regulation","HSP70 Heat Shock Proteins","Ischemic Preconditioning","Journal Article","Kidney","Kidney Diseases","Male","Natriuresis","Phosphorylation","Rats Wistar","Regional Blood Flow","Reperfusion Injury","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Sodium Potassium Exchanging ATPase","Time Factors","Water Electrolyte Balance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"remote ischemic perconditioning attenuates ischemia reperfusion induced downregulation of aqp000000000002 in rat kidney","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.12865","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-266823","identifier":[{"id":"84978879497","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27405971","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4945844","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-f0f32066-5aae-4b58-9a01-d7959ca7445c"],"keyword":["Animals","Aorta, Abdominal","Aquaporin 2","Constriction","Disease Models, Animal","Down-Regulation","HSP70 Heat-Shock Proteins","Ischemic Preconditioning","Journal Article","Kidney","Kidney Diseases","Male","Natriuresis","Phosphorylation","Rats, Wistar","Regional Blood Flow","Reperfusion Injury","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Sodium-Potassium-Exchanging ATPase","Time Factors","Water-Electrolyte Balance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-12B67B889A174BCD490653AA540A7E03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.12865","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","