:"Longitudinal analysis of the associations between antiretroviral therapy, viraemia and immunosuppression with lipid levels : the D:A:D study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-430887","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Gede, Lene Bjerring","Hahnemann, Johanne M D","Tümer, Zeynep","Brøndum-Nielsen, Karen","Grønskov, Karen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-481501"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Beckwith Wiedemann syndrome","Case Control Studies","Chromosomes Human Pair 11","DNA methylation","Feasibility Studies","Female","Genetic Testing","Humans","Journal Article","Multiplex Polymerase Chain Reaction","Pregnancy","Prenatal Diagnosis","Silver Russell syndrome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility study on the use of methylation specific mlpa for the 000000000011p000000000015 region on prenatal samples","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-481501","identifier":[{"id":"26590364","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84956657447","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9362b5bb-5141-44ab-8bdc-6edc4ed884c1"],"keyword":["Beckwith-Wiedemann Syndrome","Case-Control Studies","Chromosomes, Human, Pair 11","DNA Methylation","Feasibility Studies","Female","Genetic Testing","Humans","Journal Article","Multiplex Polymerase Chain Reaction","Pregnancy","Prenatal Diagnosis","Silver-Russell Syndrome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2274631E5C8C218C2F07A69E37318C32"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lene Bjerring","key":"gedepau","last":"Gede","name":"Gede, Lene Bjerring","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Johanne M D","key":"hahnemannpau","last":"Hahnemann","name":"Hahnemann, Johanne M D","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zeynep","key":"tümerpau","last":"Tümer","locid":"71f90c14-c463-40fb-8083-7ed2a31faa66","name":"Tümer, Zeynep","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karen","key":"brøndumnielsenpau","last":"Brøndum-Nielsen","name":"Brøndum-Nielsen, Karen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen","key":"grønskovpau","last":"Grønskov","locid":"1527824a-9524-4cbe-bbbd-673f745a1011","name":"Grønskov, Karen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26590364"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/pd.4752","issn":["01973851","10970223"],"issn_org":["01973851"],"issue":"1","journal":"Prenatal Diagnosis","pages":"100-3","status":"p","title":"Prenatal Diagnosis","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84956657447"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9362b5bb-5141-44ab-8bdc-6edc4ed884c1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Feasibility study on the use of methylation-specific MLPA for the 11p15 region on prenatal samples","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-481501","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Although several antiretroviral drugs, including the d-drugs stavudine (d4T) and didanosine (ddI), may cause biomarker-defined hepatotoxicity, their association with clinically defined end-stage liver disease (ESLD) and hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) remains unknown. DESIGN: Prospective cohort study. METHODS: Data collection on adverse events of anti-HIV drugs study (D:A:D) participants were followed until the first of ESLD (variceal bleeding, hepatic encephalopathy, hepatorenal syndrome or liver transplantation), HCC (histology or α-fetoprotein along with imaging), death, 6 months after last visit or 1 February 2014. Associations between ESLD/HCC and cumulative use of individual antiretrovirals were investigated using Poisson regression adjusting for potential confounders. RESULTS: During a median follow-up of 8.4 years, 319 ESLD/HCC cases occurred [incidence 1.01/1000 person-years (95% confidence interval 0.90-1.12)] with a 1-year mortality rate of 62.6%. After adjustment, cumulative (per 5 years) exposure to d4T [relative rate 1.46 (95% confidence interval 1.20-1.77)], ddI [1.32 (1.07-1.63)], tenofovir [TDF, 1.46 (1.11-1.93)] and (fos)amprenavir [APV; 1.47 (1.01-2.15)] was associated with increased ESLD/HCC rates. Longer exposure to emtricitabine [0.51 (0.32-0.83)] and nevirapine [0.76 (0.58-0.98)] were associated with lower ESLD/HCC rates. The ddI/d4T-associated increased ESLD/HCC rate only started to decline 6 years after cessation. CONCLUSION: Cumulative use of d4T, ddI, TDF and APV were independently associated with increased ESLD/HCC rates, and intensified monitoring of liver function should hence be considered among all individuals exposed for longer time periods. The use of d-drugs should furthermore be avoided, where there are alternatives available, and focus should be put on those with longer-term d-drugs exposure who remain at increased ESLD/HCC risk. The unexpected, and viral hepatitis-independent, TDF association calls for further investigations.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Lundgren, Jens","De Wit, Stéphane","Kovari, Helen","Reiss, Peter","Law, Matthew","El-Sadr, Wafa","Monforte, Antonella D'Arminio","Mocroft, Amanda","Smith, Colette","Fontas, Eric","Dabis, Francois","Phillips, Andrew","Sabin, Caroline"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-502431"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["D:A:D Study Group"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of antiretroviral therapy and risk of end stage liver disease and hepatocellular carcinoma in hiv positive persons","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-502431","identifier":[{"id":"84954570542","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26752282","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b67f8a11-6ff1-42c1-a37e-d62027daa947"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A08E22B761B5389D7992CE66CCE68E6B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, CHIP"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"d a d study group","name":"D:A:D Study Group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Ryom","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0087fd9d-3a4d-4da5-9f4d-2ba51ec7d7a8","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ryom","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Dilling","key":"lundgrenpau","last":"Lundgren","locid":"af310f7a-c49b-4381-bcb4-cf56e3fd80d8","name":"Lundgren, Jens","name_org":"Lundgren, Jens Dilling","orcid":"0000-0001-8901-7850","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stéphane","key":"dewitpau","last":"De Wit","name":"De Wit, Stéphane","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helen","key":"kovaripau","last":"Kovari","name":"Kovari, Helen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"reisspau","last":"Reiss","name":"Reiss, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew","key":"lawpau","last":"Law","name":"Law, Matthew","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wafa","key":"elsadrpau","last":"El-Sadr","name":"El-Sadr, Wafa","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonella D'Arminio","key":"monfortepau","last":"Monforte","name":"Monforte, Antonella D'Arminio","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Amanda","key":"mocroftpau","last":"Mocroft","name":"Mocroft, Amanda","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Colette","key":"smithpau","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Colette","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eric","key":"fontaspau","last":"Fontas","name":"Fontas, Eric","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Francois","key":"dabispau","last":"Dabis","name":"Dabis, Francois","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew","key":"phillipspau","last":"Phillips","name":"Phillips, Andrew","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Caroline","key":"sabinpau","last":"Sabin","name":"Sabin, Caroline","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26752282"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/qad.0000000000001018","issn":["02699370"],"issue":"11","journal":"AIDS","pages":"1731-43","status":"p","title":"AIDS","title_org":"AIDS (London, England)","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84954570542"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b67f8a11-6ff1-42c1-a37e-d62027daa947"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Use of antiretroviral therapy and risk of end-stage liver disease and hepatocellular carcinoma in HIV-positive persons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-502431","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Chronic kidney disease (CKD) has emerged as an important health concern in HIV-positive individuals. Preventing long-term kidney toxicity from an antiretroviral therapy is therefore critical. Selected antiretroviral agents, especially tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) and some ritonavir-boosted protease inhibitors (PI/rs), have been associated with increased risk of CKD. However, the CKD risk attributable to these agents is overall small, especially in those with low baseline risk of CKD and normal renal function. CKD risk in HIV-positive individuals can be further minimized by timely identification of those with worsening renal function and discontinuation of potentially nephrotoxic agents. Clinicians can use several monitoring tools, including the D:A:D risk score and routine measurements of estimated glomerular filtration (eGFR) and proteinuria, to identify high-risk individuals who may require an intervention. Tenofovir alafenamide (TAF), a TDF alternative, promises to be safer in terms of TDF-associated kidney and bone toxicity. While the short-term data on TAF does indicate lower eGFR decline and lower risk of proteinuria (vs. TDF), long-term data on renal safety of TAF are still awaited. Promising results have also emerged from recent trials on alternative dual-therapy antiretroviral regimens which exclude the nucleoside(tide) reverse transcriptase class as well as possibly the PI/rs, thereby reducing the drug burden, and possibly the toxicity. However, long-term safety or benefits of these dual-therapy regimens are still unclear and will need to be studied in future prospective studies. Finally, addressing risk factors such as hypertension and diabetes will continue to be important in this population.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Achhra, Amit C","Nugent, Melinda","Mocroft, Amanda","Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Wyatt, Christina M"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-542954"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","University College London","University of New South Wales"],"keyword":["Antiretroviral therapy","Dual therapy","GFR","HAART","HIV","Kidney","Proteinuria","Renal","Tenofovir","cART"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chronic kidney disease and antiretroviral therapy in hiv positive individuals recent developments","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-542954","identifier":[{"id":"27130284","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84964596246","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-fa82c913-31c4-4409-9f3f-b22ceb81da21"],"keyword":["Antiretroviral therapy","Dual therapy","GFR","HAART","HIV","Kidney","Proteinuria","Renal","Tenofovir","cART"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AA33DE355849696C3C9FC18F0037B0AE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"university of new south wales","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of New South Wales","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"icahn school of medicine at mount sinai","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, CHIP"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Amit C","key":"achhrapau","last":"Achhra","name":"Achhra, Amit C","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Melinda","key":"nugentpau","last":"Nugent","name":"Nugent, Melinda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Amanda","key":"mocroftpau","last":"Mocroft","name":"Mocroft, Amanda","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lene Ryom","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0087fd9d-3a4d-4da5-9f4d-2ba51ec7d7a8","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ryom","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina M","key":"wyattpau","last":"Wyatt","name":"Wyatt, Christina M","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27130284"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11904-016-0315-y","issn":["15483568","15483576"],"issn_org":["15483568"],"issue":"3","journal":"Current HIV - AIDS Reports","pages":"149-157","status":"p","title":"Current HIV - AIDS Reports","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964596246"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fa82c913-31c4-4409-9f3f-b22ceb81da21"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Chronic Kidney Disease and Antiretroviral Therapy in HIV-Positive Individuals : Recent Developments","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-542954","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":8,"contributors":["Skov Kristensen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-549164"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"loyalitet under pres bdn formand hans schmidt oxbülls tale på den tyske dag i 000000001955","src":["kum"],"src-code":["DI-GV-KUM"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-549164","ids":["kum-71e3ae9d-419c-4495-8ff7-afb548d34b65"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5610D23584FFE1652D035374C0863F4E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kum ministry of culture archives museums and royal library denmark","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-KUM","l3nn":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","namevar":["Ministry of Culture Denmark, The National Museum of Denmark","Ministry of Culture Denmark, The National Museum of Denmark, War and Occupation"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-KUM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"skovkristensenpau","last":"Skov Kristensen","locid":"218eaf1c-d386-477c-828e-caaa407d30d8","name":"Skov Kristensen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sofie Lene Bak m.fl.","key":"nolastnamepedh","last":"no-lastname","name":"no-lastname, Sofie Lene Bak m.fl.","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thorsten","key":"borringolesenpedh","last":"Borring Olesen","name":"Borring Olesen, Thorsten","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"eklundjürgensenpedh","last":"Eklund-Jürgensen","name":"Eklund-Jürgensen, Lene","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Erland","key":"koldingnielsenpedh","last":"Kolding Nielsen","name":"Kolding Nielsen, Erland","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"lundtoftepedh","last":"Lundtofte","name":"Lundtofte, Henrik","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus","key":"mariagerpedh","last":"Mariager","name":"Mariager, Rasmus","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob","key":"kyrilmeilepedh","last":"Kyril Meile","name":"Kyril Meile, Jakob","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788763545464"],"pages":"517-555","place":"Kbh.","publisher":"Museum Tusculanum","series":"Danish Humanist Texts and Studies","status":"p","subtitle":"Historiske &amp; kulturhistoriske studier. Festskrift til John T. Lauridsen","title":"\"Kildekunst\".","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kum-71e3ae9d-419c-4495-8ff7-afb548d34b65"],"src":["KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark"],"title":"Loyalitet under pres? BDN-formand Hans Schmidt-Oxbülls tale på 'den tyske dag' i 1955","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-549164","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this study was to examine whether the over-the-counter herbal medicinal plant St. John's wort affects glucose tolerance in healthy men. To do this, we included 10 healthy men who were examined by a 2-hr oral glucose tolerance test on three occasions: A: baseline; B: after 21 days of treatment with St. John's wort; and C: at least 6 weeks after the last capsule of St. John's wort was ingested. Plasma glucose, serum insulin and C-peptide levels were measured during an oral glucose tolerance test and used for estimation of area under the concentration-time curve (AUC) as well as indices of insulin sensitivity and insulin secretion. We found that treatment with St. John's wort increased total and incremental glucose AUC and 2-hr plasma glucose levels. Surprisingly, this effect was sustained and even further increased 6 weeks after the last capsule of St. John's wort was taken. No effect on indices of insulin sensitivity was seen, but indices of insulin secretion were reduced even after adjustment for insulin sensitivity. In conclusion, this study indicates that long-term treatment with St. John's wort may impair glucose tolerance by reducing insulin secretion in young, healthy men. The unregulated use of this over-the-counter drug might be a risk factor for impaired glucose tolerance and type 2 diabetes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Stage, Tore Bjerregaard","Damkier, Per","Christensen, Mette Marie Hougaard","Nielsen, Lene Buch-Krogh","Højlund, Kurt","Brøsen, Kim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-599635"],"event":{"end":"2015-06-30","place":"Madrid, es","start":"2015-06-27","title":"European Association of Clinical Pharmacology and Therapeutics","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Biomarkers blood","Blood Glucose metabolism","Body Mass Index","C Peptide blood","Dose Response Relationship Drug","Glucose Intolerance blood","Glycated Hemoglobin A metabolism","Humans","Insulin Resistance","Insulin blood","Insulin secretion","Male","Sample Size","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impaired glucose tolerance in healthy men treated with st john s wort","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84957928355","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-599635","identifier":[{"id":"84957928355","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26346185","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-5c53c546-a83e-4b83-b0b6-be27cba18d5b"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Biomarkers/blood","Blood Glucose/metabolism","Body Mass Index","C-Peptide/blood","Dose-Response Relationship, Drug","Glucose Intolerance/blood","Glycated Hemoglobin A/metabolism","Humans","Hypericum/adverse effects","Insulin Resistance","Insulin Secretion","Insulin/blood","Male","Plants, Medicinal/adverse effects","Sample Size","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BC52593A45A325711D1E2466FE15F669"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tore Bjerregaard","key":"stagepau","last":"Stage","locid":"b794c141-d9c5-4082-b8c5-b69f854d4c7c","name":"Stage, Tore Bjerregaard","orcid