{"abstract":"Jatropha curcas L. has been promoted as a “miracle” tree in many parts of the world, but recent studies have indicated very low levels of genetic diversity in various landraces. In this study, the genetic diversity of landrace collections of J. curcas was compared with the genetic diversity of the species from its native range, and the mating system was analyzed on the basis of microsatellite markers. The genetic diversity parameters were estimated, and analysis of molecular variance, principal coordinate analysis, and unrooted neighbor-joining tree were used to describe the relationship among populations. Results confirmed very low genetic diversity in African and Asian landraces. Mexican populations from the regions of Veracruz, Puebla, and Morelos were also found to have low levels of diversity (mostly monomorphic), while populations from Chiapas were polymorphic with an expected heterozygosity between 0.34 and 0.54. Bayesian analysis showed differentiation according to geographic locations, which was confirmed by principal coordinate analysis and neighbor-joining tree. Estimations of outcrossing rate of individual families from Chiapas showed that some mother trees were mainly outcrossing. Mating system could not be estimated in the landraces from Mali and populations from Veracruz, Puebla, and Morelos (Mexico), as these were highly monomorphic. The observed low level of genetic diversity in some of the populations and landraces suggests that breeding programs should test for genetic variation and heritability in relevant quantitative traits and estimate if sufficient gain can be expected from traditional testing and selection. Diversification of the local gene pools may be considered for breeding and selection.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Sanou, Haby","Angel Angulo-Escalante, Miguel","Martinez-Herrera, Jorge","Kone, Souleymane","Nikiema, Albert","Kalinganire, Antoine","Hansen, Jon Kehlet","Kjær, Erik Dahl","Graudal, Lars","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-400748"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"loss of genetic diversity of i jatropha curcas i l through domestication implications for its genetic improvement","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-400748","identifier":[{"id":"84923371698","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000352223000029","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-0c3d165b-2c87-4cac-94cb-cae0889c30bb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB015954E2E935CD94FEF78397765AC3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Haby","key":"sanoupau","last":"Sanou","name":"Sanou, Haby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Miguel","key":"angelanguloescalantepau","last":"Angel Angulo-Escalante","name":"Angel Angulo-Escalante, Miguel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jorge","key":"martinezherrerapau","last":"Martinez-Herrera","name":"Martinez-Herrera, Jorge","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Souleymane","key":"konepau","last":"Kone","name":"Kone, Souleymane","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Albert","key":"nikiemapau","last":"Nikiema","name":"Nikiema, Albert","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Antoine","key":"kalinganirepau","last":"Kalinganire","name":"Kalinganire, Antoine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jon Kehlet","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b8c2f3eb-b79f-46cc-b346-8300943e2129","name":"Hansen, Jon Kehlet","orcid":"0000-0002-1260-3509","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","name_org":"Kjaer, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"graudalpau","last":"Graudal","locid":"847681c5-3813-48da-814c-0a781420c600","name":"Graudal, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-3047-7419","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2135/cropsci2014.02.0165","issn":["0011183X","14350653"],"issn_org":["0011183X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Crop Science","pages":"749-759","status":"p","title":"Crop Science","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84923371698"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0c3d165b-2c87-4cac-94cb-cae0889c30bb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Loss of Genetic Diversity of <i>Jatropha curcas</i> L. through Domestication: Implications for Its Genetic Improvement","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-400748","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: The incidence and prevalence of sexual problems and sexual dysfunction among people living with cancer is high. Evidence suggests that sexual dysfunction is a threat to the joy of life and marital relationships, and can lead to stress and impaired coping ability in chronic ill patients. Yet, sexuality is still a neglected topic among health professionals. Objectives: To increase oncology and haematology nurses awareness, knowledge and skills about patients with cancer's specific and general sexual problems and how to approach an interview, where the theme is sexuality after cancer treatment. Methods: Academic Society for Cancer Nurses (FSK) has taken the initiative to form a Danish national working group in 2015 to develop and implement a national intervention with the above objectives. The effect of the intervention is evaluated by a national survey about nurses' knowledge and skills in relation to sexuality in patients with cancer. The intervention is aimed at patients living with cancer regardless of sexual orientation or sexual partner. Results: The details of the national intervention is expected to be finished by 1/5 2015. Conclusions: The patient's individual needs should be identified through initiation of conversations regarding sexual dysfunction in the medical setting. These conversations can help normalize concerns for patients, debunk myths, provide a basis for brief counselling or serve as an entree for a referral. Sexual function is an important aspect of life and should be placed on par with discussions of the disease, its treatment, and other symptoms or complications by health professionals.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Norskov, K.","Sigaard, Lene","Naundrup, D.","Nielsen, D.","Mortensen, L.","Stær, M.","Schoidt, K.","Rosberg, N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-628953"],"event":{"end":"2015-06-27","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2015-06-25","title":"The MASCC/ISOO Annual Meeting on Supportive Care in Cancer","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a danish national intervention with the purpose of increasing oncology and haematology nurses awareness knowledge and skills about sexuality in patients living with cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00520-015-2712-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-628953","ids":["sdu-c29a496f-5c76-4b34-8336-68336eb890aa"],"keyword":["*human *neoplasm *nurse *patient *skill *sexuality *hematology *oncology sexual dysfunction conversation health practitioner prevalence sexual orientation society cancer therapy interview sexual function literature counseling coping behavior"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D920EE36F64C8185D21439AD6208090A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00520-015-2712-y","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Roskilde Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"norskovpau","last":"Norskov","name":"Norskov, K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"sigaardpau","last":"Sigaard","locid":"d8981e97-47a4-401b-a6b5-fa0669b14383","name":"Sigaard, Lene","name_org":"Sigaard, L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"naundruppau","last":"Naundrup","name":"Naundrup, D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, D.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, L.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"stærpau","last":"Stær","name":"Stær, M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"schoidtpau","last":"Schoidt","name":"Schoidt, K.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"N.","key":"rosbergpau","last":"Rosberg","name":"Rosberg, N.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09414355","14337339"],"issn_org":["09414355"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Supportive Care in Cancer","paperid":"23-43-P","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Supportive Care in Cancer","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Re