es, Section for Animal Welfare and Disease Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Bisgaard","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"29a220a9-968f-4953-9aae-8d14ff34a998","name":"Petersen, Mette Bisgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7195-2103","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel Bruun","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"60a7b6e5-5f95-42bd-8608-3e98a3e329de","name":"Svendsen, Mikkel Bruun","orcid":"0000-0001-8404-9300","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kasper","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","name":"Krogh, Kasper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Liza Rosenbaum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"68689adc-896b-4527-85dd-f14287c53497","name":"Nielsen, Liza Rosenbaum","orcid":"0000-0003-2046-2387","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-82701e59-2b7c-4aba-856e-813bca95fbe2","ku-ec56cf8f-308c-4089-9b4e-afb3c0223ef0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Characterisation of Mycoplasma bovis Associated disease in Danish dairy herds 2010-2014","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.02-043965","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The persona method is gaining widespread use and support. Many researchers have reported from single cases and from novel domains on how they have used the method. However, the way companies and design groups describe personas has not been the focus of attention. This paper analyses 47 descriptions from 13 companies and compares these to an analysis of recommendations from 11 templates from literature. Furthermore, 28 interviews with Danish practitioners with experience in using personas are analyzed for content on persona descriptions. The study finds that a Danish persona style has developed that is different from the recommendations in the lack of marketing and business related information and the absence of goals as differentiator for personas. Furthermore, the inspiration and knowledge on personas originates from co-workers and seminars and not much from literature. This indicates that the community of practice influences the persona style.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Storgaard Nielsen, Kira","Stage, Jan","Billestrup, Jane"],"cuid":["S02-095.10-000906"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Design","Industry","Personas"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a template for design personas analysis of 000000000047 persona descriptions from danish industries and organizations","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.igi-global.com/article/a-template-for-design-personas/136351","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.10-000906","identifier":[{"id":"84944676900","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-115faa75-e4c6-4d98-8e77-09129739fd37","itu-f5fc005f-585b-41b7-b80e-06236e9d5b51"],"keyword":["Design","Industry","Personas"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1A138FA2FB3344146D477BFB08C98800"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, HCI-Lab","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Information Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Research Centre for Socio-Interactive Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kira Storgaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Kira Storgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"stagepau","last":"Stage","locid":"bfb986dc-20bc-4ff4-acd3-322363bfaedb","name":"Stage, Jan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jane","key":"billestruppau","last":"Billestrup","locid":"314ec179-6966-4367-9287-0a5e6c48a6b3","name":"Billestrup, Jane","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4018/ijskd.2015010104","issn":["19416253","19416261"],"issn_org":["19416253"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Sociotechnology and Knowledge Development","pages":"45-61","paperid":"4","publisher":"IGI global","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Sociotechnology and Knowledge Development","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944676900"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-115faa75-e4c6-4d98-8e77-09129739fd37","itu-f5fc005f-585b-41b7-b80e-06236e9d5b51"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Template for Design Personas : Analysis of 47 Persona Descriptions from Danish Industries and Organizations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.10-000906","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: According to current recommendations, blood samples should be taken in the morning after 15 minutes' resting time. Some components exhibit diurnal variation and in response to pressures to expand opening hours and reduce waiting time, the aims of this study were to investigate the impact of resting time prior to blood sampling and diurnal variation on biochemical components, including albumin, thyrotropin (TSH), total calcium and sodium in plasma. METHODS: All patients referred to an outpatient clinic for blood sampling were included in the period Nov 2011 until June 2014 (opening hours: 7am-3pm). Each patient's arrival time and time of blood sampling were registered. The impact of resting time and the time of day for all components was analysed using simple linear regression. The \"maximum allowable bias\" was used as quality indicator for the change in reference interval. RESULTS: Significant diurnal variation was found for albumin (n = 15,544; p<2×10-16), TSH (n = 20,019; p<2×10-16), calcium (n = 13,588; p = 2.8×10-12) and sodium (n = 51,917; p<2×10-16). Further significant influence for resting time was found for albumin (p = 2.6×10-4), TSH (p = 0.004), calcium (p = 8.9×10-7) and sodium (p = 8.7×10-16). Only TSH and albumin were clinically significantly influenced by diurnal variation. Resting time had no clinically significant effect. CONCLUSIONS: We found no need for resting 15 minutes prior to blood sampling. However, diurnal variation was found to have a significant and considerable impact on TSH and, to a minor degree, albumin. This has to be taken into account to ensure that reference intervals provided by the laboratory are valid on a 24-hour basis.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bøgh Andersen, Ida","Brasen, Claus Lohman","Christensen, Henry","Nøhr-Jensen, Lene","Nielsen, Dorthe E.","Brandslund, Ivan","Madsen, Jonna Skov"],"cuid":["S02-097.22-049670"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Blood Specimen Collection","Circadian rhythm","Humans","Journal Article","Reference Standards","Reference Values","Rest","Risk Factors","Time Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Department of Clinical Immunology and Biochemistry, Lillebaelt Hospital, Kolding, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"standardised resting time prior to blood sampling and diurnal variation associated with risk of patient misclassification results from selected biochemical components","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0140475","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.22-049670","identifier":[{"id":"84949033623","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26461522","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4604193","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-f03c691c-8707-48db-9354-ec9376a19231","ucl-b5a8e89c-62d9-4a0d-a337-756843245567"],"keyword":["Blood Specimen Collection","Circadian Rhythm","Humans","Journal Article","Reference Standards","Reference Values","Rest","Risk Factors","Time Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7D56540437E71C2E3F893343F71DE55F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0140475","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Biochemistry and Immunology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Department of Clinical Immunology and Biochemistry, Lillebaelt Hospital, Vejle, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Bioanalytikeruddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Clinical Immunology and Biochemistry, Lillebaelt Hospital, Kolding, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida","key":"bøghandersenpau","last":"Bøgh Andersen","locid":"a2b62a43-cbfb-4a37-84e3-664c695a8b96","name":"Bøgh Andersen, Ida","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida B","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Ida B","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus L.","key":"brasenpau","last":"Brasen","locid":"beca93c9-b25f-44f8-aeac-336a55cf3e7f","name":"Brasen, Claus Lohman","name_org":"Brasen, Claus L.","orcid":"0000-0001-8654-2449","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henry","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"ed0d0824-1937-4a8c-ae21-8aa9ec01c9a2","name":"Christensen, Henry","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nøhrjensenpau","last":"Nøhr-Jensen","locid":"2bfb7867-0beb-4008-a970-7f2cf6075bd3","name":"Nøhr-Jensen, Lene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"noehrjensenpau","last":"Noehr-Jensen","locid":"085a9681-3541-4435-84af-55b8acd2acd9","name":"Nøhr-Jensen, Lene","name_org":"Noehr-Jensen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0001-5176-819X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe E.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe E.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivan","key":"brandslundpau","last":"Brandslund","locid":"a81731b6-2c07-4eb3-8f89-3da6650c226b","name":"Brandslund, Ivan","orcid":"0000-0002-4203-5442","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonna S.","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"084866f4-85eb-4e1f-abc1-b09397af74e2","name":"Madsen, Jonna Skov","name_org":"Madsen, Jonna S.","orcid":"0000-0001-6668-4714","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26461522"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0140475","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"10","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0140475","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949033623"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f03c691c-8707-48db-9354-ec9376a19231","ucl-b5a8e89c-62d9-4a0d-a337-756843245567"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"Standardised Resting Time Prior to Blood Sampling and Diurnal Variation Associated with Risk of Patient Misclassification : Results from Selected Biochemical Components","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.22-049670","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Type 2 diabetes is associated with abnormal electrical conduction and sudden cardiac death, but the pathogenic mechanism remains unknown. This study describes electrophysiological alterations in a diet-induced pre-diabetic rat model and examines the underlying mechanism. METHODS: Sprague-Dawley rats were fed either high-fat diet and fructose water or normal chow and water for 6 weeks. The electrophysiological properties of the whole heart was analyzed by in vivo surface ECG recordings, as wells as ex vivo in Langendorff perfused hearts during baseline, ischemia and re-perfussion. Conduction velocity was examined in isolated tissue strips. Ion channel and gap junction conductances were analyzed by patch-clamp studies in isolated cardiomyocytes. Fibrosis was examined by Masson's Trichrome staining and thin-layer chromatography was used to analyze cardiac lipid content. Connexin43 (Cx43) expression and distribution was examined by western blotting and immunofluorescence respectively. RESULTS: Following 6 weeks of feeding, fructose-fat fed rats (FFFRs) showed QRS prolongation compared to controls (16.1 ± 0.51 (n = 6) vs. 14.7 ± 0.32 ms (n = 4), p < 0.05). Conduction velocity was slowed in FFFRs vs. controls (0.62 ± 0.02 (n = 13) vs. 0.79 ± 0.06 m/s (n = 11), p < 0.05) and Langendorff perfused FFFR hearts were more prone to ventricular fibrillation during reperfusion following ischemia (p < 0.05). The patch-clamp studies revealed no changes in Na(+) or K(+) currents, cell capacitance or gap junctional coupling. Cx43 expression was also unaltered in FFFRs, but immunofluorescence demonstrated an increased fraction of Cx43 localized at the intercalated discs in FFFRs compared to controls (78 ± 3.3 (n = 5) vs. 60 ± 4.2 % (n = 6), p < 0.01). No fibrosis was detected but FFFRs showed a significant increase in cardiac triglyceride content (1.93 ± 0.19 (n = 12) vs. 0.77 ± 0.13 nmol/mg (n = 12), p < 0.0001). CONCLUSION: Six weeks on a high fructose-fat diet cause electrophysiological changes, which leads to QRS prolongation, decreased conduction velocity and increased arrhythmogenesis during reperfusion. These alterations are not explained by altered gap junctional coupling, Na(+), or K(+) currents, differences in cell size or fibrosis.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","Calloe, Kirstine","Braunstein, Thomas Hartig","Riemann, Mads","Hofgaard, Johannes Pauli","Liang, Bo","Jensen, Christa Funch","Olsen, Kristine Boisen","Bartels, Emil D","Baandrup, Ulrik","Jespersen, Thomas","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Holstein-Rathlou, Niels-Henrik","Nielsen, Morten Schak"],"cuid":["S02-098.21-004451"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diet induced pre diabetes slows cardiac conductance and promotes arrhythmogenesis","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12933-015-0246-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.21-004451","identifier":[{"id":"26169175","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84988942633","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000357916300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC4504126","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-5b70af2c-dc63-4567-8661-d496a3af6dff","ku-e726a1fc-f256-4535-964d-445a5c6785f0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1C76C05EB129519E28937EE8253F1BF6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/162680760/Diet_induced_pre_diabetes_slows_cardiac_conductance_and_promotes_arrhythmogenesis.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12933-015-0246-8","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Cardiology and Membrane Proteins","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Anatomy, Biochemistry and Physiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, IKVH Fysiologi og ernæring samt pelsdyrfarmen","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Physiology and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for Clinical Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Nygaard","key":"axelsenlenenygaardpau","last":"Axelsen","name":"Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine","key":"calloekirstinepau","last":"Callø","locid":"9fc39d74-d0ac-4774-b837-de97103c87f0","name":"Calloe, Kirstine","name_org":"Callø, Kirstine","orcid":"0000-0002-1777-7938","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Ha