sity, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, Centre for Education Policy Research (Learning)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Center for Kvalitative Studier","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Centre for Cultural Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Pædagogisk Psykologi i Socialt Arbejde","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Qualitative Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Klaus","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8a1daf8c-059b-4dba-9581-630a15523fa3","name":"Nielsen, Klaus","orcid":"0000-0001-7287-8400","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"tanggaardpau","last":"Tanggaard","locid":"1c9bfda9-8265-4a28-a2da-8d733a2c43e2","name":"Tanggaard, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-3183-3972","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/19012276.2015.1028763","issn":["09008772","19040016"],"issn_org":["19040016"],"issue":"2","journal":"Nordic Psychology","pages":"154-167","paperid":"4","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Nordic Psychology","title_org":"Nordic Psychology (Online)","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84930753761"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0bbf47ce-1c99-4e80-9aa3-5bb374afdb14","au-c3dc2b6e-8e76-4f7d-8fb4-20218cc0ec45"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Dropping out and a crisis of trust","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.56-000616","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Individual Placement and Support (IPS) appears to be an effective vocational intervention for obtaining competitive employment for people with severe mental illness. However, no IPS studies or trials have been conducted in Denmark, a country characterized by a specialized labor market with a higher minimum wage and fewer entry-level jobs in comparison with other countries such as the US. Furthermore, long-term job retention and economic self-sufficiency have not been clearly demonstrated. Integrating methods such as cognitive remediation and work-related social skills training may be ways to address these issues. METHODS/DESIGN: The trial design is an investigator-initiated, randomized, assessor-blinded, multi-center trial. A total of 750 patients with severe mental illness will be randomly assigned into three groups: (1) IPS, (2) IPS enhanced with cognitive remediation and work-related social skills training, and (3) service as usual. The primary outcome is number of hours in competitive employment or education at 18-month follow-up. Secondary and exploratory outcomes are money earned, days to first employment, symptoms, functional level, self-esteem, and self-efficacy at 18-month follow-up. Thirty- and 60-month follow-ups will be register-based. DISCUSSION: This will be one of the largest randomized trials investigating IPS to date. The trial will be conducted with high methodological quality in order to reduce the risk of bias. If the results of this trial show that IPS, or IPS enhanced with cognitive remediation and work-related social skills training, is superior to service as usual, this will support preliminary evidence. Furthermore, it will show that the method is generalizable to a variety of labor markets and welfare systems and provide important knowledge about the effect of adding cognitive remediation and social skills training to the IPS intervention. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials registration number: NCT01722344 (registered 2 Nov. 2012).","author_count":7,"contributors":["Christensen, Thomas Nordahl","Nielsen, Iben Gammelgaard","Stenager, Elsebeth","Morthorst, Britt Reuter","Lindschou, Jane","Nordentoft, Merete","Eplov, Lene Falgaard"],"cuid":["S02-098.08-041752"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adaptation Psychological","Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Cognition","Cognitive Therapy","Cognitive remediation","Denmark","Employment Supported","Female","Humans","Individual placement and support","Job Description","Male","Mental Disorders","Mentally Disabled Persons","Middle Aged","Rehabilitation Vocational","Research Design","Self Concept","Self efficacy","Severe mental illness","Social skills","Supported employment","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome","Vocational education","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"individual placement and support supplemented with cognitive remediation and work related social skills training in denmark study protocol for a randomized controlled trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-015-0792-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.08-041752","identifier":[{"id":"84932605018","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26093636","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4479316","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-3eb92d87-7dac-4729-b307-1728ff4f2eb6","sdu-d0afe11d-361e-4031-a9bc-726c919f27dc"],"keyword":["Adaptation, Psychological","Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Cognition","Cognitive Therapy","Cognitive remediation","Competitive education","Competitive employment","Denmark","Education of Intellectually Disabled","Employment, Supported","Female","Humans","Individual placement and support","Job Description","Male","Mental Disorders","Mentally Disabled Persons","Middle Aged","Rehabilitation, Vocational","Research Design","Self Concept","Self Efficacy","Severe mental illness","Social Skills","Social skills training","Supported employment","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome","Vocational Education","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F5DB2B217BE249D06AC916B24D385760"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-015-0792-0","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154380454/s13063_015_0792_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Psychiatry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Thomas Nordahl","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Thomas Nordahl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben Gammelgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"9ae2751d-62bd-4ac8