University Press","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Nutrition","volume":"113"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84927093615"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University College Absalon","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c2c7d843-c128-42ba-ab1c-c4849a3743fa","sdu-38593beb-b05d-4792-9151-745131540ff6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Intervention effects on dietary intake among children by maternal education level: results of the Copenhagen School Child Intervention Study (CoSCIS)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-037006","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"A method was developed for simultaneous determination of the mycotoxins: ochratoxin A (OTA) and fumonisins B2 (FB2), B4 (FB4), and B6 (FB6) in green, roasted, and instant coffee. Extraction was performed by QuEChERS (quick, easy, cheap, effective, rugged, and safe) under acidic conditions followed by mixed-mode reversed phase-anion exchange solid phase extraction. OTA and FB2 were detected at levels down to 0.5 and 2 μg/kg by UHPLC-MS/MS and quantitated via isotope dilution using U−13C-labeled FB2 and OTA as internal standards. Mixing 20% isopropanol in the acetonitrile of the acidic UHPLC gradient system increased the signal intensity by 50% and decreased the ion-suppression with 50−75% in roasted coffee samples. About half of the roasted coffee samples (n = 57, from 9 countries) contained detectable levels of OTA, however, with only 5 samples above the EU regulatory limit of 5 μg/kg and the highest with 21 μg/kg. None of the 25 instant coffee samples contained OTA above the EU regulatory level of 10 μg/kg. Nonetheless, the toxin could be detected in 56% of the analyzed instant coffee samples. Fumonisins were not detected in any of the roasted or instant coffee samples (n = 82). However, in the green coffee samples (n = 18) almost half of the samples were positive with a maximum value of 164 μg/kg (sum of FB2, FB4, and FB6). This discrepancy between green coffee and processed coffees indicated that the fumonisins decompose during the roasting process, which was confirmed in roasting experiments. Here fumonisins could not be detected after roasting of the green, 164 μg/kg coffee, sample. Under the same conditions, OTA was reduced from 2.4 to 0.5 μg/kg.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Kristian Fog","Ngemela, Archard Ferdinand","Jensen, Lene Bai","Soman De Medeiros, Lívia","Rasmussen, Peter Have"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-339472"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South"],"country":["Brazil"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Federal University of São Carlos"],"keyword":["Aspergillus niger","Coffee","Fumonisin","Isotope dilution","LC MS MS","Ochratoxin A","QuEChERS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uhplc ms ms determination of ochratoxin a and fumonisins in coffee using quechers extraction combined with mixed mode spe purification","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/jf504254q","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-339472","identifier":[{"id":"25553918","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84921889258","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-74e44cee-e829-4992-96f1-ed5b7653c4d0"],"keyword":["Aspergillus niger","Coffee","Fumonisin","Isotope dilution","LC-MS/MS","Mixed-mode reversed phase-anion exchange","Ochratoxin A","QuEChERS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2BA307BC9E29853B5FAE922EA28AD15E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/jf504254q","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Metabolomics Platform"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"br","key":"federal university of são carlos","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Federal University of São Carlos","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Fog","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d2067ee9-e48c-4cf4-ac8f-ee775d8aff5a","name":"Nielsen, Kristian Fog","orcid":"0000-0002-5848-0911","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Archard Ferdinand","key":"ngemelapau","last":"Ngemela","name":"Ngemela, Archard Ferdinand","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Bai","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b7e67fe0-ade1-49ce-8243-b82cb942a492","name":"Jensen, Lene Bai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lívia","key":"somandemedeirospau","last":"Soman De Medeiros","name":"Soman De Medeiros, Lívia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Have","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"5a055633-ddec-4377-b0be-ce7e7ae75363","name":"Rasmussen, Peter Have","orcid":"0000-0003-0940-8531","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25553918"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/jf504254q","issn":["00218561","15205118"],"issn_org":["00218561"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry","pages":"1029-1034","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84921889258"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-74e44cee-e829-4992-96f1-ed5b7653c4d0"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"UHPLC-MS/MS Determination of Ochratoxin A and Fumonisins in Coffee Using QuEChERS Extraction Combined with Mixed-Mode SPE Purification","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-339472","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Jacobsen, Lene","Berg, Søren","Skov, Christian","Nielsen, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-373257"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nye moser til brakvandsaborrer i sydsjælland","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.fiskepleje.dk/Nyheder/2015/01/Brakvandsaborre-sydsjaelland","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-373257","ids":["dtu-e5d4acf1-ce84-4d3a-a63b-82b41118d698"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-54E2C0431A00AB67322D913BDD47CC22"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.fiskepleje.dk/Nyheder/2015/01/Brakvandsaborre-sydsjaelland","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Freshwater Fisheries Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"c9b73878-bc67-4632-9a34-0c1244b7983d","name":"Jacobsen, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","locid":"a89cb62d-3997-46ee-ab67-1d575fc67ec2","name":"Berg, Søren","orcid":"0000-0001-8772-0921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"f825c923-9ddc-4c63-885b-be6e6bddfb12","name":"Skov, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8547-6520","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59d1209-447c-4660-bc17-af58d6b9461b","name":"Nielsen, Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-9961-2933","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["dtu-e5d4acf1-ce84-4d3a-a63b-82b41118d698"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Nye moser til brakvandsaborrer i Sydsjælland","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-373257","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: SK channels have functional importance in the cardiac atrium of many species, including humans. Pharmacological blockage of SK channels has been reported to be antiarrhythmic in animal models of atrial fibrillation, however, the exact antiarrhythmic mechanism of SK channel inhibition remains unclear. OBJECTIVES: We speculated that together with a direct inhibition of repolarizing SK current, the previously observed depolarization of the atrial resting membrane potential (RMP) after SK channel inhibition reduces sodium channel availability thereby prolonging the effective refractory period (ERP) and slowing the conduction velocity. We therefore aimed at elucidating these properties of SK channel inhibition and the underlying antiarrhythmic mechanisms by using; microelectrode action potential recordings and conduction velocity measurements in isolated rat atrium. Automated patch-clamping and two-electrode voltage-clamp was used to access INa and IK,ACh respectively. RESULTS: The SK channel inhibitor N-(pyridin-2-yl)-4-(pyridin-2-yl)thiazol-2-amine (ICA) exhibited antiarrhythmic effects. ICA prevented electrically induced runs of atrial fibrillation in the isolated right atrium and induced atrial post-repolarization-refractoriness and depolarized the resting membrane potential (RMP). Moreover, ICA (1-10 µM) was found to slow conduction velocity, however, due to a marked prolongation of ERP the calculated wavelength was increased. Furthermore, at increased pacing frequencies SK channel inhibition by ICA (10-30 µM) demonstrated prominent depression of other sodium channel-dependent parameters. ICA did not inhibit IK,ACh, but at concentrations above 10 µM ICA use-dependently inhibited INa. CONCLUSION: SK channel inhibition modulates multiple parameters of the action potential. It prolongs the action potential duration, and shifts the RMP towards more depolarized potentials through direct ISK block. This indirectly leads to sodium channel inhibition through accumulation of state-dependently inactivated channels, which ultimately slows conduction and decreases excitability. However a contribution from a direct sodium channel inhibition cannot be ruled. We here propose that the primary antiarrhythmic mechanism of SK channel inhibition is through direct potassium channel block and via indirect sodium channel inhibition.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Skibsbye, Lasse","Wang, Xiaodong","Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","Bomholtz, Sofia Hammami","Nielsen, Morten Schak","Grunnet, Morten","Bentzen, Bo Hjorth","Jespersen, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-450769"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antiarrhythmic mechanisms of sk channel inhibition in the rat atrium","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-450769","identifier":[{"id":"84931464891","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25856531","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5fc5a43a-7d26-4997-a7d1-5165adf7eb07"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF12E62B3F53916F61B68C91EE6D9B34"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Cardiology and Membrane Proteins"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lasse","key":"skibsbyepau","last":"Skibsbye","locid":"d3afe683-ded3-4602-b92c-87daa1943c7e","name":"Skibsbye, Lasse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiaodong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiaodong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Nygaard","key":"axelsenpau","last":"Axelsen","locid":"2632f623-a6d6-49e1-884c-0560715787be","name":"Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sofia Hammami","key":"bomholtzpau","last":"Bomholtz","locid":"9f04bcba-d1b2-43c3-96f9-324521d9ff10","name":"Bomholtz, Sofia Hammami","orcid":"0000-0001-7221-4532","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Schak","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b203113e-fe9b-4863-8eb0-3022ca8cc9e2","name":"Nielsen, Morten Schak","orcid":"0000-0002-9718-5421","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"grunnetpau","last":"Grunnet","locid":"b17b3f5b-0621-42a0-9870-a5921c3ee2b9","name":"Grunnet, Morten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo Hjorth","key":"bentzenpau","last":"Bentzen","locid":"59e5d901-5519-4467-870f-b60d716e9b6f","name":"Bentzen, Bo Hjorth","orcid":"0000-0002-0253-4992","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"db23d6cb-3abe-4ba2-b1d3-44f918c72e51","name":"Jespersen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-6575-360X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25856531"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/fjc.0000000000000259","issn":["01602446","15334023"],"issn_org":["01602446"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Cardiovascular Pharmacology","pages":"165-176","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cardiovascular Pharmacology","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84931464891"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5fc5a43a-7d26-4997-a7d1-5165adf7eb07"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Antiarrhythmic Mechanisms of SK Channel Inhibition in the Rat Atrium","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-450769","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The aim was to explore whether the incidence of tonsillar squamous cell carcinomas (TSCCs) increased in Eastern Denmark, 2000-2010, and whether human papillomavirus (HPV) could explain the increase, and to assess the association of HPV prevalence with gender, age, and origin (i.e., the certainty of tonsillar tumor origin). We applied HPV DNA PCR and p16 immunohistochemistry to all TSCCs registered in the Danish Head and Neck Cancer Group (DAHANCA) and in the Danish Pathology Data Bank (n = 632). Pathologists reviewed and subdivided the tumors into two groups: specified and nonspecified TSCCs. Approximately 10% of HPV-positive tumors was genotyped by amplicon next-generation sequencing. The overall crude incidence of TSCCs increased significantly (2.7% per year) and was explained by an increasing incidence of HPV-positive TSCCs (4.9% per year). The overall HPV prevalence was 58%, with HPV16 being the predominant HPV type. In multivariate analysis, the HPV prevalence was associated with age (<55 vs. >60 years) (OR, 1.72; 95% CI 1.13-2.63) and origin (nonspecified vs. specified TSCCs) (OR, 0.15; 95% CI 0.11-0.22). The association of HPV prevalence with origin increased over time in specified TSCCs (OR per year, 1.10; 95% CI 1.01-1.19), whereas no change over time was observed among nonspecified TSCCs (OR per year, 0.99; 95% CI 0.90-1.08). In conclusion, the observed increase in the number of HPV-positive TSCCs can explain the increasing number of TSCCs in Eastern Denmark, 2000-2010. HPV prevalence was associated with younger age (<55 years) and a high certainty of tonsillar tumor origin.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Garnaes, Emilie","Kiss, Katalin","Andersen, Luise","Therkildsen, Marianne Hamilton","Franzmann, Maria B","Filtenborg-Barnkob, Bettina","Høgdall, Estrid","Krenk, Lene","Josiassen, Michael","Lajer, Christel Bræmer","Specht, Lena","Frederiksen, Kirsten","Friis-Hansen, Lennart","Nielsen, Finn Cilius","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Norrild, Bodil","von Buchwald, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-476501"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a high and increasing hpv prevalence in tonsillar cancers in eastern denmark 000000002000 000000002010 the largest registry based study to date","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-476501","identifier":[{"id":"84923073169","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25283302","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8aecf14d-488f-4a09-b387-b367a2c698c2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4245EC020C58F319E433B9ACF1D92198"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Emilie","key":"garnaespau","last":"Garnaes","name":"Garnaes, Emilie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Katalin","key":"kisspau","last":"Kiss","name":"Kiss, Katalin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Luise","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Luise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne H","key":"therkildsenpau","last":"Therkildsen","locid":"2450e96f-b92a-415f-a003-b457b37b7908","name":"Therkildsen, Marianne Hamilton","name_org":"Therkildsen, Marianne H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","