{"abstract":"To develop and validate a taxonomy to classify and support the analysis of adverse events related to patient handovers in hospital settings. A taxonomy was established using descriptions of handover events extracted from incident reports, interviews and root cause analysis reports. The inter-rater reliability and distribution of types of handover failures and causal factors. The taxonomy contains five types of failures and seven types of main causal factors. The taxonomy was validated against 432 adverse handover event descriptions contained in incident reports (stratified random sample from the Danish Patient Safety Database, 200 events) and 47 interviews with staff conducted at a large hospital in the Capital Region (232 events). The most prevalent causes of adverse events are inadequate competence (30 %), inadequate infrastructure (22 %) and busy ward (18 %). Inter-rater reliability (kappa) was 0.76 and 0.87 for reports and interviews, respectively. Communication in clinical contexts has been widely recognized as giving rise to potentially hazardous events, and handover situations are particularly prone to failures of communication or unclear allocation of responsibility. The taxonomy provides a tool for analyzing adverse handover events to identify frequent causes among reported handover failures. In turn, this provides a basis for selecting safety measures including handover protocols and training programmes.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Andersen, Henning Boje","Siemsen, Inger Margrete D.","Petersen, Lene Funck","Nielsen, Jacob","Østergaard, Doris"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340894"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adverse events","Communication","Handover","Patient handoff","Patient handover","Patient safety","Taxonomies","Taxonomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development and validation of a taxonomy of adverse handover events in hospital settings","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/101901140/Development_and_validation_of_a_taxonomy.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340894","identifier":[{"id":"84925482599","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-79bac143-dcd8-4679-abff-6594b6b523c1"],"keyword":["Adverse events","Communication","Handover","Hospital settings","Patient handoff","Patient handover","Patient safety","Taxonomies","Taxonomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4873D360FC3F81ABB068DD514CC4DC55"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10111-014-0303-1","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/101901140/Development_and_validation_of_a_taxonomy.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Technology and Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["University Hospital Herlev"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henning Boje","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a4c14257-7af7-40ed-a3d0-a635bf40f0c3","name":"Andersen, Henning Boje","orcid":"0000-0002-4787-8502","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Inger Margrete D.","key":"siemsenpau","last":"Siemsen","name":"Siemsen, Inger Margrete D.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Funck","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Lene Funck","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jacob","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Doris","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","name":"Østergaard, Doris","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10111-014-0303-1","issn":["14355558","14355566"],"issn_org":["14355558"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cognition, Technology and Work","pages":"79-87","publisher":"Springer London","status":"p","title":"Cognition, Technology and Work","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925482599"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-79bac143-dcd8-4679-abff-6594b6b523c1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Development and validation of a taxonomy of adverse handover events in hospital settings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340894","year":"2015","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"OncomiRs miR-21 and miR-155 have been linked to lymphomagenesis, but information on their implication in diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) is limited. Here, we used locked nucleic acid-based in situ hybridization (ISH) detection techniques on formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded DLBCL tissue samples to identify miR-155 and miR-21 at the cellular level in 56 patients diagnosed with DLBCL, and compared them to miR array data. miR-155 was observed in tumor cells in 19/56 (33.9%) of the samples evaluated by ISH. miR-21 was localized to the stromal compartment in 41/56 (73.2%). A subset of these, 16/56 (28.6%), also showed labeling in tumor cells. When comparing ISH-scores and miR array data, miR-155 in tumor cells, identified by ISH, was associated with miR-155 expression in miR array data (P=0.030). Equally, miR-21 expression by miR array data were highly associated with miR-21 ISH-scores in the stromal cells (P=0.002), whereas no association between miR array data and ISH of miR-21 in tumor cells was observed (P=0.673). We found no association of miR-155 and miR-21 with overall survival or germinal center B-cell-like (GCB) versus non-GCB-like subtypes of DLBCL. In conclusion, miR-ISH added to the biological interpretation of miR expression in DLBCL compared with miR array data, but miR-155 and miR-21 ISH did not add prognostic information in this series.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Munch-Petersen, Helga D","Ralfkiaer, Ulrik","Sjö, Lene Dissing","Hother, Christoffer","Asmar, Fazila","Nielsen, Boye S","Brown, Peter","Ralfkiaer, Elisabeth","Grønbæk, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-395989"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Female","Gene Expression Regulation Neoplastic","Humans","Lymphoma Large B Cell Diffuse","Male","MicroRNAs","Middle Aged","RNA Neoplasm","Stromal Cells"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differential expression of mir 000000000155 and mir 000000000021 in tumor and stroma cells in diffuse large b cell lymphoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-395989","identifier":[{"id":"25265435","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84925872555","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-043e0fc1-4922-4137-9597-082a6b361175"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Female","Gene Expression Regulation, Neoplastic","Humans","Lymphoma, Large B-Cell, Diffuse","Male","MicroRNAs","Middle Aged","RNA, Neoplasm","Stromal Cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2DF9AE1EE2D2D97B843AA1C856E8EFA4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Helga D","key":"munchpetersenhelgadpau","last":"Munch-Petersen","name":"Munch-Petersen, Helga D","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulrik","key":"ralfkiaerulrikpau","last":"Ralfkiaer","name":"Ralfkiaer, Ulrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene D","key":"sjölenedissingpau","last":"Sjö","locid":"5f179427-1ae6-4519-a858-32ca986f7db8","name":"Sjö, Lene Dissing","name_org":"Sjö, Lene D","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christoffer","key":"hotherchristofferpau","last":"Hother","name":"Hother, Christoffer","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fazila","key":"asmarfazilapau","last":"Asmar","name":"Asmar, Fazila","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Boye S","key":"nielsenboyespau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Boye S","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"brownpeterpau","last":"Brown","name":"Brown, Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Elisabeth","key":"ralfkiaerelisabethpau","last":"Ralfkiaer","locid":"316fda1e-aadd-4fea-a78f-a2a08f83757d","name":"Ralfkiaer, Elisabeth","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"grønbækkirstenpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"82ff4ce1-979f-44c9-b095-72c4a3dca507","name":"Grønbæk, Kirsten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25265435"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/pai.0000000000000073","issn":["15334058","15412016"],"issn_org":["15412016"],"issue":"3","journal":"Applied Immunohistochemistry & Molecular Morphology","pages":"188-195","status":"p","title":"Applied Immunohistochemistry & Molecular Morphology","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925872555"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-043e0fc1-4922-4137-9597-082a6b361175"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Differential Expression of miR-155 and miR-21 in Tumor and Stroma Cells in Diffuse Large B-Cell Lymphoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-395989","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Topoisomerase 1 (TOP1) and 2A (TOP2A) are potential predictive biomarkers for irinotecan and anthracycline treatment, respectively, in colorectal cancer (CRC), and we have recently reported a high frequency of gene gain of the TOP1 and TOP2A genes in CRC. Furthermore, Mismatch Repair (MMR) subtypes of CRC have been associated with benefit from adjuvant chemotherapy of primary CRC. Given the involvement of the topoisomerase enzymes in DNA replication and repair, we raised the hypothesis that an association may exist between TOP gene copy numbers and MMR proficiency/deficiency in CRC. MATERIAL AND METHODS: Test cohort: FISH analysis with an in-house TOP1/CEN20 probe mix and a commercially available TOP2A/CEN17 (Dako, Glostrup, Denmark) probe mix was performed on archival formalin fixed paraffin embedded (FFPE) tissue samples from 18 patients with proficient MMR (pMMR) CRC and 18 patients with deficient MMR (dMMR) CRC. TOP1 and TOP2A gene copy numbers and their ratios per nucleus were correlated with MMR status using the Mann-Whitney test. Validation cohort: FFPE samples from 154 patients with primary stage III CRC (originally included in the RANX05 study) were classified according to MMR status by immunohistochemical analysis using validated antibodies for MLH1, MLH2, MSH6 and PMS2, and information on TOP1, CEN20, TOP2A and CEN17 status was previously published for this cohort. RESULTS: The observed TOP1 gene copy numbers in the 36 CRC test cohort were significantly greater (p < 0.01) in the pMMR subgroup (mean: 3.84, SD: 2.03) than in the dMMR subgroup (mean: 1.50, SD: 0.12). Similarly, the TOP2A copy numbers were significantly greater (p < 0.01) in the pMMR subgroup (mean: 1.99, SD: 0.52) than in the dMMR subgroup (mean: 1.52, SD: 0.10). These findings were confirmed in the validation cohort, where in the pMMR subgroup 51% had ≥2 extra TOP1 copies per cell, while all tumors classified as dMMR had diploid TOP1 status and mean TOP2A copy numbers were 2.30 (SD: 1.36) and 1.80 (SD: 0.31) (p = 0.01) in the pMMR subgroup vs. dMMR subgroup, respectively. DISCUSSION AND CONCLUSION: Our results show that TOP1 and TOP2A gene copy numbers are increased in the pMMR subgroup. We propose that this preference may reflect a selective pressure to gain and/or maintain the gained extra copies of topoisomerase genes whose products are required to cope with high replication stress present in the pMMR tumors, thereby providing a survival advantage selectively in pMMR tumors. Future studies should test this concept and explore potential differences between pMMR and dMMR tumors in response to Top1 and Top2 inhibitors.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Sønderstrup, Ida Marie Heeholm","Nygård, Sune Boris","Poulsen, Tim Svenstrup","Linnemann, Dorte","Stenvang, Jan","Nielsen, Hans Jørgen","Bartek, Jiri","Brünner, Nils","Nørgaard, Peter","Riis, Lene Buhl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-468204"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"topoisomerase 000000000001 and 000000000002a gene copy numbers are elevated in mismatch repair proficient colorectal cancers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-468204","identifier":[{"id":"25777966","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84929506829","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7cd314c5-3a63-4d15-a476-4b643e47484b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-700030E12AC11A3BEA4DAB44B9EF9905"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Molecular Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ida Marie Heeholm","key":"sønderstruppau","last":"Sønderstrup","name":"Sønderstrup, Ida Marie Heeholm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sune Boris","key":"nygårdpau","last":"Nygård","locid":"402a6a61-31e7-44d8-8f5d-70b8447a0d4a","name":"Nygård, Sune Boris","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tim Svenstrup","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"2a791cba-1299-480a-b01a-2609fc5a74a5","name":"Poulsen, Tim Svenstrup","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorte","key":"linnemannpau","last":"Linnemann","locid":"e2322cce-22a2-4ce2-ad9e-3c921f8334aa","name":"Linnemann, Dorte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan","key":"stenvangpau","last":"Stenvang","locid":"f30506ab-ea0e-4605-89ab-2225b093d78a","name":"Stenvang, Jan","orcid":"0000-0001-5647-4828","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hans Jørgen",