{"abstract":"Ash dieback caused by the pathogenic fungus Hymenoscyphus fraxineus [previously known as H. pseudoalbidus (sexual stage) and Chalara fraxinea (asexual stage)] is a widespread problem in Europe. Here, we assess crown damage from natural infection and necrosis development following artificial controlled inoculations on full-sib and half-sib progeny from Danish Fraxinus excelsior clones with contrasting and well-characterized levels of susceptibility to the disease. The inoculation assay was performed on a total of 123 offspring, and necrosis development monitored over two years. The offspring from low susceptible mother clones developed smaller necroses when compared to offspring from susceptible clones. Their crown damage due to natural infections was also significantly less. The correlation coefficient between average crown damages of mother clones and the average of their progeny was 0.85 (natural infections), while the correlation between crown damage of mother clones and the average necrosis development in their progeny after controlled inoculation was 0.73. The correlation between resistance of parent trees and crown damage/necrosis development on their offspring confirms the presence of heritable resistance and indicates that a bioassay based on controlled inoculations has the potential of becoming a fast and cost-effective tool for estimation of dieback susceptibility in breeding programmes for resistance in ash trees.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lobo, Albin","McKinney, Lea Vig","Hansen, Jon Kehlet","Kjær, Erik Dahl","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-451492"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic variation in dieback resistance in fraxinus excelsior confirmed by progeny inoculation assay","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-451492","identifier":[{"id":"84944513561","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6102957f-8e4c-42f7-9283-a93af58060e6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4FEE733B51A244DCE22513BF5AFFCE73"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Albin","key":"lobopau","last":"Lobo","locid":"50b0d4fe-6e8d-4245-aded-c406110ff0b0","name":"Lobo, Albin","orcid":"0000-0002-9580-2860","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lea Vig","key":"mckinneypau","last":"McKinney","locid":"060df27a-59d3-4457-81a2-185cca16ae68","name":"McKinney, Lea Vig","orcid":"0000-0001-6601-4614","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jon Kehlet","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b8c2f3eb-b79f-46cc-b346-8300943e2129","name":"Hansen, Jon Kehlet","orcid":"0000-0002-1260-3509","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/efp.12179","issn":["14374781","14390329"],"issn_org":["14374781"],"issue":"5","journal":"Forest Pathology","pages":"379-387","status":"p","title":"Forest Pathology","title_org":"Forest Pathology (Print)","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944513561"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6102957f-8e4c-42f7-9283-a93af58060e6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genetic variation in dieback resistance in Fraxinus excelsior confirmed by progeny inoculation assay","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-451492","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Aims: To examine contemporary rates of severe hypoglycemia (SH) and identify the effect of predictors of SH in a pediatric type 1 diabetes population. Methods: The national diabetes register provided data on children residing in Denmark from 2008 to 2013 in this register-based population study. Robust Poisson regression models were applied. Results: The study population [n = 2,715 (50.9 % boys), mean (SD) age at onset; 8.1 (4.0) years, diabetes duration; 5.6 (4.9) years] comprised 7,390 person-years of data and 561 events of SH. The overall incidence of SH was 7.6 per 100 person-years. The incidence rate peaked with 16.0 per 100 person-years in 2008 reaching a nadir of 4.9 in 2011. Overall, insulin pump reduced the rate of SH with 27 % compared to any pen treatment (P = 0.003). When stratifying pen treatment, premixed insulin increased the rate of SH by 1.9-fold (P = 0.0015) and NPH increased the rate by 1.6-fold (P = 0.003) versus pump treatment, whereas long-acting insulin analogues were comparable with pump treatment (P = 0.1485). We found no association of SH with glycemic control (P > 0.05). Conclusions: A nationwide halving in rates of severe hypoglycemia was observed during the study period independent of the prevailing average HbA1c level. Changes in diabetes care and successful educational programs may have influenced the lower incidence rate of severe hypoglycemia.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Fredheim, Siri","Johansen, A.","Thorsen, Steffen Ullitz","Kremke, B.","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Olsen, Bo Sanderhoff","Lyngsøe, Lene","Sildorf, S. M.","Pipper, Christian Bressen","Mortensen, Henrik B","Johannesen, Jesper","Svensson, Jannet"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-454915"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Children","Hypoglycemia","Insulin therapy","Register","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nationwide reduction in the frequency of severe hypoglycemia by half","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/record/display.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84930081623&origin=resultslist&sort=plf-f&src=s&st1=Nationwide+reduction+in+the+frequency+of+severe+hypoglycemia+by+half&st2=&sid=095E7B63AB04ACB9147B6682EE127391.euC1gMODexYlPkQec4u1Q%3a280&sot=b&sdt=b&sl=75&s=TITLE%28Nationwide+reduction+in+the+frequency+of+severe+hypoglycemia+by+half%29&relpos=0&citeCnt=3&searchTerm=","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-454915","identifier":[{"id":"84930081623","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25528006","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-66f3b798-2999-4259-ae86-ac46be7306e2"],"keyword":["Children","Hypoglycemia","Insulin therapy","Register","Type 1 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8C31769E782907A35CB15B22438F665D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_