{"abstract":"No consensus exists on how to define abnormally rapid deterioration in renal function (Rapid Progression, RP). We developed an operational definition of RP in HIV-positive persons with baseline estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) >90ml/min/1.73m2 (using Cockcroft Gault) in the Data Collection on Adverse Events of Anti-HIV Drugs (D:A:D) study from 2004 to 2011.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Kamara, David A","Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Ross, Michael","Kirk, Ole","Reiss, Peter","Morlat, Philippe","Moranne, Olivier","Fux, Christoph A","Mocroft, Amanda","Sabin, Caroline","Lundgren, Jens","Smith, Colette J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-484433"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["IT Service"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of a definition for rapid progression rp of renal function in hiv positive persons the d a d study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2369-15-51","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-484433","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3987148","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84898407890","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24666792","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-983be5c1-60f7-4ff1-95ea-820e25accfe3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F405E6949EA4A2B5E83E2613CFCEACC7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2369-15-51","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen",