{"abstract":"Whilst several antiretroviral drugs have been associated with moderate chronic kidney disease (CKD), their contribution to advanced CKD and end-stage renal disease (ESRD) remain unknown.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Mocroft, Amanda","Kirk, Ole","Ross, Michael","Reiss, Peter","Fux, Christophe A","Morlat, Philippe","Moranne, Olivier","Smith, Colette","El-Sadr, Wafaa","Law, Matthew","Lundgren, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-464948"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["IT Service"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predictors of advanced chronic kidney disease and end stage renal disease in hiv positive persons","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/QAD.0000000000000042","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-464948","identifier":[{"id":"84892373117","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24361680","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-777da245-6a4c-4e63-bad4-87837205c7cb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-31B6E61F2E51ACB1F10DE2169EE55336"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/QAD.0000000000000042","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, CHIP"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["IT Service"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Ryom","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0087fd9d-3a4d-4da5-9f4d-2ba51ec7d7a8","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ryom","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Amanda","key":"mocroftpau","last":"Mocroft","name":"Mocroft, Amanda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole","key":"kirkpau","last":"Kirk","locid":"67bce469-8913-44ac-8d6d-7dff1171c771","name":"Kirk, Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael","key":"rosspau","last":"Ross","name":"Ross, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"reisspau","last":"Reiss","name":"Reiss, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christophe A","key":"fuxpau","last":"Fux","name":"Fux, Christophe A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Philippe","key":"morlatpau","last":"Morlat","name":"Morlat, Philippe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Olivier","key":"morannepau","last":"Moranne","name":"Moranne, Olivier","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Colette","key":"smithpau","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Colette","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wafaa","key":"elsadrpau","last":"El-Sadr","name":"El-Sadr, Wafaa","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew","key":"lawpau","last":"Law","name":"Law, Matthew","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens D","key":"lundgrenpau","last":"Lundgren","locid":"af310f7a-c49b-4381-bcb4-cf56e3fd80d8","name":"Lundgren, Jens","name_org":"Lundgren, Jens D","orcid":"0000-0001-8901-7850","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24361680"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/qad.0000000000000042","issn":["02699370"],"issue":"2","journal":"AIDS","pages":"187-199","status":"p","title":"AIDS","title_org":"AIDS (London, England)","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84892373117"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-777da245-6a4c-4e63-bad4-87837205c7cb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Predictors of advanced chronic kidney disease and end-stage renal disease in HIV-positive persons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-464948","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Premise of the study: Microsatellite primers were developed for an indigenous fruit tree, Parkia biglobosa, as a tool to study reproductive biology and population structure. Here we use the primers to determine the number of fathers per pod.  Methods and Results: Microsatellite loci were enriched in a genomic sample and isolated using pyrosequencing. Eleven primer pairs were characterized in two populations of P. biglobosa in Burkina Faso (each with 40 trees). The number of alleles per locus ranged from eight to 15, and one locus had null alleles. We genotyped seeds from 24 open-pollinated pods. The genotypic profiles of seeds per pod suggest that all seeds are outcrossed and that only one pollen donor sires all ovules in a single fruit.  Conclusions: Ten microsatellite markers were highly polymorphic. All seeds per pod of P. biglobosa were full siblings. The markers will be useful for reproductive and population genetic studies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lassen, Kristin Marie","Kjær, Erik Dahl","Ouédraogo, Moussa","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-497127"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Burkina Faso"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre national de semences forestières"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microsatellite primers for i parkia biglobosa i fabaceae mimosoideae reveal that a single plant sires all seeds per pod","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3732/apps.1400024","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-497127","identifier":[{"id":"25202634","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84946599927","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4103441","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-ad8d7f58-b696-4762-bc32-43e027b7160b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D0510CF1B012E951B1C8849317D54A17"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3732/apps.1400024","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.bioone.org/doi/full/10.3732/apps.1400024","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"bf","key":"centre national de semences forestières","loc":["Burkina Faso","Africa"],"name":"Centre national de semences forestières","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Kristin Marie","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"dfd9adc7-d5d9-4b69-9d66-dd59e504e238","name":"Lassen, Kristin Marie","orcid":"0000-0003-3274-4875","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Moussa","key":"ouédraogopau","last":"Ouédraogo","name":"Ouédraogo, Moussa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25202634"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3732/apps.1400024","issn":["21680450"],"issue":"6","journal":"Applications in Plant Sciences","paperid":"1400024","status":"p","title":"Applications in Plant Sciences","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84946599927"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ad8d7f58-b696-4762-bc32-43e027b7160b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Microsatellite Primers for <i>Parkia biglobosa</i> (Fabaceae: Mimosoideae) Reveal that a Single Plant Sires All Seeds Per Pod","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-497127","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To overcome problems and delays of the preparation of autologous serum eye drops, a production line of ABO-specific allogeneic serum eye drops from male blood donors was set up in a blood bank. Feasibility, clinical routine, safety and efficacy were evaluated in a cohort of patients with severe ocular surface disorders. METHODS: Serum was derived from 450 ml whole-blood donations from regular male blood donors, produced and tested according to good manufacturing practice and legislation regulating blood products in Denmark. Serum was diluted to 20% (v/v) with NaCl 0.9%, filtered, bottled, registered and stored at -30°C in the blood bank. Upon request, frozen ABO-identical serum drops in lots of 14 bottles could be provided immediately. Safety and efficacy were evaluated in 34 patients with severe ocular surface disease refractory to conventional medical therapy. Patients were treated six times daily for minimum 2-4 weeks. Objective findings and subjective symptoms were compared between day 0 and after 4 weeks of treatment using the Wilcoxon signed-rank test. RESULTS: Clinically, no side-effects were observed. In total, 59% of the patients with ocular surface changes improved objectively (slit-lamp examination). Partial or full healing of corneal changes, as well as subjective relief of symptoms, was observed in 16 of 20 patients with keratoconjunctivitis sicca (p < 0.001). The 14 patients with persistent epithelial defect experienced neither objective nor subjective improvements during serum treatment. CONCLUSION: Ready-made ABO-identical allogeneic serum eye drops were straightforwardly produced, quality-assured and registered as a safe standard blood product for the treatment of certain cases of severe dry eye disease. Therapeutic efficacy was comparable to previous reports on autologous serum drops.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Harritshøj, Lene Holm","Nielsen, Connie","Ullum, Henrik","Hansen, Morten Bagge","Julian, Hanne Olsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-516292"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ABO Blood Group System","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Blood Banks","Blood Donors","Blood Safety","Corneal Dystrophies Hereditary","Female","Humans","Keratoconjunctivitis sicca","Male","Middle Aged","Ophthalmic Solutions","Serum","Treatment Outcome","Wound Healing","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ready made allogeneic abo specific serum eye drops production from regular male blood donors clinical routine safety and efficacy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.12386","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-516292","identifier":[{"id":"85027925758","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24629028","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-cdaf6125-78d7-4bde-ac83-5e7f3cd370fa"],"keyword":["ABO Blood-Group System","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Blood Banks","Blood Donors","Blood Safety","Corneal Dystrophies, Hereditary","Epithelium, Corneal","Female","Humans","Keratoconjunctivitis Sicca","Male","Middle Aged","Ophthalmic Solutions","Serum","Treatment Outcome","Wound Healing","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BB378B9E3366E3D7C136909C280A09DD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.12386","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lene Holm","key":"harritshøjpau","last":"Harritshøj","name":"Harritshøj, Lene Holm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Connie","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Connie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"ullumpau","last":"Ullum","locid":"ef594d49-5aeb-4d32-80b4-4bfc281b5cbb","name":"Ullum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-9058","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Bagge","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"31f07839-f4e2-44f2-8668-3bd6d1a24b2f","name":"Hansen, Morten Bagge","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Olsen","key":"julianpau","last":"Julian","locid":"91fa26d0-853d-4a22-a466-8c314cc15a6c","name":"Julian, Hanne Olsen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24629028"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.12386","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"8","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"783-786","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027925758"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cdaf6125-78d7-4bde-ac83-5e7f3cd370fa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ready-made allogeneic ABO-specific serum eye drops : production from regular male blood donors, clinical routine, safety and efficacy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-516292","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The lysogenic state of the λ switch is exceptionally stable, still, it is capable of responding to DNA-damage and rapidly enter the lytic state. We invented an assay where PNA mediated tethering of a plasmid allowed for single molecule investigations of the effect of supercoiling on the efficiency of the epigenetic λ switch. Compared with non-supercoiled DNA, the presence of supercoils enhances the CI-mediated DNA looping probability and renders the transition between the looped and unlooped states steeper, thus increasing the Hill coefficient. Interestingly, the transition occurs exactly at the CI concentration corresponding to the minimum number of CI molecules capable of maintaining the pRM-repressed state. Based on these results we propose that supercoiling maintains the pRM-repressible state as CI concentration decline during induction and thus prevent autoregulation of cI from interfering with induction.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Norregaard, Kamilla","Andersson, Magnus","Sneppen, Kim","Nielsen, Peter E.","Brown, Stanley","Oddershede, Lene Broeng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-530164"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of supercoiling on the λ switch","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4161/bact.27517","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-530164","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3875608","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24386605","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e4fcc04a-745d-47f5-ba29-cea31f06d0cd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D2AF5D406273FECEB7D0B9F8D254F114"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4161/bact.27517","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Biocomplexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kamilla","key":"norregaardpau","last":"Norregaard","locid":"c34c6d45-ccd4-4be4-9728-7f492a6b4583","name":"Norregaard, Kamilla","orcid":"0000-0003-1953-9703","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Magnus","key":"anderssonpau","last":"Andersson","name":"Andersson, Magnus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim","key":"sneppenpau","last":"Sneppen","locid":"50bdf992-9fe4-4a9e-ba66-909b7e259a51","name":"Sneppen, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-9820-3567","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Eigil","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"74cb6e41-3bfc-4d0a-a0df-7bd8fa9c2856","name":"Nielsen, Peter E.","name_org":"Nielsen, Peter Eigil","orcid":"0000-0001-8771-330X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stanley","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","locid":"fe5af114-5058-406e-87f5-18be42ae3241","name":"Brown, Stanley","orcid":"0000-0002-8453-8144","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene B","key":"oddershedepau","last":"Oddershede","locid":"7474640c-fb11-45b8-abd4-8de4232d5060","name":"Oddershede, Lene Broeng","name_org":"Oddershede, Lene B","orcid":"0000-0003-2923-2844","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24386605"],"pub":{"doi":"10.4161/bact.27517","issn":["21597073","21597081"],"issn_org":["21597073"],"issue":"2","journal":"Bacteriophage","pages":"1-5","paperid":"e27517","status":"p","title":"Bacteriophage","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e4fcc04a-745d-47f5-ba29-cea31f06d0cd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of supercoiling on the λ switch","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-530164","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"I programserien Myteradio går Radio24syv i samarbejde med KORA bag om tallene og ser på nogle af de udfordringer, den offentlige sektor har. Foruden forskere fra KORA er der politikere og praktikere i studiet.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pedersen, Lene Holm","Arendt, Jacob Nielsen","Skaksen, Jan Rose","Kjellberg, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-662546"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"radio velfærdsstatens myter","src":["vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-662546","ids":["vive-2038700b-e6c3-4613-b007-61c7cee43aa8"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-97A51FC95291C6E318A53AECF79ABEBB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["VIVE - The Danish Center for Social Science Research, VIVE Governance and Management"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Holm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"72dca908-d942-4f38-818a-449bafe3542a","name":"Pedersen, Lene Holm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Nielsen","key":"arendtpau","last":"Arendt","locid":"5f27594c-28dd-40f8-8fdc-145943379191","name":"Arendt, Jacob Nielsen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Rose","key":"skaksenpau","last":"Skaksen","locid":"8d6fc116-93b4-436e-9a97-22019e749c34","name":"Skaksen, Jan Rose","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"kjellbergpau","last":"Kjellberg","locid":"aeaf985c-6162-47fa-a509-3f31a2829d5d","name":"Kjellberg, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0003-4336-2397","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["vive-2038700b-e6c3-4613-b007-61c7cee43aa8"],"src":["VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Radio: Velfærdsstatens myter","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-662546","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Snabelklove er en lidelse hos rådyr som medfører at klovene bliver meget lange. I nogle tilfælde er både bi- og hovedklove forvoksede. På grund af de deforme klove ændres dyrets benstilling, hvilket hos andre dyrearter er forbundet med lange smertevoldende forløb – og det må formodes også at være tilfældet for rådyr. Årsagen hos rådyr er ukendt, men i jægerkredse har der været spekuleret i misdannelser eller hormonforstyrrelser eller for lidt slid af klovene på grund af jordbundsforholdene. Formålet med denne undersøgelser er at fastlægge om laminitis (også kaldet forfangenhed) er den del af det kompleks af fodringsbetingende lidelser, der kan ses hos rådyr efter bratte foderskift. Hvis det viser sig at bratte foderskift kan relateres til fund af snabelklove skal resultatet anvendes til at fremme sundhedstilstanden i den danske rådyrpopulation ved at vejlede/rådgive jægere om risici ved fodring i naturen. Hos danske rådyr med og uden snabelklove er der fundet kroniske laminitisforandringer i form af konkav klovform, divergerende klovfurer, rotation af klovbenet og uregelmæssige læderhudslameller. På grund af forandringernes kroniske stadie er det ikke muligt at identificere årsagen til tilstanden, men en fodrings-relateret ætiologi kan ikke afvises. Den hyppige forekomst af klovbensrotation - også i klove der visuelt blev vurderet som normale – bør give mistanke om hyppige episoder med en udløsende faktor, da forandringer forenelig med laminitis er almindelig forekommende blandt danske rådyr. Dyr med snabelklove vil have stærkt nedsat velfærd som følge af smerte ved bevægelse, hvorfor der skal udvises forsigtighed ved fodring af vildtet, samt sikres bortskydning af dyr med snabelklove. Resultaterne blive præsenteret i bl.a. Danmarks Jægerforbunds medlemsblad ”Jægerne” og en publikation til et internationalt tidsskrift.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Mette Sif","Buelund, Lene Elisabeth","Holm, Elisabeth","Larsen, Gitte","Nielsen, Dorte Hald","Jensen, Tim Kåre","Chriél, Mariann"],"cuid":["S02-096.55-035536"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"snabelklove hos danske rådyr","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/104281871/Snabelklove_hos_danske_r_dyr.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.55-035536","ids":["dtu-802291fd-57fa-42b7-b3e0-a50b52ddba99","ku-7ccd6b00-2fc1-4475-ab4c-5c8aed18e4fb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-B9DEDE3D422AF8CC7B2CD91B6757FB4C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/104281871/Snabelklove_hos_danske_r_dyr.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341917734/Snabelklove_hos_danske_r_dyr.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Bacteriology, Pathology and Parasitology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Section for Veterinary Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Sif","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5d04b165-7fc1-46cf-88f7-35be695b954c","name":"Hansen, Mette Sif","orcid":"0000-0002-8132-8475","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene Elisabeth","key":"buelundpau","last":"Buelund","locid":"08519bcf-e2b1-4ae0-8da9-bd7653cd8a9d","name":"Buelund, Lene Elisabeth","orcid":"0000-0002-4730-4111","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elisabeth","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"07c945b3-4fe0-496a-9734-095800683729","name":"Holm, Elisabeth","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"ea426e5f-93bd-48f5-a3c8-e5f8004413a7","name":"Larsen, Gitte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dorte Hald","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc3c2ecf-7eeb-4376-baa7-616bf7a33353","name":"Nielsen, Dorte Hald","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tim Kåre","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"2b93571f-6d81-4827-b040-467f1dee1c12","name":"Jensen, Tim Kåre","orcid":"0000-0002-8048-4695","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mariann","key":"chriélpau","last":"Chriél","locid":"1a5d6261-6bd2-4940-baab-5d5fcc3c0f7c","name":"Chriél, Mariann","orcid":"0000-0001-5306-4495","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"13","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-802291fd-57fa-42b7-b3e0-a50b52ddba99","ku-7ccd6b00-2fc1-4475-ab4c-5c8aed18e4fb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Snabelklove hos danske rådyr","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.55-035536","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This study aimed to test whether the digestive and metabolic characteristics of pseudo ruminants provide superior ability to utilise low-quality diets compared to true ruminants. A total of 18 mature, non-pregnant, non-lactating female animals, including six llamas (Lama glama), six Danish Landrace goats and six Shropshire sheep, were used in a crossover design study. The experiment lasted for two periods of three weeks. Half of the animals were fed either high-quality grass hay (HP) or low-quality grass seed straw (LP) during each period. Animals were placed in metabolic cages during the last 5 d, and gaseous exchange was measured by open-circuit indirect calorimetry for 22 h. Metabolisable energy for maintenance (MEm) and fasting energy expenditure (FEExp) were estimated by regression approach. Dry matter (DM) intake per kg0.75 was substantially reduced in llamas and sheep, but not in goats, on the LP compared to HP diet. Llamas had lower daily energy expenditure (324 kJ · kg-0.75) than sheep (416 kJ · kg-0.75) and goats (404 kJ · kg-0.75) on the LP diet. Llamas in comparison with sheep and goats had lower methane emission (0.83 vs 1.34 and 1.24 l · d-1 · kg-0.75, p < 0.05), lower MEm (328 vs 438 and 394 kJ · d-1 · kg-0.75, p < 0.05) and lower FEExp (246 vs 333 and 414 kJ · d-1 · kg-0.75, p < 0.05), respectively. In conclusion, llamas had lower basal metabolic rate and hence maintenance requirements for energy.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Mette O.","Kiani, Ali","Tejada, Einstein","Chwalibog, Andre","Alstrup, Lene"],"cuid":["S02-099.82-017781"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Iran"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lorestan University"],"keyword":["Animal Feed","Animal Nutritional Physiological Phenomena","Animals","Camelids New World","Cross Over Studies","Diet","Digestibility","Energy Metabolism","Energy expenditure","Female","Goats","Methane","Methane production","Nitrogen","Nitrogen metabolism","Poaceae","Sheep"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"energy metabolism and methane production in llamas sheep and goats fed high and low quality grass based diets","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1745039X.2014.912039","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.82-017781","identifier":[{"id":"84901657024","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24870266","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-467e8967-9f21-42c5-a0a8-1d020ab7242a","ku-022008a0-a9bd-41ae-81ea-b8e19eec8731"],"keyword":["Animal Feed","Animal Nutritional Physiological Phenomena","Animals","Camelids, New World","Cross-Over Studies","Diet","Energy Metabolism","Female","Methane","Nitrogen","Poaceae","digestibility","energy expenditure","goats","llamas","methane production","nitrogen metabolism","sheep"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F0703B74FE56750501B214FBEE5E094C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84901657024&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1745039X.2014.912039","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, IKVH Fysiologi og ernæring samt pelsdyrfarmen","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Physiology and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ir","key":"lorestan university","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Lorestan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Institut for Husdyrvidenskab - Husdyrernæring og miljø"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Olaf","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3ddfc1f7-7a66-4a68-bb50-5524f3dc6009","name":"Nielsen, Mette Olaf","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ali","key":"kianipau","last":"Kiani","name":"Kiani, Ali","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Einstein","key":"tejadapau","last":"Tejada","name":"Tejada, Einstein","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"André","key":"chwalibogpau","last":"Chwalibog","locid":"58d32614-fd52-4a13-9d64-99976fdb456e","name":"Chwalibog, André","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"alstruppau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"7b470fb3-335f-4a7b-9aa0-0b9fd32f017d","name":"Alstrup, Lene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24870266"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/1745039x.2014.912039","issn":["14772817","1745039X"],"issn_org":["1745039X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Archives of Animal Nutrition","pages":"171-185","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Archives of Animal Nutrition","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901657024"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-467e8967-9f21-42c5-a0a8-1d020ab7242a","ku-022008a0-a9bd-41ae-81ea-b8e19eec8731"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Energy metabolism and methane production in llamas, sheep and goats fed high- and low-quality grass-based diets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.82-017781","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this experiment was to examine whether the positive response in milk production to increased crude protein (CP) supply in dairy cows was dependent on the digestibility of the forage. Forty-eight lactating Danish Holstein cows were used in a 4 × 4 Latin square design experiment with 4 rations: (1) high digestibility and high CP concentration (HdHp), (2) high digestibility and low CP concentration (HdLp), (3) low digestibility and high CP concentration (LdHp), and (4) low digestibility and low CP concentration (LdLp). All rations contained 30% corn silage, 25% grass-clover silage, and 45% concentrate on a dry matter (DM) basis. Different digestibilities were obtained by replacing a high-digestible grass-clover silage combined with a high-digestible corn silage with a low-digestible grass-clover silage combined with a low-digestible corn silage. Organic matter digestibilities were 79.8 and 74.7% in the high- and low-digestibility rations, respectively. Dietary CP concentration in the ration was increased by substituting barley and sugar beet pulp with rapeseed meal and soybean meal, whereby CP increased from 13.9 to 14.0% (Lp) to 15.7 to 16.0% (Hp). All cows were offered 3 kg of the same concentrate per day in the automatic milking system in addition to the mixed ration. Every feeding period lasted 3 wk, and DM intake and milk yield were measured in the last week in each period, and milk samples for determining milk composition, including fatty acid content, and blood samples were taken during the last 3 d of each period. Dry matter intake increased by 2.2 kg/d on Hd compared with Ld and by 0.7 kg/d on Hp compared with Lp. The positive effect on DM intake was reflected in the energy-corrected milk (ECM) yield, as a higher ration digestibility increased the ECM yield by 1.7 kg/d and a higher CP concentration increased it by 1.2 kg/d. We detected no interaction between forage digestibility and CP concentration on milk production. Reduced digestibility was accompanied by an increase in the plasma level of glucose, suggesting that other nutrients were limiting to milk production. In conclusion, milk production responses to dietary CP supply appeared independent of forage digestibility","author_count":6,"contributors":["Alstrup, Lene","Weisbjerg, Martin Riis","Hymøller, Lone","Larsen, Mette Krogh","Lund, Peter","Nielsen, Mette Olaf"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-021323"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Milk fatty acids"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"milk production response to varying protein supply is independent of forage digestibility in dairy cows","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3168/jds.2013-7585","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-021323","identifier":[{"id":"24835962","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84902656027","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-766bf237-5baf-41a9-b6c1-f1b014a43b2d","ku-616e6d00-d8ae-4bcf-a1c5-171e7857e680"],"keyword":["corn and grass clover silage","mammary nutrient supply and extraction","milk fatty acids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A2F6BA2338F6F191A3251D5A9DDB2BBD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3168/jds.2013-7585","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Institut for Husdyrvidenskab - Husdyrernæring og miljø"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, IKVH Fysiologi og ernæring samt pelsdyrfarmen","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, Physiology and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"alstruppau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"7b470fb3-335f-4a7b-9aa0-0b9fd32f017d","name":"Alstrup, Lene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Riis","key":"weisbjergpau","last":"Weisbjerg","locid":"501c877c-de2b-4cd2-9f3c-42e223238a40","name":"Weisbjerg, Martin Riis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"hymøllerpau","last":"Hymøller","locid":"83604264-1a7d-48c9-86d9-1867667f74cc","name":"Hymøller, Lone","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Krogh","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5ce6d5da-bd09-4304-a9d9-495e00e51fdd","name":"Larsen, Mette Krogh","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"c933cda2-363e-4cb6-b596-3df7ef3d30ed","name":"Lund, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-9113-4500","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mette Olaf","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3ddfc1f7-7a66-4a68-bb50-5524f3dc6009","name":"Nielsen, Mette Olaf","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24835962"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3168/jds.2013-7585","issn":["00220302","15253198"],"issn_org":["00220302"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Dairy Science","pages":"4412-4422","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Dairy Science","volume":"97"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902656027"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-766bf237-5baf-41a9-b6c1-f1b014a43b2d","ku-616e6d00-d8ae-4bcf-a1c5-171e7857e680"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Milk production response to varying protein supply is independent of forage digestibility in dairy cows","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-021323","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: As a subregistry to the Western Denmark Heart Registry (WDHR), the Western Denmark Cardiac Computed Tomography Registry (WDHR-CCTR) is a clinical database established in 2008 to monitor and improve the quality of cardiac computed tomography (CT) in Western Denmark. OBJECTIVE: We examined the content, data quality, and research potential of the WDHR-CCTR. METHODS: We retrieved 2008-2012 data to examine the 1) content; 2) completeness of procedure registration using the Danish National Patient Registry as reference; 3) completeness of variable registration comparing observed vs expected numbers; and 4) positive predictive values as well as negative predictive values of 19 main patient and procedure variables. RESULTS: By December 31, 2012, almost 22,000 cardiac CTs with up to 40 variables for each procedure have been registered. Of these, 87% were coronary CT angiography performed in patients with symptoms indicative of coronary artery disease. Compared with the Danish National Patient Registry, the overall procedure completeness was 72%. However, an additional medical record review of 282 patients registered in the Danish National Patient Registry, but not in the WDHR-CCTR, showed that coronary CT angiographies accounted for only 23% of all nonregistered cardiac CTs, indicating >90% completeness of coronary CT angiographies in the WDHR-CCTR. The completeness of individual variables varied substantially (range: 0%-100%), but was >85% for more than 70% of all variables. Using medical record review of 250 randomly selected patients as reference standard, the positive predictive value for the 19 variables ranged from 89% to 100% (overall 97%), whereas the negative predictive value ranged from 97% to 100% (overall 99%). Stratification by center status showed consistently high positive and negative predictive values for both university (96%/99%) and nonuniversity centers (97%/99%). CONCLUSION: WDHR-CCTR provides ongoing prospective registration of all cardiac CTs performed in Western Denmark since 2008. Overall, the registry data have a high degree of completeness and validity, making it a valuable tool for clinical epidemiological research.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Hüche","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Tilsted, Hans-Henrik","Sand, Niels Peter","Jensen, Jesper Møller","Bøttcher, Morten","Diederichsen, Axel C.","Lambrechtsen, Jess","Kristensen, Lone Deibjerg","Mickley, Hans","Munkholm, Henrik","Gøtzsche, Ole","Knudsen, Lars Lyhne","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Pedersen, Lars","Schmidt, Morten"],"cuid":["S03-092.36-008980"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Lene Hüche"],"keyword":["Coronary computed tomography angiography","Database","Epidemiology","Registries"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Department of Cardiology, Lillbaelt Hospital-Vejle"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the western denmark cardiac computed tomography registry a review and validation study","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S73728","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-092.36-008980","identifier":[{"id":"84920460306","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25657592","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4317160","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-ba29b185-8001-4fdc-85db-b133cc069dbe","au-5247fdc6-bbd0-46a9-8eae-8003977e82da","sdu-372d02db-c116-48b2-90c6-6fc1c752f8a2"],"keyword":["Coronary computed tomography angiography","Database","Epidemiology","Registries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientifi