{"abstract":"Surgical resection enhances long-term survival after lung cancer, but survivors face functional deficits and report on poor quality of life long time after surgery. This study evaluated short and long-term effects of supervised group exercise training on health-related quality of life and physical performance in patients, who were radically operated for lung cancer.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Brocki, Barbara C.","Andreasen, Jane","Nielsen, Lene Rodkjaer","Nekrasas, Vytautas","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Westerdahl, Elisabeth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-107524"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short and long term effects of supervised versus unsupervised exercise training on health related quality of life and functional outcomes following lung cancer surgery a randomized controlled trial","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lungcan.2013.10.015","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-107524","identifier":[{"id":"84891738419","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000330153200017","type":"wos"},{"id":"24246508","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-c605c3ed-5ade-46a2-b98b-e66dad116ed5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC9024848DD49812120EE05919A1E813"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lungcan.2013.10.015","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Fysio- og Ergoterapi [Klinik Akut]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Akut","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara Cristina","key":"brockipau","last":"Brocki","locid":"ec127331-af99-478d-95fd-0e55c9ed5b84","name":"Brocki, Barbara C.","name_org":"Brocki, Barbara Cristina","orcid":"0000-0001-7085-6507","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jane","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"afdfbe5c-39d0-4504-a751-4e3e2b5b0b6c","name":"Andreasen, Jane","orcid":"0000-0001-8000-1553","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Rodkjaer","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"63f7a97d-df2b-4456-b8ec-a410908c834f","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rodkjaer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vytautas","key":"nekrasaspau","last":"Nekrasas","locid":"958f4198-da6f-43f9-8649-cd88c0775d8b","name":"Nekrasas, Vytautas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"gorstrasmussenpau","last":"Gorst-Rasmussen","locid":"2aa85786-c0b1-42ec-93d4-eb7a75696409","name":"Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth","key":"westerdahlpau","last":"Westerdahl","name":"Westerdahl, Elisabeth","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24246508"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.lungcan.2013.10.015","issn":["01695002","18728332"],"issn_org":["01695002"],"issue":"1","journal":"Lung Cancer","pages":"102-108","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Lung Cancer","volume":"83"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84891738419"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c605c3ed-5ade-46a2-b98b-e66dad116ed5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Short and long-term effects of supervised versus unsupervised exercise training on health-related quality of life and functional outcomes following lung cancer surgery - A randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-107524","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The persona method is gaining widespread use and support. Many researchers have reported from single cases and novel domains how they have used the method. Few have conducted literature studies in order to identify and discuss the different understandings of the method. Fewer still have reported on ethnographic studies of practice. This paper falls within the last category, reporting on a study on how practitioners in Denmark use the method, and their perceptions of benefits and challenges when using the method. Finally, different casts of personas obtained from the involved companies are analysed. The findings are compared to reported studies of practice. Contrary to the existing findings the study reports that the method is well integrated into existing practices.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Hansen, Kira Storgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384013"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Denmark","Ethnographic study","integration into practice","persona method","practitioner perceptions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"personas is applicable a study on the use of personas in denmark","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/74977691/06_01_2014_chi_2014_personas_are_applic_revised_final.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-384013","identifier":[{"id":"84900407256","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bc0c8e5a-9697-4ec8-939c-407d6b56202e"],"keyword":["Denmark","ethnographic study","integration into practice","persona method","practitioner perceptions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1E17D651B878B7D7FFC2918C0394DD6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2556288.2557080","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/74977691/06_01_2014_chi_2014_personas_are_applic_revised_final.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","The Department, Computer Games and Interaction Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kira Storgaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Kira Storgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2556288.2557080","eisbn":["9781450324731"],"pages":"1665-1674","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the SIGCHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84900407256"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bc0c8e5a-9697-4ec8-939c-407d6b56202e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Personas is Applicable : A Study On the Use of Personas In Denmark","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384013","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: It is unknown why patients with extensive ulcerative colitis (UC) have a higher risk of colorectal cancer compared with patients with left-sided UC. This study characterizes the inflammatory processes in left-sided UC, pancolitis, and UC-associated dysplasia at the transcriptional level to identify potential biomarkers and transcripts of importance for the carcinogenic behavior of chronic inflammation. METHODS: The Affymetrix GeneChip Human Genome U133 Plus 2.0 was applied on colonic biopsies from UC patients with left-sided UC, pancolitis, dysplasia, and controls. Reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction and immunohistochemistry were performed for validating selected transcripts in the initial cohort and in 2 independent cohorts of patients with UC. Microarray data were analyzed by principal component analysis, and reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction and immunohistochemistry data by the Wilcoxon's rank-sum test. RESULTS: The principal component analysis results revealed separate clusters for left-sided UC, pancolitis, dysplasia, and controls. Close clustering of dysplastic and pancolitic samples indicated similarities in gene expression. Indeed, 101 and 656 parallel upregulated and downregulated transcripts, respectively, were identified in specimens from dysplasia and pancolitis. Validation of selected transcripts hereof identified insulin receptor alpha (INSRA) and MAP kinase interacting serine/threonine kinase 2 (MKNK2) with an enhanced expression in dysplasia compared with left-sided UC and controls, whereas laminin γ2 (LAMC2) was found with a lower expression in dysplasia compared with the remaining 3 groups. CONCLUSIONS: This study demonstrates pancolitis and left-sided UC as distinct inflammatory processes at the transcriptional level, and identifies INSRA, MKNK2, and LAMC2 as potential critical transcripts in the inflammation-driven preneoplastic process of UC.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bjerrum, Jacob Tveiten","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Riis, Lene Buhl","Pittet, Valerie","Mueller, Christoph","Rogler, Gerhard","Olsen, Jørgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-399637"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transcriptional analysis of left sided colitis pancolitis and ulcerative colitis associated dysplasia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/MIB.0000000000000235","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-399637","identifier":[{"id":"84925769300","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25358065","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-0a55682e-1d6f-4e5d-8f0b-35f197573d62"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C3D7CF2DACBBD66F12F471C9ED8A3E4C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/MIB.0000000000000235","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, ICMM Section 8","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Morphogenesis and Differentiation Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob T","key":"bjerrumpau","last":"Bjerrum","locid":"fe4b37d0-7b36-4636-925f-e1d395b9e573","name":"Bjerrum, Jacob Tveiten","name_org":"Bjerrum, Jacob T","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Ole H","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59658c4-dde8-4749-9b5c-f4ec5910dd02","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","name_org":"Nielsen, Ole H","orcid":"0000-0003-4612-8635","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene B","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","name_org":"Riis, Lene B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Valerie","key":"pittetpau","last":"Pittet","name":"Pittet, Valerie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christoph","key":"muellerpau","last":"Mueller","name":"Mueller, Christoph","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gerhard","key":"roglerpau","last":"Rogler","name":"Rogler, Gerhard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"dd6747c2-2376-4486-a000-1b4f1222eaaf","name":"Olsen, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-1974-6446","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25358065"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/mib.0000000000000235","issn":["10780998","15364844"],"issn_org":["10780998"],"issue":"12","journal":"Inflammatory Bowel Diseases","pages":"2340-2352","status":"p","title":"Inflammatory Bowel Diseases","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925769300"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0a55682e-1d6f-4e5d-8f0b-35f197573d62"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transcriptional analysis of left-sided colitis, pancolitis, and ulcerative colitis-associated dysplasia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-399637","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND:Alzheimer's disease (AD) is a progressive, incurable neurodegenerative disease and the most common type of dementia. It cannot be prevented, cured or drastically slowed, even though AD research has increased in the past 5-10 years. Instead of focusing on the brain volume or on the single brain structures like hippocampus, this paper investigates the relationship and proximity between regions in the brain and uses this information as a novel way of classifying normal control (NC), mild cognitive impaired (MCI), and AD subjects.METHODS:A longitudinal cohort of 528 subjects (170 NC, 240 MCI, and 114 AD) from ADNI at baseline and month 12 was studied. We investigated a marker based on Procrustes aligned center of masses and the percentile surface connectivity between regions. These markers were classified using a linear discriminant analysis in a cross validation setting and compared to whole brain and hippocampus volume.RESULTS:We found that both our markers was able to significantly classify the subjects. The surface connectivity marker showed the best results with an area under the curve (AUC) at 0.877 (p","author_count":6,"contributors":["Erleben, Lene Lillemark","Sørensen, Lauge","Pai, Akshay Sadananda Uppinakudru","Dam, Erik Bjørnager","Nielsen, Mads","Initiative, Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-461818"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-BIMQ"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-BIMQ","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"brain region s relative proximity as marker for alzheimer s disease based on structural mri","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2342-14-21","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-461818","identifier":[{"id":"84902110801","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7270a86c-eaca-44f0-8701-43fe06271521"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3EFD282BCA3C2B1BD19985B276508048"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2342-14-21","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/113739949/1471_2342_14_21.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"biomediq","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-BIMQ","l3nl":"Biomediq","l3nn":"Biomediq","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Biomediq","namevar":["Biomediq A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-BIMQ","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Lillemark","key":"erlebenpau","last":"Erleben","locid":"0e3ad371-b61c-4c7c-b26c-605c583bbb40","name":"Erleben, Lene Lillemark","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lauge Emil","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"330d1478-c602-4767-8d45-30063bff33ea","name":"Sørensen, Lauge","name_org":"Sørensen, Lauge Emil","orcid":"0000-0002-1181-7150","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Akshay Sadananda Uppinakudru","key":"paipau","last":"Pai","locid":"2a07c27f-433e-456a-8b47-984c22cf325f","name":"Pai, Akshay Sadananda Uppinakudru","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Erik Bjørnager","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","name":"Dam, Erik Bjørnager","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mads","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52f8d6fb-fd83-4d11-ad65-3e183ca401f2","name":"Nielsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0003-1535-068X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging","key":"initiativepau","last":"Initiative","name":"Initiative, Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2342-14-21","issn":["14712342"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Medical Imaging","paperid":"21","status":"p","title":"BMC Medical Imaging","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902110801"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Biomediq","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7270a86c-eaca-44f0-8701-43fe06271521"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Brain region's relative proximity as marker for Alzheimer's disease based on structural MRI","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-461818","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The invasive fungal pathogen, Hymenoscyphus pseudoalbidus V. Queloz, has decimated stands of Fraxinus excelsior L. over most of the species' natural distribution area. We assessed crown damage from 2009 to 2014 (at ages 8, 11 and 13) in 43 open-pollinated ash families planted in north-eastern Zealand, Denmark, and confirmed the presence of substantial genetic variation in ash dieback susceptibility. The average crown damage increased in the trial from 61% in 2009 to 66% in 2012 and 72% in 2014, while the estimated heritability was 0.42 in both 2009 and 2012 but increased to 0.53 in 2014. Genetic correlation between assessments was 0.88 between 2009 and 2012 and 0.91 between 2009 and 2014, suggesting fairly good possibilities for early selection of superior genotypes in the presence of high infection levels in the trial. The level of crown damage had strong negative effect on growth and survival. Only 34% of the trees with high levels of damage in 2009 were still alive in 2014, emphasising that high susceptibility is associated with low fitness.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lobo, Albin","Hansen, Jon Kehlet","McKinney, Lea Vig","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Kjær, Erik Dahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-472465"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic variation in dieback resistance growth and survival of i fraxinus excelsior i under the influence of i hymenoscyphus pseudoalbidus i","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02827581.2014.950603","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-472465","identifier":[{"id":"85027916811","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-840973ea-eb31-4971-8ce8-e023946d4a13"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-17E5CB3E45C3FFE8A1F57074BA50FAF3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02827581.2014.950603","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Albin","key":"lobopau","last":"Lobo","locid":"50b0d4fe-6e8d-4245-aded-c406110ff0b0","name":"Lobo, Albin","orcid":"0000-0002-9580-2860","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jon Kehlet","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b8c2f3eb-b79f-46cc-b346-8300943e2129","name":"Hansen, Jon Kehlet","orcid":"0000-0002-1260-3509","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lea Vig","key":"mckinneypau","last":"McKinney","locid":"060df27a-59d3-4457-81a2-185cca16ae68","name":"McKinney, Lea Vig","orcid":"0000-0001-6601-4614","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/02827581.2014.950603","issn":["02827581","14004089"],"issn_org":["02827581"],"issue":"6","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Forest Research","pages":"519-526","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Forest Research","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027916811"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-840973ea-eb31-4971-8ce8-e023946d4a13"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genetic variation in dieback resistance : growth and survival of <i>Fraxinus excelsior</i> under the influence of <i>Hymenoscyphus pseudoalbidus</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-472465","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Pentapharsodinium dalei is a widely distributed cold-water dinoflagellate, which is used in palaeoecology as an indicator of relatively warmer conditions in polar and subpolar regions. This species has been proposed to be one of the first indicators of global warming at high latitudes.We developed the first microsatellite markers for P. dalei to facilitate the study of spatial and temporal population genetic changes. Single cysts were isolated from surface sediments in Koljö Fjord, Sweden. After cyst germination, single vegetative cells were isolated for establishing monoclonal cultures. Six dinucleotide polymorphic microsatellite markers were developed as multiplex polymerase chain reactions and were genotyped in 32 strains. The number of alleles per locus varied between 4 and 12, and the estimated gene diversity varied from 0.588 to 0.891. The haploid state of the vegetative cells was confirmed. The six selected microsatellites will be useful to explore population dynamics in P. dalei from contemporary planktonic and revived benthic samples to enable, for example, detailed studies into the evolutionary consequences of anthropogenic and climate-driven habitat changes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lundholm, Nina","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","Ribeiro, Sofia","Ellegaard, Marianne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-491829"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microsatellite markers for the palaeo temperature indicator em pentapharsodinium dalei em dinophyceae","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-491829","identifier":[{"id":"84893736161","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a4b52aa7-1fee-45de-b0f1-caf1a6945223"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D625AB0A8B704FB9169B82F92880A10B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Natural History Museum of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nina","key":"lundholmpau","last":"Lundholm","locid":"8a8a8b45-8d40-4f5f-b3e2-ad8b18835107","name":"Lundholm, Nina","orcid":"0000-0002-2035-1997","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sofia","key":"ribeiropau","last":"Ribeiro","name":"Ribeiro, Sofia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne","key":"ellegaardpau","last":"Ellegaard","locid":"df3f99c8-5911-475c-a99e-92a56cbb9981","name":"Ellegaard, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0002-6032-3376","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10811-013-0123-3","issn":["09218971","15735176"],"issn_org":["09218971"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Applied Phycology","pages":"417-420","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Phycology","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84893736161"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a4b52aa7-1fee-45de-b0f1-caf1a6945223"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Microsatellite markers for the palaeo-temperature indicator <em>Pentapharsodinium dalei</em> (Dinophyceae)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-491829","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this article is to review recent literature on antiretroviral treatment (ART) and immune suppression as risk factors for renal impairment in HIV-positive persons, and to discuss pending research questions within this field.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Mocroft, Amanda","Lundgren, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-535815"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antiretroviral therapy immune suppression and renal impairment in hiv positive persons","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/COH.0000000000000023","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-535815","identifier":[{"id":"84892369108","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24225381","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ee87b3c3-2b7a-4f12-a06d-8e203130e4a1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C913028AEEECD2554C2B4BE3A867B135"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/COH.0000000000000023","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, CHIP"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Ryom","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0087fd9d-3a4d-4da5-9f4d-2ba51ec7d7a8","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ryom","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Amanda","key":"mocroftpau","last":"Mocroft","name":"Mocroft, Amanda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens D","key":"lundgrenpau","last":"Lundgren","locid":"af310f7a-c49b-4381-bcb4-cf56e3fd80d8","name":"Lundgren, Jens","name_org":"Lundgren, Jens D","orcid":"0000-0001-8901-7850","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24225381"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/coh.0000000000000023","issn":["1746630X","17466318"],"issn_org":["1746630X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Current Opinion in HIV and AIDS","pages":"41-7","status":"p","title":"Current Opinion in HIV and AIDS","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84892369108"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ee87b3c3-2b7a-4f12-a06d-8e203130e4a1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Antiretroviral therapy, immune suppression and renal impairment in HIV-positive persons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-535815","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Bacillus spp. are commonly used as probiotic species in the feed industry, however, their benefits need to be confirmed. This study describes a high throughput screening combined with the detailed characterization of endospore-forming bacteria with the aim to identify new Bacillus spp. strains for use as probiotic additives in pig feed. A total of 245 bacterial isolates derived from African fermented food, feces and soil were identified by 16S rRNA gene sequencing and screened for antimicrobial activity and growth in the presence of antibiotics, bile salts and at pH 4.0. Thirty-three Bacillus spp. isolates with the best characteristics were identified by gyrB and rpoB gene sequencing as B. amyloliquefaciens subsp. plantarum, B. amyloliquefaciens subsp. amyloliquefaciens, B. subtilis subsp. subtilis, B. licheniformis, B. mojavensis, B. pumilus and B. megaterium. These isolates were further investigated for their activity against the pathogenic bacteria, antibiotic susceptibility, sporulation rates, biofilm formation and production of glycosyl hydrolytic enzymes. Additionally, ten selected isolates were assessed for heat resistance of spores and the effect on porcine epithelial cells IPEC-J2. Isolates of B. amyloliquefaciens, B. subtilis and B. mojavensis, showed the best overall characteristics and, therefore, potential for usage as probiotic additives in feed. A large number of taxonomically diverse strains made it possible to reveal species and subspecies-specific trends, contributing to our understanding of the probiotic potential of Bacillus species.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Larsen, Nadja","Thorsen, Line","Kpikpi, Elmer Nayra","Stuer-Lauridsen, Birgitte","Cantor, Mette Dines","Nielsen, Bea","Brockmann, Elke","Derkx, Patrick M.F.","Jespersen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-538528"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Ghana"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Techonlogy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of em bacillus em spp strains for use as probiotic additives in pig feed","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00253-013-5343-6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-538528","identifier":[{"id":"24201893","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84898920747","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f321ac96-0ad7-462e-9b25-e1004c073f08"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D3A60D6C639FCF297B96752DF6C9333"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00253-013-5343-6","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology, Gut Health, and Fermentation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gh","key":"kwame nkrumah university of science and techonlogy","loc":["Ghana","Africa"],"name":"Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Techonlogy","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Chr. Hansen"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","coun