as probiotic additives in pig feed","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-538528","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Nine structurally related paramagnetic acetylacetonato nickel(II) complexes: [Ni(acac) 2] and trans-[Ni(acac) 2(X) 2]nH/D 2O, X = H 2O, D 2O, NH 3, MeOH, PMePh 2, PMe 2Ph, or [dppe] 1/2, n = 0 or 1, dppe = 1,2-bis(diphenylphosphino)ethane, as well as cis-[Ni(F 6-acac) 2(D 2O) 2], F 6-acac = hexafluoroacetylonato, have been characterized by solid state 13C MAS NMR spectroscopy. 2H MAS NMR was used to probe the local hydrogen bonding network in [Ni(acac) 2(D 2O) 2]D 2O and cis-[Ni(F 6-acac) 2(D 2O) 2]. The complexes serve to benchmark the paramagnetic shift, which can be associated with the resonances of atoms of the coordinated ligands. The methine (CH) and methyl (CH 3) have characteristic combinations of the isotropic shift (δ) and anisotropy parameters (d, η). The size of the anisotropy (d), which is the sum of the chemical shift anisotropy (CSA) and the paramagnetic electron-nuclei dipolar coupling, is much more descriptive than the isotropic shift. Moreover, the CSA is found to constitute up to one-third of the total anisotropy and should be taken into consideration when 13C anisotropies are used for structure determination of paramagnetic materials. The 13C MAS NMR spectra of trans-[Ni(acac) 2(PMe 2Ph) 2], trans-[Ni(acac) 2(PMePh 2) 2], and the noncrystallographically characterized trans-[Ni(acac) 2(dppe)] n were assigned using these correlations. The complexes with L = H 2O, D 2O, NH 3, and MeOH can be prepared by a series of solid state desorption and sorption reactions. Crystal structures for trans-[Ni(acac) 2(NH 3) 2] and trans-[Ni(acac) 2(PMePh 2) 2] are reported.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lennartson, Anders","Christensen, Lene Ulrikke","McKenzie, Christine J.","Nielsen, Ulla Gro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586465"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"solid state sup 000000000013 sup c and sup 000000000002 sup h nmr investigations of paramagnetic ni ii acac sub 000000000002 sub l sub 000000000002 sub complexes","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ic402354r","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-586465","identifier":[{"id":"84891796730","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24325293","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-2e532060-63e1-453a-8c4b-7e138a6cadf1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-270593F1AB55D55D3A1BF2FC7F6B6EC8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/ic402354r","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/ic402354r","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"lennartsonpau","last":"Lennartson","locid":"9b9e068c-b087-4843-bbdd-834528e8f9d8","name":"Lennartson, Anders","name_org":"Lennartson, A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Ulrikke","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Lene Ulrikke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"C. J.","key":"mckenziepau","last":"McKenzie","locid":"a8cebd0f-6903-4172-bb3b-f8de1630baf3","name":"McKen