,"name":"Nielsen, Lene Lyngø","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"delmarpedh","last":"Delmar","name":"Delmar, Charlotte","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Astrid","key":"laubergpedh","last":"Lauberg","name":"Lauberg, Astrid","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgith","key":"pedersenpedh","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Birgith","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771291704"],"pages":"211-232","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Klim","status":"p","title":"Omsorgsetik i klinisk sygepleje"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bcd55bd3-5c86-4296-8f62-3d9cc66ec6ed"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Mestring af hverdagslivet med bivirkninger fra kræftbehandling - et patientperspektiv","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-104786","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Persona, one of the human centered design methodologies for information systems (IS), has been widely applied and tested in Europe and North America. Although the persona approach has attracted attention in Japan recent years, its creation process has not been properly articulated nor understood in the Japanese IS domain. In order to gain the maximum effect of introducing persona and contribute to the usage of systems with high social impact such as e-government applications, it is of critical importance to conduct appropriate persona development processes. In this article we introduce effective as well as pragmatic persona creation processes from a stakeholder involvement point of view, exemplified by a case of persona creation for a Danish e-Government portal site. The e-Government portal became widely known to be a successful e-Government case all over the world, which indirectly indicate the validity of the persona approach applied to the portal. The high acceptance of created personas among development team shows our persona methodology has high potential to contribute to conduct similar large scale IS development projects with socially high impacts, which are expected to increase in Japan.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jensen, Mika Yasuoka","Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381972"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Information systems","Persona","Stakeholder"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"大規模システムのための参加型ペルソナ構築 デンマークの電子政府の事例より","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381972","ids":["itu-2fdc72b0-03c3-438e-8fcf-999a75cc8341"],"keyword":["information systems","persona","stakeholder"],"lang":"Japanese","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-64FB059CD4BAAE4B846F5CEE3190FFA8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mika Yasuoka","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Mika Yasuoka","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18842135"],"issue":"1","journal":"Information Systems Society of Japan","pages":"14-30","paperid":"1","status":"p","title":"Information Systems Society of Japan","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2fdc72b0-03c3-438e-8fcf-999a75cc8341"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"大規模システムのための参加型ペルソナ構築 : デンマークの電子政府の事例より","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381972","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Background Patients have medicines reviews conducted by different health care professionals in different settings. Introducing a clinical panel to drug related problems (DRPs) to evaluate their clinical significance is common practice. The clinical panel discuss the potential consequences and come to a mutual agreement on the level of clinical significance. However, to what degree does the panel agree?Purpose To compare the agreement between different health care professionals who have evaluated the clinical significance of DRPs.Materials and methods DRPs were identified in 30 comprehensive medicines reviews conducted by a clinical pharmacist. Two hospital pharmacists, a general practitioner and two specialists in pain management from hospital care (the Panel) evaluated each DRP considering the potential clinical outcome for the patient. The DRPs were rated either nil, low, minor, moderate or highly clinically significant. Agreement was analysed using Kappa statistics. A Kappa value of 0.8 to 1.0 indicated nearly perfect agreement between ratings of the Panel members.Results The Panel rated 45 percent of the total 162 DRPs as of moderate clinical significance. However, the overall kappa score was 0.12 showing nil agreement when comparing the ratings of clinical significance. The Panel disagreed on which DRPs were of minor or moderate clinical significance. Further analysis of the interrelationship of the five Panel members described fair agreement between one specialist and the two pharmacists. In two types of DRPs, sub-therapeutic dosing and side effects, the Panel agreed fairly well on moderate clinical significance.Conclusions Each profession rates the clinical significance of DRPs differently, especially in cases of intervention by pharmacist versus practitioner, and opinion also varies within each profession. Take into account the profession and setting when clinical relevance of DRPs is discussed in the literature and when choosing a method for evaluating the clinical significance of DRPs.Acknowledgement Many thanks to Grünenthalfonden and Actavisfonden, participants in the project ‘Drug Related Problems in the Frontier between Primary and Secondary Health Care’.No conflict of interest.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Villesen, Christine","Hojsted, Jette","Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","Nørgaard, Lotte Stig","Nielsen, Per Rotbøll","Christrup, Lona Louring"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-419686"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of 000000000005 health care professionals ratings of the clinical significance of drug related problems","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-419686","ids":["ku-2c0d2b04-eddf-405d-86e2-b2e7fea5da2f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9471053622E7C43BFA15315BBD00FF8F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Pharmacology Pharmacotherapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christine","key":"villesenpau","last":"Villesen","locid":"4753fb2b-ea99-4b97-ad66-9c4ad065d40c","name":"Villesen, Christine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jette","key":"hojstedpau","last":"Hojsted","locid":"d455f1b1-ef0b-4fc8-a3f3-370a1bac3ac0","name":"Hojsted, Jette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Juel","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lotte Stig","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"7dbf5d7d-7d8c-4260-b41c-0446c7cc7740","name":"Nørgaard, Lotte Stig","orcid":"0000-0002-3490-0475","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Per Rotbøll","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Per Rotbøll","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lona Louring","key":"christruppau","last":"Christrup","locid":"acf7258c-1e63-48a1-9bef-d6b6c5b8eeca","name":"Christrup, Lona Louring","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/ejhpharm-2013-000436.151","issn":["20479956","20479964"],"issn_org":["20479956"],"journal":"European Journal of Hospital Pharmacy","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Hospital Pharmacy","title_org":"European Journal of Hospital Pharmacy - Science and Practice","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2c0d2b04-eddf-405d-86e2-b2e7fea5da2f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Comparison of 5 health care professionals’ratings of the clinical significance of drug related problems","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-419686","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"FTIR smog chamber techniques were used to measure k(Cl + (CF 3)2CFOCH3) = (1.80 ± 0.42) × 10-13, k(Cl + (CF3)2CFOCHO) = (1.47 ± 0.56) × 10-14, and k(OH + (CF3) 2CFOCH3) = (1.55 ± 0.24) × 10-14 cm3 molecule-1 s-1. The chlorine-atom initiated oxidation of (CF3)2CFOCH3 in air in the absence of NOX results in conversion of (CF3) 2CFOCH3 into the formate, (CF3) 2CFOCHO, in a yield indistinguishable from 100%. In the presence of NOX, the (CF3)2CFOCHO yield was decreased by approximately 17%, which we attribute to the formation of peroxy and/or alkoxy nitrates. The atmospheric lifetime of (CF3)2CFOCH 3 was estimated to 3.7 years. The infrared spectrum of (CF 3)2CFOCH3 was measured and a global warming potential GWP100 = 354 was determined.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Andersen, Lene Løffler","Østerstrøm, Freja From","Nielsen, Ole John","Andersen, Mads Peter Sulbæk","Wallington, Timothy J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-424908"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ford Motor Company"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"atmospheric chemistry of cf sub 000000000003 sub sub 000000000002 sub cfoch sub 000000000003 sub","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cplett.2014.05.036","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-424908","identifier":[{"id":"84901934778","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-350066ef-1979-4efe-af09-30ca59a1dd29"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2CB2D1DB59390F1218B35184FF2C1EA2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cplett.2014.05.036","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"ford motor company","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ford Motor Company","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Løffler","key":"andersenleneløfflerpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lene Løffler","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Freja From","key":"østerstrømfrejafrompau","last":"Østerstrøm","locid":"827145e9-1a90-49d5-8567-447da007cf5e","name":"Østerstrøm, Freja From","orcid":"0000-0003-4125-3365","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole John","key":"nielsenolejohnpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5a14c7c0-570f-4c1f-9b79-fa0a5a7c84fb","name":"Nielsen, Ole John","orcid":"0000-0002-0088-3937","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Peter Sulbæk","key":"andersenmadspetersulbækpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"ba43edb9-8086-4c24-b138-e59208866132","name":"Andersen, Mads Peter Sulbæk","orcid":"0000-0002-7976-5852","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Timothy J.","key":"wallingtontimothyjpau","last":"Wallington","name":"Wallington, Timothy J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cplett.2014.05.036","issn":["00092614","18734448"],"issn_org":["00092614"],"journal":"Chemical Physics Letters","pages":"5-9","status":"p","title":"Chemical Physics Letters","volume":"607"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901934778"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-350066ef-1979-4efe-af09-30ca59a1dd29"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Atmospheric chemistry of (CF<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>CFOCH<sub>3</sub>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-424908","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This protocol describes how to monitor individual naturally supercoiled circular DNA plasmids bound via peptide nucleic acid (PNA) handles between a bead and a surface. The protocol was developed for single-molecule investigation of the dynamics of supercoiled DNA, and it allows the investigation of both the dynamics of the molecule itself and of its interactions with a regulatory protein. Two bis-PNA clamps designed to bind with extremely high affinity to predetermined homopurine sequence sites in supercoiled DNA are prepared: one conjugated with digoxigenin for attachment to an anti-digoxigenin-coated glass cover slide, and one conjugated with biotin for attachment to a submicron-sized streptavidin-coated polystyrene bead. Plasmids are constructed, purified and incubated with the PNA handles. The dynamics of the construct is analyzed by tracking the tethered bead using video microscopy: less supercoiling results in more movement, and more supercoiling results in less movement. In contrast to other single-molecule methodologies, the current methodology allows for studying DNA in its naturally supercoiled state with constant linking number and constant writhe. The protocol has potential for use in studying the influence of supercoils on the dynamics of DNA and its associated proteins, e.g., topoisomerase. The procedure takes ~4 weeks.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Norregaard, Kamilla","Andersson, Magnus","Nielsen, Peter E.","Brown, Stanley","Oddershede, Lene Broeng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460789"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tethered particle analysis of supercoiled circular dna using peptide nucleic acid handles","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nprot.2014.152","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-460789","identifier":[{"id":"25144271","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84907030958","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-70bf80de-c04e-4f93-af07-c24ea5e0d59e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0851959763D39341AFE2F3DD5C0909E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.nature.com/nprot/journal/v9/n9/full/nprot.2014.152.html#affil-auth","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nprot.2014.152","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Biocomplexity","University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kamilla","key":"norregaardpau","last":"Norregaard","locid":"c34c6d45-ccd4-4be4-9728-7f492a6b4583","name":"Norregaard, Kamilla","orcid":"0000-0003-1953-9703","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Magnus","key":"anderssonpau","last":"Andersson","name":"Andersson, Magnus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Eigil","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"74cb6e41-3bfc-4d0a-a0df-7bd8fa9c2856","name":"Nielsen, Peter E.","name_org":"Nielsen, Peter Eigil","orcid":"0000-0001-8771-330X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stanley","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","locid":"fe5af114-5058-406e-87f5-18be42ae3241","name":"Brown, Stanley","orcid":"0000-0002-8453-8144","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene B","key":"oddershedepau","last":"Oddershede","locid":"7474640c-fb11-45b8-abd4-8de4232d5060","name":"Oddershede, Lene Broeng","name_org":"Oddershede, Lene B","orcid":"0000-0003-2923-2844","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25144271"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/nprot.2014.152","issn":["17502799","17542189"],"issn_org":["17542189"],"issue":"9","journal":"Nature Protocols","pages":"2206-23","status":"p","title":"Nature Protocols","title_org":"Nature Protocols (Print)","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84907030958"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-70bf80de-c04e-4f93-af07-c24ea5e0d59e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tethered particle analysis of supercoiled circular DNA using peptide nucleic acid handles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-460789","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"AIM: While collagenous colitis represents the most common form of the collagenous gastroenteritides, the collagenous entities affecting the proximal part of the gastrointestinal tract are much less recognized and possibly overlooked. The aim was to summarize the latest information through a systematic review of collagenous gastritis, collagenous sprue, and a combination thereof. METHOD: The search yielded 117 studies which were suitable for inclusion in the systematic review. Excluding repeated cases, 89 case reports and 28 case series were reported, whereas no prospective studies with or without control groups were identified. Further, no randomized, controlled trials were identified. The total number of patients with proximal collagenous gastroenteritides reported was 330. RESULTS: An overview of clinical presentations, prognosis, pathophysiology and histopathology, as well as management of these disorders is presented. The prognosis of both collagenous gastritis and sprue seems not to be as dismal as considered previously. Data point to involvement of immune or autoimmune mechanisms potentially driven by luminal antigens initiating the fibroinflammatory condition. CONCLUSIONS: To reach the diagnosis it is recommended that biopsies are obtained during gastroduodenoscopies. Therapies with anti-secretory strategies, glucocorticoids, and in some cases iron supplementation are suggested, although rational treatment options from randomized, controlled trials do not exist for these rare or even overlooked disorders.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Riis, Lene Buhl","Danese, Silvio","Bojesen, Rasmus Dahlin","Soendergaard, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-482021"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biopsy","Colitis Collagenous","Collagen","Collagenous Sprue","Endoscopy Gastrointestinal","Gastritis","Gastroenteritis","Glucocorticoids","Humans","Iron compounds","Prognosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proximal collagenous gastroenteritides clinical management a systematic review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/07853890.2014.899102","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-482021","identifier":[{"id":"84905506705","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24716737","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-94497842-f2b0-48ba-ab83-dc8250e0e4a9"],"keyword":["Biopsy","Colitis, Collagenous","Collagen","Collagenous Sprue","Endoscopy, Gastrointestinal","Gastritis","Gastroenteritis","Glucocorticoids","Humans","Iron Compounds","Prognosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-125890A86FCA28A07013F7BBAB3CE1A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/07853890.2014.899102","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Ole Haagen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59658c4-dde8-4749-9b5c-f4ec5910dd02","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","orcid":"0000-0003-4612-8635","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Buhl","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Silvio","key":"danesepau","last":"Danese","name":"Danese, Silvio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus Dahlin","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","name":"Bojesen, Rasmus Dahlin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christoffer","key":"soendergaardpau","last":"Soendergaard","name":"Soendergaard, Christoffer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24716737"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/07853890.2014.899102","issn":["07853890","13652060"],"issn_org":["07853890"],"issue":"5","journal":"Annals of Medicine","pages":"311-317","status":"p","title":"Annals of Medicine","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905506705"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-94497842-f2b0-48ba-ab83-dc8250e0e4a9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Proximal collagenous gastroenteritides: : Clinical management. A systematic review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-482021","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Personas is a technique that supports designing and engineering interactive systems with the focus on the end-users. This paper reports from a case study, where we interviewed four software developers about their usage of personas in software development practice. The purpose of was to identify the practices of personas development in the software development industry. How the respondents perceive personas and its use does not always correlate with what is described as best practice in the literature. We found that practitioners are not using personas as stated in the literature but are developing their own practices both in regards to when and how personas are created.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Billestrup, Jane","Stage, Jan","Bruun, Anders","Nielsen, Lene","Nielsen, Kira Storgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776395"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Persona creation","Personas","Software development practice"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"creating and using personas in software development experiences from practice","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-44811-3_16","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776395","identifier":[{"id":"84921417164","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-41483743-e0b6-405d-8121-063ce390993d"],"keyword":["Persona creation","Personas","Software development practice"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-6115A0BC4B3998436902BB95EF6C652E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-44811-3_16","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Computer Games and Interaction Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"billestrupjanepau","last":"Billestrup","name":"Billestrup, Jane","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"stagejanpau","last":"Stage","name":"Stage, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"bruunanderspau","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenlenepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kira Storgaard","key":"nielsenkirastorgaardpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Kira Storgaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefan","key":"sauerstefanpedh","last":"Sauer","name":"Sauer, Stefan","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"bogdanchristianpedh","last":"Bogdan","name":"Bogdan, Christian","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"forbrigpeterpedh","last":"Forbrig","name":"Forbrig, Peter","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Regina","key":"bernhauptreginapedh","last":"Bernhaupt","name":"Bernhaupt, Regina","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marco","key":"wincklermarcopedh","last":"Winckler","name":"Winckler, Marco","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-44811-3_16","edition":"2014","eisbn":["9783662448113"],"isbn":["9783662448106"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"251-258","place":"Berlin","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Human-Centered Software Engineering (HCSE)","volume":"8742"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84921417164"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-41483743-e0b6-405d-8121-063ce390993d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Creating and Using Personas in Software Development: Experiences from Practice.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776395","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: To systematically review and perform a meta-analysis of the diagnostic accuracy and post-test outcomes of conventional exercise electrocardiography (XECG) and single-photon emission computed tomography (SPECT) compared with coronary computed tomography angiography (coronary CTA) in patients suspected of stable coronary artery disease (CAD). METHODS AND RESULTS: We systematically searched for studies published from January 2002 to February 2013 examining the diagnostic accuracy (defined as at least ≥50% luminal obstruction on invasive coronary angiography) and outcomes of coronary CTA (≥16 slice) in comparison with XECG and SPECT. The search revealed 11 eligible studies (N = 1575) comparing the diagnostic accuracy and 7 studies (N = 216.603) the outcomes of coronary CTA vs. XECG or/and SPECT. The per-patient sensitivity [95% confidence interval (95% CI)] to identify significant CAD was 98% (93-99%) for coronary CTA vs. 67% (54-78%) (P < 0.001) for XECG and 99% (96-100%) vs. 73% (59-83%) (P = 0.001) for SPECT. The specificity (95% CI) of coronary CTA was 82% (63-93%) vs. 46% (30-64%) (P < 0.001) for XECG and 71% (60-80%) vs. 48% (31-64%) (P = 0.14) for SPECT. The odds ratio (OR) of downstream test utilization (DTU) for coronary CTA vs. XECG/SPECT was 1.38 (1.33-1.43, P < 0.001), for revascularization 2.63 (2.50-2.77, P < 0.001), for non-fatal myocardial infarction 0.53 (0.39-0.72, P < 0.001), and for all-cause mortality 1.01 (0.87-1.18, P = 0.87). CONCLUSION: The up-front diagnostic performance of coronary CTA is higher than of XECG and SPECT. When compared with XECG/SPECT testing, coronary CTA testing is associated with increased DTU and coronary revascularization.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene H","Ortner, Nino","Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","Achenbach, Stephan","Leipsic, Jonathon","Abdulla, Jawdat"],"cuid":["S02-088.60-016194"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Coronary Angiography","Coronary artery disease","Electrocardiography","Exercise Test","Humans","Tomography Emission Computed Single Photon","Tomography X Ray Computed"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the diagnostic accuracy and outcomes after coronary computed tomography angiography vs conventional functional testing in patients with stable angina pectoris a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjci/jeu027","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-088.60-016194","identifier":[{"id":"84904107172","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24618659","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-314307a7-fbeb-4434-80ed-c8942b1dec6d","ku-9548d7e8-8ba3-47ce-8f4c-0f7ef279c691"],"keyword":["Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Disease","Electrocardiography","Exercise Test","Humans","Tomography, Emission-Computed, Single-Photon","Tomography, X-Ray Computed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-58E650A0BF6F26030A0FD35388423089"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjci/jeu027","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene H","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"fec74066-6332-450a-a34b-3d202e143683","name":"Nielsen, Lene H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nino","key":"ortnerpau","last":"Ortner","name":"Ortner, Nino","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne L","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"6bcdb292-78dc-4e8b-9fea-814d6a6852c9","name":"Nørgaard, Bjarne Linde","name_org":"Nørgaard, Bjarne L","orcid":"0000-0002-4758-7203","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephan","key":"achenbachpau","last":"Achenbach","name":"Achenbach, Stephan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathon","key":"leipsicpau","last":"Leipsic","name":"Leipsic, Jonathon","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jawdat","key":"abdullapau","last":"Abdulla","locid":"90506a0f-e2cc-4235-9ccb-b04de2df199e","name":"Abdulla, Jawdat","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24618659"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjci/jeu027","issn":["15252167","15322114"],"issn_org":["20472404"],"issue":"9","journal":"European Heart Journal Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"961-71","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84904107172"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-314307a7-fbeb-4434-80ed-c8942b1dec6d","ku-9548d7e8-8ba3-47ce-8f4c-0f7ef279c691"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The diagnostic accuracy and outcomes after coronary computed tomography angiography vs. conventional functional testing in patients with stable angina pectoris : a systematic review and meta-analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.60-016194","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The aim of this study was to examine whether educational meetings and group detailing could increase the use of drugs from the ward lists or the drug formulary in hospitals. Methods: Twelve medical wards from two hospitals were randomized into three groups: control, basic and extended intervention. All wards had a ward list review before interventions. Moreover, the basic intervention consisted of an educational meeting, and the extended intervention included two group detailing sessions. The proportion of drugs used from the ward list or hospital drug formulary (HDF) was the primary outcome. Data (defined daily doses [DDDs], numbers and cost [Euros]) on drugs sold to the wards were retrieved from the two hospitals from 1 July 2011 to 31 August 2012. Baseline data: from July to September 2011, and follow-up data: from June to August 2012. Results: The proportion of formulary drugs used increased for the extended intervention group (0.04, range -0.02 to 0.09) and basic intervention group (0.03, range -0.03 to 0.09) in comparison with a decrease in the control group (-0.01, range -0.03 to -0.02). The interventions did not significantly change odds for selecting drugs from the formulary in comparison with the control group (basic intervention: OR 1.09 [95 % CI 0.81 to 1.46]; extended intervention: OR 1.00 [95 % CI 0.75 to 1.35]). Conclusions: In this study, educational meetings and group detailing do not significantly improve adherence to ward lists or HDF. The adherence to the formularies at baseline was relatively high, which may explain why the interventions did not have a significant effect.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Plet, Hanne T.","Kjeldsen, Lene J.","Christensen, René Depont","Nielsen, Gitte Søndergaard","Hallas, Jesper"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-004543"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Plet, Hanne T."],"keyword":["Cluster randomized controlled trial","Educational meetings","Group detailing","Hospital","Hospital drug formulary","Intervention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["The Research Unit for General Practice, Copenhagen, Denmark"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"do educational meetings and group detailing change adherence to drug formularies in hospitals a cluster randomized controlled trial","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00228-013-1589-2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-004543","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000329095900012","type":"wos"},{"id":"84891844788","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24077960","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-5d902b25-d41f-4ee2-87ea-4e36012bac0b","sdu-0337667e-9132-4eef-8723-6aaf18f1cb40"],"keyword":["Cluster-randomized controlled trial","Educational meetings","Group detailing","Hospital","Hospital drug formulary","Intervention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E7517D4BE30FA1AE6E158F0948571765"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00228-013-1589-2","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Akut","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinisk Farmakologi [Klinik Akut]"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["SAFE Amgros I/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["The Research Unit for General Practice, Copenhagen, Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne T.","key":"pletpau","last":"Plet","locid":"0df2aaa5-9380-43ba-b749-febb40cb7e1c","name":"Plet, Hanne T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene J.","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Lene J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"René dePont","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"3f33c4f0-abcb-42c6-85af-2d24bcf025ff","name":"Christensen, René dePont","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte Søndergaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0d038015-2e02-4bb1-a4f6-2b47fe9788d1","name":"Nielsen, Gitte Søndergaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hallaspau","last":"Hallas","locid":"1fc2d4e1-080d-4c53-bd96-63186af28ae9","name":"Hallas, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8097-8708","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24077960"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00228-013-1589-2","issn":["00316970","14321041"],"issn_org":["00316970"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","pages":"109-116","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84891844788"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","amgros","safe amgros i/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5d902b25-d41f-4ee2-87ea-4e36012bac0b","sdu-0337667e-9132-4eef-8723-6aaf18f1cb40"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Do educational meetings and group detailing change adherence to drug formularies in hospitals? A cluster randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-004543","year":"2014","yearsub":2014}
{"abstract":"Background: A drug related problems database (DRP-database) was developed on request by clinical pharmacists. The information from the DRP-database has only been used locally e.g. to identify focus areas and to communicate identified DRPs to the hospital wards. Hence the quality of the data at the national level is unknown, which may compromise national analyses for benchmarking and identification of national focus areas. Objective: The aim of the study was to evaluate the use in practice, reliability and reproducibility of the DRPs documented in the Danish drug related problems database. Setting: Danish hospital pharmacies. Methods: Practice use of the DRP-database was explored by an electronic questionnaire distributed to hospital pharmacies, and consisted of questions regarding current and previous use of the DRP-database. The reliability was evaluated by comparing the categorization of 24 cases by clinical pharmacists with categorization performed by the project group. Reproducibility was explored by re-categorization of a sample of existing records in the DRP-database by two project group members individually. Main outcome measures: Observed proportion of agreement and Fleiss' kappa as measures of inter-rater reliability and reproducibility. Results: The practice use study of 12 hospital pharmacy locations revealed that when implementing the DRP-database, the majority of identified DRPs are documented in the DRP-database, however, some variations throughout the country exist. The interrater reliability study of 34 clinical pharmacists showed high inter-rater reliability with the project group (Fleiss' kappa = 0.79 with 95 % CI (0.70; 0.88)), and the reproducibility study also documented high inter-rater reliability of a sample of 379 records from the DRP-database re-categorized by two project group members (Fleiss' kappa = 0.81 with 95 % CI (0.78; 0.85)). Conclusion: The study showed high reliability and reproducibility of the DRP-database, however, some local variation in the use of the DRP-database throughout the country existed affecting the overall quality. These findings indicate that data in the DRP-database may be pooled, and national analyses may be conducted to explore development areas for common interest.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","Birkholm, Trine","Fischer, Hanne","Graabæk, Trine","Hansen, Merete Kjær","Kibsdal, Karina Porsborg","Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","Truelshøj, Tania Holtum"],"cuid":["S03-097.51-012049"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kjeldsen, Lene Juel"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre for Clinical Research"],"keyword":["Appropriateness","Clinical pharmacists","Clinical pharmacy","DRP","Database","Denmark","Hospital","Hospitals","Medication review","Pharmacology","Recommendations","SYSTEM","Ward"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["The Danish Research Unit of Hospital Pharmacy, AMGROS I/S, Copenhagen"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a national drug related problems database evaluation of use in practice reliability and reproducibility","src":["aau","dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11096-014-9957-2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.51-012049","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000340093900012","type":"wos"},{"id":"24899212","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84905980842","type":"scopus"}],"i