{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To evaluate whether early reductions in CT perfusion parameters predict response to pre-operative chemotherapy prior to surgery for gastroesophageal junction (GEJ) and gastric cancer. MATERIALS AND METHODS: Twenty-eight patients with adenocarcinoma of the gastro-esophageal junction (GEJ) and stomach were included. Patients received three series of chemotherapy before surgery, each consisting of a 3-week cycle of intravenous epirubicin, cisplatin or oxaliplatin, concomitant with capecitabine peroral. The patients were evaluated with a CT perfusion scan prior to, after the first series of, and after three series of chemotherapy. The CT perfusion scans were performed using a 320-detector row scanner. Tumour volume and perfusion parameters (arterial flow, blood volume and permeability) were computed on a dedicated workstation with a consensus between two radiologists. Response to chemotherapy was evaluated by two measures. Clinical response was defined as a tumour size reduction of more than 50%. Histological response was evaluated based on residual tumour cells in the surgical specimen using the standardized Mandard Score 1 to 5, in which values of 1 and 2 were classified as responders, and 3 to 5 were classified as nonresponders. RESULTS: A decrease in tumour permeability after one series of chemotherapy was positively correlated with clinical response after three series of chemotherapy. Significant changes in permeability and tumour volume were apparent after three series of chemotherapy in both clinical and histological responders. A cut-off value of more than 25% reduction in tumour permeability yielded a sensitivity of 69% and a specificity of 58% for predicting clinical response. CONCLUSION: Early decrease in permeability is correlated with the likelihood of clinical response to pre-operative chemotherapy in GEJ and gastric cancer. As a single diagnostic test, CT Perfusion only has moderate sensitivity and specificity in response assessment of pre-operative chemotherapy making it insufficient for clinical decision purposes.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lundsgaard Hansen, Martin","Fallentin, Eva","Lauridsen, Carsten","Law, Ian","Federspiel, Birgitte","Bæksgaard, Lene","Svendsen, Lars Bo","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-530008"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma","Adult","Aged","Esophagogastric Junction","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Neoadjuvant Therapy","Prospective Studies","Stomach Neoplasms","Tomography X Ray Computed","Tumor Markers Biological"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computed tomography ct perfusion as an early predictive marker for treatment response to neoadjuvant chemotherapy in gastroesophageal junction cancer and gastric cancer a prospective study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0097605","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-530008","identifier":[{"id":"24845062","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84901299865","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4028233","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-e4bf1389-44aa-4964-bc43-f57318e0c9ae"],"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma","Adult","Aged","Esophagogastric Junction","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Neoadjuvant Therapy","Prospective Studies","Stomach Neoplasms","Tomography, X-Ray Computed","Tumor Markers, Biological"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9BF0BB20F6E6FECDBFC90AB11CC83A2C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0097605","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"lundsgaardhansenpau","last":"Lundsgaard Hansen","name":"Lundsgaard Hansen, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"fallentinpau","last":"Fallentin","name":"Fallentin, Eva","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","name":"Lauridsen, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ian","key":"lawpau","last":"Law","name":"Law, Ian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte","key":"federspielpau","last":"Federspiel","name":"Federspiel, Birgitte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"bæksgaardpau","last":"Bæksgaard","name":"Bæksgaard, Lene","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"247c86c0-0475-4af7-a7be-f67a38812a1e","name":"Svendsen, Lars Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24845062"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0097605","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"5","journal":"PLOS ONE","pages":"1-10","paperid":"e97605","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901299865"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e4bf1389-44aa-4964-bc43-f57318e0c9ae"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computed Tomography (CT) Perfusion as an Early Predictive Marker for Treatment Response to Neoadjuvant Chemotherapy in Gastroesophageal Junction Cancer and Gastric Cancer - A Prospective Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-530008","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The objective of this study was to evaluate the scientific literature concerning asbestos and lung cancer, emphasizing low-level exposure. A literature search in PubMed and Embase resulted in 5,864 citations. Information from included studies was extracted using SIGN. Twenty-one statements were evidence graded. The results show that histology and location are not helpful in differentiating asbestos-related lung cancer. Pleural plaques, asbestos bodies, or asbestos fibers are useful as markers of asbestos exposure. The interaction between asbestos and smoking regarding lung cancer risk is between additive and multiplicative. The findings indicate that the association between asbestos exposure and lung cancer risk is basically linear, but may level off at very high exposures. The relative risk for lung cancer increases between 1% and 4% per fiber-year (f-y)/mL, corresponding to a doubling of risk at 25-100 f-y/mL. However, one high-quality case-control study showed a doubling at 4 f-y/mL.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Snabe","Bælum, Jesper","Rasmussen, Jesper","Dahl, Søren","Olsen, Karen Ege","Albin, Maria","Gerner Hansen, Niels-Christian","Lee Sherson, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-626010"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Asbestos","Lung Neoplasms","Lung cancer","Occupational Exposure"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"occupational asbestos exposure and lung cancer a systematic review of the literature","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/19338244.2013.863752","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-626010","identifier":[{"id":"84895795261","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24410115","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b820a6e1-da74-496f-b6a9-bf96aa6ef919"],"keyword":["Asbestos","Interaction between exposures","Lung cancer","Lung neoplasms","Occupational exposure","Smoking and asbestos"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6A0217BAD336E2D28D074A0DE82C1854"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/19338244.2013.863752","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Occupational and Environmental Medicine (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Snabe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e61e2c03-f2e6-49f5-8431-ed72245a72d5","name":"Nielsen, Lene Snabe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bælumpau","last":"Bælum","locid":"c8e0780b-a76a-4aef-be25-d870d305b527","name":"Bælum, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8221-4664","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c290c007-4167-4bcb-884a-36426c54b2da","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"aa50a5b3-6715-4224-adea-ac2f0afad794","name":"Dahl, Søren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen Ege","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d5fca320