ity, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Akut","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinisk Farmakologi [Klinik Akut]"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Juel","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"birkholmpau","last":"Birkholm","name":"Birkholm, Trine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Hanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"graabækpau","last":"Graabæk","locid":"67e97b89-6918-4950-9557-f5e3939a3c57","name":"Graabæk, Trine","orcid":"0000-0001-6848-3107","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Karina Porsborg","key":"kibsdalpau","last":"Kibsdal","locid":"89c12003-fb35-4888-b6a7-a25ecf8ffa78","name":"Kibsdal, Karina Porsborg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Vestergaard","key":"ravnnielsenpau","last":"Ravn-Nielsen","name":"Ravn-Nielsen, Lene Vestergaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tania Holtum","key":"truelshøjpau","last":"Truelshøj","name":"Truelshøj, Tania Holtum","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24736894"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11096-014-9939-4","issn":["22107703","22107711"],"issn_org":["22107703"],"issue":"4","journal":"International Journal of Clinical Pharmacy","pages":"734-741","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Clinical Pharmacy","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905963146"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","amgros"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1570d332-0c27-4d44-9149-93bae76d34d6","sdu-3bdd7ba8-3ce4-4da0-9b72-e707b349da87"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Characterization of drug-related problems identified by clinical pharmacy staff at Danish hospitals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.95-001100","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Background Blood transfusions are frequently given to patients with septic shock. However, the benefits and harms of different hemoglobin thresholds for transfusion have not been established. Methods In this multicenter, parallel-group trial, we randomly assigned patients in the intensive care unit (ICU) who had septic shock and a hemoglobin concentration of 9 g per deciliter or less to receive 1 unit of leukoreduced red cells when the hemoglobin level was 7 g per deciliter or less (lower threshold) or when the level was 9 g per deciliter or less (higher threshold) during the ICU stay. The primary outcome measure was death by 90 days after randomization. Results We analyzed data from 998 of 1005 patients (99.3%) who underwent randomization. The two intervention groups had similar baseline characteristics. In the ICU, the lower-threshold group received a median of 1 unit of blood (interquartile range, 0 to 3) and the higher-threshold group received a median of 4 units (interquartile range, 2 to 7). At 90 days after randomization, 216 of 502 patients (43.0%) assigned to the lower-threshold group, as compared with 223 of 496 (45.0%) assigned to the higher-threshold group, had died (relative risk, 0.94; 95% confidence interval, 0.78 to 1.09; P=0.44). The results were similar in analyses adjusted for risk factors at baseline and in analyses of the per-protocol populations. The numbers of patients who had ischemic events, who had severe adverse reactions, and who required life support were similar in the two intervention groups. Conclusions Among patients with septic shock, mortality at 90 days and rates of ischemic events and use of life support were similar among those assigned to blood transfusion at a higher hemoglobin threshold and those assigned to blood transfusion at a lower threshold; the latter group received fewer transfusions. (Funded by the Danish Strategic Research Council and others; TRISS ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT01485315 .).","author_count":42,"contributors":["Holst, Lars B","Haase, Nicolai","Wetterslev, Jørn","Wernerman, Jan","Guttormsen, Anne B","Karlsson, Sari","Johansson, Pär I","Aneman, Anders","Vang, Marianne L","Winding, Robert","Nebrich, Lars","Nibro, Helle L","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Lauridsen, Johnny R M","Nielsen, Jane S","Oldner, Anders","Pettilä, Ville","Cronhjort, Maria B","Andersen, Lasse H","Pedersen, Ulf G","Reiter, Nanna","Wiis, Jørgen","White, Jonathan O","Russell, Lene","Thornberg, Klaus J","Hjortrup, Peter B","Müller, Rasmus G","Møller, Morten H","Steensen, Morten","Tjäder, Inga","Kilsand, Kristina","Odeberg-Wernerman, Suzanne","Sjøbø, Brit","Bundgaard, Helle","Thyø, Maria A","Lodahl, David","Mærkedahl, Rikke","Albeck, Carsten","Illum, Dorte","Kruse, Mary","Winkel, Per","Perner, Anders"],"cuid":["S03-098.79-002205"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["TRISS Trial Group","the TRISS Trial Group and the Scandinavian Critical Care Trials Group"],"keyword":["Aged","Erythrocyte Transfusion","Female","Hemoglobins","Humans","Intensive Care Units","Ischemia","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Ischemia","Risk","Shock Septic","Single Blind Method"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lower versus higher hemoglobin threshold for transfusion in septic shock","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1056/NEJMoa1406617","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-098.79-002205","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000342674800007","type":"wos"},{"id":"84907880388","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25270275","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-2bd07ded-472b-4962-91b5-a1