{"abstract":"Patients with cancer experience side effects related to their antineoplastic treatment. Demands for efficiency limit the time patients spend with health professionals. This requires that professionals are able to offer adequate support to patients in coping with side effects of treatment in everyday life. However, it appears that the level of information about and support in living with side effects may be insufficient.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pedersen, Birgith","Koktved, Dorte Pallesen","Nielsen, Lene Lyngø"],"cuid":["S02-093.55-007877"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"living with side effects from cancer treatment a challenge to target information","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1471-6712.2012.01085.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-093.55-007877","identifier":[{"id":"84880280882","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23034150","type":"pmid"},{"id":"WOS:000321625800026","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-a30a2d76-b61e-4a9b-9ec3-967645d9f0f1","au-eb404ad6-33bf-4db1-a7c7-b6a1d655531a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-37B60EF78691AC865C5CC24C6A96DD4C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1471-6712.2012.01085.x","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD