":"Fink, Per","orcid":"0000-0003-2921-4099","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus Vinther","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"033d1aa9-948f-4ed4-be3e-200d0100b399","name":"Nielsen, Claus Vinther","orcid":"0000-0002-2467-1103","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","eisbn":["9788792462831"],"isbn":["9788792462824"],"pages":"72","place":"København","publisher":"Komiteen for Sundhedsoplysning","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a0330523-d475-42b2-a7ca-46c756ac3453"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Funktionelle lidelser : Klinisk vejledning for almen praksis, DSAM","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-220600","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The primary aim of this study was to investigate the effect of different training types and secondary to test gender differences on the training-related cortical plasticity induced by three different tongue training paradigms: 1. Therapeutic tongue exercises (TTE), 2. Playing computer games with the tongue using Tongue Drive System (TDS) and 3. Tongue-protrusion task (TPT). Forty-eight participants were randomized into 3 groups with 1 h of TTE, TDS, or TPT. Stimulus–response curves of motor evoked potentials (MEPs) and motor cortex mapping for tongue muscles and first dorsal interosseous (FDI) (control) were established using transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) at three time-points: (1) before tongue training, (2) immediately after training, (3) 1 h after training. Subject-based reports of motivation, fun, pain and fatigue were evaluated on 0-10 numerical rating scales (NRS) after training. The resting motor thresholds of tongue MEPs were lowered by training with TDS and TPT (P<0.011) but not by TTE (P=0.167). Tongue MEP amplitudes increased after training with TDS and TPT (P<0.030) but not with TTE (P=0.302). Men had higher MEPs than women in the TDS group (P<0.045) at all time-points. No significant effect of tongue training on FDI MEPs was observed (P>0.335). The tongue cortical motor map areas were not significantly increased by training (P>0.142). Training with TDS was most motivating and fun (P<0.001) and TTE was rated most painful (P<0.001). Fatigue level was not different between groups (P>0.071). These findings suggest a differential effect of tongue training paradigms on training-induced cortical plasticity and subject-based scores of fun, motivation and pain in healthy subjects.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kothari, Mohit","Svensson, Peter","Jensen, Jim","Kjærsgaard, Annette","Jeonghee, Kim","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Ghovanloo, Maysam","Baad-Hansen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-249257"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Cortical plasticity","Motor learning","Tongue training","Transcranial magnetic stimulation TMS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"training induced cortical plasticity compared between three tongue training paradigms","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23632170","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-249257","identifier":[{"id":"84878178065","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d1dfbb4b-da83-4fdb-9949-26fb58826226"],"keyword":["Tongue Drive System (TDS)","Transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS)","cortical plasticity","motor learning","tongue training"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2E1E516675CD9EAD8B66F878C9E65EDF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23632170","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Orofacial Pain and Jaw Function"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital of Hammel, Neuro Rehabilitation Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mohit","key":"kotharipau","last":"Kothari","locid":"04b2613a-b642-417f-9f1d-08167c4832ec","name":"Kothari, Mohit","orcid":"0000-0002-8191-9769","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"163ec423-3f89-45a0-8cd8-81455aa6a507","name":"Svensson, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jim","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jim","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette","key":"kjærsgaardpau","last":"Kjærsgaard","locid":"1658b2ce-3e2b-4db3-b619-db3b89d8d337","name":"Kjærsgaard, Annette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"jeongheepau","last":"Jeonghee","name":"Jeonghee, Kim","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Feldbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maysam","key":"ghovanloopau","last":"Ghovanloo","name":"Ghovanloo, Maysam","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"baadhansenpau","last":"Baad-Hansen","locid":"6938b236-4958-4da7-bbeb-dccb0abc973c","name":"Baad-Hansen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-2399-7910","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03064522","03610713"],"issn_org":["03064522"],"journal":"Neuroscience","pages":"1-12","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Neuroscience","volume":"246"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84878178065"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d1dfbb4b-da83-4fdb-9949-26fb58826226"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Training induced cortical plasticity compared between three tongue training paradigms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-249257","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Biosynthetic pathways of secondary metabolites from fungi are currently subject to an intense effort to elucidate the genetic basis for these compounds due to their large potential within pharmaceutics and synthetic biochemistry. The preferred method is methodical gene deletions to identify supporting enzymes for key synthases one cluster at a time. In this study, we design and apply a DNA expression array for Aspergillus nidulans in combination with legacy data to form a comprehensive gene expression compendium. We apply a guilt-by-association-based analysis to predict the extent of the biosynthetic clusters for the 58 synthases active in our set of experimental conditions. A comparison with legacy data shows the method to be accurate in 13 of 16 known clusters and nearly accurate for the remaining 3 clusters. Furthermore, we apply a data clustering approach, which identifies cross-chemistry between physically separate gene clusters (superclusters), and validate this both with legacy data and experimentally by prediction and verification of a supercluster consisting of the synthase AN1242 and the prenyltransferase AN11080, as well as identification of the product compound nidulanin A. We have used A. nidulans for our method development and validation due to the wealth of available biochemical data, but the method can be applied to any fungus with a sequenced and assembled genome, thus supporting further secondary metabolite pathway elucidation in the fungal kingdom.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Andersen, Mikael Rørdam","Hoof, Jakob Blæsbjerg","Klitgaard, Andreas","Petersen, Lene Maj","Zachariasen, Mia","Hansen, Tilde J","Holberg Blicher, Lene","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","Nielsen, Kristian Fog","Mortensen, Uffe Hasbro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365213"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aspergilli","Natural products","Polyketide synthases","Secondary metabolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accurate prediction of secondary metabolite gene clusters in filamentous fungi","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1205532110","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-365213","identifier":[{"id":"23248299","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84871997235","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3538241","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-cb159602-7b06-4f48-8736-949416e1ee71"],"keyword":["Aspergilli","Natural products","Polyketide synthases","Secondary metabolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF373BE4081B40A181415641CD5CDC33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1205532110","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikael Rørdam","key":"andersenmikaelrørdampau","last":"Andersen","locid":"2b65dbe3-5af3-4d59-84ef-d999b36e5376","name":"Andersen, Mikael Rørdam","orcid":"0000-0003-4794-6808","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Blæsbjerg","key":"hoofjakobblæsbjergpau","last":"Nielsen","loc