{"abstract":"Diabetes increases the risk of cardiovascular complications including arrhythmias, but the underlying mechanisms remain to be established. Decreased conduction velocity (CV), which is an independent risk factor for re-entry arrhythmias, is present in models with streptozotocin (STZ) induced type 1 diabetes. Whether CV is also disturbed in models of type 2 diabetes is currently unknown.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Olsen, Kristine Boisen","Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","Braunstein, Thomas Hartig","Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","Andersen, Claus B","Ploug, Thorkil","von Holstein-Rathlou, Niels-Henrik","Nielsen, Morten Schak"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-448233"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"myocardial impulse propagation is impaired in right ventricular tissue of zucker diabetic fatty zdf rats","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1475-2840-12-19","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-448233","identifier":[{"id":"84872273146","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3561236","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23327647","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5b89e340-6236-49e3-97e0-75f3c73d2efc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7865DA7AF6B8F00555E6144AA888781A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1475-2840-12-19","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe,