":"Jespersen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-2555-5948","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mogens","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"8798000a-c1ff-4e17-ab23-c5fafd78d7f2","name":"Jakobsen, Mogens","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ronald Ross","key":"watsonpedh","last":"Watson","name":"Watson, Ronald Ross","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Victor R.","key":"preedypedh","last":"Preedy","name":"Preedy, Victor R.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sherma","key":"editorspedh","last":"Editors","name":"Editors, Sherma","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-1-61779-803-0_4","isbn":["9781617798023"],"pages":"39-60","publisher":"Humana Press","series":"Nutrition and Health","status":"p","title":"Chocolate in health and nutrition"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85013228014"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-708e1b7e-51f1-4031-9a6b-56839f7189bb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The microbiology of cocoa fermentation","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-460673","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Scotch broom, Cytisus scoparius, spreads rapidly in parts of Denmark and is considered an invasive species by some authors. However, the species has been present in the Danish flora for centuries and is therefore considered native to Denmark. In the present study we explore whether Danish Scotch broom consists of one or two gene pools with potential differences in phenotype and invasiveness. One plastid and five nuclear microsatellite markers were used to reveal potential substructuring of Danish Scotch broom. Nine populations were included representing populations exhibiting invasive behaviour and populations showing non-invasive behaviour. An Italian population was used as reference. Bayesian analysis based on genetic markers indicated that the sampled populations form two distinct gene pools, and this pattern was supported by neighbour-joining trees. Measurements of height and width of the analysed plants showed that the two gene pools correspond to populations exhibiting either a horizontal habit and non-invasive behaviour or an erect habit and, in some cases, invasive behaviour. The Italian population clustered with the erect ones. We discuss the origin and taxonomic status of the two gene pools and conclude that Danish horizontal Scotch broom should be given a formal taxonomic status in order to initiate conservation activities for its protection.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rosenmeier, Lars","Kjær, Erik Dahl","Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-473044"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the scotch broom em cytisus scoparius em fabaceae a paradox in denmark an invasive plant or endangered native species","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.2012.01319.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-473044","identifier":[{"id":"84872611445","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8501ca26-d1e5-4841-95e9-38c1f6d24b16"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-33B94415B866E140AE1DC738ADC8A3EC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.2012.01319.x","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"rosenmeierpau","last":"Rosenmeier","locid":"e69c0f13-190c-493d-9ae8-ee78e19455ee","name":"Rosenmeier, Lars","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik Dahl","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"e1bdaffb-0384-4159-aa20-a913a2cee948","name":"Kjær, Erik Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8624-1611","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1095-8339.2012.01319.x","issn":["00244074","10958339"],"issn_org":["00244074"],"issue":"2","journal":"Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society","pages":"429-440","status":"p","title":"Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society","volume":"171"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84872611445"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8501ca26-d1e5-4841-95e9-38c1f6d24b16"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Scotch broom, <em>Cytisus scoparius</em> (Fabaceae), a paradox in Denmark – an invasive plant or endangered native species?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-473044","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Chlorhexidine is used as a disinfectant to prevent surgical infections. Recently, studies have indicated that chlorhexidine usage has selected methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus strains that are tolerant to chlorhexidine and that this may be related to the presence of the qacA/B-encoded efflux pumps. Here, we evaluated if high-level exposure to chlorhexidine selects for tolerant colonizing Staphylococcus epidermidis and we addressed the consequences of long-term exposure to chlorhexidine.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Skovgaard, Sissel","Larsen, Marianne Halberg","Nielsen, Lene Nørby","Skov, Robert Leo","Wong, Christian","Westh, Henrik","Ingmer, Hanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-505246"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recently introduced em qaca b em genes in em staphylococcus epidermidis em do not increase chlorhexidine mic mbc","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/jac/dkt182","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-505246","identifier":[{"id":"23739538","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84887822370","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bb510e1b-0ee1-4e27-be4e-10876daf2635"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5A21D61D0F7D71915CC3EF5FF2B66A26"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/jac/dkt182","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"