ffno":"","first":"Richard","key":"farliepau","last":"Farlie","name":"Farlie, Richard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"hosethpau","last":"Hoseth","name":"Hoseth, Eva","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Torben","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Torben","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Olav Bjørn","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Olav Bjørn","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Inger","key":"stornespau","last":"Stornes","name":"Stornes, Inger","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars O.","key":"vejerslevpau","last":"Vejerslev","name":"Vejerslev, Lars O.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle","key":"zingenbergpau","last":"Zingenberg","name":"Zingenberg, Helle","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23494847"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/uog.12460","issn":["09607692","14690705"],"issn_org":["09607692"],"issue":"5","journal":"Ultrasound in Obstetrics & Gynecology","pages":"530-5","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Ultrasound in Obstetrics & Gynecology","title_org":"Ultrasound in obstetrics & gynecology : the official journal of the International Society of Ultrasound in Obstetrics and Gynecology","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84886949371"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b19c7e28-827b-4912-aea2-c084bfc144f8","ku-50dd4953-19bd-4169-a020-6e179bd586ff","sdu-df00febd-10cc-45d9-8512-a1b4b82293c9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Detection of triploidy at 11-14 weeks of gestation : A cohort study of 198,000 pregnant women","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-087.50-025622","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background: Germ-line mutations in the DNA mismatch repair genes MLH1, MSH2, and MSH6 predispose to the development of colorectal cancer (Lynch syndrome or hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal cancer). These mutations include disease-causing frame-shift, nonsense, and splicing mutations as well as large genomic rearrangements. However, a large number of mutations, including missense, silent, and intronic variants, are classified as variants of unknown clinical significance. Methods: Intronic MLH1, MSH2, or MSH6 variants were investigated using in silico prediction tools and mini-gene assay to asses the effect on splicing. Results: We describe in silico and in vitro characterization of nine intronic MLH1, MSH2, or MSH6 mutations identified in Danish colorectal cancer patients, of which four mutations are novel. The analysis revealed aberrant splicing of five mutations (MLH1 c. 588 + 5G > A, MLH1 c. 677 + 3A > T, MLH1 c. 1732-2A > T, MSH2 c. 1276 + 1G > T, and MSH2 c. 1662-2A > C), while four mutations had no effect on splicing compared to wild type (MLH1 c. 117-34A > T, MLH1 c. 1039-8 T > A, MSH2 c. 2459-18delT, and MSH6 c. 3439-16C > T). Conclusions: In conclusion, we classify five MLH1/MSH2 mutations as pathogenic, whereas four MLH1/MSH2/MSH6 mutations are classified as neutral. This study supports the notion that in silico prediction tools and mini-gene assays are important for the classification of intronic variants, and thereby crucial for the genetic counseling of patients and their family members.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Petersen, Sanne M","Dandanell, Mette","Rasmussen, Lene J","Gerdes, Anne-Marie Axø","Krogh, Lotte Nylandsted","Bernstein, Inge","Okkels, Henrik","Wikman, Friedrik","Nielsen, Finn C","Hansen, Thomas V O"],"cuid":["S03-091.37-011778"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Adaptor Proteins Signal Transducing","Colorectal Neoplasms","Colorectal cancer","DNA Binding Proteins","Denmark","European Continental Ancestry Group","Genetic Counseling","HNPCC","Humans","Introns","Lynch syndrome","MutS Homolog 2 Protein","Mutation","Nuclear Proteins","RNA Splice Sites"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Human Genetik"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"functional examination of mlh000000000001 msh000000000002 and msh000000000006 intronic mutations identified in danish colorectal cancer patients","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2350-14-103","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-091.37-011778","identifier":[{"id":"84884859439","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3850734","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000325793000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"24090359","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f6661a8f-b426-4096-a96b-8dc076f52343","ku-62eb1a58-0384-40aa-a07c-92d484794383","sdu-778d8da1-a450-4358-94d7-9c44f5389d0a"],"keyword":["Adaptor Proteins, Signal Transducing","Colorectal Neoplasms","Colorectal cancer","DNA-Binding Proteins","Denmark","European Continental Ancestry Group","Genetic Counseling","HNPCC","Humans","Introns","Lynch syndrome","Mini-gene assay","Mismatch repair genes MLH1, MSH2, and MSH6","MutS Homolog 2 Protein","Mutation","Nuclear Proteins","RNA Splice Sites","Splicing defect"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-CB62D40606974499FC87499BDA9D0D60"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2350-14-103","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.bi