{"abstract":"Liver diseases are the leading causes of death in human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-positive persons since the widespread use of combination antiretroviral treatment (cART). Most of these deaths are due to hepatitis C (HCV) or B (HBV) virus coinfections. Little is known about other causes. Prolonged exposure to some antiretroviral drugs might increase hepatic mortality.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Kovari, Helen","Sabin, Caroline A","Ledergerber, Bruno","Nielsen, Lene Ryom","Worm, Signe W","Smith, Colette","Phillips, Andrew","Reiss, Peter","Fontas, Eric","Petoumenos, Kathy","De Wit, Stéphane","Morlat, Philippe","Lundgren, Jens","Weber, Rainer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-418769"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Hospital Zürich"],"keyword":["Adult","Anti Retroviral Agents","Antiretroviral Therapy Highly Active","Data Collection","Drug Related Side Effects and Adverse Reactions","Female","Follow Up Studies","HIV Infections","Humans","Incidence","Liver failure","Male","Middle Aged","Prospective Studies","Survival Analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antiretroviral drug related liver mortality among hiv positive persons in the absence of hepatitis b or c virus coinfection the data collection on adverse events of anti hiv drugs study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/cid/cis919","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-418769","identifier":[{"id":"23090925","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84874781674","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3582358","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-2a77d8df-2c21-45db-ac86-d79