{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Adimpong, David Bichala","Sørensen, Kim I.","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","Thorsen, Line","Rasmussen, Thomas B.","Derkx, Patrick M.F.","Jespersen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-467029"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"draft whole genome sequence of em bacillus sonorensis em strain l000000000012 a source of nonribosomal lipopeptides","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/123276868/Genome_Announc._2013_Adimpong_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-467029","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3622994","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84937840238","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23538904","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7ae738ce-63e5-491c-a139-646914906adf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1274433C8D04AC555799FBF187163BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/123276868/Genome_Announc._2013_Adimpong_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://genomea.asm.org/content/1/2/e00097-13.full","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/genomeA.00097-13","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology, Gut Health, and Fermentation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Chr. Hansen"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"David Bichala","key":"adimpongpau","last":"Adimpong","locid":"4db0ae2e-8bbf-4026-8e4d-cdd58029a5b0","name":"Adimpong, David Bichala","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kim I.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Kim I.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dennis Sandris","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"thorsenpau","last":"Thorsen","locid":"c882a60f-763a-4496-93be-335fe3451a41","name":"Thorsen, Line","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thomas B.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Patrick M.F.","key":"derkxpau","last":"Derkx","name":"Derkx, Patrick M.F.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"a156c6e3-9562-4d35-9305-53a39c62e076","name":"Jespersen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-2555-5948","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23538904"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/genomea.00097-13","issn":["21698287"],"issue":"2","journal":"Genome Announcements","status":"p","title":"Genome Announcements","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84937840238"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7ae738ce-63e5-491c-a139-646914906adf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Draft whole-genome sequence of <em>Bacillus sonorensis </em>strain L12, a source of nonribosomal lipopeptides","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-467029","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Intestinal epithelial cell (IEC) death signalling through the Fas receptor is impaired in active ulcerative colitis (UC). This is possibly due to the activation of cytoprotective pathways resulting in limitation of the tissue injury secondary to inflammation. We hypothesized that inflammatory signalling like the nuclear factor (NF)-κB or mitogen activated protein kinase (MAPK) pathways could be involved in (a) the modification of Fas mediated apoptosis responses and (b) the regulation of the Fas receptor inhibitor cellular FLICE-like inhibitory protein (c-FLIP). Phospho-ERK was upregulated in IECs in active UC as well as IECs exposed to pro-inflammatory cytokines in vitro. Similarly, the short form of c-FLIP (c-FLIPS) was found to be upregulated in IECs from patients with active UC. c-FLIPS was the main splice variant found in both HT-29 cells and primary human IECs. Both splice variants were induced by TNF-α, IL-1β and IFN-γ, while IL-10 induced c-FLIPL expression; TNF-α also induced c-FLIPS in primary IECs. Inhibition of NF-κB, JNK and p38 pathways did not affect c-FLIP expression, whereas ERK inhibition by MEK1 RNA silencing and pharmacologic inhibitors decreased c-FLIPS expression. Similarly, ERK - but not NF-κB - inhibited Fas ligand and TNF-α-mediated apoptosis responses in both cell line experiments and primary IECs. The present study identifies the MEK-ERK pathway as a major regulator of apoptosis in IECs during flares of UC and an inducer of c-FLIPS. The results explain the resistance to receptor mediated epithelial apoptosis in active UC. Oncogenic c-FLIP could promote propagation of DNA-damaged IECs and contribute to cancer development in UC.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","Coskun, Mehmet","Vainer, Ben","Riis, Lene Buhl","Soendergaard, Christoffer","Nielsen, Ole Haagen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-468465"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","CASP8 and FADD Like Apoptosis Regulating Protein","Colitis Ulcerative","Colon","Cytokines","Epithelial Cells","Extracellular Signal Regulated MAP Kinases","HT29 Cells","Humans","Middle Aged","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"erk controls epithelial cell death receptor signalling and cellular flice like inhibitory protein c flip in ulcerative colitis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00109-013-1003-7","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-468465","identifier":[{"id":"23371318","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84879837232","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7d4ca9a9-8e21-4567-845e-686bf6065165"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","CASP8 and FADD-Like Apoptosis Regulating Protein","Colitis, Ulcerative","Colon","Cytokines","Epithelial Cells","Extracellular Signal-Regulated MAP Kinases","HT29 Cells","Humans","Middle Aged","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DB2F543D3CBD8E19C2370B7CFFCD935A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00109-013-1003-7","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jakob Benedict","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","locid":"e31587ea-e362-4ce5-942d-bc27c0f0d340","name":"Seidelin, Jakob Benedict","orcid":"0000-0003-3230-7966","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mehmet","key":"coskunpau","last":"Coskun","locid":"6a19eccb-de97-41ce-9daa-a75afe94aa20","name":"Coskun, Mehmet","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ben","key":"vainerpau","last":"Vainer","locid":"87ab1fdc-ec92-4c01-87a4-3e4dcc3b8684","name":"Vainer, Ben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","name_org":"Riis, Lene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christoffer","key":"soendergaardpau","last":"Soendergaard","name":"Soendergaard, Christoffer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole Haagen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59658c4-dde8-4749-9b5c-f4ec5910dd02","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","orcid":"0000-0003-4612-8635","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23371318"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00109-013-1003-7","issn":["09462716","14321440"],"issn_org":["09462716"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Molecular Medicine","pages":"839-49","status":"p","title":"Journal of Molecular Medicine","volume":"91"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879837232"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7d4ca9a9-8e21-4567-845e-686bf6065165"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"ERK controls epithelial cell death receptor signalling and cellular FLICE-like inhibitory protein (c-FLIP) in ulcerative colitis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-468465","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background: Patients suffering from schizophrenia and affective disorder have an increased risk of the metabolic syndrome (MeS); hence identification of patients developing MeS may help preventing morbidity and mortality. Aims: The aim of the study was to evaluate the effect of outreach visit by clinical pharmacists to support the implementation of screening of MeS at a psychiatric ward. Methods: The study was conducted at the psychiatric ward, Odense University Hospital. In 2008, clinical guidelines for systematic screening and prevention of metabolic risk were developed and implemented by passive dissemination (PD) followed by a period of active implementation (AI). AI contained outreach visits by clinical pharmacists on a weekly basis. Patients with affective disorder or schizophrenia were included. The study was designed as a before-and-after study, and electronic patient charts were used for assessment of adherence to the clinical guidelines. Results: In total, 205 patients were included in the study (93 patients in the PD group, 112 patients in the AI group). A significant improvement of the use of the screening sheet from 36% in the PD group to 81% in the AI group was found (p < 0.001). Consequently, the quality of the screening increased significantly resulting in 45% in the AI group being identified with MeS compared with 10% in the PD group (p < 0.001). Conclusion: The outreach visits by clinical pharmacists significantly improved the use of the screening sheet and resulted in a significant increase in the proportion of patients identified with MeS (p < 0.001). Clinical implications: The increase in the use of a screening sheet for MeS among patients admitted to a psychiatric ward as a result of outreach visits by clinical pharmacist improve assessment for MeS. This may lead to better identification of patients suffering from MeS and hence increase the possibility of treating MeS and preventing morbidity and mortaligy.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","Hansen, Per Sveistrup","Kristensen, Anne Mette Fisker","Christensen, Anders","Sørensen, Claus Havregaard","Nielsen, Bent"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-574535"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Female","Humans","Male","Mass Screening","Metabolic Syndrome complications","Metabolic syndrome","Middle Aged","Mood Disorders complications","Pharmacists","Psychiatric Department Hospital","Psychiatry","Schizophrenia complications"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outreach visits by clinical pharmacists improve screening for the metabolic syndrome among mentally ill patients","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/08039488.2012.732115","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Declaration of interest: The authors report no conflicts of interest. The authors alone are responsible for the content and writing of the paper. The study received funding from “ Sygehusapotekernes og Amgros ’ forsknings-og udviklingspulje ” ."],"id":"S01-000.00-574535","identifier":[{"id":"23126478","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84880291802","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-04a867ac-0ae1-424e-b9a2-4cd692aa997e"],"keyword":["Adult","Clinical pharmacy service","Female","Humans","Male","Mass Screening","Metabolic Syndrome/complications","Metabolic syndrome","Middle Aged","Mood Disorders/complications","Pharmacists","Psychiatric Department, Hospital","Psychiatry","Schizophrenia/complications"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF0870587FB2DD968727575A5D989EA2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/08039488.2012.732115","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Amgros"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Psychiatry (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Juel","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Per Sveistrup","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2aba59a6-7a93-4034-9ca4-e6f90b825d94","name":"Hansen, Per Sveistrup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Mette Fisker","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Anne Mette Fisker","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"2e62405a-7162-42dc-be77-dd8fea4b729e","name":"Christensen, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Havregaard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"929e4d6c-5f39-48de-a579-4cb5ce1beeae","name":"Sørensen, Claus Havregaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bent","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"adc563a7-67eb-4f54-82b6-40cacc21d300","name":"Nielsen, Bent","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23126478"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/08039488.2012.732115","issn":["08039488","08039496"],"issn_org":["08039488"],"issue":"4","journal":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","pages":"249-257","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880291802"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","amgros"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-04a867ac-0ae1-424e-b9a2-4cd692aa997e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Outreach visits by clinical pharmacists improve screening for the metabolic syndrome among mentally ill patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-574535","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Forskningsprojektet ”Retention of Vocational Students in the Danish VET System” undersøger de påvirkelige faktorer, der kan bidrage til at mindske frafaldet på de erhvervsfaglige uddannelser (EUD). For etablering af en sådan viden er dannet et konsortium bestående af såvel forskere med stor erfaring med kvantitative forskningsmetoder på uddannelsesområdet som forskere med betydelige kompetencer inden for pædagogisk, didaktisk og institutionel forskning.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Nielsen, Klaus","Jørgensen, Christian Helms","Koudahl, Peter","Munk, Martin D.","Pilegaard Jensen, Torben","Tanggaard, Lene","Grønborg, Lisbeth","Hvitved, Louise","Ingemann, Lene","Jonasson, Charlotte","Lippke, Lena"],"cuid":["S02-084.78-002031"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"OT":["Arbejdsliv og læring"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kort kvalitativ rapport om fastholdelse af erhvervsskoleelever i det danske erhvervsuddannelsessystem","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://psy.au.dk/fileadmin/Psykologi/Forskning/Forskningsprojekter/Fastholdelse_af_erhvervsskoleelever/Populaerversion280813finalrev.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-084.78-002031","ids":["aau-288a5575-9109-4ef0-be8d-9dfbf13064dd","aau-e44f311b-9431-4869-a9ea-4df8ae210352"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-2-08A2CCE02F6CAFDF634161E62D616F2D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://psy.au.dk/fileadmin/Psykologi/Forskning/Forskningsprojekter/Fastholdelse_af_erhvervsskoleelever/Popu