":"Petersen","locid":"dc422bc6-c2db-4b28-b66f-9038758645ed","name":"Petersen, Lone Kjeld","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"seibækpau","last":"Seibæk","locid":"2bf95667-24b9-444b-b3e1-a62965aac67a","name":"Seibæk, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-2396-8669","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-042ad8e2-b274-4475-b8bb-e0e0f0f68fb7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Kinesiotapes effekt på lymfødem i underekstremiteterne efter operation for livmoderhalskræft","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-131662","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"A fatal accident is reported in which a small single-engine light airplane crashed. The airplane carried two persons in the front seats, both of whom possessed valid pilot certificates. Both victims were subject to autopsy, including post-mortem computed tomography scanning (PMCT) prior to the autopsy. The autopsies showed massive destruction to the bodies of the two victims but did not identify any signs of acute or chronic medical conditions that could explain loss of control of the airplane. PMCT, histological examination, and forensic chemical analysis also failed to identify an explanation for the crash. A detailed review of an airplane identical to the crashed airplane was performed in collaboration with the Danish Accident Investigation Board and the Danish National Police, National Centre of Forensic Services. The injuries were described using the abbreviated injury scale, the injury severity score, 3-dimensional reconstructions of the PMCT, and an injury pattern analysis. We describe how, on basis of these data, we reached a conclusion about which of the two victims was the most likely to have been in control of the airplane at the time of accident. Furthermore, we argue that all victims of fatal airplane crashes should be subject to forensic autopsy, including PMCT and forensic chemical analysis. The continuous accumulation of knowledge about injury patterns from “simple” accidents is the foundation for the correct analysis of “difficult” accidents.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Høyer, Christian Bjerre","Nielsen, Trine Skov","Nagel, Lise Loft","Uhrenholt, Lars","Boel, Lene Warner Thorup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-138227"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation of a fatal airplane crash autopsy computed tomography and injury pattern analysis used to determine who was steering the plane at time of accident a case report","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12024-011-9239-4","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-138227","identifier":[{"id":"21528420","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84860643865","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0f79dfd9-f15d-4c38-9312-3389f1671290"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-14B0CEAF7ACF6D9068AD61C40143E8A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21528420","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12024-011-9239-4","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Forensic Medicine","Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Unit of Medical Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Bjerre","key":"høyerpau","last":"Høyer","locid":"9ab64a69-e1b5-4618-a4a2-f26f615814e4","name":"Høyer, Christian Bjerre","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine Skov","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4f2a6062-3188-41cc-9eb2-4588187e5782","name":"Nielsen, Trine Skov","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Loft","key":"nagelpau","last":"Nagel","locid":"9483fda2-0f3a-4b48-b970-ff17335d9ac0","name":"Nagel, Lise Loft","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"uhrenholtpau","last":"Uhrenholt","locid":"3fdbbf4d-7b71-451b-b15e-928ae109fcab","name":"Uhrenholt, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2823-3995","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Warner Thorup","key":"boelpau","last":"Boel","locid":"cf69d33f-562c-489b-9564-9a9dc15c0a16","name":"Boel, Lene Warner Thorup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21528420"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12024-011-9239-4","issn":["1547769X","15562891"],"issn_org":["1547769X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Forensic Science, Medicine, and Pathology","pages":"179-188","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Forensic Science, Medicine, and Pathology","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860643865"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0f79dfd9-f15d-4c38-9312-3389f1671290"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Investigation of a fatal airplane crash: autopsy, computed tomography, and injury pattern analysis used to determine who was steering the plane at time of accident. A case report.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-138227","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
