4101-b180-38c11ad19a12"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Børn i praksis","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-490046","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Aim: To evaluate self-reported satisfaction and barriers to initiating real-time continuous glucose monitoring in early pregnancy among women with pregestational diabetes. Methods: Fifty-four women with Type 1 diabetes and 14 women with Type 2 diabetes were offered continuous glucose monitoring for 6 days at median 9 (range 6-14) gestational weeks and were asked to answer a semi-structured questionnaire on patient satisfaction. Results: Median HbA(1c) was 49 (range 34-86) mmol/mol) [6.6 (5.3-10.0) %] and duration of diabetes was 12 (0.5-37) years. Continuous glucose monitoring was used for 6 (0.5-7) days, with 43 (65%) women using continuous glucose monitoring for at least 5 days. The women experienced 2.7 (0-12) alarms per 24 h, of which approximately one third was technical alarms and one third disturbed their sleep. Sixteen women (24%) reported discomfort with continuous glucose monitoring during daytime and twelve (18%) during sleep. Many women reported improved diabetes understanding (52%) and would recommend continuous glucose monitoring to others (83%). Twenty-four patients (36%) had continuous glucose monitoring removed earlier than planned (before the intended 6 days of initial monitoring). Ten women (15%) did not wish to use continuous glucose monitoring again in pregnancy. Main causes behind early removal of continuous glucose monitoring were self-reported skin irritation, technical problems and continuous glucose monitoring inaccuracy. No differences were found in continuous glucose monitoring use, inconvenience or compliance with respect to diabetes type. Conclusions: The majority of pregnant women with diabetes found real-time continuous glucose monitoring useful and the intervention was equally tolerated regardless of diabetes type. Nevertheless, continuous glucose monitoring was frequently removed earlier than planned, primarily because of skin irritation, technical problems and inaccuracy.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Secher, A L","Madsen, A B","Nielsen, Lene Ringholm","Barfred, C","Stage, E","Andersen, Heine","Damm, Peter","Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","Ringholm, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-505869"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient satisfaction and barriers to initiating real time continuous glucose monitoring in early pregnancy in women with diabetes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1464-5491.2011.03426.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-505869","identifier":[{"id":"21883435","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84855802576","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bc6296c3-ddd5-4f2a-9c55-2a40d9f172c9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F657930194A1D10E8D37D0FFA93FC5A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1464-5491.2011.03426.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Orthopaedics and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"A L","key":"secherpau","last":"Secher","name":"Secher, A L","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"A B","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, A B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Ringholm","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ringholm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"C","key":"barfredpau","last":"Barfred","name":"Barfred, C","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"E","key":"stagepau","last":"Stage","name":"Stage, E","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Heine","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Heine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"P","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","locid":"884d03d5-5981-4d33-80c6-adb21f836deb","name":"Damm, Peter","name_org":"Damm, P","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"E R","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"3acd58f4-6d64-4a89-a406-d2f43b310500","name":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","name_org":"Mathiesen, E R","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"ringholmpau","last":"Ringholm","name":"Ringholm, Lene","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21883435"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1464-5491.2011.03426.x","issn":["07423071","14645491"],"issn_org":["07423071"],"issue":"2","journal":"Diabetic Medicine","pages":"272-7","status":"p","title":"Diabetic Medicine","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855802576"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bc6296c3-ddd5-4f2a-9c55-2a40d9f172c9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Patient satisfaction and barriers to initiating real-time continuous glucose monitoring in early pregnancy in women with diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-505869","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: In heart failure, a reduced exercise capacity is the prevailing symptom and an important prognostic marker of future outcome. The purpose of the study was to assess the relation of coronary flow reserve (CFR) to diastolic and systolic function in heart failure and to determine which are the limiting factors for exercise capacity. METHODS AND RESULTS: Forty-seven patients with left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF)","author_count":8,"contributors":["Snoer, Martin","Monk-Hansen, Tea","Olsen, Rasmus Huan","Pedersen, Lene Roerholm","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Rasmusen, Hanne","Dela, Flemming","Prescott, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514806"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coronary flow reserve as a link between diastolic and systolic function and exercise capacity in heart failure","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjci/jes269","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-514806","identifier":[{"id":"23169759","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84879233524","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cb3bbc32-023e-42de-b63d-ed88903bd934"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-555A467B30FD3F82B717F26EF426604F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ehjci/jes269","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"snoerpau","last":"Snoer","locid":"ad63ffae-8804-4380-9001-900cdc21e8c3","name":"Snoer, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tea","key":"monkhansenpau","last":"Monk-Hansen","name":"Monk-Hansen, Tea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus Huan","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Rasmus Huan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Roerholm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"9628a5c2-b78d-4447-abae-d2ef657f9230","name":"Pedersen, Lene Roerholm","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olav Wendelboe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d9fc9e11-583d-43d9-994c-df128b7bf5cc","name":"Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","orcid":"0000-0003-3532-9431","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne","key":"rasmusenpau","last":"Rasmusen","name":"Rasmusen, Hanne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming","key":"delapau","last":"Dela","locid":"5d84458e-34c1-4874-a128-7fc3cb13f7f2","name":"Dela, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0001-9970-9535","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eva","key":"prescottpau","last":"Prescott","locid":"f6d11fc8-7565-487b-943a-3c67db7e9e75","name":"Prescott, Eva","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23169759"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjci/jes269","issn":["15252167","15322114"],"issn_org":["15252167"],"journal":"European Heart Journal Cardiovascular Imaging","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal Cardiovascular Imaging"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879233524"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cb3bbc32-023e-42de-b63d-ed88903bd934"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Coronary flow reserve as a link between diastolic and systolic function and exercise capacity in heart failure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-514806","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"We present a fully automated framework for scoring a patients risk of cardiovascular disease (CVD) and mortality from a standard lateral radiograph of the lumbar aorta. The framework segments abdominal aortic calcifications for computing a CVD risk score and performs a survival analysis to validate the score. Since the aorta is invisible on X-ray images, its position is reasoned from (1) the shape and location of the lumbar vertebrae and (2) the location, shape, and orientation of potential calcifications. The proposed framework follows the principle of Bayesian inference, which has several advantages in the complex task of segmenting aortic calcifications. Bayesian modeling allows us to compute CVD risk scores conditioned on the seen calcifications by formulating distributions, dependencies, and constraints on the unknown parameters. We evaluate the framework on two datasets consisting of 351 and 462 standard lumbar radiographs, respectively. Promising results indicate that the framework has potential applications in diagnosis, treatment planning, and the study of drug effects related to CVD.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Petersen, Peter Kersten","Ganz, Melanie","Mysling, Peter","Nielsen, Mads","Erleben, Lene Lillemark","Crimi, Alessandro","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-530761"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NBIO","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NBIO","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a bayesian framework for automated cardiovascular risk scoring on standard lumbar radiographs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-530761","identifier":[{"id":"84857991479","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e5f49105-2450-4f78-bf48-a00fd297cfcc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9C197366538EA22FED7DCF1FD70691D4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"nordic bioscience","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NBIO","l3nl":"Nordic Bioscience","l3nn":"Nordic Bioscience","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nordic Bioscience","namevar":["Nordic Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NBIO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Synarc Imaging Technol. A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Peter Kersten","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"23b8fde0-51e9-43d6-b89c-40300ada67a7","name":"Petersen, Peter Kersten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Melanie","key":"ganzpau","last":"Ganz","locid":"a0225c8e-a6e9-4116-a301-a65b1d7a7b5b","name":"Ganz, Melanie","orcid":"0000-0002-9120-8098","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"myslingpau","last":"Mysling","locid":"f07749fa-c5e6-45f7-9d3c-485d27b2788c","name":"Mysling, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Mads","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52f8d6fb-fd83-4d11-ad65-3e183ca401f2","name":"Nielsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0003-1535-068X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Lene Lillemark","key":"erlebenpau","last":"Erleben","locid":"0e3ad371-b61c-4c7c-b26c-605c583bbb40","name":"Erleben, Lene Lillemark","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alessandro","key":"crimipau","last":"Crimi","locid":"da1d3a06-e1ca-491f-a5d5-c5942cdb337d","name":"Crimi, Alessandro","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tmi.2011.2174646","issn":["02780062","1558254X"],"issn_org":["02780062"],"issue":"3","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging","pages":"663-676","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Medical Imaging","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857991479"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Nordic Bioscience","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","synarc imaging technol. a/s (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e5f49105-2450-4f78-bf48-a00fd297cfcc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Bayesian framework for automated cardiovascular risk scoring on standard lumbar radiographs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-530761","year":"2012","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Background/aims: High levels of pro-inflammatory cytokines are linked to inflammatory bowel disease (IBD). The transcription factor Caudal-related homeobox transcription factor 2 (CDX2) plays a crucial role in differentiation of intestinal epithelium and regulates several inflammatory bowel disease- (IBD-) susceptibility genes, including MEP1A. The aim was to investigate the expression of CDX2 and meprin 1A (MEP1A) in colitis; to assess if they are regulated by tumor necrosis factor-α (TNF-α), and finally to reveal if CDX2 is involved in a TNF-α-induced down-regulation of MEP1A. Methods: Expression of CDX2 and MEP1A was investigated in colonic biopsies of ulcerative colitis (UC) patients and in dextran sodium sulfate (DSS)-induced colitis. CDX2 protein expression was investigated by immunoblotting and immunohistochemical procedures. CDX2 and MEP1A regulation was examined in TNF-α-treated Caco-2 cells by reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction and with reporter gene assays, and the effect of anti-TNF-α treatment was assessed using infliximab. Finally, in vivo CDX2-DNA interactions were investigated by chromatin immunoprecipitation. Results: The CDX2 and MEP1A mRNA expression was significantly decreased in active UC patients and in DSS-colitis. Colonic biopsy specimens from active UC showed markedly decreased CDX2 staining. TNF-α treatment diminished the CDX2 and MEP1A mRNA levels, a decrease which, was counteracted by infliximab treatment. Reporter gene assays showed significantly reduced CDX2 and MEP1A activity upon TNF-α stimulation. Finally, TNF-α impaired the ability of CDX2 to interact and activate its own, as well as the MEP1A expression. Conclusions: The present results indicate that a TNF-α-mediated down-regulation of CDX2 can be related to suppressed expression of MEP1A during intestinal inflammation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Coskun, Mehmet","Olsen, Anders Krüger","Holm, Thomas Lindebo","Kvist, Peter Helding","Nielsen, Ole Hagen","Riis, Lene Buhl","Olsen, Jørgen","Troelsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-565574"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tnf α induced down regulation of cdx000000000002 suppresses mep000000000001a expression in colitis","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-565574","identifier":[{"id":"84858984691","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-8e505631-eb0e-4931-acad-eeb50bc57eec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-C83E615F7BA274B5572248484B275860"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","