{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE:  To determine the influence of type 1 diabetes mellitus (T1DM) on the first trimester serum markers of fetal aneuploidy; pregnancy-associated plasmaprotein-A (PAPP-A) and free beta subunit of human chorionic gonadotropin (freeβ-hCG) and to evaluate the influence of glycemic control on these parameters in the pregnant diabetic women.  DESIGN:  Retrospective study.  SETTING:  Data were extracted from electronic obstetric and laboratorydatabases at two Danish University Hospitals.  POPULATION:  Based on 36 415 pregnancies without T1DM (non-T1DM) and 331 pregnancies with T1DM; β-hCG and PAPP-A were obtained at 8+0 to 14+2 gestational weeks.  METHODS:  Medians for PAPP-A and free β-hCG were generated and multiple of the normal gestation-specific median (MoM) values were calculated for each separate pregnancy. After adjustment for maternal weight, ethnicity and smoking status, MoM values were compared across the T1DM and non-T1DM groups, respectively. Additionally, the relationship between PAPP-A MoM and HgbA1C was examined in 348 T1DM pregnancies by Spearman's rank correlation. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES. Difference in biochemical marker levels between T1DM and non-T1DM.  RESULTS:  PAPP-A was 0.86 MoM in T1DM pregnancies and 1.01 MoM in non-T1DM pregnancies, p < 0.0001. Conversely, free β-hCG was not altered in T1DM pregnancies (T1DM 0.99 MoM, non-T1DM 0.98 MoM; p=0.14). There was a significant inverse correlation between HgbA1C and PAPP-A (rho=-0.12, p=0.02).  CONCLUSIONS:  In T1DM pregnancies, PAPP-A MoM values were lower than in non-T1DM pregnancies. This suggests that correction should be considered in first trimester biochemical screening for fetal aneuploidy in T1DM women.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Madsen, Helen Nordahl","Ekelund, Charlotte Kvist","Tørring, Niels","Ovesen, Per Glud","Friis-Hansen, Lennart","Ringholm Nielsen, Lene","Petersen, Olav Bjørn"],"cuid":["S02-098.41-018463"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Fetal Diseases","disease health science and nursing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of type 000000000001 diabetes and glycemic control on fetal aneuploidy biochemical markers","src":["au","via"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0412.2011.01212.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.41-018463","identifier":[{"id":"21671890","type":"pmid"},{"id":"83455219288","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4f8943b0-a04d-4260-aff1-212738618b01","via-1882e3ae-5e42-4eb4-b798-0b0d6839e495"],"keyword":["disease, health science and nursing","fetal diseases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-45CFA9A845378835540F9CEBBDDEB8D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0412.2011.01212.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of clinical biochemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Uddannelser, Sundhedsuddannelserne, Bioanalytikeruddannelsen Aarhus N"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno