{"abstract":"With the aim of identifying proteins important for host interaction and virulence, we have screened an expression library of NCTC 11168 Campylobacter jejuni genes for highly immunogenic proteins. A commercial C. jejuni open reading frame (ORF) library consisting of more than 1,600 genes was transformed into the Escherichia coli expression strain BL21(DE3), resulting in 2,304 clones. This library was subsequently screened for immunogenic proteins using antibodies raised in rabbit against a clinical isolate of C. jejuni; this resulted in 52 highly reactive clones representing 25 different genes after sequencing. Selected candidate genes were inactivated in C. jejuni NCTC 11168, and the virulence was examined using INT 407 epithelial cell line and motility, biofilm, autoagglutination, and serum resistance assays. These investigations revealed C. jejuni antigen 0034c (Cj0034c) to be a novel virulence factor and support the usefulness of the method. Further, several antigens were tested as vaccine candidates in two mouse models, in which Cj0034c, Cj0404, and Cj0525c resulted in a reduction of invasion in spleen and liver after challenge.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Nørby","Luijkx, Thomas A.","Vegge, Christina Skovgaard","Johnsen, Christina Kofoed","Nuijten, Piet","Wren, Brendan W.","Ingmer, Hanne","Krogfelt, Karen Angeliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-405448"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","Merck, Nobilon International B.V."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of immunogenic and virulence associated em campylobacter jejuni em proteins","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/CVI.05161-11","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-405448","identifier":[{"id":"84856413301","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3272937","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"22155767","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-142d7557-658e-476e-a40a-bd763db97dd0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-80740005CF8CC9C1EE967AD53AAE2649"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/CVI.05161-11","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"merck nobilon international b v","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Merck, Nobilon International B.V.","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"london school of hygiene and tropical medicine","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Nørby","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1a4f890a-d171-4c2f-ae00-dd1e024c25ab","name":"Nielsen, Lene Nørby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas A.","key":"luijkxpau","last":"Luijkx","name":"Luijkx, Thomas A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina Skovgaard","key":"veggepau","last":"Vegge","locid":"8417c320-b0d5-43c8-8d57-d29be3d8fac5","name":"Vegge, Christina Skovgaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christina Kofoed","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Christina Kofoed","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Piet","key":"nuijtenpau","last":"Nuijten","name":"Nuijten, Piet","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Brendan W.","key":"wrenpau","last":"Wren","name":"Wren, Brendan W.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne","key":"ingmerpau","last":"Ingmer","locid":"abe2cd31-84e7-4f06-81a3-33e08bf93b8f","name":"Ingmer, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0002-8350-5631","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Karen Angeliki","key":"krogfeltpau","last":"Krogfelt","name":"Krogfelt, Karen Angeliki","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22155767"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/cvi.05161-11","issn":["1556679X","15566811"],"issn_org":["1556679X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Clinical and Vaccine Immunology","pages":"113-119","status":"p","title":"Clinical and Vaccine Immunology","title_org":"Clinical and Vaccine Immunology (Online)","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84856413301"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-142d7557-658e-476e-a40a-bd763db97dd0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Identification of immunogenic and virulence-associated <em>Campylobacter jejuni </em>proteins","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-405448","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Nectins belong to a family of immunoglobulin (Ig)-like cell-adhesion molecules comprising four members, nectin-1 through nectin-4. Nectins are involved in formation of the mechanical adhesive puncta adherentia junctions of synapses. Nectins share the same overall structural topology with an extracellular region containing three Ig modules, a transmembrane region, and a cytoplasmic region. In nectin-1, the first and second Ig module in the extracellular region are necessary for the trans-interaction with nectin-3 and formation of cis-dimers, respectively. The function of the third Ig module of nectin-1 remains unknown. We here report the structure in solution of the third, membrane-proximal Ig module of mouse nectin-1 (nectin-1 Ig3) solved by means of nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy. It belongs to the C1 set of the Ig superfamily. Nectin-1 Ig3 was produced as a recombinant protein and induced neurite outgrowth in primary cultures of hippocampal and cerebellar granule neurons, an effect abolished by treatment with the fibroblast growth factor receptor (FGFR) inhibitor SU5402, or by transfection with a dominant-negative FGFR1 construct. We showed by surface plasmon resonance (SPR) analysis that nectin-1 Ig3 directly interacted with various isoforms of FGFR. Nectin-1 Ig3 induced phosphorylation of FGFR1c in the same manner as the whole nectin-1 ectodomain, and promoted survival of cerebellar granule neurons induced to undergo apoptosis. Finally, we constructed a peptide, nectide, by employing in silico modeling of various FGFR ligand-binding sites. Nectide mimicked all the effects of nectin-1 Ig3. We suggest that FGFR is a downstream signaling partner of nectin-1.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bojesen, Kirsten Borup","Clausen, Ole","Rohde, Kristian","Christensen, Claus","Zhang, Lanjun","Li, Shizhong","Køhler, Lene Boding","Nielbo, Steen","Nielsen, Janne","Gjørlund, Michelle D","Poulsen, Flemming Martin","Bock, Elisabeth","Berezin, Vladimir"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-409983"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Amino Acid Sequence","Animals","Apoptosis","Cell Adhesion Molecules","Cell Survival","Crystallography X Ray","Fibroblast Growth Factor 2","HEK293 Cells","Hippocampus","Humans","Mice","Molecular Sequence Data","Neurites","Neurons","Phosphorylation","Primary Cell Culture","Protein Binding","Protein Isoforms","Protein Processing Post Translational","Protein Structure Secondary","Protein Structure Tertiary","Rats","Rats Wistar","Receptor Fibroblast Growth Factor Type 1","Signal Transduction","Surface plasmon resonance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nectin 000000000001 binds and signals through the fibroblast growth factor receptor","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M112.345215","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-409983","identifier":[{"id":"84868255070","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22955284","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3481338","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-1bbdf8d0-b470-4156-9999-2306d383f909"],"keyword":["Amino Acid Sequence","Animals","Apoptosis","Cell Adhesion Molecules","Cell Survival","Crystallography, X-Ray","Fibroblast Growth Factor 2","HEK293 Cells","Hippocampus","Humans","Mice","Molecular Sequence Data","Neurites","Neurons","Phosphorylation","Primary Cell Culture","Protein Binding","Protein Isoforms","Protein Processing, Post-Translational","Protein Structure, Secondary","Protein Structure, Tertiary","Rats","Rats, Wistar","Receptor, Fibroblast Growth Factor, Type 1","Receptors, Platelet-Derived Growth Factor","Signal Transduction","Surface Plasmon Resonance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-645C49CD2CC2212A67B09C2D3C317941"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M112.345215","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Eyepath Lab","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Molpharm Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten Borup","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","locid":"d3ae0dea-dd3f-4de1-b496-4d935754e837","name":"Bojesen, Kirsten Borup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"bf56d11d-6b1f-4609-8f38-23b964e3987d","name":"Clausen, Ole","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian","key":"rohdepau","last":"Rohde","locid":"b383085c-c86a-40b7-b3db-bb71ff9b2fb0","name":"Rohde, Kristian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"b40b0043-c4ee-470e-abb6-60dfc19c486c","name":"Christensen, Claus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lanjun","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"2cf0237a-cff9-4b81-9933-ca6e5d9ab613","name":"Zhang, Lanjun","orcid":"0000-0003-4042-0643","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shizhong","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"b242718d-db3f-485a-b34c-efffff27eb3c","name":"Li, Shizhong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Boding","key":"køhlerpau","last":"Køhler","locid":"cc88a3e6-58ee-48ec-ac9e-acdeece881c9","name":"Køhler, Lene Boding","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen","key":"nielbopau","last":"Nielbo","name":"Nielbo, Steen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4e80c802-ca59-4c3a-8621-8e1557cf122a","name":"Nielsen, Janne","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michelle Denise","key":"gjørlundpau","last":"Gjørlund","locid":"c14de171-38a0-4051-9fb0-534bbb2d6e3d","name":"Gjørlund, Michelle D","name_org":"Gjørlund, Michelle Denise","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming Martin","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"cbb78be8-909a-4ab4-bfc1-6808c8951ce5","name":"Poulsen, Flemming Martin","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Elisabeth Marianne","key":"bockpau","last":"Bock","locid":"cf857aa5-80e0-45c0-8a8b-6a682bc89bc1","name":"Bock, Elisabeth","name_org":"Bock, Elisabeth Marianne","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vladimir","key":"berezinpau","last":"Berezin","locid":"840f7697-fabc-4151-a4c9-3bbe18083b84","name":"Berezin, Vladimir","orcid":"0000-0002-9197-8199","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22955284"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m112.345215","issn":["00219258","10678816"],"issn_org":["00219258"],"issue":"44","journal":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","pages":"37420-37433","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","volume":"287"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84868255070"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1bbdf8d0-b470-4156-9999-2306d383f909"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nectin-1 binds and signals through the fibroblast growth factor receptor","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-409983","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Diabet. Med. 29, 558-566 (2012) ABSTRACT: Aims To explore incidence, risk factors, possible pathophysiological factors and clinical management of hypoglycaemia during pregnancy in women with Type 1 diabetes. Methods Literature review. Results In women with Type 1 diabetes, severe hypoglycaemia occurs three to five times more frequently in early pregnancy than in the period prior to pregnancy, whereas in the third trimester the incidence of severe hypoglycaemia is lower than in the year preceding pregnancy. The frequency distribution of severe hypoglycaemia is much skewed, as 10% of the pregnant women account for 60% of all recorded events. Risk factors for severe hypoglycaemia during pregnancy include a history with severe hypoglycaemia in the year preceding pregnancy, impaired hypoglycaemia awareness, long duration of diabetes, low HbA(1c) in early pregnancy, fluctuating plasma glucose values (= 3.9 mmol/l or = 10.0 mmol/l) and excessive use of supplementary insulin injections between meals. Pregnancy-induced nausea and vomiting seem not to be contributing factors. Conclusions Striving for near-normoglycaemia with focus on reduction of plasma glucose fluctuations during pregnancy should have high priority among clinicians with the persistent aim of improving pregnancy outcome among women with Type 1 diabetes. Pre-conception counselling, carbohydrate counting, use of insulin analogues, continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion (insulin pump) therapy and real-time continuous glucose monitoring with alarms for low glucose values might be relevant tools to obtain near-normoglycaemia without episodes of severe hypoglycaemia.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Ringholm","Pedersen-Bjergaard, U","Thorsteinsson, Birger","Damm, Peter","Mathiesen, Elisabeth R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-433963"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hypoglycaemia during pregnancy in women with type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1464-5491.2012.03604.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-433963","identifier":[{"id":"22313112","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84859833625","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-43dcab94-c8aa-4475-a84b-f4100dbea671"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1875FA53D7AF573B541BE5659883C8FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1464-5491.2012.03604.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Orthopaedics and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lene Ringholm","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ringholm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"U","key":"pedersenbjergaardpau","last":"Pedersen-Bjergaard","name":"Pedersen-Bjergaard, U","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"B","key":"thorsteinssonpau","last":"Thorsteinsson","locid":"6ad96c95-f3af-4f85-b392-b02c0eb34d0a","name":"Thorsteinsson, Birger","name_org":"Thorsteinsson, B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"P","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","locid":"884d03d5-5981-4d33-80c6-adb21f836deb","name":"Damm, Peter","name_org":"Damm, P","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"E R","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"