{"abstract":"Type 1 diabetes mellitus in pregnant women increases the risk of adverse outcomes for mother and offspring. Careful preconception counselling and screening is important, with particular focus on glycaemic control, indications for antihypertensive therapy, screening for diabetic nephropathy, diabetic retinopathy and thyroid dysfunction, as well as review of other medications. Supplementation with folic acid should be initiated before conception in order to minimize the risk of fetal malformations. Obtaining and maintaining tight control of blood glucose and blood pressure before and during pregnancy is crucial for optimizing outcomes; however, the risk of severe hypoglycaemia during pregnancy is a major obstacle. Although pregnancy does not result in deterioration of kidney function in women with diabetic nephropathy and normal serum creatinine levels, pregnancy complications such as pre-eclampsia and preterm delivery are more frequent in these women than in women with T1DM and normal kidney function. Rapid-acting insulin analogues are considered safe to use in pregnancy and studies on long-acting insulin analogues have provided reassuring results. Immediately after delivery the insulin requirement declines to approximately 60% of the prepregnancy dose, and remains 10% lower than before pregnancy during breastfeeding.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Ringholm","Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","Kelstrup, Louise","Damm, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-400888"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"managing type 000000000001 diabetes mellitus in pregnancy from planning to breastfeeding","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nrendo.2012.154","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-400888","identifier":[{"id":"84867676486","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22965164","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-0c7b3830-3350-4b85-8822-01ac4b179af1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77A808F6131D2E7C3C38BD068BB71C79"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nrendo.2012.154","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Orthopaedics and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lene Ringholm","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ringholm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elisabeth R","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"3acd58f4-6d64-4a89-a406-d2f43b310500","name":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","name_org":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"kelstruppau","last":"Kelstrup","name":"Kelstrup, Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","locid":"884d03d5-5981-4d33-80c6-adb21f836deb","name":"Damm, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22965164"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/nrendo.2012.154","issn":["17458374","17595029"],"issn_org":["17595029"],"issue":"11","journal":"Nature Reviews Endocrinology","pages":"659-67","status":"p","title":"Nature Reviews Endocrinology","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867676486"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0c7b3830-3350-4b85-8822-01ac4b179af1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Managing type 1 diabetes mellitus in pregnancy-from planning to breastfeeding","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-400888","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"A porcine model was used to examine the potential of human and porcine Staphylococcus aureus isolates to induce haematogenously spread osteomyelitis. Pigs were inoculated in the right femoral artery with one of the following S. aureus strains: S54F9 (from a porcine lung abscess; n = 3 animals), NCTC-8325-4 (a laboratory strain of human origin; n = 3 animals) and UAMS-1 (a human osteomyelitis isolate; n = 3 animals). Two pigs were sham inoculated with saline. At 11 or 15 days post infection the animals were scanned by computed tomography before being killed and subjected to necropsy examination. Osteomyelitis lesions were present in the right hind limb of all pigs inoculated with strain S54F9 and in one pig inoculated with strain NCTC-8325-4. Microscopically, there was extensive loss of bone tissue with surrounding granulation tissue. Sequestrated bone trabeculae were intermingled with colonies of S. aureus as demonstrated immunohistochemically. By peptide nucleic acid fluorescence in situ hybridization bacterial aggregates were demonstrated to be embedded in an opaque matrix, indicating that the bacteria had formed a biofilm. Development of experimental osteomyelitis was therefore dependent on the strain of bacteria inoculated and on the formation of a biofilm.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Johansen, L K","Koch, J","Frees, Dorte","Aalbæk, Bent","Nielsen, Ole Lerberg","Leifsson, Páll S.","Iburg, Tine Moesgaard","Svalastoga, Eiliv Lars","Buelund, Lene Elisabeth","Bjarnsholt, Thomas","Høiby, Niels","Jensen, Henrik Elvang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-430942"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Biofilms","Bone and Bones","DNA Bacterial","Disease Models Animal","Female","Hindlimb","In Situ Hybridization Fluorescence","Osteomyelitis","Specific Pathogen Free Organisms","Staphylococcal Infections","Staphylococcus aureus","Swine","Swine Diseases"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pathology and biofilm formation in a porcine model of staphylococcal osteomyelitis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcpa.2012.01.018","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-430942","identifier":[{"id":"22534025","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84864409666","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3ec2811b-f81e-429f-a71a-b9c44b48592a"],"keyword":["Animals","Biofilms","Bone and Bones","DNA, Bacterial","Disease Models, Animal","Female","Hindlimb","In Situ Hybridization, Fluorescence","Osteomyelitis","Specific Pathogen-Free Organisms","Staphylococcal Infections","Staphylococcus aureus","Swine","Swine Diseases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DECAFAAAD0C74AA1664E8912386B749B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcpa.2012.01.018","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"L K","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, L K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J","key":"kochpau","last":"Koch","name":"Koch, J","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"D","key":"freespau","last":"Frees","locid":"3c8c5596-8ecf-42c8-9a46-f67c6d95fed3","name":"Frees, Dorte","name_org":"Frees, D","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"B","key":"aalbæk