"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lea Vig","key":"mckinneyleavigpau","last":"McKinney","locid":"060df27a-59d3-4457-81a2-185cca16ae68","name":"McKinney, Lea Vig","orcid":"0000-0001-6601-4614","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Rostgaard","key":"nielsenlenerostgaardpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8e8b51ee-3f45-4ebe-b2fb-fa79f1256d08","name":"Nielsen, Lene Rostgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-7214-8691","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Nørgaard","key":"hansenlarsnørgaardpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d80deb4b-74d4-457a-87c3-2af0abd2c8e6","name":"Hansen, Lars Nørgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon Kehlet","key":"hansenjonkehletpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b8c2f3eb-b79f-46cc-b346-8300943e2129","name":"Hansen, Jon Kehlet","orcid":"0000-0002-1260-3509","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25568043"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1752-4571.2011.00222.x","issn":["17524563","17524571"],"issn_org":["17524563"],"issue":"3","journal":"Evolutionary Applications","pages":"219-228","status":"p","title":"Evolutionary Applications","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84859102425"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-74a39492-0398-4014-a3c0-b3d5e6f47480"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Adaptive potential of ash (<em>Fraxinus excelsior</em>) populations against the novel emerging pathogen <em>Hymenoscyphus pseudoalbidus</em>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-463186","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT: BACKGROUND: The aim of this study was to investigate the effect of various classes of clinically relevant antibiotics at sub-lethal concentrations on virulence gene expression and biofilm formation in Staphylococcus aureus. FINDINGS: LacZ promoter fusions of genes related to staphylococcal virulence were used to monitor the effects of antibiotics on gene expression in a disc diffusion assay. The selected genes were hla and spa encoding alpha-hemolysin and Protein A, respectively and RNAIII, the effector molecule of the agr quorum sensing system. The results were confirmed by quantitative real-time PCR. Additionally, we monitored the effect of subinhibitory concentrations of antibiotics on the ability of S. aureus to form biofilm in a microtiter plate assay. The results show that sub-lethal antibiotic concentrations diversely modulate expression of RNAIII, hla and spa. Consistently, expression of all three genes were repressed by aminoglycosides and induced by fluoroquinolones and penicillins. In contrast, the beta-lactam sub-group cephalosporins enhanced expression of RNAIII and hla but diversely affected expression of spa. The compounds cefalotin, cefamandole, cefoxitin, ceftazidime and cefixine were found to up-regulate spa, while down-regulation was observed for cefuroxime, cefotaxime and cefepime. Interestingly, biofilm assays demonstrated that the spa-inducing cefalotin resulted in less biofilm formation compared to the spa-repressing cefotaxime. CONCLUSIONS: We find that independently of the cephalosporin generation, cephalosporins oppositely regulate spa expression and biofilm formation. Repression of spa expression correlates with the presence of a distinct methyloxime group while induction correlates with an acidic substituted oxime group. As cephalosporines target the cell wall penicillin binding proteins we speculate that subtle differences in this interaction fine-tunes spa expression independently of agr.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Nørby","Roggenbuck, Michael","Haaber, Jakob Krause","Ifrah, Dan","Ingmer, Hanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-482093"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diverse modulation of spa transcription by cell wall active antibiotics in staphylococcus aureus","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1756-0500-5-457","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-482093","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3504574","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84865282147","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22920188","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9468b149-b995-45f5-8024-4a16b58355da"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-095A86C9E5F30C29272AEF3303370D80"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1756-0500-5-457","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Nørby","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1a4f890a-d171-4c2f-ae00-dd1e024c25ab","name":"Nielsen, Lene Nørby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"roggenbuckpau","last":"Roggenbuck","locid":"3ada6f69-2ab7-4d6a-b7c7-0f96d669dab7","name":"Roggenbuck, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Krause","key":"haaberpau","last":"Haaber","locid":"8003db93-f327-4cbc-ac20-8065a0eb45f5","name":"Haaber, Jakob Krause","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dan","key":"ifrahpau","last":"Ifrah","locid":"d1889d53-a58f-4662-9d27-da861d526908","name":"Ifrah, Dan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne","key":"ingmerpau","last":"Ingmer","locid":"abe2cd31-84e7-4f06-81a3-33e08bf93b8f","name":"Ingmer, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0002-8350-5631","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22920188"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1756-0500-5-457","issn":["17560500"],"issue":"457","journal":"BMC Research Notes","pages":"457","status":"p","title":"BMC Research Notes","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865282147"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9468b149-b995-45f5-8024-4a16b58355da"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diverse modulation of spa transcription by cell wall active antibiotics in Staphylococcus aureus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-482093","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Background/aims: High levels of pro-inflammatory cytokines are linked to inflammatory bowel disease (IBD). The transcription factor Caudal-related homeobox transcription factor 2 (CDX2) plays a crucial role in differentiation of intestinal epithelium and regulates IBD-susceptibility genes, including meprin 1A (MEP1A). The aim was to investigate the expression of CDX2 and MEP1A in colitis; to assess if they are regulated by tumor necrosis factor-a (TNF-a), and finally to reveal if CDX2 is involved in a TNF-a-induced down-regulation of MEP1A. Methods: Expression of CDX2 and MEP1A was investigated in colonic biopsies of ulcerative colitis (UC) patients and in dextran sodium sulfate (DSS)-induced colitis. CDX2 protein expression was investigated by immunoblotting and immunohistochemical procedures. CDX2 and MEP1A regulation was examined in TNF-a-treated Caco-2 cells by reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction and with reporter gene assays, and the effect of anti-TNF-a treatment was assessed using infliximab. Finally, in vivo CDX2-DNA interactions were investigated by chromatin immunoprecipitation. Results: The CDX2 and MEP1A mRNA expression was significantly decreased in active UC patients and in DSS-colitis. Colonic biopsy specimens from active UC showed markedly decreased CDX2 staining. TNF-a treatment diminished the CDX2 and MEP1A mRNA levels, a decrease which, was counteracted by infliximab treatment. Reporter gene assays showed significantly reduced CDX2 and MEP1A activity upon TNF-a stimulation. Finally, TNF-a impaired the ability of CDX2 to interact and activate its own, as well as the MEP1A expression. Conclusions: The present results indicate that a TNF-a-mediated down-regulation of CDX2 can be related to suppressed expression of MEP1A during intestinal inflammation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Coskun, Mehmet","Olsen, Anders Krüger","Holm, Thomas Lindebo","Kvist, Peter Helding","Nielsen, Ole Haagen","Riis, Lene Buhl","Olsen, Jørgen","Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-483384"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tnf a induced down regulation of cdx000000000002 suppresses mep000000000001a expression in colitis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbadis.2012.01.012","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-483384","identifier":[{"id":"22326557","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84858984691","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-967bbe3f-c1fa-4d6c-a281-c2cd56706b53"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-C83E615F7BA274B5572248484B275860"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbadis.2012.01.012","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mehmet","key":"coskunmehmetpau","last":"Coskun","locid":"6a19eccb-de97-41ce-9daa-a75afe94aa20","name":"Coskun, Mehmet","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Krüger","key":"olsenanderskrügerpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"af701802-1145-4e46-94ff-1fc07a549b94","name":"Olsen, Anders Krüger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas Lindebo","key":"holmthomaslindebopau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Thomas Lindebo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Helding","key":"kvistpeterheldingpau","last":"Kvist","name":"Kvist, Peter Helding","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole Haagen","key":"nielsenolehaagenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d59658c4-dde8-4749-9b5c-f4ec5910dd02","name":"Nielsen, Ole Haagen","orcid":"0000-0003-4612-8635","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Buhl","key":"riislenebuhlpau","last":"Riis","locid":"8ec061c0-f464-42fd-ac8d-f972f86292cd","name":"Riis, Lene Buhl","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen","key":"olsenjørgenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"dd6747c2-2376-4486-a000-1b4f1222eaaf","name":"Olsen, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-1974-6446","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jesper Thorvald","key":"troelsenjesperthorvaldpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"555180dd-5ada-4311-8be9-88685cec10a0","name":"Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22326557"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbadis.2012.01.012","issn":["03044165","18728006"],"issn_org":["03044165"],"issue":"6","journal":"BBA General Subjects","pages":"843-51","status":"p","title":"BBA General Subjects","volume":"1822"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84858984691"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-967bbe3f-c1fa-4d6c-a281-c2cd56706b53"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"TNF-a-induced down-regulation of CDX2 suppresses MEP1A expression in colitis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-483384","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
