{"abstract":"It has been speculated that gastrointestinal infection with Helicobacter pylori (HP) contributes to the development of Parkinson's disease (PD). We used nationwide Danish registers to investigate this hypothesis.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted","Qiu, J","Friis, S","Wermuth, Lene","Ritz, B"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-601128"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"treatment for helicobacter pylori infection and risk of parkinson s disease in denmark","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1468-1331.2011.03643.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-601128","identifier":[{"id":"84860896167","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22248366","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3330170","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-619c5438-f21f-4b5d-8eff-6095906a2cce"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-84537C5EDD4629C5D90AE95B221F1166"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1468-1331.2011.03643.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Neurology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"H H","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e1703e06-01b8-4d46-a1d1-4c4d5af99fa5","name":"Nielsen, Helle Hvilsted","name_org":"Nielsen, H H","orcid":"0000-0002-7319-1368","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"qiupau","last":"Qiu","name":"Qiu, J","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L","key":"wermuthpau","last":"Wermuth","locid":"0a2f7ea5-6a32-4590-a4f7-268caaa4ad2c","name":"Wermuth, Lene","name_org":"Wermuth, L","orcid":"0000-0001-6930-8562","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"B","key":"ritzpau","last":"Ritz","name":"Ritz, B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22248366"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1468-1331.2011.03643.x","issn":["13515101","14681331"],"issn_org":["13515101"],"issue":"6","journal":"European Journal of Neurology","pages":"864-9","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Neurology","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860896167"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-619c5438-f21f-4b5d-8eff-6095906a2cce"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Treatment for Helicobacter pylori infection and risk of Parkinson's disease in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-601128","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT: BACKGROUND: Despite twinning being common in Africa, few prospective twin studies have been conducted. We studied twinning rate, perinatal mortality and the clinical characteristics of newborn twins in urban Guinea-Bissau. METHODS: The study was conducted at the Bandim Health Project (BHP), a health and demographic surveillance site in Bissau, the capital of Guinea-Bissau. The cohort included all newborn twins delivered at the National Hospital Simao Mendes and in the BHP study area during the period September 2009 to August 2011 as well as singleton controls from the BHP study area. Data regarding obstetric history and pregnancy were collected at the hospital. Live children were examined clinically. For a subset of twin pairs zygosity was established by using genetic markers. RESULTS: Out of the 5262 births from mothers included in the BHP study area, 94 were twin births, i.e. a community twinning rate of 18/1000. The monozygotic rate was 3.4/1000. Perinatal mortality among twins vs. singletons was 218/1000 vs. 80/1000 (RR = 2.71, 95% CI: 1.93-3.80). Among the 13783 hospital births 388 were twin births (28/1000). The hospital perinatal twin mortality was 237/1000.Birth weight <2000g (RR = 4.24, CI: 2.39-7.51) and caesarean section (RR = 1.78, CI: 1.06-2.99) were significant risk factors for perinatal twin mortality. Male sex (RR = 1.38, CI: 0.97-1.96), unawareness of twin pregnancy (RR = 1.64, CI: 0.97-2.78) and high blood pressure during pregnancy (RR = 1.77, CI: 0.88-3.57) were borderline non-significant. Sixty-five percent (245/375) of the mothers who delivered at the hospital were unaware of their twin pregnancy. CONCLUSIONS: Twins had a very high perinatal mortality, three-fold higher than singletons. A birth weight <2000g was the strongest risk factor for perinatal death, and unrecognized twin pregnancy was common. Urgent interventions are needed to lower perinatal twin mortality in Guinea-Bissau.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","Lund, Najaaraq","Jepsen, Frida Staarup","Camala, Luis","Gomes, Margarida Alfredo","Christensen, Kaare","Christiansen, Lene","Jensen, Dorte Møller","Aaby, Peter","Beck-Nielsen, Henning","Benn, Christine Stabell","Sodemann, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-606056"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Guinea-Bissau"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bandim Health Project"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a prospective study of twinning and perinatal mortality in urban guinea bissau","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2393-12-140","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-606056","identifier":[{"id":"23216795","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84870367295","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3534574","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-72cdc309-a451-44a5-8fec-b64bed3ae838"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C9A2366C6EDB8CF6E34215DA315F1E81"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2393-12-140","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gw","key":"bandim health project","loc":["Guinea-Bissau","Africa"],"name":"Bandim Health Project","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"bjerregaardandersenpau","last":"Bjerregaard-Andersen","locid":"a8a0b3c8-4070-4770-86b2-1cb837092b6b","name":"Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4128-5714","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Najaaraq","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Najaaraq","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Frida Staarup","key":"jepsenpau","last":"Jepsen","name":"Jepsen, Frida Staarup","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Luis","key":"camalapau","last":"Camala","name":"Camala, Luis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Margarida Alfredo","key":"gomespau","last":"Gomes","name":"Gomes, Margarida Alfredo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaare","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"35c0eca6-0f49-465b-9bbd-ce71bcf2c4ac","name":"Christensen, Kaare","orcid":"0000-0002-5429-5292","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"fc457305-ddbb-4418-8648-e5fc4c63f490","name":"Christiansen, Lene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a221b393-70f9-4f53-902e-63d1a13f8f60","name":"Jensen, Dorte Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-3298-9824","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"aabypau","last":"