{"abstract":"AIMS/HYPOTHESIS: Low birthweight (BW) is associated with increased risk of type 2 diabetes. We compared glucose metabolism in adult BW-discordant monozygotic (MZ) twins, thereby controlling for genetic factors and rearing environment. METHODS: Among 77,885 twins in the Danish Twin Registry, 155 of the most BW-discordant MZ twin pairs (median BW difference 0.5 kg) were assessed using a 2 h oral glucose tolerance test with sampling of plasma (p-)glucose, insulin, C-peptide, glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide and glucagon-like peptide-1. HOMA for beta cell function (HOMA-β) and insulin resistance (HOMA-IR), and also insulin sensitivity index (BIGTT-SI) and acute insulin response (BIGTT-AIR), were calculated. Subgroup analyses were performed in those with: (1) double verification of BW difference; (2) difference in BW >0.5 kg; and (3) no overt metabolic disease (type 2 diabetes, hyperlipidaemia or thyroid disease). RESULTS: No intra-pair differences in p-glucose, insulin, C-peptide, incretin hormones, HOMA-β, HOMA-IR or BIGTT-SI were identified. p-Glucose at 120 min was higher in the twins with the highest BW without metabolic disease, and BIGTT-AIR was higher in those with the highest BW although not in pairs with a BW difference of >0.5 kg. CONCLUSIONS/INTERPRETATION: BW-discordant MZ twins provide no evidence for a detrimental effect of low BW on glucose metabolism in adulthood once genetic factors and rearing environment are controlled for.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Frost, M","Petersen, I","Brixen, K.","Beck-Nielsen, Henning","Holst, Jens Juul","Christiansen, L","Højlund, Kurt","Christensen, K"],"cuid":["S02-088.77-042057"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Birthweight","Fetal programming","Incretin hormones","Oral glucose tolerance","Twins","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adult glucose metabolism in extremely birthweight discordant monozygotic twins","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-012-2695-x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-088.77-042057","identifier":[{"id":"22955993","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84868213923","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-47ba7dfa-4344-4bdb-a124-aa72b7f55dcc","sdu-76bf12df-0c74-4a62-b873-53dbab0f0735"],"keyword":["Birthweight","Fetal programming","Incretin hormones","Oral glucose tolerance","Twins","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4FCCBBC879EEAA9A9BBA2690DDA12FDD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-012-2695-x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Epidemiology, Biostatistics and Biodemography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Studienævnet for Saxo-Instituttet"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Institut for Klinisk Medicin"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Frost Munk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"26ef8020-923a-483f-bd05-7f0c9d47d99c","name":"Frost, Morten","name_org":"Nielsen, Morten Frost Munk","orcid":"0000-0002-5608-1589","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M","key":"frostpau","last":"Frost","name":"Frost, M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"I","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1a691ed4-4171-4008-8829-14e807a2b7f7","name":"Petersen, Inge","name_org":"Petersen, I","orcid":"0000-0001-8057-8336","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"K","key":"brixenpau","last":"Brixen","locid":"411e6234-c5c5-40d5-ab2e-6a992e759e7e","name":"Brixen, K.","name_org":"Brixen, K","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H","key":"becknielsenpau","last":"Beck-Nielsen","locid":"0e78b588-9e9c-4acc-a1b8-8bcccea0b5a5","name":"Beck-Nielsen, Henning","name_org":"Beck-Nielsen, H","orcid":"0000-0002-7428-7898","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L","key":