{"abstract":"The vasoactive markers of cardiac overload Atrial Natriuretic Peptide (ANP) and Brain Natriuretic Peptide (BNP) are elevated in preeclampsia. This study documents higher ANP concentrations as early as at 9 weeks in type 1 diabetic women subsequently developing preeclampsia suggesting that preeclampsia is associated with cardiovascular changes in early pregnancy.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Ringholm","Pedersen-Bjergaard, Ulrik","Thorsteinsson, Birger","Boomsma, Frans","Damm, Peter","Mathiesen, Elisabeth R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-418197"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"atrial natriuretic peptide anp in early pregnancy is associated with development of preeclampsia in type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2011.06.007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-418197","identifier":[{"id":"80052691812","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-297ceb5b-7543-4be7-9243-32d43d90f878"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E7C6D6E70343E1840677857506DAC975"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2011.06.007","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Orthopaedics and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lene Ringholm","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ringholm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulrik","key":"pedersenbjergaardpau","last":"Pedersen-Bjergaard","name":"Pedersen-Bjergaard, Ulrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birger","key":"thorsteinssonpau","last":"Thorsteinsson","locid":"6ad96c95-f3af-4f85-b392-b02c0eb34d0a","name":"Thorsteinsson, Birger","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Frans","key":"boomsmapau","last":"Boomsma","name":"Boomsma, Frans","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","locid":"884d03d5-5981-4d33-80c6-adb21f836deb","name":"Damm, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elisabeth R","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"3acd58f4-6d64-4a89-a406-d2f43b310500","name":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","name_org":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.diabres.2011.06.007","issn":["01688227","15721671"],"issn_org":["01688227"],"issue":"3","journal":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80052691812"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-297ceb5b-7543-4be7-9243-32d43d90f878"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Atrial Natriuretic Peptide (ANP) in early pregnancy is associated with development of preeclampsia in type 1 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-418197","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Pregnancy in women with pregestational diabetes is associated with high perinatal morbidity and mortality. Stillbirth accounts for the majority of cases with perinatal death. Intrauterine growth restriction, pre-eclampsia, foetal hypoxia and congenital malformations may be contributing factors, but more than 50% of stillbirths are unexplained. Majority of stillbirths are characterised by suboptimal glycaemic control during pregnancy. Foetal hypoxia and cardiac dysfunction secondary to poor glycaemic control are probably the most important pathogenic factors in stillbirths among pregnant diabetic women. There is thus a need for new strategies for improving glycaemic control to near-normal levels throughout pregnancy and for preventing and treating hypertensive disorders in pregnancy. Antenatal surveillance tests including ultrasound examinations of the foetal growth rate, kick counting and non-stress testing of foetal cardiac function are widely used. However, future research should establish better antenatal surveillance tests to identify the infants susceptible to stillbirth before it happens.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","Damm, Peter","Nielsen, Lene Ringholm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-488379"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stillbirth in diabetic pregnancies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpobgyn.2010.11.001","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-488379","identifier":[{"id":"21256813","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79651469165","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9edf0383-f814-4ca9-bce3-0b5884bb1df5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3FB8A38EE6C6E185CCA1D2F7397D6B3A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpobgyn.2010.11.001","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Orthopaedics and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Elisabeth R","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"3acd58f4-6d64-4a89-a406-d2f43b310500","name":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R.","name_org":"Mathiesen, Elisabeth R","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","locid":"884d03d5-5981-4d33-80c6-adb21f836deb","name":"Damm, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Ringholm","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene Ringholm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21256813"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bpobgyn.2010.11.001","issn":["15216934","15321932"],"issn_org":["15216934"],"issue":"1","journal":"Best Practice & Research: Clinical Obstetrics & Gynaecology","pages":"105-11","status":"p","title":"Best Practice & Research: Clinical Obstetrics & Gynaecology","volume":"25"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-79651469165"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9edf0383-f814-4ca9-bce3-0b5884bb1df5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Stillbirth in diabetic pregnancies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-488379","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Dual energy X-ray absorptiometry (DEXA) is a reference method for assessing body composition but is seldom `accessible in veterinary settings. Computed tomography (CT) can provide similar body composition estimates and we propose that it can be used in body composition studies in animals. We compared CT and DEXA data from 73 healthy adult neutered domestic cats. Three approaches for measuring adipose tissue percentage from full-body CT scans were explored. By examining the frequency distribution of voxels by Hounsfield unit (HU) value, it is possible to calculate a fat index (Fat%) that is in close agreement with the fat percentages obtained from DEXA scans. Fat% values obtained by the best of the methods had a mean difference of 0.96% (95% confidence interval 0.33-1.59%) from the DEXA results. Fat% obtained by the other two methods were characterized by good correlation but poor agreement and in one of the methods, the difference between the values from the two modalities was proportional to their mean. By using CT, it is possible to obtain body composition estimates that are in close agreement with those available using DEXA. While the significance of individual Fat% measurements obtained from CT can be difficult to interpret and to compare between centers, CT can contribute to research studies concerned either with nutrition or with obesity-related disorders.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Buelund, Lene Elisabeth","Nielsen, Dorte Hald","McEvoy, Fintan","Svalastoga, Eiliv Lars","Bjørnvad, Charlotte Reinhard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-517159"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Absorptiometry Photon","Adipose tissue","Animals","Body composition","Cats","Female","Male","Tomography X Ray Computed"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measurement of body composition in cats using computed tomography and dual energy x ray absorptiometry","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1740-8261.2010.01765.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-517159","identifier":[{"id":"21388470","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79952471230","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cf0f77c9-27e8-4364-970e-5d3e143702d1"],"keyword":["Absorptiometry, Photon","Adipose Tissue","Animals","Body Composition","Cats","Female","Male","Tomography, X-Ray Computed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-CBFE72AAD3917923C858E43041031F9A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1740-8261.2010.01765.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Small Animal Clinical Sciences, LUKKET: 2012 Røntgen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene E","key":"buelundpau","last":"Buelund","locid":"08519bcf-e2b1-4ae0-8da9-bd7653cd8a9d","name":"Buelund, Lene Elisabeth","name_org":"Buelund, Lene E","orcid":"0000-0002-4730-4111","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dorte H","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc3c2ecf-7eeb-4376-baa7-616bf7a33353","name":"Nielsen, Dorte Hald","name_org":"Nielsen, Dorte H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Fintan","key":"mcevoypau","last":"McEvoy","locid":"38cc3ea7-06d4-43f9-b239-092f41bcd16b","name":"McEvoy, Fintan","orcid":"0000-0003-4195-8816","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eiliv L","key":"svalastogapau","last":"Svalastoga","locid":"246e22f3-4624-4ec6-945c-372a2b6af487","name":"Svalastoga, Eiliv Lars","name_org":"Svalastoga, Eiliv L","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte R","key":"bjornvadpau","last":"Bjornvad","locid":"f946e17b-7ca4-4847-ac8a-a0e8f3e95efb","name":"Bjørnvad, Charlotte Reinhard","name_org":"Bjornvad, Charlotte R","orcid":"0000-0002-2876-1667","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21388470"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1740-8261.2010.01765.x","issn":["10588183","17408261"],"issn_org":["10588183"],"issue":"2","journal":"Veterinary Radiology & Ultrasound","pages":"179-184","status":"p","title":"Veterinary Radiology & Ultrasound","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79952471230"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cf0f77c9-27e8-4364-970e-5d3e143702d1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Measurement of body composition in cats using computed tomography and dual energy X-ray absorptiometry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-517159","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
