or Severe Sepsis/Septic Shock trial): Study protocol, design and rationale for a double-blinded, randomised clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.79-040358","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This study investigated microbiological, clinical, and management issues and outcomes for Danish fungemia patients. Isolates and clinical information were collected at six centers. A total of 334 isolates, 316 episodes, and 305 patients were included, corresponding to 2/3 of the national episodes. Blood culture positivity varied by system, species, and procedure. Thus, cases with concomitant bacteremia were reported less commonly by BacT/Alert than by the Bactec system (9% [11/124 cases] versus 28% [53/192 cases]; P <0.0001), and cultures with Candida glabrata or those drawn via arterial lines needed longer incubation. Species distribution varied by age, prior antifungal treatment (57% occurrence of C. glabrata, Saccharomyces cerevisiae, or C. krusei in patients with prior antifungal treatment versus 28% occurrence in those without it; P = 0.007), and clinical specialty (61% occurrence of C. glabrata or C. krusei in hematology wards versus 27% occurrence in other wards; P = 0.002). Colonization samples were not predictive for the invasive species in 11/100 cases. Fifty-six percent of the patients had undergone surgery, 51% were intensive care unit (ICU) patients, and 33% had malignant disease. Mortality increased by age (P = 0.009) and varied by species (36% for C. krusei, 25% for C. parapsilosis, and 14% for other Candida species), severity of underlying disease (47% for ICU patients versus 24% for others; P = 0.0001), and choice but not timing of initial therapy (12% versus 48% for patients with C. glabrata infection receiving caspofungin versus fluconazole; P = 0.023). The initial antifungal agent was deemed suboptimal upon species identification in 15% of the cases, which would have been 6.5% if current guidelines had been followed. A large proportion of Danish fungemia patients were severely ill and received suboptimal initial antifungal treatment. Optimization of diagnosis and therapy is possible.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Arendrup, Maiken Cavling","Sulim, Sofia","Holm, Anette","Nielsen, Lene","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Knudsen, Jenny Dahl","Drenck, Niels Erik","Christensen, Jens Jørgen","Johansen, Helle Krogh"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-014451"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Antifungal Agents","Candida","Child","Child Preschool","Denmark","Female","Fungemia","Humans","Infant","Infant Newborn","Male","Middle Aged","Risk Factors","Saccharomyces cerevisiae","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic issues clinical characteristics and outcomes for patients with fungemia","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/JCM.00179-11","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-014451","identifier":[{"id":"80052219362","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21715585","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3165619","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-19a1faec-5d94-4822-aaa4-286ca3966823","ku-81af09ea-f040-484e-ab67-a35cf4eeb767","sdu-36a94e62-c918-4176-b253-c48bb62da13b"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Antifungal Agents","Candida","Child","Child, Preschool","Denmark","Female","Fungemia","Humans","Infant","Infant, Newborn","Male","Middle Aged","Risk Factors","Saccharomyces cerevisiae","Treatment Outcome","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-C9548EA816DA169251