{"abstract":"The combination of delivery systems such as cationic liposomes and immunopotentiating molecules is a promising approach for the rational design of vaccine adjuvants. In this study, a synthetic analogue of the mycobacterial lipid monomycoloyl glycerol (MMG), referred to as MMG-1, was synthesized and combined with the cationic surfactant dimethyldioctadecylammonium (DDA). The purpose of the study was to provide a thorough pharmaceutical characterization of the resulting DDA/MMG-1 binary system and to evaluate how incorporation of MMG-1 affected the adjuvant activity of DDA liposomes. Thermal analyses demonstrated that MMG-1 was incorporated into the DDA lipid bilayers, and cryo-transmission electron microscopy (TEM) confirmed that liposomes were formed. The particles had a polydisperse size distribution and an average diameter of approximately 400 nm. Evaluation of the colloidal stability indicated that at least 18 mol% MMG-1 was required to stabilize the DDA liposomes as the average particle size remained constant during storage for 6 months. The improved colloidal stability is most likely caused by increased hydration of the lipid bilayer. This was demonstrated by studying Langmuir–Blodgett monolayers of DDA and MMG-1 which revealed an increased surface pressure in the presence of high concentrations of MMG-1 when the DDA/MMG-1 monolayers were fully compressed, indicating an increased interaction with water due to enhanced hydration of the lipid head groups. Finally, immunization of mice with the tuberculosis fusion antigen Ag85B-ESAT-6 and DDA/MMG-1 liposomes induced a strong cell-mediated immune response characterized by a mixed Th1/Th17 profile and secretion of IgG1 and IgG2c antibodies. The Th1/Th17-biased immunostimulatory effect was increased in an MMG-1 concentration-dependent manner with maximal observed effect at 31 mol% MMG-1. Thus, incorporation of 31 mol% MMG-1 into DDA liposomes results in an adjuvant system with favorable physical as well as immunological properties.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nordly, Pernille Juul","Korsholm, Karen Smith","Pedersen, Esra Alici","Khilji, Tayba Sajid","Franzyk, Henrik","Jørgensen, Lene","Nielsen, Hanne Mørck","Agger, Else Marie","Foged, Camilla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-408681"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Former Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incorporation of a synthetic mycobacterial monomycoloyl glycerol analogue stabilizes dimethyldioctadecylammonium liposomes and potentiates their adjuvant effect em in vivo em","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-408681","identifier":[{"id":"78650711244","type":"scopus"},{"id":"20940050","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-197c7ac9-f494-47c6-8fa0-6a3e680e33c7"],"keyword":["Former Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7C4A28818D9058810CBCF7C0E14C7F9C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pernille Juul","key":"nordlypau","last":"Nordly","locid":"1e38073a-2d72-4587-8658-a6b5bfd40090","name":"Nordly, Pernille Juul","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Karen Smith","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","name":"Korsholm, Karen Smith","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Esra Alici","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5c619cb4-377c-4131-925b-27c771735438","name":"Pedersen, Esra Alici","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tayba Sajid","key":"khiljipau","last":"Khilji","locid":"9d90c4ea-70e5-4780-a72d-c4a32ee66e36","name":"Khilji, Tayba Sajid","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"franzykpau","last":"Franzyk","locid":"5120ce68-6886-4ac8-8178-310a47d19261","name":"Franzyk, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2822-1927","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Lene","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"d44a0998-9a19-40de-8d46-eb4234a9d3c4","name":"Jørgensen, Lene","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Mørck","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7b0450b3-f634-47ec-912c-b07ecd943be8","name":"Nielsen, Hanne Mørck","orcid":"0000-0002-7285-9100","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Else Marie","key":"aggerpau","last":"Agger","name":"Agger, Else Marie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"fogedpau","last":"Foged","locid":"4fa50122-02cc-483c-b233-6702750f9798","name":"Foged, Camilla","orcid":"0000-0003-2812-5588","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["20940050"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejpb.2010.10.001","issn":["09396411","18733441"],"issn_org":["09396411"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Journal of Pharmaceutics and Biopharmaceutics","pages":"89-98","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pharmaceutics and Biopharmaceutics","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78650711244"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-197c7ac9-f494-47c6-8fa0-6a3e680e33c7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Incorporation of a synthetic mycobacterial monomycoloyl glycerol analogue stabilizes dimethyldioctadecylammonium liposomes and potentiates their adjuvant effect <em>in vivo</em>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-408681","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"A new type of resorbable biomaterial intended for pelvic reconstruction was tested with respect to tissue regeneration and biocompatibility in rats. The biomaterial consisted of methoxypolyethyleneglycol-poly (lactic-co-glycolic acid) (MPEG-PLGA). Implants were pure, enriched with extra-cellular matrix (ECM) or estrogen. Methods Ten implants of each type were tested for 3 and 8 weeks, respectively. Histological assessment of connective tissue organization, inflammation, vascularization, and thickness of regenerated tissue was undertaken. Results All implants had a high degree of biocompatibility. ECM-enriched implants had significantly higher inflammatory scores compared to pure implants at 3 weeks. At 8 weeks, neither of the parameters differed significantly. No trace of the implants remained. Conclusions The MPEG-PLGA is highly biocompatible, degrades quickly, and seems inert in the process of tissue regeneration. Thus, it is hardly a candidate per se in reinforcement of pelvic reconstruction, but it could have a future role as carrier for stem cells.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Boennelycke, Marie","Christensen, Lise","Nielsen, Lene Feldskov","Everland, Hanne","Lose, Gunnar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-415317"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tissue response to a new type of biomaterial implanted subcutaneously in rats","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00192-010-1257-3","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-415317","identifier":[{"id":"79951661211","type":"scopus"},{"id":"20838988","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-24b15028-882c-449a-a142-0e87d01c6572"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8ED67C5F47CDD0AEFF0D20C646B35713"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00192-010-1257-3","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Gynaecology, Obstetrics and Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Marie","key":"boennelyckepau","last":"Boennelycke","locid":"94d27192-afd2-4a82-acfd-5ea28621ff12","name":"Boennelycke, Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lise","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Lise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene Feldskov","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene Feldskov","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne","key":"everlandpau","last":"Everland","name":"Everland, Hanne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gunnar","key":"losepau","last":"Lose","locid":"8953a978-1cfd-4afc-9320-fad5203487a1","name":"Lose, Gunnar","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["20838988"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00192-010-1257-3","issn":["09373462","14333023"],"issn_org":["09373462"],"issue":"2","journal":"International Urogynecology Journal","pages":"191-6","status":"p","title":"International Urogynecology Journal","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79951661211"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-24b15028-882c-449a-a142-0e87d01c6572"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tissue response to a new type of biomaterial implanted subcutaneously in rats","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-415317","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
